        "8780": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "8785": {"synopsis":"Row of one byte a pixel: IXL bytes at HL inverted.","comment":"D = the bytes"},
        "8787": {"synopsis":"One pixel inverted.","comment":"One pixel inverted"},
        "8792": {"comment":"Across the row"},
        "8795": {"synopsis":"Copies C bytes (256 for 0) between the screen at DE and the store at ($5B9B), which moves on\npast them:\n1. $5C92 bit 7 set: from the screen to the store.\n2. Otherwise from the store to the screen, combined by $5C92 bits 0-2: 0 copied, 1 AND, 2\n   OR, 3 XOR, 4-7 copied except the bytes equal to $5C93 (LDIRX).\nWCH_STORE_GO is the same with HL = the store's place.\nExit: HL = the store's new place (also at $5B9B), DE = past the screen bytes.","comment":"HL = the store"},
        "8798": {"synopsis":"The same with HL = the store's place.","comment":"Which way, and how"},
        "8801": {"comment":"To the store?"},
        "8805": {"comment":"Then from the screen"},
        "8806": {"synopsis":"How the bytes are combined: $5C92 bits 0-2.","comment":"The way they combine"},
        "8808": {"comment":"0: copied"},
        "8810": {"comment":"1: AND"},
        "8813": {"comment":"2: OR"},
        "8816": {"comment":"3: XOR"},
        "8819": {"comment":"4-7: A = the byte to skip"},
        "8822": {"comment":"Count kept"},
        "8823": {"comment":"BC = 256 for C = 0"},
        "8825": {"comment":"Copied, bytes equal to A left out"},
        "8829": {"synopsis":"1: ANDed.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8830": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"One byte ANDed"},
        "8835": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "8837": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8839": {"synopsis":"2: ORed.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8840": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"One byte ORed"},
        "8845": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "8847": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8849": {"synopsis":"3: XORed.","comment":"B = the count"},
        "8850": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"One byte XORed"},
        "8855": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "8857": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8859": {"synopsis":"0: copied.","comment":"Count kept"},
        "8860": {"comment":"BC = 256 for C = 0"},
        "8862": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "8864": {"synopsis":"The count back.","comment":"Count back"},
        "8865": {"synopsis":"HL = the store's place again (it was DE when saving), kept at $5B9B.","comment":"To the store?"},
        "8869": {"comment":"No: HL is the store"},
        "8871": {"comment":"Yes: HL = the store"},
        "8872": {"synopsis":"The store's new place.","comment":"The store's new place"},
        "8876": {"synopsis":"The screen addresses of cell column A on pixel row D.\nExit: DE = the pixel byte, HL = its attribute.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"E = the pixel column"},
        "8880": {"synopsis":"The same for pixel column E on pixel row D (PIXELAD).","comment":"HL = the pixel byte"},
        "8882": {"comment":"A = the row"},
        "8883": {"comment":"The row / 64"},
        "8887": {"comment":"D = $58 + row / 64"},
        "8890": {"comment":"E = the row and column bits"},
        "8891": {"comment":"DE = pixel byte, HL = attribute"},
        "8893": {"synopsis":"Half of a block graphic: from bits 0 and 1 of E (shifted out), a row whose left B + 1 pixels\nare bit 1 and the next C + 1 pixels bit 0, stored 4 times at HL (moved on). C = 0 counts as\n256, which fills the rest of the byte.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "8894": {"comment":"Bit 0 out"},
        "8896": {"comment":"Into bit 7"},
        "8897": {"synopsis":"Bit 0 spread over the right part's width (C).","comment":"Spread over C more pixels"},
        "8902": {"comment":"Bit 1 out"},
        "8904": {"comment":"In front of it"},
        "8905": {"synopsis":"Bit 1 spread over the left part's width (B), the right part moving along.","comment":"Spread over B more pixels"},
        "8909": {"comment":"Four rows of it"},
        "8911": {"synopsis":"One row of the four stored.","comment":"One row stored"},
        "8913": {"comment":"Four times"},
        "8916": {"synopsis":"HL = the window's character set for character width A (the place of code 0's glyph; the sets\nin page 16 made by WCH_MAKE_FONTS, seen through MMU 7): 3 and 4 $EC00, 5 and 6 $EF00, 7\n$F700, 8 $FB00. Called from $16D7 and $1914.\nOther widths: error code $0A (report B).","comment":"Below 3?"},
        "8920": {"comment":"Above 8?"},
        "8924": {"comment":"3-4: the 3-pixel set"},
        "8927": {"comment":"Width 3 or 4?"},
        "8930": {"comment":"The 5-pixel set"},
        "8932": {"comment":"5 or 6?"},
        "8935": {"comment":"7: the 7-pixel set"},
        "8938": {"comment":"8: ROM 3's set"},
        "8941": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B) through $27AF: a character width outside 3-8.","comment":"Error code $0A"},
        "8943": {"comment":"Stops with it"},
        "8946": {"synopsis":"The window records' starting values (+$0D to +$20), written by WCH_SET_RECORDS. First the\nwhole 20 bytes of the record at $F30D (mode 1, LoRes): character set $FB00, width 8, mask\n$FF, 16 x 12 cells at 0,0 (last column 15, last row 11), pixel rows 0-$60, +$19 = $10,\npauses every 12 rows (+$1A, +$1B = 1), 16 characters a line in 8-pixel cells, mode 1, ink 0,\npaper $FF. Then ($2306) the 15 bytes the other four share: the same set, width and mask, 32\nx 24 cells, last column 31, last row 23, pixel rows 0-$C0, +$19 = $10, pauses every 24 rows.\nThen each one's 5 (+$1C to +$20: characters a line, cell width, mode, ink/attribute, paper):\n$2315 for $F40D: 32, 8, mode 2 (Layer 2), 0, $FF; $231A for $FB0D: 64, 16, mode 9 (hi-res),\n0, 0; $231F for $F70D: 32, 8, mode 5 (standard), $38, 0; $2324 for $FF0D: 32, 8, mode $0D\n(hi-colour), $38, 0."},
        "9001": {"synopsis":"Start-up set-up of the window channels' workspace in 8K page 16 (called from $0271):\n1. $270A: page 11 and 16 into MMU 4 and 5 (page 16 at $A000), the stack moved.\n2. Unless B is 1: page 16's $A000-$A151 cleared, $FF at $A000-$A002 and $A028-$A02A, $3FF7\n   at $A020 and $A048, ($5B69 + 1) x 2 at $A050 and $10 at $A051; then ROM 2's $01BD with HL\n   = 1, its E kept at $5B58.\n3. ROM 3's character set ($3D00, $300 bytes) copied to $BC00 by ROM 3's LDIR at $33C3, and\n   the narrower sets made from it (WCH_MAKE_FONTS).\n4. MMU 4-5 back ($2799); then, through the address pushed at the start, WCH_INIT_RECS.","comment":"WCH_INIT_RECS runs after"},
        "9005": {"comment":"E = B"},
        "9006": {"comment":"MMU 4-5: pages 11 and 16"},
        "9011": {"comment":"B = 1?"},
        "9012": {"comment":"Then no clearing"},
        "9014": {"comment":"$A000-$A151"},
        "9023": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "9026": {"comment":"A = $5B69 + 1"},
        "9030": {"comment":"x 2 to $A050"},
        "9034": {"comment":"$10 to $A051"},
        "9039": {"comment":"$FF to $A000-$A002, $A028-$A02A"},
        "9055": {"comment":"$3FF7 to $A020 and $A048"},
        "9064": {"comment":"HL = 1"},
        "9067": {"comment":"ROM 2's $01BD"},
        "9070": {"comment":"Its E kept"},
        "9074": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's character set to $BC00 and the narrower sets.","comment":"ROM 3's character set"},
        "9077": {"comment":"To $BC00 (page 16 + $1C00)"},
        "9080": {"comment":"$300 bytes"},
        "9083": {"comment":"Copied with ROM 3 paged in"},
        "9086": {"comment":"The other sets made from it"},
        "9089": {"comment":"MMU 4-5 back"},
        "9094": {"synopsis":"With page 11 and 16 in MMU 6-7 ($2708): the window records written (WCH_SET_RECORDS), and\n$F700-$F72F and $FB00-$FB2F each copied $30 bytes on ($0F54); then MMU 6-7 and the stack\nback ($2797).","comment":"MMU 6-7: pages 11 and 16"},
        "9097": {"comment":"The five records"},
        "9100": {"comment":"$F700-$F72F copied $30 on"},
        "9106": {"comment":"$FB00-$FB2F copied $30 on"},
        "9112": {"comment":"MMU 6-7 and the stack back"},
        "9115": {"synopsis":"Makes page 16's narrower character sets (page 16 in MMU 5), 96 characters each:\n1. The 7-pixel set at $B800: ROM 3's at $BC00 with each row one pixel left.\n2. The 3-pixel set at $AD00 (bits 7-5) and the 5-pixel set at $B000 (bits 4-0 moved to 7-3),\n   from WCH_FONT_BYTES: the top row blank, rows 1-6 from the table, the bottom row blank\n   unless WCH_FONT_LOW gives one.\nKeeps IX. Also from $1968.","comment":"ROM 3's set"},
        "9118": {"comment":"The 7-pixel set"},
        "9121": {"comment":"3 x 256 bytes"},
        "9124": {"synopsis":"One row moved a pixel left.","comment":"One row"},
        "9126": {"comment":"One pixel left"},
        "9129": {"comment":"Across 256 bytes"},
        "9131": {"comment":"The next 256"},
        "9134": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "9136": {"comment":"The bottom rows' table"},
        "9140": {"comment":"The packed set"},
        "9143": {"comment":"The 3-pixel set"},
        "9146": {"comment":"96 characters"},
        "9148": {"synopsis":"One character: 8 rows.","comment":"8 rows"},
        "9150": {"synopsis":"One row.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "9151": {"comment":"The top row?"},
        "9153": {"comment":"Blank"},
        "9155": {"comment":"The bottom row?"},
        "9159": {"comment":"A = the count of characters left"},
        "9160": {"comment":"This character next in the table?"},
        "9163": {"comment":"A = 0, flags kept"},
        "9165": {"comment":"No: blank"},
        "9167": {"comment":"Yes: its row"},
        "9169": {"comment":"A = the row from the pair"},
        "9172": {"comment":"Past the pair"},
        "9176": {"synopsis":"Rows 1-6: the next byte of WCH_FONT_BYTES.","comment":"Rows 1-6: from the packed set"},
        "9178": {"synopsis":"The row's bits 7-5 into the 3-pixel set, its bits 4-0 into the 5-pixel set ($300 on).","comment":"Kept"},
        "9179": {"comment":"Bits 7-5: the 3-pixel row"},
        "9182": {"comment":"D + 3: the 5-pixel set"},
        "9185": {"comment":"Back"},
        "9186": {"comment":"Bits 4-0 to 7-3"},
        "9189": {"comment":"The 5-pixel row"},
        "9190": {"comment":"Back to the 3-pixel set"},
        "9193": {"comment":"The next row"},
        "9194": {"comment":"8 rows?"},
        "9197": {"comment":"96 characters?"},
        "9199": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "9202": {"synopsis":"The packed narrow character set for codes $20-$7F, read by WCH_MAKE_FONTS: 6 bytes a\ncharacter, its pixel rows 1-6. In each byte bits 7-5 are the 3-pixel glyph's row and bits\n4-0 the 5-pixel glyph's (e.g. 'A' at $24B8)."},
        "9778": {"synopsis":"The bottom rows that are not blank in WCH_FONT_BYTES' glyphs, read by WCH_MAKE_FONTS: pairs\nof (the count of characters left, $60 for the first; the row byte), in the order of the\ncharacters: '$', 'Q', '_', 'g', 'j', 'p', 'q', 'y' and the copyright sign ($7F)."},
        "9796": {"synopsis":"With page 11 and 16 in MMU 6-7 ($2708): the window records written again (WCH_SET_RECORDS);\nthen back ($2797). Called from page 1 ($14BF).","comment":"MMU 6-7: pages 11 and 16"},
        "9799": {"comment":"The five records"},
        "9802": {"comment":"MMU 6-7 and the stack back"},
        "9805": {"synopsis":"Writes the five window records, 35 bytes each, at $F30D, $F40D, $FB0D, $F70D and $FF0D (page\n16 in MMU 7), from WCH_DEFAULTS: the first's 20 bytes, then for the others the shared 15 and\ntheir own 5 (WCH_WRITE_REC); 15 zero bytes after each.\nExit: BC = $2329, past the tables.","comment":"The first record's 20 bytes"},
        "9808": {"comment":"To $F30D"},
        "9816": {"comment":"15 zero bytes after"},
        "9819": {"comment":"The second: $F40D"},
        "9822": {"comment":"BC = its 5 own bytes"},
        "9825": {"comment":"Written"},
        "9828": {"comment":"The third: $FB0D"},
        "9834": {"comment":"The fourth: $F70D"},
        "9840": {"comment":"The fifth: $FF0D"},
        "9843": {"synopsis":"Writes a record at DE: the 15 bytes at HL, the 5 at BC, then 15 zero bytes.\nExit: BC = past the 5 bytes, the next record's; HL kept.","comment":"The shared part kept"},
        "9844": {"comment":"The own part"},
        "9845": {"comment":"15 bytes"},
        "9850": {"comment":"HL = the own part"},
        "9851": {"comment":"5 bytes"},
        "9855": {"comment":"15 zero bytes"},
        "9858": {"comment":"BC = the next own part"},
        "9860": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9862": {"synopsis":"15 zero bytes at DE, moved on.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"15"},
        "9864": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "9865": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9870": {"synopsis":"WCH_BYTES_ADDR with carry: in Layer 2 MMU 7 gets the next page too, 16K in all.","comment":"Carry: MMU 7 as well"},
        "9871": {"synopsis":"HL = the byte of pixel column L on pixel row H of a screen of one byte a pixel, paged in:\n1. Layer 2 ($5C7F bit 1): the 8K page holding the row (NextReg $13, the Layer 2 shadow bank,\n   x 2 + row / 32) into MMU 6, and with carry the next one into MMU 7; HL = $C000 + the row\n   within the page x 256 + the column.\nExit: B = $E0 (the page's end), C = $FF.\n2. LoRes: HL = $4000 + row x 128 + column; the lower half (from $5800 up, $6000 in bank 5)\n   seen at $C000 through MMU 6's page 11.\nExit: B = $58 or $D8 (the half's end), C = $7F.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"Layer 2?"},
        "9875": {"comment":"No: LoRes"},
        "9877": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "9878": {"comment":"Carry kept"},
        "9879": {"comment":"E = row / 32: the 8K part"},
        "9886": {"comment":"H = $C0 + the row within it"},
        "9892": {"comment":"NextReg $13: Layer 2's shadow bank"},
        "9899": {"comment":"Read"},
        "9902": {"comment":"x 2: its first 8K page"},
        "9903": {"comment":"Plus the part"},
        "9905": {"comment":"Into MMU 6"},
        "9908": {"comment":"Both slots?"},
        "9911": {"comment":"The next page into MMU 7"},
        "9916": {"synopsis":"B = the 8K page's end, C = the row's length - 1.","comment":"DE back"},
        "9917": {"comment":"B = the page's end, C = $FF"},
        "9921": {"synopsis":"LoRes: two rows of 128 to each 256 bytes.","comment":"H = row / 2"},
        "9923": {"comment":"Odd row?"},
        "9925": {"comment":"Then the second 128 bytes"},
        "9927": {"synopsis":"HL in the upper half, or moved to the lower one at $C000.","comment":"H = $40 + row / 2"},
        "9929": {"comment":"B = the upper half's end, C = $7F"},
        "9932": {"comment":"In the upper half?"},
        "9935": {"comment":"Lower half: at $C000 (page 11)"},
        "9938": {"comment":"B = its end"},
        "9941": {"synopsis":"WCH_BYTES_ON with carry: MMU 7's page on by one too.","comment":"Carry: MMU 7 too"},
        "9942": {"synopsis":"HL has reached the end (B) of this part of a screen of one byte a pixel: in Layer 2 (C bit\n7) HL back by $2000 and the next page into MMU 6 (MMU 7's too with carry); in LoRes HL moved\nto the lower half ($C000 up) and B = $D8.","comment":"Layer 2?"},
        "9946": {"comment":"HL back to $C000 up"},
        "9948": {"comment":"MMU 6's page"},
        "9950": {"synopsis":"The page in MMU slot A's NextReg one on.","comment":"Kept"},
        "9951": {"comment":"NextReg A selected"},
        "9956": {"comment":"Its page"},
        "9959": {"comment":"The next"},
        "9963": {"comment":"Only MMU 6?"},
        "9964": {"comment":"Then MMU 7's"},
        "9966": {"comment":"Carry clear: once"},
        "9969": {"synopsis":"LoRes: on to the lower half.","comment":"LoRes: on to the lower half"},
        "9973": {"comment":"B = its end"},
        "9976": {"synopsis":"E = A, a control code's parameter; then WCH_MODE.","comment":"E = the parameter"},
        "9977": {"synopsis":"The screen mode, from $5C7F bits 0-3 (the same values as a window's +$1E):\n0: A = 0, Z, NC (the standard ULA screen).\n1, 2: carry, A = 1 or 2 (one byte a pixel: 1 LoRes, 2 Layer 2).\n4-7: A = 0, Z (standard); 8-11: A = 1 (hi-res); 12-15: A = 2 (hi-colour); 3: A = $FF.\nCallers that then DEC A have Z for hi-res.\nChanges: F.","comment":"The screen mode"},
        "9980": {"comment":"Bits 0-3"},
        "9982": {"comment":"0: standard"},
        "9983": {"comment":"1 or 2?"},
        "9985": {"comment":"Carry: one byte a pixel"},
        "9986": {"comment":"Bits 3-2"},
        "9990": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "9992": {"synopsis":"Gives window code its working memory: MMU 6 and 7 get 8K pages $0B and $10 (the window data\nat $C000-$FFFF), and SP moves to the alternate stack when it is at $5C00 or above.\n1. The return address is taken off the stack (BC), so it survives the stack switch.\n2. SP at or above $5C00: SP and the word at $5B6A are exchanged; $5B8E = the old SP's high\n   byte, which tells WIN_STACK_BACK to switch back.\n3. MMU_MAP_WIN pages $0B/$10 in; the old pages go to $5B8A (MMU 6) and $5B8B (MMU 7).\nExit: HL = the old pages.\nChanges: A, BC, D, HL; $5B8A, $5B8E, $5B6A.","comment":"First slot: NextReg $56 (MMU 6)"},
        "9994": {"synopsis":"WIN_MAP_IN for a pair of MMU slots chosen by the caller:\nEntry: D = the first slot's NextReg ($54 maps the pages at $8000-$BFFF instead).","comment":"BC = the return address"},
        "9995": {"comment":"HL = SP"},
        "9999": {"comment":"SP at $5C00 or above?"},
        "10004": {"comment":"Yes: the alternate stack from $5B6A, SP kept there"},
        "10012": {"synopsis":"The stack is settled: $5B8E = the high byte of SP at entry, then the pages are mapped.","comment":"Kept: the old SP's high byte"},
        "10015": {"comment":"The return address back on the (new) stack"},
        "10016": {"comment":"Pages $0B/$10 in, the old ones in HL"},
        "10019": {"comment":"Kept for WIN_MAP_OUT"},
        "10023": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_STRING with E = $80: prints the string at HL whose last character has bit 7 set.","comment":"Terminator: bit 7"},
        "10027": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_STRING with E = $FF: prints the $FF-ended string at HL. The Browser prints all\nits screen texts this way (IX = its window).","comment":"Terminator: $FF"},
        "10029": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_STRING ($01C6, as documented): prints a string to the window at IX.\nEntry: HL = the string; E = $FF (ended by $FF), $80 (last character has bit 7 set) or less\nthan $80 (E characters, or fewer if a $FF comes first); IX = the window.\n1. HL is kept at $5B8F; WIN_MAP_IN pages the window data in, WIN_CHECK_MODE checks the\n   window belongs to the current mode.\n2. D = the count (E < $80) or $FF; each character goes to the window's printer at $1D40\n   until the count runs out, a byte >= the terminator ($FF) is met, or a bit-7 byte (E =\n   $80) has been printed without its bit 7.\n3. Out through WIN_MAP_OUT.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; $5B8F.","comment":"The string's address"},
        "10032": {"comment":"Window data in"},
        "10035": {"comment":"The window must be the current mode's"},
        "10041": {"comment":"D = $FF: no count"},
        "10043": {"comment":"E < $80?"},
        "10047": {"comment":"Yes: D = the count, E = $FF the terminator"},
        "10050": {"synopsis":"One character of the string.","comment":"The next character"},
        "10052": {"comment":"At or past the terminator?"},
        "10055": {"comment":"Yes: this one is the last"},
        "10057": {"comment":"$FF ends the string unprinted"},
        "10060": {"comment":"Bit 7 off the last character"},
        "10062": {"synopsis":"Print the character (E) through the window printer at $1D40."},
        "10064": {"comment":"E = the character for the printer"},
        "10065": {"comment":"Print it in the window"},
        "10070": {"comment":"Count down (D = $FF never runs out)"},
        "10075": {"synopsis":"Prints the character A in the window at IX: pages in, checks the mode, prints through $1D40\nand pages out. Window control codes go this way one byte at a time (AT row, column ...).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"E = the character"},
        "10076": {"comment":"Window data in"},
        "10079": {"comment":"The window must be the current mode's"},
        "10082": {"comment":"Print E in the window"},
        "10087": {"synopsis":"WIN_PRINT_A without the mode check, entering the window printer at $1D47 (past its bit 5\ntest of IX+$19).","comment":"E = the character"},
        "10091": {"comment":"Print it, past the window printer's first test"},
        "10094": {"synopsis":"Undoes WIN_MAP_IN: MMU 6 and 7 back to the pages saved at $5B8A, then WIN_STACK_BACK.","comment":"The pages saved by WIN_MAP_IN"},
        "10097": {"comment":"MMU 6 back"},
        "10101": {"comment":"MMU 7 back"},
        "10105": {"synopsis":"Back to the caller's stack when WIN_MAP_IN switched it ($5B8E >= $5C): SP and $5B6A\nexchanged again.","comment":"The stack switched in WIN_MAP_IN?"},
        "10111": {"comment":"Yes: back to the caller's stack"},
        "10120": {"synopsis":"Prints the BC bytes at DE in the window at IX, one by one through WIN_PRINT_A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC bytes left?"},
        "10123": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "10126": {"comment":"Print it"},
        "10131": {"comment":"On to the next"},
        "10135": {"synopsis":"Leaves window code: MMU 6/7 restored from $5B8A (MMU67_RESTORE's way) and the stack switched\nback.","comment":"First slot: MMU 6"},
        "10137": {"synopsis":"WIN_LEAVE with D = the first MMU slot chosen by the caller.","comment":"Pages back from $5B8A"},
        "10140": {"comment":"Stack back"},
        "10142": {"synopsis":"Checks that the window at IX belongs to the current mode: the low nibble of $5C7F against\nIX+$1E. Equal, or differing by XOR 5, passes; otherwise error $5E is reported through ROM 1\n(stack and bank 0 restored first by RST $30).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The current mode (low nibble of $5C7F)"},
        "10147": {"comment":"The window's mode?"},
        "10151": {"comment":"Differing by XOR 5 is allowed too"},
        "10157": {"comment":"Error $5E"},
        "10159": {"synopsis":"Reports error A from window code: RST $30 first (SP from $5B6A, RAM bank 0 at $C000), then\nROM 1's $0DA5. Does not return.","comment":"SP from $5B6A, RAM bank 0 at $C000"},
        "10160": {"synopsis":"Reports error A through ROM 1's $0DA5 (its error entry, just past its RST $08 at $0DA3, with\nthe code in A). Does not return.","comment":"ROM 1's error entry, A = the code"},
        "10163": {"synopsis":"MMU 6 and 7 back to the pages saved at $5B8A (window data paged out).\nExit: HL = the pages they held.\nChanges: A, D, HL.","comment":"First slot: MMU 6"},
        "10165": {"synopsis":"Puts the pages saved at $5B8A into MMU slot D and D+1.","comment":"The saved pages"},
        "10170": {"synopsis":"Puts 8K pages $0B and $10 into MMU slot D and D+1 (the window data).\nExit: HL = the pages they held.","comment":"Pages $0B (MMU 6) and $10 (MMU 7)"},
        "10173": {"synopsis":"Exchanges two MMU slots' pages with L and H through ports $243B/$253B: NextReg D gets L,\nNextReg D+1 gets H.\nExit: L, H = the pages they held; D = the second NextReg.\nChanges: A, D, HL."},
        "10174": {"comment":"Select NextReg D"},
        "10179": {"comment":"Read its page, then write L"},
        "10184": {"comment":"L = the old page"},
        "10185": {"comment":"Select NextReg D + 1"},
        "10190": {"comment":"Read its page, then write H"},
        "10194": {"comment":"H = the old page"},
        "10197": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_LINEIN ($01C3, as documented): line input in a window, with cursor movement and\nediting.\nEntry: HL = the buffer; A = its size, or 0 with C = the size and B = the flags; E = the\ncharacters already in it; D = the cursor (B bit 2); IX = the window (B bit 7: the current\nmode's full-screen window, IX = $F200 + $100 x mode, or 0 for mode 0, which prints through\nROM 3).\n1. FLAGX bit 7 set; the flags go into FLAGX (bit 0 -> bit 2: stop after a change, bit 1 ->\n   bit 3: stop on a key not in the table, bit 4 -> bit 4: rewind first) and TV_FLAG (bit 5\n   -> bit 1: codes $80 and above accepted, bit 6 -> bit 2: BREAK allowed).\n2. $5B9A = the cursor, $5B9B = the size, $5B9C = the length; the window data paged in, the\n   mode checked and IX+$1B zeroed.\n3. Rewind (FLAGX bit 4): the print position goes back over the text's width.\n4. The loop: the text before the cursor, the cursor, the rest, spaces over what the last\n   drawing left; then a key (with its click) is looked up in LINEIN_KEYS. Keys from $20 are\n   inserted; a failed edit or a full buffer rasps.\n5. At the end: E = the length, D = the cursor, B = FLAGX bits 2-3 (bit 0: stopped after a\n   change, bit 1: stopped on key C), C = the key that ended it ($0D for ENTER); IX+$1B is\n   set from the window's fields $18, $1A and $22.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX; FLAGX, TV_FLAG bits 1-2.","comment":"FLAGX bit 7 set"},
        "10201": {"comment":"A = 0: the flags in B, the size in C"},
        "10204": {"comment":"Otherwise C = the size A, no flags"},
        "10207": {"synopsis":"B bit 7: IX = the current mode's full-screen window.","comment":"Use the current mode's full-screen window?"},
        "10211": {"comment":"IX = 0: no window (mode 0)"},
        "10215": {"comment":"The current mode"},
        "10222": {"comment":"IX = $F200 + $100 x mode"},
        "10226": {"synopsis":"Size 0: nothing to do.","comment":"Size 0?"},
        "10229": {"comment":"A = the length"},
        "10230": {"comment":"Starting cursor given in D?"},
        "10235": {"synopsis":"$5B9A = the starting cursor; the flags into FLAGX and TV_FLAG.","comment":"The cursor"},
        "10238": {"comment":"The buffer"},
        "10241": {"comment":"FLAGX: bits 2, 3 and 4 cleared"},
        "10248": {"comment":"B bit 4 (rewind) to FLAGX bit 4"},
        "10253": {"comment":"B bits 0-1 to FLAGX bits 2-3"},
        "10254": {"comment":"Bits 0-1 up to bits 2-3"},
        "10258": {"comment":"Into FLAGX"},
        "10260": {"comment":"B bits 5-6 to TV_FLAG bits 1-2"},
        "10261": {"comment":"Bits 5-6 to bits 1-2"},
        "10266": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bits 1-2 replaced"},
        "10274": {"comment":"B = the length given"},
        "10275": {"comment":"More than the size?"},
        "10279": {"comment":"Then the size"},
        "10280": {"synopsis":"$5B9B = the size, $5B9C = the length; then the window data paged in.","comment":"Size and length kept"},
        "10284": {"comment":"Window data in"},
        "10287": {"comment":"A window?"},
        "10291": {"comment":"Then it must be the current mode's"},
        "10294": {"comment":"IX+$1B = 0"},
        "10298": {"comment":"D = the cursor"},
        "10302": {"comment":"Rewind asked for? (FLAGX bit 4, cleared)"},
        "10309": {"comment":"C = size, B = length; HL = the buffer"},
        "10318": {"comment":"Yes: E = the text's width"},
        "10321": {"comment":"and the print position back over it"},
        "10324": {"synopsis":"Ready to draw: $5B9B = $0D, the key returned when ENTER ends the input.","comment":"ENTER's code, returned in C at the end"},
        "10329": {"comment":"An empty buffer?"},
        "10333": {"comment":"FLAGX bits 6-7 both clear? (bit 7 was set above)"},
        "10340": {"comment":"Then two quotes, the cursor between them"},
        "10342": {"comment":"and a second one"},
        "10346": {"comment":"The cursor after the first"},
        "10347": {"comment":"Length 2"},
        "10349": {"synopsis":"Nothing drawn yet: width 0 on the stack.","comment":"Width of the last drawing: none"},
        "10351": {"synopsis":"Draws the line: the text before the cursor, the cursor, the rest (E = the width printed),\nspaces over the end of the last drawing; then the print position back to the cursor.","comment":"From the start of the buffer"},
        "10354": {"comment":"E counts the columns printed"},
        "10356": {"comment":"The text before the cursor"},
        "10360": {"comment":"Input over? Then no cursor"},
        "10367": {"comment":"The rest of the text"},
        "10372": {"comment":"Less printed than last time?"},
        "10374": {"comment":"Then spaces over the rest"},
        "10377": {"comment":"Input over?"},
        "10383": {"comment":"Wait for a key (with its click)"},
        "10390": {"comment":"Look it up in the key table"},
        "10396": {"comment":"Handled: rasp if it failed, then draw"},
        "10398": {"comment":"A key from $20: insert it"},
        "10402": {"comment":"Another control key: may it end the input?"},
        "10409": {"comment":"Yes: it is returned in C"},
        "10412": {"comment":"Input over, not by a change"},
        "10416": {"synopsis":"No carry (the edit failed): the rasp. Then back over the line and draw again.","comment":"Rasp if the edit failed"},
        "10423": {"synopsis":"Back over the E columns just printed, then draw again.","comment":"Back over the E columns printed"},
        "10428": {"comment":"Draw again"},
        "10430": {"synopsis":"Input over: the exit registers are set and the window data paged out.","comment":"E = the length"},
        "10431": {"comment":"IX+$1B = IX+$1A + 1 - (IX+$18 - IX+$22) / 8"},
        "10434": {"comment":"Minus IX+$22"},
        "10437": {"comment":"Divided by 8"},
        "10444": {"comment":"IX+$1A minus that, plus 1"},
        "10449": {"comment":"Into IX+$1B"},
        "10452": {"comment":"B = FLAGX bits 2-3: why the input ended"},
        "10460": {"comment":"C = the key that ended it"},
        "10464": {"comment":"Window data out"},
        "10471": {"comment":"Stack back and return"},
        "10474": {"synopsis":"A key from $20: SPACE with CAPS SHIFT down may be BREAK; codes from $80 need TV_FLAG bit 1;\nthen the key goes in at the cursor if the buffer has room.","comment":"SPACE?"},
        "10479": {"comment":"Is CAPS SHIFT down? (port $FEFE)"},
        "10484": {"comment":"Yes: perhaps BREAK"},
        "10487": {"synopsis":"H = the key; codes from $80 only when allowed.","comment":"H = the key"},
        "10489": {"comment":"A code from $80?"},
        "10493": {"comment":"Only when tokens/graphics are allowed"},
        "10499": {"synopsis":"Room for one more? Then the tail moves up one byte and the key goes in.","comment":"Buffer full?"},
        "10503": {"comment":"Key kept (in H)"},
        "10504": {"comment":"HL = the cursor's place in the buffer"},
        "10510": {"comment":"Length and cursor one more"},
        "10512": {"comment":"Bytes from the cursor to the end of the buffer"},
        "10516": {"comment":"Move them up one byte"},
        "10519": {"comment":"BC = how many"},
        "10522": {"comment":"HL = one past them"},
        "10525": {"comment":"Last byte to move"},
        "10526": {"comment":"Each one byte up"},
        "10529": {"synopsis":"Tail moved: the key into the gap."},
        "10531": {"synopsis":"The key into the buffer at the cursor; a change may end the input.","comment":"A = the key"},
        "10532": {"comment":"Into the gap"},
        "10533": {"comment":"A change may end the input"},
        "10536": {"comment":"Draw again"},
        "10538": {"synopsis":"SPACE with CAPS SHIFT down and BREAK allowed (TV_FLAG bit 2): ROM 1's $3E75 decides (NZ:\ncarry on); otherwise the window data is paged out, the stack switched back, and ROM 1's\n$001E stops the program.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"BREAK allowed?"},
        "10543": {"comment":"ROM 1 decides; NZ: carry on"},
        "10547": {"comment":"Window data out"},
        "10550": {"comment":"Back to the caller's stack"},
        "10558": {"comment":"ROM 1's $001E stops the program"},
        "10561": {"synopsis":"Key table of IDE_WINDOW_LINEIN, read by the table dispatcher at $15A1: 17 entries of a key\ncode and a handler address, ended by $FF at $2974. Each handler works on B = the length, D =\nthe cursor, C = the size; carry = done, no carry = rasp.\n$00 cursor to end, $03 delete to start, $04 word left, $05 word right, $07 clear line, $08\nleft, $09 right, $0A down a line, $0B up a line, $0C delete left, $0D ENTER, $10 delete to\nend, $11 alternate ROM's $13A0, $18 delete right, $1B delete word left, $1C delete word\nright, $1D cursor to start."},
        "10613": {"synopsis":"Key $07: the line emptied, length and cursor 0.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Length 0, cursor 0"},
        "10616": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10618": {"synopsis":"Key $08: cursor one left.\nExit: carry, or no carry (cursor unchanged) at the start.","comment":"Cursor one left"},
        "10619": {"comment":"Still 0 or more? Done"},
        "10621": {"comment":"No: back to 0, failed"},
        "10624": {"synopsis":"Key $09: cursor one right.\nExit: carry, or no carry (Z) at the end.","comment":"Cursor at the end?"},
        "10627": {"comment":"No: one right"},
        "10630": {"synopsis":"Key $0B: cursor back by the window's width (the start if that is before it). The width is\nfrom $16AE: 32 with no window, else IX+$1C, halved when IX+$25 bit 4 is set.","comment":"One left first"},
        "10634": {"comment":"A = the width"},
        "10637": {"comment":"Minus the old cursor"},
        "10640": {"comment":"Past the start: cursor 0"},
        "10644": {"comment":"Otherwise cursor back a whole line"},
        "10646": {"synopsis":"Key $0A: cursor on by the window's width (the end if that is past it).","comment":"One right first"},
        "10650": {"comment":"A = the width"},
        "10653": {"comment":"Plus the old cursor"},
        "10655": {"comment":"Past the end: cursor at the end"},
        "10659": {"comment":"Otherwise cursor on a whole line"},
        "10662": {"synopsis":"Key $00: cursor to the end. No carry if it is there already.","comment":"Already at the end?"},
        "10665": {"comment":"Cursor to the end"},
        "10668": {"synopsis":"Key $1D: cursor to the start. No carry if it is there already.","comment":"Already at the start?"},
        "10671": {"comment":"Cursor to the start"},
        "10675": {"synopsis":"Key $18: deletes the character under the cursor (one right, then LINEIN_DEL_LEFT).","comment":"At the end: nothing under the cursor"},
        "10678": {"comment":"One right, then delete left"},
        "10679": {"synopsis":"Key $0C: deletes the character left of the cursor: the bytes from the cursor move down one\n(B of them: the old length), B and D one less; a change may end the input.\nExit: carry; no carry with the cursor at the start.","comment":"At the start?"},
        "10684": {"comment":"HL = the cursor's place"},
        "10689": {"comment":"DE = one before it"},
        "10692": {"comment":"Text after the cursor?"},
        "10696": {"comment":"Move the bytes down one"},
        "10701": {"synopsis":"Moved: length and cursor one less."},
        "10703": {"comment":"Length and cursor one less"},
        "10705": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10706": {"synopsis":"After a change: with FLAGX bit 2 (stop after any change) FLAGX bit 4 is set (input over) and\nbit 3 cleared. Keeps the carry.","comment":"Stop after a change?"},
        "10712": {"synopsis":"Input over: FLAGX bit 4 set, bit 3 (stopped on a key) cleared.","comment":"Input over"},
        "10714": {"comment":"Not by a key"},
        "10717": {"synopsis":"Key $0D (ENTER): input over, FLAGX bit 2 cleared (not a change).\nExit: carry.","comment":"Not by a change"},
        "10722": {"comment":"Done; input over"},
        "10725": {"synopsis":"A = the character left of the cursor.\nExit: Z if it is a space.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"The buffer"},
        "10728": {"comment":"Plus the cursor, minus one"},
        "10732": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "10736": {"synopsis":"A = the character at the cursor.\nExit: Z if it is a space.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"The buffer"},
        "10739": {"comment":"Plus the cursor"},
        "10742": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "10746": {"synopsis":"Key $04: cursor left over spaces, then over the word before them, to its first character.","comment":"At the start?"},
        "10749": {"synopsis":"Over the spaces left of the cursor.","comment":"Space left of the cursor?"},
        "10754": {"comment":"Yes: one left, while possible"},
        "10759": {"comment":"Done"},
        "10761": {"synopsis":"Over the word: until a space is left of the cursor.","comment":"Space left of the cursor? Then done"},
        "10766": {"comment":"No: one left, while possible"},
        "10773": {"synopsis":"Key $05: cursor right over the word under it, then over the spaces after it.","comment":"At the end?"},
        "10776": {"synopsis":"Over the word: until a space is under the cursor.","comment":"Space under the cursor?"},
        "10781": {"comment":"No: one right, while possible"},
        "10788": {"synopsis":"Over the spaces: until a character that is not a space.","comment":"Not a space under the cursor? Then done"},
        "10793": {"comment":"A space: one right, while possible"},
        "10800": {"synopsis":"Key $1B: deletes left of the cursor: the spaces, then the word before them.","comment":"At the start?"},
        "10803": {"synopsis":"Deleting the spaces.","comment":"Space left of the cursor?"},
        "10808": {"comment":"Yes: delete it, while possible"},
        "10815": {"synopsis":"Deleting the word.","comment":"Space left of the cursor? Then done"},
        "10820": {"comment":"No: delete it, while possible"},
        "10827": {"synopsis":"Key $1C: deletes the word under the cursor, then the spaces after it.","comment":"At the end?"},
        "10830": {"synopsis":"Deleting the word.","comment":"Space under the cursor?"},
        "10835": {"comment":"No: delete it, while possible"},
        "10842": {"synopsis":"Deleting the spaces.","comment":"Not a space under the cursor? Then done"},
        "10847": {"comment":"A space: delete it, while possible"},
        "10854": {"synopsis":"Key $03: deletes everything left of the cursor, one character at a time.","comment":"Delete left"},
        "10857": {"comment":"Until nothing is left of the cursor"},
        "10861": {"synopsis":"Key $10: deletes from the cursor to the end (length = cursor).\nExit: carry.","comment":"Length = the cursor"},
        "10864": {"synopsis":"Key $11: handled by the alternate ROM's $13A0.","comment":"To the alternate ROM"},
        "10870": {"synopsis":"Prints A spaces over what the last drawing left past the new end, then moves back over them.\nEntry: A = the count, Z when it is 0 (nothing done).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"No extra columns: nothing to do"},
        "10872": {"comment":"E = the count"},
        "10874": {"comment":"Spaces"},
        "10880": {"comment":"Then back over them"},
        "10885": {"synopsis":"Moves the print position back E columns: E x code 8 (through ROM 3) with no window; in a\nwindow E x code $0C with IX+$28 = $FF meanwhile. Nothing for E = 0.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"E = 0?"},
        "10888": {"comment":"A window?"},
        "10892": {"comment":"No window: code 8 (left), E times"},
        "10896": {"comment":"Window: code $0C as a backspace, E times"},
        "10905": {"comment":"IX+$28 back to 0"},
        "10910": {"synopsis":"Prints the character A, E times (tokens expanded).\nChanges: E = 0, F.","comment":"Print A (a token as its keyword)"},
        "10917": {"comment":"E times"},
        "10921": {"synopsis":"Prints the cursor: one of four 8-byte pictures from $0E07 (mode 0, a block on the bottom 3\nrows), $0E0F (mode 1, stripes), $0E17 (mode 2, a vertical bar), $0E1F (caps lock in mode 0,\na block on the top 3 rows) is copied to $5B9D, UDG is pointed there and code $90 printed;\nthen UDG is restored ($0E58 swaps it).\nExit: E one more. Keeps BC, DE (but E), HL."},
        "10924": {"comment":"A = the cursor kind (0-3)"},
        "10927": {"comment":"As a code from $92"},
        "10930": {"comment":"Picture 2 + kind: offset x 8"},
        "10935": {"comment":"From the 8-byte pictures at $0DF7"},
        "10944": {"comment":"Copied to $5B9D"},
        "10951": {"comment":"UDG = $5B9D; HL = the old UDG"},
        "10955": {"comment":"Code $90: the first UDG, the cursor picture"},
        "10960": {"comment":"UDG back"},
        "10967": {"comment":"The cursor took one column"},
        "10969": {"synopsis":"A = the cursor kind: MODE's bits 0-1 when not 0; otherwise 3 with caps lock (FLAGS2 bit 3),\nelse 0.","comment":"MODE: E or G?"},
        "10975": {"comment":"Caps lock (FLAGS2 bit 3)?"},
        "10981": {"comment":"Kind 3"},
        "10984": {"synopsis":"A + $92: the cursor kind turned into a code from $92.","comment":"From kind to code"},
        "10987": {"synopsis":"Prints A characters from HL (tokens expanded), E counting the columns.\nExit: HL past them.\nChanges: AF, E, HL.","comment":"B = the count, plus one for DJNZ"},
        "10992": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "10994": {"comment":"Printed, counting its columns"},
        "10997": {"synopsis":"Until the count runs out."},
        "11001": {"synopsis":"E = the columns that the B characters at HL take when printed (tokens expanded). Keeps BC,\nHL.","comment":"Count from 0"},
        "11005": {"comment":"B plus one for DJNZ"},
        "11008": {"synopsis":"One character counted.","comment":"The next character"},
        "11010": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "11013": {"synopsis":"Until the count runs out."},
        "11018": {"synopsis":"Counts the character A in E: one per character, a keyword's length for a token.","comment":"The action: E + 1"},
        "11024": {"synopsis":"One column: E + 1."},
        "11026": {"synopsis":"Prints the character A, a keyword's text for a token, with E counting the columns.","comment":"The action: print it"},
        "11030": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at HL for the character A, or for each character of its keyword when A is\na token to expand (EXPAND_TEST). Keeps HL.","comment":"A token to expand?"},
        "11033": {"comment":"No: straight to the action"},
        "11035": {"comment":"Yes: the action for each keyword character"},
        "11036": {"comment":"BC = the action"},
        "11038": {"comment":"Each keyword character to it"},
        "11044": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine at HL with the caller's HL back from the stack.","comment":"HL back, the action's address on the stack"},
        "11046": {"synopsis":"Prints A, E one more: in a window through $16C0 (the window printer, registers kept); with\nno window by ROM 3's PRINT_A, with the window data paged out meanwhile and back in after\n($1942).","comment":"One more column"},
        "11047": {"comment":"A window?"},
        "11051": {"comment":"Yes: print in it, registers kept"},
        "11054": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "11057": {"comment":"No window: E = the character"},
        "11058": {"comment":"Window data out"},
        "11062": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: through the current channel"},
        "11063": {"comment":"Window data back in"},
        "11066": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "11070": {"synopsis":"Is A a token to print as a keyword? Codes below $A5 are not. With no window they are; in a\nwindow they are when the UDG picture for code A (UDG + 8 x (A - $90)) would lie past $FFFF,\notherwise they print as graphics.\nExit: carry = expand. Keeps the registers but F.","comment":"Below $A5: not a token (no carry)"},
        "11074": {"comment":"No window: expand (carry)"},
        "11079": {"comment":"Window: HL = UDG + 8 x (A - $90)"},
        "11081": {"comment":"HL = A"},
        "11084": {"comment":"Minus $90"},
        "11088": {"comment":"Times 8"},
        "11091": {"comment":"Plus UDG"},
        "11096": {"comment":"Carry: the picture would pass $FFFF"},
        "11099": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at BC for each character of keyword A (a token from $A5), from ROM 3's\nKEYWORD_TABLE found by its FIND_ENTRY and read byte by byte through ROM 3 ($007B: LD\nA,(HL)).\nA space comes first for keywords from the 33rd on, unless suppressed (IX+$25 bit 1 in a\nwindow, FLAGS bit 0 without); a space follows a keyword ending in a letter or $.\nChanges: AF, HL."},
        "11100": {"comment":"A = the keyword's number"},
        "11102": {"comment":"ROM 3's KEYWORD_TABLE"},
        "11105": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_ENTRY: DE = keyword A"},
        "11108": {"comment":"HL = the keyword"},
        "11110": {"comment":"One of the first 32: no leading space"},
        "11112": {"comment":"A window?"},
        "11118": {"comment":"Window: its leading-space flag"},
        "11124": {"synopsis":"No window: FLAGS bit 0 decides the leading space.","comment":"No window: FLAGS bit 0"},
        "11128": {"synopsis":"Leading space unless suppressed.","comment":"Not suppressed: a leading space"},
        "11131": {"synopsis":"One character of the keyword, read in ROM 3.","comment":"ROM 3 at $007B: LD A,(HL) in ROM 3"},
        "11134": {"comment":"Next byte"},
        "11135": {"synopsis":"The character (bit 7 off) to the routine; the last one decides the trailing space."},
        "11138": {"comment":"Bit 7 off"},
        "11140": {"comment":"To the action"},
        "11146": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry: not the last? Then on"},
        "11149": {"comment":"Last was '$'? Then a trailing space"},
        "11153": {"comment":"Below 'A'? No trailing space"},
        "11156": {"synopsis":"A space to the routine.","comment":"A space (bit 7 set: the last)"},
        "11160": {"synopsis":"Jumps to the routine at BC.","comment":"Jump to the action at BC"},
        "11162": {"synopsis":"Function 4 of the window channel (from $0443): WIN_FUNC_4_DO under the other register set.","comment":"Back to the caller's register set"},
        "11168": {"synopsis":"The window data paged in; then, in the other register set, B selects:\n0: A = IX+$21, HL = IX+$22 (high) and IX+$23 (low), then as below;\n1: D must be 0 (else $1B7E); IX+$2D = E, then $1AF9;\n2 and up: A = IX+$15 + 1, H = IX+$18, L = 0.\nThen (0 and 2 up): E = A - IX+$13; HL = E x IX+$1D + L; E = H - IX+$17.\nOut through WIN_MAP_OUT.","comment":"Window data in"},
        "11171": {"comment":"The other register set: B the function"},
        "11172": {"comment":"B = 0?"},
        "11175": {"comment":"Function 0: from IX+$21 to IX+$23"},
        "11186": {"synopsis":"B = 1: IX+$2D = E (D must be 0).","comment":"B = 1?"},
        "11188": {"comment":"D must be 0"},
        "11193": {"comment":"IX+$2D = E"},
        "11201": {"synopsis":"B from 2: from IX+$15 and IX+$18.","comment":"Functions from 2: IX+$15 + 1"},
        "11207": {"comment":"H = IX+$18"},
        "11210": {"synopsis":"HL = (A - IX+$13) x IX+$1D + L; E = H - IX+$17.","comment":"E = A - IX+$13"},
        "11214": {"comment":"Times IX+$1D"},
        "11219": {"comment":"A = H"},
        "11222": {"comment":"HL = the product + L"},
        "11224": {"comment":"E = H - IX+$17"},
        "11228": {"synopsis":"Back to the first register set and out.","comment":"Back; window data out"},
        "11232": {"synopsis":"Runs the system's own Browser (reached through the handler word at $08E1, and from\nBROWSER_RESUME for a '<' type).\n1. The marker word at $E3C7 in 8K page $10 is read (its low byte cleared): $5245, left by\n   BRW_CD_MARK when the Browser went into a directory to run something there, means going\n   back to the parent first (IDE_PATH change to \"..\").\n2. $0EDD, ROM 1's $14B9 and $1003 are called; $3B92 builds the filetype list at $F700 from\n   the text at $1483.\n3. IDE_BROWSER with HL = $F700, DE = the help text at $12E7, A = $FF (every capability and\n   the system's settings) and B = $0F (every extra capability).\n4. Ends at $11B8.","comment":"8K page $10 at $E000"},
        "11236": {"comment":"The marker word, low byte cleared"},
        "11244": {"comment":"Page $0F back"},
        "11248": {"comment":"$5245: a directory to leave first?"},
        "11256": {"comment":"Yes: IDE_PATH change to \"..\""},
        "11267": {"synopsis":"In the right directory: screen, filetypes, then the Browser.","comment":"Screen and settings set up"},
        "11276": {"comment":"The filetype list built at $F700"},
        "11279": {"comment":"Filetypes, help text $12E7"},
        "11285": {"comment":"Every capability; system settings"},
        "11287": {"comment":"Every extra capability"},
        "11289": {"comment":"Run the Browser"},
        "11292": {"synopsis":"Out through $11B8."},
        "11295": {"synopsis":"Carries on after the Browser has run a filetype's command (from $0E87), by the separator\nthat followed the type ($D5E9): ':' (or below) ends at $11B8; '<' restarts the system's\nBrowser (BROWSER_RESTART); ';' calls the alternate ROM's $02FC with A = 0 and enters\nIDE_BROWSER with the registers it returns.","comment":"The separator after the type that ran"},
        "11298": {"comment":"':' or below: end"},
        "11302": {"comment":"'<': the system Browser again"},
        "11304": {"comment":"';': the alternate ROM's $02FC first"},
        "11310": {"synopsis":"IDE_BROWSER ($01BA, as documented): the file browser.\nEntry: HL = the supported filetypes (entries of a length byte and \"TYPE:command\", ended by\n$FF); DE = the help text for the two bottom lines ($FF-ended), or 0 for the settings calls\n(BRW_SETTINGS); A = the capabilities mask; B = the extra capabilities (when A bit 6 is set).\n1. $D5D4 = A, $D5D5 = B (or 0), $D5CE = HL, $D5D0 = DE, $D5DC = 0.\n2. BRW_SAVE_SCREEN, BRW_SHOW (settings, screen, directory, selection), BRW_HELP.\n3. The key loop: SPACE must be up first; $34D1 shows the selection; a key (with its click)\n   is dispatched through the table at $3CFA, or $3D21 (fewer keys) when the directory is\n   empty; a failed key rasps. FLAGS2 bit 5 set by a handler redraws the help text.\nExit (by BRW_EXIT, SP back from $D5D6): carry; Z with HL = the short name (at $E090) and DE\n= the long name (at $DA31) after ENTER on a listed type; NZ after SPACE. A type with a\ncommand after its ':' runs the command instead (BRW_RUN_TYPE). Failure: no carry, A = the\nerror.","comment":"The capabilities kept"},
        "11311": {"comment":"DE = 0: the settings calls"},
        "11316": {"comment":"The capabilities back"},
        "11317": {"comment":"The capabilities mask"},
        "11320": {"comment":"Extra capabilities in B?"},
        "11325": {"synopsis":"$D5D5 = the extra capabilities (0 without A bit 6).","comment":"Kept (or 0)"},
        "11328": {"comment":"The filetypes"},
        "11331": {"comment":"The help text"},
        "11335": {"comment":"$D5DC = 0"},
        "11339": {"comment":"Save what the Browser changes"},
        "11342": {"comment":"Settings, screen, directory, selection"},
        "11345": {"synopsis":"The help text again, then the next key.","comment":"The help text"},
        "11348": {"synopsis":"Waits for SPACE to be up, then reads and dispatches one key.","comment":"SPACE still down? Wait"},
        "11355": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: no key waiting"},
        "11359": {"comment":"SP kept for BRW_EXIT"},
        "11363": {"comment":"The selection shown"},
        "11366": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 3 cleared"},
        "11370": {"comment":"Wait for a key (with its click)"},
        "11374": {"comment":"Entries in the directory?"},
        "11378": {"comment":"None: the shorter key table"},
        "11383": {"comment":"Some: the full key table"},
        "11386": {"synopsis":"Key A through the table at HL.","comment":"The key back"},
        "11387": {"comment":"Run the key's handler"},
        "11390": {"comment":"Redraw asked for: the help text again"},
        "11394": {"synopsis":"Dispatches key A through the key table at HL (by $15A1: entries of a key and a handler word,\n$FF-ended); no entry, or a handler returning no carry, gives the rasp. MODE = 0 after.\nExit: NZ if FLAGS2 bit 5 is set (the caller redraws).","comment":"Find and run the key's handler"},
        "11397": {"comment":"None, or it failed: the rasp"},
        "11400": {"comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "11404": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5: redraw?"},
        "11409": {"synopsis":"Sets the print position in the Browser's window ($F700): AT, row E, column D, through\nWIN_PRINT_A.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; IX = $F700.","comment":"The Browser's window"},
        "11413": {"comment":"AT"},
        "11420": {"comment":"Row E"},
        "11426": {"comment":"Column D"},
        "11430": {"synopsis":"Copies the $FF-ended text at HL, the $FF too, to $D827.\nExit: HL = $D827.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"BC = the source"},
        "11432": {"comment":"To $D827"},
        "11435": {"synopsis":"Copies the $FF-ended text at BC, the $FF too, to HL.\nExit: HL = where it went.\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "11436": {"synopsis":"One byte, until the $FF has been copied.","comment":"Copy a byte"},
        "11440": {"comment":"Until the $FF has been copied"},
        "11445": {"synopsis":"Reads the next part of a long directory: $D5E4 (the part number) one more, and the last\nentry of the full buffer ($D3C3, entry $F7) becomes the preloaded entry at $C738; then as\nBRW_READ_DIR.","comment":"The next part of the directory"},
        "11449": {"comment":"Its last entry becomes the preloaded one"},
        "11452": {"comment":"To the preloaded entry"},
        "11456": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "11461": {"comment":"Then read"},
        "11463": {"synopsis":"Reads the directory into the catalog buffer at $C738 (13-byte entries, up to $F7 of them).\n1. $D5EA bit 3 cleared (sort again), $D5E4 = 0 (first part), $D5E1 = view flag bit 6\n   (directories first); the preloaded entry zeroed.\n2. \"Processing...\" is shown ($1526).\n3. Directories first: DOS_CATALOG of \"*.*\" (directories only, the second catalog handle,\n   kept at $D5DF); the last one is set aside at $C738 so the files go after them.\n4. DOS_CATALOG of the filter from the settings (files only when directories went first;\n   handle kept at $D5DD); the set-aside entry is put back.\n5. $D5E2 = the number of entries; $D5EA bit 3 set (the next part needs no new sort).","comment":"Sort again"},
        "11468": {"synopsis":"BRW_READ_DIR keeping $D5EA bit 3 (the sorted result is reused).","comment":"Part 0"},
        "11472": {"comment":"Directories first? (view flag bit 6)"},
        "11480": {"comment":"Preloaded entry zeroed"},
        "11484": {"synopsis":"\"Processing...\" shown; then the catalog calls.","comment":"\"Processing...\""},
        "11491": {"comment":"No entries yet"},
        "11493": {"comment":"Directories first?"},
        "11499": {"comment":"File name \"*.*\" (from $000B)"},
        "11505": {"comment":"Directories only, second handle"},
        "11511": {"comment":"The directories' handle"},
        "11514": {"comment":"None found?"},
        "11517": {"comment":"The count instead of 0"},
        "11518": {"comment":"Buffer full?"},
        "11522": {"comment":"The last one set aside: files start there"},
        "11526": {"comment":"Directories done"},
        "11530": {"synopsis":"The files' catalog, with the filter from the settings as the file name.","comment":"The filter from the settings to $D827"},
        "11536": {"comment":"B = the entries so far"},
        "11538": {"comment":"Files only when directories went first"},
        "11547": {"comment":"Catalog the files"},
        "11550": {"comment":"The files' handle"},
        "11555": {"comment":"A = all the entries"},
        "11557": {"comment":"The set-aside entry back"},
        "11561": {"synopsis":"$D5EA bit 3 set; $D5E2 = the number of entries.","comment":"The next call needs no new sort"},
        "11564": {"comment":"Bit 3"},
        "11566": {"comment":"The count"},
        "11570": {"synopsis":"Zeroes the 13-byte preloaded entry at $C738.\nExit: DE = $C738.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"The preloaded entry"},
        "11574": {"comment":"13 zero bytes"},
        "11577": {"synopsis":"Zeroes B bytes from DE."},
        "11581": {"comment":"DE = $C738"},
        "11583": {"synopsis":"Exchanges the 13-byte entry at DE with the one at $C738. Keeps DE.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"Swap 13 bytes with $C738"},
        "11589": {"synopsis":"One byte each way."},
        "11590": {"comment":"Exchange one byte"},
        "11594": {"comment":"Next"},
        "11600": {"synopsis":"One DOS_CATALOG call for the Browser.\nEntry: B = the entries already in the buffer; C = the filter bits (bit 7: the second handle\nand no files; bit 6: no directories); DE = the buffer's first entry (preloaded).\n1. B = $F8 - B, the room left. $D5EA bit 3 (already sorted) sets C bit 4.\n2. The sort/filter mode in A: C bits 7-6, system files left out unless the view shows them\n   ($D5EA bit 4), \".\" and \"..\" left out when $D5EA bit 5 is set, the sort mode from\n   BRW_SORT_MODE, sorting on (bit 3) unless the mode is 1 (unsorted). C bit 6 cleared.\n3. DOS_CATALOG with HL = $D827 (the file name).\nExit: A = the entries returned (0 on failure); DE = the last of them; HL = the directory\nhandle. $D5E3 = 0.","comment":"B = the room left in entries"},
        "11604": {"comment":"Sorted already? Then suppress a new sort"},
        "11613": {"synopsis":"A bits 4-5 from the view flags: system files, \".\" and \"..\".","comment":"Bit 4: hide system files unless shown"},
        "11618": {"comment":"C bits 7-6: no files / no directories"},
        "11623": {"comment":"The sort mode, bits 0-2"},
        "11626": {"comment":"A = the sort mode"},
        "11632": {"comment":"Bits 0-2 into H"},
        "11636": {"comment":"Mode 1 (unsorted)?"},
        "11642": {"comment":"Otherwise sorting on"},
        "11644": {"synopsis":"DOS_CATALOG with the mode in A.","comment":"A = the sort/filter mode"},
        "11645": {"comment":"C bit 6 is reserved"},
        "11647": {"comment":"The file name"},
        "11650": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_CATALOG"},
        "11653": {"comment":"A = 0 if it failed"},
        "11660": {"comment":"A = the entries returned"},
        "11662": {"synopsis":"DE = $C738 + 13 x A: the last entry returned."},
        "11663": {"comment":"DE = $C738 + 13 x A"},
        "11664": {"comment":"13 bytes an entry"},
        "11668": {"comment":"From the buffer's start"},
        "11674": {"comment":"The first match"},
        "11676": {"synopsis":"Finds the filetype entry for a catalog entry.\nEntry: HL = the entry's 8th byte (its type follows); C = which match is wanted (1 = the\nfirst).\n1. Type LNK: exit with carry and Z.\n2. The filetypes at $D5CE are searched (TYPE_MATCH; the separator after the matching types\n   must be ':', ';' or '<'); the C-th match wins: $D5E9 = its separator, $D5B8 = $FE.\n3. No match and no type (a space): the file is opened and its +3DOS header read (DOS_OPEN,\n   DOS_REF_HEAD, DOS_CLOSE): a program is looked up as BAS, a 6912-byte CODE file as SCR.\nExit: carry and NZ: HL = the command after the separator, A = its length (0: none); no\ncarry: not a listed type.","comment":"Start counting at 0"},
        "11678": {"synopsis":"BRW_FIND_TYPE with B set by the caller: B = 1 stops after the LNK test (no carry, Z, when\nnot LNK)."},
        "11680": {"comment":"Type LNK?"},
        "11688": {"comment":"LNK: carry and Z"},
        "11690": {"comment":"B = 1 stops here"},
        "11691": {"comment":"B one less"},
        "11693": {"comment":"DE = the type"},
        "11695": {"comment":"The filetype list"},
        "11698": {"synopsis":"The next filetype entry: its length (0 skipped, $FF the end).","comment":"Entry length"},
        "11700": {"comment":"$FF: the end"},
        "11703": {"comment":"0: skip"},
        "11706": {"comment":"Keep the type, the entry, its length"},
        "11709": {"comment":"Does the type list match?"},
        "11714": {"comment":"A separator after it?"},
        "11718": {"comment":"No: next entry"},
        "11720": {"comment":"The C-th match?"},
        "11723": {"comment":"B = the entry's length"},
        "11725": {"synopsis":"Matched: on to the separator after the type list.","comment":"On to the separator"},
        "11728": {"comment":"Separator?"},
        "11733": {"comment":"$D5E9 = the separator"},
        "11736": {"comment":"NZ; A = the command's length"},
        "11741": {"synopsis":"No match: past this entry.","comment":"Past this entry"},
        "11743": {"comment":"HL past the entry"},
        "11748": {"synopsis":"No filetype matched: only a file without a type is looked at further.","comment":"No type (a space)?"},
        "11753": {"synopsis":"Not a listed type: no carry.","comment":"Not listed: no carry"},
        "11755": {"synopsis":"No type: the file's header decides.","comment":"Back to the name"},
        "11761": {"comment":"The name built at $D827"},
        "11769": {"comment":"File 0, mode 1, open an existing one"},
        "11774": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_OPEN"},
        "11778": {"comment":"Opened"},
        "11782": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_REF_HEAD, IX = the header"},
        "11788": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_CLOSE"},
        "11793": {"comment":"HL = the header"},
        "11797": {"comment":"A = the type, DE = the length"},
        "11802": {"comment":"A program?"},
        "11803": {"comment":"Then look it up as BAS"},
        "11806": {"synopsis":"Looked up again as the type after HL.","comment":"As BAS or SCR"},
        "11809": {"comment":"CODE?"},
        "11813": {"comment":"6912 bytes?"},
        "11820": {"comment":"Then look it up as SCR"},
        "11825": {"synopsis":"Matches a file's 3-character type with a filetype entry's type list.\nEntry: DE = the file's type (bit 7 ignored, space-filled); HL = the list: types separated by\n',' and ended by a separator, where '?' matches any character and '*' all the rest, and a\ncapital in the file's type also matches a small letter.\nExit: Z = a match, HL at the separator; NZ = none. Keeps DE.","comment":"Three characters"},
        "11828": {"synopsis":"One character of the type.","comment":"'*' matches the rest"},
        "11831": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11834": {"comment":"Back on the pattern"},
        "11835": {"comment":"The file's character"},
        "11839": {"comment":"The file's type shorter?"},
        "11843": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "11844": {"comment":"Yes: next"},
        "11846": {"comment":"A capital: as a small letter"},
        "11848": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "11850": {"comment":"Above 'Z'?"},
        "11854": {"comment":"Small letter"},
        "11856": {"comment":"The same now?"},
        "11859": {"synopsis":"'?' matches anything.","comment":"'?' matches anything"},
        "11862": {"comment":"Neither: this type fails"},
        "11864": {"synopsis":"This character matched.","comment":"Next character"},
        "11867": {"synopsis":"All matched: on past the rest of the list (from a ',') to the separator."},
        "11868": {"comment":"More types after a ','?"},
        "11873": {"synopsis":"Skipping the other types in the list.","comment":"Skip to the separator"},
        "11875": {"comment":"A separator: matched (Z)"},
        "11879": {"comment":"The end without one: no match"},
        "11884": {"synopsis":"No match: NZ.","comment":"NZ"},
        "11887": {"synopsis":"The file's type ended: the pattern must end here too.","comment":"The pattern ends here too?"},
        "11892": {"comment":"A separator: matched"},
        "11897": {"synopsis":"This type failed: the next one after a ',', else no match.","comment":"This type failed"},
        "11898": {"synopsis":"Looking for the next ',' or the end of the list.","comment":"A ',': try the next type"},
        "11901": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11904": {"comment":"Separator or end: no match"},
        "11909": {"comment":"The end: no match"},
        "11914": {"comment":"Keep looking"},
        "11916": {"synopsis":"Z if A is a filetype separator: ':', ';' or '<'.\nChanges: F.","comment":"':'?"},
        "11919": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "11922": {"comment":"'<'?"},
        "11925": {"synopsis":"Z if A ends a line of text: $FF, $0D or $0A.\nChanges: F.","comment":"$FF?"},
        "11928": {"synopsis":"Z if A is $0D or $0A.\nChanges: F.","comment":"CR?"},
        "11931": {"comment":"LF?"},
        "11934": {"synopsis":"Key $0E: the extended menu, when the extra capabilities allow it (bit 2).\n1. $D5D8 = SP; the file named at $1490 (enBrowsext.cfg) is loaded to $C000 by $3BB7.\n2. A page of up to 8 items is built: each line of the file gives an item (AT its row and\n   column, 4 to a row, 13 characters wide) at $E090, its first capital shown inverse and\n   taken, made small, as its key. The text ends at ':'; then optional conditions, 'f' (files\n   only), 'd' (directories only), '.' and a type list for the selected entry; then ':' and\n   the item's command. Lines without them, or whose conditions fail, give no item.\n3. The key table at $D827 starts with SPACE (close) and $0E (the next page); each item adds\n   its key and handler BRW_MENU_ITEM, with the command's address kept $100 bytes higher.\n4. The menu is printed and keys dispatched until a handler ends it.","comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "11938": {"comment":"The extended menu allowed?"},
        "11945": {"comment":"SP kept for closing the menu"},
        "11949": {"comment":"Load enBrowsext.cfg to $C000"},
        "11955": {"synopsis":"Builds a menu page from the text at HL."},
        "11956": {"comment":"Key table: SPACE and $0E first"},
        "11968": {"comment":"The key table's next free place"},
        "11969": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "11970": {"comment":"The menu's text"},
        "11973": {"comment":"No items yet"},
        "11975": {"synopsis":"The next line: an item, at AT row 22 + C/4, column 13 x (C AND 3).","comment":"IX = this item's start"},
        "11978": {"comment":"No key yet"},
        "11980": {"comment":"AT"},
        "11983": {"comment":"Row 22 + item / 4"},
        "11984": {"comment":"Item / 4"},
        "11988": {"comment":"Plus row 22"},
        "11993": {"comment":"Column 13 x (item AND 3)"},
        "11994": {"comment":"Item AND 3"},
        "11997": {"comment":"Times 13"},
        "12001": {"comment":"The column"},
        "12004": {"comment":"At most 13 characters"},
        "12006": {"synopsis":"One character of the item's text (at most 13).","comment":"The next character"},
        "12008": {"comment":"':' : conditions follow"},
        "12012": {"comment":"Line end: no item"},
        "12017": {"comment":"Not a small letter?"},
        "12021": {"synopsis":"Into the menu text.","comment":"Into the text"},
        "12023": {"comment":"Up to 13"},
        "12025": {"synopsis":"The item is dropped: its text pointer back to its start.","comment":"The item dropped"},
        "12028": {"comment":"To the line end"},
        "12030": {"synopsis":"A capital: the first one is shown inverse (INVERSE 1, the letter, INVERSE 0) and its small\nletter becomes the item's key.","comment":"A key already?"},
        "12034": {"comment":"This one is the key"},
        "12036": {"comment":"INVERSE 1, the letter, INVERSE 0"},
        "12042": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "12044": {"comment":"INVERSE 0"},
        "12050": {"comment":"Small: into the key table"},
        "12052": {"comment":"Key into the key table"},
        "12055": {"comment":"Room left?"},
        "12056": {"comment":"Text full: no item"},
        "12060": {"synopsis":"':' : the item's conditions, then its command.","comment":"Is the selected entry a directory?"},
        "12064": {"comment":"Small letter"},
        "12067": {"comment":"'f': files only"},
        "12071": {"comment":"A directory? Then no item"},
        "12076": {"synopsis":"'d': directories only.","comment":"'d': directories only"},
        "12080": {"comment":"A file? Then no item"},
        "12085": {"synopsis":"'.': the selected entry's type must match the list.","comment":"The entry's type"},
        "12086": {"comment":"'.': a type list to match"},
        "12092": {"comment":"Does it match?"},
        "12099": {"synopsis":"A condition failed: the item is dropped."},
        "12102": {"synopsis":"The conditions must end with ':'.","comment":"':' must follow"},
        "12106": {"comment":"No: no item"},
        "12108": {"comment":"The key table entry"},
        "12110": {"comment":"Handler BRW_MENU_ITEM"},
        "12117": {"comment":"The command's address $100 bytes higher"},
        "12118": {"comment":"The command's address"},
        "12121": {"comment":"Back to the key table"},
        "12124": {"comment":"One more item"},
        "12125": {"comment":"8 items: the page is full"},
        "12129": {"synopsis":"On to the end of the line; the end of the text ends the page.","comment":"Line end?"},
        "12132": {"comment":"Yes: the next item"},
        "12135": {"comment":"$FF: the end of the text"},
        "12138": {"comment":"Skip a character"},
        "12142": {"synopsis":"The text ended: no further page (D = 0).","comment":"D = 0: no more pages"},
        "12144": {"synopsis":"$D5DA = where the next page starts; the menu text and the key table ended by $FF; no items\nends the menu.","comment":"Where the next page starts"},
        "12148": {"comment":"Menu text ended"},
        "12151": {"comment":"Key table ended"},
        "12153": {"comment":"Any items?"},
        "12158": {"synopsis":"The menu printed at the bottom of the screen.","comment":"Bottom lines cleared"},
        "12164": {"comment":"Print the menu"},
        "12170": {"synopsis":"A key, dispatched through the menu's key table at $D827.","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 3 cleared"},
        "12174": {"comment":"Wait for a key (with its click)"},
        "12177": {"comment":"Through the menu's key table"},
        "12183": {"comment":"Redraw asked for?"},
        "12187": {"synopsis":"SPACE: the menu closes (SP back from $D5D8).","comment":"Back to the Browser's level"},
        "12191": {"synopsis":"$D5DC = 0; FLAGS2 bit 5 set (the help text is redrawn).\nExit: carry.","comment":"$D5DC = 0"},
        "12195": {"comment":"Help text redrawn"},
        "12199": {"comment":"Done"},
        "12201": {"synopsis":"Key $0E: the next page of items, or the menu closes when there is none.","comment":"Back to the Browser's level"},
        "12208": {"comment":"More text?"},
        "12215": {"synopsis":"To the start of the next line.","comment":"On to the line end"},
        "12220": {"comment":"Then build the next page"},
        "12223": {"comment":"$FF: none"},
        "12228": {"synopsis":"Prints the $FF-ended text at HL through WIN_PRINT_A.\nExit: HL past the $FF.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "12230": {"comment":"$FF ends the text"},
        "12234": {"comment":"Print it"},
        "12240": {"synopsis":"A menu item's key (HL from $15A1 past its table entry; the command's address is $100 bytes\nhigher).\n1. Text before a separator is copied, zero-ended, to $DA31 and handed to ROM 1's $2B6C, the\n   screen's bottom lines cleared first; NZ back ends the item.\n2. A separator and text after it: the text (to the line end) is copied to $F700, the\n   selected file's name built at $D827, and the text run as a filetype command\n   (BRW_RUN_CMD).\nExit: no carry if the command has no separator.","comment":"The command's address"},
        "12245": {"comment":"Starts with a separator?"},
        "12251": {"comment":"Copy the text to $DA31"},
        "12254": {"synopsis":"The text before the separator, to $DA31."},
        "12258": {"comment":"Line end: done"},
        "12262": {"comment":"Until a separator"},
        "12267": {"comment":"Zero-ended"},
        "12271": {"comment":"Bottom lines cleared"},
        "12277": {"comment":"Help text redrawn later"},
        "12281": {"comment":"ROM 1's $2B6C with the text"},
        "12288": {"comment":"NZ: the item ends here"},
        "12289": {"synopsis":"A separator must follow.","comment":"A separator?"},
        "12294": {"comment":"No: no carry"},
        "12297": {"comment":"C = the separator"},
        "12298": {"comment":"Copy the line to $F700, B counting"},
        "12304": {"synopsis":"The command text, to $F700, B counting it."},
        "12305": {"comment":"Copy a byte"},
        "12309": {"comment":"Until the line end (copied too)"},
        "12315": {"comment":"The selected entry's name at $D827"},
        "12320": {"comment":"A = the separator"},
        "12324": {"synopsis":"Key 'g': shows a guide, when the extra capabilities allow it (bit 1). $D5E9 = '<' (the\nBrowser restarts after).\n1. A RUN directory: the Browser goes into it (BRW_CD_MARK) and shows run.gde.\n2. Otherwise the long name's type is changed to .gde (at $DA31); if there is no such file\n   beside it, c:/docs/guides/ is put in front (at $F700); if neither exists,\n   c:/docs/guides/browser.gde.\n3. Shown by $0933.","comment":"Guides allowed?"},
        "12331": {"comment":"'<': the Browser restarts after"},
        "12336": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "12341": {"comment":"Type RUN?"},
        "12346": {"comment":"Into it, marked for a return"},
        "12349": {"comment":"\"run.gde\""},
        "12354": {"synopsis":"Not a RUN directory: its long name ($38AA) with the type .gde; no long name: browser.gde.","comment":"The long name to $DA31"},
        "12359": {"comment":"Find its last '.'"},
        "12363": {"comment":"B = 0, C = 1"},
        "12366": {"synopsis":"B counts the name; C = the position after its last '.'.","comment":"The next character"},
        "12368": {"comment":"$FF: the end"},
        "12371": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "12374": {"comment":"A '.'?"},
        "12378": {"comment":"C = its position"},
        "12381": {"synopsis":"Over 255 characters: B stays 255."},
        "12382": {"synopsis":"B = the length without the type (all of it with no '.').","comment":"No '.'? Then the whole name"},
        "12386": {"synopsis":"\".gde\" written over the type.","comment":"DE = the end of the name"},
        "12391": {"comment":"\".gde\" and $FF"},
        "12401": {"comment":"Does it exist?"},
        "12406": {"comment":"\"c:/docs/guides/\""},
        "12418": {"synopsis":"The name after \"c:/docs/guides/\".","comment":"The name after it"},
        "12424": {"comment":"Does that exist?"},
        "12434": {"synopsis":"Neither exists: the Browser's own guide.","comment":"\"c:/docs/guides/browser.gde\""},
        "12438": {"synopsis":"HL = the guide's name."},
        "12439": {"synopsis":"Shown through $0933.","comment":"Show it"},
        "12442": {"synopsis":"Does the file named at HL exist? DOS_OPEN (file 0, access mode 1, open an existing one only)\nand DOS_CLOSE.\nExit: carry if it opened.","comment":"Open action 1, create action 0"},
        "12445": {"comment":"File 0, access mode 1"},
        "12447": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_OPEN"},
        "12450": {"comment":"Not there: no carry"},
        "12451": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_CLOSE"},
        "12456": {"comment":"It exists"},
        "12458": {"synopsis":"Keys ENTER and '0': acts on the selected entry (C = 2 with SYMBOL SHIFT held, else 1).\n1. A directory: entered (BRW_CD), except a RUN directory without SYMBOL SHIFT when RUN\n   directories may run (extra capability bit 0): the Browser goes into it (BRW_CD_MARK) and\n   runs the command at $154C (CLS:LOAD\"RUN.BAS\").\n2. A file: its filetype is looked up (BRW_FIND_TYPE); not listed: no carry. A link (LNK) is\n   loaded to $C000 and followed (BRW_FOLLOW_LINK).\n3. Listed: the short name is copied to $E090 and the long one read to $DA31; with no command\n   the Browser returns to its caller with them (BRW_RETURN_SEL); otherwise the Browser is\n   left and the command runs (BRW_RUN_CMD).","comment":"C = 2 with SYMBOL SHIFT"},
        "12460": {"comment":"Is SYMBOL SHIFT up?"},
        "12467": {"comment":"Yes: C = 1"},
        "12468": {"synopsis":"The selected entry's name to $D827; Z for a file.","comment":"Name to $D827; a directory?"},
        "12471": {"comment":"A file"},
        "12473": {"comment":"SYMBOL SHIFT: just enter it"},
        "12476": {"comment":"May RUN directories run?"},
        "12484": {"comment":"Then is it one?"},
        "12487": {"synopsis":"NZ: into the directory.","comment":"Enter the directory"},
        "12490": {"comment":"Into it, marked for a return"},
        "12494": {"comment":"CLS:LOAD\"RUN.BAS\""},
        "12497": {"comment":"Separator '<'"},
        "12499": {"synopsis":"$D5E9 = the separator A; then the command at HL runs.","comment":"$D5E9 = the separator"},
        "12504": {"synopsis":"A file: its filetype.","comment":"Its filetype"},
        "12507": {"comment":"Not listed"},
        "12508": {"comment":"Not a link"},
        "12511": {"comment":"Load the link file to $C000"},
        "12521": {"comment":"Follow it"},
        "12523": {"synopsis":"Runs a selected file's filetype command, or returns the file to the caller.\nEntry: HL = the command, A = its length (0: none).\n1. The short name ($D827) is copied to $E090 and the long name read to $DA31 ($38AA).\n2. No command: BRW_RETURN_SEL. Otherwise the Browser is left (BRW_LEAVE) and the command,\n   ended by a $0D put in for the time, is run through $094C.\nExit: no carry (the byte after the command restored).","comment":"A command?"},
        "12526": {"comment":"The short name to $E090"},
        "12535": {"comment":"The long name to $DA31"},
        "12538": {"comment":"A command: leave the Browser"},
        "12544": {"comment":"No command: return the names"},
        "12548": {"comment":"End of the command"},
        "12551": {"comment":"A $0D there for the time"},
        "12554": {"comment":"HL = the command"},
        "12556": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "12561": {"comment":"The byte back"},
        "12562": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "12564": {"synopsis":"$D5E9 = A (the separator that followed the type); $D5B8 = $FE.\nChanges: A.","comment":"The separator"},
        "12567": {"comment":"$D5B8 = $FE"},
        "12573": {"synopsis":"IDE_PATH change into the directory named at $D827, and the word $5245 at $E3C7 in 8K page\n$10: the mark that makes BROWSER_RESTART go back to the parent.\nExit: carry from IDE_PATH.","comment":"The directory's name"},
        "12576": {"comment":"ROM 2: IDE_PATH change"},
        "12581": {"comment":"8K page $10 at $E000"},
        "12585": {"comment":"The marker $5245"},
        "12592": {"comment":"Page $0F back"},
        "12597": {"synopsis":"Follows a link file loaded at HL: it must start with \"NextLink\" and a line end.\n1. The next line is a directory: entered and shown (BRW_CD).\n2. A line after that is a file name: $3847 is called on it, then it is copied, zero-ended,\n   to $C400; the directory's parts are searched for it ($34DA, $3664, $3705) and it is\n   selected ($3751); with C = 1 it is then acted on as by ENTER. Not found: the last entry\n   is selected, no carry.\nExit: carry = done; no carry = not a link.","comment":"\"NextLink\""},
        "12602": {"synopsis":"Checking \"NextLink\".","comment":"The same?"},
        "12606": {"synopsis":"Not a link: no carry.","comment":"No: no carry"},
        "12611": {"comment":"A line end must follow"},
        "12617": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "12623": {"comment":"Into that directory"},
        "12628": {"synopsis":"A file name line follows?"},
        "12630": {"comment":"A file name line?"},
        "12635": {"comment":"None: done (carry)"},
        "12638": {"comment":"The file name"},
        "12646": {"comment":"Copied to $C400"},
        "12649": {"synopsis":"The name to $C400."},
        "12655": {"comment":"Zero-ended"},
        "12657": {"comment":"$D5EA bit 7 cleared"},
        "12662": {"synopsis":"Searching a part of the directory.","comment":"This part of the directory"},
        "12665": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "12667": {"synopsis":"The next entry."},
        "12668": {"comment":"The entries in this part"},
        "12672": {"comment":"Past the last?"},
        "12676": {"comment":"The next part, if any"},
        "12683": {"comment":"None: the last entry selected"},
        "12686": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "12689": {"synopsis":"Entry D tested by $3664: Z ends the search.","comment":"This entry?"},
        "12694": {"comment":"Select it"},
        "12699": {"comment":"C = 1: act on it as by ENTER"},
        "12704": {"comment":"Done"},
        "12706": {"synopsis":"Copies the next line of the text at HL (line ends skipped first) to $D827, $FF-ended.\nExit: carry = a line copied, HL at its end; no carry = the text ended ($FF) or the line was\ntoo long.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"To $D827"},
        "12709": {"comment":"At most $1FE characters"},
        "12712": {"synopsis":"Line ends skipped; $FF ends the text.","comment":"$FF: the text ended"},
        "12716": {"comment":"Line ends skipped"},
        "12722": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Copy a character"},
        "12724": {"comment":"Line end next?"},
        "12730": {"comment":"Room for more?"},
        "12736": {"comment":"Too long: no carry"},
        "12738": {"synopsis":"$FF after the line.\nExit: carry.","comment":"$FF after it"},
        "12743": {"synopsis":"Z if the entry's type (after HL, the entry's 8th byte) is RUN.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"\"RUN\""},
        "12746": {"synopsis":"Z if the 3 characters after DE (bit 7 ignored) are those at HL.\nEntry: HL = the 3 characters, DE = the byte before the type.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the 3 characters"},
        "12749": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Next character, bit 7 off"},
        "12753": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "12759": {"synopsis":"SPACE: the Browser returns to its caller with carry and NZ (BRW_LEAVE).","comment":"NZ: SPACE"},
        "12763": {"synopsis":"ENTER on a listed type with no command: the Browser returns to its caller with carry and Z,\nHL = the short name ($E090), DE = the long name ($DA31).","comment":"The long name"},
        "12766": {"comment":"The short name"},
        "12769": {"comment":"Z: a file chosen"},
        "12770": {"synopsis":"SP back from $D5D6 (the caller's level), then BRW_LEAVE.","comment":"Back to the Browser's caller level"},
        "12774": {"synopsis":"Puts things back when the Browser ends; keeps AF (carry set), DE and HL.\n1. The sort memory of both catalog handles is freed: DOS_CATALOG with B = 2, C = $A0, then\n   $20, A = 0 (the way the API document advises), on \"c:\" at $C752.\n2. $1078 restores NextRegs $15 and $14 and other settings; BRW_STATE_COPY brings back\n   $5B68-$5B89.\n3. The bottom lines cleared; the mode saved at $D693 set again (ROM 1's $14A9); the channel\n   saved at $D73A selected again (ROM 3's CHAN_SET_FLAGS); $0EC9.","comment":"Carry: success"},
        "12778": {"comment":"\"c:\" to $C752"},
        "12788": {"comment":"Preloaded entry zeroed"},
        "12792": {"comment":"B = 2, C = $A0, A = 0: free handle 2's sort"},
        "12798": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_CATALOG"},
        "12803": {"comment":"B = 2, C = $20, A = 0: free handle 1's"},
        "12807": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_CATALOG"},
        "12810": {"comment":"NextRegs and settings back"},
        "12813": {"comment":"$5B68-$5B89 back"},
        "12816": {"comment":"Bottom lines cleared"},
        "12819": {"comment":"The saved mode"},
        "12822": {"comment":"set again by ROM 1"},
        "12825": {"comment":"The saved channel"},
        "12828": {"comment":"ROM 3's CHAN_SET_FLAGS: selected again"},
        "12831": {"comment":"$0EC9 to finish"},
        "12834": {"comment":"DE, HL and AF back"},
        "12838": {"synopsis":"Saves what the Browser changes: $5B68-$5B89 (BRW_STATE_COPY), the mode ($5C7F to $D693),\nCURCHL (to $D73A); then mode 5 (ROM 1's $14A9), stream 2 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT) and $1014.","comment":"No carry: save"},
        "12839": {"comment":"$5B68-$5B89 saved"},
        "12842": {"comment":"The mode"},
        "12848": {"comment":"CURCHL"},
        "12854": {"comment":"Mode 5"},
        "12859": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: stream 2"},
        "12867": {"synopsis":"Key 'l': drive C: made the default (DOS_SET_DRIVE), c:/links created if missing (IDE_PATH\nmake, errors ignored) and entered.","comment":"Drive C:"},
        "12869": {"comment":"ROM 2: DOS_SET_DRIVE"},
        "12872": {"comment":"\"c:/links\""},
        "12878": {"comment":"ROM 2: IDE_PATH make (errors ignored)"},
        "12883": {"comment":"Enter it"},
        "12885": {"synopsis":"Key $07: into the parent directory (\"..\").","comment":"\"..\""},
        "12893": {"synopsis":"Into the directory named at $D827, then BRW_SHOW.","comment":"The directory's name"},
        "12896": {"synopsis":"Into the directory named at HL through ROM 2's $0506; no carry from it returns. Then\nBRW_SHOW.","comment":"ROM 2's $0506"},
        "12900": {"synopsis":"Draws the Browser and reads the directory.\n1. $3F4A with HL = $09F7 and DE = $D633; IX = $F700, code $18 with $D63A to the window.\n2. The top line ($14A0, then the filter from the settings at $E4C9), loading the settings\n   first (BRW_LOAD_PREFS).\n3. The attribute bytes get $D639: $5AA9 always, $5AB7 with view bit 4, $5AB8 without bit 5,\n   $5AB9 with bit 2.\n4. $3463, $3505, the help text, BRW_READ_DIR.\n5. The path at $D92C is compared with the one kept at $E3C9 (page $10) and kept there: a new\n   directory selects entry 0; the same one reads on to the part saved at $E4DD and selects\n   the saved entry (or the last).","comment":"$3F4A with the text at $09F7"},
        "12909": {"comment":"The Browser's window"},
        "12913": {"comment":"Code $18 with $D63A"},
        "12919": {"comment":"The top line"},
        "12925": {"comment":"Settings loaded"},
        "12928": {"comment":"The filter"},
        "12934": {"comment":"E = the colour for the flags shown"},
        "12938": {"comment":"Always"},
        "12942": {"comment":"Show system files?"},
        "12953": {"synopsis":"View flag bit 5.","comment":"Hide \".\" and \"..\"?"},
        "12959": {"synopsis":"View flag bit 2.","comment":"View flag bit 2?"},
        "12965": {"synopsis":"The rest of the screen, then the directory."},
        "12968": {"comment":"The help text"},
        "12974": {"comment":"Read the directory"},
        "12977": {"comment":"8K page $10 at $E000"},
        "12981": {"comment":"The path against the kept one"},
        "12987": {"comment":"XL = 0: the same so far"},
        "12990": {"synopsis":"One byte of the path compared and copied; XL = 1 at a difference.","comment":"The same byte?"},
        "12994": {"comment":"No: XL = 1"},
        "12998": {"synopsis":"Copied, until the $FF.","comment":"Kept; until the $FF"},
        "13003": {"comment":"A new directory?"},
        "13007": {"comment":"The saved part and entry"},
        "13010": {"comment":"Page $0F back"},
        "13014": {"synopsis":"Reads on until the saved part is reached.","comment":"The saved part?"},
        "13020": {"comment":"No: a full buffer has more parts"},
        "13027": {"comment":"Read the next part"},
        "13034": {"synopsis":"Selects the last entry (H = $FF, limited to the count).","comment":"The last entry"},
        "13036": {"synopsis":"Selects entry H, at most the last.","comment":"Any entries?"},
        "13042": {"comment":"A = the last entry"},
        "13043": {"comment":"H beyond it? Then the last"},
        "13047": {"synopsis":"Selects entry A ($374C).","comment":"Select entry A"},
        "13050": {"synopsis":"Prints the help text at $D5D0 on the bottom lines ($13D2, the paste prompt, when $D5DC bit 7\nis set). FLAGS2 bit 5 cleared; the two lines cleared first (BRW_TEXT_1445, BRW_TEXT_14CD).","comment":"The help text"},
        "13053": {"comment":"Paste waiting? (bit 7)"},
        "13059": {"comment":"Then the paste prompt"},
        "13062": {"synopsis":"BRW_HELP with the text at HL.","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 cleared"},
        "13066": {"synopsis":"The lines cleared, then the text."},
        "13067": {"comment":"Bottom lines cleared"},
        "13074": {"synopsis":"Prints the $FF-ended text at HL in the window at IX (WIN_STR_FF).","comment":"Print the text"},
        "13077": {"synopsis":"Loads the Browser's settings from page $10 (BRW_PREFS_COPY): the filter to $D827, the view\nand sort flags to $D5EA and $D5EB. A bad checksum or signature (the word after them must be\n$62FF) sets the flags 0 and the filter \"*.*\" and saves that (BRW_SAVE_PREFS).","comment":"Load the settings to $D827"},
        "13081": {"comment":"Bad checksum?"},
        "13083": {"comment":"View and sort flags"},
        "13093": {"comment":"The signature word"},
        "13096": {"comment":"Must be $62FF"},
        "13103": {"synopsis":"Settings not valid: flags 0, filter \"*.*\".","comment":"Flags 0"},
        "13108": {"comment":"Filter \"*.*\""},
        "13111": {"comment":"Saved"},
        "13115": {"synopsis":"IDE_BROWSER with DE = 0: the Browser's settings, by A.\n0: the filter (15 bytes) to HL, C = the view flags, B = the sort flags;\n1: the view and sort flags from C and B, the filter from HL, saved;\n2-7: colour schemes and palette, by $0FE4;\n8 and up: no carry, A = $15.","comment":"The function in A"},
        "13116": {"comment":"8 and up?"},
        "13120": {"comment":"Error $15, no carry"},
        "13123": {"synopsis":"A = 0: get; A = 1: set; 2 and up: $0FE4.","comment":"A = 0: get"},
        "13126": {"comment":"2 and up: colour schemes"},
        "13130": {"comment":"A = 1: view flags C, sort flags B"},
        "13136": {"synopsis":"A = 0: the settings to the caller.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The buffer"},
        "13137": {"comment":"Settings loaded"},
        "13141": {"comment":"The filter to the buffer"},
        "13149": {"comment":"C = view flags, B = sort flags"},
        "13153": {"comment":"Done"},
        "13155": {"synopsis":"Toggles settings: the view flags XOR B, the sort flags XOR C; saved with the filter\n(BRW_SAVE_PREFS)."},
        "13156": {"comment":"The saved filter to $D827"},
        "13161": {"comment":"View flags XOR B"},
        "13168": {"comment":"Sort flags XOR C"},
        "13171": {"comment":"The filter"},
        "13174": {"synopsis":"Saves the settings to page $10: the saved position at $E4DD zeroed; the 15-byte filter from\nHL, the view and sort flags, the word $62FF built at $D827 and copied with its checksum to\n$E4C9 (BRW_PREFS_COPY).\nExit: carry.","comment":"8K page $10 at $E000"},
        "13178": {"comment":"Saved part and entry zeroed"},
        "13185": {"comment":"Page $0F back"},
        "13189": {"comment":"The filter, 15 bytes"},
        "13197": {"comment":"The view and sort flags"},
        "13204": {"comment":"The signature $62FF"},
        "13210": {"comment":"Carry: save"},
        "13211": {"synopsis":"Copies the 19 bytes of settings between $D827 and $E4C9 (8K page $10 in MMU 7 meanwhile),\nsumming them: with carry to $E4C9, the sum stored after them; without, from $E4C9, Z when\nthe sum matches the stored one.\nExit: carry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"19 bytes from $D827 to $E4C9"},
        "13219": {"comment":"No carry: the other way"},
        "13222": {"synopsis":"Page $10 in; C = the sum.","comment":"8K page $10 at $E000"},
        "13226": {"comment":"C = the sum"},
        "13228": {"synopsis":"One byte copied and summed.","comment":"Copy a byte"},
        "13232": {"comment":"Add it"},
        "13236": {"comment":"The sum: the same as stored?"},
        "13238": {"comment":"Stored after the copy"},
        "13239": {"comment":"Page $0F back"},
        "13245": {"synopsis":"Copies the 34 bytes $5B68-$5B89 to or from $E395-$E3B6 in 8K page $10: no carry saves them,\ncarry brings them back.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Kept copy in page $10"},
        "13248": {"comment":"The variables' end"},
        "13251": {"comment":"34 bytes"},
        "13254": {"comment":"No carry: save them"},
        "13257": {"synopsis":"Page $10 in, the bytes copied downwards, page $0F back.","comment":"8K page $10 at $E000"},
        "13261": {"comment":"Copy downwards"},
        "13263": {"comment":"Page $0F back"},
        "13268": {"synopsis":"Prints the window text at $1445 (control codes for the bottom lines).","comment":"Text at $1445"},
        "13273": {"synopsis":"Prints the window text at $14CD.","comment":"Text at $14CD"},
        "13276": {"synopsis":"Prints the $FF-ended text at HL in the Browser's window: IX = $F700, then WIN_STR_FF.","comment":"The Browser's window"},
        "13283": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL + 8, then the text whose address is word A AND 3 of the table at HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; IX = $F700."},
        "13285": {"comment":"The text at HL + 8"},
        "13294": {"comment":"Word A AND 3 of the table"},
        "13296": {"comment":"Word A of the table"},
        "13299": {"comment":"HL = the text's address"},
        "13303": {"comment":"Print that text"},
        "13305": {"synopsis":"Builds the selected entry's name at $D827 ($340A), then BRW_SEL_IS_DIR.","comment":"The name built at $D827"},
        "13311": {"synopsis":"Is the selected entry ($D5E6) a directory? Bit 7 of its 8th byte.\nExit: NZ = a directory, HL = that byte, no carry.","comment":"The selected entry"},
        "13314": {"comment":"Its 8th byte"},
        "13318": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "13319": {"comment":"Bit 7: a directory"},
        "13322": {"synopsis":"Copies the current entry's short name ($D5E6) to DE as NAME.TYP (COPY_ENTRY_NAME).","comment":"HL = the current entry"},
        "13325": {"synopsis":"Copies the 8.3 name of the catalog entry at HL to DE:\n1. The eight name characters, bit 7 masked off, spaces dropped.\n2. When the name starts with '.' (the '.' and '..' entries) that is all.\n3. Otherwise '.' and the three type characters, spaces dropped.\nExit: the text $FF-terminated, DE at the $FF.\nChanges: A, B, DE, HL."},
        "13327": {"comment":"The eight name characters"},
        "13332": {"comment":"HL = the entry again; the type's address kept"},
        "13333": {"comment":"The name's first character"},
        "13337": {"comment":"'.' or '..'? Then no type"},
        "13340": {"comment":"'.' before the type"},
        "13344": {"comment":"The three type characters"},
        "13346": {"synopsis":"Copies B characters from HL to DE, bit 7 masked off and spaces dropped, then puts $FF at DE\n(DE left on it).","comment":"Next character, attribute bit off"},
        "13350": {"comment":"Spaces dropped"},
        "13356": {"synopsis":"The next character."},
        "13358": {"comment":"$FF after the text"},
        "13362": {"synopsis":"Key 'u' in the browser: unmounts the default drive.\n1. Nothing unless the capabilities in $D5D4 allow it (bit 5, unmount).\n2. Drive C is never unmounted.\n3. IDE_DOS_UNMAP for the drive; on failure nothing more.\n4. browser.cfg reloaded (LOAD_SYSCFG), then on to the next drive (KEY_DRIVE).","comment":"May drives be unmounted (capability bit 5)?"},
        "13368": {"comment":"A = $FF: get"},
        "13370": {"comment":"DOS_SET_DRIVE (ROM 2): A = the default drive"},
        "13373": {"comment":"Drive C is never unmounted"},
        "13376": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "13377": {"comment":"IDE_DOS_UNMAP (ROM 2) for drive L"},
        "13380": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "13381": {"comment":"browser.cfg read again if needed"},
        "13384": {"synopsis":"Key 'd' in the browser: makes the next drive that can be selected the default one. The drive\nletters are tried in turn from the current one, P wrapping to A, by DOS_SET_DRIVE; the first\nthat it accepts is kept and the browser redrawn ($3264). Back at the starting drive nothing\nchanges.","comment":"A = $FF: get"},
        "13386": {"comment":"DOS_SET_DRIVE (ROM 2): A = the default drive"},
        "13389": {"comment":"C = the drive started from"},
        "13390": {"synopsis":"The next letter, Q wrapping to A.","comment":"The next letter"},
        "13391": {"comment":"Past P?"},
        "13395": {"comment":"Back to A"},
        "13397": {"synopsis":"Back at the first drive? Otherwise this one tried.","comment":"Round to the start again?"},
        "13399": {"comment":"B = the letter tried"},
        "13401": {"comment":"DOS_SET_DRIVE (ROM 2): make it the default"},
        "13406": {"comment":"Accepted: the browser redrawn with the new drive"},
        "13409": {"comment":"Not accepted: the next letter"},
        "13411": {"synopsis":"Shows the default drive and its current directory on screen line 0:\n1. Line 0 cleared.\n2. The drive letter (DOS_SET_DRIVE with $FF) into $5B79 and $5B7A, and \"X:\" with $FF at\n   $D92C.\n3. IDE_PATH (get) fills $D92C with the path.\n4. The window code at $1506 printed.\n5. At most the last 51 characters of the path copied to $DA31 and printed in 51 columns\n   (PRINT_FITTED).\n6. Line 0 coloured with the bar colour ($D63A).","comment":"Screen line 0 cleared"},
        "13417": {"comment":"The drive and path built at $D92C"},
        "13421": {"comment":"A = $FF: get"},
        "13423": {"comment":"DOS_SET_DRIVE (ROM 2): A = the default drive"},
        "13426": {"comment":"Kept in $5B79 and $5B7A"},
        "13434": {"comment":"\"X:\" and $FF at $D92C"},
        "13443": {"comment":"Reason 1: get"},
        "13445": {"comment":"IDE_PATH (ROM 2): the path to $D92C"},
        "13448": {"comment":"The window code at $1506"},
        "13455": {"comment":"A counts the path's length"},
        "13456": {"synopsis":"Counts the path's characters up to the $FF."},
        "13459": {"comment":"Until the $FF"},
        "13462": {"comment":"HL = the last character"},
        "13464": {"comment":"C = the length, at most 51"},
        "13471": {"synopsis":"DE = $DA31 + C; the tail of the path copied backwards.","comment":"DE = $DA31 + C"},
        "13477": {"comment":"The tail of the path and its $FF copied"},
        "13481": {"comment":"Printed in 51 columns"},
        "13486": {"comment":"Line 0"},
        "13488": {"synopsis":"Screen line L coloured with the bar colour ($D63A) (FILL_LINE_ATTR).","comment":"A = the bar colour"},
        "13493": {"synopsis":"Classifies the current entry for its colour.\nEntry: A = 1 to skip the filetype list for a file (a file then is class 0).\nExit: A = 0 a file of no listed type, 1 a file of type LNK, 2 a file of a type in the\nfiletype list ($D5CE), 3 a directory of type RUN, 4 any other directory.","comment":"B = A on entry"},
        "13494": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "13498": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "13500": {"comment":"A file: LNK, or a type in the list?"},
        "13505": {"comment":"0: neither"},
        "13508": {"comment":"1: LNK; 2: a listed type"},
        "13513": {"synopsis":"A directory: 3 for type RUN, otherwise 4.","comment":"Type RUN?"},
        "13516": {"comment":"3: RUN"},
        "13519": {"comment":"4: another directory"},
        "13521": {"synopsis":"Colours the current entry's screen line with the highlight colour of its class ($D63B +\nENTRY_CLASS).","comment":"Class of the current entry (the list searched)"},
        "13525": {"comment":"The highlight colours"},
        "13530": {"synopsis":"Colours the current entry's screen line with the normal colour of its class ($D643 +\nENTRY_CLASS). When classes 0 and 2 share a colour ($D643 = $D645), the filetype list is not\nsearched. DE kept.","comment":"The normal colours"},
        "13537": {"comment":"A = 1 when classes 0 and 2 share a colour"},
        "13539": {"comment":"Class of the current entry"},
        "13545": {"synopsis":"HL = the colour table, A = the class: that colour, the line the entry's row ($D5E8) + 2.","comment":"A = the colour for the class"},
        "13548": {"comment":"The entry's row on the page"},
        "13551": {"comment":"Its screen line (rows start at line 2)"},
        "13555": {"synopsis":"Fills the 32 attribute bytes of screen line L (0 to 23) with A.\nChanges: BC, HL.","comment":"BC = the attribute area"},
        "13558": {"comment":"HL = 32 * L"},
        "13564": {"comment":"HL = the line's first attribute"},
        "13565": {"comment":"32 columns"},
        "13567": {"synopsis":"One attribute byte."},
        "13573": {"synopsis":"Draws the browser's status line (screen line 1):\n1. Line 1 cleared and coloured with the bar colour.\n2. The texts at $13FD; then 'n', or 'ff' when directories come first (bit 6 of $D5EA).\n3. The search hint ($143A) when the order is by long name, ascending.\n4. The sort mode's name ($14EC table) and the view mode's name ($14F9 table).\n5. The key letters coloured with $D639: columns 0, 11, 18, 19, 22, 26, and 7 or 8 by the\n   reverse bit.\n6. Code $18 with the colour at $D633 (SEND_CODE18).","comment":"Screen line 1 cleared"},
        "13579": {"comment":"Coloured with the bar colour"},
        "13584": {"comment":"Code $18 with the bar colour"},
        "13590": {"comment":"The status line's texts"},
        "13596": {"comment":"Directories first (bit 6)?"},
        "13601": {"comment":"'n'"},
        "13605": {"comment":"'f', twice"},
        "13612": {"synopsis":"Prints the letter in A."},
        "13615": {"comment":"A = the sort flags (1 when sorting is not allowed)"},
        "13619": {"comment":"The search hint, for order by long name, ascending"},
        "13627": {"comment":"A = the sort flags"},
        "13629": {"comment":"The sort mode's name"},
        "13635": {"comment":"The view mode's name, by $D5EA"},
        "13644": {"comment":"C = the key letters' colour"},
        "13648": {"comment":"The key letters on line 1 coloured"},
        "13667": {"comment":"A = the sort flags"},
        "13668": {"comment":"Bit 2 (reverse) to bit 0"},
        "13672": {"comment":"Column 7 or 8: '+' or '-' coloured"},
        "13676": {"comment":"Code $18 with the colour at $D633"},
        "13679": {"synopsis":"Sends control code $18 and then A to the window record at IX = $F700 (through $275B).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"The window record"},
        "13684": {"comment":"Control code $18"},
        "13689": {"comment":"Then A"},
        "13694": {"synopsis":"Exit: when sorting is allowed (bit 3 of $D5D5), A = the sort flags ($D5EB) and carry set;\notherwise A = 1 (unsorted) and carry clear.","comment":"Sorting allowed (bit 3 of the second capabilities)?"},
        "13699": {"comment":"No: A = 1 (unsorted), no carry"},
        "13702": {"comment":"Yes: A = the sort flags"},
        "13705": {"comment":"Carry: sorting allowed"},
        "13707": {"synopsis":"Key 'h' in the browser: searches the listing for a name as it is typed.\n1. Only when sorting is allowed and the order is by long name, ascending (SORT_FLAGS_GET,\n   bits 2-0 all 0).\n2. Bit 7 of $D5EA cleared (files searched); the texts at $150B (\"Search:\") and $1514 shown.\n3. Each time the text changes it is copied from the editor's buffer $E1D2 to $C400 with a 0\n   after it; BIN_SEARCH finds where it belongs; that entry is selected (the page redrawn\n   when the catalog block changed) and highlighted.\n4. The line editor ($27D5, B = 7, C = 41) runs again until it returns B = 0; key $0E toggles\n   bit 7 of $D5EA (files or directories) and searches again.\nExit: carry set, FLAGS2 bit 5 set.","comment":"A = the sort flags"},
        "13710": {"comment":"Long names, ascending, allowed? Otherwise no search"},
        "13713": {"comment":"Bit 7 of $D5EA cleared: files first"},
        "13718": {"comment":"The search prompt"},
        "13724": {"comment":"The EXTEND key's help text"},
        "13730": {"comment":"E = 0: no text yet"},
        "13733": {"comment":"B = 3: the first time round"},
        "13735": {"synopsis":"One search: the text copied to $C400, BIN_SEARCH, the entry selected.","comment":"The editor's state kept"},
        "13737": {"comment":"C = the text's length"},
        "13740": {"comment":"The paging value for the copy"},
        "13746": {"comment":"The text from the editor's buffer"},
        "13749": {"comment":"... to $C400"},
        "13752": {"comment":"Any characters typed?"},
        "13754": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13757": {"comment":"A 0 after them"},
        "13759": {"comment":"D = where the text belongs"},
        "13762": {"comment":"The catalog block changed?"},
        "13766": {"comment":"No: the old entry's normal colour back"},
        "13769": {"comment":"The found entry selected"},
        "13775": {"synopsis":"The block changed: the page redrawn (SELECT_REDRAW).","comment":"Yes: the page redrawn with it selected"},
        "13779": {"synopsis":"The new entry highlighted.","comment":"The entry highlighted"},
        "13782": {"synopsis":"The print position to row 22, column 8 (the search text's place).","comment":"Row 22, column 8: the search text's place"},
        "13788": {"comment":"The editor's state back"},
        "13790": {"comment":"B = 0: the search ends"},
        "13794": {"comment":"The line editor: B = 7, C = 41"},
        "13805": {"comment":"Bit 1 clear: the text changed, search again"},
        "13809": {"comment":"MODE = 0"},
        "13815": {"comment":"Key $0E (EXTEND)?"},
        "13818": {"comment":"No: the editor again"},
        "13820": {"comment":"Toggles files or directories (bit 7)"},
        "13831": {"synopsis":"Done: FLAGS2 bit 5 set, carry set.","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 set"},
        "13835": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "13837": {"synopsis":"Finds where the text at $C400 belongs in the listing, by long name, moving to the previous\nor next catalog block when it lies outside this one.\nExit: D = the entry index (the exact match, or the first entry after the text); B bit 0 set\nwhen the block changed; Z when the match was exact.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"B = 0: no block change yet; C = 0"},
        "13840": {"synopsis":"This block: C = 1 when it is the first one (no previous block).","comment":"The first block?"},
        "13846": {"comment":"Yes: C = 1"},
        "13848": {"synopsis":"The text against the first entry, then the last.","comment":"Entry 0"},
        "13851": {"comment":"The text against the first entry"},
        "13854": {"comment":"Equal: found"},
        "13855": {"comment":"Before it: the previous block"},
        "13857": {"comment":"D = the last entry"},
        "13862": {"comment":"The text against the last entry"},
        "13865": {"comment":"Equal: found"},
        "13866": {"comment":"After it: the next block"},
        "13868": {"synopsis":"E and D the bounds: done when they meet; otherwise the middle one compared and a bound moved\nto it.","comment":"The bounds met?"},
        "13871": {"comment":"Adjacent? Then D is the answer"},
        "13874": {"comment":"A = the middle"},
        "13878": {"comment":"D = the middle; compared"},
        "13882": {"comment":"HL = the bounds"},
        "13883": {"comment":"XH = the middle"},
        "13885": {"comment":"Equal: found at D"},
        "13886": {"comment":"DE = the bounds again"},
        "13887": {"comment":"Before the middle?"},
        "13889": {"comment":"After: E = the middle"},
        "13893": {"synopsis":"The text comes before the middle: D = the middle.","comment":"Before: D = the middle"},
        "13897": {"synopsis":"Before the first entry: the previous block searched, if there is one.","comment":"The first block: nothing before it"},
        "13900": {"comment":"The previous block"},
        "13905": {"comment":"The block changed"},
        "13907": {"comment":"Moved: search there"},
        "13909": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "13912": {"synopsis":"After the last entry: the next block searched, if there is one.","comment":"The next block"},
        "13919": {"comment":"The block changed"},
        "13921": {"comment":"Moved: search there"},
        "13924": {"synopsis":"Compares the text at $C400 with the long name of entry D, letters in either case equal. In\ndirectories-first mode (bit 6 of $D5EA) only the half that bit 7 of $D5EA picks is compared:\nwith bit 7 clear (files) every directory counts as before the text; with it set\n(directories) every file counts as after it.\nExit: Z when equal; carry when the text comes before the entry; NZ and no carry when after.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL, IX; DE kept.","comment":"The index kept"},
        "13925": {"comment":"DE = 13 * (D + 1)"},
        "13930": {"comment":"DE = the entry ($C738 holds the start entry)"},
        "13935": {"comment":"Directories first (bit 6)?"},
        "13942": {"comment":"The entry a directory (bit 7 of byte 7)?"},
        "13952": {"comment":"A file: files searched (bit 7 clear)?"},
        "13955": {"comment":"Directories searched: NZ and carry, text before"},
        "13960": {"synopsis":"A directory: compared only when directories are searched (bit 7 set).","comment":"A directory: directories searched (bit 7 set)?"},
        "13963": {"comment":"Files searched: NZ, no carry, text after"},
        "13967": {"synopsis":"The entry's long name to $DA31 (ENTRY_LFN_AT) with any name tag removed (STRIP_NAME_TAG);\nthen the two texts compared.","comment":"The entry's long name to $DA31"},
        "13971": {"comment":"Its name tag removed"},
        "13978": {"comment":"HL = the name, DE = the text, both one before"},
        "13984": {"synopsis":"The next pair of characters.","comment":"The next pair"},
        "13986": {"comment":"The text ended?"},
        "13990": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "13993": {"comment":"C = the text's character, upper case"},
        "13998": {"comment":"B = the name's, upper case"},
        "14003": {"comment":"The same in either case?"},
        "14008": {"comment":"Differ: the flags from the comparison"},
        "14010": {"synopsis":"The text ended: Z when the name ends too; otherwise carry.","comment":"Z when the name ends here too ($FF)"},
        "14015": {"synopsis":"A lower-case letter in A made upper case.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Below 'a'?"},
        "14018": {"comment":"Above 'z'?"},
        "14021": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "14024": {"synopsis":"Keys $0B and '7' in the browser: the selection up one entry (MOVE_UP).","comment":"One entry"},
        "14028": {"synopsis":"Keys $08 and '5' in the browser: the selection up one page of 19 entries (MOVE_UP).","comment":"19 entries"},
        "14030": {"synopsis":"The selection moved up E entries: within the block, the entry selected; past its start, the\nprevious block loaded and the entry selected there; at the very first entry, entry 0.","comment":"The old entry's normal colour back"},
        "14033": {"comment":"A = the new index"},
        "14038": {"comment":"Still in this block: select it"},
        "14040": {"comment":"The first block?"},
        "14046": {"comment":"Back to the old index"},
        "14048": {"comment":"Already at entry 0?"},
        "14050": {"comment":"Entry 0 selected"},
        "14053": {"synopsis":"Into the previous block ($F7 entries a full block)."},
        "14054": {"comment":"The previous block loaded"},
        "14057": {"comment":"A = the (negative) index"},
        "14058": {"comment":"Its index in that full block"},
        "14062": {"synopsis":"Loads the previous catalog block: the catalog restarted ($2CCC) and stepped forward ($2CB5)\nto block $D5E4 - 1.\nExit: carry when it moved; A = 0, Z and no carry at the first block.","comment":"The block number"},
        "14066": {"comment":"Block 0: nothing before it (Z, no carry)"},
        "14067": {"comment":"The block wanted"},
        "14069": {"comment":"The catalog read from the start"},
        "14073": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "14074": {"comment":"Block 0 wanted: done"},
        "14075": {"synopsis":"One block on."},
        "14076": {"comment":"One block on"},
        "14080": {"comment":"Blocks still to step over?"},
        "14083": {"comment":"Moved: carry"},
        "14085": {"synopsis":"Loads the next catalog block when this one is full ($F7 entries in $D5E2) ($2CB5). An empty\nnext block puts the previous one back (PREV_BLOCK).\nExit: carry when it moved; otherwise no carry.","comment":"The block full ($F7 entries)?"},
        "14091": {"comment":"No: no carry, nothing more"},
        "14092": {"comment":"The next block read"},
        "14095": {"comment":"Any entries in it?"},
        "14099": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "14101": {"comment":"Empty: the previous block back"},
        "14104": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "14106": {"synopsis":"Keys $0A and '6' in the browser: the selection down one entry (MOVE_DOWN).","comment":"One entry"},
        "14110": {"synopsis":"Keys $09 and '8' in the browser: the selection down one page of 19 entries (MOVE_DOWN).","comment":"19 entries"},
        "14112": {"synopsis":"The selection moved down E entries: within the block, the entry selected; past its end, the\nnext block loaded (if any) and the entry selected there, or the last entry.","comment":"The old entry's normal colour back"},
        "14115": {"comment":"D = the number of entries"},
        "14119": {"comment":"A = the new index"},
        "14123": {"comment":"Past 255?"},
        "14125": {"comment":"Still in this block: select it"},
        "14128": {"synopsis":"Past the end of a full block: B = the index in the next one.","comment":"B = the index in the next block"},
        "14131": {"comment":"The next block, if any"},
        "14136": {"comment":"Moved"},
        "14138": {"comment":"D = the last entry's index"},
        "14140": {"comment":"Already on it?"},
        "14145": {"comment":"The last entry selected"},
        "14148": {"synopsis":"The next block: B, or its last entry when it is shorter.","comment":"A = the last entry of the new block"},
        "14152": {"comment":"Is B past it?"},
        "14155": {"comment":"No: entry B"},
        "14156": {"synopsis":"Selects entry A with the page always redrawn ($D5E3 = $FF) (SELECT_ENTRY).","comment":"The page shown made invalid: redrawn"},
        "14161": {"synopsis":"Selects entry A of the catalog block:\n1. $D5E5 = A; the block and entry (L, H) stored at $E4DD in bank $10.\n2. Its page (19 entries each) and row found.\n3. When the page is not the one shown ($D5E3), lines 2 to 20 cleared and each entry of the\n   page drawn (DRAW_ENTRY_ROW).\n4. $D5E8 = the row, $D5E6 = the entry's address.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"The new index"},
        "14164": {"comment":"L = the block, H = the index"},
        "14168": {"comment":"Bank $10 at $E000"},
        "14172": {"comment":"Kept at $E4DD"},
        "14175": {"comment":"Bank $0F back"},
        "14179": {"comment":"B counts the pages"},
        "14181": {"comment":"HL = one page before the first entry"},
        "14184": {"synopsis":"HL to the next page's first entry, B counting pages, while A stays 19 or more.","comment":"One page on"},
        "14189": {"comment":"19 entries a page"},
        "14193": {"comment":"A = the row on the page"},
        "14197": {"comment":"The page shown already?"},
        "14204": {"comment":"The new page shown"},
        "14208": {"comment":"D = the page, E = 19"},
        "14212": {"comment":"E = 19 * page"},
        "14214": {"comment":"A = the entries left from it"},
        "14218": {"comment":"More than 19?"},
        "14221": {"comment":"A = 19"},
        "14222": {"synopsis":"A = the number of rows on the page (19 at most); lines 2 to 20 cleared."},
        "14224": {"comment":"Lines 2 to 20 cleared"},
        "14231": {"comment":"B = the rows + 1"},
        "14233": {"comment":"C = screen line 2"},
        "14236": {"comment":"Row 0"},
        "14240": {"synopsis":"Draws one entry on its screen row.\nEntry: HL = the entry, A = its row on the page, C = the screen line, B = the rows left + 1.\n1. Its long name read (ENTRY_LFN_AT) and the details kept (STORE_LFN_INFO); the name tag\n   removed (STRIP_NAME_TAG) unless bit 2 of $D5EA is set.\n2. The name printed at column 0 in the width for the view mode (NAME_WIDTHS, PRINT_FITTED).\n3. A directory gets \"<RUN>\" (type RUN) or \"<DIR>\" at column 46.\n4. A file gets, by the view mode in bits 1-0 of $D5EA, nothing, its size (PRINT_FILE_SIZE),\n   its date and time (ROM 1's $3747) or its attribute letters (MAKE_ATTR_TEXT), after the\n   name.\n5. The line given its normal colour (NORMAL_CURRENT).","comment":"The row on the page"},
        "14243": {"comment":"The entry's address"},
        "14246": {"comment":"B, C kept"},
        "14247": {"comment":"Its long name"},
        "14251": {"comment":"Date, time and size kept"},
        "14254": {"comment":"The name at $DA31"},
        "14257": {"comment":"Name tags shown (bit 2 of $D5EA)?"},
        "14260": {"comment":"No: its tag removed"},
        "14266": {"comment":"E = the screen line"},
        "14268": {"comment":"Column 0"},
        "14273": {"comment":"The view mode (bits 1-0)"},
        "14278": {"comment":"C = the name's width for the mode"},
        "14285": {"comment":"The long name printed"},
        "14291": {"comment":"D = the column after the name"},
        "14293": {"comment":"A directory? (HL = entry + 7)"},
        "14297": {"comment":"A file"},
        "14299": {"comment":"Column 46"},
        "14305": {"comment":"Type RUN?"},
        "14308": {"comment":"\"<DIR>\""},
        "14313": {"comment":"\"<RUN>\""},
        "14316": {"synopsis":"Prints the bit-7-ended tag at HL.","comment":"Bit-7-ended text printed"},
        "14321": {"synopsis":"A file: the column after the name; then the view mode's detail.","comment":"AT the column after the name"},
        "14325": {"comment":"The view mode"},
        "14330": {"comment":"0: nothing"},
        "14333": {"comment":"1?"},
        "14335": {"comment":"The size"},
        "14340": {"synopsis":"Mode 2: date and time; mode 3 attributes."},
        "14343": {"comment":"2: DE = the time"},
        "14347": {"comment":"BC = the date"},
        "14351": {"comment":"Date and time printed by ROM 1's $3747"},
        "14356": {"synopsis":"Mode 3: the four attribute letters.","comment":"3: the attribute letters at $5B9D"},
        "14360": {"comment":"Past the two spaces"},
        "14362": {"comment":"Four characters"},
        "14367": {"synopsis":"The line coloured; on to the next entry and row.","comment":"The line's normal colour"},
        "14370": {"comment":"B, C back"},
        "14371": {"comment":"HL = the next entry"},
        "14378": {"comment":"A = the next row"},
        "14382": {"comment":"C = the next screen line"},
        "14383": {"synopsis":"One row fewer; more to draw?","comment":"More rows to draw?"},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"$D5E8 = the row; $D5E6 = the page's first entry + 13 * row.","comment":"HL = the page's first entry"},
        "14388": {"comment":"A = the row"},
        "14392": {"comment":"DE = 13 * row"},
        "14397": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "14401": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "14403": {"synopsis":"Four bytes, the columns a long name may take by the view mode in bits 1-0 of $D5EA: 45\n(nothing), 37 (size), 34 (date and time), 45 (attributes). Read by DRAW_ENTRY_ROW."},
        "14407": {"synopsis":"Removes a name tag from the $FF-terminated name at HL (FIND_NAME_TAG): the type, from its\n'.', copied over the tag.\nExit: carry when there is no tag (the name unchanged).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"A tag found?"},
        "14411": {"synopsis":"One character, up to the $FF.","comment":"The type copied over the tag"},
        "14419": {"synopsis":"Looks for a tag of the form '{' ... two hex digits '}' just before the name's type: the hex\nnumber is the tag's length, '{' to '}'.\nEntry: HL = the $FF-terminated name.\nExit: no carry, HL = the type's '.' (or the end) and DE = the tag's '{'; carry when there is\nnone.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC = 0: CPIR looks at up to 64K"},
        "14422": {"comment":"Find the $FF"},
        "14426": {"comment":"DE, HL = the $FF"},
        "14429": {"comment":"BC (minus the length) kept"},
        "14430": {"synopsis":"Backwards for the '.' before the type.","comment":"One back"},
        "14432": {"comment":"The type's '.'?"},
        "14436": {"comment":"Counting to the start"},
        "14437": {"comment":"Before the start?"},
        "14441": {"comment":"No '.': HL = the end"},
        "14444": {"synopsis":"A '}' before the type?"},
        "14445": {"comment":"DE = the '.' (or the end)"},
        "14447": {"comment":"The character before"},
        "14449": {"comment":"'}'?"},
        "14453": {"comment":"E = the low digit"},
        "14458": {"comment":"The high digit"},
        "14461": {"comment":"A = the tag's length"},
        "14465": {"comment":"BC = length - (position + 2)"},
        "14467": {"comment":"Longer than the text before it?"},
        "14471": {"comment":"BC = 3 - length"},
        "14478": {"comment":"HL = where the '{' should be"},
        "14480": {"comment":"'{' there?"},
        "14484": {"comment":"HL = the '.', DE = the '{'"},
        "14485": {"comment":"No carry: a tag"},
        "14487": {"synopsis":"HL one back; A = the hex digit there (0-9, A-F, a-f), or 0 when it is not one.","comment":"One character back"},
        "14489": {"comment":"'0'-'9'?"},
        "14494": {"comment":"'A'-'F'?"},
        "14499": {"comment":"'a'-'f'?"},
        "14504": {"comment":"Not a digit: 0"},
        "14506": {"synopsis":"ENTRY_LFN_AT for the current entry ($D5E6).","comment":"HL = the current entry"},
        "14509": {"synopsis":"Reads the long name of the catalog entry at HL into $DA31 by IDE_GET_LFN, the filespec \"*.*\"\n(from $000B) copied to $D827 first. The directory handle is $D5DD, or $D5DF for a directory\nwhen directories come first (bit 6 of $D5EA).\nExit: as IDE_GET_LFN: carry, BC = date, DE = time, HL:IX = the size."},
        "14510": {"comment":"IX = the files' directory handle"},
        "14514": {"comment":"Bit 7 of byte 7: a directory?"},
        "14522": {"comment":"Directories first (bit 6)?"},
        "14529": {"comment":"IX = the directories' handle"},
        "14533": {"synopsis":"DE = the entry; the filespec to $D827; IDE_GET_LFN.","comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "14534": {"comment":"The filespec \"*.*\" (at $000B)"},
        "14537": {"comment":"... copied to $D827"},
        "14540": {"comment":"BC = the name's buffer"},
        "14543": {"comment":"IDE_GET_LFN (ROM 2): HL filespec, IX handle, DE entry"},
        "14547": {"synopsis":"Key 'r' in the browser: renames the current entry. Its long name is put in the line editor\nwith the cursor before the type, \"New name: \" asked (when the capabilities allow renaming,\nbit 1 of $D5D4), and DOS_RENAME run (DOS_RENAME_DO).","comment":"The current entry's long name"},
        "14551": {"comment":"Into the editor, at most 90 characters"},
        "14559": {"comment":"\"New name: \" if renaming is allowed (bit 1)"},
        "14564": {"comment":"Nothing typed?"},
        "14565": {"comment":"DE = the new name"},
        "14566": {"comment":"HL = the old long name"},
        "14569": {"comment":"Rename it"},
        "14572": {"synopsis":"Puts the name at HL in the line editor's buffer ($E152), at most D characters\n(COPY_TO_EDITBUF), and finds where the cursor goes: before the name tag, or before the type.\nExit: B = the cursor's column, D = the most, E = the length.","comment":"D = the most, kept"},
        "14574": {"comment":"The name to the editor's buffer"},
        "14579": {"comment":"D = the most again"},
        "14582": {"comment":"HL = the '.', DE = a tag's '{'"},
        "14586": {"comment":"DE = the start, HL = where the cursor goes"},
        "14588": {"comment":"B = the cursor's column"},
        "14593": {"synopsis":"Key 'k' in the browser: makes a directory. When the capabilities allow it (bit 2 of $D5D4) a\nname is asked (\"New name: \") and IDE_PATH (make) run; an error is shown (SHOW_DOS_ERROR) and\nthe browser redrawn.","comment":"Making directories allowed (bit 2)? Empty text"},
        "14596": {"comment":"\"New name: \""},
        "14599": {"comment":"Nothing typed?"},
        "14600": {"comment":"Reason 2: make"},
        "14602": {"comment":"IDE_PATH (ROM 2): the directory named at HL"},
        "14605": {"comment":"Error shown, browser redrawn"},
        "14607": {"synopsis":"ASK_NEW_NAME with the cursor at E (an empty text when E = 0).","comment":"B = the cursor"},
        "14608": {"synopsis":"Asks \"New name: \" (INPUT_PROMPTED, at most 90 characters) when the capabilities in $D5D4\nhave one of the bits in D; otherwise returns Z and no carry.\nEntry: B = the cursor, E = the length of the text already in the buffer.","comment":"One of the capability bits in D?"},
        "14613": {"comment":"At most 90 characters"},
        "14615": {"comment":"\"New name: \""},
        "14620": {"synopsis":"INPUT_PROMPTED with the cursor at E."},
        "14621": {"synopsis":"Shows the prompt at HL and edits a line in the buffer at $E152 ($27D5): D = the most\ncharacters, B = the cursor, E = the length of the text already there. The result is copied\nto $D827, $FF-terminated, trailing spaces removed.\nExit: Z and no carry for an empty answer; otherwise carry and HL = its first character other\nthan a space. FLAGS2 bit 5 set.","comment":"The prompt shown"},
        "14628": {"comment":"C = the most, D = the cursor"},
        "14630": {"comment":"B = 4"},
        "14632": {"comment":"The line edited in the buffer at $E152"},
        "14639": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 set"},
        "14643": {"comment":"E = the length typed"},
        "14644": {"comment":"Nothing: Z, no carry"},
        "14647": {"comment":"The buffer's page"},
        "14653": {"comment":"The text copied"},
        "14656": {"comment":"... to $D827, 90 characters"},
        "14667": {"comment":"HL = the length"},
        "14670": {"comment":"HL = the text's end"},
        "14671": {"synopsis":"The $FF put on the last trailing space, backwards.","comment":"$FF there"},
        "14673": {"comment":"The character before"},
        "14675": {"comment":"A trailing space?"},
        "14679": {"comment":"HL = the text's start"},
        "14680": {"synopsis":"Leading spaces skipped.","comment":"A space?"},
        "14683": {"comment":"No: carry, HL = the text"},
        "14685": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "14688": {"synopsis":"Key 'e' in the browser: erases the current entry. When the capabilities allow it (bit 3 of\n$D5D4) and \"Erase <name>?\" is answered Y: a directory by IDE_PATH (delete), a file by\nDOS_DELETE with \"erasing...\" shown; then any error shown and the browser redrawn.","comment":"\"Erase \""},
        "14691": {"comment":"Erasing allowed (bit 3)? Y?"},
        "14696": {"comment":"A file"},
        "14698": {"comment":"A directory: reason 3 (delete)"},
        "14700": {"comment":"IDE_PATH (ROM 2): the directory named at HL"},
        "14703": {"synopsis":"No carry: the error shown (SHOW_DOS_ERROR); then the browser redrawn ($3264).","comment":"Failed: the error shown"},
        "14706": {"synopsis":"The browser redrawn ($3264).","comment":"The browser redrawn"},
        "14709": {"synopsis":"A file: \"erasing...\" shown; DOS_DELETE."},
        "14710": {"comment":"\"erasing...\""},
        "14717": {"comment":"DOS_DELETE (ROM 2): the file named at HL"},
        "14723": {"synopsis":"Key 'f' in the browser: asks \"Filter:\" (at most 14 characters) and filters the listing by\nthe answer, \"*.*\" when it is empty ($3376); the browser redrawn.","comment":"At most 14 characters, cursor at 0"},
        "14726": {"comment":"\"Filter:\""},
        "14732": {"comment":"The filter typed"},
        "14735": {"comment":"Something typed?"},
        "14737": {"comment":"No: \"*.*\""},
        "14740": {"synopsis":"HL = the filter.","comment":"The filter set and the listing read again"},
        "14745": {"synopsis":"Key 'a' in the browser: asks \"User area (0..15): \" (at most 2 characters) and makes the\nnumber typed the default user area by DOS_SET_USER (0 for an empty answer); the browser\nredrawn. A character other than a digit, or a failed call, gives up quietly.","comment":"At most 2 characters, cursor at 0"},
        "14748": {"comment":"\"User area (0..15): \""},
        "14754": {"comment":"E = 0: the user area for an empty answer"},
        "14758": {"comment":"The digits"},
        "14761": {"synopsis":"The next digit into E (E * 10 + digit).","comment":"The next character"},
        "14763": {"comment":"The end ($FF)?"},
        "14767": {"comment":"Below '0': given up"},
        "14771": {"comment":"Above '9': given up"},
        "14775": {"comment":"DE = E * 10"},
        "14777": {"comment":"+ the digit"},
        "14781": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_USER with E.","comment":"A = the user area"},
        "14782": {"comment":"DOS_SET_USER (ROM 2)"},
        "14785": {"comment":"Failed: given up"},
        "14788": {"synopsis":"Key 'o' in the browser: the sort mode (bits 1-0 of $D5EB) one back, 0 wrapping to 3 (when\nsorting is allowed).","comment":"The sort flags"},
        "14792": {"comment":"The bits that make the mode one less"},
        "14799": {"synopsis":"Keys '-' and '+' in the browser: the reverse-sort bit (bit 2 of $D5EB) toggled (when sorting\nis allowed).","comment":"The reverse bit"},
        "14801": {"synopsis":"C = the sort bits to toggle; nothing unless sorting is allowed (SORT_FLAGS_GET).","comment":"No view bits"},
        "14804": {"comment":"Sorting allowed?"},
        "14808": {"comment":"No: nothing"},
        "14811": {"synopsis":"Key '.' in the browser: toggles hiding '.' and '..' (bit 5 of $D5EA).","comment":"Bit 5: hide '.' and '..'"},
        "14813": {"synopsis":"B = the view bits to toggle (in $D5EA), C = the sort bits (in $D5EB).","comment":"No sort bits"},
        "14815": {"synopsis":"The flags toggled and the listing read again ($3363); the browser redrawn.","comment":"Flags toggled, listing read again"},
        "14820": {"synopsis":"Key '{' in the browser: toggles bit 2 of $D5EA (the name tags left on the long names, see\nDRAW_ENTRY_ROW).","comment":"Bit 2"},
        "14824": {"synopsis":"Key 's' in the browser: toggles showing system files (bit 4 of $D5EA).","comment":"Bit 4: system files"},
        "14828": {"synopsis":"Key 'x' in the browser: toggles directories before files (bit 6 of $D5EA).","comment":"Bit 6: directories first"},
        "14832": {"synopsis":"Key 'i' in the browser: the view mode (bits 1-0 of $D5EA) one on, 3 wrapping to 0: nothing,\nsizes, dates and times, attributes. The listing is read again, the status line redrawn and\nthe page redrawn with the same entry selected.","comment":"The view flags"},
        "14835": {"comment":"The bits that make the mode one more"},
        "14841": {"comment":"No sort bits"},
        "14843": {"comment":"Toggled, listing read again"},
        "14846": {"comment":"The status line redrawn"},
        "14849": {"synopsis":"The current entry selected again with the page redrawn (SELECT_REDRAW).","comment":"The current index"},
        "14853": {"comment":"The page redrawn"},
        "14856": {"synopsis":"Key 'n' in the browser: shows the current entry's whole long name on row 10 (lines 2 to 20\ncleared), waits for a key and redraws the page.","comment":"The current entry's long name"},
        "14860": {"comment":"Lines 2 to 20 cleared"},
        "14867": {"comment":"Row 10, column 0"},
        "14873": {"comment":"No width limit"},
        "14875": {"comment":"The whole name printed"},
        "14878": {"comment":"\"Press any key\""},
        "14884": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 set"},
        "14888": {"comment":"A key waited for"},
        "14893": {"synopsis":"Key 'v' in the browser: marks the current entry to be moved (MARK_SOURCE with $D5DC = 2),\nafter \"Move\" is answered Y.","comment":"2: move"},
        "14895": {"comment":"\"Move\" (in ROM 1)"},
        "14900": {"synopsis":"Key 'c' in the browser: marks the current file to be copied (MARK_SOURCE with $D5DC = 1),\nafter \"Copy\" is answered Y. A directory cannot be copied.","comment":"1: copy"},
        "14902": {"comment":"\"Copy\" (in ROM 1)"},
        "14905": {"synopsis":"Marks the current entry as the source of a later paste (key 'p'), when the capabilities\nallow copying (bit 0 of $D5D4) and the question at HL (in ROM 1) is answered Y\n(ASK_IF_ALLOWED):\n1. $D5DC = A, bit 7 set (a paste waits); a directory is refused for a copy (bit 0 of A).\n2. The current path (from $D92C) and the entry's long name stored at $E090, the length of\n   the path in $D5D2.\nExit: carry; FLAGS2 bit 5 set.","comment":"The operation"},
        "14908": {"comment":"Copying allowed (bit 0)? Y?"},
        "14913": {"comment":"HL = the operation"},
        "14916": {"comment":"A file?"},
        "14918": {"comment":"A directory: may be moved, not copied"},
        "14922": {"synopsis":"Bit 7 set: the path and name stored.","comment":"Bit 7: a paste waits"},
        "14924": {"comment":"The entry's long name to $DA31"},
        "14927": {"comment":"The current path"},
        "14931": {"comment":"... to $E090"},
        "14935": {"synopsis":"The end of the path.","comment":"The path's end"},
        "14940": {"comment":"DE = its $FF"},
        "14941": {"comment":"HL = the path's length"},
        "14949": {"comment":"Kept in $D5D2"},
        "14952": {"comment":"The long name after the path"},
        "14958": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 set"},
        "14962": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "14964": {"synopsis":"Key 'p' in the browser: pastes the entry marked by 'c' or 'v' into the current directory.\n1. Nothing unless a paste waits (bit 7 of $D5DC, cleared now).\n2. \"Paste here\"/\"Move here\" (ROM 1 texts) answered Y.\n3. \"Paste as: \" asked, the source's long name offered.\n4. The destination (the current path and the answer) built at $DA31 and copied to $D827.\n5. A move by DOS_RENAME from the path at $E090; a copy by ROM 1's $3EB1 with \"copying...\"\n   shown.\n6. AFTER_DOS_OP.","comment":"The waiting operation"},
        "14968": {"comment":"Bit 7 to carry"},
        "14969": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "14971": {"comment":"No paste waiting"},
        "14972": {"comment":"Copy?"},
        "14974": {"comment":"\"Paste here\""},
        "14979": {"comment":"\"Move here\""},
        "14982": {"synopsis":"The question asked.","comment":"Asked, Y or N"},
        "14985": {"comment":"HL = the source's long name"},
        "14993": {"comment":"Into the editor, at most 90 characters"},
        "14998": {"comment":"\"Paste as: \""},
        "15004": {"comment":"Nothing typed: done"},
        "15006": {"comment":"The destination built at $DA31"},
        "15011": {"comment":"The current path"},
        "15015": {"comment":"Then the new name"},
        "15019": {"comment":"The whole copied to $D827"},
        "15026": {"comment":"DE = the destination"},
        "15027": {"comment":"Copy (bit 0)?"},
        "15033": {"comment":"A move: HL = the source's path and name"},
        "15036": {"synopsis":"DOS_RENAME: HL = the old name, DE = the new one; then AFTER_DOS_OP.","comment":"DOS_RENAME (ROM 2): HL old name, DE new"},
        "15041": {"synopsis":"A copy: \"copying...\" shown, $D7FD = $80; ROM 1's $3EB1.","comment":"$D7FD = $80"},
        "15046": {"comment":"\"copying...\""},
        "15052": {"comment":"The copy, by ROM 1's $3EB1"},
        "15055": {"synopsis":"After a file operation: browser.cfg reloaded (LOAD_SYSCFG), the prompt lines cleared, then\nAFTER_DOS_CALL (the error, if carry is clear, and the browser redrawn).","comment":"The result kept"},
        "15056": {"comment":"browser.cfg read again if needed"},
        "15059": {"comment":"The prompt lines cleared"},
        "15063": {"comment":"Error shown, browser redrawn"},
        "15066": {"synopsis":"Shows the +3DOS error code A as a message: codes 0-9 become $3E-$47, others A + $19, printed\nby ROM 1's $0D1B in FLASH 1 on the prompt lines; then a buzz (CLICK) and a key waited for.","comment":"Codes 0-9?"},
        "15070": {"comment":"Their messages from $3E"},
        "15074": {"synopsis":"Codes 10 and up: A + $19.","comment":"Codes 10 and up: from $23"},
        "15076": {"synopsis":"The prompt lines cleared; the message in FLASH 1."},
        "15077": {"comment":"The prompt lines cleared"},
        "15080": {"comment":"FLASH 1"},
        "15087": {"comment":"The message, by ROM 1's $0D1B"},
        "15090": {"comment":"FLASH 0"},
        "15096": {"comment":"A tone"},
        "15099": {"comment":"A key waited for"},
        "15103": {"synopsis":"Key 'm' in the browser: when the capabilities allow it (bit 4 of $D5D4), the SD card\nremounted through ROM 1's $2BA1 with C = 3; then AFTER_DOS_OP.","comment":"Remounting allowed (bit 4)?"},
        "15109": {"comment":"The prompt lines cleared"},
        "15112": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 set"},
        "15116": {"comment":"C = 3"},
        "15118": {"comment":"Remounted by ROM 1's $2BA1"},
        "15121": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "15124": {"synopsis":"Copies the $FF-terminated text at HL into the line editor's buffer at $E152 (MMU 6 paged by\n$1942 and $27B3 around it), at most D characters.\nExit: E = the length (D = 0).","comment":"The text's start kept"},
        "15125": {"comment":"BC = -1"},
        "15128": {"synopsis":"BC = the text's length.","comment":"Counting to the $FF"},
        "15134": {"comment":"256 or more?"},
        "15138": {"comment":"Fewer than D?"},
        "15142": {"synopsis":"Too long: D characters.","comment":"Too long: D"},
        "15145": {"synopsis":"The copy made with the right page.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "15146": {"comment":"The buffer's page selected"},
        "15152": {"comment":"The editor's buffer"},
        "15158": {"comment":"The text copied"},
        "15161": {"comment":"The page back"},
        "15164": {"comment":"E = the length"},
        "15166": {"synopsis":"Asks the yes/no question at HL (in ROM 1) about the current entry when the capabilities in\n$D5D4 have the bit in E. Returns to its caller only when the capability is there and the\nanswer is Y, with HL = $D827, the entry's short name, and NZ for a directory; otherwise it\nreturns to the caller's caller.","comment":"The capability in E?"},
        "15170": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "15171": {"comment":"No: back to the caller's caller"},
        "15173": {"synopsis":"The prompt lines cleared; ROM 1's $2B6C asks the question at HL and waits for Y or N (Z for\nY). N returns to the caller's caller; Y gives HL = $D827, the current entry's short name\n(COPY_CUR_NAME), NZ for a directory.","comment":"The question"},
        "15174": {"comment":"The prompt lines cleared"},
        "15178": {"comment":"Asked by ROM 1's $2B6C: Z for Y"},
        "15181": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 5 set"},
        "15186": {"comment":"N: back to the caller's caller"},
        "15188": {"comment":"The entry's short name to $D827"},
        "15191": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "15195": {"synopsis":"Prints the $FF-terminated text at $DA31 in at most C columns (no limit for C = $FF): a\nlonger text keeps its first C - 17 characters, a '~' and its last 16. The copy is made at\n$E152 with bank $10 at $E000 (MMU 7), then printed ($272D).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Bank $10 at $E000"},
        "15199": {"comment":"B = the width + 1"},
        "15201": {"comment":"The text"},
        "15204": {"comment":"... copied to $E152"},
        "15209": {"synopsis":"Copies characters until the $FF or the width.","comment":"One character"},
        "15213": {"comment":"The $FF copied?"},
        "15216": {"comment":"Room for more?"},
        "15218": {"synopsis":"Too long: the end of the text found.","comment":"Too long: the text's end"},
        "15223": {"comment":"HL = its last character"},
        "15225": {"comment":"DE = the last place but one"},
        "15227": {"comment":"The last 16 characters"},
        "15232": {"comment":"A '~' before them"},
        "15235": {"synopsis":"MMU 7 back to bank $0F; the copy printed.","comment":"Bank $0F back"},
        "15239": {"comment":"E = the width, HL = the copy"},
        "15241": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15244": {"synopsis":"When the capabilities in $D5D4 have bit 7 (system use: the filetypes from browser.cfg),\nLOAD_BROWSER_CFG.","comment":"System configuration (capability bit 7)?"},
        "15250": {"synopsis":"Reads c:/nextzxos/browser.cfg into $F701 (READ_FILE: at most $7FD bytes, $F701-$FEFF first\nfilled with $FF) and turns its lines into a filetype list: each line's length written in the\nbyte before it ($F700 for the first), a line ending at $0D, $0A or $FF; the file's closing\n$FF becomes an empty last entry, and the $FF filling after it ends the list.","comment":"The buffer"},
        "15254": {"comment":"$7FE bytes; the name \"c:/nextzxos/browser.cfg\""},
        "15260": {"comment":"The file read"},
        "15264": {"synopsis":"One line: its length counted.","comment":"DE = the line's start"},
        "15266": {"comment":"HL = the byte before it"},
        "15267": {"comment":"B counts its characters"},
        "15269": {"synopsis":"The next character; the end of the line?","comment":"The next character"},
        "15271": {"comment":"$FF, $0D or $0A?"},
        "15276": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "15279": {"synopsis":"The length stored; on unless the file ended ($FF).","comment":"The length before the line"},
        "15280": {"comment":"HL = past the line's end"},
        "15281": {"comment":"The $FF (the end)?"},
        "15284": {"comment":"The $FF that ended the file"},
        "15285": {"comment":"Made 0: an empty last entry"},
        "15287": {"synopsis":"READ_TO_C000 with BC = $700 (at most $6FF bytes).","comment":"At most $6FF bytes"},
        "15290": {"synopsis":"READ_FILE into $C000.","comment":"Into $C000"},
        "15301": {"synopsis":"Reads the file named at DE into HL, at most BC - 1 bytes: BC + 1 bytes from HL first filled\nwith $FF; the name copied to $D827 by $0983 (which expands $7F to \"c:/nextzxos/\"); DOS_OPEN\nfile 0 (BC = DE = 1), DOS_READ (C = bank 7), DOS_CLOSE.\nExit: carry and HL = the end of the bytes read; no carry when the file did not open.","comment":"The buffer, size and name kept"},
        "15304": {"comment":"DE = HL + 1"},
        "15307": {"comment":"The buffer filled with $FF"},
        "15311": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "15312": {"comment":"The name expanded to $D827"},
        "15321": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "15324": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "15325": {"comment":"DE = BC = 1"},
        "15330": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN (ROM 2): file 0, exclusive read"},
        "15333": {"comment":"DE = the size"},
        "15334": {"comment":"Less one"},
        "15335": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "15336": {"comment":"Did not open"},
        "15339": {"comment":"B = file 0, C = bank 7"},
        "15342": {"comment":"DOS_READ (ROM 2): DE bytes to HL"},
        "15345": {"comment":"Not all read: DE = the bytes left"},
        "15347": {"comment":"All read"},
        "15350": {"synopsis":"DE = the bytes not read (0 when all were); DOS_CLOSE."},
        "15351": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "15353": {"comment":"DOS_CLOSE (ROM 2)"},
        "15357": {"comment":"HL = the bytes asked for"},
        "15358": {"comment":"Less those not read"},
        "15361": {"comment":"The buffer's start"},
        "15362": {"comment":"HL = the end of what was read"},
        "15363": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "15365": {"synopsis":"Copies the current path ($D92C) to DE (COPY_FF_TEXT).","comment":"The current path"},
        "15368": {"synopsis":"Copies the $FF-terminated text at HL to DE, the $FF too.\nExit: DE at the $FF copied, HL at it in the source.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"One character copied"},
        "15370": {"comment":"The $FF?"},
        "15376": {"synopsis":"Keeps IDE_GET_LFN's details: the date (BC) in $5C74, the time (DE) in $5C3F, the size's low\nword (IX) in $5B6E and high word (HL) in $5B70.\nChanges: nothing else.","comment":"The date"},
        "15380": {"comment":"The time"},
        "15384": {"comment":"The size's low word"},
        "15388": {"comment":"The size's high word"},
        "15392": {"synopsis":"Prints the 32-bit size in $5B6E-$5B71 as 13 characters, right-aligned, with commas between\ngroups of three digits and spaces for leading zeros, by the powers of ten at POWERS_OF_TEN.","comment":"HL = the size's low word"},
        "15395": {"comment":"DE = its high word"},
        "15399": {"comment":"The powers of ten"},
        "15403": {"comment":"A = ' ': no digit yet"},
        "15405": {"comment":"Nine powers"},
        "15407": {"synopsis":"One power of ten: a comma (or a space while no digit has been printed) where the table says;\nthen the digit."},
        "15408": {"comment":"A separator before this digit?"},
        "15414": {"comment":"Still blank?"},
        "15416": {"comment":"Then a space"},
        "15419": {"comment":"Otherwise a comma"},
        "15421": {"synopsis":"The separator printed.","comment":"Printed"},
        "15425": {"synopsis":"The power taken off the size while it goes, the digit counted up.","comment":"BC = the power's low word"},
        "15431": {"comment":"DE:HL less it"},
        "15435": {"comment":"BC = its high word, the flag off"},
        "15446": {"comment":"Went below 0?"},
        "15448": {"comment":"The digit one more"},
        "15449": {"comment":"From ' '?"},
        "15453": {"comment":"Then '1'"},
        "15457": {"synopsis":"One subtraction too many: the power added back; the digit printed.","comment":"The power added back"},
        "15476": {"comment":"The digit printed"},
        "15479": {"comment":"Still blank?"},
        "15483": {"comment":"The next digit counts from '0'"},
        "15485": {"synopsis":"The next table entry.","comment":"The next power"},
        "15491": {"comment":"All nine?"},
        "15493": {"comment":"The units digit"},
        "15498": {"synopsis":"Nine 32-bit powers of ten, 1,000,000,000 down to 10, low word first; bit 7 of the high word\nset on 100,000,000, 100,000 and 100 marks a comma before that digit. Read by\nPRINT_FILE_SIZE."},
        "15534": {"synopsis":"Builds \"  dasp  \" at $5B9D from the attribute bits of the entry bytes at HL (bit 7 of each):\nthe first gives 'd', the fourth 'a', the third 's', the second 'p'; a letter is '-' when its\nbit is clear.\nEntry: HL = entry + 7.\nExit: DE = $5B9D.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "15535": {"comment":"The first byte's bit 7"},
        "15540": {"comment":"Bit 0"},
        "15541": {"synopsis":"The second byte: bit 3.","comment":"The second byte's bit 7"},
        "15546": {"comment":"Bit 3"},
        "15548": {"synopsis":"The third byte: bit 2.","comment":"The third byte's bit 7"},
        "15553": {"comment":"Bit 2"},
        "15555": {"synopsis":"The fourth byte: bit 1.","comment":"The fourth byte's bit 7"},
        "15560": {"comment":"Bit 1"},
        "15562": {"synopsis":"The text built, a letter or '-' for each bit from bit 0.","comment":"B, C = the bits"},
        "15564": {"comment":"The text at $5B9D"},
        "15568": {"comment":"Two spaces"},
        "15574": {"comment":"'d' (bit 0)"},
        "15579": {"comment":"'a' (bit 1)"},
        "15584": {"comment":"'s' (bit 2)"},
        "15589": {"comment":"'p' (bit 3)"},
        "15594": {"comment":"Two spaces"},
        "15601": {"synopsis":"Puts the letter in A at DE, or '-' when bit 0 of C (shifted out) is clear.","comment":"The bit set?"},
        "15605": {"comment":"No: '-'"},
        "15607": {"synopsis":"The character stored; DE on."},
        "15610": {"synopsis":"The browser's key table, read by $15A1 from $2C77: three bytes per key, the key code then\nthe routine's address, ended by $FF. Enter and '0' $30AA, 'e' KEY_ERASE, 'c' KEY_COPY, 'r'\nKEY_RENAME, 'v' KEY_MOVE, $0E $2E9E, $0A and '6' KEY_DOWN, $09 and '8' KEY_PAGE_DOWN, 'h'\nKEY_SEARCH, 'n' KEY_NAME, then BROWSER_KEYS_FEW."},
        "15649": {"synopsis":"The keys that work on an empty listing too (from $2C72 when $D5E2 = 0): $0B and '7' KEY_UP,\n$08 and '5' KEY_PAGE_UP, space $31D7, 'd' KEY_DRIVE, 'm' KEY_REMOUNT, 'k' KEY_MAKE_DIR, 'u'\nKEY_UNMOUNT, 'f' KEY_FILTER, 'p' KEY_PASTE, $07 $3255, 'l' $3243, '.' KEY_DOTS, 's'\nKEY_SYSTEM, 'i' KEY_INFO_MODE, 'x' KEY_DIRS_FIRST, 'o' KEY_SORT_MODE, '-' and '+'\nKEY_SORT_DIR, 'a' KEY_USER_AREA, 'g' $3024, '{' KEY_RESERVED_B2; $FF."},
        "15719": {"synopsis":"Two key entries copied by $2EB4 to the start of the key table built at $D827: space $2F9B,\n$0E $2FA9."},
        "15725": {"synopsis":"Prints the CPU speed choice ($D5BB, 0-3) at row 6, column 8 ($07B5 with A = $FF): its text\nfrom SPEED_TEXTS by SPEED_OFFSETS.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"Row 6, column 8"},
        "15730": {"comment":"The speed choice"},
        "15733": {"comment":"HL = its offset byte"},
        "15742": {"comment":"BC = the offset"},
        "15743": {"comment":"HL = its text"},
        "15744": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "15747": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "15749": {"synopsis":"Four offsets, each from its own byte to the speed's text in SPEED_TEXTS."},
        "15753": {"synopsis":"The CPU speed choices, each $FF-ended: \" 3.5MHz >\", \"<  7MHz >\", \"< 14MHz >\", \"< 28MHz  \"."},
        "15793": {"synopsis":"Waits for an interrupt (HALT) and reads NextReg $07: A = the CPU speed, 0-3.\nExit: BC = $253B (the NextReg data port).\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Wait for an interrupt"},
        "15794": {"comment":"NextReg $07: the CPU speed"},
        "15799": {"comment":"0-3"},
        "15802": {"synopsis":"The CPU speed choice ($D5BB) one higher, at most 3, and shown (SHOW_SPEED).","comment":"The choice one higher"},
        "15806": {"comment":"Past 3?"},
        "15809": {"synopsis":"$D5BB = A; shown.","comment":"Stored and shown"},
        "15814": {"synopsis":"The CPU speed choice ($D5BB) one lower, at least 0, and shown.","comment":"The choice one lower"},
        "15818": {"comment":"Below 0?"},
        "15821": {"synopsis":"Runs ROM 3's TONE_OUT (DE, HL as it takes them) with the CPU at 3.5MHz (NextReg $07 = 0), so\nthat the tone's pitch and length do not depend on the speed; the speed put back afterwards.","comment":"A = the CPU speed now"},
        "15825": {"comment":"NextReg $07 = 0: 3.5MHz"},
        "15828": {"comment":"ROM 3's TONE_OUT"},
        "15831": {"comment":"The speed back"},
        "15836": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 1 with the alternate ROM enabled\n(NextReg $8C = $80 by $007B), then on return passes through $007B again and selects ROM 1\n($3E93). BC kept ($5B54). No caller in this page.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "15840": {"comment":"BC = the word after the CALL; past it"},
        "15846": {"comment":"Last: back to ROM 1"},
        "15850": {"comment":"Before it: $007B again"},
        "15854": {"comment":"The address to run"},
        "15855": {"comment":"First: the alternate ROM on"},
        "15862": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3DFF."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 2 (NextReg $8E = 2), with $3E13 (back to\nROM 2) as its way back. BC kept through $5B54. Reached by RST $20.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "15876": {"comment":"BC = the word after the CALL; past it"},
        "15882": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 2 selected"},
        "15886": {"comment":"The address to run"},
        "15887": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "15891": {"synopsis":"Selects ROM 2 (NextReg $8E = 2); also the way back of CALL_ROM2.","comment":"ROM 2 selected"},
        "15896": {"synopsis":"A click of RASP / 2 (CLICK_A with HL = $0C80).","comment":"RASP / 2"},
        "15901": {"comment":"The pitch"},
        "15904": {"synopsis":"A short tone: DE = A, HL as given, at 3.5MHz (TONE_3M5). Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "15906": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "15909": {"synopsis":"TONE_3M5; IX back.","comment":"The tone at 3.5MHz"},
        "15915": {"synopsis":"A tone with DE = $30 and HL = $0300, at 3.5MHz (TONE_3M5). Keeps IX.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "15917": {"comment":"The length"},
        "15920": {"comment":"The pitch"},
        "15925": {"synopsis":"Shows a message in the lower screen:\n1. ATTR_P set to BORDCR's value while the lower screen is made ready ($0EC9) and stream -3\n   selected (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT).\n2. The $FF-terminated text at HL printed.\n3. With Z on entry, a C, R or I key waited for (E = 0, 1, 2); otherwise any key ($11E0).\n4. The lower screen made ready again, stream -2 selected.\nExit: A = E. No caller in this page.","comment":"The flags (Z: ask) and the text kept"},
        "15927": {"comment":"ATTR_P kept"},
        "15931": {"comment":"ATTR_P = BORDCR's value"},
        "15937": {"comment":"The lower screen made ready"},
        "15940": {"comment":"A = -3"},
        "15942": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: the lower screen"},
        "15945": {"comment":"ATTR_P back"},
        "15950": {"synopsis":"One character of the text, until the $FF.","comment":"One character"},
        "15952": {"comment":"The $FF?"},
        "15959": {"synopsis":"The text printed: an answer, or any key.","comment":"Z: an answer wanted"},
        "15962": {"comment":"Any key"},
        "15965": {"synopsis":"The lower screen made ready, stream -2, A = E.","comment":"The key kept"},
        "15966": {"comment":"The lower screen made ready"},
        "15969": {"comment":"A = -2"},
        "15971": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT: the upper screen"},
        "15975": {"comment":"A = E"},
        "15977": {"synopsis":"Waits for C (E = 0), R (1) or I (2), in either case.","comment":"A key"},
        "15980": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "15982": {"comment":"'C': E = 0"},
        "15988": {"comment":"'R': E = 1"},
        "15993": {"comment":"'I': E = 2"},
        "15998": {"comment":"Anything else: again"},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in ROM 1 (NextReg $8E = 1), with $3E93 (back to\nROM 1) as its way back. BC kept through $5B54. Reached by RST $18.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "16004": {"comment":"BC = the word after the CALL; past it"},
        "16010": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 1 selected"},
        "16014": {"comment":"The address to run"},
        "16015": {"synopsis":"BC back from $5B54; ROM 1 selected; on to the address on the stack.","comment":"BC back"},
        "16019": {"synopsis":"Selects ROM 1 (NextReg $8E = 1); also the way back of CALL_ROM1.","comment":"ROM 1 selected"},
        "16024": {"synopsis":"Finds the string array of the current channel V (its letter at +$0F of the channel, looked\nup by ROM 3's GET_CHAR and LV_LETTER ($28BC) with CH_ADD pointed at it). Error $12 unless it\nis a one-dimensional string array.\nExit: DE = its first character, BC = its length, HL = the position (the word at +$0D); carry\nwhen the position is inside the array.","comment":"CH_ADD kept"},
        "16028": {"comment":"HL = the channel's +$0F: the letter"},
        "16035": {"comment":"CH_ADD there"},
        "16038": {"comment":"The channel's +$0F kept, CH_ADD too"},
        "16040": {"comment":"The alternate registers kept"},
        "16045": {"comment":"ROM 3's GET_CHAR: A = the letter"},
        "16048": {"comment":"ROM 3's LV_LETTER at $28BC: the variable"},
        "16051": {"comment":"The alternate registers back"},
        "16056": {"comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "16061": {"comment":"No such variable: error $12"},
        "16064": {"comment":"A string array?"},
        "16071": {"comment":"Past its length to its dimensions"},
        "16074": {"comment":"One dimension?"},
        "16077": {"synopsis":"One dimension, or error $12.","comment":"Otherwise error $12"},
        "16080": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "16084": {"comment":"DE = its first character"},
        "16085": {"comment":"HL = the channel's +$0F"},
        "16086": {"comment":"HL = the position (the word at +$0D)"},
        "16091": {"comment":"Inside the array? (carry)"},
        "16096": {"synopsis":"A channel V's input: A = the character at the position, and the position one on; error $07\npast the end.","comment":"The array and the position"},
        "16099": {"comment":"Past the end: error $07"},
        "16101": {"comment":"The character there"},
        "16103": {"synopsis":"The position (the word at +$0D) one on; carry set.","comment":"HL = the channel's +$0D"},
        "16110": {"comment":"The position one on"},
        "16117": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "16119": {"synopsis":"A channel V's output: A put at the position, and the position one on; error $07 past the\nend.","comment":"The character kept"},
        "16120": {"comment":"The array and the position"},
        "16123": {"synopsis":"Past the end: error $07.","comment":"Past the end: error $07"},
        "16126": {"comment":"Its place"},
        "16127": {"comment":"The character stored"},
        "16131": {"synopsis":"A channel V's position operation, by B: 0 gives the position in DE:HL; 1 sets it from DE:HL\n(error $07 when DE is not 0 or it is past the end); 2 and up give the length in DE:HL.","comment":"DE:HL kept"},
        "16133": {"comment":"A = B, the operation"},
        "16135": {"comment":"The array and the position"},
        "16139": {"comment":"0?"},
        "16142": {"comment":"0: DE:HL = 0:position"},
        "16148": {"synopsis":"1 sets the position; 2 and up give the length (VCH_PTR_LEN).","comment":"1?"},
        "16151": {"comment":"The high word must be 0"},
        "16157": {"comment":"HL = the new position"},
        "16159": {"comment":"Past the end?"},
        "16163": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "16165": {"comment":"Stored at the channel's +$0D"},
        "16176": {"synopsis":"2 or more: DE:HL = the array's length.","comment":"2 or more: DE:HL = 0:length"},
        "16184": {"synopsis":"Draws the editor's title bar (DRAW_TITLE_BAR) from the menu text for $D5B8 = 0 ($0A15) or\notherwise $0A23, the colours at $D6DA; nothing when $D5B8 = 8.","comment":"The editor's mode"},
        "16187": {"comment":"8: no bar"},
        "16190": {"comment":"The menu for mode 0"},
        "16196": {"comment":"For the others"},
        "16199": {"synopsis":"DE = $D6DA.","comment":"The colours"},
        "16202": {"synopsis":"Draws a title bar on line 21:\n1. The UDGs pointed at $0DF7 for the time ($0E50).\n2. Lines $15-$17 cleared ($1274).\n3. IX = the window record for the screen mode (bits 3-0 of $5C7F, 0 taken as 5): ($F2 +\n   mode) * 256.\n4. TITLE_CTRL_START, code $18 with byte 7 of the colours at DE, code $14 with 0 and 26\n   spaces (with 1 and 57 spaces when bit 3 of $5C7F is set).\n5. Six stripes: code $18 with bytes 1-6 of the colours, the UDG characters $90 and $91 in\n   turn between them (one before the first too when bit 3 is set).\n6. TITLE_CTRL_END; the UDGs back.\n7. The first menu item's name from HL, up to ':' or a control code, its '_' marks dropped;\n   then the codes at $0023 with byte 0 of the colours.\nEntry: HL = the menu text, DE = the 8 colour bytes.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "16204": {"comment":"The menu text, the colours kept"},
        "16206": {"comment":"UDG = $0DF7 for the bar's graphics"},
        "16209": {"comment":"The old UDG kept"},
        "16211": {"comment":"Lines $15-$17 cleared"},
        "16214": {"comment":"The screen mode"},
        "16219": {"comment":"0 taken as 5"},
        "16223": {"synopsis":"IX = ($F2 + mode) * 256.","comment":"IX = the window record for the mode"},
        "16230": {"comment":"The bar's opening codes"},
        "16238": {"comment":"Byte 7: the bar's colour (code $18's value)"},
        "16246": {"comment":"Code $14"},
        "16251": {"comment":"Wide screen (bit 3 of $5C7F)?"},
        "16255": {"comment":"... 0, then 26 spaces"},
        "16260": {"comment":"... 1, then 57 spaces"},
        "16263": {"synopsis":"The first character (C), then B spaces."},
        "16264": {"comment":"Code $14's value"},
        "16269": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "16270": {"comment":"A space"},
        "16276": {"comment":"Until all printed"},
        "16278": {"comment":"DE = the colours"},
        "16279": {"comment":"Byte 0 kept"},
        "16281": {"comment":"Z when the bar was wide"},
        "16282": {"comment":"Six stripes; first character $90"},
        "16285": {"synopsis":"One stripe: its colour, its character."},
        "16287": {"comment":"The stripe's character (wide bar: also first)"},
        "16291": {"comment":"Code $18"},
        "16299": {"comment":"The next stripe's colour"},
        "16305": {"comment":"$90 and $91 in turn"},
        "16309": {"comment":"Z: the character before each next stripe"},
        "16312": {"comment":"The closing codes"},
        "16318": {"comment":"A = byte 0 of the colours"},
        "16319": {"comment":"The UDG back"},
        "16323": {"comment":"HL = the menu text"},
        "16325": {"synopsis":"The next character of the item's name.","comment":"The next character"},
        "16327": {"comment":"':' ends the name"},
        "16331": {"comment":"So does a control code"},
        "16335": {"comment":"'_' (the key mark) dropped"},
        "16340": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "16346": {"synopsis":"The text at $0023 and the colour at DE+0.","comment":"The codes at $0023 (bit 7 ended)"},
        "16352": {"comment":"Their value: byte 0 of the colours"},
        "16359": {"synopsis":"Window codes printed before the bar by DRAW_TITLE_BAR: $1E $08, $16 $15 $00 (row 21, column\n0), $18 (its value following in the code), $FF."},
        "16366": {"synopsis":"Window codes printed after the stripes by DRAW_TITLE_BAR: a space, $16 $15 $00 (row 21,\ncolumn 0), $FF."},
        "16371": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3FFF."}
      }
    },
