      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"RST $00: calls the routine in ROM 2 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word: NOP, then JP $3F00 (the ROM 2 stub, which reads the word through the return\naddress and pages ROM 2 with NextReg $8E). The NextZXOS API calls (IDE_..., DOS_...) are\nmade this way."},
        "1": {"comment":"The word after the RST is the routine in ROM 2"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: stops with an error; the byte after the RST holds the error code (the report minus\none, as in ROM 3: $0B is report C). On at $0DA3.","comment":"The code is the byte after the RST"},
        "16": {"synopsis":"RST $10: runs a function chosen by the byte after the RST (with bit 7 set a word follows it,\nkept at $5B54-style in $5B5A by $0E77). HL is kept at $5B52 and AF pushed; the dispatcher at\n$0E77 reads the byte through the return address, pages this ROM into MMU slot 1 and takes\nthe routine from the word table at $3E00 (two entries, both $3439 in this page). Only $0517\nhas the byte pattern of an RST $10 in this range, and it lies in SYNTAX_ENTRIES (data).","comment":"HL kept for the function"},
        "19": {"comment":"HL = the address of the function byte"},
        "21": {"comment":"On to the dispatcher"},
        "24": {"synopsis":"RST $18: SP swapped with the one kept at $5B6A and RAM bank 7 paged in at $C000 (NextReg $8E\n= $78), through $2B05. RST $30 undoes it.","comment":"Alternate SP and bank 7"},
        "27": {"synopsis":"LDIR, then RET. Reached from page 2's LDIR_ROM_1 ($0E94), which pushes $001B as the address to\nrun in this ROM."},
        "30": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $10 (report H, \"STOP in INPUT\"). Page 0 calls it as ROM 1's $001E (its\nRST $18 with the word $001E at $293F)."},
        "32": {"synopsis":"RST $20: CH_ADD + 1, then on past what is skipped (spaces, most control codes and their\noperands) by $3ECF; A = the character. ENTER and $0E (a number's marker) are returned, not\nskipped. The same job as ROM 3's NEXT_SKIP.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "35": {"comment":"Past it and past what is skipped"},
        "40": {"synopsis":"RST $28: calls the routine in ROM 3 whose address is the word after the RST, then returns\npast the word: BC kept at $5B54, HL exchanged with the return address, and on at $2CF7 (ROM\n3 paged through $5B48, back through $5B3E, which pages this ROM).","comment":"BC kept while the word is read"},
        "44": {"comment":"HL = the word's address; HL kept on the stack"},
        "45": {"comment":"On to the paging"},
        "48": {"synopsis":"RST $30: SP swapped back with the one kept at $5B6A and RAM bank 0 paged in at $C000,\nthrough $2AEE. Undoes RST $18.","comment":"Back to the main SP and bank 0"},
        "56": {"synopsis":"INT (interrupt mode 1), with this ROM paged in: AF and HL pushed, H = 0, A = $80, then\nDIVMMC_ON: port $E3 = $80 puts the DivMMC memory (bank 0) at $0000-$1FFF, and the interrupt\ngoes on in that memory from $0048. INT_EXIT ($0060) pops the two registers again.","comment":"Kept for INT_EXIT"},
        "58": {"comment":"H = 0"},
        "60": {"comment":"DivMMC memory on, its bank 0"},
        "70": {"synopsis":"Port $E3 = A (from INT_DIVMMC, $80): the DivMMC memory replaces this ROM at $0000-$1FFF, so\nthe next instruction is fetched from the DivMMC memory's $0048, not from the bytes here.","comment":"From the next fetch on, DivMMC memory at $0000"},
        "72": {"synopsis":"The text \"C:/DOT/FM\" ended by $FF ($0048-$0051). Never executed (DIVMMC_ON has paged the\nDivMMC memory in by then), and nothing in this page reads it."},
        "82": {"synopsis":"Takes the last value off the calculator stack ($3842: A, E, D, C, B its five bytes) and\ntests it: Z when the first four bytes are all 0 (B, the fifth, not tested). Called from\n$1CEE, $1CFE, $1D14, $1D6A, $2075, $208B.\nExit: A = the OR of the four bytes; B, C, D, E the value.","comment":"A, E, D, C, B = the value taken off"},
        "85": {"comment":"Z: the first four bytes all 0?"},
        "89": {"synopsis":"Calls the DivMMC memory's $299C (through $26CB), then returns. Called from $3E76.","comment":"DivMMC memory's $299C"},
        "96": {"synopsis":"The end of an interrupt: HL and AF back (as INT_DIVMMC pushed them), interrupts on, RET.\nNothing in this page jumps here.","comment":"As INT_DIVMMC pushed them"},
        "98": {"comment":"Interrupts back on"},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI: RETN at once."},
        "104": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine in the alternate ROM whose address is the word after the CALL (ROM select\nleft at 1), then returns past the word:\n1. BC kept at $5B54; BC = the word.\n2. $007B pushed as the way back, then the routine.\n3. BC back; ALT_ROM_ON pages the alternate ROM in and its RET enters the routine. The\n   routine returns to the alternate ROM's own $007B, which must page it out again.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "108": {"comment":"HL = the address of the word after the CALL"},
        "109": {"comment":"BC = the word, the routine's address"},
        "113": {"comment":"Return address past the word; HL back"},
        "114": {"synopsis":"CALL_ALT's second half with BC = the routine: the way back and the routine pushed, then\nALT_ROM_ON. CLASS_E jumps here for a routine word with bits 7-6 = 10.","comment":"Way back: the alternate ROM's $007B"},
        "118": {"comment":"The routine, entered by RET"},
        "119": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "123": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8C = $80 (the alternate ROM replaces the ROM for reads), then RET. Entered by RET\nfrom CALL_ALT and CALL_ALT_ROM0, and the end of CALL_ALT itself.","comment":"Alternate ROM on, read in place of the ROM"},
        "127": {"comment":"Into the routine"},
        "128": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine in the alternate ROM whose address is the word after the CALL, with ROM\nselect 0 (ROM 0's position), then returns past the word:\n1. BC = the word.\n2. Pushed, last-run first: $3E93 (the way back to this ROM), $007B, the routine, $007B.\n3. JP $3E8F: BC back and NextReg $8E = 0; the RET at $3E97 runs in ROM 0, whose $007B pages\n   the alternate ROM in and enters the routine.\n4. The routine returns through the alternate ROM's $007B, then $3E93 pages ROM 1 back.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "132": {"comment":"HL = the address of the word after the CALL"},
        "133": {"comment":"BC = the routine's address"},
        "137": {"comment":"Return address past the word; HL back"},
        "138": {"comment":"Last way back: $3E93 pages ROM 1"},
        "142": {"comment":"Then the alternate ROM's $007B"},
        "146": {"comment":"The routine"},
        "147": {"comment":"First: ROM 0's $007B pages the alternate ROM in"},
        "151": {"comment":"BC back, ROM 0 paged; its RET runs the chain"},
        "154": {"synopsis":"Token $A3 followed by ATTR, INK, PAPER, BRIGHT or FLASH and a number (class 0, entries\n$0533-$054B), when running: sets that field of an attribute byte kept for ROM 2.\nEntry: DE = the high byte of the word after class 0; the two bytes after it are the field's\nlargest value and its bit position + 1 (ATTR $FF,1; INK 7,1; PAPER 7,4; BRIGHT 1,7; FLASH\n1,8).\n1. A = the number ($3823, 0-255); above the largest value is report K.\n2. Value and mask moved up to the field's bits.\n3. In bank 7: the byte from ROM 2's $006D (HL = $3760), the field replaced, the byte to ROM\n   2's $0072; bank 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"DE = the field's two parameter bytes"},
        "156": {"comment":"A = the number, 0-255"},
        "159": {"comment":"C = the largest value, B = bit position + 1"},
        "163": {"comment":"D = the value"},
        "164": {"comment":"Above the largest value?"},
        "168": {"comment":"Report K, \"Invalid colour\""},
        "170": {"synopsis":"Value and mask one bit up, until B is used up.","comment":"Shifted far enough?"},
        "173": {"comment":"Value and mask one bit up"},
        "179": {"synopsis":"In bank 7: the byte read, the field replaced, the byte written back.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "180": {"comment":"C = the mask inverted: the bits kept"},
        "183": {"comment":"HL = $3760: which byte ROM 2 reads and writes"},
        "186": {"comment":"ROM 2's $006D (not in the API list): A = the byte"},
        "189": {"comment":"The field cleared and the new value put in"},
        "191": {"comment":"ROM 2's $0072: the byte written back"},
        "194": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "196": {"synopsis":"Token $A3 with no sub-keyword after it (class $0E, its entry at $0530):\n1. At the statement's end (STMT_END_TEST) A = $10.\n2. Otherwise an expression (SCAN_EXPR through $0DFC); checking ends here (STATEMENT_END). A\n   string goes to A3_FILE; a number must be 48 (A = $18 after RRCA), else report A ($334E).\n3. Running, A3_RUN: in bank 7, ROM 2's $0D70 with A; a clear carry is an error (A3_ERROR).\n4. The machine restarted: bank 0, A' kept for NextReg $8C, $5B5C = 0, NSPPC = $FF, FLAGS bit\n   4 cleared, a $3E at RAMTOP and SP below it, $1303 pushed and ERR_SP pointing at it, FLAGS\n   bit 1 set; then COPY_TO_5BB8 runs RAM_SWITCH_CODE at $5BB8 with HL = $006B, DE = $5B00,\n   BC = $0058 for its LDIR.","comment":"At the statement's end?"},
        "199": {"comment":"A = $10 for no number"},
        "203": {"comment":"Otherwise the expression"},
        "206": {"comment":"Checking ends here"},
        "209": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "215": {"comment":"A = the number, 0-255"},
        "218": {"comment":"Only 48 gives $18"},
        "221": {"comment":"Any other number: report A"},
        "224": {"synopsis":"Running: ROM 2's $0D70 with A ($10, or $18 for 48) in bank 7; then the restart.","comment":"Checking ends here"},
        "227": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "228": {"comment":"ROM 2's $0D70 (not in the API list), with A"},
        "231": {"comment":"Carry clear: an error"},
        "233": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "234": {"comment":"A kept for NextReg $8C","synopsis":"A3_RUN past its RST $30: the restart, with ROM 2's result in A' and E. Nothing in this page\njumps here: the JP $00EA at $01C1 runs from RAM with the alternate ROM read, so it lands in\nthe alternate ROM's $00EA."},
        "235": {"comment":"$5B5C = 0"},
        "239": {"comment":"NSPPC = $FF"},
        "243": {"comment":"A = E, for NextReg $82"},
        "244": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 4 cleared"},
        "248": {"comment":"HL = RAMTOP"},
        "251": {"comment":"A $3E byte there, the stack below it"},
        "255": {"comment":"$1303 the return address under ERR_SP"},
        "259": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "263": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 1 set"},
        "267": {"comment":"HL, DE, BC for the LDIR at $5BC4"},
        "276": {"comment":"The other set: the copy to $5BB8"},
        "277": {"comment":"RAM_SWITCH_CODE, $1C bytes"},
        "283": {"comment":"Copied and run"},
        "285": {"synopsis":"Token $A3 with a string: the name copied from bank 0 to bank 7's $DA31 ($2B1C) with $FF\nafter it; $14A9 with A = 0; ROM 2's IDE_SNAPLOAD ($00FD: loads and runs the snapshot, HL =\nthe name ended by $FF). If it comes back, its error (A3_ERROR).","comment":"DE = the string's start, BC its length"},
        "289": {"comment":"To bank 7's $DA31"},
        "295": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "296": {"comment":"$FF after the name"},
        "299": {"comment":"$14A9 with A = 0"},
        "303": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "306": {"comment":"IDE_SNAPLOAD: a return is an error"},
        "309": {"synopsis":"The error ROM 2 returned in A, through $0DCE (bank 0, then FILE_ERROR_A with the code byte\n$FF: A's error).","comment":"ROM 2's error in A"},
        "312": {"synopsis":"Token $A3 LOAD (class $0C, entry $0553), when running:\n1. In bank 7, ROM 2's $0D70 with A = $10; a clear carry is an error (A3_ERROR).\n2. Interrupts' enables cleared (NextReg $C4 = 0), SP = $5BFF.\n3. RAM banks 7 down to 0 paged at $C000 in turn (port $7FFD, bit 4 set) and filled with 0,\n   keeping bank 5's $C000-$DAFF; FRAMES kept round it.\n4. A = E; RAM_RESET_CODE copied to $5BB8 and run there (COPY_TO_5BB8).","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "313": {"comment":"ROM 2's $0D70 with A = $10"},
        "318": {"comment":"Carry clear: an error"},
        "321": {"comment":"Interrupt enables off"},
        "325": {"comment":"A stack in low RAM"},
        "328": {"comment":"FRAMES kept in IX and L"},
        "336": {"comment":"Bank 7 first"},
        "341": {"synopsis":"One RAM bank (H - 1) paged at $C000 and filled with 0.","comment":"A = the bank, with ROM bit 4"},
        "345": {"comment":"Paged at $C000"},
        "348": {"comment":"The whole 16K"},
        "357": {"comment":"Bank 5?"},
        "361": {"comment":"From $DB00 only: bank 5's $C000-$DAFF kept"},
        "366": {"synopsis":"The fill: L (0) into the first byte, then LDIR.","comment":"L = 0 into each byte"},
        "370": {"comment":"The next bank down"},
        "373": {"comment":"FRAMES back"},
        "381": {"comment":"A = E, for NextReg $82"},
        "383": {"comment":"RAM_RESET_CODE, $38 bytes"},
        "389": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL to $5BB8 and runs them there (the RET goes to $5BB8), with the other\nregister set exchanged in first.","comment":"To $5BB8, run there"},
        "395": {"comment":"The other set for the code"},
        "397": {"synopsis":"Code run at $5BB8 (copied by A3_CMD, $1C bytes): ROM 3 selected (NextReg $8E = 3), NextReg\n$82 = A (E from ROM 2's $0D70), NextReg $8C = A' (its A); $1B76 pushed; with bit 5 of A' set\n(ROM 1 locked) JP $0EDF, in the ROM now paged; otherwise $5B43 (ROM 2), the LDIR (HL =\n$006B, DE = $5B00, BC = $0058: the RAM routines refreshed from ROM 2) and JP $5B00.","comment":"ROM 3 selected"},
        "401": {"comment":"Port decoding enables"},
        "405": {"comment":"Alternate ROM setting"},
        "408": {"comment":"Return address for what follows"},
        "412": {"comment":"Bit 5: ROM 1 locked?"},
        "414": {"comment":"JP $0EDF in the paged ROM, not here"},
        "417": {"comment":"ROM 2 through the RAM routine"},
        "420": {"comment":"$58 bytes from $006B to $5B00"},
        "422": {"comment":"Into them"},
        "425": {"synopsis":"Code run at $5BB8 (copied by A3_LOAD, $38 bytes):\n1. ROM 3 selected, NextReg $82 = A, port $7FFD = 0.\n2. With the alternate ROM visible only to writes (NextReg $8C = $C0), its word at $25C6 =\n   $5BD3 (RAM_HOOK_CODE's copy); then NextReg $8C = $80 and JP $00EA, in the alternate ROM.","comment":"ROM 3 selected"},
        "429": {"comment":"Port decoding enables"},
        "432": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = 0"},
        "435": {"comment":"Alternate ROM seen by writes only"},
        "439": {"comment":"Its word at $25C6 = $5BD3, the hook below"},
        "445": {"comment":"Alternate ROM read again"},
        "449": {"comment":"JP $00EA in the alternate ROM, not here"},
        "452": {"synopsis":"Part of RAM_RESET_CODE, run at $5BD3 when the alternate ROM goes through its word at $25C6:\ndrops its return address, puts $36A8 back into that word (NextReg $8C = $C0 while writing),\nselects NextReg $24 at port $243B, sets NextReg $C4 = $81 and goes on at $2831 (in the\nalternate ROM).","comment":"Its return address dropped"},
        "453": {"comment":"Alternate ROM seen by writes only"},
        "457": {"comment":"The word at $25C6 back to $36A8"},
        "463": {"comment":"Alternate ROM read again"},
        "467": {"comment":"NextReg $24 selected"},
        "474": {"comment":"Interrupt enables: ULA and expansion bus"},
        "478": {"comment":"In the alternate ROM"},
        "481": {"synopsis":"Token $A3 SCREEN$ with two numbers (class 8, then $0C; entry $054C), when running: the\nsecond must be 0-127 and the first 0 or 1 (report B otherwise); $5C81 = the second + 128 x\nthe first; then the DivMMC memory's $2250 with HL = $2252.","comment":"A = the second number"},
        "484": {"comment":"Above 127: report B"},
        "486": {"synopsis":"Report B when NC (the number too big)."},
        "490": {"comment":"A = the first number"},
        "493": {"comment":"Above 1: report B"},
        "497": {"comment":"Its bit 0 into carry"},
        "498": {"comment":"A = the second number again"},
        "502": {"comment":"The first one's 1 as bit 7"},
        "504": {"synopsis":"$5C81 = the value; the DivMMC memory's $2250 with HL = $2252.","comment":"Kept at $5C81"},
        "507": {"comment":"HL = $2252 for it"},
        "510": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $2250"},
        "516": {"synopsis":"Token $A3 CHR$ with a number (class 0, entry $0550), when running: the number must be 32, 64\nor 85 (report B otherwise); in bank 7, the alternate ROM's $1365 (ROM 0's position) with L =\nthe number; bank 0.","comment":"A = the number"},
        "519": {"comment":"The number 32, 64 or 85?"},
        "527": {"comment":"Any other: report B"},
        "532": {"synopsis":"In bank 7, the alternate ROM's $1365 with L = the number.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "533": {"comment":"L = the number"},
        "534": {"comment":"Alternate ROM's $1365, ROM 0's position"},
        "539": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "541": {"synopsis":"Syntax offsets, one byte for each character code from $1D to $FF, read by STMT_BEGIN at\n$0200 + the statement's first character: the entry's address is $0300 + the byte (in\nSYNTAX_ENTRIES or, above $FF, in the overlap with SUBKEY_TABLES' page). Codes $1D-$20 hold 0\n(never read: RST $20 skips them); most other characters hold $1F (the entry at $031F, report\nC); letters and '%' hold $25 (the entry at $0325: an assignment without LET); ':' $22 (an\nempty statement), '@' $28, ';' $40 (as REM). The command tokens, NextBASIC's $81-$A3 and ROM\n3's DEF FN-COPY ($CE-$FF), hold their own entries' offsets; function tokens $A5-$CD hold\n$1F."},
        "768": {"synopsis":"Each statement's syntax entry, read item by item by SYNTAX_ITEM from $0300 + its\nSYNTAX_OFFSETS byte. A byte from $20 is a character or token the line must have next\n(SYNTAX_CHAR); a byte below $20 an operand class, run through CLASS_TABLE. Classes 0, 3,\n$0C, $0D, $0E and $10 are followed by the word of the routine that ends the entry; class 5\nby a word and goes on; class $0F by one byte, a table in SUBKEY_TABLES' page ($0400 + the\nbyte); classes 2, 7 and $0B end the entry with no word. A routine word's top two bits choose\nwhere it runs (CLASS_E): 00 this ROM, 01 ROM 3 ($4000 off), 10 the alternate ROM, 11 the\nDivMMC memory. Entries overlap: INK-OVER start at $0300 (class 7), MERGE, VERIFY, LOAD and\nSAVE at $0301 (class $0B), LET at $0302 (class 2). Then: GO TO $0303, RUN $0305, COPY $0307,\ntokens $97 $0309, $8F $030B, $9A $030D, $9B $030F, $9C $0311, $9D $0313, $A3 $0315, LINE\n$0317; token $81 $0319, $82 $031C; report C $031F; ':' $0322; letters $0325; '@' $0328; MOVE\n$032B; IF $032E; $84 $0331; GO SUB $0334; STOP $0337; PRINT $033A; INPUT $033D; ';' and REM\n$0340; NEW $0343; LIST $0346; RANDOMIZE $0349; CONTINUE $034C; CLEAR $034F; CLS $0352; PAUSE\n$0355; READ $0358; DATA $035B; RESTORE $035E; LPRINT $0361; LLIST $0364; DEF FN $0367; CLOSE\n# $036A; ERASE $036D; CAT $0370; tokens $90-$94 $0373-$037F; $96 $0382; $98 $0385; $99\n$0388; $9E $038B; $9F $038E; $A4 $0391; $85 $0394; PLOT $0397; DRAW $039B; BEEP $039F; OUT\n$03A3; BORDER $03A7; FORMAT $03AB; $95 $03AE; $A0-$A2 $03B2-$03BA; $88 $03BE; POKE $03C2;\nCIRCLE $03C7; $89 $03CC; $83 $03D1; RETURN $03D4; DIM $03DA; OPEN # $03E0; $A9 $03E6; NEXT\n$03EC; FOR $03F3. Routines named by the $2700-$33FF helper: PRINT_CMD (word at $033B),\nINPUT_CMD ($033E), LPRINT_CMD ($0362), REMOUNT_CMD ($0389), POKE_BYTES ($03C5), CIRCLE_RUN\n($03CA), POKE_WORDS ($03CF)."},
        "1018": {"synopsis":"Calls the alternate ROM's $1A1C (CALL_ALT_ROM0), then returns. Between the syntax tables;\nnothing in pages 0-2 refers to it.","comment":"Alternate ROM's $1A1C, ROM 0's position"},
        "1024": {"synopsis":"Sub-keyword tables for the commands with alternatives, each read by class $0F\n(SUBKEY_LOOKUP) at $0400 + the byte after the class: a count n, n characters or tokens, then\nn + 1 offsets, the default's first, each the distance from its own byte to the entry that\nfollows. $0400 COPY: ENTER, ':'. $040A COPY string TO: SCREEN$, LPRINT, '#'. $0412 token\n$9A: NEW. $0419 token $9A n: token $93, GO TO, GO SUB, POKE, token $89, COPY, ERASE, token\n$9C, CLEAR, RESTORE, LINE, LIST, MERGE, USR, FORMAT. $0439 GO TO: '#'. $043D RUN: AT. $0441\nMOVE string: IN, OUT, TO. $0449 token $8F: TO. $044D token $97: token $8E. $0451 LINE:\nMERGE. $0455 token $9B: token $9A, DIM. $045B token $9D: DIM, FORMAT, OVER, CLEAR. $0465\ntoken $9C: token $9D, OVER, token $9A, AT, ERASE, CLEAR, DIM. $0475 token $A3: ATTR, INK,\nPAPER, FLASH, BRIGHT, SCREEN$, CHR$, LOAD. Two entries sit between them: $0406 (COPY's\ndefault: a string, TO, then $040A) and $0416 (token $9A's default: a number, then $0419)."},
        "1159": {"synopsis":"The syntax entries that SUBKEY_TABLES' offsets lead to, in SYNTAX_ENTRIES' form,\n$0487-$0555: COPY at the end $0487; COPY string TO's $048A-$0491; the 16 of token $9A n\n$0495-$04C8; GO TO's $04C9-$04CC; RUN's $04D1-$04D4; MOVE's $04D7-$04DF; token $8F's\n$04E3-$04E6; $97's $04E9-$04EC; LINE's $04EF-$04F3; $9B's $04F7-$04FD; $9D's $0503-$050D;\n$9C's $0510-$052A; token $A3's $0530-$0553. The five class 0 entries for SET_ATTR_FIELD\n($0533 ATTR, $0538 INK, $053D PAPER, $0542 BRIGHT, $0547 FLASH) each have two more bytes\nafter their word, the field's largest value and bit position + 1. Routines named by the\n$2700-$33FF helper: BANK_ALLOC_CMD (word at $0497), BANK_POKE_BYTES ($04A6), BANK_POKE_WORDS\n($04AB), BANK_1346_CMD ($04AE), BANK_COPY_CMD ($04B1), BANK_FILL_CMD ($04B4), BANK_BLOCK_CMD\n($04B7), BANK_FREE_CMD ($04BA), SET_CPU_SPEED ($04D5), SAVED_ERR_STOP ($04E4)."},
        "1366": {"synopsis":"Operand classes: 17 bytes, one for each class 0-$10, each the distance from its own byte to\nthe class's routine, read by SYNTAX_ITEM (ADD HL,A twice): CLASS_0 $0592, CLASS_1 $05A3,\nCLASS_2 $05B0, CLASS_3 $0593, CLASS_4 $0642, CLASS_5 $0650, CLASS_6 $0635, CLASS_7 $05FC,\nCLASS_8 $063C, CLASS_9 $05C1, CLASS_A $05BB, CLASS_B $05F9, CLASS_C $056F, CLASS_D $056A,\nCLASS_E $0570, CLASS_F $0631, CLASS_10 $0567."},
        "1383": {"synopsis":"Class $10: as class $0E, but the return to SYNTAX_NEXT is dropped first, so the routine does\nnot come back to the statement loop (the report C entry, $09AF, and ':', $0962).","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "1384": {"comment":"Then CLASS_E drops STMT_RET's too"},
        "1386": {"synopsis":"Class $0D, an optional number ($0DF0), then as class $0C.","comment":"DE = the routine word's address, kept"},
        "1387": {"comment":"The number, if any"},
        "1391": {"synopsis":"Class $0C: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_E (STATEMENT_END first).","comment":"Z: the statement must end here"},
        "1392": {"synopsis":"Class $0E (and the end of classes 0, 3, $0C, $0D and $10): the routine whose word is at DE\nruns, when checking and when running.\n1. The return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped; with Z set, STATEMENT_END (checking stops here).\n2. BC = the word. Its top two bits choose where the routine runs: 00 this ROM (PUSH and\n   RET), 01 ROM 3 ($3EBF: bit 6 cleared, back through $5B3E), 10 the alternate ROM ($0072:\n   bit 7 cleared, ROM select 1), 11 the DivMMC memory ($26DA with A = $8A, bits 7 and 6\n   cleared). A = the byte at HL for the routine.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "1393": {"comment":"Z: the statement's end first"},
        "1396": {"comment":"BC = the routine's word"},
        "1401": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry, bit 6 into the sign"},
        "1403": {"comment":"A = the byte at HL"},
        "1404": {"comment":"Bit 7: the alternate ROM or DivMMC memory"},
        "1406": {"comment":"Bit 6: ROM 3"},
        "1409": {"comment":"This ROM: the routine entered by RET"},
        "1411": {"synopsis":"A routine word with bit 7 set: bit 6 clear, the alternate ROM (CALL_ALT's second half at\n$0072); set, the DivMMC memory ($26DA with A = $8A).","comment":"Bit 6 clear: the alternate ROM"},
        "1416": {"comment":"Bit 6 set: the DivMMC memory"},
        "1418": {"comment":"A kept for $26DA"},
        "1421": {"comment":"DivMMC memory with $E3 = $8A"},
        "1426": {"synopsis":"Class 0: a number (CLASS_6), and the statement's end; then the routine whose word follows\n(CLASS_E with Z set), which here is in this ROM ($2D08, $2D14) or wherever its top bits say,\nnot in ROM 3 as with the +3E ROM 1's class 0.","comment":"Z set: the statement must end"},
        "1427": {"synopsis":"Class 3: a number (CLASS_6), then the routine whose word follows (CLASS_E). The flags pushed\nare SYNTAX_ITEM's (NZ), so STATEMENT_END is not called.","comment":"The flags kept"},
        "1428": {"comment":"The number"},
        "1431": {"comment":"A = the character after it"},
        "1436": {"comment":"DE = the routine word's address"},
        "1443": {"synopsis":"Class 1: ROM 3's CLASS_1 (a variable to assign to). Also called from $0666, $068D, $06E9,\n$0775 and others.","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_1"},
        "1449": {"synopsis":"A statement that starts with a letter or '%' (offset $25, class $0E): an assignment without\nLET. CH_ADD back to the first character (A = it, from XH), then CLASS_2.","comment":"A = the statement's first character"},
        "1451": {"comment":"CH_ADD back onto it"},
        "1456": {"synopsis":"Class 2, an assignment (LET and LET_IMPLIED): the return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped, CH_ADD\npushed; a '%' variable goes to LET_PERCENT, any other to LET_VAR.","comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "1457": {"comment":"The variable's place kept"},
        "1458": {"comment":"An integer variable ('%')?"},
        "1466": {"synopsis":"Past the current character, then CLASS_A."},
        "1467": {"synopsis":"Class $0A: ROM 3's CLASS_A (a string). Also called from $15F8.","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_A"},
        "1473": {"synopsis":"Class 9 (PLOT, DRAW, CIRCLE):\n1. Running: stream -2 and its colours ($133A).\n2. The colour items ($2F69).\n3. When $3FED gives carry (the mode set in $5C7F's low 4 bits), the word at $5C6C rebuilt\n   from P_FLAG: bit 0 (OVER) clear, D = its low byte (or its high byte with bit 2, INVERSE);\n   bit 0 set, E = $FF and D = high XOR low (or kept with bit 2).\n4. Two numbers (CLASS_8).","comment":"Running?"},
        "1477": {"comment":"Stream -2 and its colours"},
        "1480": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "1483": {"comment":"The colour items"},
        "1486": {"comment":"Carry for the mode in $5C7F?"},
        "1491": {"comment":"HL = the word at $5C6C"},
        "1494": {"comment":"B = P_FLAG"},
        "1500": {"comment":"OVER?"},
        "1504": {"comment":"E = $FF"},
        "1505": {"comment":"INVERSE too?"},
        "1509": {"comment":"D = high XOR low"},
        "1514": {"synopsis":"No OVER: D = the low byte, or with INVERSE the high byte.","comment":"D = the low byte"},
        "1515": {"comment":"INVERSE?"},
        "1519": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "1520": {"synopsis":"The word at $5C6C = DE.","comment":"Kept at $5C6C"},
        "1524": {"synopsis":"The current character, then two numbers (CLASS_8).","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "1527": {"comment":"Two numbers"},
        "1529": {"synopsis":"Class $0B, MERGE, VERIFY, LOAD and SAVE: on at $15DF.","comment":"The tape and disk commands"},
        "1532": {"synopsis":"Class 7, INK to OVER as statements:\n1. TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared.\n2. Running: stream -2 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT), the temporary colours from the permanent ones\n   (ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP), $5C7F bit 5 set.\n3. CLASS_7_ITEM. The return to SYNTAX_NEXT is dropped, so the statement loop goes on through\n   STMT_RET.","comment":"Running?"},
        "1536": {"comment":"XH = the statement's token, kept"},
        "1538": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared"},
        "1544": {"comment":"Stream -2"},
        "1549": {"comment":"Temporary colours from the permanent ones"},
        "1552": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 5 set while the item is read"},
        "1556": {"synopsis":"The item: A = the token, $2F84 reads the colour; $5C7F bit 5 cleared; the statement's end;\nthen the temporary colours made permanent: ATTR_P and MASK_P from ATTR_T and MASK_T, and\nP_FLAG's temporary bits (even) copied into its permanent bits (odd).","comment":"A = the token"},
        "1557": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "1558": {"comment":"The colour item"},
        "1561": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 5 cleared"},
        "1565": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "1568": {"comment":"ATTR_P, MASK_P = ATTR_T, MASK_T"},
        "1574": {"comment":"P_FLAG: temporary bits to permanent ones"},
        "1585": {"synopsis":"Class $0F: a choice of what follows (SUBKEY_LOOKUP).","comment":"The sub-keyword table"},
        "1588": {"synopsis":"Past the current character, then CLASS_6."},
        "1589": {"synopsis":"Class 6: ROM 3's CLASS_6 (a number). Called from many commands.","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_6"},
        "1595": {"synopsis":"Past the current character, then CLASS_8."},
        "1596": {"synopsis":"Class 8: ROM 3's CLASS_8 (two numbers separated by ',').","comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_8"},
        "1602": {"synopsis":"Class 4: ROM 3's CLASS_4 (a FOR or NEXT variable) with FLAGS bit 0 cleared first; set by it\nafterwards is error $60.","comment":"FLAGS bit 0 cleared"},
        "1606": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLASS_4"},
        "1609": {"comment":"Bit 0 set by it?"},
        "1614": {"comment":"Error $60"},
        "1616": {"synopsis":"Class 5: the word after the class is a routine for the '#' form; T_ADDR moves past it.\nWithout a '#' next, the entry goes on. With one: the return to SYNTAX_NEXT dropped, the\nroutine pushed; a number (the stream), TO, and a numeric variable (CLASS_1), else report C;\nthe statement's end; running, the stream selected (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT) and the routine\nentered by RET.","comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "1617": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "1621": {"comment":"T_ADDR past the word"},
        "1624": {"comment":"A '#' next?"},
        "1627": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT's return dropped"},
        "1628": {"comment":"The routine kept"},
        "1629": {"comment":"The stream's number"},
        "1632": {"comment":"TO must follow"},
        "1637": {"comment":"Past it; the variable"},
        "1641": {"comment":"Numeric?"},
        "1648": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "1653": {"comment":"A = the stream"},
        "1656": {"comment":"Selected; RET into the routine"},
        "1660": {"synopsis":"An assignment to a '%' variable: the DivMMC memory's $29A9; carry clear means done (the\nstatement's end); carry set goes on as an ordinary assignment from the start\n(LET_PERCENT_NO).","comment":"DivMMC memory's $29A9"},
        "1665": {"comment":"Carry: not handled there"},
        "1667": {"comment":"The kept CH_ADD dropped"},
        "1668": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "1672": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD back to the variable; then LET_VAR.","comment":"CH_ADD back to the variable"},
        "1677": {"synopsis":"An assignment:\n1. The variable (CLASS_1).\n2. '=': the value (ROM 3's VAL_FETCH) and the statement's end.\n3. ',': several variables (LET_LIST).\n4. Otherwise an operator and '=' (ASSIGN_OP), then LET_COMPOUND (or LET_STR_PLUS).","comment":"The variable"},
        "1680": {"comment":"A = the character after it"},
        "1683": {"comment":"Plain '='?"},
        "1687": {"comment":"The kept CH_ADD dropped"},
        "1688": {"comment":"Past '='; ROM 3's VAL_FETCH"},
        "1695": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "1699": {"synopsis":"Not '=': a list of variables, or an operator.","comment":"A list of variables?"},
        "1703": {"comment":"The kept CH_ADD dropped"},
        "1704": {"comment":"C = the operator's code"},
        "1707": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 2: the special variable kind?"},
        "1713": {"synopsis":"x op= value: the variable's value stacked (LET_VAR_VALUE), the operand read, the operation\ndone and the result assigned (LET_OPERAND); the statement's end.","comment":"The variable's value"},
        "1716": {"comment":"The operand, the operation, the assignment"},
        "1719": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "1723": {"synopsis":"With FLAGS2 bit 2 set and '+' (code $CF): a number (ROM 3's CLASS_6), the statement's end;\nrunning, the DivMMC memory's $24F1, $2860 (with HL = DEST) and $2855 add it to what DEST\npoints at. Other operators go to LET_COMPOUND.","comment":"'+'?"},
        "1728": {"comment":"A number"},
        "1734": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "1737": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $24F1: DE = the number"},
        "1742": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "1744": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "1747": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $2860: DE = the value"},
        "1752": {"comment":"Value + the number"},
        "1756": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $2855 stores it"},
        "1762": {"synopsis":"Several variables, a, b, ... op= values:\n1. Each variable read (CLASS_1) with its FLAGS byte pushed; B counts them.\n2. The operator (ASSIGN_OP).\n3. The values, each by SCAN_EXPR, at most as many as variables (report C); running, a string\n   value in the workspace is copied and kept as an offset from WORKSP.\n4. Each value's type checked (LET_TYPE_CHECK), the last value also for the variables left\n   over.\n5. Running: each variable assigned in turn (LET_LIST_ASSIGN). Ends with CH_ADD after the\n   values and STATEMENT_END.","comment":"B = 0 variables"},
        "1766": {"synopsis":"The next variable, after a ','."},
        "1768": {"comment":"Past ','; the variable"},
        "1773": {"synopsis":"One more variable: its FLAGS byte pushed."},
        "1774": {"comment":"One more"},
        "1775": {"comment":"Its FLAGS byte kept on the stack"},
        "1779": {"comment":"Another ','?"},
        "1787": {"comment":"C = the operator's code"},
        "1790": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "1792": {"comment":"D = the variables, E = the values"},
        "1793": {"comment":"E = 0 values"},
        "1795": {"synopsis":"One value: SCAN_EXPR; running, a string's text copied into the workspace when it lies\noutside it, and its address stored as an offset from WORKSP.","comment":"One more value"},
        "1798": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "1801": {"comment":"Running, and a string?"},
        "1810": {"comment":"DE, BC = its start and length"},
        "1821": {"comment":"Below the end of the stack?"},
        "1825": {"comment":"Or below WORKSP?"},
        "1831": {"comment":"Already in the workspace"},
        "1833": {"synopsis":"The string copied into new room in the workspace (WORK_ROOM)."},
        "1834": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM, BC bytes"},
        "1839": {"comment":"The string copied"},
        "1842": {"synopsis":"Its start stored on the stack as start - WORKSP.","comment":"DE = start - WORKSP"},
        "1850": {"comment":"Into the stacked value's address"},
        "1859": {"synopsis":"More values than variables is report C; the value's type checked; another ',' gives another\nvalue."},
        "1861": {"comment":"More values than variables?"},
        "1866": {"comment":"This value's type for its variable"},
        "1869": {"comment":"Another ','?"},
        "1879": {"synopsis":"X_PTR = the place after the values; the last value checked against each variable left over.","comment":"X_PTR = after the values"},
        "1882": {"comment":"B = the values' count"},
        "1883": {"synopsis":"A variable without a value of its own: checked against the last value.","comment":"Variables left over?"},
        "1893": {"synopsis":"Checking: done (LET_LIST_END). Running: CH_ADD back to the first variable and\nLET_LIST_ASSIGN for each.","comment":"E = the values' count"},
        "1894": {"comment":"HL = the first variable"},
        "1895": {"comment":"B = the variables' count"},
        "1896": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "1902": {"comment":"CH_ADD back to the first variable"},
        "1905": {"comment":"Variable 1 first"},
        "1907": {"synopsis":"Variable B: looked up (CLASS_1); with the plain '=' only its kind matters, otherwise its\nvalue stacked (LET_VAR_VALUE); then its value: value B, or the last one when there are fewer\nvalues."},
        "1909": {"comment":"The variable"},
        "1914": {"comment":"The operator plain '='?"},
        "1921": {"comment":"A string: C = $38"},
        "1928": {"synopsis":"The value's number: B, or E when B is more."},
        "1929": {"comment":"B = variable, E = values"},
        "1933": {"comment":"Fewer values than this?"},
        "1938": {"synopsis":"HL = that value's 5 bytes on the calculator stack (STKBOT + 5 x (n - 1)).","comment":"D = the value's number - 1"},
        "1940": {"comment":"DE = that x 5"},
        "1944": {"comment":"From STKBOT"},
        "1948": {"comment":"A, E, D, C, B = the value"},
        "1958": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "1963": {"comment":"Its start back from the offset"},
        "1968": {"synopsis":"The value put on top of the calculator stack ($386C); then plain '=' assigns it (LLA_PLAIN),\nanother operator first applies it (LET_APPLY_OP).","comment":"Stacked as the operand"},
        "1972": {"comment":"E = the operator's code"},
        "1975": {"comment":"Plain '='?"},
        "1981": {"comment":"The operation, then the assignment"},
        "1986": {"synopsis":"Plain '=': the value assigned (LET_ASSIGN with FLAGS).","comment":"A = FLAGS"},
        "1992": {"synopsis":"Past the ',' to the next variable, until all are assigned."},
        "1994": {"comment":"Past ','"},
        "1995": {"comment":"The next variable"},
        "1999": {"comment":"B = the variables' count"},
        "2000": {"synopsis":"The FLAGS bytes taken off the stack (B of them); CH_ADD = X_PTR (after the values);\nSTATEMENT_END.","comment":"One FLAGS byte dropped"},
        "2003": {"comment":"CH_ADD after the values"},
        "2009": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "2013": {"synopsis":"An operator: the variable's value stacked first (LET_VAR_VALUE)."},
        "2018": {"synopsis":"Checks value E against variable E of D: the variable's FLAGS byte from the stack; for a\nstring variable the operator's code is the string one (STR_OP_CODE, report C if none); the\nvalue's FLAGS bit 6 must match the code's bit 6, else report C.\nExit: C as on entry.","comment":"The variable's place on the stack"},
        "2028": {"comment":"A string variable?"},
        "2030": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "2031": {"comment":"Then the string operator's code"},
        "2034": {"comment":"The value's type against the code's"},
        "2038": {"comment":"C back"},
        "2042": {"comment":"Wrong: report C"},
        "2045": {"synopsis":"The operand after the operator: a '%' expression through the DivMMC memory\n(LET_OPERAND_INT); otherwise ROM 3's OPERAND_PUSH2 with D = 0, B = 1, which reads it and\ndoes the operation. Then LET_ASSIGN.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "2048": {"comment":"An integer expression?"},
        "2052": {"comment":"FLAGS kept"},
        "2056": {"comment":"D = 0, B = 1"},
        "2060": {"comment":"ROM 3's OPERAND_PUSH2"},
        "2063": {"synopsis":"A = the FLAGS kept; then LET_ASSIGN."},
        "2064": {"synopsis":"The result assigned through ROM 3's $1C5E (VAL_FETCH_A after its SCAN_EXPR: the type check\nand the assignment), with A = the variable's FLAGS.","comment":"ROM 3's VAL_FETCH_A, its second half"},
        "2071": {"synopsis":"A '%' operand: the DivMMC memory's $2400; then the operation (LET_APPLY_OP with the code it\nleaves)."},
        "2072": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $2400"},
        "2077": {"comment":"D, E back"},
        "2078": {"synopsis":"The operation C applied to the two values on the calculator stack (ROM 3's OP_APPLY_NOW with\nB = 0), then LET_ASSIGN_AF.","comment":"FLAGS kept"},
        "2082": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "2084": {"comment":"ROM 3's OP_APPLY_NOW"},
        "2089": {"synopsis":"Stacks the variable's current value, for an operator:\n1. FLAGS2 bit 2 set: DE = the DivMMC memory's $2860 value at DEST; running, stacked as a\n   number ($3867).\n2. A new variable (FLAGX bit 1) is report 2.\n3. A number: running, its 5 bytes at DEST + 1 copied to the stack (ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER).\n4. A string: running, DEST and STRLEN stacked ($385E), then C turned into the string\n   operator (STR_OP_CODE).","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 2?"},
        "2096": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "2099": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $2860: DE = the value"},
        "2104": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "2106": {"comment":"Running: stacked"},
        "2115": {"synopsis":"A BASIC variable: new is report 2; a number or a string.","comment":"A new variable?"},
        "2122": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "2125": {"comment":"A string?"},
        "2131": {"comment":"The number's 5 bytes"},
        "2132": {"comment":"Checking: nothing to stack"},
        "2137": {"comment":"ROM 3's PUSH_NUMBER"},
        "2146": {"synopsis":"A string variable: running, DE = DEST, BC = STRLEN stacked; then STR_OP_CODE.","comment":"DE = the string"},
        "2148": {"comment":"BC = STRLEN"},
        "2152": {"comment":"Running: stacked"},
        "2160": {"synopsis":"The code for an operator on a string: '+' ($CF) gives $17, $C4 gives $7B, '=' ($F8) gives\n$38; anything else is report C.\nExit: C = the code.","comment":"'+': join"},
        "2166": {"comment":"$C4: string with a number"},
        "2171": {"comment":"'=': plain"},
        "2173": {"synopsis":"C = $38, the plain '=' code for a string (called with Z set: it returns at once)."},
        "2176": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\")."},
        "2178": {"synopsis":"Reads an assignment operator at CH_ADD (A its character): one of ASSIGN_OP_CHARS, followed\nby '=' (report C otherwise), and CH_ADD after the '='.\nExit: C = its code from ASSIGN_OP_CODES. The last character, '^', followed by '|' instead\ngives D = $FF and C = 0.","comment":"The 11 operator characters"},
        "2184": {"comment":"A one of them?"},
        "2186": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "2188": {"comment":"Not the last ('^')?"},
        "2192": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "2196": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "2198": {"comment":"'|'?"},
        "2202": {"comment":"D = $FF"},
        "2207": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD back onto the '^'.","comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "2211": {"synopsis":"C = the code, 11 bytes on from the character found.","comment":"Into ASSIGN_OP_CODES"},
        "2216": {"synopsis":"The '=' (now, or after the next character).","comment":"The operator itself '='?"},
        "2220": {"comment":"Past it: '=' must follow"},
        "2225": {"synopsis":"Past the '='."},
        "2227": {"synopsis":"ASSIGN_OP's 11 operator characters, searched by CPIR: '+' '-' '*' '/' '&' '|', tokens $8C\n$8D $8B, '=', '^'."},
        "2238": {"synopsis":"The operators' codes, in ASSIGN_OP_CHARS' order, read 11 bytes on from the character found:\n$CF $C3 $C4 $C5 $FD $FE $C1 $C2 $FC $F8 $C6."},
        "2249": {"synopsis":"Class $0F's work: the byte at T_ADDR (DE) gives the table at $0400 + it; A, the current\ncharacter, is searched among its n characters. Found: the offset in that character's place;\nnot found: the default offset (the first). T_ADDR = the entry it leads to; $5B5E = A. Not\nfound: back to SYNTAX_NEXT with the character not taken. Found: a character below $80 is\nleft for the entry; a token is passed (NEXT_SKIP).","comment":"HL = the table"},
        "2253": {"comment":"DE = BC = n"},
        "2258": {"comment":"The characters"},
        "2259": {"comment":"A one of them?"},
        "2263": {"comment":"Found: HL = its offset's byte"},
        "2264": {"synopsis":"HL + the offset = the entry; T_ADDR = it.","comment":"The entry, by the offset"},
        "2266": {"comment":"T_ADDR"},
        "2269": {"comment":"The character kept at $5B5E"},
        "2272": {"comment":"Not found: back to SYNTAX_NEXT"},
        "2273": {"comment":"A character: left for the entry"},
        "2275": {"comment":"A token: past it"},
        "2278": {"synopsis":"Z when A is ')', ENTER or ':'."},
        "2281": {"synopsis":"Z when A is ENTER or ':' (the statement's end)."},
        "2287": {"synopsis":"Stops with an error after closing file 0 (CLOSE_FILE_0): the code is the byte after the\nCALL, or, with its bit 7 set, A's +3DOS error turned into one (FILE_ERROR_A).","comment":"A, the +3DOS error, kept"},
        "2288": {"comment":"File 0 closed first"},
        "2292": {"synopsis":"FILE_ERROR without closing file 0: the byte after the CALL is the code; with bit 7 set, A (a\n+3DOS error) is turned into one: below 10 + $3D, else + $18. The error raised by RUN-like\ncode built on the stack: CALL $0DA3 followed by the code byte.","comment":"HL = the byte after the CALL"},
        "2294": {"comment":"Bit 7: the code from A?"},
        "2298": {"comment":"Below 10?"},
        "2302": {"comment":"Errors 0-9: + $3D"},
        "2306": {"synopsis":"Error 10 up: + $18."},
        "2308": {"synopsis":"E = the code."},
        "2309": {"synopsis":"CALL $0DA3 and the code byte built on the stack (CD A3 0D, code) and run there; ERROR_1's\nhandler reads the code through the return address.","comment":"H = the code, L = $0D"},
        "2313": {"comment":"CALL $0DA3: $CD, $A3"},
        "2318": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "2319": {"comment":"HL = SP, the code's start"},
        "2323": {"comment":"Run on the stack"},
        "2324": {"synopsis":"The end of a statement's operands. Running: returns, and the command's routine goes on.\nChecking: the two returns dropped, and on to STMT_NEXT for what follows the statement.","comment":"Running: go on"},
        "2329": {"comment":"Checking: the command's return dropped"},
        "2331": {"comment":"The statement's end checked"},
        "2333": {"synopsis":"Checks the edit line's syntax (from LINE_ENTER): FLAGS bit 7 cleared (check, do not run),\nthe line number read past (ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO), SUBPPC = 0, ERR_NR = $FF; then STMT_START\nat the current character.","comment":"Checking, not running"},
        "2337": {"comment":"ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO: past the number"},
        "2340": {"comment":"SUBPPC = 0"},
        "2344": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF, no report"},
        "2348": {"synopsis":"STMT_START with A the current character. AFTER_RUN pushes it as the way back for a trapped\nerror; $1CF3 and $1D80 jump here.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "2353": {"synopsis":"BREAK tested ($2B50), then STMT_BEGIN with A the current character (from $1DF4, $1E53,\n$25E8).","comment":"BREAK pressed?"},
        "2356": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "2361": {"synopsis":"REM and ';' (class $0E): the return to STMT_RET dropped and the rest of the line skipped\n(LINE_END).","comment":"STMT_RET's return dropped"},
        "2362": {"synopsis":"The end of a line: when checking, done. When running, the next line from NXTLIN ($3995 finds\nit; none left: return), then LINE_GO.","comment":"Checking: done"},
        "2367": {"synopsis":"Running: the line at NXTLIN, if there is one (from $1CD5, $1D03, $1D7D).","comment":"HL = NXTLIN"},
        "2370": {"comment":"Another line? NC: the program's end"},
        "2374": {"synopsis":"Runs the line at HL: NXTLIN = HL, CH_ADD = DE (before its text), SUBPPC = 0; then STMT_LOOP.\nFrom AFTER_RUN's RUN_SETUP at $0B8E.","comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "2377": {"comment":"CH_ADD = DE"},
        "2381": {"comment":"SUBPPC = 0"},
        "2387": {"synopsis":"Where a command returns to: BREAK tested ($2B50), then STMT_NEXT.","comment":"BREAK pressed?"},
        "2390": {"synopsis":"After a statement: ENTER ends the line (LINE_END), ':' starts the next (STMT_LOOP), anything\nelse is report C.","comment":"A = the current character"},
        "2393": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "2397": {"comment":"Not ':': report C"},
        "2401": {"synopsis":"The statement loop: past the ':' to the next statement."},
        "2402": {"synopsis":"One statement: SUBPPC + 1 (from $FF: the line ends at once; past 127: report C); then\nSTMT_BEGIN.","comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "2405": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: no more statements"},
        "2409": {"comment":"One more; past 127 is report C"},
        "2413": {"synopsis":"The statement at A:\n1. The workspace and calculator stack emptied (STKBOT = STKEND = WORKSP), MEM = MEMBOT.\n2. ENTER ends the line (LINE_END).\n3. Otherwise its syntax entry: $0300 + the byte at $0200 + A (SYNTAX_OFFSETS), with A kept\n   in XH and STMT_RET pushed; past the character, then SYNTAX_ITEM.","comment":"Workspace and calculator stack emptied"},
        "2422": {"comment":"MEM = MEMBOT"},
        "2428": {"comment":"An empty statement at the line's end?"},
        "2432": {"comment":"The first character kept in XH"},
        "2435": {"comment":"Its offset from SYNTAX_OFFSETS"},
        "2438": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "2439": {"comment":"STMT_RET the way back"},
        "2443": {"comment":"Past the first character"},
        "2448": {"synopsis":"SYNTAX_ITEM again from T_ADDR: the return address each item leaves.","comment":"HL = T_ADDR"},
        "2451": {"synopsis":"Reads the entry's next item at HL, T_ADDR following it, SYNTAX_NEXT pushed: below $20 an\noperand class, its routine from CLASS_TABLE (distance byte at $0556 + the class) entered\nwith DE = T_ADDR, A = the current character and NZ; $20 and up, SYNTAX_CHAR.","comment":"The item"},
        "2453": {"comment":"T_ADDR past it"},
        "2456": {"comment":"SYNTAX_NEXT the way back"},
        "2460": {"comment":"A character or token?"},
        "2464": {"comment":"DE = T_ADDR"},
        "2465": {"comment":"The class's distance byte"},
        "2471": {"comment":"HL = the class's routine"},
        "2474": {"comment":"A = the current character, NZ"},
        "2479": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\"). Also the routine of\nSYNTAX_ENTRIES' $031F (characters that start no statement)."},
        "2481": {"synopsis":"The character or keyword (in C) must be the line's next, else report C; then past it.","comment":"C = what the entry wants"},
        "2485": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "2488": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "2490": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from DE onto the machine stack (SP lowered by BC) and runs them there with\nROM 3 paged in (ROM 3's JP (HL) at $250E); then SP back up by BC. From $3F51 and $3F7A.","comment":"HL = -BC"},
        "2496": {"comment":"SP lowered by BC"},
        "2499": {"comment":"BC and the code's start kept"},
        "2501": {"comment":"The code copied there"},
        "2504": {"comment":"HL = its start"},
        "2505": {"comment":"ROM 3's JP (HL): run in ROM 3"},
        "2508": {"comment":"SP back up by BC"},
        "2512": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = E_LINE; A = the edit line's first character (past spaces).","comment":"CH_ADD = E_LINE"},
        "2518": {"comment":"A = the first character"},
        "2522": {"synopsis":"What the edit line holds: NC for a command (a '.', a keyword from $CE but LET, a NextBASIC\nkeyword $8F-$A4, or anything followed by ':'); C for a line that reads like one expression,\nwith Z when it starts with LET.\nExit: CH_ADD at the end or at the ':'.","comment":"A = the line's first character"},
        "2525": {"comment":"A dot command?"},
        "2528": {"comment":"LET?"},
        "2532": {"comment":"Another command keyword?"},
        "2535": {"comment":"A function keyword?"},
        "2539": {"comment":"Tokens $8F-$A4: commands"},
        "2542": {"synopsis":"B = the first character; the line read to its end."},
        "2543": {"synopsis":"The next character: ':' means a command (NC, Z); ENTER ends the scan.","comment":"The next character"},
        "2546": {"comment":"':': a command line"},
        "2547": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "2551": {"comment":"Carry; Z for LET"},
        "2556": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q, \"Parameter error\")."},
        "2558": {"synopsis":"What runs when the edited line is entered:\n1. DF_SZ = 2; the handler in $5B6C = ENTER_HANDLER; ERR_NR = $FF; $5B3A (the RAM routine\n   that enters GO_HANDLER) put under ERR_SP; CH_ADD to the line.\n2. Unless the byte at $D5B8 in bank 7 is 4, CHECK_LINE.\n3. With 4: a line that is not one expression is report Q (LINE_KIND NC), one starting with\n   LET is CHECK_LINE; otherwise CALC_LINE. Nothing in pages 0-2 calls $09FE in a form the\n   decoder shows.","comment":"DF_SZ = 2"},
        "2562": {"comment":"The handler: ENTER_HANDLER"},
        "2568": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF"},
        "2572": {"comment":"$5B3A under ERR_SP: errors go to GO_HANDLER"},
        "2580": {"comment":"CH_ADD to the line"},
        "2583": {"comment":"The byte at $D5B8 in bank 7"},
        "2588": {"comment":"Not 4: the line checked"},
        "2593": {"comment":"A command line?"},
        "2596": {"comment":"NC: report Q"},
        "2598": {"comment":"LET: checked as a command"},
        "2601": {"synopsis":"An edit line that reads like one expression (with $D5B8 = 4):\n1. PPC = $FFFE; checked (FLAGS bit 7 clear) by SCAN_EXPR: it must be numeric and end the\n   line, else report Q.\n2. ENTER fed to the alternate ROM's $03D6.\n3. Run (FLAGS bit 7 set) with the handler AFTER_RUN: SCAN_EXPR again, numeric else report Q.\n4. CALC_RESULT's work: the result's 5 bytes kept at $5B6E; one byte of room (ROM 3's\n   WORK_ROOM) at K_CUR; stream -1 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT), the number printed into it (ROM\n   3's PRINT_FP), the old channel back (ROM 3's CHAN_SET_FLAGS); each character printed fed\n   to the alternate ROM's $03D6 (CALC_RESULT_LOOP); then ENTER printed (PRINT_ENTER).","comment":"PPC = $FFFE: a direct command"},
        "2607": {"comment":"Checking"},
        "2611": {"comment":"CH_ADD to the line"},
        "2614": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "2617": {"comment":"Not numeric: report Q"},
        "2623": {"comment":"Not the line's end: report Q"},
        "2627": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "2629": {"comment":"To the alternate ROM's $03D6"},
        "2634": {"comment":"Running"},
        "2638": {"comment":"CH_ADD to the line again"},
        "2641": {"comment":"The handler: AFTER_RUN"},
        "2647": {"comment":"The expression, evaluated"},
        "2650": {"comment":"Not numeric: report Q"},
        "2656": {"comment":"The result's 5 bytes to $5B6E"},
        "2670": {"comment":"One byte of room in the workspace"},
        "2676": {"comment":"K_CUR = it; kept"},
        "2680": {"comment":"The current channel kept"},
        "2684": {"comment":"Stream -1"},
        "2689": {"comment":"The number printed"},
        "2692": {"comment":"The old channel back"},
        "2696": {"comment":"DE = where the text began"},
        "2697": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "2703": {"synopsis":"One character to the alternate ROM's $03D6.","comment":"The next character"},
        "2704": {"comment":"To the alternate ROM's $03D6"},
        "2710": {"comment":"Until the length is used up"},
        "2715": {"synopsis":"Prints ENTER ($0D) through ROM 3's PRINT_A. Also called from $0C79, $191B, $1952.","comment":"ENTER"},
        "2717": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "2721": {"synopsis":"In bank 7: file 0 closed (DOS_CLOSE, $0109); if that fails, abandoned (DOS_ABANDON, $010C, B\n= 0). Bank 0.","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "2722": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "2724": {"comment":"DOS_CLOSE"},
        "2727": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "2729": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "2731": {"comment":"DOS_ABANDON"},
        "2734": {"synopsis":"Bank 0; done.","comment":"Bank 0"},
        "2736": {"synopsis":"Where an error, or the end of a check or run, comes back to (entered as ROM 1's $0AB0 by\npage 0's code at $00CB, which runs at $5B3A in RAM; $5B3A is what this page puts under\nERR_SP): file 0 closed (CLOSE_FILE_0), streams 0-2 closed (CLOSE_STREAMS), then the handler\nwhose address is in $5B6C (ENTER_HANDLER, AFTER_RUN or LINE_STORED_END here).","comment":"File 0 closed"},
        "2739": {"comment":"Streams 0, 1 and 2 closed"},
        "2742": {"comment":"The handler in $5B6C"},
        "2745": {"synopsis":"JP (HL): a CALL here calls the routine at HL (from $2665)."},
        "2746": {"synopsis":"Closes streams 0, 1 and 2 and their channels: IDE_STREAM_CLOSE (ROM 2's $0059) with A = 0,\n1, 2. Also called from $2C99.","comment":"A = 0 first"},
        "2747": {"synopsis":"Stream A closed (IDE_STREAM_CLOSE); then the next, up to 2."},
        "2748": {"comment":"IDE_STREAM_CLOSE, stream A"},
        "2752": {"comment":"The next, up to 2"},
        "2758": {"synopsis":"Runs the line at DE as a direct command for ROM 2 (its CALL $3F00-style call at page 2's\n$0FAA, with $5B68 bit 0 set):\n1. The machine stack from SP up to RAMTOP copied to RAM page $10's $2216 (through MMU slot\n   1; the length kept at its $2393), SP = RAMTOP + 1.\n2. A word $3Exx pushed; the word at $5C0B = SP.\n3. RUN_SETUP. AFTER_RUN copies the stack back and returns ($0C28) while $5B68 bit 0 is set.","comment":"RAM page $10 at $2000"},
        "2762": {"comment":"HL = RAMTOP + 1 - SP: the stack's length"},
        "2769": {"comment":"Kept in that page"},
        "2774": {"comment":"HL = SP"},
        "2779": {"comment":"The stack copied to $2216 there"},
        "2785": {"comment":"SP = RAMTOP + 1"},
        "2786": {"comment":"This ROM back at $2000"},
        "2790": {"comment":"B = $3E pushed at the stack's top"},
        "2793": {"comment":"The word at $5C0B = SP"},
        "2799": {"synopsis":"Where checking a line ends (GO_HANDLER, set by LINE_ENTER):\n1. With a report pending (ERR_NR bit 7 clear): returns, back to the editor.\n2. No report: the line's number (ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO); a numbered line is stored ($0D3C).\n3. An empty line: returns.\n4. A direct command: three returns dropped; unless TV_FLAG bit 6 is set, ROM 0's $0EC9\n   first; TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared; then, in bank 7, by the byte at $D5B8 and $5C7F, ROM 0's\n   $272B (IX = $FB00, HL = $0048) and $0EDD with $3689 round it; bank 0; RUN_SETUP with DE =\n   E_LINE.","comment":"A report pending?"},
        "2804": {"comment":"ROM 3's EDIT_LINE_NO: BC = the number"},
        "2807": {"comment":"A numbered line: stored"},
        "2812": {"comment":"An empty line?"},
        "2818": {"comment":"A direct command: three returns dropped"},
        "2821": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6?"},
        "2827": {"comment":"No: ROM 0's $0EC9"},
        "2832": {"synopsis":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared; in bank 7, with $D5B8 = 8: $D5BA = $5B7B, $D5B9 = $5C7F, and with\n$5C7F bit 3 ROM 0's $272B.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "2836": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "2837": {"comment":"The byte at $D5B8 8?"},
        "2844": {"comment":"$D5BA = the byte at $5B7B"},
        "2850": {"comment":"$D5B9 = the byte at $5C7F"},
        "2856": {"comment":"Its bit 3?"},
        "2860": {"comment":"IX = $FB00, HL = $0048"},
        "2867": {"comment":"ROM 0's $272B"},
        "2872": {"synopsis":"ROM 0's $0EDD, with $3689 before and after it when the word at $D5B7 has its low byte's bit\n6 and its high byte clear; bank 0; then RUN_SETUP with DE = E_LINE.","comment":"The word at $D5B7"},
        "2875": {"comment":"Z: low bit 6 and high byte both 0?"},
        "2880": {"comment":"Z: $3689 first"},
        "2883": {"comment":"ROM 0's $0EDD"},
        "2889": {"comment":"Z: $3689 after"},
        "2892": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "2893": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "2897": {"synopsis":"Runs the line at DE as a direct command:\n1. The handler in $5B6C = AFTER_RUN; $105E (MMU slot 1 from $5B58 and more).\n2. $5B3A under ERR_SP.\n3. The alternate ROM's $2E20.\n4. TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared, SCR_CT = $19 - the screen line, FLAGS bit 7 set (running).\n5. PPC = $FFFE, HL = WORKSP - 1; $38D4 with A = $FF; then LINE_GO with DE one back.","comment":"The handler: AFTER_RUN"},
        "2903": {"comment":"The line kept"},
        "2908": {"comment":"$5B3A under ERR_SP"},
        "2917": {"comment":"Alternate ROM's $2E20"},
        "2923": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "2928": {"comment":"SCR_CT = $19 - the line"},
        "2936": {"comment":"Running"},
        "2940": {"comment":"DE one before the line"},
        "2941": {"comment":"PPC = $FFFE: a direct command"},
        "2947": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - 1, NXTLIN for it"},
        "2951": {"comment":"$5B77 = $FF"},
        "2958": {"comment":"Run"},
        "2961": {"synopsis":"The handler after a numbered line is stored ($0D44 sets it): in bank 7 ROM 0's $0EDD; ERR_NR\n= $0F; AFTER_RUN's finish (AR_FINISH).","comment":"Bank 7"},
        "2962": {"comment":"ROM 0's $0EDD"},
        "2967": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "2968": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $0F"},
        "2974": {"synopsis":"Where a run ends, with or without a report (the handler in $5B6C):\n1. $3B18 with C = $23, and $3A86 when it gives NC.\n2. With a report: if CURCHL's low byte is not $5C, $5EBA = $5B77; after report 9 or L the\n   statement after (SUBPPC + 1); OLDPPC and OSPPC from PPC and SUBPPC.\n3. SUBPPC back.\n4. No report: AR_FINISH.\n5. A report: its code + 1, PPC, SUBPPC and the byte at $5B77 stored in the DivMMC memory\n   ($3140-$3146, through $3EB7/$3EB9); $3A86 with C = $4B: NC means a handler takes it\n   ($3A40 with A = $4B, ERR_NR = $FF, and the run goes on at STMT_AT_CHAR with $5B3A under\n   it); carry, AR_FINISH.","comment":"Two words kept"},
        "2976": {"comment":"$3B18 with C = $23"},
        "2981": {"comment":"NC: $3A86"},
        "2986": {"comment":"SUBPPC kept"},
        "2991": {"comment":"A report? (ERR_NR + 1 = 0: none)"},
        "2997": {"comment":"The code kept in A'"},
        "2998": {"comment":"CURCHL's low byte $5C?"},
        "3003": {"comment":"$5EBA = $5B77"},
        "3009": {"synopsis":"Report 9 or L: CONTINUE goes on with the next statement.","comment":"The code + 1"},
        "3010": {"comment":"Report 9?"},
        "3014": {"comment":"Report L?"},
        "3018": {"synopsis":"SUBPPC + 1."},
        "3019": {"synopsis":"OLDPPC and OSPPC = PPC and SUBPPC (the three bytes $5C45-$5C47 to $5C6E-$5C70).","comment":"PPC, SUBPPC to OLDPPC, OSPPC"},
        "3027": {"synopsis":"SUBPPC back; a report is offered to the error trap.","comment":"SUBPPC as it was"},
        "3031": {"comment":"No report: finish"},
        "3034": {"comment":"The code + 1 to the DivMMC memory's $3140"},
        "3041": {"comment":"PPC to $3142"},
        "3051": {"comment":"SUBPPC to $3144"},
        "3063": {"comment":"The byte at $5B77 to $3146"},
        "3073": {"comment":"$5B3A under it"},
        "3077": {"comment":"STMT_AT_CHAR the way on"},
        "3081": {"comment":"C = $4B"},
        "3083": {"comment":"A handler? Carry: none"},
        "3088": {"comment":"$3A40 with A = $4B"},
        "3093": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no report"},
        "3097": {"comment":"The run goes on"},
        "3098": {"synopsis":"The two words for the trap dropped (also from $2C9C)."},
        "3100": {"synopsis":"The alternate ROM's $2D87; with $5B68 bit 0 set (RUN_LINE_SAVED), the stack copied back from\nRAM page $10 and a return to ROM 2's caller; otherwise REPORT_CODE.","comment":"Alternate ROM's $2D87"},
        "3105": {"comment":"Run for ROM 2 (RUN_LINE_SAVED)?"},
        "3112": {"comment":"RAM page $10 at $2000"},
        "3116": {"comment":"SP = RAMTOP + 1 - the length kept"},
        "3128": {"comment":"The stack copied back from $2216"},
        "3134": {"comment":"This ROM back at $2000"},
        "3138": {"comment":"Back to ROM 2's caller"},
        "3139": {"synopsis":"The report: FLAGS bit 5 cleared; A = ERR_NR + 1 and WORKSP kept; FLAGX and X_PTR's high byte\n= 0. In bank 7, with $D5B8 = 8 and $5C7F's low 4 bits 9: ROM 0's $2727 (IX = $FB00, HL =\n$004C); otherwise PRINT_ENTER. Then ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS, ROM 0's $0EC9, TV_FLAG bit 5 set,\nstream -3 ($1368).","comment":"No key waiting"},
        "3143": {"comment":"A = ERR_NR + 1, kept"},
        "3148": {"comment":"WORKSP kept"},
        "3155": {"comment":"FLAGX = 0"},
        "3158": {"comment":"X_PTR's high byte = 0"},
        "3161": {"comment":"The byte at $D5B8 in bank 7"},
        "3166": {"comment":"Is it 8?"},
        "3170": {"comment":"$5C7F's low 4 bits 9?"},
        "3179": {"comment":"IX = $FB00, HL = $004C"},
        "3186": {"comment":"ROM 0's $2727"},
        "3193": {"synopsis":"ENTER printed."},
        "3196": {"synopsis":"The edit line emptied (ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS), ROM 0's $0EC9, TV_FLAG bit 5 set, stream -3\n($1368 with A = $FD); then the code.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_EDIT_WS"},
        "3199": {"comment":"ROM 0's $0EC9"},
        "3204": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 set"},
        "3208": {"comment":"Stream -3"},
        "3213": {"comment":"DE = WORKSP as kept"},
        "3214": {"comment":"A = ERR_NR + 1"},
        "3216": {"comment":"ERR_NR $FE?"},
        "3220": {"comment":"The text at DE printed"},
        "3225": {"synopsis":"No report (0) and the byte at $D5B8 not 0: no report printed (on at $0D10).","comment":"Report 0, OK?"},
        "3228": {"comment":"The byte at $D5B8 in bank 7"},
        "3233": {"comment":"Not 0: no report shown"},
        "3236": {"synopsis":"The code's character: 0-9 a digit, 10-$1C a capital letter, $1D-$2B a small letter, $2C up\nnone.","comment":"Below 10: a digit"},
        "3240": {"comment":"$1D up?"},
        "3244": {"comment":"$2C up: no character"},
        "3248": {"comment":"$1D-$2B: 'a' up"},
        "3252": {"synopsis":"10-$1C: 'A' up."},
        "3254": {"synopsis":"The code's character (ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT) and a space.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT"},
        "3257": {"comment":"A space"},
        "3262": {"synopsis":"The report's message ($0D1B with A = the code + 1).","comment":"The message"},
        "3266": {"synopsis":"\", \" (ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE, message 0 of $1536), then the line and statement.","comment":"Message 0 of ROM 3's $1536: \", \""},
        "3273": {"comment":"CURCHL's low byte $5C?"},
        "3278": {"comment":"The byte at $5B77, if not $FF"},
        "3284": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "3288": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_BC_NUM"},
        "3291": {"comment":"':'"},
        "3296": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "3298": {"synopsis":"BC = PPC; it becomes E_PPC when no number came first, the line is a program line, there is a\nreport, and the report is not 0, $0C or $14 (codes + 1 $0D, $15).","comment":"BC = PPC"},
        "3302": {"comment":"The number printed already?"},
        "3304": {"comment":"A direct command?"},
        "3308": {"comment":"No report?"},
        "3314": {"comment":"Report C?"},
        "3318": {"comment":"Report L?"},
        "3322": {"comment":"E_PPC = the line"},
        "3326": {"synopsis":"The line number (ROM 3's PRINT_BC_NUM), ':', the statement (SUBPPC without bit 7); $5B6A =\n$5BFF; ROM 0's $0E60.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_BC_NUM"},
        "3329": {"comment":"':'"},
        "3334": {"comment":"C = SUBPPC without bit 7"},
        "3341": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_BC_NUM"},
        "3344": {"comment":"The alternate SP back to $5BFF","synopsis":"No report printed (a nonzero byte at $D5B8 in bank 7): the alternate stack pointer ($5B6A)\nback to $5BFF, then on to ROM 0's $0E60, which does not come back here."},
        "3350": {"comment":"ROM 0's $0E60"},
        "3355": {"synopsis":"Prints the message of report code A:\n1. A code below $1D is a 48K report: ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE with its REPORT_MESSAGES table\n   ($1391), message A + 1.\n2. Otherwise A - $1D (capped at $4A, so codes over $67 share the last entry) indexes the 75\n   words at $2705; the message there is printed by $37D6 (text with bit 7 on its last\n   character). Called from page 0 and page 2 too (RST $18 / CALL $3F00 with $0D1B).\nEntry: A = the report code.","comment":"A 48K report (code below $1D)?"},
        "3359": {"comment":"The own reports: index A - $1D"},
        "3361": {"comment":"Past the table's last entry ($4A)?"},
        "3365": {"comment":"All higher codes share the last entry"},
        "3367": {"synopsis":"The message's address from the word table at $2705.","comment":"BC = the index"},
        "3370": {"comment":"The table of message addresses at $2705"},
        "3375": {"comment":"DE = the message's address"},
        "3378": {"comment":"Printed by $37D6 (bit-7-ended text)"},
        "3381": {"synopsis":"A 48K report's message: ROM 3's REPORT_MESSAGES through PRINT_MESSAGE.","comment":"ROM 3's REPORT_MESSAGES table"},
        "3384": {"comment":"Message A + 1 printed (ROM 3's PRINT_MESSAGE)"},
        "3388": {"synopsis":"Stores the edit line as program line BC:\n1. E_PPC = BC; $5B6C = $0B91 (where $0AB0 goes on after closing the files) and $5B3A stacked\n   (dropped at the end).\n2. The text's length is WORKSP - CH_ADD - 1.\n3. An old line BC is removed (ROM 3's FIND_LINE, NEXT_ITEM, RECLAIM).\n4. A text of just the ENTER stores nothing: the alternate ROM's $13F9 is called with HL =\n   E_PPC, its result into E_PPC.\n5. Otherwise room for the text and a four-byte head (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM, PROG kept), the text\n   copied, the number (high byte first) and the length put in front.\nEntry: BC = the line number, CH_ADD at the text. Called from $0AF9.","comment":"E_PPC = BC, the line's number"},
        "3392": {"comment":"DE = CH_ADD, the line's text"},
        "3396": {"comment":"$5B6C = $0B91, for the JP (HL) at $0AB9"},
        "3402": {"comment":"$5B3A stacked: closes files, then jumps via $5B6C"},
        "3406": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - CH_ADD - 1: the text's length"},
        "3412": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "3413": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "3415": {"comment":"ROM 3's FIND_LINE"},
        "3418": {"comment":"Not there: no old line to remove"},
        "3420": {"comment":"The old line's length (ROM 3's NEXT_ITEM)"},
        "3423": {"comment":"The old line removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM)"},
        "3426": {"synopsis":"Only an ENTER?","comment":"BC = the text's length"},
        "3427": {"comment":"Just the ENTER (length 1)?"},
        "3430": {"comment":"No: the line goes in"},
        "3432": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the alternate stack"},
        "3434": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC"},
        "3437": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's $13F9 with HL = E_PPC"},
        "3442": {"comment":"E_PPC = its result"},
        "3446": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the main stack again"},
        "3447": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3449": {"synopsis":"Room for the line and its four-byte head (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), PROG kept; the text copied;\nthe length and the number written in front.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "3450": {"comment":"BC + 4: room for the number and the length too"},
        "3454": {"comment":"HL = the place before the line found"},
        "3455": {"comment":"PROG kept over the call"},
        "3460": {"comment":"The room opened (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "3463": {"comment":"PROG restored"},
        "3467": {"comment":"BC = the text's length"},
        "3469": {"comment":"DE = the room's last byte"},
        "3470": {"comment":"HL = the text's last byte (WORKSP - 2)"},
        "3475": {"comment":"The text copied, last byte first"},
        "3477": {"comment":"HL = E_PPC, the line's number"},
        "3481": {"comment":"The length word and the number in front"},
        "3482": {"comment":"Length high byte"},
        "3484": {"comment":"Length low byte"},
        "3486": {"comment":"Number low byte"},
        "3488": {"comment":"Number high byte (numbers are stored high first)"},
        "3489": {"synopsis":"The $5B3A address dropped; done.","comment":"The $5B3A address dropped"},
        "3491": {"synopsis":"RST $08: stops with the error code in the byte after the RST (CALL $08EF builds such an RST\non the stack).\n1. $5B5E = the code.\n2. A code below $1D is a 48K report: ROM 3 is entered at $5B5D, the byte before the code.\n3. Otherwise (ERROR_128_OWN) ERR_NR = the code, SP = ERR_SP, the alternate ROM's $1852 is\n   called with A = 0 (in bank 7), X_PTR = CH_ADD, ROM 3's CALC_RESET, and RET goes to the\n   address at ERR_SP.\nEntry: the stacked return address points at the code byte.","comment":"HL = the address of the code byte"},
        "3492": {"comment":"A = the error code"},
        "3493": {"synopsis":"ERROR_128 with the code in A: the entry page 0 uses (RST $18 / DEFW $0DA5).","comment":"$5B5E = the code"},
        "3496": {"comment":"A code below $1D is ROM 3's own report"},
        "3501": {"comment":"ROM 3 entered at $5B5D, whose next byte is the code"},
        "3504": {"synopsis":"NextZXOS's own reports (code $1D up): ERR_NR = the code, the stack and the calculator reset,\nthen the return to ERR_SP's address.","comment":"Back to the code"},
        "3505": {"comment":"ERR_NR = the code"},
        "3508": {"comment":"The stack back to ERR_SP"},
        "3512": {"comment":"Bank 7 and the alternate stack"},
        "3513": {"comment":"A = 0 for the alternate ROM's $1852"},
        "3519": {"comment":"Bank 0 and the main stack again"},
        "3520": {"comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD: where the error was"},
        "3526": {"comment":"ROM 3's CALC_RESET; RET goes to ERR_SP's address"},
        "3530": {"synopsis":"Stops with the error that A holds, as returned by a ROM 2 call: CALL $08F4 takes the byte\n$FF after the CALL, which tells $08EF's code to make the report code from A (A + $3D below\n10, A + $18 otherwise). Reached by the JP NC at $30AE. The RST $30 and JR after it are never\nreached, since $08F4 does not return.","comment":"Error from A: the $FF after the CALL says so"},
        "3534": {"comment":"Bank 0 first","synopsis":"Pages RAM bank 0 back in (RST $30), then DOS_ERROR: stops with the error a ROM 2 call left\nin A. Jumped to from $0135 (A3_ERROR) and $2B9C."},
        "3537": {"synopsis":"Calculator code copied onto the stack and run by $09BA (10 bytes, from $3F4B): RST $28,\nstk-data ($34) 65536 ($40 $41 $00 $00), multiply ($04), addition ($0F), end-calc ($38), RET.\nWith x and y on the calculator stack it leaves x + y * 65536."},
        "3547": {"synopsis":"Calculator code copied onto the stack and run by $09BA (13 bytes, from $3F74): RST $28,\nexchange ($01), st-mem-1 ($C1), delete ($02), stk-data ($34) 65536 ($40 $41 $00 $00),\nn-mod-m ($32), get-mem-1 ($E1), end-calc ($38), RET. With x and y stacked it leaves y MOD\n65536, INT (y / 65536) and x."},
        "3560": {"synopsis":"Z when checking syntax (FLAGS bit 7 clear), NZ when running.\nChanges: F.","comment":"FLAGS bit 7: Z when checking syntax"},
        "3565": {"synopsis":"An optional number: at the statement's end 0 is stacked when running ($3887); otherwise the\nexpression must be a number (ROM 3's CLASS_6, through $3EC1). Nothing in the four pages\nrefers to $0DED.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD, A the character there"},
        "3568": {"comment":"End of the statement here?","synopsis":"NUM_OR_ZERO with A already the character at CH_ADD (from $056B)."},
        "3571": {"comment":"Yes: 0 stacked when running"},
        "3574": {"comment":"Otherwise a number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "3580": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR, through $3EC1 (which stacks $5B3E so that the RET comes back to this\nROM).","comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR, through $3EC1"},
        "3586": {"synopsis":"Parses OPT_RANGE's optional ', a [TO b]', then an optional STEP s and an optional STOP or\nRUN, shifting a flag bit for each into HL and D/E: STEP given or not into HL; STOP or RUN\ngiven into D and, for RUN, a 1 into E. The alternate ROM's page 1 calls it\n($0BBE, $0BCD); nothing in NextZXOS's four pages does.\nEntry: HL, DE = the flags so far.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "3587": {"comment":"The optional range: two flag bits into HL"},
        "3590": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3591": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "3594": {"comment":"STEP?"},
        "3596": {"comment":"Carry clear: no STEP"},
        "3600": {"comment":"STEP: past it, then a number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "3603": {"comment":"Carry set: STEP given"},
        "3604": {"synopsis":"The STEP flag (carry) shifted into HL.","comment":"The flags back"},
        "3605": {"comment":"The STEP flag shifted into HL"},
        "3610": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "3611": {"comment":"STOP?"},
        "3615": {"comment":"RUN?"},
        "3619": {"comment":"Neither: a 0 bit into D, D's bit 7 to carry"},
        "3621": {"comment":"And into E"},
        "3623": {"synopsis":"STOP or RUN: a 1 bit into D, past the keyword; carry set for RUN.","comment":"STOP or RUN: a 1 bit into D"},
        "3626": {"comment":"Past the keyword, AF and HL kept"},
        "3631": {"comment":"Carry set for RUN, clear for STOP"},
        "3634": {"synopsis":"The carry into E.","comment":"The bit into E"},
        "3637": {"synopsis":"An optional ', a [TO b]' at CH_ADD: with no ',' (or a ',' followed by another ',', STEP or\nSTOP) two 0 bits are shifted into HL; otherwise the first number (ROM 3's CLASS_6), and the\nsecond after TO, or the first stacked twice when running; then two 1 bits.\nEntry: HL = the flags.\nExit: HL = the flags shifted left 2.","comment":"DE = the flags so far"},
        "3638": {"comment":"Two flag bits"},
        "3640": {"comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "3643": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "3645": {"comment":"Carry clear: no range"},
        "3648": {"comment":"No ',': two 0 bits"},
        "3650": {"comment":"Past the ','"},
        "3651": {"comment":"Another ',', STEP or STOP: no range either"},
        "3663": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "3664": {"comment":"The first number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "3667": {"comment":"TO after it?"},
        "3671": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "3675": {"comment":"The number off the calculator stack"},
        "3678": {"comment":"Put back"},
        "3681": {"comment":"And stacked again: the range is one number"},
        "3686": {"synopsis":"TO: past it, the second number.","comment":"TO: past it, then the second number"},
        "3689": {"synopsis":"A range: two 1 bits.","comment":"The flags back"},
        "3690": {"comment":"Two 1 bits: a range given"},
        "3693": {"synopsis":"HL = the flags; carry shifted in B times.","comment":"HL = the flags"},
        "3694": {"synopsis":"Shifts the carry into HL B times: HL = HL x 2 + carry, B times.\nExit: AF as on entry.\nChanges: B, HL.","comment":"The carry kept"},
        "3695": {"synopsis":"One bit.","comment":"The carry restored each time"},
        "3697": {"comment":"HL doubled, the carry into bit 0"},
        "3699": {"comment":"B times"},
        "3701": {"comment":"The carry back as it came"},
        "3703": {"synopsis":"RST $10 (from $0010, which parks HL at $5B52 and stacks AF): a function call by the byte\nafter the RST.\n1. The page in MMU slot 1 is read from the byte at $2000 (the page there holds its own\n   number).\n2. Bit 7 of the function byte set: the word after it goes to $5B5A.\n3. Functions 0 and 1 jump through the word table at $3E00 (both entries are $3439), with the\n   ROM paged into MMU slot 1 and BC, HL, AF as the caller had them; any other number goes to\n   $3439 too.\n4. RST10_BACK is stacked to put the old page back into slot 1 and return past the inline\n   bytes.\nNo RST $10 occurs in this ROM's code.","comment":"BC parked at $5B54 (HL is at $5B52)"},
        "3707": {"comment":"A = the byte at $2000: the page now in MMU slot 1"},
        "3710": {"comment":"B = that page, for the way back"},
        "3711": {"comment":"A = the function byte after the RST"},
        "3713": {"comment":"Doubled; bit 7 to carry"},
        "3714": {"comment":"Bit 7: a word follows too"},
        "3716": {"synopsis":"Only functions 0 and 1; their table entry.","comment":"Only functions 0 and 1 exist"},
        "3718": {"comment":"Others go to $3439"},
        "3721": {"comment":"C = 2 x the function"},
        "3722": {"comment":"The caller's AF back"},
        "3723": {"comment":"The way back: past the inline bytes"},
        "3724": {"comment":"The old page and the index kept"},
        "3725": {"comment":"Then RST10_BACK, which restores the page"},
        "3729": {"comment":"The ROM into MMU slot 1 ($2000-$3FFF)"},
        "3733": {"comment":"HL = $3E00 + 2 x function: the table entry"},
        "3736": {"comment":"BC = the routine's address"},
        "3739": {"comment":"Stacked, to RET into"},
        "3740": {"comment":"BC and HL back as the caller left them"},
        "3747": {"comment":"Into the routine"},
        "3748": {"synopsis":"Bit 7 set: the word after the function byte into $5B5A.","comment":"The function byte's word into $5B5A"},
        "3757": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "3758": {"comment":"On with the function"},
        "3760": {"synopsis":"Where RST10_DISPATCH's routines return: the old page back into MMU slot 1, A kept, then the\nRET past the inline bytes.","comment":"HL = the old page (H), the routine's HL stacked"},
        "3761": {"comment":"A kept in L"},
        "3762": {"comment":"The old page back into MMU slot 1"},
        "3766": {"comment":"A back"},
        "3767": {"comment":"HL back; RET past the inline bytes"},
        "3769": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at BC with 8K page A in MMU slot 1 ($2000-$3FFF), then puts the ROM back\nthere. Nothing in the four pages refers to $0EB9.\nEntry: A = the page, BC = the routine.","comment":"8K page A into MMU slot 1"},
        "3772": {"comment":"The routine at BC"},
        "3775": {"comment":"The ROM back into MMU slot 1"},
        "3780": {"synopsis":"Jumps to BC (CALL $0EC4 calls the routine at BC).","comment":"RET into BC"},
        "3782": {"synopsis":"Finds where a name is defined in the program: a label ('@'), a $91 name or a DEF FN, by IXh\n(the kind's character) and IXl (the character that ends the name).\n1. X_PTR = HL, the name.\n2. A program in the usual place ($5B65 = $FF): the index in the 8K page at $5B58\n   (FIND_NAME_MAIN). A program in bank $5B65: that bank at $C000, its signature checked\n   ($39D1), its index built first when $C000 bit 7 is clear ($1015), then FIND_NAME_BANK.\n3. The index's list for the kind and the name's first letter is searched; names past the\n   indexed part are looked for line by line (FIND_NAME_SCAN), each statement that starts\n   with the kind's character compared, spaces and case ignored (NAME_CHAR).\nExit: carry when found: D' = the statement's number, IX = the line's text, BC = its length,\nHL at the name in the line. Bank 0 is back for a program in a bank.","comment":"X_PTR = the name looked for"},
        "3785": {"comment":"$5B65 = $FF: the program is in the usual place"},
        "3789": {"comment":"Yes: the index in the page at $5B58"},
        "3792": {"comment":"A = the bank holding the program"},
        "3793": {"comment":"The bank at $C000 ($32D0)"},
        "3796": {"comment":"Its \"BC\" signature checked; A = $C000's low byte"},
        "3799": {"comment":"Bit 7 clear: no index yet"},
        "3800": {"comment":"Built first"},
        "3803": {"comment":"Then the bank's index"},
        "3805": {"synopsis":"No entry in the lists: a search line by line from the first line the index left out (its\noffset at +$A1).","comment":"The index's base: $2000 in slot 1"},
        "3811": {"comment":"...or, for a program in a bank, ($FFF8)"},
        "3817": {"comment":"The word at +$A1: where unindexed lines start","synopsis":"HL = the index's header base; the word at +$A1 is where the unindexed lines start."},
        "3824": {"comment":"HL = BC (the program's start) + that offset"},
        "3826": {"comment":"The ROM back into MMU slot 1"},
        "3830": {"synopsis":"The next line; past the program, not found.","comment":"A line number's high byte, or a variable"},
