        "4053": {"comment":"DE = the lines' start"},
        "4054": {"comment":"HL = the bank's index"},
        "4059": {"synopsis":"Where to start looking for line BC in the usual program: the index's 8K page ($5B58) into\nMMU slot 1, then LINE_INDEX_LOOK with DE = PROG. Called from $3965.","comment":"The index's 8K page into MMU slot 1"},
        "4065": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "4069": {"comment":"HL = the index, at $2000"},
        "4072": {"synopsis":"The line table: BC (capped at the highest number, at +$9F) shifted right by the shift at\n+$9E picks a word of the table whose offset is at +$9C; HL = the lines' start + that word.\nExit: HL = the line to start at, BC as on entry; the ROM back in MMU slot 1.","comment":"The line number and the lines' start kept"},
        "4074": {"comment":"The line table's header at +$9C"},
        "4078": {"comment":"DE = the table's offset"},
        "4082": {"comment":"A' = the shift"},
        "4085": {"comment":"HL = the highest line number"},
