        "4094": {"comment":"Then BC = the highest"},
        "4097": {"synopsis":"The entry for BC.","comment":"HL = the table's offset"},
        "4098": {"comment":"DE = the line number"},
        "4100": {"comment":"B = the shift"},
        "4102": {"comment":"DE = the number >> the shift"},
        "4104": {"comment":"HL at that entry (a word each)"},
        "4106": {"comment":"DE = the entry: an offset from the start"},
        "4109": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "4110": {"comment":"HL = the line to start looking at"},
        "4111": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "4112": {"comment":"The ROM back into MMU slot 1"},
        "4117": {"synopsis":"Builds the index of a program held in the bank at $C000:\n1. The program's end found from $C002.\n2. $C000 bit 7 set (an index exists).\n3. An end at $FE00 or above leaves no room: $C001 bit 7 set and FLAGS bit 0 set, and only\n   the line table is made (BUILD_INDEX_GO).\n4. Otherwise $FFF8 = the index's start (the program's end), BUILD_INDEX makes it, $FFFC =\n   its end, $FFFE = $FFF7, $FFFA = 0.\nChanges: IX kept.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "4119": {"comment":"The bank's first line"},
        "4122": {"synopsis":"The next line, until the program's end.","comment":"A line's high byte, or the end"},
        "4124": {"comment":"Past the last line?"},
        "4128": {"comment":"Past the number"},
        "4129": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "4133": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "4134": {"comment":"On"},
        "4136": {"synopsis":"DE = the program's end.","comment":"DE = the program's end"},
        "4137": {"comment":"$C000 bit 7: an index is made"},
        "4142": {"comment":"The end at $FE00 or above?"},
        "4145": {"comment":"Then no room for an index"},
        "4147": {"comment":"HL = the program's end"},
        "4148": {"comment":"$FFF8 = the index's start"},
        "4151": {"comment":"DE = the first line"},
        "4154": {"comment":"The index built after the program"},
        "4157": {"comment":"$FFFC = its end"},
        "4160": {"comment":"$FFFE = $FFF7"},
        "4166": {"comment":"$FFFA = 0"},
        "4172": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "4175": {"synopsis":"No room: the line table only.","comment":"$C001 bit 7: no room"},
        "4178": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0: no name lists"},
        "4182": {"comment":"HL = the first line"},
        "4183": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "4184": {"comment":"The line table only, at HL"},
        "4187": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "4190": {"synopsis":"Builds the index of the usual program in the 8K page at $5B58 (mapped at $2000), then\nBUILD_INDEX. Called from $0B58 and $1AB7.","comment":"The index's 8K page into MMU slot 1"},
        "4196": {"comment":"HL = the index's place ($2000)"},
        "4199": {"comment":"DE = PROG"},
        "4203": {"synopsis":"Builds a program's index at HL:\n1. FLAGS2 bit 5 and FLAGS bit 0 cleared.\n2. (BUILD_INDEX_GO) The CPU at 28MHz while it runs.\n3. Unless FLAGS bit 0 is set, 79 list heads (3 kinds x 26 letters, and the lists' end)\n   pointing at empty lists.\n4. Each line, statement by statement: one starting with '@', $91 or DEF FN adds a 5-byte\n   entry to its kind's and letter's list (the statement number, the name's offset, the\n   line's offset); when the room runs out ($FFE6) $5B52 keeps the first line left out\n   (FLAGS2 bit 5). A line with a $98 has every $FA at a statement start changed to $83.\n5. The line table: the highest number at +$9F, the smallest shift that fits the room up to\n   $FFF6 at +$9E, then a word per 2^shift line numbers giving the first line at or after it.\n   The first line left out goes at +$A1.\n6. The CPU speed and the ROM in MMU slot 1 put back.\nEntry: HL = the index's place, DE = the program's start.","comment":"$5C6A bit 5: no line left out yet"},
        "4207": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0: name lists wanted"},
        "4211": {"synopsis":"With FLAGS bit 0 as the caller left it: the speed raised, then the work.","comment":"A = NextReg 7 (CPU speed)"},
        "4216": {"comment":"The speed kept"},
        "4219": {"comment":"28MHz while building"},
        "4223": {"comment":"The program's start and the index's kept"},
        "4225": {"comment":"Lists not wanted?"},
        "4229": {"comment":"Then skip their heads"},
        "4231": {"comment":"DE = the empty lists, $A3 bytes on"},
        "4237": {"comment":"A = 0: an empty list's end mark"},
        "4238": {"comment":"79 list heads: 3 kinds x 26, and one more"},
        "4240": {"synopsis":"One list head and its empty list.","comment":"The head points at its own end mark"},
        "4244": {"comment":"The end mark"},
        "4248": {"synopsis":"The lines scanned; HL' = 0, $5B54 = 0.","comment":"HL = the index"},
        "4249": {"comment":"HL' = 0"},
        "4253": {"comment":"$5B54 = 0: no line number yet"},
        "4256": {"comment":"HL = the program's start"},
        "4257": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4258": {"synopsis":"A line: its number into $5B54.","comment":"A = the line number's high byte, or the end"},
        "4259": {"comment":"Past the program?"},
        "4264": {"comment":"BC = the line number"},
        "4268": {"comment":"$5B54 = it: the last line seen"},
        "4272": {"comment":"Past the length word"},
        "4273": {"comment":"The line's start kept"},
        "4274": {"comment":"B = 1: the first statement"},
        "4276": {"comment":"$5C6A bit 6: not a line with $98 yet"},
        "4280": {"synopsis":"The statement's first character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "4282": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
