        "4654": {"comment":"Spaces and control codes skipped"},
        "4658": {"comment":"'[' or above: as it is"},
        "4661": {"comment":"Below 'A': as it is"},
        "4664": {"comment":"A capital made small"},
        "4667": {"synopsis":"The line's end: ':'.","comment":"The line's end reads as ':'"},
        "4670": {"synopsis":"FIND_STMT_CHAR from CH_ADD.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "4673": {"synopsis":"Looks for a statement, within the next D (0 = any), whose first character (spaces and\ncontrol codes skipped) is E: statements end at ':', THEN or $98 outside quotes, numbers'\nhidden 5 bytes skipped.\nExit: no carry with HL at it; carry at the line's end or after D statements.\nChanges: AF, C, D, HL.","comment":"C = 0: outside quotes"},
        "4675": {"synopsis":"A new statement: one fewer to look at.","comment":"D statements looked at?"},
        "4676": {"comment":"Carry: not found"},
        "4678": {"synopsis":"Its first character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "4680": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4684": {"comment":"Spaces and control codes skipped"},
        "4688": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "4689": {"comment":"No: skip this statement"},
        "4691": {"comment":"Found: no carry, HL at it"},
        "4693": {"synopsis":"Past a number's marker and 5 bytes.","comment":"Past a number's 5 bytes"},
        "4697": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "4698": {"synopsis":"Skips to the next statement's start (FIND_STMT_CHAR's inner loop): C = 0 outside quotes, D\nstatements."},
        "4699": {"synopsis":"SKIP_STMT with A already the character at HL.","comment":"A number's marker?"},
        "4703": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "4707": {"comment":"Quotes counted in C (bit 0: inside)"},
        "4710": {"synopsis":"A separator?","comment":"A ':'?"},
        "4714": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "4718": {"comment":"$98?"},
        "4722": {"synopsis":"Outside quotes: a new statement.","comment":"Outside quotes: a new statement starts"},
        "4726": {"synopsis":"The line's end?","comment":"The line's end?"},
        "4728": {"comment":"Otherwise on"},
        "4730": {"synopsis":"The line ended: carry.","comment":"D down once more"},
        "4731": {"comment":"Carry: the line ended"},
        "4733": {"synopsis":"Reads NextReg A through ports $243B and $253B.\nExit: A = its value, BC = $253B.","comment":"NextReg A selected"},
        "4738": {"comment":"BC = $253B"},
        "4739": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "4742": {"synopsis":"Goes to where a name is defined (called from $21E4 and $2618):\n1. $5B92 = SP; the frame for the jump made by $3A40, the return address kept on top.\n2. A ($21-$23) picks the kind at NAME_KINDS: IXh its character, IXl its terminator.\n3. FIND_NAME with HL = CH_ADD ($5B8A = it).\n4. Not found: error code $61 for $91, $18 (report P) for DEF FN, $65 for a label.\n5. Found: X_PTR = past the name; CH_ADD = the name in the line (in the bank's window for a\n   program in a bank).\nExit: DE = the line's number, HL = the next line, A = the statement's number.","comment":"$5B92 = SP on entry"},
        "4746": {"comment":"The return address taken off into AF'"},
        "4749": {"comment":"The frame for the jump made ($3A40)"},
        "4752": {"comment":"The return address back on top"},
        "4755": {"comment":"A = $21-$23 picks the kind"},
        "4758": {"comment":"The kinds at NAME_KINDS, two bytes each"},
        "4763": {"comment":"IXh = the kind's character"},
        "4767": {"comment":"IXl = the character that ends its name"},
        "4770": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD: the name"},
        "4773": {"comment":"A program in a bank?"},
        "4777": {"comment":"Then HL made relative to it ($39E3)"},
        "4780": {"comment":"$5B8A = the name's place"},
        "4783": {"comment":"Looked up (FIND_NAME)"},
        "4786": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "4788": {"comment":"Not found: $91?"},
        "4792": {"comment":"Error code $61 ($2159)"},
        "4795": {"comment":"DEF FN?"},
        "4799": {"comment":"'@': error code $65"},
        "4801": {"synopsis":"Error code $18 (report P, FN without DEF).","comment":"Error code $18 (report P, FN without DEF)"},
        "4803": {"synopsis":"Found: CH_ADD at the name, DE = the line's number.","comment":"X_PTR = past the name"},
        "4807": {"comment":"The line's place kept"},
        "4809": {"comment":"IXh = the statement's number"},
        "4813": {"comment":"A program in a bank?"},
        "4819": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "4820": {"comment":"HL = the line's place, the name's stacked"},
        "4821": {"comment":"Back 4: the line's start"},
        "4825": {"comment":"Made a bank address ($3925)"},
        "4828": {"comment":"HL = the name again"},
        "4829": {"comment":"Less ($5EBB)"},
        "4836": {"comment":"...plus $5DB6: CH_ADD in the bank's window"},
        "4840": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "4843": {"comment":"DE = the line's number, high byte first"},
        "4847": {"comment":"HL = the line's place"},
        "4850": {"synopsis":"The usual program: CH_ADD = the name; the line's number and the next line.","comment":"CH_ADD = the name"},
        "4853": {"comment":"HL = the line's text"},
        "4854": {"comment":"Back to the line's start"},
        "4857": {"comment":"DE = its number (stored high byte first)"},
        "4860": {"comment":"Past the number and the length"},
        "4864": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "4865": {"synopsis":"A = the statement's number.","comment":"A = the statement's number"},
        "4868": {"synopsis":"The kinds of name JUMP_TO_NAME looks for, two bytes each (the kind's character, the\ncharacter that ends the name), for A = $21-$23: '@' and ':', $91 and '(', DEF FN ($CE) and\n'('."},
        "4874": {"synopsis":"A name ending with ':' (CHECK_NAME), then the end of the statement. Reached from the syntax\ntable (the word at $0329).","comment":"E = ':': a label's name ends with it"},
        "4876": {"comment":"The name checked"},
        "4879": {"comment":"The statement ends (checking: on to the next)"},
        "4883": {"synopsis":"CHECK_NAME for a name ending with '('.","comment":"E = '(': the name ends with it"},
        "4885": {"synopsis":"Checks a name at CH_ADD: a letter, letters and digits, an optional '$', then the character\nin E (for ':' the line's end will do). Report C otherwise.\nEntry: E = the terminator.\nExit: Z; D = $40 for a number's name, 0 for a string's; CH_ADD at the terminator.","comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "4888": {"comment":"Not a letter?"},
        "4891": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "4893": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "4894": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4895": {"comment":"D = $40: a number's name"},
        "4898": {"comment":"A letter or a digit?"},
        "4901": {"comment":"Then on"},
        "4903": {"comment":"A '$'?"},
        "4907": {"comment":"Past it: the end must follow"},
        "4909": {"comment":"D = 0: a string's name"},
        "4912": {"synopsis":"The line's end for a ':' name?","comment":"The line's end"},
        "4916": {"comment":"...counts as ':' for a label"},
        "4920": {"synopsis":"Report C, Nonsense in BASIC.","comment":"Report C, Nonsense in BASIC"},
        "4922": {"synopsis":"The upper screen made current when running (from $05C5): TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared, stream -2\n(ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT), the mode's colours made temporary (MODE_TO_TEMP); in a mode other\nthan 0 also MASK_T bits 7-3 set and P_FLAG bit 6 cleared.","comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0: the main screen"},
        "4926": {"comment":"Stream -2, the upper screen (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT)"},
        "4931": {"comment":"The mode's colours made temporary"},
        "4934": {"comment":"Mode 0: done"},
        "4935": {"comment":"MASK_T: bits 7-3 set"},
        "4942": {"comment":"P_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "4947": {"synopsis":"When running, makes stream A current (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT); for the channels 'S' and 'K'\nthen SC_MODE_COLOURS. Checking syntax it returns to its caller's caller.\nEntry: A = the stream.","comment":"Checking syntax: back to the caller's caller"},
        "4950": {"comment":"Stream A made current (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT)"},
        "4953": {"comment":"C = the channel's letter it left?"},
        "4954": {"comment":"'S'?"},
        "4958": {"comment":"'K'?"},
        "4962": {"comment":"Another channel: nothing more"},
        "4963": {"synopsis":"STREAM_COLOURS for stream -2 (the upper screen), without the letter test. Checking syntax it\nreturns to its caller's caller.","comment":"Stream -2, the upper screen"},
        "4965": {"comment":"Checking syntax: back to the caller's caller"},
        "4968": {"synopsis":"Stream A made current, then SC_MODE_COLOURS (from $0C8A with A = -3).","comment":"Stream A made current (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT)"},
        "4971": {"synopsis":"The mode's colours made temporary; outside mode 0 they are also sent down the stream as\ncontrol codes built at $5B9D: $18 or PAPER ($11) and the paper (from $3FED's carry), INK\n($10) and the ink, INVERSE ($14) and OVER ($15) from P_FLAG's temporary bits (ROM 3's\nPRINT_STRING).","comment":"The mode's colours made temporary"},
        "4974": {"comment":"Mode 0: done"},
        "4975": {"comment":"Carry from the mode ($3FED)"},
        "4978": {"comment":"The control codes built at $5B9D"},
        "4983": {"comment":"BC = the mode's ink (C) and paper (B)"},
        "4987": {"comment":"$18 first: no paper code"},
        "4989": {"comment":"...without carry"},
        "4991": {"comment":"With carry: $11 (PAPER) and B"},
        "4996": {"comment":"$10 (INK)"},
        "4998": {"synopsis":"INK and the rest."},
        "4999": {"comment":"And C"},
        "5001": {"comment":"$14 (INVERSE)"},
        "5004": {"comment":"P_FLAG"},
        "5008": {"comment":"Its bit 2: the temporary inverse"},
        "5014": {"comment":"$15 (OVER)"},
        "5017": {"comment":"Its bit 0: the temporary over"},
        "5021": {"comment":"HL past the codes"},
        "5022": {"comment":"BC = their number"},
        "5026": {"comment":"Printed (ROM 3's PRINT_STRING), DE their start"},
        "5030": {"synopsis":"Makes the current mode's colours temporary: mode 0 ($5C7F bits 3-0 = 0) by ROM 3's\nCOLOURS_TO_TEMP (carry set). Other modes: the ink from $5B5F + n and the paper from $5B88 +\nn (n from the mode, 0-7) into $5C6C-$5C6D, and P_FLAG's temporary bits from its permanent\nones (carry clear).","comment":"The mode in $5C7F's low 4 bits"},
        "5035": {"comment":"Mode 0: the 48K way"},
        "5037": {"comment":"A = mode / 2"},
        "5038": {"comment":"...bit 2 of that set"},
        "5042": {"comment":"...halved again and 1 more"},
        "5044": {"synopsis":"n = 0-7.","comment":"0-7: which pair of colours"},
        "5046": {"comment":"HL = $5B5F + it"},
        "5051": {"comment":"E = the ink"},
        "5052": {"comment":"HL = $5B88 + it"},
        "5056": {"comment":"D = the paper"},
        "5057": {"comment":"$5C6C = ink, $5C6D = paper"},
        "5061": {"comment":"P_FLAG"},
        "5064": {"comment":"Bits 1, 3, 5, 7 copied down"},
        "5070": {"comment":"...to bits 0, 2, 4, 6: temporary from permanent"},
        "5072": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP; carry.","comment":"ROM 3's COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "5075": {"comment":"Carry: mode 0"},
        "5077": {"synopsis":"A command taking a mode and an optional kind (reached from the syntax table, the word at\n$0511), probably LAYER: m [, k]. m is 0-2 (else report B). Mode 0 takes no k. Mode 1 needs k\n0-3 (bits 2-3 of the mode). Mode 2 takes an optional k 0-1, which shows (1) or hides (0)\nLayer 2 (port $123B bit 1, copied to $5B7B). Then SET_MODE.\nEntry: A = the character after the first number.","comment":"A second number after a ','?"},
        "5081": {"comment":"Past it, then the number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "5084": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "5087": {"comment":"A = the second number"},
        "5090": {"comment":"0-3 only"},
        "5094": {"synopsis":"Report B, Integer out of range.","comment":"Report B, Integer out of range"},
        "5096": {"synopsis":"No second number: $FF.","comment":"The statement must end"},
        "5099": {"comment":"A = $FF: no second number"},
        "5101": {"synopsis":"The first number: the mode.","comment":"The second number kept"},
        "5102": {"comment":"A = the first number, the mode"},
        "5105": {"comment":"D = the second"},
        "5106": {"comment":"0-2 only"},
        "5110": {"comment":"E = the mode"},
        "5111": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "5114": {"comment":"Mode 0 takes no second number"},
        "5117": {"comment":"Set"},
        "5119": {"synopsis":"Mode 1 or 2.","comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "5122": {"comment":"A = the second number"},
        "5123": {"comment":"0-3 only (a missing one is $FF: report B)"},
        "5127": {"comment":"Times 4, into bits 2-3"},
        "5129": {"comment":"E = mode 1 and its kind"},
        "5133": {"synopsis":"Mode 2: the optional Layer 2 switch.","comment":"A = the second number"},
        "5134": {"comment":"None?"},
        "5138": {"comment":"0-1 only"},
        "5142": {"comment":"Bit 1 of port $123B: Layer 2 shown or not"},
        "5148": {"comment":"$5B7B = the port's value"},
        "5151": {"synopsis":"Sets the screen mode: $5C7F bits 3-0 = E (bits 1-0 the mode, bits 3-2 mode 1's kind).\nChannels K and S get their output routine: ROM 3's PRINT_OUT ($09F4) in mode 0, $5B4D (the\nRAM routine that selects ROM 0) otherwise. Modes 2 and 3 end there (carry). Modes 0 and 1:\nMMU slot 3 gets page $0B (mode 0) or $11 (mode 1) with their contents traded (SWAP_MMU3);\nport $FF's mode bits = 0, or for mode 1 kinds 2 and 3 6 and 2, with bits 5-3 from $5B62;\nNextReg $15 bit 7 (LoRes) set for mode 1 kind 0 only.\nEntry: E = the mode, D = mode 1's kind.","comment":"$5C7F's low 4 bits = E"},
        "5160": {"comment":"A = the mode (bits 0-1)"},
        "5162": {"comment":"The page pair for mode 0"},
        "5165": {"comment":"E = the mode"},
        "5166": {"comment":"BC = ROM 3's PRINT_OUT, for mode 0"},
        "5169": {"comment":"Mode 0"},
        "5171": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "5172": {"comment":"Carry: modes 2 and 3"},
        "5175": {"comment":"Mode 1: the other page pair"},
        "5178": {"comment":"A = mode 1's kind"},
        "5180": {"comment":"Kind 0: E = $80 (NextReg $15 bit 7, LoRes)"},
        "5184": {"comment":"E = 0 for the others"},
        "5186": {"comment":"Kind 1: A = 0"},
        "5189": {"comment":"Kind 2: A = 6"},
        "5194": {"comment":"...kind 3: A = 2 (port $FF's mode bits)"},
        "5196": {"synopsis":"BC = $5B4D for the modes other than 0.","comment":"BC = $5B4D (the RAM routine selecting ROM 0)"},
        "5199": {"synopsis":"Channels K and S get the routine.","comment":"The page pair kept"},
        "5200": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5203": {"comment":"Channel K's output: BC"},
        "5210": {"comment":"Channel S's output: BC"},
        "5213": {"comment":"The page pair back"},
        "5214": {"comment":"Modes 2 and 3: done"},
        "5215": {"comment":"D = port $FF's mode bits"},
        "5217": {"comment":"MMU slot 3's page set (SWAP_MMU3)"},
        "5221": {"comment":"$5B62's bits 5-3 kept"},
        "5226": {"comment":"The mode bits added"},
        "5227": {"comment":"Port $FF (the Timex screen modes)"},
        "5229": {"comment":"NextReg $15 bit 7 = E's"},
        "5231": {"synopsis":"NEXTREG_MASK for NextReg $15 (sprites and layers).","comment":"NextReg $15 (sprites and layers)"},
        "5233": {"synopsis":"NextReg A = (its value AND D) OR E.\nExit: A = the value written.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Its value read"},
        "5236": {"comment":"Bits kept by D"},
        "5237": {"comment":"...bits set by E"},
        "5238": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "5241": {"synopsis":"Puts 8K page H into MMU slot 3 ($6000-$7FFF), unless it is there already, trading the 8K\ncontents of pages H and L (L put into slot 4 for the copy, slot 4's old page back after), so\nthe bytes seen at $6000 stay the same. Interrupts are off while it runs.\nEntry: H, L = the pages.","comment":"NextReg $53 (MMU slot 3) selected"},
        "5244": {"comment":"E = $54 (MMU slot 4) for later"},
        "5250": {"comment":"A = slot 3's page"},
        "5252": {"comment":"Already page H?"},
        "5254": {"comment":"Interrupts off for the swap"},
        "5255": {"comment":"Slot 3 = page H"},
        "5257": {"comment":"NextReg $54 selected"},
        "5261": {"comment":"A = slot 4's page"},
        "5263": {"comment":"Slot 4 = page L"},
        "5265": {"comment":"The two 8K pages' contents traded"},
        "5271": {"comment":"B = slot 4's old page"},
        "5272": {"synopsis":"One byte each way.","comment":"A byte of slot 3 ($6000 up)"},
        "5274": {"comment":"...and of slot 4 ($8000 up) swapped"},
        "5279": {"comment":"Up to $8000 in DE"},
        "5283": {"comment":"Slot 4's page back"},
        "5287": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "5289": {"synopsis":"SET_MODE with A: bits 3-0 the mode and its kind (from page 0, RST $18 / DEFW $14A9). IX\nkept.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "5291": {"comment":"E = A's low 4 bits: mode and kind"},
        "5294": {"comment":"D = the kind (bits 2-3)"},
        "5299": {"comment":"Set"},
        "5302": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "5305": {"synopsis":"Resets the Next's display (from pages 0 and 2): the palettes (PALETTES_RESET), the sprites\n(SPRITES_RESET), ROM 0's $2644, Layer 2 in bank 9 (NextRegs $12, $13), the LoRes, ULA, Layer\n2 and tilemap scrolls 0, the tilemap Y offset, ULA control and tilemap control 0, mode 0\n(SET_MODE), Layer 2 hidden (port $123B, $5B7B), the layer order SLU (NextReg $15 bits 4-2),\nand the clip windows (CLIP_THREE).","comment":"All the palettes (PALETTES_RESET)"},
        "5308": {"comment":"The sprites cleared (SPRITES_RESET)"},
        "5311": {"comment":"ROM 0's $2644"},
        "5316": {"comment":"NextRegs $12, $13 = 9: Layer 2 in bank 9"},
        "5324": {"comment":"NextRegs $32, $33 = 0: LoRes scroll"},
        "5332": {"comment":"NextRegs $26, $27 = 0: ULA scroll"},
        "5337": {"comment":"NextRegs $16, $17 = 0: Layer 2 scroll"},
        "5342": {"comment":"NextRegs $2F, $30 = 0: tilemap X scroll"},
        "5347": {"comment":"NextReg $31 = 0: tilemap Y offset"},
        "5351": {"comment":"NextReg $68 = 0: ULA control"},
        "5354": {"comment":"NextReg $6B = 0: tilemap off"},
        "5357": {"comment":"Mode 0 (E = 0)"},
        "5360": {"comment":"Port $123B = 0: Layer 2 hidden"},
        "5366": {"comment":"$5B7B = 0 too"},
        "5369": {"comment":"NextReg $15 bits 4-2 cleared: SLU order"},
        "5375": {"comment":"The clip windows reset"},
        "5377": {"synopsis":"NextReg L = E and NextReg L + 1 = D.\nChanges: BC, L.","comment":"NextReg L = E"},
        "5385": {"comment":"NextReg L + 1 = D"},
        "5393": {"synopsis":"Resets every clip window: the tilemap's, Layer 2's, the ULA's (CLIP_THREE), then the\nsprites'. Called from page 0.","comment":"Tilemap, Layer 2 and ULA windows, then sprites'"},
        "5396": {"synopsis":"The sprites' clip window to the full screen (NextReg $19).","comment":"The sprites' window"},
        "5400": {"synopsis":"The clip windows of the tilemap (X to 159, Y to 255), Layer 2 and the ULA (the full 256 x\n192).","comment":"The tilemap's window: X to 159, Y to 255"},
        "5405": {"comment":"Set"},
        "5408": {"comment":"Layer 2's window"},
        "5413": {"comment":"The ULA's window"},
        "5415": {"synopsis":"CLIP_SET with X2 255, Y2 191.","comment":"D = 255, E = 191: the full screen"},
        "5418": {"synopsis":"Clip window L (NextReg $18-$1B) = 0 to D across, 0 to E down, after resetting every window's\nwrite index (NextReg $1C = $0F).\nChanges: BC, HL.","comment":"X1 and Y1 = 0"},
        "5422": {"comment":"NextReg $1C = $0F: every window's index reset"},
        "5435": {"comment":"NextReg L selected"},
        "5438": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "5439": {"comment":"X1 = 0"},
        "5441": {"comment":"X2 = D"},
        "5443": {"comment":"Y1 = 0"},
        "5445": {"comment":"Y2 = E"},
        "5448": {"synopsis":"Sprites off (NextReg $15 bits 1-0 cleared), all 128 sprites hidden (attribute 3 = 0 through\nNextReg $78), $24DF-$2CFF of 8K page $10 cleared, then the sprites' clip window.","comment":"NextReg $15 bits 1-0 cleared: no sprites"},
        "5454": {"comment":"NextReg $34 = A, the value just written"},
        "5457": {"comment":"128 sprites"},
        "5459": {"synopsis":"One sprite.","comment":"Each one's attribute 3 = 0 (hidden)"},
        "5465": {"comment":"8K page $10 into MMU slot 1"},
        "5469": {"comment":"$24DF-$2CFF filled with 0"},
        "5481": {"comment":"The ROM back into MMU slot 1"},
        "5485": {"comment":"Then the sprites' clip window"},
        "5487": {"synopsis":"Resets the palettes: the ULA's two get the 16 colours at $3DE3 (repeated over 256 entries);\nLayer 2's and the sprites' two get each entry equal to its index. Then $5C7F bit 4 set,\nNextReg $43 = 0, the fallback colour black ($4A), the tilemap's transparent index $0F ($4C),\nULANext off (SET_ULANEXT), and $E3 as the global and the sprites' transparent colour ($14,\n$4B). Reached also from the syntax table (the word at $050E).","comment":"The ULA's first palette first"},
        "5488": {"synopsis":"One ULA palette.","comment":"NextReg $43 = A: the palette written"},
        "5492": {"comment":"H = 0: 256 entries"},
        "5494": {"comment":"From index 0"},
        "5497": {"synopsis":"The colour table from its start.","comment":"The 16 colours at $3DE3"},
        "5500": {"synopsis":"One entry; $AA ends the table.","comment":"The next colour"},
        "5502": {"comment":"$AA: the table's end, start it again"},
        "5506": {"comment":"Written; the index goes up"},
        "5509": {"comment":"256 times"},
        "5512": {"comment":"The palette back"},
        "5513": {"comment":"The ULA's second palette ($40) next"},
        "5515": {"comment":"Both done?"},
        "5517": {"comment":"D = $10: Layer 2's first palette; E = 2 rounds"},
        "5520": {"synopsis":"One palette of Layer 2 or the sprites.","comment":"NextReg $43 = D"},
        "5524": {"comment":"From index 0"},
        "5528": {"synopsis":"Entry n = n.","comment":"Each entry = its own index"},
        "5531": {"comment":"256 entries"},
        "5534": {"comment":"The second palette done ($40 set)?"},
        "5536": {"comment":"The second palette next"},
        "5540": {"comment":"D = $20: the sprites' palettes"},
        "5542": {"comment":"Two rounds"},
        "5545": {"comment":"$5C7F bit 4 set"},
        "5549": {"comment":"NextReg $43 = 0"},
        "5553": {"comment":"NextReg $4A = 0: black fallback"},
        "5556": {"comment":"NextReg $4C = $0F: tilemap transparent index"},
        "5560": {"comment":"ULANext off"},
        "5564": {"comment":"$E3: the transparent colour"},
        "5566": {"comment":"NextReg $14 = $E3 (global)"},
        "5569": {"comment":"NextReg $4B = $E3 (sprites)"},
        "5573": {"synopsis":"Sets the ULANext ink mask A: 0 turns ULANext off; otherwise A must be one less than a power\nof 2 (report B) and ULANext goes on (NextReg $43 bit 0). $5B64 and NextReg $42 = A. Called\nfrom $34AD too (at SET_ULANEXT_GO).\nEntry: A = the mask.","comment":"H = the ink mask"},
        "5574": {"comment":"0: ULANext off"},
        "5577": {"comment":"A + 1 AND A: is A one less than a power of 2?"},
        "5579": {"comment":"No: report B"},
        "5582": {"comment":"E = 1: ULANext on"},
        "5583": {"synopsis":"NextReg $43 bit 0 = E; $5B64 and NextReg $42 = H.","comment":"NextReg $43 bit 0 = E"},
        "5591": {"comment":"$5B64 = the mask"},
        "5595": {"comment":"NextReg $42 = the mask (ink bits)"},
        "5599": {"synopsis":"SAVE, LOAD, VERIFY and MERGE (from the JP at $05F9; T_ADDR's low byte tells which: 0 SAVE, 1\nLOAD, 2 VERIFY, 3 MERGE, made from the token in IXh):\n1. A '*' is skipped; the name (ROM 3's CLASS_A).\n2. When running: the header's room (17 or 34 bytes); LOAD \"*\" alone with a disk drive as\n   LOAD's default calls ROM 2's DOS_BOOT, and on '#' goes on with the name \"disk\" and ROM\n   2's $0E14 after the command.\n3. The device: 'T:' or a drive letter A-P before the name, else the default ($5B7A for SAVE\n   and VERIFY, $5B79 for LOAD and MERGE); a name of just 'x:' sets that default\n   (DOS_SET_DRIVE for a drive).\n4. The name to the header (SAVE needs 1-10 characters, report F) and, for a disk, whole to\n   $F700 in bank 7.\n5. What follows: DATA, $9A (a 16K bank), $9C (the screen's picture), $EE or $BA (from the\n   DivMMC's code), SCREEN$, CODE, or a program with LINE.\n6. SAVE: SAVE_CONTROL ($1B49). The others: headers read from tape or the disk file opened,\n   then LOAD_CONTROL. The command runs on past $19FF (MERGE_LOAD, SAVE_CONTROL ... to $1BB9,\n   covered by the $1A00 draft).","comment":"The caller's AF dropped"},
        "5600": {"comment":"T_ADDR's low byte = 3 for MERGE"},
        "5605": {"comment":"A = the command's token"},
        "5607": {"comment":"MERGE?"},
        "5611": {"comment":"SAVE 0, LOAD 1, VERIFY 2 from the token"},
        "5615": {"comment":"Into T_ADDR's low byte"},
        "5616": {"synopsis":"The name: a leading '*' skipped.","comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "5619": {"comment":"A '*' before the name is skipped"},
        "5624": {"comment":"The name (ROM 3's CLASS_A, a string)"},
        "5627": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "5630": {"comment":"Then on to what follows the name"},
        "5633": {"comment":"17 bytes for one header (SAVE)"},
        "5636": {"comment":"LOAD, VERIFY, MERGE?"},
        "5642": {"comment":"34 bytes: the wanted header and the one read"},
