        "6650": {"comment":"X_PTR = IX, kept over ROM 3's calls"},
        "6654": {"comment":"An old array (or a program)?"},
        "6656": {"comment":"An old variable, or a program, to replace?"},
        "6658": {"comment":"A new array: the length kept"},
        "6659": {"comment":"Its name's letters counted (ROM 3's COUNT_DEST_NAME)"},
        "6662": {"comment":"A = the count + 1 (B = $FF less the count)"},
        "6664": {"comment":"Room goes before the variables' $80 end"},
        "6668": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6670": {"comment":"Plus the count + 1"},
        "6672": {"comment":"The count + 1 kept"},
        "6673": {"comment":"No letters counted?"},
        "6676": {"comment":"One more byte (a long name's $7F)"},
        "6677": {"synopsis":"Two more bytes, for the length word; the room made before the $80 (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), the\nname written into it (ROM 3's WRITE_STR_NAME) and the length word after it; then\nLOAD_ARR_DATA.","comment":"The length word's two bytes"},
        "6679": {"comment":"The room (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "6682": {"comment":"IX back on the loaded header"},
        "6686": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "6687": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6688": {"comment":"B = the count + 1"},
        "6689": {"comment":"The wanted header's byte 14: the array's letter"},
        "6692": {"comment":"IXh = it, IXl = the count + 1"},
        "6696": {"comment":"The name into the room (ROM 3's WRITE_STR_NAME)"},
        "6699": {"comment":"HL = past the name"},
        "6700": {"comment":"DE = the array's length"},
        "6701": {"comment":"The length word after the name"},
        "6705": {"comment":"On to load the array into it"},
        "6707": {"synopsis":"An old array, or a program: only a new length longer than the old one needs more room, and\nthat is tested ($388F: report 4 when the difference + 5 does not fit); then LOAD_KIND.","comment":"The new length kept"},
        "6708": {"comment":"And the old variable's address"},
        "6709": {"comment":"HL = the old length (the wanted header's)"},
        "6715": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6716": {"comment":"HL = new, DE = old"},
        "6717": {"comment":"New - old - 1: not longer?"},
        "6722": {"comment":"The difference + 5"},
        "6726": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "6728": {"comment":"Room for it? (report 4 when not)"},
        "6731": {"synopsis":"A program: LOAD_PROGRAM. An array: the type, old length and new length go on the calculator\nstack as a string value ($385E), then the old array is replaced through ROM 3's\nLET_WHOLE_STR ($2B82: a new copy with the same name, the old one reclaimed), IXh = the\narray's letter; then LOAD_ARR_DATA.","comment":"DE = the old length"},
        "6732": {"comment":"HL = the old variable"},
        "6733": {"comment":"The type: 0, a program?"},
        "6739": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "6741": {"comment":"The old variable kept"},
        "6742": {"comment":"A, DE, BC stacked as a string value ($385E)"},
        "6745": {"comment":"HL = the old variable"},
        "6746": {"comment":"BC = the old length"},
        "6748": {"comment":"The wanted header's array letter"},
        "6751": {"comment":"Into IXh"},
        "6753": {"comment":"Replaced (ROM 3's LET_WHOLE_STR)"},
        "6756": {"comment":"DE = the new length"},
        "6757": {"synopsis":"IX back on the header (X_PTR), HL on the array's data: on to load DE bytes there ($19EB).","comment":"IX = the header again"},
        "6761": {"comment":"HL = the data's first byte"},
        "6762": {"comment":"Store the length and load"},
        "6765": {"synopsis":"LOAD of a program: the old program and variables removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL, from DE to\nE_LINE - 1), room made for the new length (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), VARS set from the header's\nprogram length, two calls to other memories ($2A06 in the DivMMC's, $2D87 in the alternate\nROM) before the data is loaded ($19EB) and LOADED_PROG_FIX after it. Then an auto-start line\n(the header's bytes 13-14, under $4000) is gone to: the return address is replaced by $0931\nand GO_TO_LINE runs with A = $FF (the main program).","comment":"DE = the old program's start"},
        "6766": {"comment":"HL = the variables' end marker"},
        "6770": {"comment":"X_PTR = the header"},
        "6774": {"comment":"The old program and variables gone"},
        "6777": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "6779": {"comment":"The room's place kept"},
        "6780": {"comment":"The room (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "6783": {"comment":"IX = the header again"},
        "6787": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "6788": {"comment":"BC = the header's program length"},
        "6794": {"comment":"HL = the variables' start"},
        "6795": {"comment":"VARS"},
        "6798": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2A06"},
        "6803": {"comment":"And the alternate ROM's at $2D87"},
        "6808": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "6809": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "6810": {"comment":"The header kept"},
        "6812": {"comment":"The data loaded"},
        "6815": {"comment":"And put to use"},
        "6818": {"comment":"IX = the header"},
        "6820": {"comment":"B = the auto-start line's high byte"},
        "6823": {"comment":"$4000 or more: none?"},
        "6826": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "6827": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "6830": {"comment":"A = $FF: the main program"},
        "6832": {"comment":"Return through $0931 instead"},
        "6836": {"comment":"Go to the line"},
        "6839": {"synopsis":"After a program is loaded or merged: ROM 1's $105E (which maps the bank in $5B58 at MMU 1\nand works through the program from PROG) and the alternate ROM's $2E20.","comment":"Through the program"},
        "6842": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's routine at $2E20"},
        "6848": {"synopsis":"MERGE: the alternate ROM's $2D87 first; the program loaded into the workspace (ROM 3's\nWORK_ROOM, an $80 after it, then $19EB), then its lines (MERGE_LINES) and variables\n(MERGE_VARS) put into the program one by one.","comment":"The alternate ROM's routine at $2D87"},
        "6853": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6859": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6860": {"comment":"One more for the $80"},
        "6861": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM)"},
        "6864": {"comment":"The end marker"},
        "6866": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "6867": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "6868": {"comment":"The room kept"},
        "6869": {"comment":"The program loaded into it"},
        "6872": {"comment":"HL = the merged program"},
        "6873": {"comment":"DE = the old program"},
        "6877": {"synopsis":"The next merged line, until the variables start (bits 6-7 of its first byte).","comment":"Its first byte"},
        "6878": {"comment":"A variable, or the end?"},
        "6882": {"synopsis":"Compares the merged line's number with the program's: a bigger one moves on through the\nprogram (ROM 3's NEXT_LINE).","comment":"The high bytes"},
        "6886": {"comment":"Different: that decides"},
        "6888": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "6890": {"synopsis":"Both pointers back to the lines' starts."},
        "6892": {"comment":"The merged line not bigger: put it in"},
        "6894": {"comment":"The merged line kept"},
        "6895": {"comment":"HL = the program's line"},
        "6896": {"comment":"The next one (ROM 3's NEXT_LINE)"},
        "6899": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6901": {"comment":"Compare again"},
        "6903": {"synopsis":"Puts the line in through the DivMMC memory's routine at $2200 (Z replaces the line with the\nsame number); then the next one.","comment":"Into the program (Z: replacing)"},
        "6908": {"comment":"The next merged line"},
        "6910": {"synopsis":"The merged variables, one by one, until the $80; then LOADED_PROG_FIX.","comment":"The variable's first byte"},
        "6911": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "6912": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "6914": {"comment":"Yes: finish"},
        "6916": {"comment":"The merged variable kept"},
        "6917": {"comment":"The program's variables"},
        "6920": {"synopsis":"Looks for a variable with the same first byte in the program's.","comment":"Its first byte"},
        "6921": {"comment":"The end: not there"},
        "6925": {"comment":"The same first byte?"},
        "6928": {"synopsis":"The next one (ROM 3's VAR_SKIP).","comment":"Past this variable (ROM 3's VAR_SKIP)"},
        "6931": {"comment":"Try it"},
        "6933": {"synopsis":"The same first byte: $7F (a string with a long name) has its name's first letter compared\nbefore the letters; a long number name ($A0 type) goes to MERGE_VAR_LONG; any other is the\nsame variable.","comment":"A long-named string?"},
        "6937": {"comment":"DE = the merged one"},
        "6939": {"comment":"The program's kept"},
        "6940": {"comment":"The bytes after the $7F"},
        "6942": {"comment":"Its first letter the same?"},
        "6944": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6946": {"comment":"Yes: the other letters"},
        "6948": {"synopsis":"A long name ($A0 type): the letters must match too.","comment":"Bits 7-5"},
        "6950": {"comment":"A long name?"},
        "6952": {"comment":"No: the same variable"},
        "6954": {"comment":"DE = the merged one"},
        "6956": {"comment":"The program's kept"},
        "6957": {"synopsis":"Letter by letter, to the one with bit 7.","comment":"The next letters"},
        "6959": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "6961": {"comment":"No"},
        "6963": {"comment":"The last letter?"},
        "6966": {"comment":"Yes: the same variable"},
        "6969": {"synopsis":"Not the same: on."},
        "6972": {"synopsis":"The same: A = $FF, so Z (replace)."},
        "6974": {"synopsis":"Puts the variable in through the DivMMC memory's routine at $2200 (Z replaces the one\nfound); then the next one.","comment":"DE = where it goes"},
        "6975": {"comment":"HL = the merged variable"},
        "6976": {"comment":"Z when one is replaced"},
        "6978": {"comment":"Into the variables"},
        "6983": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "6985": {"synopsis":"SAVE once the header is made (from $18E1): tape ($5B5E = 'T') goes to SAVE_TAPE. A disk:\n1. File 0 opened on the alternate stack through ROM 2's +3DOS call DOS_OPEN ($0106): the\n   name at $F700 (bank 7), access mode 3, create action 1 (a new file with a header), open\n   action 3 (an old file renamed to .BAK first).\n2. Its header data located (DOS_REF_HEAD, $010F).\n3. The type into it, then the length and the two parameter words (6 bytes from the header's\n   byte 11, copied into bank 7 by $2B1C). Failing calls stop through $08EF with the +3DOS\n   error. Then DATA_AND_CLOSE.","comment":"The device: tape?"},
        "6990": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6992": {"comment":"The data's start kept"},
        "6993": {"comment":"The alternate stack, bank 7 at $C000"},
        "6994": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "6996": {"comment":"Access mode 3"},
        "6998": {"comment":"Create: a new file with a header"},
        "7000": {"comment":"Open: the old one renamed to .BAK"},
        "7002": {"comment":"The name, in bank 7"},
        "7005": {"comment":"The header kept"},
        "7007": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_OPEN"},
        "7010": {"comment":"Opened?"},
        "7012": {"comment":"No: back to the normal stack"},
        "7013": {"comment":"Stop with +3DOS's error"},
        "7017": {"synopsis":"Opened: its header data located (ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD).","comment":"File 0"},
        "7019": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD: IX = its header data"},
        "7022": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "7024": {"comment":"No: back to the normal stack"},
        "7025": {"comment":"Stop with +3DOS's error"},
        "7029": {"synopsis":"The type, length, start and second word into the file's header data; then the data.","comment":"IX = the header, the header data kept"},
        "7031": {"comment":"HL = the header data"},
        "7032": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7033": {"comment":"The type"},
        "7036": {"comment":"Into the header data, in bank 7"},
        "7038": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7039": {"comment":"DE = the header"},
        "7042": {"comment":"HL = it, DE = the header data"},
        "7043": {"comment":"The header's byte 11"},
        "7047": {"comment":"Length, start and second word"},
        "7050": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7051": {"comment":"Copied into bank 7"},
        "7054": {"comment":"HL = the data's start"},
        "7055": {"comment":"The data, then the file closed"},
        "7058": {"synopsis":"SAVE to tape: the 17-byte header at IX (ROM 3's SA_BYTES, flag 0), then a gap of 50 HALTs\nbefore the data (DATA_AND_CLOSE).","comment":"The data's start kept"},
        "7059": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "7062": {"comment":"Flag 0: a header"},
        "7063": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "7065": {"comment":"Saved (ROM 3's SA_BYTES)"},
        "7070": {"comment":"50 frames"},
        "7072": {"synopsis":"The gap: 50 HALTs."},
        "7075": {"comment":"HL = the data's start"},
        "7076": {"synopsis":"The data block of SAVE, LOAD or VERIFY (also from $19F1): tape goes straight to DATA_BLOCK.\nA disk file: DATA_BLOCK, then file 0 closed (ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE, $0109) on the alternate\nstack; failing is a stop through $08EF with the +3DOS error.","comment":"The device: tape?"},
        "7081": {"comment":"Yes: the block only"},
        "7083": {"comment":"The block"},
        "7086": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "7088": {"comment":"The alternate stack"},
        "7089": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_CLOSE"},
        "7092": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7093": {"comment":"Closed: done"},
        "7094": {"comment":"Stop with +3DOS's error"},
        "7098": {"synopsis":"Saves, loads or verifies the data block at HL (DE = its length, IX = the header) by where it\nlives, the byte at $5B65: $FF ordinary memory (DATA_PLAIN with bank 0); $FE the screen\n(DATA_SCREEN); $FD through bank 7's $C000 (DATA_VIA_BANK7); otherwise a 16K bank\n(DATA_IN_BANK).","comment":"Where the data lives"},
        "7101": {"comment":"$FF: ordinary memory"},
        "7105": {"comment":"$FE: the screen"},
        "7109": {"comment":"$FD?"},
        "7111": {"comment":"No: a bank number"},
        "7113": {"synopsis":"$5B65 = $FD: the block goes through bank 7 at $C000: the DivMMC memory's routine at $2A18\n(on the alternate stack), the block transferred with bank 7 (DATA_IN_BANK7), then for LOAD\n$2A18 once more.","comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7119": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7120": {"comment":"The start kept"},
        "7121": {"comment":"Bank 7's $C000"},
        "7125": {"comment":"The alternate stack"},
        "7126": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2A18"},
        "7131": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7132": {"comment":"HL = $C000"},
        "7134": {"comment":"Bank 7"},
        "7136": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "7139": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "7142": {"comment":"LOAD?"},
        "7146": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "7147": {"comment":"The alternate stack"},
        "7148": {"comment":"$2A18 again"},
        "7153": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7155": {"synopsis":"$5B65 a bank number: it is mapped at $C000 ($32D0), the normal stack back, then the block\ntransferred with it (DATA_LEN).","comment":"C = the bank"},
        "7156": {"comment":"Mapped at $C000"},
        "7159": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7160": {"comment":"Transfer"},
        "7162": {"synopsis":"$5B65 = $FE, the screen: with bit 1 of $5C7F set, Layer 2's three banks (DATA_LAYER2);\notherwise two $1800-byte blocks of bank 5 (the pixels at $4000 and those at $6000, seen at\n$C000 and $E000), each through DATA_GO.","comment":"Layer 2 shown?"},
        "7168": {"comment":"Bank 5's first $1800 bytes"},
        "7174": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "7175": {"comment":"Bank 5"},
        "7177": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "7180": {"comment":"Then its $2000-$37FF"},
        "7184": {"comment":"Bank 5"},
        "7186": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "7189": {"synopsis":"Layer 2: its first 16K bank read from NextReg $12 through ports $243B/$253B, then three\nbanks of $4000 bytes from it on, each at $C000 (DATA_GO).","comment":"Port $243B: NextReg select"},
        "7192": {"comment":"NextReg $12, Layer 2's bank"},
        "7196": {"comment":"Port $253B"},
        "7197": {"comment":"C = the bank"},
        "7199": {"comment":"Three banks"},
        "7201": {"synopsis":"One 16K bank at $C000.","comment":"The bank at $C000"},
        "7204": {"comment":"16K"},
        "7207": {"comment":"Count and bank kept"},
        "7208": {"comment":"Transferred"},
        "7212": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "7216": {"synopsis":"DATA_LEN with C = A (the bank)."},
        "7217": {"synopsis":"DATA_GO with DE = the header's length (bytes 11-12)."},
        "7223": {"synopsis":"Saves, loads or verifies DE bytes at HL, with bank C at $C000 (0: none); nothing for DE = 0.\nA disk file: ROM 2's DOS_WRITE ($0115) for SAVE, DOS_READ ($0112) otherwise, file 0, on the\nalternate stack; failing is a stop through $08EF with the +3DOS error. Tape: DATA_TAPE.","comment":"Nothing to do?"},
        "7226": {"comment":"The device: tape?"},
        "7231": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7233": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "7237": {"comment":"The alternate stack"},
        "7238": {"comment":"File 0"},
        "7240": {"comment":"Not SAVE: read"},
        "7242": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_WRITE"},
        "7245": {"comment":"Then the check"},
        "7247": {"synopsis":"LOAD or VERIFY: ROM 2's DOS_READ.","comment":"ROM 2's DOS_READ"},
        "7250": {"synopsis":"Back to the normal stack; carry is success.","comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7251": {"comment":"Done"},
        "7252": {"comment":"Stop with +3DOS's error"},
        "7256": {"synopsis":"Tape: bank C (when not 0) mapped at $C000 ($32D0), IX = the start; SAVE through ROM 3's\nSA_BYTES, LOAD and MERGE (carry) or VERIFY (no carry) through ROM 3's LD_BYTES, flag $FF.\nThen TAPE_RESULT.","comment":"A bank?"},
        "7260": {"comment":"Mapped at $C000 (the alternate stack)"},
        "7263": {"synopsis":"IX = the start; SAVE or not?","comment":"IX = the start"},
        "7266": {"comment":"SAVE?"},
        "7270": {"comment":"No: load or verify"},
        "7272": {"comment":"The data block's flag"},
        "7274": {"comment":"Saved (ROM 3's SA_BYTES)"},
        "7277": {"comment":"Success"},
        "7278": {"synopsis":"The tape result in carry: kept while the normal stack is put back ($2AEE, when SP is below\n$5C00, so on the alternate stack); success returns, failing goes to REPORT_R.","comment":"The flags kept in C"},
        "7280": {"comment":"SP below $5C00?"},
        "7287": {"comment":"Yes: the normal stack back"},
        "7290": {"comment":"The flags again"},
        "7292": {"comment":"Success: done"},
        "7293": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $1A (report R, \"Tape loading error\") through the error routine at\n$08EF (also from $19DD, a length that does not fit).","comment":"Error $1A"},
        "7297": {"synopsis":"LOAD, VERIFY or MERGE: carry for all but VERIFY (T_ADDR 2), then ROM 3's LD_BYTES with flag\n$FF.","comment":"T_ADDR - 2: 0 VERIFY, else carry (load)"},
        "7302": {"comment":"The data block's flag"},
        "7304": {"comment":"Loaded or verified (ROM 3's LD_BYTES)"},
        "7307": {"comment":"The result"},
        "7309": {"synopsis":"Prints a header type of 4 or 5 (from $191F) as \"Layer \" (the bit-7 text at $3F99) and the\ndigit A + $2D (1 or 2).","comment":"The digit: '1' for 4, '2' for 5"},
        "7312": {"comment":"The text \"Layer \""},
        "7315": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "7319": {"comment":"The digit (ROM 3's PRINT_A)"},
        "7323": {"synopsis":"From $18BE (LOAD, VERIFY or MERGE): E_PPC = 0, and the word at $D74E in bank 7 too.","comment":"E_PPC = 0"},
        "7329": {"comment":"The alternate stack, bank 7"},
        "7330": {"comment":"Its word at $D74E = 0"},
        "7333": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
        "7335": {"synopsis":"A one-line IF whose condition is false: the rest of the line is searched, statement by\nstatement (':' and THEN start one; numbers and strings skipped), for one that starts with\nELSE ($98): the statement after it runs ($0961). The end of the line goes on with the next\nline ($093F).","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "7338": {"synopsis":"A new statement: SUBPPC + 1; does it start with ELSE?","comment":"SUBPPC + 1"},
        "7341": {"comment":"Its first character"},
        "7344": {"comment":"ELSE?"},
        "7346": {"comment":"Yes: run what follows it"},
        "7349": {"synopsis":"The next byte of the statement."},
        "7351": {"comment":"A number's hidden form?"},
        "7355": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "7359": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "7363": {"comment":"The end of the line?"},
        "7367": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "7371": {"synopsis":"Inside a string: to the closing quote (or the line's end)."},
        "7373": {"comment":"The closing quote?"},
        "7377": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "7381": {"synopsis":"No ELSE: on with the next line."},
        "7384": {"synopsis":"Past the 5 bytes of a number."},
        "7390": {"synopsis":"IF after its condition, from ROM 3 (the word at its $1C0E) and from IF_ELSE_IF: SUBPPC + 1,\nBC kept; then IF_THEN_TEST.","comment":"SUBPPC + 1"},
        "7394": {"synopsis":"Also named by the syntax table ($03D2). Without THEN, IF_BLOCK. With it: checking goes on\nwith the statement after THEN; running, a true condition (the value on the calculator stack,\n$0052) runs it, a false one looks for an ELSE (IF_FIND_ELSE).","comment":"THEN?"},
        "7396": {"comment":"No: a block IF"},
        "7398": {"comment":"Past THEN"},
        "7400": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7404": {"comment":"Yes: check what follows"},
        "7406": {"comment":"The condition: false?"},
        "7409": {"comment":"Yes: look for ELSE"},
        "7411": {"synopsis":"Runs (or checks) the statement at CH_ADD ($092C)."},
        "7414": {"synopsis":"IF ... THEN from IF_AFTER_COND: checking, or a true condition, goes on after THEN; a false\none goes on with the next line ($093F)."},
        "7415": {"comment":"Past THEN"},
        "7416": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7420": {"comment":"Yes: check what follows"},
        "7422": {"comment":"The condition: true?"},
        "7425": {"comment":"Yes: run what follows"},
        "7427": {"comment":"No: the next line"},
        "7430": {"synopsis":"IF after its condition, from the syntax table ($032F) and $2FDA, A = the character after it:\nTHEN goes to IF_THEN_LINE, anything else to IF_BLOCK.","comment":"THEN?"},
        "7434": {"synopsis":"IF without THEN, the start of a block: it must be the line's first statement (report C,\nSYNTAX_ERR_C). Checking ends here. Running: a true condition goes on with the next line; a\nfalse one skips the block (IF_SKIP_ELSE).","comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "7437": {"comment":"Not the first statement: report C"},
        "7441": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "7444": {"comment":"The condition: true?"},
        "7447": {"comment":"Yes: on into the block"},
        "7448": {"synopsis":"Skips lines to the block's ELSE ($98) or its end (token $84), with nested blocks counted.","comment":"Stop at ELSE"},
        "7450": {"synopsis":"Skips lines to one starting with token C or the block's end (token $84): B = 1, the nesting;\nSUBPPC = 1; the return address dropped. Running out of lines is error $64 (\"No ENDIF\").","comment":"One level deep"},
        "7452": {"comment":"SUBPPC = 1"},
        "7455": {"comment":"The return address dropped"},
        "7456": {"synopsis":"The next line ($3995): its first token decides.","comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "7460": {"comment":"To it (DE = its text, PPC set)"},
        "7464": {"comment":"No more lines: error $64"},
        "7466": {"comment":"NXTLIN = the line after it"},
        "7469": {"comment":"CH_ADD = its text"},
        "7473": {"comment":"The first token"},
        "7474": {"comment":"Token $84, a block's end?"},
        "7478": {"comment":"The wanted token?"},
        "7481": {"comment":"IF?"},
        "7485": {"comment":"Token $83?"},
        "7487": {"comment":"Neither: the next line"},
        "7489": {"synopsis":"IF (or token $83) at a line's start: its condition read ($0634); a THEN after it is a\none-line IF, otherwise a nested block, B + 1.","comment":"Count kept"},
        "7490": {"comment":"Past it, the condition"},
        "7494": {"comment":"THEN: a one-line IF"},
        "7498": {"comment":"One more level"},
        "7501": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $64 (\"No ENDIF\")."},
        "7503": {"synopsis":"Token $84: one level less; the block's own end goes on after it ($0953).","comment":"A nested one: on"},
        "7505": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7506": {"comment":"On with the next statement"},
        "7509": {"synopsis":"The wanted ELSE (or token C): only at the block's own level. Followed by IF or token $83,\nIF_ELSE_IF; otherwise what follows it runs.","comment":"Nested?"},
        "7511": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "7513": {"comment":"What follows it"},
        "7514": {"comment":"IF?"},
        "7518": {"comment":"Token $83?"},
        "7520": {"comment":"No: run what follows"},
        "7522": {"synopsis":"ELSE IF: the condition read ($0634); with THEN it is a one-line IF (IF_THEN_ROM3); otherwise\ntrue runs the statements after it, false goes on to the next ELSE.","comment":"The condition"},
        "7525": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "7530": {"comment":"True?"},
        "7533": {"comment":"Yes: run what follows"},
        "7535": {"comment":"Balances the POP at IF_SKIP_TO"},
        "7536": {"comment":"Look for the next ELSE"},
        "7538": {"synopsis":"ELSE met in the flow (from the syntax table, $0386): as a line's first statement,\nELSE_BLOCK; otherwise the rest of the line is skipped when running and checked when checking\n(ELSE_REST).","comment":"L = SUBPPC"},
        "7541": {"comment":"The first statement?"},
        "7544": {"synopsis":"Running: on with the next line ($093F); checking: the rest of the statement checked ($092C).","comment":"The return address dropped"},
        "7545": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7549": {"comment":"Yes: the next line"},
        "7552": {"comment":"Checking: go on"},
        "7555": {"synopsis":"ELSE starting a line: running, the lines up to the block's end (token $84) are skipped\n(IF_SKIP_TO with C = $84). Checking: an IF or token $83 after it has its condition checked,\nand THEN after that.","comment":"Stop only at the block's end"},
        "7557": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7561": {"comment":"Yes: skip the rest of the block"},
        "7563": {"comment":"IF after it?"},
        "7567": {"comment":"Token $83?"},
        "7571": {"synopsis":"The condition checked; without THEN the statement ends there.","comment":"The condition"},
        "7574": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "7576": {"comment":"No: the statement ends"},
        "7579": {"comment":"Past THEN"},
        "7582": {"synopsis":"The block end token ($84, probably ENDIF; from the syntax table, $0332): it must be the\nline's first statement (report C); nothing to do.","comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "7586": {"comment":"Not the first: report C"},
        "7588": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "7592": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\")."},
        "7594": {"synopsis":"Reads a name ($1313) and, inside the brackets after it, a list of parameters ($2568 with D =\n$C0); the ')' must follow (report C).\nExit: D = the name's kind (from $1313), CH_ADD past the ')'.","comment":"The name"},
        "7597": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "7598": {"comment":"The kind kept"},
        "7599": {"comment":"Parameters: variables, with defaults"},
        "7601": {"comment":"An empty list?"},
        "7603": {"comment":"No: the list"},
        "7607": {"comment":"The ')'?"},
        "7609": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7611": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7613": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($04E7): up to four numeric variables, separated by ',', each assigned\n(when running, $3DCF) the word at $3140, $3142, $3144, $3146 in turn, read through the\nDivMMC memory's routine at $2860 ($3F93).","comment":"The first word's address"},
        "7616": {"synopsis":"The next variable (CLASS_1 through $05A3): it must be numeric (report C).","comment":"Kept"},
        "7617": {"comment":"A variable to assign to"},
        "7620": {"comment":"Numeric?"},
        "7624": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7626": {"comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "7628": {"comment":"DE = the word ($2860 in the DivMMC memory)"},
        "7631": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "7633": {"comment":"Stacked as a small number"},
        "7636": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7639": {"comment":"Yes: assigned"},
        "7642": {"comment":"E = the address's low byte"},
        "7644": {"comment":"The fourth done?"},
        "7647": {"comment":"The next word"},
        "7649": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "7652": {"comment":"','?"},
        "7654": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "7655": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7658": {"synopsis":"ON (from the syntax table, $0374): followed by ERROR ($8F): checking ends at once ($0931);\nrunning, an ON ERROR entry ($4B) already at the GO SUB stack's top is dropped ($3BFD); ON\nERROR alone stops there; otherwise only a program may do it (error $5F, NEED_PROGRAM), an\nentry of type $4B is made ($3A40) and the rest of the line is passed over ($093A). Not\nERROR: ON_NUMBER.","comment":"ERROR?"},
        "7660": {"comment":"No: a number"},
        "7662": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7663": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7668": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "7671": {"comment":"The GO SUB stack's top entry"},
        "7676": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "7677": {"comment":"ON ERROR's?"},
        "7679": {"comment":"Yes: dropped"},
        "7682": {"comment":"What follows"},
        "7685": {"comment":"Nothing?"},
        "7688": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7689": {"comment":"Only in a program"},
        "7692": {"comment":"The ON ERROR entry"},
        "7698": {"comment":"The rest of the line passed over"},
        "7701": {"synopsis":"ON with a number (CLASS_6 through $0635; nothing after it is report C): checking ends there.\nRunning: n (0 when over 255 or not whole) goes to the statement scan at $123E with D = n + 1\nand E = ELSE ($98); CH_ADD and SUBPPC follow what it passed, and the statement found runs\n(bit 7 of SUBPPC set unless it is an ELSE), on through $0931.","comment":"The number"},
        "7704": {"comment":"Nothing after it?"},
        "7706": {"comment":"Yes: report C"},
        "7708": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "7711": {"comment":"BC = it (carry or NZ: no)"},
        "7714": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "7718": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "7722": {"synopsis":"Out of range: C = $FF, so 0."},
        "7724": {"synopsis":"C = n + 1: the statement count.","comment":"C = n + 1"},
        "7725": {"comment":"B = D = it"},
        "7727": {"comment":"ELSE stops the scan"},
        "7729": {"comment":"The scan"},
        "7732": {"comment":"CH_ADD = where it stopped"},
        "7735": {"comment":"The statements passed"},
        "7737": {"comment":"HL' = SUBPPC"},
        "7741": {"comment":"Added"},
        "7744": {"comment":"The character there"},
        "7745": {"comment":"The line's end?"},
        "7748": {"comment":"ELSE?"},
        "7749": {"comment":"No: the next character"},
        "7752": {"comment":"ELSE?"},
        "7753": {"comment":"HL = SUBPPC"},
        "7756": {"comment":"No: its bit 7 set"},
        "7758": {"synopsis":"Past an ELSE, then the statement runs ($0931)."},
        "7759": {"comment":"Past ELSE"},
        "7762": {"comment":"The return address dropped"},
        "7766": {"synopsis":"FOR after its limit (from the syntax table, $03F8; ROM 3's FOR_VALUES leaves the STEP to\nthis ROM): the STEP's number, or 1 when there is none, stacked; checking ends there. A GO\nSUB-stack entry is made ($3A40) with the type from FOR_ENTRY_TYPE, its address kept at\n$5B8E. An ordinary variable: ROM 3's FOR_VALUES; an integer one: FOR_INT. A loop that is\nover before it starts skips to its NEXT and the entry is dropped ($3C12).","comment":"STEP?"},
        "7770": {"comment":"No: a step of 1"},
        "7772": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7776": {"comment":"Yes: stacked"},
        "7781": {"synopsis":"The STEP's value (CLASS_6 through $0634)."},
        "7784": {"synopsis":"The statement's end (checking stops); the loop's GO SUB-stack entry.","comment":"Checking: done"},
        "7787": {"comment":"A = the loop's type"},
        "7790": {"comment":"The entry made"},
        "7793": {"comment":"Its address"},
        "7797": {"comment":"Kept at $5B8E"},
        "7800": {"comment":"An ordinary variable?"},
        "7802": {"comment":"No: an integer one"},
        "7804": {"comment":"The values (ROM 3's FOR_VALUES)"},
        "7807": {"comment":"The loop runs: done"},
        "7808": {"comment":"Over before it starts: to its NEXT"},
        "7811": {"synopsis":"The loop's entry dropped ($3C12)."},
        "7815": {"synopsis":"Skips to the NEXT of an ordinary FOR loop: STMT_SEARCH for NEXT ($F3) with the test at\n$2CE2; none is report I (FOR_NO_NEXT).","comment":"The test for its variable"},
        "7821": {"synopsis":"An integer variable's loop: the step, limit and start taken from the calculator stack into\nits slots at DEST + $34, + $68 and + 0 (FOR_INT_POP); the limit compared (INT_LIMIT_CMP); a\nloop over before it starts skips to its NEXT (FOR_INT_SKIP) and the entry is dropped.","comment":"The step"},
        "7827": {"comment":"The limit"},
        "7833": {"comment":"The start"},
        "7839": {"comment":"Within the limit?"},
        "7842": {"comment":"Yes: the loop runs"},
        "7843": {"comment":"No: to its NEXT"},
        "7846": {"comment":"And the entry dropped"},
        "7848": {"synopsis":"Skips to the NEXT of an integer loop: the test at $2CCB."},
        "7852": {"synopsis":"STMT_SEARCH for NEXT ($F3) with the test at IX; carry (none) is FOR_NO_NEXT.","comment":"NEXT"},
        "7854": {"comment":"The search"},
        "7857": {"comment":"Found: done"},
        "7858": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $11 (report I, \"FOR without NEXT\")."},
        "7860": {"synopsis":"Stops with error $5F (\"Direct command error\") unless CH_ADD is in the program (below\nE_LINE).","comment":"A = 0: a program needed"},
        "7863": {"synopsis":"The opposite test (A = 1): error $5F unless CH_ADD is in the edit line."},
        "7865": {"synopsis":"E_LINE - CH_ADD: carry when CH_ADD is at or past E_LINE (the edit line), reversed for A bit\n0 set; carry is error $5F.","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "7868": {"comment":"DE = CH_ADD"},
        "7872": {"comment":"Carry: in the edit line"},
        "7874": {"comment":"The direct test?"},
        "7878": {"comment":"Reversed"},
        "7879": {"synopsis":"No carry: allowed."},
        "7880": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $5F (\"Direct command error\")."},
        "7882": {"synopsis":"The GO SUB-stack entry type of a FOR loop: $1D for an ordinary variable; for an integer one\n(FLAGS2 bit 2) 3 + half of DEST's low byte less $64, its slot's number in the table at\n$325E.\nExit: A = the type.","comment":"An integer variable?"},
        "7886": {"comment":"No: $1D"},
        "7889": {"comment":"DEST's low byte"},
        "7892": {"comment":"Less $64"},
        "7894": {"comment":"Halved"},
        "7896": {"comment":"Plus 3"},
        "7899": {"synopsis":"NEXT (from the syntax table, $03F1): the loop's entry looked for ($3B18 with its type; none:\nNEXT_NO_LOOP). An ordinary variable: ROM 3's NEXT_VAR_TEST must find the same loop (else\nNEXT_VAR_ERR), then ROM 3's NEXT_STEP; an integer one: NEXT_INT. A loop going on goes back\nto its start ($3AC8 with the entry); a finished one drops its entry (NEXT_DONE).","comment":"The loop's type"},
        "7902": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "7903": {"comment":"Its GO SUB-stack entry"},
        "7906": {"comment":"None"},
        "7908": {"comment":"The entry kept"},
        "7909": {"comment":"An ordinary variable?"},
        "7911": {"comment":"No: integer"},
        "7913": {"comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "7915": {"comment":"The same loop? (ROM 3's NEXT_VAR_TEST)"},
        "7918": {"comment":"A = B"},
        "7920": {"comment":"No"},
        "7922": {"comment":"The step added (ROM 3's NEXT_STEP)"},
        "7925": {"comment":"The loop is over"},
        "7927": {"synopsis":"Back to the statement after the FOR ($3AC8 with the entry)."},
        "7932": {"synopsis":"An integer loop: value + step into the value's slot (past 65535 or below 0 the loop is\nover), then compared with the limit (INT_LIMIT_CMP).","comment":"The value's slot"},
        "7935": {"comment":"DE = the value"},
        "7939": {"comment":"The step's slot"},
        "7942": {"comment":"DE = the step"},
        "7945": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "7946": {"comment":"Plus the step"},
        "7947": {"comment":"A negative step?"},
        "7951": {"comment":"Yes: carry the other way"},
        "7952": {"synopsis":"Out of range: over; otherwise stored.","comment":"Out of range: over"},
        "7954": {"comment":"DE = the new value"},
        "7955": {"comment":"Into the value's slot"},
        "7961": {"comment":"Within the limit?"},
        "7964": {"comment":"Yes: loop back"},
        "7966": {"synopsis":"The loop is over: its entry dropped ($3BFD).","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "7971": {"synopsis":"NEXT_VAR_TEST found no match: for an integer type the error in A goes through $0DA5;\notherwise NEXT_NO_LOOP."},
        "7972": {"comment":"H = the code"},
        "7973": {"comment":"An ordinary loop?"},
        "7980": {"synopsis":"No loop for this NEXT: an integer variable, report 1; an ordinary one: a variable not found\n(FLAGX bit 1) is report 2 ($252D), a FOR variable (bit 7 of its name byte at $5B8C) returns,\nanything else is report 1.","comment":"The type"},
        "7981": {"comment":"An integer variable?"},
        "7985": {"comment":"Not found?"},
        "7989": {"comment":"Yes: report 2"},
        "7992": {"comment":"The variable"},
        "7995": {"comment":"A FOR variable?"},
        "7998": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $00 (report 1, \"NEXT without FOR\")."},
        "8000": {"synopsis":"Takes the last calculator value as an integer (the DivMMC memory's $24F1; carry goes on to\n$13E6), then INT_STORE.","comment":"The slot kept"},
        "8001": {"comment":"DE = the value ($24F1 in the DivMMC memory)"},
        "8006": {"comment":"Not an integer"},
        "8010": {"synopsis":"Stores DE in the integer slot at DEST + BC (the DivMMC memory's $2855, through $3EB9)."},
        "8017": {"synopsis":"Fetches the integer slot at DEST + DE into DE (the DivMMC memory's $2860, through $3F93)."},
        "8024": {"synopsis":"Compares an integer loop's value with its limit, by the step's sign.\nExit: no carry while the loop goes on (value not past the limit).","comment":"The limit"},
        "8030": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8031": {"comment":"The value"},
        "8037": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "8038": {"comment":"The step"},
        "8041": {"comment":"Negative?"},
        "8046": {"comment":"DE = the value"},
        "8047": {"comment":"HL = the limit"},
        "8050": {"comment":"Limit - value: carry when past it"},
        "8054": {"synopsis":"A negative step: carry when the value is below the limit.","comment":"Limit - value - 1"},
        "8057": {"comment":"Carry when below it"},
        "8059": {"synopsis":"From page 0 (the words at its $1B32 and $1B3D) and from LOOP_EXIT_END: the character after\nHL. Token $85 leaves the innermost loop (LOOP_EXIT); ELSE ($98) puts CH_ADD at DE and ends\nthe statement; anything else is report C ($09AF).","comment":"The next character"},
        "8062": {"comment":"Token $85?"},
        "8066": {"comment":"ELSE?"},
        "8068": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8071": {"comment":"CH_ADD = DE"},
        "8075": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8079": {"synopsis":"Token $85: leaves the innermost loop. Running: the GO SUB stack's innermost entry ($3B18\nwith C = $20) must be a loop, a type below $1F (else the loop error, LOOP_ERR). Something\nafter the token other than the statement's end goes to $25D5 (the entry dropped, then a\njump). Otherwise, running: back at the loop's start ($3AC8), then on to its end: REPEAT's\n(LOOP_LEAVE), an ordinary FOR's NEXT (FOR_SKIP), an integer FOR's NEXT (FOR_INT_SKIP with\nDEST its slot); the entry dropped ($3BFD).","comment":"Past the token"},
        "8080": {"synopsis":"Also named by the syntax table ($0395): LOOP_EXIT past its token.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "8086": {"comment":"Any entry"},
        "8088": {"comment":"The innermost one"},
        "8091": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "8092": {"comment":"Not a loop?"},
        "8094": {"comment":"Yes: the loop error"},
        "8097": {"synopsis":"What follows the token.","comment":"DE = the entry"},
        "8098": {"comment":"The character after the token"},
        "8101": {"comment":"The statement's end?"},
        "8104": {"comment":"X_PTR = here"},
        "8107": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "8108": {"comment":"No: a jump"},
        "8111": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "8115": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8117": {"comment":"The entry kept"},
        "8118": {"comment":"At $5B8E too"},
        "8121": {"comment":"Back at the loop's start"},
        "8124": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "8126": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "8127": {"comment":"REPEAT's?"},
        "8131": {"comment":"Yes: leave it"},
        "8136": {"synopsis":"Not REPEAT: an ordinary FOR goes to its NEXT (FOR_SKIP).","comment":"An ordinary FOR's?"},
        "8140": {"comment":"Yes: to its NEXT"},
        "8145": {"synopsis":"An integer FOR: DEST = $325E + 2 x its type (the variable's slot), then to its NEXT.","comment":"Type x 2"},
        "8146": {"comment":"The slots' table"},
        "8151": {"comment":"DEST"},
        "8154": {"comment":"To its NEXT"},
        "8157": {"synopsis":"The loop's entry dropped ($3BFD)."},
        "8161": {"synopsis":"Back after the token (X_PTR): a ':' checks for more (EXIT_CHECK); otherwise the statement\nends.","comment":"DE = CH_ADD"},
        "8165": {"comment":"HL = after the token"},
        "8169": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "8171": {"comment":"Yes: again"},
        "8173": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "8177": {"synopsis":"Searches the program onwards from CH_ADD for a statement starting with token E that the test\nat IX accepts (no carry): STMT_NEXT_TOKEN finds each one, STMT_TEST asks. PPC is kept in\nNEWPPC, which takes each line's number on the way; D counts statements (starting at\n-SUBPPC).\nExit: carry when the program ends first. Otherwise no carry; PPC = the line, SUBPPC = the\nstatement's number, CH_ADD in it.","comment":"PPC"},
        "8180": {"comment":"Into NEWPPC"},
        "8183": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "8186": {"comment":"D = -SUBPPC"},
        "8189": {"synopsis":"The next statement with token E (STMT_NEXT_TOKEN).","comment":"The current character"},
        "8192": {"comment":"The next one with the token"},
        "8195": {"synopsis":"Also called from KEPT_VARS_CLEAR with STMT_IN_LINE's carry: carry (none) returns; otherwise\nthe test and the search go on.","comment":"None: carry"},
        "8196": {"synopsis":"The test; refused, the rest of the line searched on ($125B).","comment":"The test (IX)"},
        "8199": {"comment":"Accepted"},
        "8201": {"comment":"Refused: the current character"},
        "8204": {"comment":"Outside quotes"},
        "8206": {"comment":"Searched on"},
        "8209": {"comment":"CH_ADD = where it stopped"},
        "8212": {"comment":"Another in the line: test it"},
        "8214": {"comment":"The line's statements counted out"},
        "8218": {"synopsis":"Accepted: SUBPPC = -D, PPC = NEWPPC; no carry."},
        "8219": {"comment":"A = -D"},
        "8220": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "8223": {"comment":"NEWPPC"},
        "8226": {"comment":"Into PPC"},
        "8229": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "8231": {"synopsis":"The search's test: a jump to IX."},
        "8233": {"synopsis":"The next statement starting with token E: in this line after a ':' ($1241), or in the next\nlines. A program in a bank ($5B77 not $FF) goes through $3925; the main program line by line\nfrom NXTLIN, each line's number into NEWPPC.\nExit: carry when the program ends; otherwise CH_ADD at the token.","comment":"':'?"},
        "8235": {"comment":"Yes: the rest of this line"},
        "8237": {"synopsis":"The next line.","comment":"The program's bank"},
        "8240": {"comment":"$FF: the main program"},
        "8243": {"comment":"E kept"},
        "8244": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8245": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "8248": {"comment":"The next line in the bank"},
        "8251": {"comment":"C = E"},
        "8252": {"comment":"The end: carry"},
        "8254": {"comment":"Bits 7 and 6 cleared"},
        "8258": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "8261": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "8262": {"comment":"E back"},
        "8265": {"synopsis":"The main program: the line's number byte; bits 6-7 set is the program's end (carry); NXTLIN\npast the line.","comment":"The number's high byte"},
        "8267": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "8270": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "8271": {"comment":"The line kept"},
        "8272": {"comment":"Its length"},
        "8278": {"comment":"Past the line"},
        "8279": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "8283": {"synopsis":"The line's number into NEWPPC; D = 0; the line searched.","comment":"BC = the line's number"},
        "8287": {"comment":"NEWPPC"},
        "8291": {"comment":"Past the length"},
        "8292": {"comment":"No statement count"},
        "8294": {"synopsis":"Searches the line from HL for token E ($1241); found, CH_ADD is there; otherwise the next\nline.","comment":"The search"},
        "8297": {"comment":"CH_ADD"},
        "8300": {"comment":"Found"},
        "8301": {"comment":"The next line"},
        "8303": {"synopsis":"REPEAT (from the syntax table, $04EA, and other ROMs): a GO SUB-stack entry of type $1E\nholding the place after it ($3A40).","comment":"Type $1E"},
        "8309": {"synopsis":"REPEAT UNTIL (the syntax table, $04ED), after its condition: false goes back to the loop's\nstart ($3AC4 with type $1E); true drops the loop's entry ($3B22, $3BFD). No REPEAT entry is\nthe loop error.","comment":"The condition: Z when false"},
        "8312": {"comment":"REPEAT's type"},
        "8314": {"comment":"True: leave"},
        "8316": {"comment":"False: back to the loop's start"},
        "8319": {"comment":"Found: done"},
        "8320": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $60 (\"Loop error\")."},
        "8322": {"synopsis":"The loop is over: its entry found and dropped.","comment":"The entry"},
        "8325": {"comment":"None: the loop error"},
        "8327": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "8331": {"synopsis":"WHILE (from the syntax table, $0383), after its condition: true goes on; false drops the\nREPEAT entry and leaves the loop (LOOP_LEAVE).","comment":"The condition: true?"},
        "8334": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "8335": {"comment":"REPEAT's type"},
        "8337": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "8340": {"comment":"None: the loop error"},
        "8342": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "8345": {"synopsis":"Leaves a REPEAT loop: STMT_SEARCH for REPEAT ($97) with the test at $2CBB, which counts\nnested REPEATs in the byte at $5C92 (set to 1) and accepts the REPEAT UNTIL ($8E) that\nbrings it to 0; then on past that statement ($35BC). None is the loop error.","comment":"One loop open"},
        "8349": {"comment":"REPEAT"},
        "8351": {"comment":"The nesting test"},
        "8355": {"comment":"The search"},
        "8358": {"comment":"None: the loop error"},
        "8360": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8363": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($0368): running, the rest of the line is passed over ($35BC).\nChecking: a name and its bracketed parameters (NAME_PARAMS), then optionally '=' and an\nexpression of the name's kind (report C when not).","comment":"Running?"},
        "8366": {"comment":"Yes: the line passed over"},
        "8369": {"comment":"The name and parameters"},
        "8372": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "8374": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8376": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8377": {"comment":"The kind kept"},
        "8378": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "8382": {"comment":"Its kind"},
        "8385": {"comment":"The name's?"},
        "8388": {"synopsis":"Not the same kind: report C."},
        "8393": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($0377), followed there by ENDPROC_CMD ($037A): running is error $5F;\nchecking reads a name and its bracketed parameters (NAME_PARAMS).","comment":"Running?"},
        "8396": {"comment":"Yes: error $5F"},
        "8399": {"comment":"The name and parameters"},
        "8402": {"synopsis":"Checking: the statement ends here."},
        "8405": {"synopsis":"ENDPROC (from the syntax table, $037A). Checking: '=' and a list of values ($254A, D = $80).\nRunning: after an optional '=', the values' place goes to X_PTR (copied to the buffer at\n$5CB6 first, $39E3, when the program is in a bank) and DEFADD to $5B8C; the procedure's\nentry (type $22) is found and returned to ($3AC4; none is error $61, \"No DEFPROC\"). The\ncalling PROC's line is then past its brackets ($217B): with TO after them, each variable in\nits list gets the next value (ENDPROC_TO); otherwise the entry is dropped ($3A8A).","comment":"Running?"},
        "8409": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8411": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "8413": {"comment":"No: end"},
        "8415": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8416": {"comment":"Expressions only"},
        "8418": {"comment":"The values"},
        "8423": {"synopsis":"Running: the values found, the PROC entry returned to.","comment":"Past an '='"},
        "8428": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "8432": {"comment":"In a bank: the statement copied out"},
        "8435": {"comment":"X_PTR = the values"},
        "8438": {"comment":"DEFADD"},
        "8441": {"comment":"Kept at $5B8C"},
        "8444": {"comment":"The procedure's type"},
        "8446": {"comment":"Its entry: back to the caller"},
        "8449": {"comment":"None: error $61"},
        "8451": {"comment":"The stack kept at $5B94"},
        "8455": {"comment":"Past the caller's brackets"},
        "8458": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "8461": {"comment":"No: finish"},
        "8463": {"synopsis":"One variable of the TO list: it is looked up (CLASS_1, $05A3); the next value evaluated at\nthe other place (the places swapped by $2C9F before and after); the kinds must match (report\nQ, PARAM_ERR); an integer variable (FLAGS2 bit 2) goes to ENDPROC_INT, others are assigned\n($3DCF).","comment":"Past TO or ','"},
        "8464": {"comment":"The variable"},
        "8467": {"comment":"To the values"},
        "8470": {"comment":"The variable's kind"},
        "8474": {"comment":"The value"},
