        "8529": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8531": {"comment":"Yes: the next one"},
        "8533": {"synopsis":"The procedure's entry dropped ($3A8A)."},
        "8537": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $61 (\"No DEFPROC\"); also from $12B8."},
        "8539": {"synopsis":"An integer variable: DEST - $3264 must be a slot below 26 (else ENDPROC_LET); the value is\ntaken as an integer (the DivMMC memory's $24F1) and stored in slot A by its $28B5.","comment":"DEST"},
        "8542": {"comment":"Less the slots' start"},
        "8547": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "8549": {"comment":"Yes: an ordinary LET"},
        "8551": {"comment":"The slot's number"},
        "8553": {"comment":"Below 26?"},
        "8555": {"comment":"No: an ordinary LET"},
        "8557": {"comment":"The slot kept"},
        "8558": {"comment":"The value as an integer"},
        "8563": {"comment":"The slot"},
        "8564": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "8569": {"comment":"The next variable"},
        "8571": {"synopsis":"Moves CH_ADD past the bracketed list at it: from the character after the '(' to its matching\n')', with nested brackets counted (B), strings (C bit 0) and hidden numbers skipped.\nExit: CH_ADD after the ')'.","comment":"HL = the character"},
        "8574": {"comment":"One bracket open; C = 0 after the DEC"},
        "8577": {"synopsis":"A quote: C bit 0 flips."},
        "8578": {"synopsis":"The next byte."},
        "8580": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "8584": {"comment":"Inside a string?"},
        "8586": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "8588": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "8592": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "8596": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "8600": {"comment":"Past its 5 bytes"},
        "8606": {"synopsis":"A ')': one bracket less; the last one sets CH_ADD.","comment":"Still nested"},
        "8608": {"comment":"CH_ADD after it"},
        "8612": {"synopsis":"A '(': one more."},
        "8615": {"synopsis":"PROC, or a procedure in an expression: D = the program's bank ($FF: the main one), A' = the\nentry type ($22 a statement, $23 a function). Running, a bank other than $FF is prepared\n($38BB); $5B65 = the bank.\nChecking: the name ($1313), its arguments in brackets ($254A, D = 0), the ')' (report C); a\nstatement may have TO and a list of variables ($2565).\nRunning (PROC_RUN): the return address goes to $5B97, the DEFPROC found by $1286, and each\nparameter bound to its argument (PROC_PARAM); then PROC_ENTER.","comment":"Running?"},
        "8619": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "8620": {"comment":"Checking: no bank"},
        "8622": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "8623": {"comment":"No: prepared"},
        "8626": {"synopsis":"$5B65 = the bank; running goes to PROC_RUN.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8627": {"comment":"$5B65"},
        "8630": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "8636": {"comment":"The name"},
        "8639": {"comment":"Its kind kept"},
        "8640": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "8641": {"comment":"')' at once?"},
        "8643": {"comment":"Arguments: expressions or arrays"},
        "8645": {"comment":"No: the arguments"},
        "8648": {"comment":"The ')'?"},
        "8650": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8653": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8655": {"comment":"The entry type"},
        "8656": {"comment":"A function: done"},
        "8659": {"comment":"The character"},
        "8660": {"comment":"TO?"},
        "8662": {"comment":"Yes: the variables"},
        "8666": {"synopsis":"Running a PROC: the return address to $5B97; the DivMMC memory's $2890; the DEFPROC looked\nup ($1286), its NXTLIN, line and statement kept at $5B8E, $5B90 and $5B96.","comment":"The return address"},
        "8667": {"comment":"Kept at $5B97"},
        "8670": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2890"},
        "8675": {"comment":"A = the entry type"},
        "8676": {"comment":"The DEFPROC found"},
        "8679": {"comment":"Its NXTLIN"},
        "8682": {"comment":"Its line"},
        "8686": {"comment":"Its statement"},
        "8689": {"synopsis":"The DEFPROC's next parameter: $86 (passed by reference) goes to PROC_REF; DATA ($E4) to\nPROC_DATA; others to PROC_VALUE.","comment":"The next character of the DEFPROC"},
        "8690": {"comment":"$86?"},
        "8692": {"comment":"No"},
        "8694": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8695": {"comment":"To the caller's argument"},
        "8698": {"comment":"'%': report Q"},
        "8702": {"comment":"A string: report Q"},
        "8706": {"comment":"Its start kept"},
        "8707": {"comment":"Looked up (ROM 3's LOOK_VARS)"},
        "8713": {"comment":"Not found: report 2"},
        "8716": {"comment":"Past the name"},
        "8719": {"comment":"DE = its start"},
        "8720": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "8723": {"comment":"LOOK_VARS's C kept"},
        "8724": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "8726": {"comment":"The name's place stacked"},
        "8729": {"comment":"E = LOOK_VARS's C"},
        "8730": {"comment":"Kind $90: a reference"},
