        "8736": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "8738": {"comment":"No"},
        "8740": {"comment":"Past \"()\""},
        "8742": {"comment":"An array"},
        "8744": {"synopsis":"Past a ',' to the DEFPROC's list again.","comment":"','?"},
        "8746": {"comment":"Yes: past it"},
        "8749": {"comment":"Back to the DEFPROC"},
        "8752": {"comment":"LOOK_VARS's C bit 6 clear?"},
        "8756": {"comment":"Bit 5 clear?"},
        "8760": {"synopsis":"D bit 6 set (C bit 6 clear, or bits 6 and 5 both set)."},
        "8762": {"synopsis":"On to make the local name (PROC_MAKE_LOCAL)."},
        "8764": {"synopsis":"A value parameter (DATA goes to PROC_DATA): the caller's next argument; with none left (')'\nor ',') the parameter is made with no value (D = $20). An argument that is a whole array\n(ARRAY_ARG) is passed by its place (D = $81, or $85 for an integer array); otherwise its\nvalue is evaluated (D = $80).","comment":"DATA?"},
        "8766": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8768": {"comment":"To the caller's argument"},
        "8771": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "8775": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8777": {"comment":"No: an argument"},
        "8779": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8780": {"synopsis":"No argument: back to the DEFPROC; its ')' ends the binding; otherwise the parameter has no\nvalue.","comment":"Back to the DEFPROC"},
        "8783": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "8785": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8788": {"comment":"Kind $20: no value"},
        "8792": {"synopsis":"An argument: a whole array?","comment":"An array with \"()\"?"},
        "8795": {"comment":"No: an expression"},
        "8797": {"comment":"Kind $85: an integer array"},
        "8799": {"comment":"Z: integer"},
        "8801": {"comment":"The array's length word"},
        "8805": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8806": {"comment":"DE = its data"},
        "8807": {"comment":"Its place stacked"},
        "8810": {"comment":"Kind $81: an array"},
        "8812": {"synopsis":"Past the ')'."},
        "8815": {"synopsis":"An argument with no parameter left: report Q."},
        "8818": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q, \"Parameter error\")."},
        "8820": {"synopsis":"The argument evaluated ($0DFC), kind $80.","comment":"The value"},
        "8823": {"comment":"Kind $80"},
        "8825": {"synopsis":"Past a ',', back to the DEFPROC: its ')' with an argument left is report Q; otherwise the\nkind gets FLAGS bit 6 (a number).","comment":"','?"},
        "8827": {"comment":"Yes: past it"},
        "8830": {"comment":"Back to the DEFPROC"},
        "8833": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "8835": {"comment":"Yes: report Q"},
        "8837": {"comment":"The value's kind"},
        "8842": {"comment":"With D's"},
        "8844": {"synopsis":"The parameter made a local variable from its name in the DEFPROC ($3C1C, D the kind; no\ncarry is report Q); then the next one after ',' or the end (PROC_PARAM_END).","comment":"The local variable"},
        "8847": {"comment":"Failed: report Q"},
        "8849": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "8852": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8854": {"comment":"No: the end"},
        "8856": {"comment":"The next parameter"},
        "8859": {"synopsis":"DATA in the DEFPROC: the arguments left are read by READ. A frame for them goes on the\nmachine stack: DATADD (as an offset from PROG for the main program), FLAGS2 bit 7, the type\n$45 with the bank in $5B78; ERR_SP set; DATADD goes back to just before the caller's next\nargument, $5B78 = the program's bank, FLAGS2 bit 7 set.","comment":"Past DATA"},
        "8860": {"comment":"Two words held"},
        "8862": {"comment":"Into the alternate set"},
        "8863": {"comment":"The bank in use for DATA"},
        "8866": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "8867": {"comment":"DATADD"},
        "8870": {"comment":"The main program?"},
        "8873": {"comment":"Yes: made an offset from PROG"},
        "8880": {"synopsis":"The frame pushed.","comment":"DATADD"},
        "8881": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 7"},
        "8886": {"comment":"One byte of it"},
        "8888": {"comment":"Type $45, C = the bank"},
        "8891": {"comment":"The held words back"},
        "8892": {"comment":"Pushed back"},
        "8893": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "8897": {"comment":"And the other"},
        "8898": {"comment":"To the caller's arguments"},
        "8901": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "8904": {"comment":"For READ"},
        "8907": {"synopsis":"Back over spaces to the character before the argument."},
        "8909": {"comment":"A space or control?"},
        "8913": {"comment":"DATADD there"},
        "8916": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 7: READ uses it"},
        "8920": {"comment":"Finish"},
        "8922": {"synopsis":"The DEFPROC's ')' must follow (report Q).","comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "8925": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "8927": {"comment":"No: report Q"},
        "8929": {"synopsis":"Into the procedure: $263A adds HL - ($5B8A) to the word just below the stack position kept\nat $5B92; CH_ADD past the caller's ')'; the bank selected ($38D4); PPC, NXTLIN and SUBPPC\nfrom the DEFPROC ($5B90, $5B8E, $5B96); the return address back on the stack. Then\nPROC_ENTRY_SET.","comment":"The entry's offset"},
        "8932": {"comment":"Back to the caller's line"},
        "8935": {"comment":"Past the ')'"},
        "8936": {"comment":"The bank"},
        "8939": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "8942": {"comment":"The DEFPROC's line"},
        "8945": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "8948": {"comment":"Its NXTLIN"},
        "8951": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "8954": {"comment":"Its statement"},
        "8957": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "8960": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "8964": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "8968": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8969": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $2907, then DEFADD = ERR_SP + 2 (also from LOCAL_CMD and VARS_RUN).","comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2907"},
        "8974": {"synopsis":"DEFADD = ERR_SP + 2.","comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "8979": {"comment":"DEFADD"},
        "8983": {"synopsis":"PROC with a bank (from the syntax table, $04A1): running, the bank number from the\ncalculator stack ($3823, report B over 255); then PROC_GO.","comment":"Running?"},
        "8987": {"comment":"Yes: A = the bank"},
        "8992": {"synopsis":"PROC (from the syntax table, $037D): the program's current bank ($5B77); then PROC_GO."},
        "8995": {"synopsis":"D = the bank, A' = $22 (a statement): PROC_CALL, then the statement's end.","comment":"D = the bank"},
        "8996": {"comment":"A statement's entry type"},
        "8999": {"comment":"The call"},
        "9002": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9006": {"synopsis":"A procedure in an expression (from ROM 2 and ROM 3): the caller's state goes on the machine\nstack: DEFADD, $5B65, X_PTR and the 15 bytes $5B8A-$5B98, then an error frame (a return\nthrough $5B3A, ERR_SP) so that the procedure runs as if from the edit line. PROC_CALL with\nA' = $23 and the current bank. Checking: FLAGS bit 6 takes the name's kind (PROC_FN_KIND).\nRunning: the DEFPROC's '=' expression is evaluated ($0DFC), the entry $23 returned to\n($3A86), the caller's brackets passed ($217B); then PROC_FN_BACK.","comment":"The caller's registers kept"},
        "9007": {"comment":"DEFADD"},
        "9011": {"comment":"$5B65"},
        "9015": {"comment":"X_PTR"},
        "9019": {"comment":"15 bytes of stack"},
        "9024": {"comment":"Their address kept"},
        "9025": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "9026": {"comment":"$5B8A-$5B98"},
        "9032": {"comment":"Copied there"},
        "9034": {"comment":"BC = their address"},
        "9035": {"comment":"HL = $5BFE"},
        "9038": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "9039": {"comment":"DEFADD"},
        "9042": {"comment":"Less the area - 2"},
        "9047": {"comment":"A = 0, flags"},
        "9048": {"comment":"The return address $5B3A"},
        "9052": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "9055": {"comment":"ERR_SP = here"},
        "9059": {"comment":"The old one kept"},
        "9060": {"comment":"A function's entry type"},
        "9063": {"comment":"The caller's registers"},
        "9064": {"comment":"Past the token"},
        "9065": {"comment":"The call"},
        "9068": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "9072": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9074": {"comment":"Past the '='"},
        "9075": {"comment":"The value"},
        "9078": {"comment":"The function's type"},
        "9080": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "9083": {"comment":"Past its brackets"},
        "9086": {"synopsis":"The caller's state back from the machine stack: ERR_SP, the 15 bytes at $5B8A, X_PTR, $5B65\nand DEFADD.","comment":"The old ERR_SP"},
        "9090": {"comment":"The 15 bytes"},
        "9094": {"comment":"Back to $5B8A"},
        "9102": {"comment":"SP above them"},
        "9103": {"comment":"X_PTR"},
        "9107": {"comment":"$5B65"},
        "9111": {"comment":"DEFADD"},
        "9116": {"synopsis":"Checking: FLAGS bit 6 = the name's kind (D bit 6).","comment":"FLAGS"},
        "9120": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "9122": {"comment":"The name's"},
        "9126": {"synopsis":"LOCAL (from the syntax table, $0380). Checking: a list of variables, each with an optional\n'=' and default ($2568, D = $80). Running: LOCAL_CHECK, the DivMMC memory's $2890, then each\nvariable made local ($3C1C, D = 2), separated by ','; then PROC_ENTRY_SET.","comment":"Running?"},
        "9130": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9132": {"comment":"Variables with defaults"},
        "9134": {"comment":"The list"},
        "9137": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9140": {"synopsis":"Running: not inside a loop, the DivMMC memory's $2890, then the variables.","comment":"Not inside a loop"},
        "9143": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $2890"},
        "9148": {"synopsis":"One variable made local.","comment":"Kind 2"},
        "9150": {"comment":"Made local"},
        "9153": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9156": {"comment":"','?"},
        "9158": {"comment":"No: finish"},
        "9161": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9164": {"synopsis":"The GO SUB stack's innermost entry ($3B18 with C = $20) must not be a loop (a type below\n$1F: the loop error); then the DivMMC memory's $28A2.","comment":"Any entry"},
        "9166": {"comment":"The innermost one"},
        "9169": {"comment":"Its type"},
        "9170": {"comment":"A loop?"},
        "9172": {"comment":"Yes: the loop error"},
        "9175": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's routine at $28A2"},
        "9181": {"synopsis":"A list of numeric variables that keep their value in the program line (from the syntax\ntable, $031D, and ROM 2 and ROM 3; probably the statement of token $82, which\nKEPT_VARS_CLEAR looks for). Followed by CLEAR ($FD): KEPT_VARS_CLEAR. Checking: before each\nname 6 bytes are put into the line (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM), a hidden number $0E and 5 zero\nbytes; the name must be a numeric variable (ROM 3's LV_LETTER, C bit 5; report C); an\noptional '=' and a number. Running: KEPT_VARS_RUN.","comment":"CLEAR?"},
        "9186": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9190": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9192": {"synopsis":"Checking one variable: its hidden number made.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "9195": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "9198": {"comment":"Room before the name (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "9201": {"comment":"Its first byte"},
        "9202": {"comment":"The hidden number marker"},
        "9204": {"comment":"5 zero bytes"},
        "9207": {"synopsis":"One zero byte."},
        "9211": {"comment":"Past it, to the name"},
        "9214": {"comment":"A letter must start it (ROM 3's LV_LETTER)"},
        "9217": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "9219": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9222": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9225": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "9227": {"comment":"Yes: the number"},
        "9230": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "9233": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "9236": {"comment":"','?"},
        "9238": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9241": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9244": {"synopsis":"Running, for each variable: the hidden number must be there (report C); only in a program\n(NEED_PROGRAM), not inside a loop (LOCAL_CHECK). The bank ($5B77), the number's offset (from\nPROG, or inside the bank by $3A2F) and its 5 bytes go to $5CA6-$5CAE; the 8 bytes from $5CA7\nare stacked as a string ($386C) and the variable is made local with kind $D0 ($3C1C), so it\nrefers to the number in the line. Then the next one after ','; at the end PROC_DEFADD.","comment":"The hidden number?"},
        "9246": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9249": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9250": {"comment":"Only in a program"},
        "9253": {"comment":"Not inside a loop"},
        "9256": {"comment":"HL = the marker"},
        "9257": {"comment":"Its 5 bytes"},
        "9258": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9259": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "9262": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "9263": {"comment":"E = 0"},
        "9265": {"comment":"At $5CA6"},
        "9269": {"comment":"The main program?"},
        "9270": {"comment":"No: inside the bank"},
        "9272": {"comment":"PROG"},
        "9276": {"comment":"An offset from it"},
        "9279": {"synopsis":"The offset at $5CA8, the value copied to $5CAA; CH_ADD past it; the 8 bytes from $5CA7\nstacked; the local made.","comment":"The offset"},
        "9282": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "9283": {"comment":"To $5CAA"},
        "9289": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "9291": {"comment":"CH_ADD past it"},
        "9294": {"comment":"The 8 bytes from $5CA7"},
        "9300": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "9303": {"comment":"Kind $D0"},
        "9305": {"comment":"Made local"},
        "9308": {"comment":"The top three stack words"},
        "9311": {"comment":"C of the third one less"},
        "9312": {"comment":"Put back"},
        "9315": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9318": {"comment":"','?"},
        "9320": {"comment":"No: DEFADD"},
        "9323": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9326": {"synopsis":"In a bank: the offset worked out by $3A2F."},
        "9332": {"synopsis":"The list followed by CLEAR: every such statement in the program (token $82 with a hidden\nnumber after it) gets its numbers reset: the place now is kept in an entry of type $21\n($3A40), the program searched from its first line (GO_TO_LINE with BC = 0, then STMT_SEARCH\nwith the test KEPT_VARS_TEST). Each variable's number becomes its '=' value or 0 (the 5\nbytes at $3FB8), copied into the bank too for a program in one. At the end the entry $21 is\nreturned to ($3A86; none is report 7).","comment":"Past CLEAR"},
        "9333": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "9336": {"comment":"A return entry"},
        "9341": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "9344": {"comment":"Line 0"},
        "9347": {"comment":"Its first line"},
        "9350": {"comment":"HL = its text"},
        "9351": {"comment":"Before it"},
        "9352": {"comment":"The test"},
        "9356": {"comment":"Token $82, no statement count"},
        "9359": {"comment":"Searched in the line"},
        "9362": {"comment":"And on"},
        "9365": {"comment":"The result"},
        "9367": {"synopsis":"The next statement with token $82 and a hidden number.","comment":"The test"},
        "9371": {"comment":"Token $82"},
        "9373": {"comment":"The search"},
        "9376": {"synopsis":"None left: KEPT_VARS_END."},
        "9378": {"synopsis":"One variable: its hidden number given the '=' value, or 0.","comment":"HL = the marker"},
        "9381": {"comment":"Its value's place"},
        "9382": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9383": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9387": {"comment":"CH_ADD at the name"},
        "9390": {"comment":"The name (ROM 3's LV_LETTER)"},
        "9393": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9396": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "9398": {"comment":"The constant 0"},
        "9401": {"comment":"No: 0"},
        "9403": {"comment":"The value"},
        "9406": {"comment":"HL = it, dropped from the stack"},
        "9409": {"synopsis":"The 5 bytes into the line; the alternate ROM's $30FE; a program in a bank gets them copied\nthere too (bank mapped by $32D0, address by $3A2F).","comment":"DE = the hidden number"},
        "9413": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "9415": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's routine at $30FE"},
        "9420": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "9423": {"comment":"The main program?"},
        "9426": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "9427": {"comment":"Mapped at $C000"},
        "9430": {"comment":"DE = the value's last byte"},
        "9432": {"comment":"Its place in the bank"},
        "9436": {"comment":"HL = the value's last byte"},
        "9440": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "9442": {"comment":"Back to the normal stack"},
