        "9446": {"comment":"','?"},
        "9448": {"comment":"No: the next statement"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9453": {"synopsis":"STMT_SEARCH's test for KEPT_VARS_CLEAR: the token must be followed by a hidden number ($0E):\nno carry; otherwise carry.","comment":"The character after the token"},
        "9454": {"comment":"A hidden number?"},
        "9459": {"synopsis":"Back to where CLEAR was ($3A86 with type $21); none is report 7. Also named by the syntax\ntable ($03D8).","comment":"The return entry's type"},
        "9461": {"comment":"Back to it"},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $06 (report 7, \"RETURN without GO SUB\")."},
        "9467": {"synopsis":"Is the name at CH_ADD a whole array, a name followed by \"()\"? An ordinary one is looked up\n(ROM 3's LOOK_VARS; not found is report 2); an integer one ('%' and a letter, ARRAY_ARG_INT)\nneeds no look-up.\nExit: no carry when it is not: CH_ADD back at the name. Carry for an array: CH_ADD at the\n')'; Z and E = the letter (0-25) for an integer array.","comment":"DE = the name's start"},
        "9469": {"comment":"'%'?"},
        "9473": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "9476": {"comment":"No: not an array"},
        "9477": {"synopsis":"Through the name's letters and digits."},
        "9478": {"comment":"A letter or a digit?"},
        "9483": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "9485": {"comment":"Yes: past it"},
        "9488": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "9492": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9493": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9495": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD at the name's start again (HL then the place reached); no carry unless Z (both\nbrackets).","comment":"HL = the start"},
        "9496": {"comment":"CH_ADD there"},
        "9499": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "9501": {"comment":"Not \"()\": no"},
        "9502": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "9503": {"comment":"Looked up (ROM 3's LOOK_VARS)"},
        "9509": {"comment":"DE = the ')'"},
        "9510": {"comment":"CH_ADD there"},
        "9515": {"comment":"Found: carry"},
        "9517": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $01 (report 2, \"Variable not found\"); also from $0847, $1F35 and\n$2209."},
        "9519": {"synopsis":"'%': a letter must follow, then \"()\": its number 0-25 in E.","comment":"Past '%'"},
        "9520": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "9523": {"comment":"H - 1 (no use found)"},
        "9524": {"comment":"No: not an array"},
        "9526": {"comment":"Lower case"},
        "9528": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9529": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9530": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "9534": {"comment":"The next"},
        "9535": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9539": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "9540": {"comment":"0 for 'a'"},
        "9543": {"comment":"Z, carry: an integer array"},
        "9546": {"synopsis":"Checks a list of arguments separated by ',': each an expression ($0DFC), empty, or (D bit 7\nclear) a whole array (ARRAY_ARG).\nExit: A = the character after the list.","comment":"The kind kept"},
        "9547": {"comment":"Expressions only?"},
        "9551": {"comment":"',': an empty one"},
        "9555": {"comment":"A whole array?"},
        "9558": {"comment":"No: an expression"},
        "9560": {"comment":"Past its ')'"},
        "9563": {"synopsis":"An expression."},
        "9566": {"synopsis":"Another after ','?","comment":"The kind back"},
        "9567": {"comment":"','?"},
        "9569": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9573": {"synopsis":"The variables after TO (D = 0)."},
        "9575": {"synopsis":"Past TO or ','."},
        "9576": {"synopsis":"Checks a list of variables separated by ',' (also from $1DB3, $23AE and $34BB). D bit 6:\nDATA alone (then ')' must follow) ends it, and $86 (by reference) may come before a name,\nbut not before '%' (report Q). D bit 7: a whole array (ARRAY_ARG) is allowed, and '=' with a\ndefault of the variable's kind (else report Q). Otherwise each is a variable (CLASS_1,\n$05A3).","comment":"The character"},
        "9579": {"comment":"Parameters?"},
        "9581": {"comment":"No"},
        "9583": {"comment":"DATA?"},
        "9587": {"comment":"$86?"},
        "9591": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9592": {"comment":"'%'?"},
        "9596": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q, \"Parameter error\")."},
        "9598": {"synopsis":"One variable.","comment":"The kind kept"},
        "9599": {"comment":"Arrays and defaults?"},
        "9603": {"comment":"A whole array?"},
        "9606": {"comment":"No"},
        "9608": {"comment":"Past its ')'"},
        "9612": {"synopsis":"A variable (CLASS_1); with D bit 7, an optional '=' and default.","comment":"The variable"},
        "9615": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9619": {"comment":"Defaults allowed?"},
        "9623": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "9627": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9628": {"comment":"The variable's kind"},
        "9632": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9633": {"comment":"The default"},
        "9637": {"comment":"Its kind"},
        "9640": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "9643": {"comment":"No: report Q"},
        "9645": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9648": {"synopsis":"Another after ','?"},
        "9653": {"synopsis":"DATA: the ')' must follow.","comment":"Past DATA"},
        "9654": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9656": {"comment":"No: report Q"},
        "9659": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($049B): $5C75 = 0 (a jump, not a call), then JUMP_BANK.","comment":"A jump"},
        "9663": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($049E): JUMP_IN_BANK with B = 0 (a number needed), then on through\n$0931."},
        "9670": {"synopsis":"C = B; running: $38BB, then the bank number from the calculator stack ($3823); then\nJUMP_TARGET with A = the bank.","comment":"C = B"},
        "9671": {"synopsis":"Also from $35D2, with C given.","comment":"Running?"},
        "9676": {"comment":"The bank prepared"},
        "9679": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "9683": {"comment":"To the target"},
        "9685": {"synopsis":"From LOOP_EXIT with something after its token: running, the loop's entry dropped ($3BFD);\nthen JUMP_PLAIN.","comment":"Running?"},
        "9691": {"comment":"Yes: the entry dropped"},
        "9694": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($04CA): $5C75 = 0 (a jump); JUMP_CMD."},
        "9698": {"synopsis":"From the syntax table ($0335): JUMP_CURRENT with B = 0; then on through $0931.","comment":"A number needed"},
        "9703": {"synopsis":"The return address dropped; on through $0931."},
        "9707": {"synopsis":"C = B, A = the program's bank ($5B77); then JUMP_TARGET.","comment":"C = B"},
        "9708": {"synopsis":"Also from $35E3 (C = $FF, B = 1): A = the program's bank, then JUMP_TARGET.","comment":"The current bank"},
        "9711": {"synopsis":"A jump or call ($5C75 zero or not) in bank A ($5B65), the return address kept at $5B56. The\ntarget: with C = $FF, PROC ($93, kind $22) or FN ($A8, kind $23) and a name; '@' and a label\n(kind $21); otherwise a line number (JUMP_LINE). A named target is found by $1286 (running),\nits line, NXTLIN and statement set; a jump then drops the GO SUB entry $1286 made ($3C12), a\ncall adds the distance moved to the word below $5B92.","comment":"The bank"},
        "9714": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "9718": {"comment":"The character"},
        "9721": {"comment":"C = $FF?"},
        "9722": {"comment":"No"},
        "9724": {"comment":"C back"},
        "9725": {"comment":"Kind $22, '('"},
        "9728": {"comment":"PROC?"},
        "9732": {"comment":"Kind $23"},
        "9733": {"comment":"FN?"},
        "9737": {"synopsis":"'@' and a label?","comment":"'@'?"},
        "9739": {"comment":"No: a line number"},
        "9741": {"comment":"Kind $21"},
        "9744": {"synopsis":"A named target: checking, JUMP_NAME_CHECK; running, found by $1286.","comment":"Past the token"},
        "9745": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9749": {"comment":"No"},
        "9751": {"comment":"A = the kind"},
        "9752": {"comment":"Found"},
        "9755": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "9758": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "9762": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "9765": {"comment":"The bank"},
        "9768": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "9771": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "9775": {"comment":"A call?"},
        "9779": {"comment":"No: the entry dropped"},
        "9782": {"comment":"HL = X_PTR - 1"},
        "9786": {"synopsis":"Adds HL - ($5B8A) to the word just below the stack position kept at $5B92 (also from\nPROC_ENTER).","comment":"$5B8A"},
        "9791": {"comment":"HL - it"},
        "9793": {"comment":"DE = the difference"},
        "9794": {"comment":"The stack position"},
        "9797": {"comment":"The word below it"},
        "9798": {"comment":"Low byte"},
        "9802": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "9806": {"synopsis":"Checking a named target: the name ($1315); with C = $FF that is all; otherwise the\nstatement's end.","comment":"The kind kept"},
        "9807": {"comment":"The name"},
        "9810": {"comment":"A = the kind"},
        "9811": {"comment":"C = $FF?"},
        "9812": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "9816": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "9818": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9821": {"synopsis":"A line number: B = 0 needs a number (CLASS_6, $0635), B = 1 an optional one ($0DF0); then\nthe statement's end. A call ($5C75 not 0) makes an entry of type $21 ($3A40). The number\ntaken (report B over 65535, $381B), then GO_TO_LINE in bank $5B65.","comment":"CLASS_6"},
        "9824": {"comment":"B = 0?"},
        "9826": {"comment":"No: an optional number"},
        "9829": {"synopsis":"The number read; the statement's end; a call's entry.","comment":"The number"},
        "9832": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "9835": {"comment":"A call?"},
        "9839": {"comment":"Type $21"},
        "9841": {"comment":"Yes: the entry"},
        "9844": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "9848": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "9851": {"comment":"The bank"},
        "9854": {"synopsis":"Goes to line BC of the program in bank A (also from LOAD_PROGRAM, KEPT_VARS_CLEAR and\n$362B): PPC = BC, the bank selected ($38D4), the line looked for ($3962). Found: NXTLIN,\nCH_ADD at its text and SUBPPC = 1, with carry. None: GO_TO_END.","comment":"PPC"},
        "9858": {"comment":"The bank selected"},
        "9861": {"comment":"The line"},
        "9864": {"comment":"Not there"},
        "9866": {"comment":"Its text (DE) and the next line (HL)"},
        "9869": {"comment":"DE past the length"},
        "9870": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "9871": {"synopsis":"SUBPPC = 1, NXTLIN = HL, CH_ADD = DE.","comment":"SUBPPC = 1"},
        "9875": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "9878": {"comment":"CH_ADD"},
        "9883": {"synopsis":"No such line: the main program ($5B77 = $FF), NXTLIN and CH_ADD just below WORKSP, so the\nprogram stops.","comment":"The main program"},
        "9888": {"comment":"WORKSP"},
        "9891": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - 1"},
        "9892": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "9894": {"comment":"HL = WORKSP - 2"},
        "9895": {"comment":"NXTLIN, CH_ADD"},
        "9901": {"synopsis":"Called from other memories (no caller in this ROM): the return address dropped; the next\nstack word kept at $5B56 (its high byte the value for port $E3), the one after it at $5B54\n(where to go); bank A mapped at $C000 on the alternate stack ($32D0); then port $E3 set\n(DIVMMC_OUT_E3); the RET runs from the DivMMC memory and goes to that address, HL and BC\nkept.","comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "9902": {"comment":"Dropped, HL back"},
        "9903": {"comment":"The port value's word"},
        "9904": {"comment":"At $5B56"},
        "9907": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9908": {"comment":"The address's word"},
        "9909": {"comment":"At $5B54"},
        "9912": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9913": {"comment":"Bank A at $C000, the alternate stack"},
        "9916": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "9917": {"comment":"The address"},
        "9920": {"comment":"On the stack, HL back"},
        "9921": {"comment":"BC kept at $5B54"},
        "9925": {"comment":"B = the port value"},
        "9931": {"synopsis":"CALL $26CB / DEFW addr: runs the routine at addr in the DivMMC memory, with port $E3 = $87\n(its memory at $0000, bank 7); A is kept at $5B56. Then DIVMMC_CALL: the routine returns to\n$2705 in the DivMMC memory, not in this ROM.","comment":"A kept"},
        "9934": {"comment":"Port $E3's value"},
        "9936": {"synopsis":"The word after the CALL into BC, the return address past it; BC kept at $5B54.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "9940": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "9941": {"comment":"BC = the word after it"},
        "9945": {"comment":"The return address past it"},
        "9946": {"synopsis":"Enters the DivMMC memory at BC with A = the value for port $E3 (also from $058F and $3EAE).\n$2705 is pushed as the way back: once the DivMMC memory is paged in, that address is in its\nmemory (code there pages it out again), not this ROM's error table at $2705. Then BC is\npushed, the caller's A ($5B56) and BC ($5B54) are restored, and DIVMMC_OUT_E3 sets port $E3.\nFrom the OUT on, the code runs in the DivMMC memory: its $2700-$2704 restore BC and RET into\nBC.","comment":"The way back, in the DivMMC memory"},
        "9950": {"comment":"The address"},
        "9951": {"comment":"The port value"},
        "9952": {"comment":"The caller's A"},
        "9957": {"synopsis":"CALL $26E5 / DEFW addr: the same as DIVMMC_CALL_87, with port $E3 = $8A (bank 10).","comment":"A kept"},
        "9960": {"comment":"Port $E3's value"},
        "9964": {"synopsis":"Calls the alternate ROM's routine at $2882 (from other ROMs: ROM 0's $32E9, ROM 3's $060B,\n$0613, $287A).","comment":"The alternate ROM's routine at $2882"},
        "9975": {"synopsis":"From ROM 2 ($23C9): BC is kept at $5B54; port $E3 = the high byte of the word on the stack\n(DIVMMC_OUT_E3). After the OUT the DivMMC memory is paged in, so the RET at $2704 runs there\nand goes to the address under that word."},
        "9979": {"synopsis":"B = the port value from the stack."},
        "9980": {"synopsis":"Port $E3 = B (the DivMMC control: bit 7 maps its memory at $0000-$3FFF, the low bits pick\nits bank). The OUT pages that memory in, so the next instructions ($2700-$2704: BC back from\n$5B54, RET) run from the DivMMC memory, which must hold the same bytes there.","comment":"Port $E3: the DivMMC control"},
        "9984": {"comment":"Fetched from the DivMMC memory now paged in"},
        "9989": {"synopsis":"Error message pointers: 75 words, one for each error code $1D-$67 in turn (the code less\n$1D;\ncodes past $67 use the last word), each the address of a bit-7-ended message in\nERR_MESSAGES. Read at\n$0D2A, which takes the code from ROM 0's $0E60 and prints the message through $37D6. Codes\n$1D, $1F,\n$26, $2C, $49 and $67 point at $0026, a lone space ($A0). Several codes share a message, and\ncode\n$2A points into the middle of code $29's (\"Out of range\" is the tail of \"Note Out of\nrange\")."},
        "10139": {"synopsis":"The error messages ERR_MSG_TABLE points at, each ended by bit 7 of its last character:\n\"Wrong\nfile type\", \"Too many parentheses\", \"Invalid note\", \"Note Out of range\", \"Too many tied\nnotes\",\n\"Bad filename\", \"Bad parameters\", \"Drive not found\", \"File not found\", \"Already exists\",\n\"End of\nfile\", \"Disk full\", \"Dir full\", \"Read only\", \"Bad file number\", \"In use\", \"No rename between\ndrives\", \"Too big\", \"Not bootable\", \"Not ready\", \"Seek fail\", \"Disk error\", \"Unsuitable\nmedia\",\n\"Invalid attribute\", \"Dest can't be wild\", \"Dest must be path\", \"Invalid drive\", \"Code\nlength\nerror\", \"Invalid partition\", \"Not implemented\", \"Partition open\", \"Out of handles\", \"No swap\npartition\", \"Invalid device\", \"Invalid path\", \"Fragmented - use .DEFRAG\", \"Invalid mode\",\n\"Direct\ncommand error\", \"Loop error\", \"No DEFPROC\", \"Dot command error\", \"No ENDIF\", \"No label\" (43\ntexts)."},
        "10730": {"synopsis":"\"Logical drives: \" and a $00: the drive list's heading, printed by SD_LIST_DRIVES through\n$36F5\n(which stops at a byte below $0D). Its last three bytes are MSG_COLON_SPACE."},
        "10744": {"synopsis":"\": \" and a $00, the tail of MSG_LOGICAL_DRV; printed on its own at $1922 (through $37C4)."},
        "10876": {"synopsis":"\"Erase \" and a $00: a question for ASK_YES_NO, asked by page 0 ($3960, through its $3B3E)."},
        "10885": {"synopsis":"\"Paste here\" and a $00: a question for ASK_YES_NO, asked by page 0 ($3A7E)."},
        "10896": {"synopsis":"\"Copy\" and a $00: a question for ASK_YES_NO, asked by page 0 ($3A36)."},
        "10901": {"synopsis":"\"Move\" and a $00: a question for ASK_YES_NO, asked by page 0 ($3A2F)."},
        "10906": {"synopsis":"\"Move here\" and a $00: a question for ASK_YES_NO, asked by page 0 ($3A83); $3FC0 also loads\nit."},
        "10916": {"synopsis":"The copyright lines, printed by SD_LIST_DRIVES's fresh start (at $2C0B, through $36F5): $7F\n(the\ncopyright sign), \"1982, 1986, 1987 Amstrad Plc.\", ENTER, $7F, \"2000-2023 Garry Lancaster\nv2.08\";\nbit 7 ends the last character."},
        "10979": {"synopsis":"Calls the DivMMC memory's $27A8 (port $E3 = $8A: bank 10, through $26E5) with BC = HL = 10.\nNo\ncaller was found in the four pages.\nChanges: as that routine.","comment":"BC = 10"},
        "10982": {"comment":"HL = 10"},
        "10984": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 10's $27A8"},
        "10990": {"synopsis":"RST $30: RAM bank 0 at $C000 with ROM 1 (this ROM) paged (NextReg $8E = $09), then SWAP_SP:\nback to the stack whose pointer is kept at $5B6A. Undoes RST $18 (SWAP_SP_BANK7). Also\ncalled at\n$0F38, $1C77 and $359A.\nChanges: AF' (the return address), $5B52, $5B6A.","comment":"RAM bank 0 at $C000, ROM 1 (NextReg $8E)"},
        "10994": {"synopsis":"Swaps SP with the stack pointer kept at $5B6A, the return address moved to the other stack.\nHL\nis kept through $5B52, AF through AF'. Called by COPY_BANK0_TO_7, COPY_BANK7_TO_0, $3034,\n$303C and\nPOKE_STORE.\nChanges: AF' (the return address), $5B52, $5B6A.","comment":"AF aside"},
        "10995": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "10996": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "10999": {"comment":"HL = the other stack's SP"},
        "11002": {"comment":"This one's kept at $5B6A"},
        "11006": {"comment":"Onto the other stack"},
        "11007": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "11010": {"comment":"The return address onto it"},
        "11011": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "11013": {"synopsis":"RST $18: as SWAP_SP (onto the stack whose pointer is kept at $5B6A), then RAM bank 7 at\n$C000\nwith ROM 1 (NextReg $8E = $79). RST $30 (SWAP_SP_BANK0) undoes it.\nChanges: AF' (the return address), $5B52, $5B6A.","comment":"AF aside"},
        "11014": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "11015": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "11018": {"comment":"Swap SP with the one at $5B6A"},
        "11026": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "11029": {"comment":"The return address onto it"},
        "11031": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000, ROM 1"},
        "11036": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes (BC not 0) from HL to DE, reading each with RAM bank 0 at $C000 and writing\nit\nwith bank 7 there (NextReg $8E = $09, $79), on the stack at $5B6A (SWAP_SP). Ends with bank\n0.\nCalled from $0124, $16EC and $1B8B.\nExit: HL and DE past the block, BC = 0.\nChanges: AF, AF'.","comment":"Onto the other stack"},
        "11039": {"synopsis":"One byte, read in bank 0 and written in bank 7.","comment":"Bank 0: read"},
        "11044": {"comment":"Bank 7: write"},
        "11049": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "11051": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11056": {"comment":"Bank 0 again"},
        "11060": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "11064": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes (BC not 0) from HL to DE, reading each with RAM bank 7 at $C000 and writing\nit\nwith bank 0 there (NextReg $8E = $79, $09), on the stack at $5B6A (SWAP_SP). Ends with bank\n0.\nCalled from $19A8.\nExit: HL and DE past the block, BC = 0.\nChanges: AF, AF'.","comment":"Onto the other stack"},
        "11067": {"synopsis":"One byte, read in bank 7 and written in bank 0.","comment":"Bank 7: read"},
        "11072": {"comment":"Bank 0: write"},
        "11077": {"comment":"The next byte"},
        "11079": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "11084": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "11088": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK as ROM 3's BREAK_KEY does: carry unless SPACE (port $7FFE bit 0) and CAPS SHIFT\n(port $FEFE bit 0) are both down. Both down: $3E75 (bit 1 of E from the DivMMC memory's\n$299C,\nthrough $0059) set returns NC; otherwise the caller's return address is taken off and the\nprogram\nstops: error code $0C (report D) when the caller was the CALL at $0931, $14 (report L) for\nthe one\nat $0953.\nExit: carry, no BREAK; NZ when BREAK is ignored.\nChanges: AF, HL, BC (when it stops).","comment":"Keyboard row SPACE-B"},
        "11092": {"comment":"SPACE up? Carry: no BREAK"},
        "11094": {"comment":"Row CAPS SHIFT-V"},
        "11098": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT up?"},
        "11100": {"comment":"BREAK ignored now? (DivMMC state)"},
        "11104": {"comment":"HL = the caller's return address"},
        "11105": {"comment":"From the CALL at $0931?"},
        "11112": {"comment":"Error code $14: report L"},
        "11114": {"synopsis":"Called from $0931: error code $0C (report D)."},
        "11116": {"synopsis":"Asks a yes/no question in the lower screen: the text at HL, then \"? (Y/N)\" and ENTER (at\n$3F9F),\neach through $37B9 (stream -3, then a $00-ended text); waits for a new key (FLAGS bit 5)\nthat is Y\nor N in either case (LAST_K); then ROM 0's $0EC9 clears the lower screen. Called from page 0\nthrough\nits RST $18 ($2FFC and $3B4A), with page 1's questions MSG_ERASE ... MSG_MOVE_HERE.\nEntry: HL = the question, $00-ended.\nExit: Z for Y, NZ for N; NC.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The question in the lower screen"},
        "11119": {"comment":"Then '? (Y/N)'"},
        "11125": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "11128": {"comment":"No key yet"},
        "11130": {"synopsis":"Until a new key arrives (FLAGS bit 5); keys other than Y and N wait again.","comment":"A new key?"},
        "11134": {"comment":"Taken"},
        "11136": {"comment":"LAST_K, made upper case"},
        "11141": {"comment":"Y?"},
        "11145": {"comment":"N?"},
        "11149": {"comment":"N: NZ"},
        "11150": {"synopsis":"The answer's flags kept over ROM 0's $0EC9, which clears the lower screen.","comment":"The answer's flags kept"},
        "11151": {"comment":"ROM 0: clear the lower screen"},
        "11158": {"synopsis":"REMOUNT, by its job (its word at $0389 in the syntax table, after class $0C): on the stack\nat $5B6A\nwith RAM bank 7 at $C000 (RST $18), REMOUNT with C = 2 (the drive list to stream 2); no\ncarry ends at\n$0DCE (bank 0 and the stack back, then the error reported at $0DCA); otherwise RST $30 and\nback.","comment":"Bank 7, the other stack"},
        "11159": {"comment":"Stream 2 for the drive list"},
        "11161": {"comment":"Let the card be changed"},
        "11164": {"comment":"NC: $0DCE"},
        "11167": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "11169": {"synopsis":"Lets the SD card(s) be changed, then lists the drives (as the API document says IDE_MOUNT is\nused):\n1. ROM 2's IDE_MOUNT with A = 0: all files closed, all drives and swap partitions unmapped;\n   no\ncarry (an error, A = its code) returns NC at once.\n2. \"Remove/insert SD and press Y\" in the lower screen ($37B9); waits for Y in either case\n   (ROM 0's\n$11E0 for each key); ROM 0's $0EC9 clears the lower screen.\n3. C = 2: stream 2 selected when running ($1353). ROM 2's $1AEB, then the DivMMC memory's\n   $306B (bank\n10) with A = C; for a result below 2 also its $29FA (bank 7).\n4. Result 3: returns with carry. Result 2 or more: the drive list (SD_LIST_DRIVES).\n5. Below 2, a fresh start screen first: ROM 0's $0EDD; RST $30; CPU speed 3.5 MHz (NextReg\n   $07 = 0);\nROM 2's $0F82 with HL = $2034, then $2050; RST $18; ROM 0's $1003; ROM 3's CLS_CMD; the\nDivMMC\nmemory's $2A1B (bank 7); COPYRIGHT_MSG; then the drive list.\nEntry: C = the list's stream (2); on the stack at $5B6A with bank 7 at $C000 (RST $18).\nExit: carry, done; NC with A = IDE_MOUNT's error code.","comment":"The stream kept"},
        "11170": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "11171": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_MOUNT, A = 0: close files, unmap drives"},
        "11174": {"comment":"C back"},
        "11175": {"comment":"NC: return"},
        "11176": {"comment":"C kept"},
        "11177": {"comment":"'Remove/insert SD and press Y'"},
        "11180": {"comment":"In the lower screen"},
        "11183": {"synopsis":"Until Y is pressed, in either case.","comment":"ROM 0's $11E0: A = a key"},
        "11188": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "11190": {"comment":"Y?"},
        "11194": {"comment":"ROM 0: clear the lower screen"},
        "11199": {"comment":"C back"},
        "11200": {"comment":"A = the stream"},
        "11201": {"comment":"Stream 2?"},
        "11205": {"comment":"Selected when running"},
        "11208": {"comment":"A = 2"},
        "11210": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's $1AEB, then the DivMMC memory's $306B with A = the stream; its result in A picks the\nending.","comment":"A kept"},
        "11211": {"comment":"ROM 2's $1AEB"},
        "11214": {"comment":"A back"},
        "11215": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 10's $306B: A = a result"},
        "11220": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11221": {"comment":"Below 2?"},
        "11225": {"comment":"Then DivMMC bank 7's $29FA too"},
        "11230": {"synopsis":"By the result: 3 done (carry), 2 or more the drive list, below 2 a fresh start screen first.","comment":"A = the result"},
        "11231": {"comment":"3: done, carry"},
        "11235": {"comment":"2 or more: the list"},
        "11239": {"comment":"ROM 0's $0EDD"},
        "11244": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "11245": {"comment":"CPU speed 3.5 MHz"},
        "11249": {"comment":"HL = $2034"},
        "11252": {"comment":"ROM 2's $0F82"},
        "11255": {"comment":"HL = $2050"},
        "11258": {"comment":"ROM 2's $0F82 again"},
        "11261": {"comment":"Bank 7, the other stack"},
        "11262": {"comment":"ROM 0's $1003"},
        "11267": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD"},
        "11270": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 7's $2A1B"},
        "11275": {"comment":"The copyright lines"},
        "11278": {"comment":"Printed up to bit 7"},
        "11281": {"synopsis":"Lists the drives: MSG_LOGICAL_DRV, then each letter A-P for which ROM 2's $03C4 (A = 0-15)\ngives no carry, the one equal to $5B79 (probably the current drive) in inverse video; ENTER\nat the\nend. Each character goes through $3708 (printed with bank 0 paged).\nExit: carry.","comment":"'Logical drives: '"},
        "11287": {"comment":"B = 16 drives, C = 'A'"},
        "11290": {"synopsis":"One drive letter.","comment":"A = the drive, 0-15"},
        "11293": {"comment":"ROM 2's $03C4: drive A there?"},
        "11296": {"comment":"Carry: no; the next"},
        "11298": {"comment":"INVERSE"},
        "11303": {"comment":"The letter in $5B79?"},
        "11307": {"comment":"INVERSE 0, or 1 for it"},
        "11312": {"synopsis":"INVERSE's operand: 1 for the drive in $5B79, else 0.","comment":"The operand"},
        "11315": {"comment":"The letter"},
        "11319": {"comment":"INVERSE"},
        "11324": {"comment":"0: off again"},
        "11328": {"synopsis":"The next letter.","comment":"Next letter"},
        "11331": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "11336": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "11338": {"synopsis":"\"Remove/insert SD and press Y\", ENTER and a $00: REMOUNT's prompt, printed through $37B9."},
        "11368": {"synopsis":"A command without operands (its word at $04E4 in the syntax table, after class $0C): stops\nwith an error kept in the DivMMC memory. Four words are read through $3F93 (its $2860, bank\n7, HL =\nthe address, DE = the word) from $3140, $3142, $3144 and $3146 there:\n1. The first's low byte, less one, is ERR_NR ($FF gives $63).\n2. The second is PPC, the third's low byte SUBPPC.\n3. The fourth's low byte goes to $38D4 (into $5B77).\nThen $0ABA, and the report through $0C1A.","comment":"DivMMC $3140: the error"},
        "11371": {"comment":"DE = the word there"},
        "11374": {"comment":"E = $FF?"},
        "11379": {"comment":"Then code $63"},
        "11383": {"synopsis":"Otherwise the code is E - 1.","comment":"Code = E - 1"},
        "11384": {"synopsis":"ERR_NR = A.","comment":"ERR_NR"},
        "11387": {"comment":"DivMMC $3142: the line"},
        "11393": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "11397": {"comment":"DivMMC $3144: the statement"},
        "11403": {"comment":"SUBPPC"},
        "11407": {"comment":"DivMMC $3146"},
        "11413": {"comment":"Its low byte to $38D4"},
        "11417": {"comment":"$0ABA"},
        "11420": {"comment":"The report"},
        "11423": {"synopsis":"Swaps DEFADD with the word at $5B8C, then CH_ADD with X_PTR (SWAP_CH_X_PTR). Called from\n$2113\nand $2122.\nExit: as SWAP_CH_X_PTR.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"BC = DEFADD"},
        "11427": {"comment":"HL = the word at $5B8C"},
        "11430": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "11437": {"synopsis":"Swaps CH_ADD and X_PTR, then reads the character at the new CH_ADD as $3ED0 does (stepping\npast\nspaces and control codes). Called nine times between $21F7 and $22E4.\nExit: A = the character, HL = CH_ADD.\nChanges: F, BC.","comment":"BC = CH_ADD"},
        "11441": {"comment":"HL = X_PTR"},
        "11444": {"comment":"X_PTR = the old CH_ADD"},
        "11448": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the old X_PTR; A"},
        "11451": {"synopsis":"Called through IX by the search at $209F (IX = $2CBB) at each token found: past it; when the\nnext\ncharacter is token $8E the depth at $5C92 (IY + $58) goes down by one, NC when it reaches 0\n(the\nmatch); anything else takes the depth up by one.\nExit: carry, search on; NC, found.","comment":"A = the next character"},
        "11452": {"comment":"Token $8E?"},
        "11454": {"comment":"Carry: search on"},
        "11457": {"comment":"Otherwise one level deeper"},
        "11461": {"synopsis":"One level out; NC at level 0.","comment":"One level out"},
        "11464": {"comment":"Not 0: carry"},
        "11465": {"comment":"Found: NC"},
        "11467": {"synopsis":"Called through IX by the search at $1EA8 (IX = $2CCB) at each token found: past it, the next\ncharacter must be '%' (otherwise carry); past that, the DivMMC memory's $27C0 (bank 7) gives\nHL,\ncompared with DEST.\nExit: NC when they are equal; carry otherwise.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"A = the next character"},
        "11468": {"comment":"'%'?"},
        "11470": {"comment":"No: carry"},
        "11472": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11474": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 7's $27C0"},
        "11479": {"comment":"DE = its HL"},
        "11480": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "11483": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "11487": {"comment":"Yes: NC"},
        "11488": {"comment":"No: carry"},
        "11490": {"synopsis":"Called through IX by the search at $1E87 (IX = $2CE2) at each token found: past it, a '%'\ngives\ncarry at once; otherwise the variable there ($0642, ROM 3's CLASS_4) is tested by ROM 3's\nNEXT_VAR_TEST with DE = the word at $5B8E.\nExit: NC when it is the one; carry otherwise.\nKeeps DE.","comment":"A = the next character"},
        "11491": {"comment":"'%'?"},
        "11493": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "11496": {"comment":"The variable (CLASS_4)"},
        "11499": {"comment":"DE = the word at $5B8E"},
        "11503": {"comment":"ROM 3's NEXT_VAR_TEST"},
        "11507": {"comment":"NZ: carry"},
        "11509": {"comment":"The one: NC"},
        "11511": {"synopsis":"RST $28's second half (from $002D: BC kept at $5B54, HL on the stack, HL = the address of\nthe\nword after the RST): BC = the word, the return address moved past it and HL back; $5B3E\n(which\nselects ROM 1 again) pushed as the way back, and the word as the routine; BC back, then\n$5B48 selects\nROM 3 and returns into the routine.","comment":"BC = the word after the RST"},
        "11515": {"comment":"Return past it; HL back"},
        "11516": {"comment":"Way back: $5B3E selects ROM 1"},
        "11520": {"comment":"The routine in ROM 3"},
        "11521": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "11525": {"comment":"ROM 3 selected, RET into it"},
        "11528": {"synopsis":"Sets the CPU speed (its word at $04D5 in the syntax table, after class $00): A = the number,\na\nbyte ($3823), 0-3 for 3.5, 7, 14 or 28 MHz (nextreg.txt), into NextReg $07; 4 or more is\nreport B\n($13E6).","comment":"A = the number"},
        "11531": {"comment":"4 or more: report B"},
        "11536": {"comment":"CPU speed"},
        "11540": {"synopsis":"CIRCLE when running (its word at $03CA in the syntax table, after class 9, ',' and class\n$00):\nwith a nonzero low nibble in $5C7F the DivMMC memory's $2D19 (bank 10) draws it; otherwise\nROM 3's\nCIRCLE_CMD from $232D, past its own syntax checking.","comment":"$5C7F's low nibble"},
        "11545": {"comment":"0: ROM 3 draws it"},
        "11547": {"comment":"DivMMC bank 10's $2D19"},
        "11553": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's CIRCLE_CMD from $232D, its calculation.","comment":"ROM 3's CIRCLE_CMD at $232D"},
        "11745": {"synopsis":"A separator in a print list, as ROM 3's PRINT_SEP: ';' nothing, ',' the comma control code\n($06)\nwhen running, an apostrophe ENTER (ROM 3's PRINT_NEWLINE). Then past it; at the end of the\nlist (')',\nENTER or ':', $08E6) the caller's return address is dropped.\nExit: Z when a separator was taken; NZ with A = the character when there was none.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "11748": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "11752": {"comment":"','?"},
        "11756": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "11762": {"comment":"The comma control code"},
        "11769": {"synopsis":"An apostrophe: ENTER; anything else returns NZ.","comment":"Apostrophe?"},
        "11772": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_NEWLINE"},
        "11775": {"synopsis":"Past the separator; at the end of the list the caller's return is dropped.","comment":"Past it"},
        "11776": {"comment":"The end of the list?"},
        "11781": {"comment":"Yes: the caller's return dropped"},
        "11782": {"synopsis":"Z: a separator was taken.","comment":"Z"},
        "11784": {"synopsis":"One print item: AT line,column (control code $16, then the two bytes); POINT x,y when no '('\nor\n'#' follows POINT (control code $19, then the second number as a byte and the first as a\nword, low\nbyte first); TAB column ($17 and the column's word); otherwise PRINT_EXPR. The numbers are\ntaken\nand printed only when running.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "11787": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "11791": {"comment":"Two numbers (ROM 3's CLASS_8)"},
        "11794": {"comment":"Running only"},
        "11797": {"comment":"ROM 3's TAKE_TWO_BYTES: B, C"},
        "11800": {"comment":"Control code $16"},
        "11804": {"synopsis":"POINT: with '(' or '#' after it, the POINT function in an expression (PRINT_SCAN); otherwise\nPOINT x,y.","comment":"POINT?"},
        "11808": {"comment":"A look past it"},
        "11810": {"comment":"CH_ADD left on POINT"},
        "11814": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "11818": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "11822": {"comment":"Two numbers (ROM 3's CLASS_8)"},
        "11825": {"comment":"Running only"},
        "11828": {"comment":"A = the second, a byte"},
        "11832": {"comment":"BC = the first, a word"},
        "11836": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11837": {"comment":"B = the byte"},
        "11838": {"comment":"Control code $19"},
        "11840": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_CTRL3 from $201F: C, B"},
        "11843": {"comment":"The word"},
        "11844": {"comment":"Low byte, then high"},
        "11848": {"synopsis":"TAB: one number, a word; control code $17.","comment":"TAB?"},
        "11852": {"comment":"A number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "11855": {"comment":"Running only"},
        "11858": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "11861": {"comment":"Control code $17"},
        "11863": {"synopsis":"Prints A, C and B (ROM 3's PRINT_CTRL3).","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_CTRL3"},
        "11867": {"synopsis":"Not AT, POINT x,y or TAB: a colour item (PRINT_COLOUR) or a stream change (STREAM_ALTER)\nends\nthe item; otherwise the expression (PRINT_SCAN).","comment":"A colour item?"},
        "11870": {"comment":"Not one: a stream change?"},
        "11873": {"comment":"Either: done"},
        "11874": {"synopsis":"The expression (ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR, through $0DFC); when running a number is printed by ROM\n3's\nPRINT_FP, a string by PRINT_STR.","comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR"},
        "11877": {"comment":"Running only"},
        "11880": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "11886": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_FP"},
        "11890": {"synopsis":"A string: DE = its start, BC = its length (taken off the calculator stack by $3842). On\nchannel S\nor K with a nonzero low nibble n in $5C7F (IX = $F200 + $100 x n), or on channel W (IX =\nCURCHL),\nROM 0's $2788 prints it, each character by its $275B; otherwise ROM 3's PRINT_STRING.","comment":"DE, BC = the string"},
        "11893": {"comment":"IX = CURCHL"},
        "11897": {"comment":"The channel's letter"},
        "11900": {"comment":"'S'?"},
        "11904": {"synopsis":"Channel S or K: by the low nibble of $5C7F.","comment":"$5C7F's low nibble"},
        "11909": {"comment":"0: ROM 3 prints it"},
        "11911": {"comment":"IXh = $F2 + it"},
        "11915": {"comment":"IXl = 0"},
        "11918": {"synopsis":"ROM 0's $2788 prints the BC characters at DE.","comment":"ROM 0's $2788"},
        "11924": {"synopsis":"Channel K as S; channel W always through ROM 0.","comment":"'K'?"},
        "11928": {"comment":"'W'?"},
        "11932": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's PRINT_STRING.","comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_STRING"},
        "11936": {"synopsis":"STREAM_ALTER for the character at CH_ADD.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "11939": {"synopsis":"'#' and a number, as ROM 3's STREAM_ALTER: when running that stream becomes current (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT; 16 or more is report O, error code $17).\nExit: carry when there is no '#'.","comment":"'#'?"},
        "11941": {"comment":"No: carry"},
        "11943": {"comment":"A number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "11946": {"comment":"NC"},
        "11947": {"comment":"Running only"},
        "11950": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "11953": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "11957": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "11960": {"comment":"NC: done"},
        "11962": {"synopsis":"Error code $17 (report O)."},
        "11964": {"synopsis":"STREAM_OPT with stream 2. No caller was found in the four pages.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "11966": {"synopsis":"Stream A becomes current when running ($1353); then an optional '#n' (STREAM_ALTER), and a\n';'\nor ',' after it is stepped past. Called from $35CC and $35DD.\nExit: carry when there was no '#'.","comment":"Selected when running"},
        "11969": {"comment":"'#n'?"},
        "11972": {"comment":"None: carry"},
        "11973": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "11976": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "11980": {"comment":"','?"},
        "11983": {"synopsis":"Past the separator.","comment":"Past it"},
        "11985": {"synopsis":"LPRINT (class $0E; its word at $0362 in the syntax table): PRINT_START with stream 3.","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "11989": {"synopsis":"PRINT (class $0E; its word at $033B in the syntax table): PRINT_START with stream 2.","comment":"Stream 2"},
        "11991": {"synopsis":"When running stream A becomes current ($1353); then the print list (PRINT_LIST) and the\nstatement's end ($0914).","comment":"Stream A, when running"},
        "11994": {"comment":"The items"},
        "11997": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12001": {"synopsis":"Prints a list of items and separators (PRINT, and INPUT's bracketed prompt), as ROM 3's\nPRINT_LIST: separators by PRINT_SEP, items by PRINT_ITEM; at the end ENTER, unless the list\nends at\n')'.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "12004": {"comment":"Already the end?"},
        "12009": {"synopsis":"Separators, as many as there are; then an item.","comment":"A separator?"},
        "12014": {"comment":"An item"},
        "12017": {"comment":"Then separators"},
        "12022": {"synopsis":"The end: at ')' nothing more; otherwise ENTER.","comment":"')'?"},
        "12025": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_NEWLINE"},
        "12029": {"synopsis":"INPUT (class $0E; its word at $033E in the syntax table): stream 1 when running ($1353), and\nROM 0's $0EC9 clears the lower screen; then the items (INPUT_ITEMS).","comment":"Stream 1"},
        "12031": {"comment":"Selected when running"},
        "12034": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "12039": {"comment":"ROM 0: clear the lower screen"},
        "12044": {"synopsis":"The items (INPUT_ITEM) and the statement's end; then, when the low nibble of $5C7F is 0, ROM\n3's\nINPUT code from $20A0 (the upper screen's print position, then the lower screen cleared).","comment":"The items"},
        "12047": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12050": {"comment":"$5C7F's low nibble"},
        "12055": {"comment":"Nonzero: done"},
        "12056": {"comment":"ROM 3's INPUT code at $20A0"},
        "12060": {"synopsis":"One INPUT item after any separators, as ROM 3's INPUT_ITEM: '(' a bracketed prompt list\n(PRINT_LIST, ')' required); LINE and a string variable; '%' or a letter a variable; anything\nelse a\nprompt item (PRINT_ITEM). After a separator the next item.","comment":"Separators first"},
        "12065": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "12069": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12070": {"comment":"The prompt list"},
        "12073": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "12076": {"comment":"')' must follow"},
        "12080": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12083": {"synopsis":"LINE: a variable (ROM 3's CLASS_1) that must be a string; FLAGX bit 7 set.","comment":"LINE?"},
        "12087": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12088": {"comment":"The variable (ROM 3's CLASS_1)"},
        "12091": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 7: LINE"},
        "12095": {"comment":"A number variable?"},
        "12099": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "12101": {"comment":"Yes: report C"},
        "12103": {"synopsis":"'%' or a letter: a variable; otherwise a prompt item.","comment":"'%'?"},
        "12107": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "12110": {"comment":"No: a prompt item"},
        "12112": {"synopsis":"A variable (ROM 3's CLASS_1), FLAGX bit 7 cleared.","comment":"The variable"},
        "12115": {"comment":"Not LINE"},
        "12119": {"synopsis":"Running: the answer (INPUT_VAR).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "12122": {"comment":"Running: the answer"},
        "12127": {"synopsis":"A prompt item (PRINT_ITEM).","comment":"A prompt item"},
        "12130": {"synopsis":"After a separator the next item; otherwise the items are done.","comment":"A separator?"},
        "12133": {"comment":"Yes: the next item"},
        "12136": {"synopsis":"Past a ',' or ';'; then the next colour item.","comment":"Past it"},
        "12137": {"synopsis":"The colour items a graphics statement may start with, as ROM 3's COL_ITEMS: each by\nPRINT_COLOUR, separated by ',' or ';'; anything else after an item is report C. Called from\n$05CB.\nExit: carry at the first character that is not a colour item.","comment":"A colour item?"},
        "12140": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "12141": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "12144": {"comment":"','?"},
        "12148": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "12152": {"synopsis":"Error code $0B (report C)."},
        "12154": {"synopsis":"A colour item, INK to OVER ($D9-$DE), as ROM 3's PRINT_COLOUR: past the keyword, then\nCOL_TEMP_ITEM.\nExit: carry when it is not one.","comment":"Below INK?"},
        "12157": {"comment":"Above OVER?"},
        "12161": {"comment":"The token kept"},
        "12162": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12164": {"synopsis":"One temporary colour item: A - $C9 is its control code ($10 INK ... $15 OVER); the number\nafter\nit (ROM 3's CLASS_6), then ROM 3's COL_TEMP_ITEM from $2203. Called from $0616 too.","comment":"The control code"},
        "12167": {"comment":"The number (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "12171": {"comment":"ROM 3's COL_TEMP_ITEM at $2203"},
        "12175": {"synopsis":"Running: the answer for the variable just found. ROM 3's CLEAR_WS; FLAGX bit 6 = FLAGS bit 6\n(a\nnumber wanted). On channel K the line is edited by ROM 0's $27D9 (INPUT_EDIT_K), on channel\nW too\n(INPUT_EDIT_W); on another channel characters are read into the workspace (ROM 3's\nWAIT_KEY_LOOP,\neach given a byte by ROM 3's WORK_ROOM) up to ENTER. Then INPUT_ANSWER.","comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS"},
        "12178": {"comment":"A = FLAGS"},
        "12181": {"comment":"HL = FLAGX"},
        "12184": {"comment":"Bit 6 = FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "12190": {"comment":"IX = CURCHL"},
        "12194": {"comment":"ROM 3's IN_CHAN_K: channel K?"},
        "12199": {"comment":"'W'?"},
        "12203": {"synopsis":"Another channel: one more byte in the workspace, the next character from the channel into\nit,\nuntil ENTER.","comment":"Room for one byte"},
        "12206": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM"},
        "12209": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3 cleared"},
        "12213": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 5 cleared"},
        "12217": {"comment":"ROM 3's WAIT_KEY_LOOP: a character"},
        "12220": {"comment":"Into the workspace"},
        "12221": {"comment":"Until ENTER"},
        "12225": {"synopsis":"Assigns the answer in the workspace (WORKSP to STKBOT - 1, its ENTER left out): INPUT LINE\n(FLAGX bit 7) the text as a string; otherwise the text is evaluated by ROM 3's CALC_VAL, as\nval ($1D)\nfor a number and val$ ($18) for a string. An empty answer is 0 or the empty string. The\nvalue is\nassigned through $3DD2 (ROM 3's LET_ASSIGN, after a type check) with A = FLAGX. Also called\nat $305C.","comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "12228": {"comment":"DE = WORKSP"},
        "12232": {"comment":"BC = the length, no ENTER"},
        "12237": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "12241": {"comment":"The text stacked as a string"},
        "12244": {"comment":"LINE?"},
        "12250": {"comment":"val for a number"},
        "12252": {"comment":"A number wanted?"},
        "12258": {"comment":"val$ for a string"},
        "12260": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's CALC_VAL with B = $1D (val) or $18 (val$).","comment":"ROM 3's CALC_VAL"},
        "12263": {"synopsis":"Assigns the value through $3DD2 with A = FLAGX.","comment":"A = FLAGX"},
        "12266": {"comment":"Assign (ROM 3's LET_ASSIGN)"},
        "12269": {"synopsis":"An empty answer: the empty string, or 0 for a number.","comment":"A number wanted?"},
        "12275": {"comment":"The empty string"},
        "12280": {"synopsis":"0 for a number.","comment":"Stack 0"},
        "12285": {"synopsis":"Channel K: B = $E0, C = $BF for INPUT_EDIT.","comment":"B = $E0, C = $BF"},
        "12290": {"synopsis":"Channel W: C = (IX + $12) x (IX + $1C), at most $C0, and B = $60 for INPUT_EDIT; IX =\nCURCHL.","comment":"C = $C0, the limit"},
        "12292": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "12293": {"comment":"(IX + $12) times"},
        "12296": {"synopsis":"Adds (IX + $1C) once more.","comment":"+ (IX + $1C)"},
        "12299": {"comment":"Past 255: the limit"},
        "12301": {"comment":"$C0 or more: the limit"},
        "12306": {"comment":"C = the product"},
        "12307": {"synopsis":"B = $60.","comment":"B = $60"},
        "12309": {"synopsis":"E = 0: no text yet.","comment":"E = 0"},
        "12311": {"synopsis":"Edits the answer with ROM 0's $27D9 (A = 0, B, C, D, E, HL = $E152), makes E + 1 bytes of\nroom\nat the workspace's end (ROM 3's WORK_ROOM), copies the text there with ROM 0's $1947 (on the\nstack at\n$5B6A) and puts an ENTER after it. INPUT_ANSWER then runs with an error trap: CH_ADD, ERR_SP\nand the\nword at $5B6C are saved, $5B6C = INPUT_RETRY, $5B3A is pushed as the error return;\nafterwards all\nthree come back.\nExit: DE as ROM 0's $27D9 left it, BC as at entry.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "12312": {"comment":"HL = $E152"},
        "12315": {"comment":"B, C kept for a retry"},
        "12316": {"comment":"ROM 0's $27D9: the edit"},
        "12321": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "12322": {"comment":"BC = E + 1"},
        "12326": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12327": {"comment":"ROM 3's WORK_ROOM"},
        "12330": {"comment":"BC = E + 1"},
        "12331": {"comment":"$5B8A = $100B"},
        "12337": {"comment":"HL = $E152"},
        "12340": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "12343": {"comment":"ROM 0's $1947: the text copied"},
        "12348": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "12351": {"comment":"HL = the text's end"},
        "12352": {"comment":"ENTER"},
        "12354": {"comment":"CH_ADD saved"},
        "12358": {"comment":"ERR_SP saved"},
        "12362": {"comment":"The word at $5B6C saved"},
        "12366": {"comment":"$5B6C = INPUT_RETRY"},
        "12372": {"comment":"$5B3A: the error return"},
        "12376": {"comment":"ERR_SP = here"},
        "12380": {"comment":"Assign the answer"},
        "12383": {"comment":"The error return dropped"},
        "12384": {"comment":"$5B6C back"},
        "12388": {"comment":"ERR_SP back"},
        "12392": {"comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "12396": {"comment":"DE, BC back"},
        "12399": {"synopsis":"Where an error in the answer comes back (through the word at $5B6C): ROM 0's $3E18, ROM 3's\nCLEAR_WS, $5B6C, ERR_SP and CH_ADD put back, ERR_NR = $FF; then INPUT_EDIT again with D = E\n(the text\nkept) and B = $74.","comment":"ROM 0's $3E18"},
        "12404": {"comment":"ROM 3's CLEAR_WS"},
        "12407": {"comment":"$5B6C back"},
        "12411": {"comment":"ERR_SP back"},
        "12415": {"comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "12419": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "12423": {"comment":"D = E"},
        "12425": {"comment":"C back"},
        "12426": {"comment":"B = $74"},
        "12428": {"comment":"Edit again"},
        "12430": {"synopsis":"A command running with a number on the calculator stack (its word at $04AE in the syntax\ntable,\nafter class $0C):\n1. The number must be 1346 ($0542); otherwise error code 9.\n2. A = L = $80 when bit 4 of $5B5E is set, else 0; DE = 0; ROM 2's DOS_SET_1346 (re-allocate\n   the\nmemory use of banks 1, 3, 4 and 6; NextZXOS API document) runs on the stack at $5B6A with\nbank 7 at\n$C000 (RST $18, then RST $30); no carry ends at $0DCA (the error reported).\n3. Bit 7 of $5B68 = NOT bit 4 of $5B5E. That bit lets BANK_CHECK accept banks 1, 3, 4 and 6.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "12433": {"comment":"Must be 1346"},
        "12439": {"comment":"Otherwise error code 9"},
        "12442": {"comment":"$5B5E bit 4"},
        "12447": {"comment":"$80 when set, else 0"},
        "12450": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "12453": {"comment":"HL = A"},
        "12456": {"comment":"Bank 7, the other stack"},
        "12457": {"comment":"ROM 2's DOS_SET_1346: re-allocate banks 1, 3, 4, 6"},
        "12460": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12461": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "12462": {"comment":"NC: $0DCA"},
        "12465": {"comment":"A = $5B68"},
        "12468": {"comment":"Bit 7 set"},
        "12470": {"comment":"Cleared again when L = $80"},
        "12471": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "12475": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the stack back (RST $30), then report B."},
        "12476": {"synopsis":"Error code $0A (report B). Also jumped to from $15CB, $17A9, $17B0 and $3242."},
        "12478": {"synopsis":"Fills part of a bank (class $0E; its word at $04B4 in the syntax table; the bank's number\nstacked\nbefore it). After it: nothing, a value v, offset,length, or offset,length,v; bits 7 (a\nvalue) and 6\n(offset and length) of $5B66 record which. Running: length bytes (16K by default) from the\noffset\n(0) of the bank, paged at $C000 and checked by BANK_OFFSET, are set to v (0); past the\nbank's end is\nreport B.","comment":"The flags at $5B66"},
        "12481": {"comment":"No value"},
        "12483": {"comment":"No offset, length"},
        "12485": {"comment":"The statement's end?"},
        "12490": {"comment":"One number: a value"},
        "12492": {"comment":"It (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "12495": {"comment":"','?"},
        "12499": {"comment":"Two: offset, length"},
        "12506": {"comment":"The length"},
        "12509": {"comment":"','?"},
        "12513": {"comment":"Three: and a value"},
        "12518": {"comment":"The value"},
        "12521": {"synopsis":"Running: the numbers off the calculator stack, then the fill.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12524": {"comment":"Value 0"},
        "12528": {"comment":"A value?"},
        "12532": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "12535": {"synopsis":"BC = the length, HL = the offset; 16K from 0 by default.","comment":"The value kept"},
        "12539": {"comment":"Offset and length?"},
        "12541": {"comment":"16K"},
        "12544": {"comment":"From offset 0"},
        "12548": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "12552": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "12558": {"synopsis":"The bank, then the fill.","comment":"Kept"},
        "12560": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "12563": {"comment":"BC, HL back"},
        "12565": {"comment":"D = the value"},
        "12566": {"comment":"Bank A at $C000; HL into it"},
        "12569": {"comment":"Past the bank's end?"},
        "12573": {"comment":"Yes: report B"},
        "12575": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "12576": {"comment":"DE = the next"},
        "12579": {"comment":"One byte only?"},
        "12583": {"comment":"The rest"},
        "12585": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the stack back.","comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12587": {"synopsis":"Copies between banks (class $0E; its word at $04B1 in the syntax table; the source bank\nstacked\nbefore it): TO b copies all 16K into bank b; offset,length TO b,offset2 copies length bytes.\nBoth\nranges are checked (BANK_OFFSET; past a bank's end is report B); the source is paged at\n$8000-$BFFF\n(MMU 4, 5), the destination at $C000 (MMU 6, 7); afterwards MMU 4, 5 hold bank 2 again.","comment":"TO at once?"},
        "12591": {"comment":"Two numbers (ROM 3's CLASS_8)"},
        "12594": {"comment":"TO must follow"},
        "12598": {"comment":"Two more"},
        "12601": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12604": {"comment":"BC = the destination's offset"},
        "12608": {"comment":"A = the destination bank"},
        "12612": {"comment":"The length"},
        "12616": {"comment":"The source's offset"},
        "12620": {"comment":"A = the source bank"},
        "12623": {"comment":"HL = the source's offset"},
        "12624": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "12625": {"comment":"IXh = the destination bank"},
        "12627": {"comment":"DE = the destination's offset"},
        "12630": {"synopsis":"TO b: the whole bank, 16K from offset 0 to offset 0.","comment":"The bank (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "12633": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12636": {"comment":"The destination bank"},
        "12640": {"comment":"A = the source bank"},
        "12643": {"comment":"IXh = the destination"},
        "12645": {"comment":"Offsets 0"},
        "12650": {"comment":"16K"},
        "12653": {"synopsis":"Checks both ranges, then the copy.","comment":"IXl = the source bank"},
        "12655": {"comment":"Source checked; HL into $C000"},
        "12658": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12659": {"comment":"HL = the destination's offset"},
        "12660": {"comment":"A = the destination bank"},
        "12662": {"comment":"Checked; paged at $C000"},
        "12665": {"comment":"Destination past its end?"},
        "12669": {"comment":"Report B"},
        "12672": {"comment":"HL = the source: past its end?"},
        "12676": {"comment":"Report B"},
        "12679": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "12680": {"comment":"A = the source bank"},
        "12682": {"comment":"At $8000-$BFFF"},
        "12685": {"comment":"HL into $8000-$BFFF"},
        "12687": {"comment":"Copy"},
        "12689": {"synopsis":"MMU 4, 5 back to bank 2; bank 0 at $C000 and the stack back (RST $30).","comment":"Bank 2"},
        "12691": {"comment":"At $8000-$BFFF again"},
        "12694": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12696": {"synopsis":"Moves a block of character cells between a bank and the screen through ROM 0's $20C4 (class\n3\nthen this routine; its word at $04B7 in the syntax table; the bank and a first number\nstacked\nbefore it). Two forms:\n1. offset TO[op] a,b,c,d: bit 7 of $5C92 clear.\n2. a,b,c,d TO[op] offset: bit 7 of $5C92 set (the four numbers are the first number and\n   three after\na ',').\nop is BLOCK_TO_OP's operator (0-4), stored in $5C92 bits 0-2. BLOCK_SIZE checks a,b,c,d (c\nand d the\nsize). Running: the bank is checked and paged at both $8000 and $C000 (BANK_OFFSET,\nMAP_BANK_8000),\n$5B9B = $8000 + the offset, $5C93 = the global transparency colour (NextReg $14); then ROM\n0's $20C4\nwith IX = $5C92 and HL = $218A, and MMU45_BANK2.","comment":"',' first?"},
        "12700": {"comment":"TO and its operator"},
        "12703": {"comment":"B = the operator"},
        "12704": {"comment":"Two numbers (ROM 3's CLASS_8)"},
        "12707": {"comment":"',' must follow"},
        "12709": {"synopsis":"NZ: report C ($09AF).","comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "12712": {"comment":"Two more"},
        "12715": {"comment":"A = the operator"},
        "12716": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12719": {"comment":"$5C92 = the operator"},
        "12722": {"comment":"The four numbers"},
        "12725": {"comment":"BC = the offset"},
        "12730": {"synopsis":"',': a,b,c,d TO[op] offset; bit 7 of $5C92 set.","comment":"Past ','; a number"},
        "12733": {"comment":"',' must follow"},
        "12737": {"comment":"Two more"},
        "12740": {"comment":"TO and its operator"},
        "12743": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "12744": {"comment":"The offset (ROM 3's CLASS_6)"},
        "12747": {"comment":"A = the operator"},
        "12748": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "12751": {"comment":"Bit 7: this form"},
        "12753": {"comment":"Into $5C92"},
        "12756": {"comment":"BC = the offset"},
        "12760": {"comment":"The four numbers"},
        "12764": {"synopsis":"The bank paged at $C000 and $8000, then ROM 0's $20C4 with IX = $5C92.","comment":"Offset kept"},
        "12765": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "12768": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "12769": {"comment":"Checked, paged at $C000"},
        "12772": {"comment":"A = the bank again"},
        "12774": {"comment":"At $8000-$BFFF too"},
        "12777": {"comment":"HL into $8000-$BFFF"},
        "12779": {"comment":"$5B9B = the address"},
        "12782": {"comment":"NextReg $14"},
        "12784": {"comment":"Read: the transparency colour"},
        "12787": {"comment":"$5C93 = it"},
        "12790": {"comment":"IX = the block at $5C92"},
        "12794": {"comment":"HL = $218A"},
        "12797": {"comment":"ROM 0's $20C4"},
        "12802": {"comment":"Bank 2 back; bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12805": {"synopsis":"Takes four numbers a,b,c,d off the calculator stack (ROM 3's TAKE_TWO_BYTES twice): c to\n$5CA3,\nd to $5CA4 (both not 0), a to $5CA5, b to $5CA6. a + c must not pass 32 and b + d not 24 (16\nand 12\nwhen the low nibble of $5C7F is 1); otherwise report B.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"ROM 3's TAKE_TWO_BYTES: c, d"},
        "12808": {"comment":"To $5CA3, $5CA4"},
        "12812": {"comment":"d 0?"},
        "12816": {"comment":"c 0?"},
        "12820": {"comment":"a, b"},
        "12823": {"comment":"To $5CA5, $5CA6"},
        "12827": {"comment":"E = $5C7F's low nibble"},
        "12833": {"comment":"c + a"},
        "12837": {"comment":"Past 255?"},
        "12839": {"comment":"Past 32?"},
        "12843": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "12846": {"comment":"Then past 16?"},
        "12850": {"synopsis":"The other pair: d + b.","comment":"E back"},
        "12851": {"comment":"d + b"},
        "12855": {"comment":"Past 255?"},
        "12857": {"comment":"Past 24?"},
        "12861": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "12862": {"comment":"No: it fits"},
        "12863": {"comment":"Then past 12?"},
        "12866": {"synopsis":"Report B.","comment":"Report B"},
        "12869": {"synopsis":"TO ($CC; otherwise report C through $09AF) and an optional operator after it: B = 1 for '&',\n2\n'|', 3 '^', 4 '~' (stepped past), 0 for none.\nExit: B = the operator, A = the character after.","comment":"TO?"},
        "12871": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "12874": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "12875": {"comment":"'&': 1"},
        "12881": {"comment":"'|': 2"},
        "12887": {"comment":"'^': 3"},
        "12893": {"comment":"None: 0"},
        "12895": {"comment":"'~'?"},
        "12897": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "12898": {"comment":"'~': 4"},
        "12900": {"synopsis":"Past the operator.","comment":"Past it"},
        "12902": {"synopsis":"Takes a free bank for BASIC and assigns its number to a variable (its word at $0497 in the\nsyntax\ntable, after classes 1 and $0C): on the stack at $5B6A with bank 7 at $C000 (RST $18), banks\nfrom the\none in $5B69 down to 9 are looked up by BANK_CHECK; the first that is neither BASIC's nor in\nuse is\nmarked in both maps, stacked ($3867) and assigned ($3DCF). None free: error code 3 (report\n4).","comment":"Bank 7, the other stack"},
        "12903": {"comment":"From the highest bank"},
        "12906": {"synopsis":"One bank: free?","comment":"Its bits; Z: BASIC's already"},
        "12911": {"comment":"In use?"},
        "12915": {"comment":"Marked in use"},
        "12918": {"comment":"And BASIC's"},
        "12921": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12922": {"comment":"BC = the bank"},
        "12924": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "12927": {"comment":"Assigned to the variable"},
        "12930": {"synopsis":"The next bank down, while above 8.","comment":"The next lower"},
        "12931": {"comment":"Still above 8?"},
        "12937": {"comment":"None: error code 3"},
        "12939": {"synopsis":"Gives a bank back (its number stacked; its word at $04BA in the syntax table, after class\n$0C):\nit must be 9 or more (else error code 9) and none of the three 16K banks of Layer 2 starting\nat\nNextReg $12 or at $13 (its shadow; nextreg.txt), else error code $3C. Then, when the bank is\nBASIC's\n(BANK_CHECK's Z), its bits are cleared in both maps.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "12942": {"comment":"Below 9: error code 9"},
        "12947": {"comment":"The NextReg select port"},
        "12950": {"comment":"NextReg $12"},
        "12954": {"comment":"E = Layer 2's first bank"},
        "12957": {"comment":"NextReg $13"},
        "12961": {"comment":"D = the shadow's first bank"},
        "12964": {"comment":"Three banks each"},
        "12966": {"synopsis":"Is the bank one of Layer 2's (or its shadow's) three?","comment":"The shadow's?"},
        "12970": {"comment":"Layer 2's?"},
        "12973": {"comment":"The next of each"},
        "12977": {"comment":"Bank 7, the other stack"},
        "12978": {"comment":"Its bits; BASIC's?"},
        "12983": {"comment":"The mask inverted"},
        "12986": {"comment":"Cleared in the $C028 map"},
        "12988": {"comment":"And in the $C000 map"},
        "12991": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the stack back.","comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "12993": {"synopsis":"Error code $3C: the bank belongs to Layer 2."},
        "12995": {"synopsis":"Pages bank A at $C000 for offset HL: HL must be below $4000 (otherwise report B), HL +\n$C000,\nthen BANK_MAP. Called by the bank commands and $34FD.\nExit: as BANK_MAP; HL = $C000 + the offset.","comment":"The bank aside"},
        "12996": {"comment":"Offset below $4000?"},
        "13001": {"synopsis":"Error code $0A (report B): the offset is 16K or more."},
        "13003": {"synopsis":"HL into $C000-$FFFF; then BANK_MAP.","comment":"The bank back"},
        "13004": {"synopsis":"HL into $C000-$FFFF (bits 7, 6 set), then BANK_MAP. Entered here from $3943.","comment":"HL + $C000"},
        "13008": {"synopsis":"Moves onto the stack at $5B6A and pages bank A at $C000-$FFFF (MMU 6, 7). The bank is looked\nup\nby BANK_CHECK: one already BASIC's is just paged; one in use elsewhere is error code 3\n(report 4);\na free one is marked in both maps first. Called from $0ED1, $17C4, $1BF4, $1C5C, $24D3,\n$26B9, $3915,\n$3981 and $3BD6; entered at $32CC from $3943.\nEntry: A = the bank.\nExit: on the other stack (RST $30 goes back); A = the bank's upper page (2 x bank + 1); BC,\nDE,\nHL kept.\nChanges: AF, AF', BC', DE', HL', $5B52, $5B6A.","comment":"HL to the stack, the return address out"},
        "13009": {"comment":"The other register set"},
        "13010": {"comment":"HL = the entry HL"},
        "13011": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13014": {"comment":"Onto the stack at $5B6A"},
        "13022": {"synopsis":"Looks up bank A; a free one is taken.","comment":"Its bits; Z: BASIC's already"},
        "13027": {"comment":"In use?"},
        "13031": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the stack back; error code 3 (report 4).","comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "13032": {"comment":"Error code 3"},
        "13034": {"synopsis":"Marks the bank in both maps.","comment":"In the $C028 map"},
        "13037": {"comment":"And the $C000 map"},
        "13040": {"synopsis":"Pages the bank at $C000 and returns on the new stack.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "13041": {"comment":"The main registers"},
        "13042": {"comment":"The return address onto this stack"},
        "13043": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13046": {"synopsis":"Pages bank A at $C000-$FFFF: MMU 6 = page 2A, MMU 7 = page 2A + 1 (NextRegs $56, $57).\nExit: A = 2A + 1.","comment":"Page 2A"},
        "13050": {"comment":"And 2A + 1"},
        "13055": {"synopsis":"Pages bank A at $8000-$BFFF: MMU 4 = page 2A, MMU 5 = page 2A + 1 (NextRegs $54, $55).\nExit: A = 2A + 1.","comment":"Page 2A"},
        "13059": {"comment":"And 2A + 1"},
        "13064": {"synopsis":"Called from ROM 3 through its CALL_OTHER_BC (BC = $3308; at $38D6 and $3A7A): HL must be\nbelow\n$4000 (otherwise report B); bank A is looked up and taken as by BANK_MAP, on the stack at\n$5B6A;\nthen BANK_PAGE_BACK puts bank 0 at $C000 and the stack back.\nEntry: A = the bank, HL = an offset in it.\nExit: A = the bank's upper 8K page (2 x bank + 1); HL kept.","comment":"The bank aside"},
        "13065": {"comment":"Offset below $4000?"},
        "13070": {"comment":"The bank back"},
        "13071": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "13072": {"comment":"Onto the stack at $5B6A"},
        "13080": {"comment":"Returns into $331E"},
        "13083": {"comment":"The other register set"},
        "13084": {"comment":"Look up, take and page the bank"},
        "13086": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 at $C000 and ROM 1 again, the stack back, HL back.","comment":"Bank 0 at $C000, ROM 1"},
        "13090": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "13098": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13100": {"synopsis":"Looks bank A up in the bank maps, which it reads with RAM bank 8 paged at $C000 (MMU 6, 7):\nthe\nmaps at $C000 and $C028 there hold 2 bits for each bank (byte bank / 4; the pair for bank\nAND 3 from\nbit 0 up). The $C000 map marks banks in use, the $C028 map (probably) the ones BASIC holds.\nBanks 7\nand 8 are error code 9 (report A), banks 1, 3, 4 and 6 too unless bit 7 of $5B68 is set;\nbanks above\nthe one in $5B69 are error code 3 (report 4). Errors go back to bank 0 and the main stack\nfirst (RST\n$30).\nEntry: A = the bank; on the stack at $5B6A.\nExit: C = the bank, B = its 2-bit mask, DE = its byte in the $C000 map, HL its byte in the\n$C028\nmap; Z when both its bits are set in the $C028 map.\nChanges: AF, AF'.","comment":"L = $5B68, H = $5B69"},
        "13103": {"comment":"Bank 8?"},
        "13107": {"comment":"Above 8"},
        "13109": {"comment":"Bank 7?"},
        "13113": {"comment":"Banks 1, 3, 4 and 6:"},
        "13129": {"synopsis":"Banks 1, 3, 4 and 6 only while bit 7 of $5B68 is set.","comment":"Allowed by $5B68 bit 7?"},
        "13133": {"synopsis":"Bank 0 and the stack back; error code 9.","comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "13134": {"synopsis":"Error code 9 (report A). Also jumped to from $00DD, $3097 and $3290."},
        "13136": {"synopsis":"Above 8: no higher than the bank in $5B69.","comment":"H = the highest + 1"},
        "13137": {"comment":"Above it?"},
        "13138": {"comment":"Error code 3"},
        "13140": {"synopsis":"Reads the maps in bank 8.","comment":"The bank aside"},
        "13141": {"comment":"Bank 8 at $C000"},
        "13146": {"comment":"The bank back"},
        "13147": {"comment":"C = the bank"},
        "13148": {"comment":"Bank / 4"},
        "13152": {"comment":"D = $C0"},
        "13154": {"comment":"DE = $C000 + bank / 4"},
        "13155": {"comment":"H = $C0"},
        "13156": {"comment":"HL = $C028 + bank / 4"},
        "13159": {"comment":"Bank AND 3, + 1"},
        "13164": {"comment":"$C0 rotated:"},
        "13166": {"synopsis":"The pair's mask: $C0 rotated left 2 bits, (bank AND 3) + 1 times.","comment":"Two bits on"},
        "13170": {"comment":"B = the mask"},
        "13171": {"comment":"Both set in the $C028 map?"},
        "13174": {"synopsis":"Writes a list of values into a bank, numbers as words (bit 5 of $5B68 set; class $0E, its\nword\nat $04AB in the syntax table, after class 6 and ','): as BANK_POKE_BYTES.","comment":"HL = $5B68"},
        "13177": {"comment":"Words"},
        "13181": {"synopsis":"Writes a list of values into a bank, numbers as bytes (bit 5 of $5B68 clear; class $0E, its\nword\nat $04A6 in the syntax table, after class 6 and ','): the bank and the offset are on the\ncalculator\nstack; the offset is checked by BANK_OFFSET (16K or more is report B), and each value is\nstored by\nPOKE_STORE with the bank paged. The list is POKE_ITEM's.","comment":"HL = $5B68"},
        "13184": {"comment":"Bytes"},
        "13186": {"synopsis":"Checking: the list only (POKE_PLAIN). Running: BC = the offset, A = the bank; the pointer\n$C000 + offset and the bank kept on the stack for POKE_STORE.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "13191": {"comment":"BC = the offset"},
        "13195": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "13198": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "13199": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "13200": {"comment":"Checked; HL into $C000"},
        "13203": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "13204": {"comment":"The pointer kept"},
        "13207": {"synopsis":"Writes a list of values into memory, numbers as words (bit 5 of $5B68 set; class $0E, its\nword at\n$03CF in the syntax table, after class 6 and ','): as POKE_BYTES.","comment":"HL = $5B68"},
        "13210": {"comment":"Words"},
        "13214": {"synopsis":"Writes a list of values into memory, numbers as bytes (bit 5 of $5B68 clear; class $0E, its\nword\nat $03C5 in the syntax table, after class 6 and ','): the address is on the calculator\nstack; the\nlist is POKE_ITEM's.","comment":"HL = $5B68"},
        "13217": {"comment":"Bytes"},
        "13219": {"synopsis":"No bank: A = $FF kept for POKE_STORE; running, the address (a word) is the pointer.","comment":"$FF: no bank"},
        "13221": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13222": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "13225": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "13228": {"comment":"The pointer kept"},
        "13229": {"synopsis":"One item of the list, then ',' and the next:\n1. A number: a byte or, with bit 5 of $5B68 set, a word (low byte first); a '~' after it\n   swaps the\ntwo for this item.\n2. A string: its characters; a '~' after it sets bit 7 of its last one.\nEach byte goes through POKE_STORE when running. At the end the pointer and the bank come off\nthe\nstack and the statement ends ($0914).","comment":"ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR"},
        "13232": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "13238": {"comment":"'~' after it?"},
        "13240": {"comment":"A = $5B68's flags"},
        "13245": {"comment":"Past the '~'"},
        "13248": {"comment":"The other width"},
        "13250": {"synopsis":"A number: stored as a word or a byte by bit 5 of A.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "13255": {"comment":"A word?"},
        "13259": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "13262": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "13265": {"comment":"Then its high byte"},
        "13271": {"synopsis":"A byte.","comment":"A = it"},
        "13274": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "13275": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "13278": {"synopsis":"After ',' the next item; otherwise the pointer and the bank dropped and the statement's end.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "13281": {"comment":"','?"},
        "13285": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "13288": {"synopsis":"The end of the list: the pointer and the bank flag dropped; the statement's end.","comment":"The pointer dropped"},
        "13289": {"comment":"The bank dropped"},
        "13290": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "13294": {"synopsis":"A string: each character stored; a '~' after it sets bit 7 of the last one.","comment":"D = the character after it"},
        "13295": {"comment":"'~'?"},
        "13297": {"comment":"Then past it"},
        "13300": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "13305": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13306": {"comment":"DE, BC = the string"},
        "13309": {"comment":"H = the character after it"},
        "13310": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "13314": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "13316": {"comment":"The other set: C = it"},
        "13318": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "13321": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "13322": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "13327": {"comment":"'~' after the string?"},
        "13332": {"comment":"Back to the last character"},
        "13334": {"comment":"Bit 7 set"},
        "13336": {"comment":"The pointer back one"},
        "13339": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "13340": {"comment":"Stored again"},
        "13345": {"synopsis":"Stores C at the pointer kept on the stack under the return address (the bank flag under it):\nwith A = $FF in memory as it is; otherwise with bank A paged at $C000, on the stack at $5B6A\n(SWAP_SP, MAP_BANK_C000; RST $30 after). The pointer moves on. Called by POKE_ITEM.\nChanges: AF, HL, IX.","comment":"IX = the return address"},
        "13347": {"comment":"HL = the pointer"},
        "13348": {"comment":"A = the bank, $FF none"},
        "13349": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13350": {"comment":"No bank?"},
        "13353": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "13354": {"synopsis":"The pointer moved on and kept; back to the caller.","comment":"Pointer + 1"},
        "13355": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13356": {"comment":"Back"},
        "13358": {"synopsis":"Into bank A at $C000, on the other stack.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "13359": {"comment":"The other stack"},
        "13362": {"comment":"Bank A at $C000"},
        "13365": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "13366": {"comment":"Bank 0, the stack back"},
        "13369": {"synopsis":"NEW (class $0C, its word at $0344 in the syntax table), and every RST $10 function (both\nwords of RST10_TABLE, and the codes past the table from $0E86):\n1. Interrupts off; the CPU at 28 MHz (NextReg 7 = 3).\n2. ROM 0's $01FB (the restart set-up) with B = 1, then the DivMMC memory's $2A06.\n3. DATADD = PROG - 1 (DATA_POINT_SET); the high byte of T_ADDR = 0; the routine at $25EF\n   with A = $FF and B = 1.\n4. The return address becomes $0931 (the statement loop) and CLEAR_RAMTOP clears with RAMTOP\n   as it is.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "13370": {"comment":"28 MHz"},
        "13374": {"comment":"B = 1 for ROM 0"},
        "13376": {"comment":"ROM 0's $01FB: the restart set-up"},
        "13381": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2A06"},
        "13386": {"comment":"C = $FF"},
        "13388": {"comment":"HL = PROG - 1"},
        "13392": {"comment":"DATADD = it"},
        "13395": {"comment":"T_ADDR's high byte = 0"},
        "13399": {"comment":"A = $FF, B = 1"},
        "13402": {"comment":"The routine at $25EF"},
        "13405": {"comment":"Back to the statement loop at $0931"},
        "13409": {"comment":"CLEAR with RAMTOP as it is"},
        "13411": {"synopsis":"CLEAR (class $0D, its word at $0350): BC = n (TAKE_WORD); n = 0 (or no number) keeps RAMTOP\n(CLEAR_RAMTOP). Then CLEAR_CHECK and CLEAR_NEW_STACK.","comment":"BC = n"},
        "13414": {"comment":"0?"},
        "13418": {"synopsis":"BC = RAMTOP: the new RAMTOP is the old one.","comment":"BC = RAMTOP"},
        "13422": {"synopsis":"CLEAR_CHECK with the new RAMTOP in BC, then CLEAR_NEW_STACK.","comment":"Variables, screen, limits"},
        "13425": {"synopsis":"The machine stack starts again under RAMTOP: the return address and the word below it (the\nerror address) taken off; SP = RAMTOP; the GO SUB stack's end marker ($3E in the high byte);\n$5C0B = SP; the error address pushed and ERR_SP pointed at it; then the return. Also called\nfrom page 0 (RST $18 with $3471 at $025B).","comment":"DE = the return address"},
        "13426": {"comment":"HL = the error address"},
        "13427": {"comment":"SP = RAMTOP"},
        "13431": {"comment":"The GO SUB stack's end marker"},
        "13434": {"comment":"$5C0B = SP"},
        "13438": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "13439": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "13443": {"comment":"The return address"},
        "13444": {"comment":"Back"},
        "13445": {"synopsis":"The new RAMTOP (BC) kept; the variables removed (ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL from VARS to E_LINE -\n1); the DivMMC memory's $2A0D; the screen cleared (CLS_ALL). The new RAMTOP must be above\nSTKEND + 50 and not above P_RAMT, else report M (REPORT_M); RAMTOP = it.\nEntry: BC = the new RAMTOP.","comment":"The new RAMTOP kept"},
        "13446": {"comment":"From VARS"},
        "13450": {"comment":"To E_LINE - 1"},
        "13454": {"comment":"ROM 3's RECLAIM_DE_HL: the variables removed"},
        "13457": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2A0D"},
        "13462": {"comment":"The screen cleared"},
        "13465": {"comment":"STKEND + 50"},
        "13472": {"comment":"DE = the new RAMTOP"},
        "13473": {"comment":"Not above it?"},
        "13477": {"comment":"P_RAMT"},
        "13480": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "13481": {"comment":"Not above it?"},
        "13485": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $15 (report M, \"RAMTOP no good\").","comment":"Error code $15 (report M)"},
        "13487": {"synopsis":"RAMTOP = DE.","comment":"RAMTOP = it"},
        "13492": {"synopsis":"READ (class $0E, its word at $0359):\n1. Checking: the list through the routine at $2568 with D = 0, then the statement's end.\n2. Running, for each variable: the variable (ROM 3's CLASS_1, through $05A3), the next DATA\n   item (READ_ITEM); found, it must be of the variable's type and is assigned (ROM 3's\n   $1C5E, the tail of VAL_FETCH_A); ',' goes on with the next variable.\n3. No item (READ_NO_ITEM): report Q when FLAGS2 bit 7 is set, else report E. An error inside\n   the item: report C (code $0B) becomes report Q; any other error is raised again (through\n   $0DA5).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "13497": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "13499": {"comment":"The list ($2568)"},
        "13502": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "13505": {"synopsis":"Past the ','.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "13506": {"synopsis":"One variable.","comment":"The variable (ROM 3's CLASS_1)"},
        "13509": {"comment":"Its FLAGS kept"},
        "13513": {"comment":"The next DATA item"},
        "13516": {"comment":"B = the variable's FLAGS"},
        "13517": {"comment":"None read?"},
        "13519": {"comment":"A = its FLAGS"},
        "13520": {"comment":"ROM 3's $1C5E: the types compared, assigned"},
        "13523": {"comment":"The character after the variable"},
        "13526": {"comment":"A ','? Another"},
        "13531": {"synopsis":"No item read: NZ, none left; Z, an error in it.","comment":"NZ: no item left"},
        "13533": {"comment":"ERR_NR: the error in the item"},
        "13536": {"comment":"Not report C? Raised again"},
        "13541": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $19 (report Q).","comment":"Error code $19 (report Q)"},
        "13543": {"synopsis":"FLAGS2 bit 7 set: report Q; otherwise error code $0D (report E, \"Out of DATA\").","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 7 set?"},
        "13549": {"comment":"Error code $0D (report E)"},
        "13551": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the next DATA item for READ.\n1. X_PTR = CH_ADD (the READ statement); HL = DATADD, its bank at $5B78 ($FF: main memory; a\n   bank is paged at $C000 through $32C3).\n2. At ',' or '(' the item follows; at ')' there is none (READ_NONE). Otherwise the next DATA\n   statement is looked for (the routine at $2029 with E = DATA's token $E4, the program's\n   bank $5B77 made $FF and NXTLIN kept around it); none is READ_NONE; DATADD = its place\n   (offset form).\n3. In a bank the statement is copied to $5CB6 first (STMT_COPY), bank 0 back.\n4. CH_ADD = the item; $5C0B kept (with FLAGS2 bit 7 set it is moved by GOSUB_FIND with C =\n   $22); an error trap set: $5B6C = READ_ERR_TRAP, ERR_SP at $5B3A (which goes on at $0AB0\n   and JP ($5B6C)); the item evaluated (ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR, through $0DFC).\n5. DATADD = the place after it (a copy's address turned back into the bank's); carry; the\n   trap, $5B6C and $5C0B put back; CH_ADD = X_PTR.\nExit: carry, the value on the calculator stack; NC and Z after an error (READ_ERR_TRAP); NC\nand NZ when there is no item.","comment":"X_PTR = CH_ADD"},
        "13557": {"comment":"HL = DATADD"},
        "13560": {"comment":"Its bank: $FF is main memory"},
        "13565": {"comment":"A bank: paged at $C000"},
        "13568": {"comment":"The character at DATADD"},
        "13569": {"comment":"A ','?"},
        "13573": {"comment":"A '('?"},
        "13577": {"comment":"A ')': no item"},
        "13582": {"synopsis":"Not at an item: the next DATA statement.","comment":"DE = DATADD"},
        "13583": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "13586": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13588": {"comment":"$FF meanwhile"},
        "13590": {"comment":"NXTLIN kept"},
        "13594": {"comment":"HL = DATADD"},
        "13595": {"comment":"E = DATA's token"},
        "13598": {"comment":"The next DATA statement ($2029)"},
        "13601": {"comment":"NXTLIN back"},
        "13606": {"comment":"The bank byte back"},
        "13611": {"comment":"None: no item"},
        "13613": {"comment":"D = the high byte kept"},
        "13614": {"comment":"The offset form"},
        "13618": {"comment":"DATADD = it"},
        "13621": {"comment":"H back"},
        "13622": {"synopsis":"DATADD (HL) is at the item's separator.","comment":"A bank?"},
        "13628": {"comment":"The statement copied to $5CB6"},
        "13631": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "13632": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD at the separator; the item evaluated under an error trap.","comment":"CH_ADD at the item's separator"},
        "13635": {"comment":"$5C0B kept"},
        "13639": {"comment":"Past the separator"},
        "13640": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 7 set?"},
        "13646": {"comment":"Then GOSUB_FIND with C = $22"},
        "13651": {"comment":"$5C0B = what it found"},
        "13654": {"synopsis":"The error trap: $5B6C = READ_ERR_TRAP, ERR_SP at $5B3A.","comment":"$5B6C kept"},
        "13658": {"comment":"The trap's routine"},
        "13664": {"comment":"ERR_SP kept"},
        "13668": {"comment":"ERR_SP's new target: $5B3A"},
        "13672": {"comment":"ERR_SP = it"},
        "13676": {"comment":"The item (ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR)"},
        "13679": {"comment":"A bank?"},
        "13685": {"comment":"HL - $5CB6: the offset in the copy"},
        "13689": {"comment":"+ DATADD"},
        "13694": {"synopsis":"DATADD = the place after the item.","comment":"DATADD = the place after the item"},
        "13697": {"comment":"The $5B3A word dropped"},
        "13698": {"comment":"Carry: an item"},
        "13699": {"synopsis":"ERR_SP, $5B6C, $5C0B and CH_ADD put back.","comment":"ERR_SP back"},
        "13703": {"comment":"$5B6C back"},
        "13707": {"comment":"$5C0B back"},
        "13711": {"comment":"CH_ADD = X_PTR"},
        "13718": {"synopsis":"No DATA left: bank 0 back when a bank was paged ($5B78 not $FF); $5B78 = $FF; DATADD =\nE_LINE - 1.\nExit: NC, NZ.","comment":"The DATA bank byte"},
        "13721": {"comment":"Was it $FF?"},
        "13722": {"comment":"No: bank 0 back (RST $30's routine)"},
        "13725": {"comment":"$5B78 = $FF"},
        "13728": {"comment":"DATADD = E_LINE - 1"},
        "13735": {"comment":"NC, NZ"},
        "13737": {"synopsis":"Where an error in a DATA item lands (through $5B3A, ROM 1's $0AB0 and JP ($5B6C)): A = 0, no\ncarry, then READ_RESTORE.","comment":"A = 0: NC, Z"},
        "13738": {"comment":"The rest put back"},
        "13740": {"synopsis":"DATA (class $0E, its word at $035C): checking, each item is an expression (ROM 3's\nSCAN_EXPR) up to the statement's end; running, CH_ADD moves past the statement (the\nstatement finder at $123E with D = 2, E = 0).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "13743": {"comment":"Running: skipped"},
        "13745": {"synopsis":"One item.","comment":"The item (ROM 3's SCAN_EXPR)"},
        "13748": {"comment":"Not ','? The statement must end"},
        "13753": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "13756": {"synopsis":"Running: CH_ADD past the statement.","comment":"D = 2: the next statement"},
        "13759": {"comment":"Found by the routine at $123E"},
        "13762": {"comment":"CH_ADD = there"},
        "13766": {"synopsis":"As LIST_BANK with stream 3 (the printer). Nothing in this page jumps here and its address is\nin no table found.","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "13770": {"synopsis":"The LIST form whose word is at $04C4 (in the table after $03FE): stream $FE (A), ',' or ';'\nafter a '#' item ($2EBE); the routine at $25C7 with BC = $01FF, which takes the bank number\noff the calculator stack when running; then LIST_GO.","comment":"Stream $FE"},
        "13772": {"synopsis":"The stream in A.","comment":"The stream, '#' and its separator"},
        "13775": {"comment":"BC = $01FF"},
        "13778": {"comment":"The bank from the calculator stack ($25C7)"},
        "13781": {"comment":"On"},
        "13783": {"synopsis":"LLIST (class $0E, its word at $0365): LIST_CMD with stream 3 (the printer).","comment":"Stream 3"},
        "13787": {"synopsis":"LIST (class $0E, its word at $0347):\n1. The stream: A = $FE, or LLIST's 3 (the routine at $2EBE, which takes a '#' item and the\n   ',' or ';' after it).\n2. The routine at $25EC with BC = $01FF and the program's own bank ($5B77); it takes this\n   routine's return address and keeps it at $5B56.\n3. LIST_GO: BC' = PPC; running, the newest GO SUB stack entry is returned from\n   (GOSUB_POP_TOP); an optional '()'; the statement's end; for the main program ($5B65 =\n   $FF) E_PPC = that line; the line found (LINE_FIND); found, the listing is made by the\n   alternate ROM's $19E2.","comment":"Stream $FE"},
        "13789": {"synopsis":"The stream in A.","comment":"The stream, '#' and its separator"},
        "13792": {"comment":"BC = $01FF"},
        "13795": {"comment":"The program's bank ($25EC)"},
        "13798": {"synopsis":"The listing itself (see LIST_CMD, step 3).","comment":"BC' = PPC"},
        "13803": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "13806": {"comment":"Then the newest entry returned from"},
        "13809": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "13812": {"comment":"A '('?"},
        "13816": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "13817": {"comment":"A ')' must follow"},
        "13822": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "13823": {"synopsis":"The statement's end; the line.","comment":"The statement's end"},
        "13826": {"comment":"BC = the line"},
        "13827": {"comment":"The bank: $FF is the main program"},
        "13834": {"comment":"E_PPC = the line"},
        "13838": {"synopsis":"The line found; the alternate ROM lists.","comment":"Found?"},
        "13842": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's $19E2: the listing"},
        "13848": {"synopsis":"CONTINUE (class $0C, its word at $034D): OLDPPC must be a program line (not the edit line,\nelse report N); its bank is $5EBA when the line cache area is made (BANK_AREA_TEST), $FF\notherwise. The line is taken through $267E (PPC = BC, the bank set); SUBPPC = OSPPC and\nCH_ADD = that statement (the finder at $123E with D = OSPPC); past a ':'; then the statement\nloop ($25E7).","comment":"BC = OLDPPC"},
        "13852": {"comment":"The edit line?"},
        "13854": {"comment":"Then report N"},
        "13857": {"comment":"The cache area made?"},
        "13860": {"comment":"No: $FF, the main program"},
        "13864": {"comment":"Yes: the bank at $5EBA"},
        "13867": {"synopsis":"A = the bank.","comment":"The line ($267E)"},
        "13870": {"comment":"OSPPC"},
        "13873": {"comment":"SUBPPC = it"},
        "13876": {"comment":"D = the statement"},
        "13879": {"comment":"Found ($123E)"},
        "13882": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "13885": {"comment":"A ':'? Past it"},
        "13890": {"comment":"The statement loop"},
        "13893": {"synopsis":"The RESTORE form whose word is at $04BD (in the table after $03FE): the routine at $25C6\nwith B = 1, which takes the bank number off the calculator stack when running; then\nRESTORE_GO.","comment":"B = 1"},
        "13895": {"comment":"The bank from the calculator stack"},
        "13898": {"comment":"On"},
        "13900": {"synopsis":"RESTORE (class $0E, its word at $035F):\n1. The routine at $25EB with B = 1 and the program's bank (it finds the line, CH_ADD at it,\n   inside a GO SUB stack entry of type $21; carry when a line was found).\n2. HL = CH_ADD, 5 less with carry (the byte before the line); in a bank, turned from the\n   cache ($5DB6) into a bank offset (+ ($5EBB), bits 7 and 6 cleared). Kept at $5B9D.\n3. The entry of type $21 returned from (GOSUB_RETURN_C).\n4. DATA_POINT_SET with HL = it.","comment":"B = 1"},
        "13902": {"comment":"The line ($25EB)"},
        "13905": {"synopsis":"The new DATADD from CH_ADD.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "13908": {"comment":"A line found?"},
        "13910": {"comment":"5 back: the byte before it"},
        "13914": {"synopsis":"A bank: the cache address turned into the bank's.","comment":"The program's bank"},
        "13917": {"comment":"Kept at $5B65"},
        "13920": {"comment":"$FF, main memory?"},
        "13923": {"comment":"HL - $5DB6: the offset in the cache"},
        "13927": {"comment":"+ the cached line's address"},
        "13932": {"comment":"The offset form"},
        "13936": {"synopsis":"Kept at $5B9D; the entry returned from.","comment":"Kept at $5B9D"},
        "13939": {"comment":"Type $21"},
        "13941": {"comment":"Its entry returned from"},
        "13944": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13947": {"synopsis":"DATADD = HL; its bank byte $5B78 = $5B65; FLAGS2 bit 7 cleared.\nEntry: HL = the new DATADD (an offset for a bank).","comment":"The bank byte"},
        "13950": {"comment":"For DATADD"},
        "13953": {"comment":"DATADD = HL"},
        "13956": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 7 cleared"},
        "13961": {"synopsis":"CLS (class $0C, its word at $0353); also CLEAR_CHECK's, and called from $0B40, $0B49, $37CD.\nThe low four bits of $5C7F: 0 is ROM 3's CLS_CMD. Otherwise IX = ($5C7F's bits + $F2) x 256,\n$5B84 and $5B86 = 0, the routine at $136B, then ROM 0's $275B with A = $0E; IX kept.","comment":"The low four bits of $5C7F"},
        "13966": {"comment":"0: ROM 3's CLS"},
        "13968": {"comment":"+ $F2"},
        "13970": {"comment":"IX kept"},
        "13972": {"comment":"IX = it x 256"},
        "13977": {"comment":"$5B84 = 0"},
        "13983": {"comment":"$5B86 = 0"},
        "13986": {"comment":"The routine at $136B"},
        "13989": {"comment":"A = $0E"},
        "13991": {"comment":"ROM 0's $275B"},
        "13996": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "13999": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD.","comment":"ROM 3's CLS_CMD"},
        "14003": {"synopsis":"DRAW (class $0E after x and y, its word at $039D): without a ',' the statement's end and a\nstraight line; with one, the angle (a number, through $0634), the statement's end and an\narc. When the low four bits of $5C7F are 0 they are ROM 3's LINE_DRAW and DRAW_ARC's $2394;\notherwise the DivMMC memory's $2C7A and $2C24.","comment":"A ','? An arc"},
        "14007": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14010": {"comment":"The low four bits of $5C7F"},
        "14015": {"comment":"0: ROM 3"},
        "14017": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2C7A (port $E3 = $8A)"},
        "14023": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's LINE_DRAW.","comment":"ROM 3's LINE_DRAW"},
        "14027": {"synopsis":"The angle, the statement's end, the arc.","comment":"Past ',', the angle"},
        "14030": {"comment":"The statement's end"},
        "14033": {"comment":"The low four bits of $5C7F"},
        "14038": {"comment":"0: ROM 3"},
        "14040": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2C24 (port $E3 = $8A)"},
        "14046": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's arc drawing from $2394.","comment":"ROM 3's $2394, inside DRAW_ARC"},
        "14050": {"synopsis":"PAUSE (class 0: a number and the statement's end; its word at $0356): BC = n (TAKE_WORD); n\n> 0 is ROM 3's PAUSE_LOOP with that count; PAUSE 0 is ROM 0's $11E0.","comment":"BC = n"},
        "14053": {"comment":"0?"},
        "14057": {"comment":"ROM 3's PAUSE_LOOP with BC = n"},
        "14061": {"synopsis":"ROM 0's $11E0.","comment":"ROM 0's $11E0"},
        "14067": {"synopsis":"STOP (class $0C, its word at $0338): stops with error code $08 (report 9).","comment":"Error code $08 (report 9)"},
        "14069": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL from code running with bank 7 paged (RST $18): up to a byte below $0D\nor $FF (not printed), or a character with bit 7 set (printed, bit 7 cleared). Called from\n$2C0E, $2C14.\nExit: HL past the last byte read.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "14071": {"comment":"Below $0D: the end"},
        "14074": {"comment":"$FF: the end"},
        "14077": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14078": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "14081": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14082": {"comment":"Bit 7 set? The last"},
        "14086": {"synopsis":"PRINT_A_B7 with bit 7 of A cleared.","comment":"Bit 7 cleared"},
        "14088": {"synopsis":"Prints A through ROM 3's PRINT_A from code running with bank 7 paged: RST $30 puts bank 0\n(and the usual stack) back, RST $18 bank 7 again afterwards. Called many times from\n$2C24-$2C45.","comment":"Bank 0, the usual stack"},
        "14089": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "14092": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 and the alternate stack back (RST $18); return.","comment":"Bank 7, the alternate stack"},
        "14094": {"synopsis":"NUM_OUT_5 from code running with bank 7 paged (RST $30 before, RST $18 after). Nothing in\nthe ROMs jumps here.","comment":"Bank 0, the usual stack"},
        "14095": {"comment":"HL printed"},
        "14100": {"synopsis":"Prints HL (0-65535) as five digits through ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT, a zero before the first digit\nprinted as E ($FF prints nothing); the units always (ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT). Also called\nfrom page 0 ($0738). Keeps HL.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "14101": {"comment":"Ten thousands"},
        "14104": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "14107": {"comment":"Thousands"},
        "14110": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "14113": {"comment":"On"},
        "14115": {"synopsis":"Prints HL (0-999) as three digits, as NUM_OUT_5 does. Keeps HL. Nothing in this page calls\nit.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "14116": {"synopsis":"Hundreds, tens and units.","comment":"Hundreds"},
        "14119": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "14122": {"synopsis":"Tens and units.","comment":"Tens"},
        "14125": {"comment":"ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT"},
        "14128": {"comment":"The units"},
        "14129": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A_DIGIT"},
        "14132": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "14134": {"synopsis":"Prints '-' and A (0-99) as two digits (PRINT_A_2DIG).","comment":"L = the number"},
        "14135": {"comment":"'-'"},
        "14139": {"synopsis":"Prints ':' and L (0-99) as two digits (PRINT_A_2DIG).","comment":"':'"},
        "14141": {"synopsis":"Prints A, then L (0-99) as two digits, a leading zero as '0' (ROM 3's DIGIT_OUT with E = '0'\nfrom NUM_OUT_TENS). Keeps HL.","comment":"HL = the number"},
        "14143": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A: the separator"},
        "14146": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "14147": {"comment":"A leading zero printed as '0'"},
        "14149": {"comment":"Tens and units"},
        "14151": {"synopsis":"Prints a date and time in the MS-DOS form as \"yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm\" (16 characters):\n1. BC = 0: 16 spaces instead (PRINT_16_SPACES).\n2. The year: 1980 + bits 15-9 of BC, five digits with leading zeros not printed (NUM_OUT_5,\n   E = $FF); '-' and the month (bits 8-5); '-' and the day (bits 4-0).\n3. A space and the hours (bits 15-11 of DE); ':' and the minutes (bits 10-5).\nEntry: BC = the date, DE = the time. Also called from page 0 ($3810, RST $18).","comment":"No date?"},
        "14155": {"comment":"The time kept"},
        "14156": {"comment":"The date kept"},
        "14157": {"comment":"A = the year since 1980"},
        "14160": {"comment":"HL = 1980 + it"},
        "14165": {"comment":"Leading zeros not printed"},
        "14167": {"comment":"The year"},
        "14170": {"comment":"HL = the date"},
        "14171": {"comment":"Its low byte kept"},
        "14173": {"comment":"The month's high bit into A"},
        "14176": {"comment":"Down to bits 3-0"},
        "14180": {"comment":"A = the month"},
        "14182": {"comment":"'-' and the month"},
        "14185": {"comment":"The low byte back"},
        "14186": {"comment":"A = the day"},
        "14188": {"comment":"'-' and the day"},
        "14191": {"comment":"HL = the time"},
        "14193": {"comment":"A = the hours"},
        "14199": {"comment":"L = them"},
        "14200": {"comment":"A space"},
        "14202": {"comment":"The space and the hours"},
        "14205": {"comment":"HL = the time"},
        "14206": {"comment":"Shifted: the minutes in H"},
        "14209": {"comment":"A = the minutes"},
        "14212": {"comment":"L = them"},
        "14213": {"comment":"':' and the minutes"},
        "14215": {"synopsis":"No date: 16 spaces (ROM 3's PRINT_A).","comment":"16"},
        "14217": {"synopsis":"One space.","comment":"A space"},
        "14219": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "14222": {"comment":"16 times"},
        "14225": {"synopsis":"Called from page 0 ($11EE, RST $18), with bank 7 at $C000: prints BRIGHT 1, INK 7, PAPER 0\nand AT (DATE_AT_CODES), then line ($F71F) + 9 and column 8 as AT's operands (ROM 3's $201F\ninside PRINT_CTRL3); then ROM 2's IDE_RTC ($01CC, the real-time clock: carry, BC = the date,\nDE = the time); ATTR_T = ($D6E0); and with carry from ROM 2 the date and time\n(PRINT_DATE_TIME).","comment":"BRIGHT 1, INK 7, PAPER 0, AT"},
        "14228": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "14231": {"comment":"The line: ($F71F) + 9"},
        "14236": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "14237": {"comment":"B = column 8"},
        "14239": {"comment":"ROM 3's $201F: C and B printed"},
        "14242": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_RTC: BC = date, DE = time, carry"},
        "14245": {"comment":"The colour from ($D6E0)"},
        "14248": {"comment":"ATTR_T = it"},
        "14251": {"comment":"Carry: the date and time"},
        "14255": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL up to a $FF (not printed), through ROM 3's PRINT_A.\nExit: HL at the $FF.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "14256": {"comment":"$FF: the end"},
        "14259": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "14262": {"comment":"On"},
        "14265": {"synopsis":"Selects stream $FD (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT; BC, DE, HL kept), then PRINT_TEXT_00. Called from\n$2B6C, $2B72 (with HL = YN_QUESTION) and $2BAC.","comment":"Kept"},
        "14268": {"comment":"Stream $FD"},
        "14270": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "14273": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14276": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL up to a $00 (not printed), through ROM 3's PRINT_A. Also called from\n$1925.\nExit: HL at the $00.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "14277": {"comment":"$00: the end"},
        "14279": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "14282": {"comment":"On"},
        "14285": {"synopsis":"Clears the screen (CLS_ALL), then selects stream 2 (ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT). Called from\n$0E0B, $1C09, $1C28 and from page 2 ($0ADD).","comment":"The screen cleared"},
        "14288": {"comment":"Stream 2"},
        "14290": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "14294": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at DE up to and including its character with bit 7 set (printed without it),\nthrough ROM 3's PRINT_A. Called from $0C94, $0D32, $1C93 (with DE = LAYER_TEXT).\nExit: DE past the text.","comment":"The next character"},
        "14295": {"comment":"Bit 7 cleared"},
        "14297": {"comment":"ROM 3's PRINT_A"},
        "14300": {"comment":"Again"},
        "14302": {"comment":"Bit 7 set? The last"},
        "14306": {"synopsis":"Reads the small integer at HL (5 bytes: 0, the sign $00 or $FF, the value's low and high\nbyte in two's complement, 0).\nExit: C = the sign byte, DE = the value without its sign; HL at the high byte.","comment":"The sign byte"},
        "14308": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "14309": {"comment":"Made positive"},
        "14312": {"comment":"E = it"},
        "14313": {"comment":"The high byte"},
        "14315": {"comment":"Made positive, with the borrow"},
        "14317": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "14319": {"synopsis":"Takes the number off the calculator stack into BC: a small integer at once (STKEND - 5\nfirst, SMALL_INT_GET); any other through ROM 3's FP_TO_BC from its rounding step ($2DA8,\nFPBC_ROUND).\nExit: BC = |the value|, A = C; carry when it does not fit 16 bits; Z for positive, NZ for\nnegative.","comment":"HL = STKEND - 5: the top number"},
        "14326": {"comment":"Its exponent byte"},
        "14327": {"comment":"Not 0: not a small integer"},
        "14330": {"comment":"STKEND = HL: taken off"},
        "14333": {"comment":"C = the sign, DE = the value"},
        "14336": {"comment":"Z for positive"},
        "14338": {"comment":"BC = DE"},
        "14339": {"synopsis":"C = E, A = E. Called from $2C1E (CALL NZ) and $0AC2's word."},
        "14340": {"comment":"A = C"},
        "14342": {"synopsis":"Not a small integer: ROM 3's FP_TO_BC from $2DA8 (rounded, INT, taken).","comment":"BC = ROM 3's $2DA8"},
        "14345": {"comment":"Called in ROM 3"},
        "14349": {"synopsis":"Takes the number off the calculator stack into A (FP_TO_BC).\nExit: A = |the value|; carry when it does not fit a byte; Z for positive, NZ for negative.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "14352": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "14353": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "14354": {"comment":"B = 0?"},
        "14358": {"comment":"Yes: the flags back"},
        "14360": {"synopsis":"Over 255: carry.","comment":"No: carry"},
        "14363": {"synopsis":"BC = the number on top of the calculator stack, 0-65535 (FP_TO_BC); otherwise report B\n(REPORT_B). Called from all over the page.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "14366": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "14368": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "14369": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"Integer out of range\").","comment":"Error code $0A (report B)"},
        "14371": {"synopsis":"A = the number on top of the calculator stack, 0-255 (FP_TO_A); otherwise report B.","comment":"A = the number"},
        "14374": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "14376": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "14377": {"comment":"Negative: report B"},
        "14379": {"synopsis":"BC = the number on top of the calculator stack, -65535 to 65535 in two's complement\n(FP_TO_BC, negated when negative); larger is report B.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "14382": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "14384": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "14385": {"comment":"BC negated"},
        "14393": {"synopsis":"A = the number on top of the calculator stack, -255 to 255 in two's complement (FP_TO_A,\nnegated when negative); larger is report B.","comment":"A = the number"},
        "14396": {"comment":"Too big?"},
        "14398": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "14399": {"comment":"A negated"},
        "14402": {"synopsis":"Takes the top number off the calculator stack into A, E, D, C and B (the exponent first; for\na string, DE = its start, BC = its length).","comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "14405": {"comment":"B = the fifth byte"},
        "14407": {"comment":"C = the fourth"},
        "14409": {"comment":"D = the third"},
        "14411": {"comment":"E = the second"},
        "14413": {"comment":"A = the first"},
        "14415": {"comment":"STKEND = 5 lower"},
        "14419": {"synopsis":"Takes the top number off the calculator stack without reading it.\nExit: HL = STKEND, at the dropped number's first byte.","comment":"STKEND - 5"},
        "14426": {"comment":"The new STKEND"},
        "14430": {"synopsis":"Stacks A, E, D, C and B (a string's parameters) as STK_STORE does, with FLAGS bit 6 cleared\n(a string result).","comment":"A string"},
        "14436": {"synopsis":"Stacks A as a number (STACK_BC with BC = A).","comment":"C = A"},
        "14437": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "14439": {"synopsis":"Stacks BC as a small integer (positive): 0, 0, C, B, 0 (STK_STORE).","comment":"A = 0: the exponent"},
        "14440": {"comment":"E = 0: the sign"},
        "14441": {"comment":"D = the low byte"},
        "14442": {"comment":"C = the high byte"},
        "14443": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "14444": {"synopsis":"Stacks a five-byte number held in A, E, D, C and B on the calculator stack: room for 5 more\n(TEST_ROOM, report 4 otherwise), then STK_STORE_NOCHK.","comment":"The bytes kept"},
        "14446": {"comment":"5 more must fit"},
        "14449": {"comment":"TEST_ROOM"},
        "14452": {"comment":"The bytes back"},
        "14454": {"synopsis":"The five bytes stored at STKEND without the room test; STKEND moved up. Called on its own\nfrom $0E5E, $2216, $2267.","comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "14457": {"comment":"The five stored"},
        "14467": {"comment":"STKEND = after them"},
        "14471": {"synopsis":"Running (FLAGS bit 7 set): stacks 0 (STACK_A); checking: nothing.","comment":"Checking? Nothing"},
        "14476": {"comment":"A = 0, stacked"},
        "14479": {"synopsis":"Checks that BC more bytes fit: STKEND + BC + $50 must stay below the machine stack;\notherwise report 4 (REPORT_4).\nExit: carry. Called also from $1A48, $3A43 and $3CC5.","comment":"STKEND"},
        "14482": {"comment":"+ BC"},
        "14483": {"comment":"Past 65535?"},
        "14485": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "14486": {"comment":"+ $50"},
        "14489": {"comment":"Past 65535?"},
        "14492": {"comment":"Below SP?"},
        "14495": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $03 (report 4, \"Out of memory\").","comment":"Error code $03 (report 4)"},
        "14497": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a letter or a digit (DIGIT_TEST, then ALPHA).\nChanges: F.","comment":"A digit?"},
        "14500": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "14502": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a letter, A-Z or a-z.\nChanges: F.","comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "14506": {"comment":"Up to 'Z'?"},
        "14509": {"comment":"Below 'a'?"},
        "14513": {"comment":"Up to 'z'?"},
        "14516": {"synopsis":"Carry unless A is a digit (\"0\"-\"9\").\nChanges: F.","comment":"Below '0'?"},
        "14519": {"comment":"Above '9'?"},
        "14523": {"synopsis":"Makes the line cache area when it is not there (BANK_AREA_TEST): $207 bytes opened before\nCHANS (ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM at CHANS - 1), from $5CB6 on: a statement buffer at $5CB6\n(STMT_COPY), a 256-byte line cache at $5DB6, the cached line's bank address at $5EB6, $5EBA\n(CONTINUE's bank) and the cache's base address at $5EBB. $5EBC = 0 (no line cached); $5EBA =\n$FF.\nExit: NZ.","comment":"Made already?"},
        "14526": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "14527": {"comment":"HL = CHANS - 1"},
        "14531": {"comment":"$207 bytes"},
        "14534": {"comment":"ROM 3's MAKE_ROOM"},
        "14537": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "14538": {"comment":"$5EBC = 0: none cached"},
        "14542": {"comment":"HL = $5EBA"},
        "14544": {"comment":"$FF"},
        "14546": {"comment":"NZ"},
        "14548": {"synopsis":"$5B77 (the bank of the running program, $FF for main memory) = A; a change to a bank empties\nthe line cache ($5EBC = 0, BANK_CACHE_CLEAR).\nExit: Z when A was already there; A = the bank.","comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14551": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "14553": {"comment":"The new one"},
        "14554": {"comment":"Main memory?"},
        "14557": {"synopsis":"$5EBC = 0: no line cached; A = (HL). Also called from $17CB.","comment":"$5EBC = 0"},
        "14561": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14563": {"synopsis":"Z when the line cache area is not made (CHANS's high byte is still $5C).\nChanges: AF.","comment":"CHANS's high byte"},
        "14566": {"comment":"$5C: no area"},
        "14569": {"synopsis":"Brings the line at bank address HL into the line cache:\n1. $5EB6 = HL (bits 7 and 6 set: the $C000 window).\n2. When it is within 255 bytes after the cache's base ($5EBB) and the whole line (its length\n   word + 4) ends inside the cache (below $5E00), HL = its place in the cache ($5DB6 + the\n   distance).\n3. Otherwise $5EBB = $5EB6: 256 bytes from it copied to $5DB6, the bank paged at $C000 for\n   the copy ($32D0) and bank 0 put back (RST $30); HL = $5DB6.\nEntry: HL = the line's bank address, A = the bank.\nExit: HL = the line in the cache.","comment":"Into the $C000 window"},
        "14573": {"comment":"$5EB6 = it"},
        "14576": {"comment":"The cache's base"},
        "14580": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "14581": {"comment":"Before it?"},
        "14585": {"comment":"Within 255 after it?"},
        "14589": {"comment":"HL = its place in the cache"},
        "14593": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14594": {"comment":"The length word"},
        "14599": {"comment":"HL = the line's end, about"},
        "14600": {"comment":"A kept"},
        "14601": {"comment":"Past the cache's end?"},
        "14604": {"comment":"A back"},
        "14605": {"comment":"HL = the line"},
        "14606": {"comment":"Inside: done"},
        "14607": {"synopsis":"The cache filled from the line.","comment":"The cache's new base"},
        "14613": {"comment":"The bank paged"},
        "14616": {"comment":"256 bytes to the cache"},
        "14624": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "14625": {"comment":"HL = the line in the cache"},
        "14629": {"synopsis":"The line at bank address HL (BANK_LINE_CACHE).\nExit: NC at the program's end (a first byte of $28 or more); otherwise carry, DE = the line\nin the cache and HL = the next line's bank address.","comment":"Into the cache"},
        "14632": {"comment":"Its number's high byte"},
        "14633": {"comment":"$28 or more: the end"},
        "14636": {"comment":"DE = the line"},
        "14638": {"comment":"The length word"},
        "14643": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "14644": {"comment":"HL = the next line in the cache"},
        "14645": {"comment":"Less $5DB6"},
        "14649": {"comment":"+ the cache's base: the bank address"},
        "14654": {"comment":"Carry: a line"},
        "14656": {"synopsis":"Copies the line at HL in bank A (its 4-byte header and its text; only the first byte at the\nprogram's end) to $5CB6, the bank paged at $C000 ($32CC) and bank 0 put back. A = $FF does\nnothing.\nExit: HL = $5CB6, DE past the copy. Nothing in the ROMs jumps here.","comment":"$FF: nothing"},
        "14658": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14659": {"comment":"Paged, HL in the window"},
        "14662": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "14663": {"comment":"The number's high byte"},
        "14666": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "14669": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "14670": {"comment":"+ the header"},
        "14674": {"comment":"To $5CB6"},
        "14678": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "14680": {"comment":"The program's end?"},
        "14684": {"comment":"The rest"},
        "14686": {"synopsis":"HL = $5CB6; bank 0 back.","comment":"DE past the copy"},
        "14687": {"comment":"HL = $5CB6"},
        "14688": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "14690": {"synopsis":"Finds the first line numbered BC or more in the main program (A = $FF, from the address\n$0FDB gives) or in bank A (BANK_PROG_CHECK on the bank's first word, $1015 when its bit 7 is\nclear, the start from $0FCE; bank 0 put back afterwards).\nExit: carry and HL = the line (Z when it is line BC); NC when there is none.","comment":"$FF: the main program"},
        "14693": {"comment":"HL = its start ($0FDB)"},
        "14696": {"synopsis":"One line: its number against BC.","comment":"The number's high byte"},
        "14697": {"comment":"$28 or more: the end"},
        "14700": {"comment":"DE = the number"},
        "14704": {"comment":"Compared with BC"},
        "14709": {"comment":"BC or more?"},
        "14711": {"comment":"The length word"},
        "14716": {"comment":"HL = the next line"},
        "14718": {"comment":"On"},
        "14720": {"synopsis":"Bank A.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14721": {"comment":"Paged at $C000"},
        "14724": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "14725": {"comment":"The bank's mark (BANK_PROG_CHECK)"},
        "14728": {"comment":"Its bit 7 clear?"},
        "14729": {"comment":"Then $1015"},
        "14732": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "14733": {"comment":"HL = the start ($0FCE)"},
        "14736": {"comment":"The search"},
        "14739": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "14741": {"synopsis":"Takes the line at HL as the current one: PPC = its number, and HL = the next line. In main\nmemory (the program's bank $5B77 = $FF) from HL itself; in a bank through the line cache\n(BANK_LINE_CACHE), HL then the next line's bank offset (bits 7 and 6 cleared).\nExit: NZ, NC past the program's end (a number byte with bit 6 or 7 set); carry and DE at the\nline's length high byte otherwise. Called from $0942, $1D24, $268A.","comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14744": {"comment":"$FF, main memory?"},
        "14747": {"comment":"The number's high byte"},
        "14748": {"comment":"Bits 6-7 set: the end"},
        "14752": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "14754": {"comment":"PPC = the number"},
        "14758": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "14762": {"comment":"HL = it, DE at the line"},
        "14763": {"comment":"+ the line"},
        "14764": {"comment":"+ 1: the next line"},
        "14765": {"comment":"Carry: a line"},
        "14767": {"synopsis":"A bank: the line through the cache.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14768": {"comment":"The line in the cache"},
        "14771": {"comment":"The number's high byte"},
        "14772": {"comment":"Bits 6-7 set: the end"},
        "14776": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "14778": {"comment":"PPC = the number"},
        "14782": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "14786": {"comment":"DE at the line"},
        "14787": {"comment":"Its bank address"},
        "14790": {"comment":"+ the header"},
        "14794": {"comment":"+ the length"},
        "14795": {"comment":"The offset form"},
        "14799": {"comment":"Carry: a line"},
        "14801": {"synopsis":"The word at $C000 (the paged bank's first) with bit 7 of both bytes cleared must be \"BC\"\n($4342); otherwise bank 0 back (RST $30) and report N.\nExit: A = the word's low byte (its bit 7 a flag).","comment":"The bank's first word"},
        "14804": {"comment":"Its low byte kept"},
        "14805": {"comment":"Bits 7 cleared"},
        "14809": {"comment":"\"BC\""},
        "14812": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "14813": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "14816": {"comment":"No: bank 0 back"},
        "14817": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $16 (report N, \"Statement lost\").","comment":"Error code $16 (report N)"},
        "14819": {"synopsis":"Copies the statement at HL into $5CB6, up to and including its ':' (outside quotes) or\nENTER; a control code below $10 brings the 5 bytes after it along (a number's hidden form).\nBit 0 of C follows the quotes.\nExit: HL = $5CB6, DE past the copy.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"To $5CB6"},
        "14822": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14823": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "14825": {"synopsis":"One more character outside a quote: C one down, the parity kept.","comment":"C one down"},
        "14826": {"synopsis":"The next byte copied.","comment":"The byte"},
        "14827": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "14829": {"comment":"A quote? Bit 0 of C flips"},
        "14833": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "14837": {"comment":"Not ':'? On"},
        "14842": {"comment":"Inside quotes?"},
        "14846": {"synopsis":"HL = $5CB6.","comment":"HL = $5CB6"},
        "14848": {"synopsis":"A code below $10: ENTER ends; any other brings 5 bytes.","comment":"ENTER: the end"},
        "14852": {"comment":"The 5 bytes after it"},
        "14862": {"comment":"On"},
        "14864": {"synopsis":"PROG_BASE for the line PPC.","comment":"HL = PPC"},
        "14867": {"synopsis":"The base the program's pointers are counted from, for line number HL:\n1. The edit line (HL bit 15 set): HL = E_LINE; NZ, NC.\n2. The main program ($5B77 = $FF): HL = PROG; Z, NC.\n3. A bank: HL = ($5EB6) - ($5EBB) (PROG_BASE_BANK); carry.","comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "14868": {"comment":"The edit line?"},
        "14870": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "14873": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "14874": {"comment":"The program's bank"},
        "14877": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "14878": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "14881": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "14882": {"synopsis":"HL = ($5EB6) - ($5EBB), DE kept; carry.","comment":"The cached line's bank address"},
        "14885": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "14886": {"comment":"Less the cache's base"},
        "14893": {"comment":"Carry: a bank"},
        "14895": {"synopsis":"HL, an address in the line cache, becomes the bank address it was copied from (HL - $5DB6 +\n($5EBB)). Called from $246F, $24D8.","comment":"($5EB6) - ($5EBB)"},
        "14898": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "14899": {"comment":"Less $5DB6"},
        "14903": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "14904": {"comment":"Less it"},
        "14906": {"comment":"+ ($5EB6)"},
        "14912": {"synopsis":"Puts an 11-byte entry of type A on the GO SUB stack, below the two words on top of the\nmachine stack (the statement loop's return and the error address, which ERR_SP marks):\n1. Room for 11 bytes (TEST_ROOM).\n2. The entry, from its high end: SUBPPC; PPC; NXTLIN and CH_ADD as offsets from PROG_BASE\n   (NXTLIN as it is in a bank); $5EB6; the type A; the program's bank $5B77.\n3. $5C0B = the entry; the two words back above it, ERR_SP at the error address.\nEntry: A = the type. Called from $0C12, $128D, $1E0E, $1E6E, $2071, $247A and page 2\n($27C6).","comment":"11 bytes"},
        "14915": {"comment":"Must fit"},
        "14918": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "14919": {"comment":"DE = the statement loop's return"},
        "14920": {"comment":"BC = the error address"},
        "14921": {"comment":"Kept in the other set"},
        "14922": {"comment":"H = SUBPPC"},
        "14925": {"comment":"One byte of it"},
        "14927": {"comment":"PPC"},
        "14931": {"comment":"The base (PROG_BASE)"},
        "14934": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "14935": {"comment":"NXTLIN"},
        "14938": {"comment":"A bank: as it is"},
        "14940": {"comment":"Less the base"},
        "14942": {"synopsis":"The NXTLIN word kept; CH_ADD's.","comment":"Kept"},
        "14943": {"comment":"CH_ADD"},
        "14946": {"comment":"Less the base"},
        "14949": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14950": {"comment":"$5EB6"},
        "14954": {"comment":"L = the program's bank"},
        "14957": {"comment":"H = the type"},
        "14958": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14959": {"comment":"$5C0B = the entry"},
        "14963": {"comment":"The words back"},
        "14964": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "14965": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "14969": {"comment":"The statement loop's return"},
        "14970": {"comment":"Back"},
        "14971": {"synopsis":"Returns from the newest GO SUB stack entry whatever its type: C = $5B5E = its type byte (at\nERR_SP + 3), then GOSUB_RETURN_C.","comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "14974": {"comment":"+ 3: the newest entry's type"},
        "14977": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "14978": {"comment":"$5B5E = it"},
        "14982": {"synopsis":"Returns from the GO SUB stack's newest entry of type C (GOSUB_FIND_POP); none: carry,\nnothing done. Then GOSUB_UNWIND.\nEntry: C = the type. Called from $0BA5, $0C0B, $18B3, $2378, $24F5, $3675.","comment":"Found and taken back?"},
        "14985": {"comment":"None: carry"},
        "14986": {"synopsis":"After an entry is taken back: the DivMMC memory's $290A with BC = ERR_SP; unless $5B99's\nhigh byte has bit 0 set, DATADD comes back from the entry GOSUB_FIND passed (FLAGS2 bit 7\nfrom $5B99's high byte, $5B78 = its low byte, DATADD = $5B9B, + PROG for the main program);\nthe machine stack is cut to $5C0B, the statement loop's return and the error address back\nabove it, ERR_SP at the latter.\nExit: A = 0. Also called from $2155.","comment":"BC = ERR_SP"},
        "14990": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $290A"},
        "14995": {"comment":"The DATA state seen"},
        "14998": {"comment":"None?"},
        "15002": {"comment":"FLAGS2"},
        "15005": {"comment":"Bit 7 from H"},
        "15008": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "15011": {"comment":"The DATA bank"},
        "15012": {"comment":"$5B78 = it"},
        "15015": {"comment":"HL = the DATA offset"},
        "15018": {"comment":"Main memory?"},
        "15021": {"comment":"+ PROG"},
        "15026": {"synopsis":"DATADD = HL.","comment":"DATADD = it"},
        "15029": {"synopsis":"The machine stack cut to $5C0B.","comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "15030": {"comment":"DE = the statement loop's return"},
        "15031": {"comment":"BC = the error address"},
        "15032": {"comment":"SP = $5C0B"},
        "15036": {"comment":"The error address"},
        "15037": {"comment":"ERR_SP at it"},
        "15041": {"comment":"The statement loop's return"},
        "15042": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "15043": {"comment":"Back"},
        "15044": {"synopsis":"Finds the GO SUB stack's newest entry of type C (GOSUB_FIND; none: carry) and takes it back\n(GOSUB_RESTORE). Called from $207C, $20FE.","comment":"The entry"},
        "15047": {"comment":"None"},
        "15048": {"synopsis":"Goes back to the place the 11-byte GO SUB stack entry at HL + 1 (its type byte) holds:\n1. The program's bank from its first byte (SET_PROG_BANK); $FE is report N; for a bank its\n   line ($5EB6's copy) must be found again (BANK_LINE_AT), else report N.\n2. PPC and SUBPPC; NXTLIN and CH_ADD from their offsets + PROG_BASE (NXTLIN as kept in a\n   bank).\n3. $5C0B = the entry above it (this one dropped).\nExit: A = 0, NC.\nCalled from $1EF8, $1FB9 and page 2 ($27E2).","comment":"HL = its first byte"},
        "15049": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15050": {"comment":"A = its bank"},
        "15052": {"comment":"DE = the type's address"},
        "15053": {"comment":"The program's bank = A"},
