        "15376": {"comment":"Back"},
        "15378": {"synopsis":"Drops the newest 11-byte entry (SP + 11 after the three words). Called from $1E83, $2633.","comment":"IX = the return address"},
        "15380": {"comment":"BC = the statement loop's return"},
        "15381": {"comment":"DE = the error address"},
        "15382": {"comment":"Past the newest entry"},
        "15388": {"synopsis":"Puts the variable named at CH_ADD, with its value, on the GO SUB stack as a variable-length\nentry (type 0 or 1, from IXh), so that the GO SUB stack carries it. D, set by the caller,\nholds flags: which forms are allowed, and whether a value may follow ('=' and an expression,\nVAR_VALUE).\n1. '%' first: an integer variable (VAR_STACK_INT).\n2. The name: E = its first letter in lower case; ROM 3's COUNT_NAME counts the rest; $5C5B =\n   its end; a number's hidden form after it passed.\n3. '$': a string, '(' after it an array (C = $C0) or not (C = $40); otherwise '(' a numeric\n   array (C = $80) or a number (a long name: E with bit 7 set, bit 6 clear).\n4. The value: a string's text (STK_FETCH), the 3 bytes VAR_NO_VALUE, a number's 5 bytes or\n   ZERO_NUMBER, copied onto the machine stack below the three top words (room tested,\n   TEST_ROOM).\n5. Then the length word, the bytes of a long name (the last with $A0, the others with $20)\n   or the letter, and the type bytes; $5C0B, ERR_SP and the three words set again.\nExit: carry when stacked; NC when the form is not allowed. Called from $228C, $23BE, $2459.","comment":"The first character"},
        "15391": {"comment":"'%'? An integer variable"},
        "15396": {"comment":"E = the letter"},
        "15397": {"comment":"In lower case"},
        "15399": {"comment":"ROM 3's COUNT_NAME: the rest"},
        "15402": {"comment":"B = $FF less the count"},
        "15403": {"comment":"$5C5B = the name's end"},
