        "15823": {"synopsis":"Assigns the value just evaluated to the variable at DEST through ROM 3's LET_ASSIGN\n(CALL_ROM3_BC); with FLAGS2 bit 2 set (a '%' variable) it must be a number, else report C.\nCalled from $1DD7, $2135, $327F, $3E70, $3F58, $3FCE.","comment":"FLAGS"},
        "15826": {"synopsis":"ASSIGN_CHECKED with FLAGS already in A. From $2FEA.","comment":"A '%' variable?"},
        "15832": {"comment":"A string: report C"},
        "15837": {"synopsis":"ROM 3's LET_ASSIGN.","comment":"BC = ROM 3's LET_ASSIGN"},
        "15840": {"comment":"Called there"},
        "15843": {"synopsis":"The 16 ULA colours as 8-bit palette values (RRRGGGBB): black, blue, red, magenta, green,\ncyan, yellow, white, then their bright forms; $AA after them. The palette loader at $1579\nwrites them to NextReg $41 and starts again at the $AA, so the 16 repeat through all 256\nentries."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"RST $10's function table (RST10_DISPATCH at $0E77 reads the word at $3E00 + 2 x the function\nbyte): two words, both NEW_CMD. A function byte of 2 or more goes to NEW_CMD too ($0E86)."},
        "15876": {"synopsis":"DRIVER, keyword $95 (class 8 then $0E, its word at $03B0; also called from $1535, $2C72):\nDRIVER id,call[,a[,b]] [TO v[,w[,x]]] (the DRIVER command of the API document).\n1. C = id and B = call (TAKE_BYTE each, when running); a and b, optional after ','\n   (TAKE_NUM_OPT), in DE and HL.\n2. Running: ROM 2's IDE_DRIVER ($01CF) with them; no carry is error code $12 (report J).\n3. After TO, up to three numeric variables (TO_VAR_OPT) get BC, then the two values it left\n   in DE and HL; the statement's end.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "15881": {"comment":"The call id"},
        "15884": {"comment":"Kept for B"},
        "15885": {"comment":"The driver id"},
        "15889": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "15890": {"synopsis":"The optional numbers.","comment":"Kept"},
        "15891": {"comment":"HL = a, or 0"},
        "15894": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "15895": {"comment":"HL = b, or 0"},
        "15898": {"comment":"DE = a"},
        "15899": {"comment":"BC = the ids"},
