        "15981": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "15984": {"comment":"Assigned"},
        "15987": {"synopsis":"NC.","comment":"NC"},
        "15989": {"synopsis":"Called by ROM 3's TAPE_BREAK ($04AA, $0C7B, $1F60, through its $32C5) and by page 0 ($2930):\nthe DivMMC memory's $299C (through $0059); NZ when it leaves E bit 1 set. Keeps DE.","comment":"Kept"},
        "15990": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $299C"},
        "15993": {"comment":"E bit 1?"},
        "15995": {"comment":"Back"},
        "16000": {"synopsis":"CALL $3E80 with a word after it: calls that address in ROM 0. The word is read (the return\naddress moved past it), ROM0_SELECT is pushed as the way back (ROM 0's own $3E93 selects ROM\n1 again), then ROM 0 is selected and RET goes to the address. BC is kept through $5B54. The\nsame bytes are at $3E80 in every page that calls another ROM this way.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "16004": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "16005": {"comment":"BC = the word"},
        "16009": {"comment":"The return address past it"},
        "16010": {"comment":"The way back"},
        "16014": {"comment":"The address"},
        "16015": {"synopsis":"BC back from $5B54; ROM 0; RET to the address. From $0097 (CALL $0080).","comment":"BC back"},
        "16019": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8E = 0: ROM 0 (bit 3 clear: only the ROM changes); RET. Both the way into ROM 0 and\nthe way back for page 0's calls into this ROM (pushed by its CALL $3E80).","comment":"ROM 0"},
        "16023": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16024": {"synopsis":"Control codes printed by PRINT_DATE_AT: BRIGHT 1, INK 7, PAPER 0 and AT (its two operands\nfollow from the caller), $FF ending them."},
        "16032": {"synopsis":"Calls the DivMMC memory's routine whose address is on top of the stack (port $E3 = $87,\nthrough $26DA): A kept at $5B56, BC at $5B54; the way back is $2705 and then $007B (the\nalternate ROM on). Nothing in the ROMs jumps here.","comment":"A kept"},
        "16035": {"comment":"Port $E3's value"},
        "16037": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "16041": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "16042": {"comment":"The way back through $007B"},
        "16046": {"comment":"Called (port $E3 = $87)"},
        "16049": {"synopsis":"The alternate ROM's $25A3. Called from page 0 ($3ACD, RST $18).","comment":"The alternate ROM's $25A3"},
        "16055": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $2855 with D = 0. Called from $0BDE, $0BF4, $0BFE.","comment":"D = 0"},
        "16057": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $2855 (port $E3 = $87). Also from $0BE8, $1F4E, $3FC6.","comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2855"},
        "16063": {"synopsis":"CALL_ROM3_BC with bit 6 of B cleared: a syntax-table word with bit 6 set names a ROM 3\nroutine (from $057E).","comment":"The ROM 3 address"},
        "16065": {"synopsis":"Calls the ROM 3 routine at BC: $5B3E (ROM 1 again) pushed as the way back, BC pushed, then\n$5B48 selects ROM 3 and RET goes there. Used by many routines (jumps from $05A6, $05BE,\n$0638, $063F ...).","comment":"The way back: ROM 1"},
        "16069": {"comment":"The address"},
        "16070": {"comment":"ROM 3, then the address"},
        "16073": {"synopsis":"A = the character at CH_ADD, past what is skipped (SKIP_CHAR, from HL = CH_ADD). Called from\nall over the page.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "16076": {"comment":"The test"},
        "16079": {"synopsis":"HL + 1, CH_ADD = HL, SKIP_CHAR. RST $20 jumps here with HL = CH_ADD.","comment":"One on"},
        "16080": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = HL, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "16083": {"synopsis":"A = the character at HL; $21 and up, $0D and $0E (a number's mark) are kept (return, no\ncarry). Anything else moves on: $18-$20 and the codes below $10 by one byte, $10-$15 by two,\n$16-$17 by three, CH_ADD following.\nExit: A = the character, HL = CH_ADD.","comment":"The character"},
        "16084": {"comment":"$21 and up: kept"},
        "16087": {"comment":"ENTER: kept"},
        "16090": {"comment":"A number's mark: kept"},
        "16093": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "16094": {"comment":"$18-$20: skipped"},
        "16098": {"comment":"Below $10: skipped"},
        "16102": {"comment":"$10-$15: one operand"},
        "16106": {"comment":"$16-$17: two"},
        "16109": {"synopsis":"Swaps $5B77 (the program's bank) and $5B78 (DATADD's bank), in the other register set.\nCalled from page 2 ($1EF0).","comment":"The other set"},
        "16110": {"comment":"L = $5B77, H = $5B78"},
        "16113": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "16116": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "16119": {"comment":"Back"},
        "16121": {"synopsis":"Running (FLAGS bit 7 set): returns. Checking: returns from the caller as well. Called from\n$1353, $1365, $2E12, $2E31, $2E4F, $2E65 ...","comment":"Running?"},
        "16126": {"comment":"Checking: the caller's return dropped"},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"CALL $3F00, or RST $00 ($0001), with a word after it: calls that address in ROM 2, as\nCALL_ROM0 does, with ROM2_SELECT as the way in and page 2's own $3F13 the way back.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "16132": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "16133": {"comment":"BC = the word"},
        "16137": {"comment":"The return address past it"},
        "16138": {"comment":"The way back"},
        "16142": {"comment":"The address"},
        "16143": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "16147": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8E = 2: ROM 2 (bit 3 clear); RET. Also the way back for page 2's calls into this\nROM.","comment":"ROM 2"},
        "16151": {"comment":"To the address"},
        "16152": {"synopsis":"Decides whether the character in A is skipped while scanning: no carry keeps it ($21 and up,\n$0D), carry skips it; $10-$15 also skip the one byte after them, $16-$17 the two\n(SKIP_TEST_SET). The same bytes as ROM 3's SKIP_TEST; nothing in the ROMs jumps here.\nChanges: F, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"$21 and up: kept"},
        "16155": {"comment":"ENTER: kept"},
        "16158": {"comment":"Below $10: skipped"},
        "16161": {"comment":"$18 and up: skipped"},
        "16165": {"comment":"One operand"},
        "16166": {"comment":"$16-$17?"},
        "16170": {"comment":"Two"},
        "16171": {"synopsis":"Carry set (skip), and CH_ADD = HL.","comment":"Carry: skip"},
        "16172": {"comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "16176": {"synopsis":"DIM #s,v (class 5, the routine after '#'; its word at $03DB): STREAM_TO_VAR with B = 2.","comment":"B = 2"},
        "16178": {"comment":"On"},
        "16180": {"synopsis":"NEXT #s,v (class 5; its word at $03ED): ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_IN ($005C) gives A; v = A\n(STACK_A, then STREAM_ASSIGN).","comment":"ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_IN: A = the byte"},
        "16183": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "16186": {"comment":"Assigned"},
        "16188": {"synopsis":"RETURN #s,v (class 5; its word at $03D5): STREAM_TO_VAR with B = 0.","comment":"B = 0"},
        "16190": {"synopsis":"ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_PTR ($0062) with B (2 for DIM #, 0 for RETURN #) gives two words, DE and\nHL; v = DE x 65536 + HL: both stacked (STACK_BC), the 10 calculator bytes at $0DD1 run on\nthem (through $09BA), then STREAM_ASSIGN.","comment":"ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_PTR, B = the function"},
        "16193": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "16194": {"comment":"BC = HL"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "16199": {"comment":"BC = DE"},
        "16200": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "16203": {"comment":"The calculator bytes at $0DD1"},
        "16206": {"comment":"10 of them"},
        "16209": {"comment":"Run (through $09BA)"},
        "16212": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bit 6 set (a number); ASSIGN_CHECKED.","comment":"A number"},
        "16216": {"comment":"Assigned"},
        "16219": {"synopsis":"OPEN # (class $0C after a number, ',' and a string; its word at $03E4): the string's start\nand length (STK_FETCH), the stream (TAKE_BYTE), then ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_OPEN ($0056) with A,\nDE and BC; no carry is the error code ROM 2 left in A (STREAM_FAIL_TEST).","comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "16222": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "16224": {"comment":"A = the stream"},
        "16227": {"comment":"Back"},
        "16229": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_OPEN"},
        "16232": {"synopsis":"No carry: error code A (through $0904); return.","comment":"Failed: error code A"},
        "16236": {"synopsis":"CLOSE # (class 0, a number and the statement's end; its word at $036B): A = the stream\n(TAKE_BYTE), ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_CLOSE ($0059); no carry is the error code in A\n(STREAM_FAIL_TEST).","comment":"A = the stream"},
        "16239": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_CLOSE"},
        "16242": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "16244": {"synopsis":"The form whose word is at $04CF (in the table after $03FE): the 13 calculator bytes at $0DDB\nrun on the calculator stack (through $09BA); A (TAKE_BYTE) selects a stream (ROM 3's\nSTREAM_SELECT); two words follow (FP_TO_BC each), the first into DE and the second into HL;\nthen ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_PTR ($0062) with B = 1.","comment":"The calculator bytes at $0DDB"},
        "16247": {"comment":"13 of them"},
        "16250": {"comment":"Run (through $09BA)"},
        "16253": {"comment":"A = the stream"},
        "16256": {"comment":"ROM 3's STREAM_SELECT"},
        "16259": {"comment":"The first word"},
        "16262": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "16263": {"comment":"The second"},
        "16267": {"comment":"HL = the second"},
        "16268": {"comment":"DE = the first"},
        "16269": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "16271": {"comment":"ROM 2's IDE_STREAM_PTR, B = 1"},
        "16275": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $2860. Called from $1DCC, $1F55, $2C6B, $2C7E, $2C88, $2C92.","comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2860"},
        "16281": {"synopsis":"The text \"Layer \" (bit 7 on the space), printed by PRINT_TEXT_DE from $1C90."},
        "16287": {"synopsis":"The text \"? (Y/N)\", ENTER and $00, printed by PRINT_LOWER_TEXT from $2B6F."},
        "16312": {"synopsis":"Five zero bytes: the number 0 in the calculator's form. Read by $24B6 and $3CB1 (VAR_STACK)."},
        "16317": {"synopsis":"RANDOMIZE (class $0D, its word at $034A): ROM 3's RANDOMIZE_CMD, then the DivMMC memory's\n$2855 with HL = $2A9A and DE = 0 (CALL_2855).","comment":"ROM 3's RANDOMIZE_CMD"},
        "16320": {"comment":"HL = $2A9A"},
        "16323": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "16326": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2855"},
        "16329": {"synopsis":"POINT as a statement (keyword $A9: class 8, TO, class 1, class $0C; its word at $03EA): x,y\nTO v: the DivMMC memory's $2AF0 (port $E3 = $8A) gives the value, assigned to v\n(ASSIGN_CHECKED).","comment":"The DivMMC memory's $2AF0"},
        "16334": {"comment":"Assigned"},
        "16337": {"synopsis":"The command of keyword $88 (class 8, two numbers, then $0C; its word at $03C0): NextReg r =\nv, r and v 0-255 (TAKE_BYTE each) written through ports $243B and $253B.","comment":"A = v"},
        "16340": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "16341": {"comment":"A = r"},
        "16344": {"comment":"The NextReg select port"},
        "16347": {"comment":"r selected"},
        "16349": {"comment":"BC = $253B"},
        "16350": {"comment":"A = v"},
        "16351": {"comment":"Written"},
        "16354": {"synopsis":"The command of keyword $81 (class $0C, its word at $031A): FRAMES = 0 (all three bytes).","comment":"0"},
        "16357": {"comment":"FRAMES' low word"},
        "16360": {"comment":"0"},
        "16361": {"comment":"FRAMES' high byte"},
        "16365": {"synopsis":"A = the low four bits of $5C7F: 0 returns Z, 1-2 return with carry; 3 and up return A / 4 -\n1 (NC). Called from $05CE, $136F.","comment":"The low four bits of $5C7F"},
        "16370": {"comment":"0: Z"},
        "16371": {"comment":"1-2: carry"},
        "16374": {"comment":"/ 4"},
        "16378": {"comment":"- 1"}
      }
    },
