      ],
      "lineAnnotations": {
        "0": {"synopsis":"Address $0000: NOP and a JR back to it, for good: code that reaches $0000 while this ROM is\npaged in stays here."},
        "1": {"comment":"Back to $0000 for good"},
        "8": {"synopsis":"RST $08: on to $3F18, which calls code in the DivMMC memory. The byte after the RST goes to\nA\n(a selector: probably the DivMMC RAM bank at $2000-$3FFF during the call), the word after it\nto HL (the address to run there); the caller's HL and AF are kept at $5B52 and $5B56, DE as\ngiven, and the return goes past the word.","comment":"On to $3F18 with the byte and word after the RST"},
        "11": {"synopsis":"The text \".bak\", ended by $FF: copied over a file's type by DOS_OPEN (open action 3)\nat $036D."},
        "16": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $0037."},
        "56": {"synopsis":"The maskable interrupt (IM 1) while this ROM is paged in.\n1. AF, BC and HL kept, and the number of the NextReg selected at port $243B.\n2. The DivMMC memory's $0045 called with selector 0, entering $3F31 past the DI and the\ninterrupt state test of RST_CALL_DIVMMC.\n3. The NextReg selection put back; the registers back, interrupts on.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "59": {"comment":"The NextReg select port"},
        "62": {"comment":"L = the NextReg selected now"},
        "64": {"comment":"Kept with the port"},
        "66": {"comment":"Selector 0"},
        "67": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $0045"},
        "70": {"comment":"Into the DivMMC call past its DI"},
        "73": {"comment":"Port and NextReg number back"},
        "75": {"comment":"The NextReg selection restored"},
        "77": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "80": {"comment":"Interrupts on again"},
        "82": {"synopsis":"The end of every API entry that is not implemented (16 jump-table entries): error $3A,\nrc_notimp in the document (manual).\nExit: A = $3A, carry clear.","comment":"Error $3A (rc_notimp)"},
        "84": {"comment":"Carry clear: an error"},
        "86": {"synopsis":"The stream calls: five JP instructions at the documented addresses $0056-$0062 (manual).\nIDE_STREAM_OPEN ($0056): open a stream to a channel. On at $1152 (the routine there carries\nthe\ncall's name)."},
        "89": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_CLOSE ($0059): close a stream and its channel. On at $14BE (the routine there\ncarries the call's name)."},
        "92": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_IN ($005C): a byte from the current stream. On at $1565 (the routine there\ncarries\nthe call's name)."},
        "95": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_OUT ($005F): a byte to the current stream. On at $155B (the routine there carries\nthe call's name)."},
        "98": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_PTR ($0062): the current stream's pointer, got or set. On at $156A (the routine\nthere carries the call's name)."},
        "101": {"synopsis":"Unused: one $00 before the NMI."},
        "102": {"synopsis":"The NMI: RETN at once."},
        "104": {"synopsis":"Copies through the DivMMC memory's $04DD with selector 1: from ROM 0's COLSET_PUT ($0FFB\nthere), with BC = $60 bytes, HL the source and DE the destination ($3760 when a set is\nstored), so $04DD probably copies BC bytes from HL to DE with DivMMC bank 1 at $2000-$3FFF.","comment":"DivMMC $04DD, selector 1: BC bytes HL to DE"},
        "109": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL in the DivMMC memory through its $001D with selector 1 (ROM 1's\nSET_ATTR_FIELD reads $3760 so).\nExit: A = the byte.","comment":"DivMMC $001D, selector 1: A = the byte at HL"},
        "114": {"synopsis":"Writes A at HL in the DivMMC memory through its $02E0 with selector 1 (ROM 1's\nSET_ATTR_FIELD writes $3760 back so).","comment":"DivMMC $02E0, selector 1: A written at HL"},
        "119": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $009F."},
        "160": {"synopsis":"The IDEDOS jump table: 32 JP instructions, $00A0 to $00FD, at the documented addresses of\nthe\nIDE_* calls (manual); eleven lead to NOT_IMPLEMENTED.\nIDE_VERSION ($00A0): the IDEDOS version number. On at $1A70 (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "163": {"synopsis":"IDE_INTERFACE ($00A3): initialises the card interfaces. On at $19AE (the routine there\ncarries\nthe call's name)."},
        "166": {"synopsis":"IDE_INIT ($00A6): initialises IDEDOS. On at $1ADF (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "169": {"synopsis":"IDE_DRIVE ($00A9): the handle of a unit. On to IDE_DRIVE ($01DB)."},
        "172": {"synopsis":"IDE_SECTOR_READ ($00AC): low-level sector read. On at $184A (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "175": {"synopsis":"IDE_SECTOR_WRITE ($00AF): low-level sector write. On at $1879 (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "178": {"synopsis":"IDE_FORMAT ($00B2): format a partition. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error\n$3A\n(rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "181": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_FIND ($00B5): find a partition by name. On to IDE_PART_FIND ($01E6)."},
        "184": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_NEW ($00B8): create a partition. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives\nerror $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "187": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_INIT ($00BB): initialise a partition. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED\ngives\nerror $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "190": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_ERASE ($00BE): delete a partition. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives\nerror $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "193": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_RENAME ($00C1): rename a partition. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED\ngives\nerror $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "196": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ (so spelt in the document) ($00C4): read a partition entry. On to\nIDE_PART_READ ($01EB)."},
        "199": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_WRITE ($00C7): write a partition entry. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED\ngives error $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "202": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_WINFO ($00CA): write the type-specific information. Here not implemented:\nNOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "205": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_OPEN ($00CD): open a partition. On to PART_MAP ($0740)."},
        "208": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_CLOSE ($00D0): close a partition. On to PART_UNMAP ($07CF)."},
        "211": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_GETINFO ($00D3): a byte of the type-specific information. Here not\nimplemented:\nNOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "214": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_SETINFO ($00D6): set a byte of the type-specific information. Here not\nimplemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "217": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_OPEN ($00D9): open a swap file. On at $16AC (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "220": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_CLOSE ($00DC): close a swap file. On at $1776 (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "223": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_OUT ($00DF): write a block to the swap file. On at $168B (the routine there carries\nthe call's name)."},
        "226": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_IN ($00E2): read a block from the swap file. On at $1614 (the routine there carries\nthe call's name)."},
        "229": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_EX ($00E5): exchange a block with the swap file (deprecated, rc_notimp in the\ndocument). On at $16A8 (the routine there carries the call's name)."},
        "232": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_POS ($00E8): the current block number. On at $15BD (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "235": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_MOVE ($00EB): set the current block number. On at $15C9 (the routine there carries\nthe\ncall's name)."},
        "238": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_RESIZE ($00EE): change the block size. On at $179B (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "241": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_MAP ($00F1): map a drive to a partition, a device or an image file. On to\nIDE_DOS_MAP\n($03CF)."},
        "244": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_UNMAP ($00F4): unmap a drive. On to IDE_DOS_UNMAP ($0451)."},
        "247": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_MAPPING ($00F7): a drive's mapping. On to IDE_DOS_MAPPING ($0478)."},
        "250": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_UNPERMANENT ($00FA): remove a permanent mapping. Here not implemented:\nNOT_IMPLEMENTED\ngives error $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "253": {"synopsis":"IDE_SNAPLOAD ($00FD): load and run a snapshot. On to IDE_SNAPLOAD ($082E)."},
        "256": {"synopsis":"The +3DOS jump table: 73 JP instructions, $0100 to $01D8, at the documented addresses of the\nDOS_*, DD_* and NextZXOS's own IDE_* calls (manual). Many of the floppy calls share $2599 or\n$259D; $019F, $01A8, $01AB and $01AE are not in the document.\nDOS_INITIALISE ($0100): initialise +3DOS. On at $252A."},
        "259": {"synopsis":"DOS_VERSION ($0103): the +3DOS issue and version. On at $252C (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "262": {"synopsis":"DOS_OPEN ($0106): create and/or open a file. On to DOS_OPEN ($0322)."},
        "265": {"synopsis":"DOS_CLOSE ($0109): close a file. On to DOS_CLOSE ($0258)."},
        "268": {"synopsis":"DOS_ABANDON ($010C): abandon a file. On to DOS_ABANDON ($0269)."},
        "271": {"synopsis":"DOS_REF_HEAD ($010F): point at a file's header data. On to DOS_REF_HEAD ($0226)."},
        "274": {"synopsis":"DOS_READ ($0112): read bytes into memory. On to DOS_READ ($027A)."},
        "277": {"synopsis":"DOS_WRITE ($0115): write bytes from memory. On to DOS_WRITE ($02D6)."},
        "280": {"synopsis":"DOS_BYTE_READ ($0118): read a byte. On to DOS_BYTE_READ ($022C)."},
        "283": {"synopsis":"DOS_BYTE_WRITE ($011B): write a byte. On to DOS_BYTE_WRITE ($0232)."},
        "286": {"synopsis":"DOS_CATALOG ($011E): catalogue a directory. On to DOS_CATALOG ($0200)."},
        "289": {"synopsis":"DOS_FREE_SPACE ($0121): free space on a drive. On to DOS_FREE_SPACE ($01F0)."},
        "292": {"synopsis":"DOS_DELETE ($0124): delete a file. On at $2812 (the routine there carries the call's name)."},
        "295": {"synopsis":"DOS_RENAME ($0127): rename a file. On at $2823 (the routine there carries the call's name)."},
        "298": {"synopsis":"DOS_BOOT ($012A): boot. On at $253C (the routine there carries the call's name)."},
        "301": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_DRIVE ($012D): set or get the default drive. On to DOS_SET_DRIVE ($0550)."},
        "304": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_USER ($0130): set or get the default user area. On to DOS_SET_USER ($055E)."},
        "307": {"synopsis":"DOS_GET_POSITION ($0133): a file's pointer. On to DOS_GET_POSITION ($0238)."},
        "310": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_POSITION ($0136): set a file's pointer. On to DOS_SET_POSITION ($023E)."},
        "313": {"synopsis":"DOS_GET_EOF ($0139): a file's end position. On to DOS_GET_EOF ($0246)."},
        "316": {"synopsis":"DOS_GET_1346 ($013C): the memory used in pages 1, 3, 4, 6. On to DOS_GET_1346 ($05E0)."},
        "319": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_1346 ($013F): reallocate the memory in pages 1, 3, 4, 6. On to DOS_SET_1346 ($05E5)."},
        "322": {"synopsis":"DOS_FLUSH ($0142): bring a drive up to date. On to DOS_FLUSH ($01F8)."},
        "325": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_ACCESS ($0145): change an open file's access mode. On to DOS_SET_ACCESS ($024C)."},
        "328": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES ($0148): change a file's attributes. On to DOS_SET_ATTRIBS ($0214)."},
        "331": {"synopsis":"DOS_OPEN_DRIVE ($014B): open a drive as one file (deprecated). Here not implemented:\nNOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "334": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_MESSAGE ($014E): error messages on or off. On at $259F (the routine there carries\nthe\ncall's name)."},
        "337": {"synopsis":"DOS_REF_XDPB ($0151): point at a drive's XDPB. On at $20E4 (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "340": {"synopsis":"map B ($0154): (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "343": {"synopsis":"DD_INTERFACE ($0157): is the floppy interface present. On at $259D."},
        "346": {"synopsis":"DD_INIT ($015A): initialise the disk driver. On at $259D."},
        "349": {"synopsis":"DD_SETUP ($015D): drive parameters. On at $259D."},
        "352": {"synopsis":"DD_SET_RETRY ($0160): the try/retry count. On at $259D."},
        "355": {"synopsis":"DD_READ_SECTOR ($0163): read a sector. On at $2789 (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "358": {"synopsis":"DD_WRITE_SECTOR ($0166): write a sector (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "361": {"synopsis":"DD_CHECK_SECTOR ($0169): check a sector (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "364": {"synopsis":"DD_FORMAT ($016C): format a track (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "367": {"synopsis":"DD_READ_ID ($016F): read a sector identifier (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "370": {"synopsis":"DD_TEST_UNSUITABLE ($0172): test the media (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "373": {"synopsis":"DD_LOGIN ($0175): log a disk in (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "376": {"synopsis":"DD_SEL_FORMAT ($0178): pre-initialise an XDPB for formatting (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "379": {"synopsis":"DD_ASK_1 ($017B): is unit 1 present. On at $2750 (the routine there carries the call's name)."},
        "382": {"synopsis":"DD_DRIVE_STATUS ($017E): the drive status. On at $2778 (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "385": {"synopsis":"DD_EQUIPMENT ($0181): the kind of drive (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "388": {"synopsis":"DD_ENCODE ($0184): the copy-protection intercept. On at $2619 (the routine there carries the\ncall's name)."},
        "391": {"synopsis":"DD_L_XDPB ($0187): an XDPB from a disk specification. On at $2628 (the routine there carries\nthe call's name)."},
        "394": {"synopsis":"DD_L_DPB ($018A): a DPB from a disk specification. On at $266A (the routine there carries\nthe\ncall's name)."},
        "397": {"synopsis":"DD_L_SEEK ($018D): the uPD765A seek driver. On at $259D."},
        "400": {"synopsis":"DD_L_READ ($0190): the uPD765A read driver. On at $279E (the routine there carries the\ncall's\nname)."},
        "403": {"synopsis":"DD_L_WRITE ($0193): the uPD765A write driver (deprecated). On at $2599."},
        "406": {"synopsis":"DD_L_ON_MOTOR ($0196): motor on. On at $259D."},
        "409": {"synopsis":"DD_L_T_OFF_MOTOR ($0199): start the motor-off ticker. On at $259D."},
        "412": {"synopsis":"DD_L_OFF_MOTOR ($019C): motor off. On at $259D."},
        "415": {"synopsis":"Entry $019F, not in the API document: not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A\n(rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "418": {"synopsis":"IDE_IDENTIFY ($01A2): the IDE drive's identity. Here not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives\nerror $3A (rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "421": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITIONS ($01A5): the number of open partitions. On at $1F8A (the routine there\ncarries\nthe call's name)."},
        "424": {"synopsis":"Entry $01A8, not in the API document: not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A\n(rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "427": {"synopsis":"Entry $01AB, not in the API document: not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A\n(rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "430": {"synopsis":"Entry $01AE, not in the API document: not implemented: NOT_IMPLEMENTED gives error $3A\n(rc_notimp), carry clear."},
        "433": {"synopsis":"IDE_PATH ($01B1): change, get, make or delete a directory. On to IDE_PATH ($0527)."},
        "436": {"synopsis":"IDE_CAPACITY ($01B4): a card's capacity. On to IDE_CAPACITY ($01E0)."},
        "439": {"synopsis":"IDE_GET_LFN ($01B7): a long filename. On to IDE_GET_LFN ($020B)."},
        "442": {"synopsis":"IDE_BROWSER ($01BA): the file browser. On at $10C6 (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "445": {"synopsis":"IDE_BANK ($01BD): allocate or free 8K banks. On at $0E9F (the routine there carries the\ncall's\nname)."},
        "448": {"synopsis":"IDE_BASIC ($01C0): run a BASIC command line. On at $0F9D (the routine there carries the\ncall's\nname)."},
        "451": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_LINEIN ($01C3): input a line from the window stream. On at $159E (the routine\nthere\ncarries the call's name)."},
        "454": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_STRING ($01C6): a string to the window stream. On at $15A8 (the routine there\ncarries the call's name)."},
        "457": {"synopsis":"IDE_INTEGER_VAR ($01C9): get or set a NextBASIC integer variable. On at $0FB8 (the routine\nthere carries the call's name)."},
        "460": {"synopsis":"IDE_RTC ($01CC): the real-time clock. On at $0FEF (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "463": {"synopsis":"IDE_DRIVER ($01CF): the driver API. On at $0FF7 (the routine there carries the call's name)."},
        "466": {"synopsis":"IDE_MOUNT ($01D2): unmount or remount the SD cards. On at $1A75 (the routine there carries\nthe\ncall's name)."},
        "469": {"synopsis":"IDE_MODE ($01D5): NextBASIC display mode. On at $0FFD (the routine there carries the call's\nname)."},
        "472": {"synopsis":"IDE_TOKENISER ($01D8): BASIC between plain text and tokens. On at $1080 (the routine there\ncarries the call's name)."},
        "475": {"synopsis":"IDE_DRIVE (from $00A9; also from PREC_FILL at $077E): the DivMMC memory's $0103 with\nselector\n0,\nevery register as given. The document gives only its name (\"get unit handle\").","comment":"DivMMC $0103, selector 0"},
        "480": {"synopsis":"IDE_CAPACITY (from $01B4): the DivMMC memory's $0106 with A = C, the unit.\nEntry: C = the unit, 0 or 1 (manual).\nExit: carry and DEHL = the card's size in 512-byte sectors; or carry clear and A = the\nerror.","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "481": {"comment":"DivMMC $0106"},
        "486": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_FIND (from $00B5): the DivMMC memory's $0109, registers as given.","comment":"DivMMC $0109"},
        "491": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ (from $00C4; also PART_MAP at $0752 with A = the unit, BC = the entry,\nHL = $F712): the DivMMC memory's $010C, registers as given.","comment":"DivMMC $010C"},
        "496": {"synopsis":"DOS_FREE_SPACE (from $0121): the drive letter in A made 0-15 (DRIVE_INDEX, error $16\notherwise), then the DivMMC memory's $0118.\nEntry: A = the drive, 'A'-'P' (manual).\nExit: carry, HL = the free space in K (at most 65535), BCDE the same unclamped; or carry\nclear\nand A = the error.","comment":"A = the drive 0-15, or error $16"},
        "499": {"comment":"DivMMC $0118"},
        "504": {"synopsis":"DOS_FLUSH (from $0142): the drive letter in A made 0-15 (DRIVE_INDEX, error $16 otherwise),\nthen the DivMMC memory's $011B.","comment":"A = the drive 0-15, or error $16"},
        "507": {"comment":"DivMMC $011B"},
        "512": {"synopsis":"DOS_CATALOG (from $011E): A (the sort/filter mode) kept in IX's low byte while the name\nat HL goes through the DivMMC memory's $034F (NAME_PREP), then its $017B.\nEntry: B = entries in the buffer, C = the filter, A = the sort mode, DE = the buffer, HL =\nthe name, wildcards allowed (manual).\nExit: carry, B = the entries filled, HL = the directory handle; or carry clear and A = the\nerror.","comment":"Sort/filter mode kept in IX's low byte"},
        "514": {"comment":"The name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "518": {"comment":"DivMMC $017B"},
        "519": {"synopsis":"The call byte of the RST $08 at $0206 (DOS_CATALOG). The JP $0207 at $0D44 is not a jump to here: it is\nZX81 code copied to $F000 (ZX8081_START), jumping into the ZX81 ROM."},
        "523": {"synopsis":"IDE_GET_LFN (from $01B7): the name at HL through the DivMMC memory's $034F, then its $017E.\nEntry: HL = the filespec given to DOS_CATALOG, IX = its handle, DE = the entry, BC = a\n261-byte buffer (manual).\nExit: carry, the long name at BC ended by $FF, BC = the date, DE = the time, HLIX = the\nsize;\nor carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "527": {"comment":"DivMMC $017E"},
        "532": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_ATTRIBUTES (from $0148): the name at HL through the DivMMC memory's $034F, then its\n$018A.","comment":"The name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "536": {"comment":"DivMMC $018A"},
        "541": {"synopsis":"Deletes the file named at HL: the name through the DivMMC memory's $034F, then its $0184\n(from DOS_OPEN at $0377, the old .BAK file, and from $2813 and $281E, which DOS_DELETE\nreaches).","comment":"The name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "545": {"comment":"DivMMC $0184"},
        "550": {"synopsis":"DOS_REF_HEAD (from $010F): the DivMMC memory's $013F with A = B, the file number.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "551": {"comment":"DivMMC $013F"},
        "556": {"synopsis":"DOS_BYTE_READ (from $0118): the DivMMC memory's $0148 with A = B, the file number. Also from\nDOS_READ, a byte at a time.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "557": {"comment":"DivMMC $0148"},
        "562": {"synopsis":"DOS_BYTE_WRITE (from $011B): the DivMMC memory's $014B with A = B, the file number. Also\nfrom\nDOS_WRITE, a byte at a time.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "563": {"comment":"DivMMC $014B"},
        "568": {"synopsis":"DOS_GET_POSITION (from $0133): the DivMMC memory's $014E with A = B, the file number.\nExit: carry and DEHL = the file pointer (manual); or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "569": {"comment":"DivMMC $014E"},
        "574": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_POSITION (from $0136): the DivMMC memory's $0151 with A = B, the file number, and D\n=\n0, so that the pointer is E:HL.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "575": {"comment":"Top byte 0: the pointer is E:HL"},
        "577": {"comment":"DivMMC $0151"},
        "582": {"synopsis":"DOS_GET_EOF (from $0139): the DivMMC memory's $0154 with A = B, the file number.\nExit: carry and DEHL = the end of the file (manual); or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "583": {"comment":"DivMMC $0154"},
        "588": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_ACCESS (from $0145): an access mode C over 7 gives error $1E (rc_denied in the\ndocument's list); otherwise the DivMMC memory's $0157 with A = B, the file number.","comment":"Access mode over 7?"},
        "591": {"comment":"Then error $1E, carry clear"},
        "594": {"comment":"A = the file number"},
        "595": {"comment":"DivMMC $0157"},
        "600": {"synopsis":"DOS_CLOSE (from $0109): the DivMMC memory's $0175 with A = B, the file number, on a stack\njust\nbelow $F505 (the caller's SP kept at $F505).","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "601": {"comment":"Caller's SP kept at $F505"},
        "605": {"comment":"A stack below $F505"},
        "608": {"comment":"DivMMC $0175"},
        "612": {"comment":"Caller's stack back"},
        "617": {"synopsis":"DOS_ABANDON (from $010C): the DivMMC memory's $0178 with A = B, the file number, on a stack\njust\nbelow $F505 (the caller's SP kept at $F505).","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "618": {"comment":"Caller's SP kept at $F505"},
        "622": {"comment":"A stack below $F505"},
        "625": {"comment":"DivMMC $0178"},
        "629": {"comment":"Caller's stack back"},
        "634": {"synopsis":"DOS_READ (from $0112): DE bytes of file B read to HL.\n1. Below $4000 (where the DivMMC memory sits during a DivMMC call): a byte at a time through\nDOS_BYTE_READ, the bytes not stored by this routine.\n2. From $4000 on: one call of READ_BLOCK, or, when the bytes run past $FFFF, the part up to\n$FFFF in one block and the rest from $0000 a byte at a time (DRD_WRAP).\nEntry: B = the file, C = the 16K RAM page for $C000 (manual), DE = the count, HL = the\naddress.\nExit: carry and A = 0; or carry clear, A = the error, DE = the bytes not read, HL where it\nstopped (DRW_ERROR).","comment":"Address at $4000 or above?"},
        "637": {"comment":"Then in one block"},
        "639": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "642": {"comment":"One byte read (DOS_BYTE_READ)"},
        "645": {"comment":"Registers back: the byte dropped"},
        "648": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "650": {"comment":"Next address"},
        "651": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "652": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "656": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "658": {"synopsis":"From $4000 on: the whole count in one block, unless it runs past $FFFF.","comment":"Start kept"},
        "659": {"comment":"HL = the last address"},
        "661": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "662": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "664": {"comment":"HL = past the end"},
        "665": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the start"},
        "666": {"comment":"All DE bytes in one call"},
        "669": {"synopsis":"After the block (DOS_WRITE's too): HL = past the end; A = 0 and carry when it worked.","comment":"HL = past the end"},
        "670": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "672": {"comment":"A = 0, carry: done"},
        "675": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes of file B to HL through the DivMMC memory's $0142, A = B.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "676": {"comment":"DivMMC $0142"},
        "681": {"synopsis":"Runs past $FFFF: the part up to $FFFF in one block, then the rest from $0000 by DOS_READ's\nbyte loop.","comment":"HL = the start"},
        "682": {"comment":"Count and start kept"},
        "684": {"comment":"DE = $10000 - start: the first part"},
        "692": {"comment":"HL = the count, start kept"},
        "694": {"comment":"The rest past $FFFF"},
        "697": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the start"},
        "698": {"comment":"Start, first part and file kept"},
        "701": {"comment":"The first part in one block"},
        "704": {"comment":"BC back; HL = the first part's size"},
        "706": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "708": {"comment":"HL = start + part: $0000"},
        "710": {"comment":"DE = the rest"},
        "711": {"comment":"The rest byte by byte"},
        "713": {"synopsis":"A block failed while past $FFFF: HL = where it stopped, DE = all the bytes not moved, then\nDRW_ERROR.","comment":"HL = the bytes of the part done"},
        "715": {"comment":"HL = where it stopped"},
        "717": {"comment":"BC = the rest past $FFFF"},
        "718": {"comment":"DE = all bytes left"},
        "721": {"synopsis":"The end of a failed DOS_READ or DOS_WRITE: A = the error, carry clear, Z when DE (the bytes\nleft) is 0.","comment":"Error code kept"},
        "722": {"comment":"Z when no bytes are left"},
        "724": {"comment":"A = the error, carry clear"},
        "726": {"synopsis":"DOS_WRITE (from $0115): DE bytes from HL written to file B, as DOS_READ: below $4000 a\nbyte at a time through DOS_BYTE_WRITE, from $4000 on in one block (WRITE_BLOCK), split at\n$FFFF (DWR_WRAP).\nExit: as DOS_READ.","comment":"Address at $4000 or above?"},
        "729": {"comment":"Then in one block"},
        "731": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "734": {"comment":"C = the byte to write"},
        "735": {"comment":"Written (DOS_BYTE_WRITE)"},
        "738": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "741": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "743": {"comment":"Next address"},
        "744": {"comment":"One byte fewer"},
        "745": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "749": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "751": {"synopsis":"From $4000 on: the whole count in one block, unless it runs past $FFFF.","comment":"Start kept"},
        "752": {"comment":"HL = the last address"},
        "754": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "755": {"comment":"Past $FFFF?"},
        "757": {"comment":"HL = past the end"},
        "758": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the start"},
        "759": {"comment":"All DE bytes in one call"},
        "762": {"comment":"Ends as DOS_READ's block"},
        "764": {"synopsis":"Writes DE bytes from HL to file B through the DivMMC memory's $0145, A = B.","comment":"A = the file number"},
        "765": {"comment":"DivMMC $0145"},
        "770": {"synopsis":"Runs past $FFFF: the part up to $FFFF in one block, then the rest from $0000 by\nDOS_WRITE's byte loop.","comment":"HL = the start"},
        "771": {"comment":"Count and start kept"},
        "773": {"comment":"DE = $10000 - start: the first part"},
        "781": {"comment":"HL = the count, start kept"},
        "783": {"comment":"The rest past $FFFF"},
        "786": {"comment":"Kept; HL = the start"},
        "787": {"comment":"Start, first part and file kept"},
        "790": {"comment":"The first part in one block"},
        "793": {"comment":"BC back; HL = the first part's size"},
        "795": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "797": {"comment":"HL = start + part: $0000"},
        "799": {"comment":"DE = the rest"},
        "800": {"comment":"The rest byte by byte"},
        "802": {"synopsis":"DOS_OPEN (from $0106; also from IDE_SNAPLOAD at $0871 and others).\n1. Bit 3 of C (the metadata file, manual): OPEN_META.\n2. Open action 3 (to .BAK, manual) when bit 0 of byte $314A in DivMMC bank 7 is set: action\n4 (erase) instead. Otherwise the file is first created with open action 0; if it exists\nalready (error $18), its name is copied to $FF00 with the type replaced by \"bak\" (or\n\".bak\" added when the type is over three characters or there is no dot), that file is\ndeleted (DELETE_FILE, its error ignored) and the file renamed to it (RENAME_FILE).\n3. OPEN_FILE.\nEntry: B = the file 0-15, C = the access mode, D = the create action, E = the open action,\nHL = the name (manual).\nExit: carry, Z when the file was created; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The metadata file, if bit 3 asks"},
        "805": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "806": {"comment":"Open action 3 (to .BAK)?"},
        "809": {"comment":"No: open as asked"},
        "811": {"comment":"Name kept"},
        "812": {"comment":"Byte $314A of DivMMC bank 7"},
        "815": {"comment":"DivMMC $001D, selector 7"},
        "819": {"comment":"Name back"},
        "820": {"comment":"Open action 4: erase instead"},
        "821": {"comment":"Bit 0 set?"},
        "822": {"comment":"Then open with action 4"},
        "824": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "827": {"comment":"Open action 0: a new file only"},
        "829": {"comment":"Try to create it"},
        "832": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "835": {"comment":"Created: done"},
        "836": {"comment":"An error other than $18 (exists)?"},
        "838": {"comment":"Then carry clear, A = the error"},
        "841": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "844": {"comment":"No dot seen yet"},
        "846": {"comment":"The name copied to $FF00"},
        "849": {"comment":"Start of the copy kept"},
        "850": {"synopsis":"One character of the name, up to and with the $FF.","comment":"Next character"},
        "854": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "858": {"comment":"BC = just past it"},
        "860": {"synopsis":"Until the $FF.","comment":"The $FF?"},
        "863": {"comment":"HL = the type's length"},
        "868": {"comment":"Three characters or fewer?"},
        "874": {"comment":"Then DE = just past the dot"},
        "876": {"synopsis":"\".bak\" and $FF over the dot and type, or over the $FF.","comment":"DE = the dot, or the $FF"},
        "877": {"comment":"\".bak\" and $FF (BAK_EXT_TEXT)"},
        "885": {"comment":"HL = the .bak name"},
        "887": {"comment":"An old .bak file deleted"},
        "890": {"comment":"DE = the .bak name"},
        "891": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "893": {"comment":"The file renamed to .bak"},
        "896": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "899": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "900": {"synopsis":"Opens file B: IX = $DBD0 + 56 x B (probably the file's 56-byte record), the name at HL\nthrough the DivMMC memory's $034F, then its $0172 on a stack below $F505. An access mode C\nover 7 gives error $1E.","comment":"Access mode over 7?"},
        "903": {"comment":"Error $1E then"},
        "906": {"comment":"Actions kept"},
        "907": {"comment":"IX = $DBD0 + 56 x the file number"},
        "919": {"comment":"Actions back"},
        "920": {"comment":"The name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "924": {"comment":"Caller's SP kept at $F505"},
        "928": {"comment":"A stack below $F505"},
        "931": {"comment":"DivMMC $0172"},
        "935": {"comment":"Caller's stack back"},
        "940": {"synopsis":"DOS_OPEN's bit 3 of C (open the file's metadata file, manual): bit 3 cleared, $2867 called\n(and $28DD too when bit 1 of C, write access, is set), and the actions become D = 2, E = 2\n(no header).\nExit: carry to go on; carry clear and A = the error. With bit 3 clear: carry at once.","comment":"Metadata file asked?"},
        "942": {"comment":"No: carry, go on"},
        "944": {"comment":"Bit 3 off"},
        "946": {"comment":"Access mode kept"},
        "947": {"comment":"Probably the metadata file's name"},
        "950": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "952": {"comment":"Access mode again"},
        "954": {"comment":"Write access? Then $28DD too"},
        "959": {"synopsis":"Open and create actions 2: no header.","comment":"Access mode back"},
        "960": {"comment":"Actions 2 and 2: no header"},
        "964": {"synopsis":"The flags byte of drive A (0-15): the byte at $2310 + A in the DivMMC memory, selector 0,\ndoubled. Bit 7 set means the drive is not mapped (IDE_DOS_MAP refuses a drive with it\nclear), bit 6 that it has user areas (DOS_SET_USER). Also from ROM 1's SD_LIST_DRIVES.\nExit: A = the byte x 2, carry = its bit 7, sign = its bit 6.","comment":"HL = $2310 + the drive"},
        "969": {"comment":"DivMMC $001D: A = the byte there"},
        "973": {"comment":"Carry = bit 7, sign = bit 6"},
        "975": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_MAP (from $00F1).\n1. Drive letter L made 0-15 (DRIVE_INDEX); a drive already mapped gives error $3E\n(rc_mapped).\n2. Unit A not $FF: the DivMMC memory's $0169 with A = the drive, D = the unit, BC = the\npartition.\n3. Unit $FF, an image file named at BC: DMAP_IMAGE.\nEntry: A = the unit (4 the RAMdisk, $FF an image file), BC = the partition or the image's\nname, L = the drive letter (manual).\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"D = the unit"},
        "976": {"comment":"The drive letter"},
        "977": {"comment":"A = 0-15, or error $16"},
        "980": {"comment":"E = the drive"},
        "981": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "984": {"comment":"Error $3E: mapped already"},
        "986": {"comment":"Bit 7 clear: mapped"},
        "987": {"comment":"Unit $FF: an image file?"},
        "992": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "993": {"comment":"DivMMC $0169: drive A to unit D, BC"},
        "998": {"synopsis":"An image file: 256 bytes of its name from BC to $3000 + 256 x the drive through the DivMMC\nmemory's $0703 with A = 9 (probably into DivMMC bank 9), then $2224 with BC = the name; then\neach byte of the 14 at $2302 (DivMMC memory, selector 0) with bit 7 clear and unlike the one\nbefore is tried: the DivMMC memory's $0169 with D = $80 + 16 - B ($82-$8F) and BC = $F75F.\nError $09 (rc_unsuit) moves on to the next; another error ends it. At the end of the list\nthe record at (IX+$11) is wiped (WIPE_REC_IX) and error $09 given.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "1001": {"comment":"HL = the image's name"},
        "1003": {"comment":"D = $30 + the drive"},
        "1007": {"comment":"E = 0: DE = $3000 + 256 x drive"},
        "1009": {"comment":"256 bytes"},
        "1012": {"comment":"A = 9"},
        "1014": {"comment":"DivMMC $0703, selector 0"},
        "1018": {"comment":"BC = the name"},
        "1019": {"comment":"Probably opens the image"},
        "1022": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "1024": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1025": {"comment":"Caller's HL kept"},
        "1026": {"comment":"The 14 bytes at $2302"},
        "1029": {"comment":"B = 14; C = $FF, none tried yet"},
        "1032": {"synopsis":"The next byte of the list at $2302.","comment":"DivMMC $001D: A = the byte at HL"},
        "1036": {"comment":"Next one"},
        "1037": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: skip"},
        "1041": {"comment":"Same as the last one: skip"},
        "1044": {"comment":"Kept as the last one"},
        "1045": {"comment":"A = $80 + 16 - B"},
        "1050": {"comment":"List pointer kept, caller's HL back"},
        "1051": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "1056": {"comment":"D = $82-$8F"},
        "1057": {"comment":"BC = $F75F"},
        "1060": {"comment":"DivMMC $0169: map the drive"},
        "1064": {"comment":"Registers back"},
        "1069": {"comment":"Caller's HL kept, pointer back"},
        "1070": {"comment":"Mapped?"},
        "1072": {"comment":"Error $09 (unsuitable)?"},
        "1074": {"comment":"Another error: give it"},
        "1076": {"synopsis":"The next byte, until 14 are done; then the record wiped and error $09.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "1078": {"comment":"None fitted: record wiped"},
        "1081": {"comment":"Error $09"},
        "1083": {"synopsis":"Carry clear: A = the error.","comment":"Carry clear"},
        "1084": {"comment":"Caller's HL back"},
        "1086": {"synopsis":"Mapped: the word at (IX+$11) stored as the drive's word in the table at $E438.","comment":"Caller's HL back"},
        "1087": {"comment":"BC = the word at IX+$11"},
        "1093": {"comment":"HL = $E438 + 2 x the drive"},
        "1100": {"comment":"The word stored there"},
        "1103": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1105": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_UNMAP (from $00F4): drive letter L made 0-15 (DRIVE_INDEX), then the DivMMC\nmemory's $016C. Error $16 (no drive) counts as done. When it worked and the drive's word in\nthe table at $E438 is not 0, the word is cleared and the record it points at wiped\n(WIPE_REC_DE).\nEntry: L = the drive letter (manual).\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The drive letter"},
        "1106": {"comment":"A = 0-15, or error $16"},
        "1109": {"comment":"Drive kept"},
        "1110": {"comment":"DivMMC $016C"},
        "1114": {"comment":"D = the drive"},
        "1115": {"comment":"Unmapped?"},
        "1117": {"comment":"Error $16 (no drive)?"},
        "1119": {"comment":"Then carry: nothing to do"},
        "1121": {"comment":"Other errors: carry clear"},
        "1123": {"synopsis":"The drive's word in the table at $E438 cleared and its record wiped.","comment":"HL = $E438 + 2 x the drive"},
        "1130": {"comment":"DE = the drive's word"},
        "1133": {"comment":"None?"},
        "1135": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "1137": {"comment":"The word cleared"},
        "1141": {"comment":"The record at DE wiped"},
        "1144": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_MAPPING (from $00F7).\n1. The drive letter (L AND $7F) made 0-15 (DRIVE_INDEX); $F700 = $FF.\n2. The DivMMC memory's $011E, which leaves the text at $F700. For an image file (unit\n$FF) the text is built here instead: \"Mount=\" from $1FFD, then the image's name from\n$3000 + 256 x the drive in DivMMC bank 9 (its $0769), ended by $FF; BC = 0.\n3. The text copied to the buffer: L under $80, 18 bytes padded with spaces; L with bit 7,\nup to its $FF.\nEntry: L = the drive letter (+$80 for the long text), BC = the buffer (manual).\nExit: carry, Z clear, A = the unit, BC = the partition; carry and Z when the drive is not\nmapped (error $16 turned into that); otherwise carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The letter (+$80: the long text)"},
        "1145": {"comment":"Letter and buffer kept"},
        "1147": {"comment":"Letter only"},
        "1149": {"comment":"A = 0-15, or error $16"},
        "1152": {"comment":"$F700 = $FF: no text yet"},
        "1160": {"comment":"DivMMC $011E: the mapping"},
        "1164": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1166": {"comment":"Unit $FF (an image file)?"},
        "1169": {"comment":"Letter back, both kept again"},
        "1173": {"comment":"\"Mount=\" from $1FFD to $F700"},
        "1184": {"comment":"The letter made 0-15"},
        "1189": {"comment":"HL = $3000 + 256 x the drive"},
        "1194": {"comment":"At most $F9 bytes"},
        "1196": {"comment":"A = 9"},
        "1198": {"comment":"DivMMC $0769: the image's name"},
        "1202": {"comment":"Ended by $FF"},
        "1205": {"comment":"BC = 0: no partition"},
        "1208": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "1209": {"synopsis":"A = the unit back ($FF for an image file).","comment":"A = the unit back"},
        "1210": {"synopsis":"The text from $F700 into the caller's buffer, unless there was an error.","comment":"DE = the buffer, H = the letter"},
        "1212": {"comment":"Result kept"},
        "1214": {"comment":"Error: no text"},
        "1216": {"comment":"No limit for the long text"},
        "1218": {"comment":"Long text ($80 + letter)?"},
        "1221": {"comment":"The text at $F700"},
        "1226": {"comment":"Short text: 18 bytes"},
        "1228": {"synopsis":"One character, until the $FF or the limit.","comment":"Next character"},
        "1230": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "1234": {"comment":"Into the buffer"},
        "1236": {"comment":"Until the limit"},
        "1238": {"synopsis":"Long text: ended by $FF; short: padded with spaces.","comment":"Long text?"},
        "1241": {"comment":"Then ended by $FF"},
        "1246": {"synopsis":"Any room left in the 18 bytes?","comment":"Any room left?"},
        "1250": {"comment":"Padded with spaces"},
        "1252": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "1256": {"synopsis":"Result back: Z clear on success; error $16 becomes carry and Z (not mapped).","comment":"Result back"},
        "1258": {"comment":"Z clear: mapped"},
        "1261": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1262": {"comment":"Error $16 (no drive)?"},
        "1264": {"comment":"Then carry and Z: not mapped"},
        "1266": {"comment":"Other errors: carry clear"},
        "1268": {"synopsis":"WIPE_REC_DE for the record whose address is the word at (IX+$11).","comment":"DE = the word at IX+$11"},
        "1274": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $04DB (selector 0) with HL = DE, DE = DE + 1 and BC = 5: an overlapping\ncopy, so probably the first byte's value spread over six bytes from DE ($04DB sits just\nbefore $04DD, MMC1_COPY's copy routine).\nExit: carry set.","comment":"HL = DE"},
        "1276": {"comment":"DE = DE + 1"},
        "1277": {"comment":"5 more bytes"},
        "1280": {"comment":"DivMMC $04DB"},
        "1284": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "1286": {"synopsis":"Into the directory named at HL (ROM 0's BRW_CD_HL): the name through the DivMMC memory's\n$034F, then CD_DRIVE_USER with the drive and user area it gives.\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"A = user x 16 + drive of the name"},
        "1290": {"synopsis":"With A = user area x 16 + drive (from $1C87 and $1C96 too): the drive made the default\n(SET_DRIVE_IDX), the user area made the default (DOS_SET_USER), then the path at HL made\nthe current one (IDE_PATH with reason 0).","comment":"Kept"},
        "1292": {"comment":"The drive"},
        "1294": {"comment":"Made the default"},
        "1297": {"comment":"HL back, D = user and drive"},
        "1299": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1300": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "1303": {"comment":"The user area"},
        "1307": {"comment":"Made the default (DOS_SET_USER)"},
        "1310": {"comment":"HL back, D = user and drive"},
        "1312": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1313": {"comment":"A = user and drive"},
        "1314": {"comment":"Reason 0: change the path"},
        "1316": {"comment":"Path kept"},
        "1319": {"synopsis":"IDE_PATH (from $01B1).\n1. The pathspec through the DivMMC memory's $034F.\n2. PATH_CALL: the DivMMC memory's $0181 with B = the reason and DE = $FF00, on a stack below\n$F505.\n3. Reason 1 (get the path): the $FF-ended text at HL, as $034F left HL, copied over the\ncaller's buffer.\nEntry: A = the reason: 0 change, 1 get, 2 make, 3 delete; HL = the pathspec ended by $FF\n(manual).\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"B = the reason"},
        "1320": {"comment":"Pathspec kept"},
        "1322": {"comment":"The name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "1326": {"comment":"Reason back"},
        "1327": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $0181 with DE = $FF00, then for reason 1 the path copied.","comment":"DE = $FF00"},
        "1330": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "1332": {"comment":"Caller's SP kept at $F505"},
        "1336": {"comment":"A stack below $F505"},
        "1339": {"comment":"DivMMC $0181"},
        "1343": {"comment":"Caller's stack back"},
        "1347": {"comment":"Registers back; DE = the pathspec"},
        "1350": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1351": {"comment":"Reason 1 (get the path)?"},
        "1352": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "1353": {"synopsis":"One character, up to and with the $FF.","comment":"Next character"},
        "1354": {"comment":"Into the caller's buffer"},
        "1356": {"comment":"The $FF?"},
        "1360": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_DRIVE (from $012D): A = $FF just gets the default drive; otherwise the letter made\n0-15 (DRIVE_INDEX, error $16) and passed to SET_DRIVE_IDX.\nExit: carry and A = the default drive's letter; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"$FF: just get the default?"},
        "1362": {"comment":"A = 0-15, or error $16"},
        "1365": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $016F with A = the drive 0-15 or $FF, its answer made a letter (from\nCD_DRIVE_USER too).\nExit: carry and A = the default drive's letter; or carry clear and A =\nthe error.","comment":"DivMMC $016F"},
        "1369": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1370": {"comment":"A = the drive's letter"},
        "1374": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_USER (from $0130; CD_DRIVE_USER too): A = the user area, $FF to get it.\n1. The default drive (the DivMMC memory's $016F with $FF), and its flags (DRIVE_FLAGS).\n2. Bit 6 clear (no user areas): $FF gives 0, 0 is accepted, others give error $14.\n3. Bit 6 set: SETUSR_AREAS.\nExit: carry and A = the user area; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The user area asked"},
        "1375": {"comment":"Just get the default drive"},
        "1377": {"comment":"DivMMC $016F"},
        "1381": {"comment":"D = the user area asked"},
        "1382": {"comment":"E = the drive"},
        "1383": {"comment":"Its flags"},
        "1386": {"comment":"Bit 6 set: user areas"},
        "1389": {"comment":"Only user 0 here"},
        "1390": {"comment":"$FF (just get)?"},
        "1393": {"comment":"0?"},
        "1395": {"comment":"Error $14 otherwise"},
        "1399": {"synopsis":"A drive with user areas: the DivMMC memory's $0124 with A = the drive gives the area; to set\none, user x 16 + drive is written at $2001 + 256 x the drive and its complement at $2000 +\n256 x the drive, both in DivMMC bank 9 (selector 9, its $02E0).","comment":"Drive kept"},
        "1400": {"comment":"A = the drive"},
        "1401": {"comment":"DivMMC $0124"},
        "1405": {"comment":"Drive back"},
        "1406": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1407": {"comment":"$FF: just get, A = the area"},
        "1409": {"comment":"H = $20 + the drive"},
        "1413": {"comment":"L = 1"},
        "1415": {"comment":"D = the user area"},
        "1416": {"comment":"A = user x 16 + drive"},
        "1420": {"comment":"DivMMC $02E0, selector 9: A to HL"},
        "1424": {"comment":"Its complement"},
        "1425": {"comment":"At $2000 + 256 x the drive"},
        "1430": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1432": {"synopsis":"Renames the file named at HL to the name at DE: both names through the DivMMC memory's\n$034F (B = what the first gives), then its $0187 on a stack below $F505 (from DOS_OPEN at\n$037D, and two more callers).","comment":"First name through DivMMC $034F"},
        "1436": {"comment":"Its answer kept"},
        "1437": {"comment":"The second name"},
        "1438": {"comment":"Through DivMMC $034F"},
        "1442": {"comment":"Names back in place"},
        "1443": {"comment":"B = the first name's answer"},
        "1444": {"comment":"Caller's SP kept at $F505"},
        "1448": {"comment":"A stack below $F505"},
        "1451": {"comment":"DivMMC $0187"},
        "1455": {"comment":"Caller's stack back"},
        "1460": {"synopsis":"Drive letter A (either case) made 0-15 for 'A'-'P'. Any other value drops the caller's\nreturn address, so that the caller itself ends with error $16 (rc_nodrive).\nExit: A = 0-15, carry set.","comment":"Capital letter"},
        "1462": {"comment":"A = 0 for 'A'"},
        "1464": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "1466": {"comment":"Up to 'P'?"},
        "1469": {"synopsis":"Not a drive: the caller's caller gets error $16.","comment":"Drop the caller's return"},
        "1470": {"comment":"Error $16 (no drive)"},
        "1472": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "1474": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at HL in the DivMMC memory with selector $0D (its $001D). Nothing in pages\n0-3 calls it.","comment":"DivMMC $001D, selector $0D"},
        "1479": {"synopsis":"A written at HL in the DivMMC memory with selector 0 (its $02E0). Nothing in pages 0-3\ncalls it.","comment":"DivMMC $02E0, selector 0"},
        "1484": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $04DD (the copy of MMC1_COPY) with the selector taken from the low four\nbits of the byte at $2006 (DivMMC memory, selector 0); HL handed over in $5B52 and the call\nentered at $3F2A. Nothing in pages 0-3 calls it.","comment":"Caller's HL kept"},
        "1485": {"comment":"The byte at $2006"},
        "1488": {"comment":"DivMMC $001D, selector 0"},
        "1492": {"comment":"Low four bits: the selector"},
        "1494": {"comment":"HL handed over at $5B52"},
        "1498": {"comment":"DivMMC $04DD"},
        "1501": {"comment":"Into the DivMMC call, A the selector"},
        "1504": {"synopsis":"DOS_GET_1346 (from $013C; also $1CC1): the DivMMC memory's $34B6 with selector $0D.","comment":"DivMMC $34B6, selector $0D"},
        "1509": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_1346 (from $013F; also IDE_SNAPLOAD at $087B): the DivMMC memory's $34BC with\nselector $0D.","comment":"DivMMC $34BC, selector $0D"},
        "1514": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $344D with selector $0D (from $2417, A = a drive letter there).","comment":"DivMMC $344D, selector $0D"},
        "1519": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $34F4 with selector $0D (from $1CD9).","comment":"DivMMC $34F4, selector $0D"},
        "1524": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $03B2 with selector 0 and B = 2 (from $121A and $226B).","comment":"B = 2"},
        "1526": {"comment":"DivMMC $03B2, selector 0"},
        "1531": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $3432 with selector $0D. Nothing in pages 0-3 calls it.","comment":"DivMMC $3432, selector $0D"},
        "1536": {"synopsis":"The DivMMC memory's $3440 with selector $0D. Nothing in pages 0-3 calls it.","comment":"DivMMC $3440, selector $0D"},
        "1541": {"synopsis":"Finds an unused partition record: 20 records of 19 bytes from $E46C, unused when byte 0 is 0\n(from PART_MAP, $1700 and $234A).\nExit: carry and IX = the record; carry clear and A = $3C (rc_nohandle) when all are used.\nChanges: AF, E, IX.","comment":"The first record"},
        "1545": {"comment":"20 of them"},
        "1547": {"synopsis":"Is the record unused?","comment":"Unused?"},
        "1551": {"comment":"Then carry, IX = it"},
        "1553": {"comment":"Next record (19 bytes on)"},
        "1560": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "1563": {"comment":"Error $3C: none free"},
        "1567": {"synopsis":"Checks that entry BC of unit A (5 or 6) is not in any of the 20 partition records at $E46C:\na record in use whose byte $10 bit 0 is unit - 5 and whose bytes $11-$12 are BC.\nExit: carry when it is not; carry clear and A = $3B (rc_partopen) when it is.\nChanges: AF; BC, DE, HL and IX kept.","comment":"A = unit - 5"},
        "1569": {"comment":"Registers kept"},
        "1573": {"comment":"D = unit - 5"},
        "1574": {"comment":"The records"},
        "1580": {"synopsis":"Looks at one record.","comment":"In use?"},
        "1586": {"comment":"The same unit (bit 0 of +$10)?"},
        "1594": {"comment":"The same entry (+$11)?"},
        "1602": {"comment":"Error $3B: open already"},
        "1604": {"comment":"Found: carry clear"},
        "1606": {"synopsis":"Next record.","comment":"Next record (19 bytes on)"},
        "1613": {"comment":"Any left?"},
        "1616": {"comment":"None: carry"},
        "1617": {"synopsis":"Registers back.","comment":"Registers back"},
        "1622": {"synopsis":"Points IX at the record of unit A: $E458 for unit 5, $E462 for unit 6 (from\nPART_ENTRY_POS).\nExit: carry and IX = the record; carry clear and A = $16 when A is not 5 or 6 or the\nrecord's\nbytes 0-1 are zero.\nChanges: AF, IX.","comment":"A = unit - 5"},
        "1624": {"comment":"Below 5: carry clear"},
        "1627": {"comment":"Over 6?"},
        "1631": {"comment":"Carry = unit 6"},
        "1633": {"comment":"IX = $E458 for unit 5"},
        "1639": {"comment":"IX = $E462 for unit 6"},
        "1643": {"synopsis":"IX chosen; A = 0, so the error below is skipped.","comment":"Z: no error"},
        "1644": {"synopsis":"Error $16 when NZ (A not 5 or 6); otherwise bytes 0-1 checked.","comment":"Error $16"},
        "1647": {"comment":"Bytes 0-1 both zero?"},
        "1653": {"comment":"Error $16 then"},
        "1656": {"comment":"Carry: IX = the record"},
        "1658": {"synopsis":"By unit C: 5 and up go on at $17DE with C = unit - 5 and IX = $3135; 4 (the RAMdisk in the\ndocument's numbering) calls the DivMMC memory's $353D with selector $0D and gives H = D = E\n= 0, IX = $313B, carry; below 4, error $16. Nothing in pages 0-3 calls it.","comment":"C = unit - 5"},
        "1662": {"comment":"IX = $3135"},
        "1666": {"comment":"Unit 5 and up: on at $17DE"},
        "1669": {"comment":"Unit 4?"},
        "1671": {"comment":"Error $16 below 4"},
        "1675": {"comment":"DivMMC $353D, selector $0D"},
        "1679": {"comment":"H = D = E = 0"},
        "1683": {"comment":"IX = $313B"},
        "1687": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "1689": {"synopsis":"Finds where entry BC of unit A's partition table is.\nEntry: A = the unit (5 or 6), BC = the entry.\nExit: carry, IX = the word at +8 of the unit's record, DE = the block (entry / 8), BC = the\noffset in it ((entry AND 7) x 64); carry clear and A = $16 (no unit) or $38 (past the\nentries the record allows, its word at +6).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"IX = the unit's record"},
        "1692": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1693": {"comment":"The entry count at +6"},
        "1699": {"comment":"Entry BC beyond it?"},
        "1702": {"comment":"Error $38 then"},
        "1706": {"comment":"IX = the word at +8"},
        "1715": {"comment":"Entry kept"},
        "1716": {"comment":"BC / 8"},
        "1728": {"comment":"DE = the block"},
        "1730": {"comment":"Entry back"},
        "1731": {"comment":"BC = (entry AND 7) x 64"},
        "1743": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "1745": {"synopsis":"Copies the 64 bytes of entry BC of unit A's partition table to HL: its block read into $E090\nby IDE_SECTOR_READ's routine ($184A) with B = 7 and C = 0 (from PART_FIND_NAME).\nEntry: A = the unit, BC = the entry, HL = the destination.\nExit: carry; or carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL; BC and IX kept.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "1749": {"comment":"Where entry BC is"},
        "1752": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1754": {"comment":"Offset kept"},
        "1755": {"comment":"B = 7, C = 0"},
        "1758": {"comment":"Into $E090"},
        "1761": {"comment":"Read the block ($184A)"},
        "1764": {"comment":"Offset back"},
        "1765": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1767": {"comment":"HL = the entry in the block"},
        "1771": {"comment":"DE = the destination"},
        "1772": {"comment":"64 bytes"},
        "1777": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "1780": {"synopsis":"Drops the destination.","comment":"Drop the destination"},
        "1781": {"synopsis":"Registers back.","comment":"Registers back"},
        "1785": {"synopsis":"Looks through unit A's partition table for the entry whose bytes 0-15 match the 16 at HL,\nletters in either case. Nothing in pages 0-3 calls it (IDE_PARTITION_FIND goes to the DivMMC\nmemory instead).\nEntry: A = the unit, HL = the name.\nExit: carry, BC = the entry, $F712 = its 64 bytes; carry clear and A = the error ($38 when\nBC\nwraps round to 0).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"IX kept"},
        "1787": {"comment":"From entry 0"},
        "1790": {"synopsis":"Reads entry BC.","comment":"Unit, entry, name kept"},
        "1793": {"comment":"Entry BC into $F712"},
        "1799": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1801": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "1803": {"comment":"Its 16 bytes against the entry's"},
        "1808": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Same?"},
        "1812": {"comment":"A capital letter?"},
        "1820": {"synopsis":"Small letter?","comment":"A small letter?"},
        "1828": {"synopsis":"Matches in the other case?","comment":"Same in the other case?"},
        "1833": {"synopsis":"The next character, until 16 match.","comment":"Next character"},
        "1837": {"comment":"All 16 match: carry"},
        "1838": {"synopsis":"Registers back.","comment":"Name and entry back"},
        "1840": {"synopsis":"Drops the unit; IX back.","comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "1844": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Name and entry back"},
        "1846": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "1847": {"comment":"Wrapped round to 0?"},
        "1849": {"comment":"Error $38 then"},
        "1853": {"comment":"Unit back"},
        "1854": {"comment":"Try it"},
        "1856": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_OPEN (from $00CD; also $2184): maps entry BC of unit A's partition table into\nan\nunused partition record.\n1. Error $3B when it is open already (PART_NOT_MAPPED); IX = a free record (PART_REC_FREE).\n2. The entry read to $F712 (IDE_PARTITON_READ); type (byte $10) 0, $FE or $FF gives error\n   $38.\n3. PART_REC_UNIT, then PREC_FILL.\nExit: carry and IX = the record; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Unit kept"},
        "1857": {"comment":"Open already?"},
        "1860": {"comment":"Yes: error"},
        "1862": {"comment":"A free record?"},
        "1865": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1867": {"synopsis":"Drops the unit.","comment":"Drop the unit"},
        "1869": {"synopsis":"Reads the entry and checks its type.","comment":"A = the unit"},
        "1871": {"comment":"Entry BC into $F712"},
        "1877": {"comment":"Error?"},
        "1879": {"comment":"The type (byte $10)"},
        "1882": {"comment":"0, $FE or $FF?"},
        "1885": {"comment":"Error $38 then"},
        "1889": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "1890": {"comment":"Unit and entry into the record"},
        "1893": {"synopsis":"Fills partition record IX from the entry at $F712 (from PART_MAP and $1F69), interrupts off:\n1. Bytes 0-15 = entry bytes $10-$1F.\n2. IDE_DRIVE with C, B, D = record bytes 1-3.\n3. Bytes 1-4 = BC (from IDE_DRIVE) x the word at bytes 4-5, plus byte 3 x the D it gave;\nbytes 5-6 = 0. Probably the partition's first sector as one number.\nExit: carry.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; IX and IY kept.","comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "1894": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "1897": {"comment":"Entry bytes $10-$1F to bytes 0-15"},
        "1905": {"comment":"IY and the record kept"},
        "1909": {"comment":"C, B, D = bytes 1-3"},
        "1918": {"comment":"IDE_DRIVE's routine"},
        "1921": {"comment":"E = byte 3"},
        "1924": {"comment":"D (from IDE_DRIVE) and E kept"},
        "1925": {"comment":"IX = bytes 4-5: the count"},
        "1934": {"comment":"HL:IY = 0"},
        "1941": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "1943": {"synopsis":"HL:IY + BC, the count of times.","comment":"HL:IY + BC"},
        "1947": {"comment":"Count down"},
        "1955": {"comment":"B = that D, C = byte 3"},
        "1956": {"comment":"A = the times"},
        "1957": {"comment":"BC = byte 3"},
        "1959": {"comment":"None?"},
        "1962": {"synopsis":"HL:IY + byte 3, A times.","comment":"HL:IY + byte 3"},
        "1966": {"comment":"A times"},
        "1969": {"synopsis":"Bytes 1-4 = HL:IY, bytes 5-6 = 0.","comment":"IX = the record"},
        "1971": {"comment":"Bytes 1-2 = IY"},
        "1981": {"comment":"Bytes 3-4 = HL"},
        "1987": {"comment":"Bytes 5-6 = 0"},
        "1994": {"comment":"IY back"},
        "1996": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "1997": {"comment":"Done"},
        "1999": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_CLOSE (from $00D0): frees partition record IX, byte 0 = 0.\nExit: carry.","comment":"Record unused"},
        "2005": {"synopsis":"Fills bytes $10-$12 of partition record IX: unit - 5, with bit 1 set when $1A69 (A = unit -\n5, carry clear) gives carry, then BC (from PART_MAP and $1F15).\nEntry: A = the unit, BC = the entry, IX = the record.\nAF kept.","comment":"Unit kept"},
        "2006": {"comment":"Byte $10 = unit - 5"},
        "2011": {"comment":"Bytes $11-$12 = the entry"},
        "2017": {"comment":"Carry clear for $1A69"},
        "2018": {"comment":"Ask $1A69 about the unit"},
        "2021": {"comment":"No carry: bit 1 stays clear"},
        "2023": {"comment":"Bit 1 of byte $10 set"},
        "2027": {"synopsis":"Unit back.","comment":"Unit back"},
        "2029": {"synopsis":"A:DE = DE x B, the top byte gathered in A' (from $1603).\nExit: B = 0; A' kept.\nChanges: F, BC, HL.","comment":"HL = the multiplicand"},
        "2030": {"comment":"A' = 0, the old A' kept"},
        "2033": {"comment":"A:HL the multiplicand; DE = 0"},
        "2036": {"synopsis":"One bit of B.","comment":"Bit of B set?"},
        "2040": {"comment":"C = the multiplicand's top byte"},
        "2041": {"comment":"DE + HL, A' + C and the carry"},
        "2047": {"synopsis":"Doubles A:HL unless B is used up.","comment":"No bits left?"},
        "2049": {"comment":"A:HL doubled"},
        "2051": {"comment":"Next bit"},
        "2054": {"synopsis":"A = the top byte, A' back.","comment":"Old A' back"},
        "2057": {"synopsis":"The Multiface NMI by the M1 button enabled again (NextReg $06 bit 3) and the CPU speed\nkept at $5C93 restored to NextReg $07 (from IDE_SNAPLOAD's failed DOS_OPEN at $0874, and\nfrom $0AAA). AF kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "2058": {"comment":"NextReg $06"},
        "2061": {"comment":"Multiface NMI on again"},
        "2065": {"comment":"The CPU speed kept"},
        "2068": {"comment":"Restored"},
        "2073": {"synopsis":"21 bytes copied to $5D45-$5D59 by IDE_SNAPLOAD at $08A0: $00 $30 $00 $03, eight $00, $FF and\neight $00."},
        "2094": {"synopsis":"IDE_SNAPLOAD (from $00FD; ROM 1's $0133): loads and runs the snapshot named at HL.\n1. A one-letter type: \".O\" goes on at $0CA6 with carry clear, \".P\" with carry set.\n2. Otherwise the type's last character in capitals is kept at $5C92 (MEMBOT), the DivMMC\nand Multiface NMIs are disabled (NextReg $06 bits 4 and 3), the programmed CPU speed kept\nat $5C93 and made 28MHz.\n3. File 0 opened (DOS_OPEN, exclusive read, existing file only, no header); on failure\nSNAP_NMI_SPEED and the error.\n4. DOS_SET_1346 with HL = DE = 0; $5D00 non-zero when DOS_GET_EOF's top word is (64K or\nmore); ROM 1's RESET_DISPLAY ($14B9); the attributes and the border cleared, SNAP_VARS_INIT\nto $5D45,\nand on by the type at $08B3; the loader runs on to $0AB8 (lines from $0840 in the next\nrange).\nEntry: HL = the filespec ended by $FF (manual).\nExit: does not return when it works; otherwise carry clear and A = the error (manual).","comment":"DE = the filespec"},
        "2096": {"synopsis":"Looks for the name's $FF.","comment":"Up to the $FF"},
        "2102": {"comment":"DE = 2 before the $FF"},
        "2105": {"comment":"A dot there: a one-letter type?"},
        "2108": {"comment":"DE = the last character"},
        "2110": {"comment":"No dot: a longer type"},
        "2112": {"comment":"One-letter type, upper case"},
        "2114": {"comment":".O (a ZX80 program)? NC"},
        "2116": {"synopsis":"A .O or .P file (Z set): on to ZX8081_LOAD, carry set for .P.","comment":"To ZX8081_LOAD"},
        "2119": {"comment":".P (a ZX81 program)? Carry"},
        "2121": {"comment":"Carry for a .P"},
        "2122": {"comment":"To ZX8081_LOAD with carry"},
        "2124": {"synopsis":"Not a one-letter type: the snapshot kind is the type's last letter, $5C92 = it ANDed with\n$DF.","comment":"The last letter of the name, upper case"},
        "2127": {"comment":"Kept at $5C92: 'A' SNA, 'X' SNX, $10 Z80"},
        "2130": {"comment":"NextReg 6: DivMMC and Multiface NMIs off"},
        "2135": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "2137": {"comment":"The CPU speed (NextReg 7)"},
        "2142": {"comment":"Kept at $5C93 for $0809 to restore"},
        "2144": {"comment":"$5C93 = the old speed"},
        "2147": {"comment":"Never 4 or more after AND 3"},
        "2151": {"comment":"Loading at 28 MHz (NextReg 7 = 3)"},
        "2153": {"comment":"Written"},
        "2155": {"synopsis":"Opens the snapshot as file 0, frees RAM pages 1, 3, 4 and 6 (DOS_SET_1346 with no cache and\nno RAM disk), notes in $5D00 whether the file is 64K or longer, resets the display (ROM 1's\nRESET_DISPLAY) and blacks out the screen and border with interrupts off and SP = $5BFF. The\ndefaults at $0819 go to $5D45-$5D59.","comment":"File 0, read access"},
        "2158": {"comment":"D = 0, E = 2: open an existing file"},
        "2161": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN with HL = the filespec"},
        "2164": {"comment":"Not opened: speed and NMIs back, NC"},
        "2166": {"comment":"No disk cache, no RAM disk"},
        "2169": {"comment":"DE = 0 too"},
        "2171": {"comment":"DOS_SET_1346: frees RAM pages 1, 3, 4, 6"},
        "2174": {"comment":"File 0's length (DOS_GET_EOF)"},
        "2176": {"comment":"E HL = the length"},
        "2179": {"comment":"64K or more?"},
        "2181": {"comment":"Kept at $5D00 (non-zero: a 128K SNA/SNX)"},
        "2184": {"comment":"ROM 1's RESET_DISPLAY"},
        "2189": {"comment":"No interrupts from here on"},
        "2190": {"comment":"Stack below $5C00"},
        "2193": {"comment":"All attributes 0: the screen black"},
        "2202": {"comment":"Each byte 0"},
        "2205": {"comment":"Black border"},
        "2208": {"comment":"The defaults ($0819) to $5D45-$5D59"},
        "2217": {"comment":"21 bytes"},
        "2219": {"comment":"$5D79 (header byte 86) = 4 by default"},
        "2224": {"comment":"'A' or 'X' (bit 6 set): an SNA or SNX"},
        "2229": {"comment":"Z80: SNAP_Z80_HDR"},
        "2231": {"comment":"The SNA header's 27 bytes to $5D08"},
        "2234": {"comment":"27 bytes"},
        "2239": {"comment":"Read the header back off the stack"},
        "2242": {"comment":"A = I"},
        "2243": {"comment":"$5D2D = I"},
        "2246": {"comment":"HL'"},
        "2247": {"comment":"$5D36 = HL'"},
        "2250": {"comment":"DE'"},
        "2251": {"comment":"$5D34 = DE'"},
        "2254": {"comment":"BC'"},
        "2255": {"comment":"$5D32 = BC'"},
        "2258": {"comment":"AF'"},
        "2259": {"comment":"$5D38 = AF'"},
        "2262": {"comment":"HL"},
        "2263": {"comment":"$5D27 = HL"},
        "2266": {"comment":"DE"},
        "2267": {"comment":"$5D30 = DE"},
        "2270": {"comment":"BC"},
        "2271": {"comment":"$5D25 = BC"},
        "2274": {"comment":"IY"},
        "2275": {"comment":"$5D3A = IY"},
        "2278": {"comment":"IX"},
        "2279": {"comment":"$5D3C = IX"},
        "2282": {"comment":"L = the interrupt byte, H = R"},
        "2283": {"comment":"Bit 2: interrupts enabled"},
        "2288": {"comment":"$5D3E = 1 with interrupts enabled"},
        "2291": {"comment":"R"},
        "2295": {"comment":"AF"},
        "2296": {"comment":"$5D23 = AF"},
        "2299": {"comment":"SP"},
        "2300": {"comment":"$5D2B = SP"},
        "2303": {"comment":"L = the interrupt mode, H = the border"},
        "2305": {"comment":"$5D40 = the interrupt mode"},
        "2308": {"comment":"Border in bits 3-1, as in the Z80 flags byte"},
        "2310": {"comment":"$5D2F = the border x 2"},
        "2313": {"comment":"Stack below $5C00 again"},
        "2316": {"comment":"$5D43 = $2313: an SNA header holds no PC"},
        "2319": {"comment":"Not compressed"},
        "2321": {"comment":"On with the 48K memory"},
        "2323": {"synopsis":"A Z80 file: its first 30 bytes to $5D23-$5D40 (the register image). The flags byte ($5D2F)\nof $FF counts as 1 and gets bit 0 set; R's bit 7 ($5D2E) comes from that bit 0; B = $10 when\nbit 5 (compressed) is set. A PC of 0 at $5D29 means an extended header follows\n(SNAP_Z80_EXT).","comment":"The Z80 header's 30 bytes to $5D23"},
        "2326": {"comment":"30 bytes"},
        "2331": {"comment":"The flags byte (header byte 12)"},
        "2334": {"comment":"$FF stands for 1"},
        "2339": {"comment":"Version 1's other reading"},
        "2342": {"synopsis":"R's bit 7 from the flags byte; B = the compressed bit.","comment":"R's bit 7 from the flags' bit 0"},
        "2347": {"comment":"Bit 7 out to carry"},
        "2349": {"comment":"Bit 5 (compressed) to bit 4"},
        "2352": {"comment":"B = $10 when compressed"},
        "2355": {"comment":"The PC (header bytes 6-7)"},
        "2358": {"comment":"PC 0: a version 2 or 3 header follows"},
        "2362": {"synopsis":"A 48K memory image (an SNA, an SNX or a version 1 Z80): $5D05 = B (non-zero: compressed),\n$5D43 = HL (the PC; $2313 for an SNA). The file's data goes through the buffers\n(SNAP_BUF_INIT); an SNX gets SNX_PATCH; banks 5, 2 and 0 are filled in that order. A\n64K-or-longer SNA/SNX then reads the four-byte trailer (PC, port $7FFD, TR-DOS byte), copies\nthe 16K just put in bank 0 to the bank the port value pages, and loads the other banks (not\n2, 5 or that one) in ascending order; the machine kind is 8 (128K). Otherwise it is 0 (48K).","comment":"$5D05 = the compressed flag for the 48K block"},
        "2366": {"comment":"$5D43 = the PC"},
        "2369": {"comment":"The bank loader to $5D80; the first 32K read"},
        "2372": {"comment":"An SNX?"},
        "2377": {"comment":"Yes: SNX_PATCH"},
        "2380": {"comment":"Bank 5: $4000-$7FFF"},
        "2385": {"comment":"Bank 2: $8000-$BFFF"},
        "2387": {"comment":"Into the bank at $C000 next"},
        "2390": {"comment":"Bank 0: $C000-$FFFF"},
        "2394": {"comment":"A 128K SNA/SNX?"},
        "2398": {"comment":"No: a 48K machine (A = 0)"},
        "2400": {"comment":"Hardware mode 4 (128K)"},
        "2405": {"comment":"Carry clear: four bytes"},
        "2406": {"comment":"BC = PC, E = port $7FFD, D = the TR-DOS byte"},
        "2409": {"comment":"$5D43 = the PC"},
        "2413": {"comment":"$5D46 = the port $7FFD value"},
        "2417": {"comment":"Bank 0 at $6000-$9FFF"},
        "2421": {"comment":"Bank 0's second 8K at $8000"},
        "2425": {"comment":"The 16K just read into bank 0"},
        "2428": {"comment":"Copied to the bank paged at $C000"},
        "2433": {"comment":"Bank 0 first"},
        "2434": {"synopsis":"One bank of a 128K SNA/SNX: banks 2 and 5 skipped, the paged one skipped.","comment":"Bank 2 or 5: already loaded"},
        "2442": {"comment":"D = this bank"},
        "2443": {"comment":"The bank paged at $C000?"},
        "2446": {"comment":"Its number from the port value"},
        "2450": {"comment":"Load the others from the file"},
        "2451": {"comment":"Not the paged one: read from the file"},
        "2455": {"synopsis":"The next bank, up to 7.","comment":"The next bank"},
        "2460": {"comment":"A = 8: a 128K machine"},
        "2462": {"synopsis":"On to SNAP_ROM with A = the machine kind.","comment":"To SNAP_ROM with the machine kind"},
        "2465": {"synopsis":"A version 2 or 3 Z80 file:\n1. The extended header's length (2 bytes) to $5D41; 56 or more is error 21 (rc_badparam).\n2. The extended header to $5D43 (the PC first, the hardware mode at $5D45, port $7FFD's\n   value at $5D46, byte 37 at $5D48, byte 86 at $5D79); the buffers set up (SNAP_BUF_INIT).\n3. NextReg 8 bit 0 (issue 2 keyboard) from bit 2 of $5D40.\n4. A 23-byte header's modes 3 and 4 become 4 and 5; with byte 37 bit 7 set, modes 4-6 become\n   12 and 7-8 become 13; below mode 7 $5D79 = 4.\n5. Modes 0-3 (48K): port $7FFD's value = $30 and three pages loaded (4 to bank 2, 5 to bank\n   0, 8 to bank 5; another page is error 21); kind 0.\n6. Mode 4 and up: eight pages (3-10 to banks 0-7, others error 21); the kind is $18 for mode\n   $50, $10 for mode $51, 9 for mode 12 and up, otherwise 8.","comment":"The extra header's length to $5D41"},
        "2468": {"comment":"2 bytes"},
        "2473": {"comment":"256 or more: unsupported"},
        "2478": {"comment":"To the rc_badparam exit"},
        "2480": {"comment":"56 or more: unsupported"},
        "2485": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "2486": {"comment":"The extra header to $5D43 (PC first)"},
        "2492": {"comment":"The bank loader to $5D80; the first 32K read"},
        "2495": {"comment":"NextReg 8, bit 0 (issue 2 keyboard)"},
        "2500": {"comment":"Issue 3 unless"},
        "2502": {"comment":"From bit 2 of the interrupt mode byte"},
        "2509": {"comment":"Issue 2"},
        "2511": {"synopsis":"NextReg 8 written.","comment":"NextReg 8 written"},
        "2513": {"comment":"The length again"},
        "2514": {"comment":"HL = the hardware mode"},
        "2517": {"comment":"23 bytes: a version 2 header?"},
        "2521": {"comment":"Mode 3 or 4 in version 2"},
        "2530": {"comment":"...is mode 4 or 5 in version 3"},
        "2531": {"synopsis":"Byte 37 bit 7 set with mode 4-8: mode 12 (from 4-6) or 13 (from 7-8).","comment":"Byte 37 bit 7 (modified hardware)?"},
        "2535": {"comment":"A = the hardware mode"},
        "2536": {"comment":"Not modified: as it is"},
        "2538": {"comment":"Modified, and mode 4-8?"},
        "2542": {"comment":"Below 4: as it is"},
        "2546": {"comment":"Mode 4-6 becomes 12, 7-8 becomes 13"},
        "2548": {"comment":"12 for modes 4-6"},
        "2552": {"comment":"...13 for modes 7-8"},
        "2553": {"synopsis":"The changed mode stored.","comment":"The new mode"},
        "2554": {"synopsis":"Below mode 7: header byte 86 ($5D79) = 4.","comment":"Below 7?"},
        "2558": {"comment":"Header byte 86 ($5D79) = 4"},
        "2560": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2563": {"synopsis":"The memory pages, by the hardware mode: 0-3 three pages, 4 and up eight.","comment":"Mode 0-3: a 48K machine"},
        "2566": {"comment":"Mode 4 and up: SNAP_128_PAGES"},
        "2568": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $30 (locked, ROM 1)"},
        "2570": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "2573": {"comment":"Three pages"},
        "2575": {"synopsis":"One page of a 48K Z80 file: its header (SNAP_PAGE_HDR), its bank from the page number (4 >\n2, 5 > 0, 8 > 5).","comment":"The count kept"},
        "2576": {"comment":"A = the page number, $5D05 set"},
        "2579": {"comment":"Page 4: bank 2"},
        "2581": {"comment":"E = the bank"},
        "2585": {"comment":"Page 5: bank 0"},
        "2591": {"comment":"Page 8: bank 5"},
        "2595": {"synopsis":"An extended header of 256 bytes or more (reached with NZ): error 21.","comment":"Another page: unsupported"},
        "2597": {"synopsis":"The page loaded into bank E.","comment":"Load the bank"},
        "2601": {"comment":"Next of the three"},
        "2605": {"comment":"A = 0: a 48K machine"},
        "2606": {"comment":"To SNAP_ROM"},
        "2608": {"synopsis":"Error 21 (rc_badparam): an unsupported snapshot; SNAP_FATAL reports it and stops.","comment":"Error 21, rc_badparam"},
        "2610": {"comment":"Reported, and the machine stops"},
        "2613": {"synopsis":"Eight pages of a 128K Z80 file; then the machine kind from the hardware mode.","comment":"Eight pages"},
        "2615": {"synopsis":"One page: pages 3-10 go to banks 0-7.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "2616": {"comment":"A = the page number"},
        "2619": {"comment":"Pages 3-10 are banks 0-7"},
        "2623": {"comment":"Above 10: unsupported"},
        "2627": {"comment":"Load the bank"},
        "2630": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "2631": {"comment":"Next of the eight"},
        "2634": {"comment":"Mode $50: B = $18 (ZX80 ROM)"},
        "2641": {"comment":"To SNAP_ROM_B"},
        "2643": {"comment":"Mode $51: B = $10 (ZX81 ROM)"},
        "2649": {"comment":"Mode 12 and up: A = 9 (+2A/+3)"},
        "2651": {"comment":"A = 8: a 128K machine"},
        "2653": {"comment":"Below 12: 8"},
        "2655": {"comment":"9"},
        "2656": {"synopsis":"The memory is loaded; B = the machine kind (0 48K, 8 128K, 9 +2A/+3, $18 and $10 for the Z80\nmodes $50 and $51):\n1. Bank 7 paged back at $C000 (MMU slots 6 and 7).\n2. An SNX keeps the machine's ROM and file 0 open: DE = $00FF, on to SNAP_START.\n3. Otherwise A = B XOR $18 picks the ROM file by its name's offset at $1FBD ($18 48.rom, $10\n   128.rom, $11 128-2.rom, 0 zx80.rom, 8 zx81.rom) and LOAD_MACHINE_ROM puts it in the\n   alternate ROM (an error goes to SNAP_FATAL); D = its NextReg $8C value, E = its NextReg\n   $82 value.\n4. File 0 closed, the DivMMC's automap entry points at $0000-$0038 off (NextReg $B8 = 0).\n5. The AY's ports decoded (NextReg $84 bit 0) for a 128K machine, and for a 48K one when\n   byte 37 bit 2 is set.\n6. For zx80.rom and zx81.rom the DivMMC automap off (NextReg $0A bit 4).","comment":"B = the machine kind"},
        "2657": {"synopsis":"Entered with B already the machine kind.","comment":"Bank 7 back at $C000"},
        "2661": {"comment":"Page 15 at $E000"},
        "2665": {"comment":"An SNX?"},
        "2670": {"comment":"SNX: DE = $00FF, no ROM loaded, file 0 left open"},
        "2673": {"comment":"To SNAP_START"},
        "2675": {"comment":"The name at $1FBD+A: 48.rom, 128.rom, 128-2.rom, zx80/81.rom"},
        "2676": {"comment":"Its offset in the name table"},
        "2678": {"comment":"Kept for the automap test"},
        "2679": {"comment":"The machine's ROM into the alternate ROM"},
        "2682": {"comment":"Failed: SNAP_FATAL"},
        "2684": {"comment":"D = the NextReg $8C value"},
        "2685": {"comment":"E = the NextReg $82 value"},
        "2686": {"comment":"File 0 closed (DOS_CLOSE)"},
        "2691": {"comment":"The two values back"},
        "2692": {"comment":"No automap entry points at $0000-$0038"},
        "2696": {"comment":"A 48K machine (ROM 1 locked)?"},
        "2698": {"comment":"128K: the AY always"},
        "2700": {"comment":"Then only with the AY in use (byte 37 bit 2)"},
        "2707": {"synopsis":"NextReg $84 bit 0 set: the AY ports decoded.","comment":"NextReg $84 bit 0: the AY's ports decoded"},
        "2712": {"comment":"Bit 0 set"},
        "2714": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "2716": {"synopsis":"The automap left on for the Spectrum ROMs, cleared for ZX80/ZX81.","comment":"A = the ROM name's offset"},
        "2717": {"comment":"48K, 128K or +3 ROM?"},
        "2719": {"comment":"Yes: automap kept"},
        "2721": {"comment":"ZX80/ZX81: NextReg $0A bit 4 cleared, no automap"},
        "2726": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "2728": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "2730": {"synopsis":"Starts the loaded machine: the CPU speed and NMI enables restored ($0809), then NextReg 2 =\n8 (bit 7 as read): a Multiface NMI is generated. What handles it is not in this ROM; D and E\n(the NextReg $8C and $82 values, or $00FF for an SNX) are left for it. If execution went on,\nit would run into FILE0_READ.","comment":"CPU speed and NMIs back"},
        "2733": {"comment":"NextReg 2"},
        "2738": {"comment":"...bit 7 kept, bit 3 set: a Multiface NMI"},
        "2742": {"comment":"Written: the NMI fires"},
        "2744": {"comment":"What runs now is not in this ROM"},
        "2745": {"synopsis":"Reads DE bytes of file 0 to HL, with page C at $C000 (DOS_READ, MMU slots 6 and 7 first set\nto bank 7 for +3DOS). Also reached by running on from SNAP_START.\nExit: carry: all read. NC and Z: end of file, HL = the bytes read. NC and NZ: another error,\nA = its code.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"File 0"},
        "2747": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "2748": {"comment":"Bank 7 at $C000 for +3DOS"},
        "2752": {"comment":"Page 15 at $E000"},
        "2756": {"comment":"DOS_READ: DE bytes to HL (page C at $C000)"},
        "2759": {"comment":"HL = the count asked for"},
        "2760": {"comment":"All read: carry"},
        "2761": {"comment":"End of file (rc_eof)?"},
        "2763": {"comment":"No carry either way"},
        "2764": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "2765": {"comment":"Another error: NZ, A = its code"},
        "2766": {"comment":"HL = the bytes read (DE = those not read)"},
        "2768": {"comment":"Z, no carry"},
        "2770": {"synopsis":"Reads A bytes of file 0 to HL (FILE0_READ); anything short of all of them is fatal\n(SNAP_FATAL).\nEntry: A = the count, HL = the destination.","comment":"DE = A"},
        "2771": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "2773": {"comment":"Read them"},
        "2776": {"comment":"All read"},
        "2777": {"synopsis":"A fatal snapshot error: the screen cleared (ROM 1's CLS_STREAM_2) and error A reported by\nROM 1's PRINT_REPORT as report code A + $3E (A below 10, the recoverable disk errors) or A +\n$19; then the machine loops at $0AEE for good.\nEntry: A = the +3DOS error code.","comment":"The error kept"},
        "2778": {"comment":"ROM 1's CLS_STREAM_2"},
        "2783": {"comment":"The error back"},
        "2784": {"comment":"Below 10 (a recoverable disk error)?"},
        "2786": {"comment":"Report code A + $3E"},
        "2788": {"comment":"Below 10: by $3E"},
        "2790": {"comment":"Report code A + $19"},
        "2792": {"synopsis":"A = the report code.","comment":"A = the report code"},
        "2793": {"comment":"ROM 1's PRINT_REPORT"},
        "2798": {"synopsis":"Stops here.","comment":"Stops here for good"},
        "2800": {"synopsis":"Sets up the reading of the snapshot's memory image:\n1. BANK_FILL (132 bytes from $0C22) copied to $5D80; the read offset $5D03 = 0.\n2. The two 16K banks from Layer 2's first (NextReg $12) are the buffers: $5D01 = it, $5D02 =\n   the next one.\n3. Both filled with the next 32K of file 0 (SNAP_BUF_FILL).","comment":"The bank loader (BANK_FILL) to $5D80"},
        "2806": {"comment":"132 bytes"},
        "2811": {"comment":"$5D03 = 0: the read offset"},
        "2815": {"comment":"Layer 2's first bank (NextReg $12)"},
        "2817": {"comment":"A = its 16K bank"},
        "2820": {"comment":"$5D01 = it, $5D02 = the next one"},
        "2825": {"comment":"The next bank"},
        "2828": {"comment":"Two buffers of 16K each"},
        "2829": {"comment":"The first filled from file 0"},
        "2830": {"comment":"Read into it"},
        "2833": {"comment":"Then the second"},
        "2835": {"comment":"The second bank"},
        "2836": {"synopsis":"Reads the next 16K of file 0 into bank A at $C000 (FILE0_READ); the end of the file is fine,\nanother error is fatal (SNAP_FATAL).\nEntry: A = the 16K bank.","comment":"C = the bank to read into"},
        "2837": {"comment":"16K to $C000 in it"},
        "2840": {"comment":"16K"},
        "2843": {"comment":"Read from file 0"},
        "2846": {"comment":"All read"},
        "2847": {"comment":"End of file: still fine"},
        "2848": {"comment":"Another error: SNAP_FATAL"},
        "2850": {"synopsis":"Maps the buffers for reading: HL = the address of the next byte.\n1. The read offset ($5D03) past 16K: back by 16K, the buffers swapped ($5D01/$5D02) and the\n   used one refilled with the next 16K (SNAP_BUF_FILL).\n2. MMU slots 3-4 = the first buffer ($6000-$9FFF), 5-6 = the second ($A000-$DFFF).\nExit: HL = $6000 + the offset.","comment":"HL = the read offset"},
        "2853": {"comment":"Past the first buffer?"},
        "2857": {"comment":"Back by 16K"},
        "2860": {"comment":"The buffers swap places"},
        "2863": {"comment":"A = the first bank"},
        "2865": {"comment":"D = the second"},
        "2866": {"comment":"The first now second"},
        "2868": {"comment":"The second now first"},
        "2869": {"comment":"The used one filled with the next 16K"},
        "2872": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "2873": {"synopsis":"The buffers paged in; HL = $6000 + the offset.","comment":"The buffers' banks to MMU slots 3-6"},
        "2876": {"comment":"The first at $6000-$9FFF"},
        "2878": {"comment":"Its first 8K page"},
        "2882": {"comment":"Its second 8K page"},
        "2886": {"comment":"The second at $A000-$DFFF"},
        "2887": {"comment":"Its first 8K page"},
        "2891": {"comment":"Its second 8K page"},
        "2895": {"comment":"HL = the address of the next byte"},
        "2900": {"synopsis":"Reads a Z80 page's 3-byte header (SNAP_HDR_BYTES): $5D05 = 0 when the length is $FFFF\n(stored as is), non-zero otherwise (compressed).\nExit: A = the page number.","comment":"Three bytes"},
        "2901": {"comment":"BC = the length, E = the page"},
        "2904": {"comment":"$FFFF (not compressed) gives 0"},
        "2907": {"comment":"$5D05 = 0 for an uncompressed block"},
        "2910": {"comment":"A = the page number"},
        "2912": {"synopsis":"Reads bytes from the buffers into C, B, E, and with carry clear D too; the read offset moves\npast them.\nEntry: carry set for three bytes, clear for four.","comment":"Carry kept: three bytes or four"},
        "2913": {"comment":"HL = the next byte"},
        "2916": {"comment":"C, B, E"},
        "2922": {"comment":"Carry set: done"},
        "2925": {"comment":"D as well"},
        "2926": {"comment":"HL past it"},
        "2929": {"synopsis":"Loads a 16K bank from the buffers, with no run of the decompressor pending ($5D07 = 0).\nEntry: A = the 16K bank; $5D05 = 0 for stored data, non-zero for compressed.","comment":"No run pending in the decompressor"},
        "2934": {"synopsis":"Fills bank A from the buffers by BANK_FILL at $5D80, as SNAP_LOAD_BANK but keeping a pending\nrun; the read offset ($5D03) moves past what was used.","comment":"The bank kept"},
        "2935": {"comment":"HL = the next byte"},
        "2938": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "2939": {"comment":"BANK_FILL at $5D80: 16K to bank A"},
        "2942": {"synopsis":"HL back to an offset ($6000 + $A000 wraps to 0) and stored at $5D03.","comment":"HL back to an offset ($6000 + $A000 wraps)"},
        "2946": {"comment":"The new read offset"},
        "2949": {"comment":"HL = the offset"},
        "2950": {"synopsis":"An SNX's interrupt exit made harmless:\n1. The first buffer's first 8K mapped at $6000 (the snapshot's $4000-$5FFF) and the second\n   buffer's last 8K at $A000 (its $A000-$BFFF).\n2. EI, RETI at the snapshot's $5C5C: nothing to patch. Otherwise each entry of SNX_PATCHES\n   is compared at its address; on a match the two addresses after it get $00 (NOP).\n3. NextReg 5: 50/60 Hz and the scandoubler kept, joystick 1 Kempston 1, joystick 2 Kempston\n   2.","comment":"The first buffer's first 8K at $6000"},
        "2954": {"comment":"MMU slot 3"},
        "2957": {"comment":"The second buffer's last 8K at $A000"},
        "2959": {"comment":"MMU slot 5"},
        "2962": {"comment":"EI at the snapshot's $5C5C?"},
        "2969": {"comment":"RETI after it?"},
        "2975": {"comment":"Yes: nothing to patch"},
        "2977": {"comment":"To SNX_JOYSTICKS"},
        "2979": {"synopsis":"The table's entries tried in turn.","comment":"The patch table"},
        "2982": {"synopsis":"The next entry: 0 ends the table (return).","comment":"The byte count; 0 ends the table"},
        "2984": {"comment":"None matched"},
        "2985": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "2986": {"comment":"DE = where the bytes must be"},
        "2990": {"synopsis":"One byte compared.","comment":"Compare them"},
        "2993": {"comment":"Zero when the same"},
        "2994": {"comment":"Different: the next entry"},
        "2996": {"comment":"All the same"},
        "2998": {"comment":"Two addresses follow"},
        "3000": {"synopsis":"One address set to $00.","comment":"Each gets 0 (NOP)"},
        "3004": {"comment":"A = 0 here"},
        "3007": {"synopsis":"NextReg 5: the joysticks Kempston 1 and 2.","comment":"NextReg 5"},
        "3012": {"comment":"...50/60 Hz and scandoubler kept"},
        "3014": {"comment":"...joysticks Kempston 1 and Kempston 2"},
        "3016": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3018": {"comment":"Done"},
        "3019": {"synopsis":"A mismatch: past the entry's bytes and its two addresses.","comment":"Over the rest of the bytes"},
        "3020": {"comment":"Until the entry's last byte"},
        "3022": {"comment":"And the two addresses"},
        "3026": {"comment":"Try the next entry"},
        "3028": {"synopsis":"SNX_PATCH's table. Each entry: a count n, the address (in the $6000/$A000 window) where n\nbytes must be found, the n bytes, then two addresses that get $00 on a match. The four\nentries' bytes are interrupt exits (EXX, POP IY, POP IX, POP HL/DE/BC, POP AF, EI, RETI; one\nwith EXX twice, one popping DE, BC, HL): at $7C68 (zeroing $7C64, $7C68), $7C64 ($7C64,\n$7C65), $7C6B ($7C64, $7C6B) and $A92F ($A92B, $A92F). A 0 ends the table ($0C21)."},
        "3106": {"synopsis":"Copied to $5D80 by SNAP_BUF_INIT and run there: fills a 16K bank from HL, as stored bytes or\n($5D05 non-zero) compressed with $ED $ED count byte runs (RLE_8K), 8K at a time through MMU\nslot 7 at $E000. Bank 5's first 8K goes to DivMMC RAM bank 6, and all of bank 7 to DivMMC\nRAM banks 4 and 5, at $2000 with port $E3 CONMEM (bank 5's $4000 half holds this code and\nits variables; bank 7 holds +3DOS's). Ends with port $E3 = 0.\nEntry: A = the 16K bank, HL = the data.\nExit: HL = past the data used.","comment":"The bank's first 8K page at $E000"},
        "3107": {"comment":"MMU slot 7"},
        "3110": {"comment":"A = its second page"},
        "3112": {"comment":"Bank 5 (page 11 second)?"},
        "3114": {"comment":"To BANK_FILL_B5"},
        "3116": {"comment":"Bank 7 (page 15 second)?"},
        "3118": {"comment":"To BANK_FILL_B7"},
        "3120": {"comment":"To $E000"},
        "3123": {"comment":"Compressed?"},
        "3127": {"comment":"To BANK_FILL_RLE"},
        "3129": {"comment":"No: 8K copied ($0C42 at $5DA0)"},
        "3132": {"comment":"The second page at $E000"},
        "3133": {"comment":"MMU slot 7"},
        "3136": {"comment":"DE = $E000 again"},
        "3138": {"synopsis":"Copies 8K from HL to DE ($0C42 is $5DA0 in the copy), then port $E3 = 0.","comment":"8K"},
        "3143": {"synopsis":"Port $E3 = 0: the DivMMC's memory paged out.","comment":"DivMMC memory paged out (port $E3 = 0)"},
        "3147": {"synopsis":"Compressed: both 8K halves unpacked (RLE_8K).","comment":"Compressed: 8K unpacked ($0C54 at $5DB2)"},
        "3150": {"comment":"The second page at $E000"},
        "3151": {"comment":"MMU slot 7"},
        "3154": {"comment":"DE = $E000 again"},
        "3156": {"synopsis":"Unpacks into DE up to its 8K page's end (D $00 or $40 after wrapping): a byte is stored as\nis, except $ED $ED n b, which is n copies of b. A run cut by the page's end goes on in the\nnext call: B (the copies left) and C (the byte) are kept at $5D06/$5D07. $0C54 is $5DB2 in\nthe copy.","comment":"C = the byte, B = how many still to put"},
        "3160": {"synopsis":"The next byte: a pending copy first.","comment":"A run pending?"},
        "3162": {"comment":"Yes: one more of it"},
        "3164": {"comment":"The next byte of the file"},
        "3166": {"comment":"$ED: perhaps a run"},
        "3168": {"comment":"To RLE_ED"},
        "3170": {"synopsis":"A byte stored; the page's end tested.","comment":"Into the bank"},
        "3172": {"comment":"Within this 256-byte block"},
        "3174": {"comment":"The next block"},
        "3175": {"comment":"Past the 8K page (D = $00 or $40)?"},
        "3177": {"comment":"Not yet"},
        "3179": {"comment":"The run's rest kept for the next page"},
        "3183": {"comment":"Done with this page"},
        "3185": {"synopsis":"An $ED: a run if another $ED follows; otherwise the $ED and that byte are stored.","comment":"One $ED if no second $ED follows"},
        "3187": {"comment":"C = the next byte"},
        "3188": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "3189": {"comment":"$ED $ED?"},
        "3190": {"comment":"No: the lone $ED put, then C"},
        "3192": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "3193": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "3194": {"comment":"C = the byte"},
        "3195": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "3196": {"synopsis":"One copy of the run's byte.","comment":"One of the run"},
        "3197": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "3200": {"synopsis":"Bank 5: its first 8K to DivMMC RAM bank 6, the second to page 11.","comment":"Bank 5: DivMMC RAM bank 6 at $2000 (CONMEM)"},
        "3202": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "3204": {"comment":"Its first 8K to $2000 there ($0CA1 at $5DFF)"},
        "3207": {"comment":"The second page at $E000"},
        "3208": {"comment":"MMU slot 7"},
        "3211": {"comment":"DE = $E000"},
        "3213": {"synopsis":"8K copied or unpacked by $5D05.","comment":"Compressed?"},
        "3217": {"comment":"Yes: unpacked"},
        "3219": {"comment":"No: copied"},
        "3221": {"synopsis":"Bank 7: to DivMMC RAM banks 4 and 5.","comment":"Bank 7: DivMMC RAM bank 4 at $2000 (CONMEM)"},
        "3222": {"comment":"A = $84"},
        "3224": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "3226": {"comment":"Its first 8K to $2000 there"},
        "3229": {"comment":"Its second 8K to DivMMC RAM bank 5"},
        "3231": {"comment":"Paged in"},
        "3233": {"synopsis":"8K to $2000 in the DivMMC RAM bank paged by port $E3, copied or unpacked by $5D05 ($0CA1 is\n$5DFF in the copy).","comment":"To $2000"},
        "3236": {"comment":"Copied or unpacked"},
        "3238": {"synopsis":"IDE_SNAPLOAD for a .O (ZX80, carry clear) or .P (ZX81, carry set) file:\n1. zx80.rom or zx81.rom into the alternate ROM (LOAD_MACHINE_ROM, A = 0 or 8); an error\n   returns NC with A.\n2. SP = $8000; $8000-$BFFF cleared; the file read to $8000 (.O) or $8009 (.P) (FILE_TO_MEM\n   with A = $FF); an error is fatal (SNAP_FATAL).\n3. $C000-$FFFF cleared; ZX8081_START copied to $F000.\n4. Interrupts off, the DivMMC automap off (NextReg $0A bit 4), port $7FFD = $2F, A' = 0, IY\n   = $4000, IM 1; the 16K at $8000 moved to $4000, SP = $8000, and JP $F000.\nEntry: A = 'O' or 'P', HL = the filespec.","comment":"The filespec kept"},
        "3239": {"comment":"The letter and carry (.P) kept"},
        "3240": {"comment":"A = 0 for .O, 8 for .P"},
        "3242": {"comment":"x 8"},
        "3245": {"comment":"zx80.rom or zx81.rom into the alternate ROM"},
        "3248": {"comment":"D = the letter, E = the flags"},
        "3249": {"comment":"BC = the filespec"},
        "3250": {"comment":"Failed: NC, A = the error"},
        "3251": {"comment":"Stack at $8000"},
        "3255": {"comment":"The letter and flags kept"},
        "3256": {"comment":"And the filespec"},
        "3257": {"comment":"$8000-$BFFF cleared"},
        "3260": {"comment":"HL = the filespec"},
        "3261": {"comment":"The program goes to $8000"},
        "3264": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "3266": {"comment":"...or to $8009 for a .P"},
        "3268": {"comment":"E = 9"},
        "3270": {"synopsis":"The file read into memory.","comment":"A = $FF: copied whole, not as a ROM"},
        "3272": {"comment":"The file read into memory"},
        "3275": {"comment":"Failed: SNAP_FATAL"},
        "3278": {"comment":"$C000-$FFFF cleared"},
        "3283": {"comment":"ZX8081_START to $F000"},
        "3289": {"comment":"73 bytes"},
        "3294": {"comment":"No interrupts now"},
        "3295": {"comment":"NextReg $0A bit 4 cleared: no DivMMC automap"},
        "3300": {"comment":"Bit 4 cleared"},
        "3304": {"comment":"Port $7FFD = $2F: bank 7, locked"},
        "3309": {"comment":"Written"},
        "3311": {"comment":"A' = 0"},
        "3312": {"comment":"Into A'"},
        "3313": {"comment":"Carry back: set for a .P"},
        "3314": {"comment":"IY = $4000"},
        "3318": {"comment":"Interrupt mode 1"},
        "3320": {"comment":"The 16K at $8000 moved to $4000"},
        "3326": {"comment":"BC = $4000"},
        "3330": {"comment":"SP = $8000"},
        "3332": {"comment":"ZX8081_START, at $F000"},
        "3335": {"synopsis":"Copied to $F000 by ZX8081_LOAD and run there: the alternate ROM put in place of the ROM\n(NextReg $8C = $A0, ROM 1 locked) and interrupts on. A ZX80 program: I = $0E, $3FAA pushed,\nthe ZX80 ROM's CLS_DISPLAY, $4000-$4001 = $FF, $88, then the ZX80 ROM's GOTO_CMD with BC =\n0, returning to its $0447. A ZX81 program: ZX81_START.","comment":"The alternate ROM replaces the ROM, ROM 1 locked"},
        "3339": {"comment":"Interrupts on"},
        "3340": {"comment":"A .P: ZX81_START"},
        "3342": {"comment":"I = $0E"},
        "3344": {"comment":"Into I"},
        "3346": {"comment":"$3FAA left on the stack"},
        "3350": {"comment":"The ZX80 ROM's CLS_DISPLAY"},
        "3353": {"comment":"$4000 = $FF, $4001 = $88"},
        "3356": {"comment":"The ZX80's first two bytes"},
        "3359": {"comment":"Returning into the ZX80 ROM's $0447"},
        "3362": {"comment":"As the return address"},
        "3363": {"comment":"The ZX80 ROM's GOTO_CMD with line 0"},
        "3369": {"synopsis":"A ZX81 program: $4000-$4008 from ZX81_SYSVARS (at $F040 in the copy), IX = $0281, I = $1E,\n$3E00 and $0676 pushed, then the ZX81 ROM's SLOW_FAST (names from zx81.rom.dis).","comment":"$4000-$4008 from ZX81_SYSVARS ($F040)"},
        "3380": {"comment":"IX = $0281"},
        "3384": {"comment":"I = $1E"},
        "3386": {"comment":"Into I"},
        "3388": {"comment":"$3E00 left on the stack"},
        "3392": {"comment":"Returning into the ZX81 ROM's $0676"},
        "3395": {"comment":"As the return address"},
        "3396": {"comment":"The ZX81 ROM's SLOW_FAST"},
        "3399": {"synopsis":"The 9 bytes ZX81_START puts at $4000-$4008, which a .P file does not hold (it loads from\n$4009): $FF, $80, $7FFC, $8000, $00, $FFFE."},
        "3408": {"synopsis":"Clears 16K from H x 256.\nEntry: H = the first address's high byte.\nChanges: BC, DE, HL.","comment":"From H x 256"},
        "3410": {"comment":"D = H"},
        "3411": {"comment":"DE one byte on"},
        "3413": {"comment":"16K in all"},
        "3416": {"comment":"Each byte 0"},
        "3420": {"synopsis":"20 bytes LOAD_MACHINE_ROM writes into a loaded Spectrum ROM: 6 at its $0EAC (LD BC,$F650;\nRST $08; $92; RET), 12 at its $0ECD (LD E,A; SUB $A5; JP NC,$0C10; LD BC,$FB50; RST $08;\n$92; RET) and 2 at $15BE ($0ECD). RST $08 with $92 is the esxDOS hook M_DRVAPI; C = $50 is a\ndriver ID and B ($F6, $FB) its call: COPY and the printer's output go to that driver, tokens\n($A5 and up) to the ROM's own $0C10. In the 48K ROM these addresses are COPY_CMD,\nPRBUFF_OUT, PRINT_TOKEN and the P channel's output word in CHANNEL_DATA."},
        "3440": {"synopsis":"Loads a machine's ROM file into the alternate ROM and sets the Next up for it:\n1. The name c:/machines/next/ + the 8-byte name at $1FBD + A (128-2.rom for an odd A) built\n   at $D827 ($1E14); ROM_TO_ALT loads it. An error returns NC with A.\n2. A Spectrum ROM (bit 4 of A), unless $5B68 bit 4 is set: PRINTER_PATCH written into it at\n   $0EAC, $0ECD and $15BE (LDIR_ROM_1).\n3. NextReg 3: 48K display timing ($90) for 48.rom, 128K ($A0) for the others.\n4. When NextReg $83 reads $FF: NextRegs $83 = $3F, $84 = 1 (0 for 48.rom: no AY), $85 = 1,\n   and E = $C2 ($C0 for 48.rom). Otherwise E = NextReg $82's bits 0, 2 and 5 with $C2/$C0.\n5. NextRegs $14, $4A, $D8 = 0; NextReg 6 audio chip mode AY; NextReg 8 bit 6 cleared\n   (contention on).\nEntry: A = the name's offset: 0 zx80.rom, 8 zx81.rom, $10 128.rom, $11 128-2.rom, $18\n48.rom.\nExit: carry, A = the value for NextReg $8C ($80; $A0 with ROM 1 locked for 48.rom, zx80.rom,\nzx81.rom), E = the value for NextReg $82. Page 1's A3_CMD and A3_LOAD call it with A = $10\nor $18.","comment":"The ROM's offset kept"},
        "3441": {"comment":"HL = its name at $D827 ($1E14)"},
        "3444": {"comment":"The offset back"},
        "3446": {"comment":"The ROM file into the alternate ROM"},
        "3449": {"comment":"B = the offset"},
        "3450": {"comment":"Failed: NC, A = the error"},
        "3452": {"comment":"A Spectrum ROM (offset $10, $11 or $18)?"},
        "3454": {"comment":"No: no patches"},
        "3456": {"comment":"$5B68 bit 4 set: no printer patches"},
        "3461": {"comment":"To LMR_MACHINE"},
        "3463": {"comment":"PRINTER_PATCH's 20 bytes to $C000"},
        "3472": {"comment":"HL = $C000 after"},
        "3476": {"comment":"6 bytes over the new ROM's $0EAC (COPY)"},
        "3479": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "3484": {"comment":"12 bytes over its $0ECD (printer output)"},
        "3487": {"comment":"12 bytes"},
        "3492": {"comment":"2 over its $15BE (channel P's output word)"},
        "3495": {"comment":"2 bytes"},
        "3500": {"synopsis":"The Next set up for the ROM's machine.","comment":"The ROM's offset back"},
        "3502": {"comment":"48.rom?"},
        "3504": {"comment":"Otherwise: 128K display timing"},
        "3506": {"comment":"...AY decoded (D = 1), E = $C2"},
        "3510": {"comment":"Not 48K: on"},
        "3512": {"comment":"48K display timing"},
        "3514": {"comment":"No AY (D = 0), E = $C0"},
        "3517": {"comment":"B = $C0: bit 4 clear"},
        "3518": {"synopsis":"NextReg 3 = the display timing; A = the NextReg $8C value from B's bit 4.","comment":"Bit 7 set: the timing changes"},
        "3521": {"comment":"Bit 4 set (128.rom, 128-2.rom)"},
        "3524": {"comment":"...$80, otherwise $A0 (ROM 1 locked)"},
        "3529": {"comment":"The NextReg $8C value, returned in A"},
        "3530": {"comment":"NextReg $83 all ones?"},
        "3538": {"comment":"Then $83 = $3F: no sprite or Layer 2 ports"},
        "3543": {"comment":"AY by D"},
        "3546": {"comment":"ULA+ only of bits 24-31"},
        "3550": {"comment":"E stays"},
        "3552": {"synopsis":"NextReg $83 not all ones: E combined with NextReg $82's bits 0, 2, 5.","comment":"Otherwise NextReg $82's bits 0, 2, 5 kept"},
        "3557": {"comment":"Port $FF, $DFFD, DMA ($6B) bits"},
        "3559": {"comment":"...with E's: E = NextReg $82 for the caller"},
        "3560": {"comment":"E = the value"},
        "3561": {"synopsis":"The colours, traps, audio and contention set; carry and A = the NextReg $8C value.","comment":"No global transparency colour"},
        "3565": {"comment":"Fallback colour 0"},
        "3568": {"comment":"No +3 FDC traps"},
        "3571": {"comment":"NextReg 6: audio chip mode AY"},
        "3574": {"comment":"Bits 1-0 = 01"},
        "3578": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3580": {"comment":"No effect: BC is set again"},
        "3581": {"comment":"NextReg 8 bit 6 cleared: contention on"},
        "3586": {"comment":"Bit 6 cleared"},
        "3588": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3590": {"comment":"A = the NextReg $8C value"},
        "3591": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "3593": {"synopsis":"Reads NextReg 6 (NR_READ).","comment":"NextReg 6"},
        "3595": {"synopsis":"Reads NextReg A, leaving BC = $253B so that OUT (C),A writes it back.\nEntry: A = the NextReg.\nExit: A = its value, BC = $253B.","comment":"Selected"},
        "3600": {"comment":"BC = $253B"},
        "3601": {"comment":"A = its value"},
        "3604": {"synopsis":"Sets the Next's internal port decoding to ports $7FFD, $1FFD, the +3 floating bus, both\nKempston joysticks, the DivMMC, Multiface, SPI, mouse and AY (NextRegs $82-$85 = $DA, $2B,\n$01, $00), the audio chip mode to AY (NextReg 6), and clears NextReg 8 bits 6 and 2\n(contention on, no port $FF read). Called from $257E and from page 1 (RET into it at its\n$1662).","comment":"Ports: $7FFD, $1FFD, +3 floating bus, Kempstons"},
        "3608": {"comment":"DivMMC, Multiface, SPI, mouse"},
        "3612": {"comment":"AY"},
        "3616": {"comment":"None of bits 24-31"},
        "3620": {"comment":"NextReg 6: audio chip mode AY"},
        "3623": {"comment":"Bits 1-0 = 01"},
        "3627": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3629": {"comment":"NextReg 8: contention on, port $FF read off"},
        "3634": {"comment":"Bits 6 and 2 cleared"},
        "3636": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3639": {"synopsis":"Loads the ROM file named at HL into the alternate ROM, made visible to writes only (NextReg\n$8C = $C0), from $0000: 32K for $10/$11 (the first 16K written with ROM 2 selected, the\nsecond with ROM 1), 16K with ROM 1 selected otherwise (FILE_TO_MEM with I starting at 0 or\n4).\nEntry: A = the name's offset, HL = the name.","comment":"Alternate ROM on, for writes only"},
        "3643": {"comment":"The destination: $0000"},
        "3646": {"comment":"128.rom or 128-2.rom ($10, $11)?"},
        "3650": {"comment":"Yes: I = 0, two 16K halves"},
        "3652": {"comment":"Otherwise I = 4: one, written under ROM 1"},
        "3654": {"synopsis":"Reads a whole file 4K at a time into bank 7's $C000 and passes each 4K on (FTM_COPY):\n1. The file opened as file 1 for reading (DOS_OPEN); an error returns NC.\n2. Each 4K read (DOS_READ, page 7) and copied on; the end of the file stops it with carry.\n3. File 1 closed (DOS_CLOSE, else DOS_ABANDON).\nEntry: A = the first chunk number less 1 for I ($FF: a plain copy to DE), DE = the\ndestination, HL = the name.\nExit: carry, or NC with A = the error.","comment":"I = the chunk count ($FF: plain copy)"},
        "3656": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "3657": {"comment":"File 1, read access"},
        "3660": {"comment":"D = 0, E = 2: open an existing file"},
        "3663": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN with HL = the name"},
        "3666": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3668": {"synopsis":"The next 4K read and copied on.","comment":"4K into bank 7's $C000"},
        "3671": {"comment":"4K"},
        "3674": {"comment":"HL, DE kept"},
        "3676": {"comment":"File 1, page 7"},
        "3679": {"comment":"DOS_READ"},
        "3682": {"comment":"BC = 4K, HL = $C000, DE = the destination"},
        "3685": {"comment":"The result kept"},
        "3686": {"comment":"The 4K copied on"},
        "3689": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "3690": {"comment":"The destination kept"},
        "3691": {"comment":"All read: the next 4K"},
        "3693": {"comment":"End of file: done, carry"},
        "3696": {"comment":"To FTM_CLOSE"},
        "3698": {"synopsis":"An error: NC.","comment":"Another error: NC"},
        "3699": {"synopsis":"File 1 closed or abandoned; the result returned.","comment":"Drop the destination"},
        "3700": {"comment":"The result kept"},
        "3701": {"comment":"File 1 closed (DOS_CLOSE)"},
        "3706": {"comment":"Not closed: DOS_ABANDON"},
        "3711": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "3713": {"synopsis":"Copies a 4K chunk from HL to DE: I = $FF copies it plainly (DE runs on). Otherwise I counts\nthe chunks and DE wraps within $0000-$3FFF: chunks 1-4 are copied with ROM 2 selected, 5-8\nwith ROM 1 (LDIR_ROM_1), later ones ignored.","comment":"I = $FF: a plain copy"},
        "3716": {"comment":"To FTM_LDIR"},
        "3718": {"comment":"I = the 4K chunk's number"},
        "3720": {"comment":"The destination kept within 16K"},
        "3722": {"comment":"Chunk 9 on: ignored"},
        "3725": {"comment":"Chunks 5-8 under ROM 1"},
        "3727": {"comment":"To LDIR_ROM_1"},
        "3729": {"synopsis":"The LDIR with this ROM selected.","comment":"Chunks 1-4 under ROM 2"},
        "3732": {"synopsis":"LDIR with ROM 1 selected: $5B43 and $001B pushed, then $5B3E selects ROM 1, whose LDIR_RET\nat $001B copies BC bytes from HL to DE and returns into $5B43, which selects ROM 2 again.\nThe way to write the alternate ROM's other half.\nEntry: HL, DE, BC as for LDIR.","comment":"Back through $5B43 (ROM 2 again)"},
        "3736": {"comment":"RET into ROM 1's LDIR_RET"},
        "3740": {"comment":"ROM 1 selected"},
        "3743": {"synopsis":"IDE_BANK ($01BD): allocates or frees 8K banks (the API document's call). With page $10 in\nMMU slot 7, the maps at $E000 (ZX memory, its bank count at $E050) and $E020 (DivMMC memory,\nH = 1; count at $E051) hold a bit per bank (bank n is bit n AND 7 of byte n / 8); a second\nmap 40 bytes on ($E028/$E048) marks banks that only a call with H bit 7 set may reserve\nagain or free.\n1. L = 0 (rc_bank_total): E = the bank count.\n2. L = 1 (rc_bank_alloc): the highest free bank marked (also in the second map with H bit\n   7); E = its ID; none free is error 36 (rc_inuse).\n3. L = 2 (rc_bank_reserve), 3 (rc_bank_free): bank E marked or cleared (both maps); E out of\n   range is error 21 (rc_badparam).\n4. L = 4 (rc_bank_available): E = the free banks, counted a byte at a time.\n5. Another L: error 21.\nEntry: H = 0 ZX memory, 1 DivMMC memory (bit 7 see above), L = the reason, E = the bank ID.\nExit: carry and E, or NC with A = the error; MMU slot 7 restored.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, IX.","comment":"MMU slot 7's page"},
        "3746": {"comment":"NextReg $57 (MMU slot 7)"},
        "3750": {"comment":"BC = $253B"},
        "3751": {"comment":"...kept in D"},
        "3753": {"comment":"Page $10 (the allocation maps) at $E000"},
        "3757": {"comment":"The ZX memory's map"},
        "3761": {"comment":"A = its number of 8K banks"},
        "3764": {"comment":"H = 1: DivMMC memory?"},
        "3768": {"comment":"Its map instead"},
        "3772": {"comment":"And its number of banks"},
        "3775": {"synopsis":"B = the bank count; L picks the job.","comment":"B = the total"},
        "3776": {"comment":"L = 0: rc_bank_total"},
        "3778": {"comment":"To BANK_TOTAL"},
        "3780": {"comment":"L = 1: rc_bank_alloc"},
        "3781": {"comment":"Not 1: BANK_BY_ID"},
        "3783": {"comment":"The last bank's byte in the map"},
        "3789": {"comment":"IX = that byte"},
        "3793": {"comment":"The last bank's bit in C"},
        "3798": {"comment":"Rotated A times"},
        "3800": {"synopsis":"C rotated to the last bank's bit."},
        "3805": {"comment":"E = the banks left to try"},
        "3806": {"synopsis":"Tests one bank, downwards from the highest.","comment":"This bank free?"},
        "3810": {"comment":"Free: BANK_FOUND"},
        "3812": {"comment":"No: the bank below"},
        "3815": {"comment":"None free"},
        "3817": {"comment":"Still in this byte"},
        "3819": {"comment":"The byte before"},
        "3821": {"comment":"Go on there"},
        "3823": {"synopsis":"Error 36 (rc_inuse), no carry.","comment":"Error 36, rc_inuse"},
        "3825": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "3828": {"synopsis":"E = the free bank's ID.","comment":"E = the bank found"},
        "3829": {"synopsis":"Bank C of byte IX marked in use (in the second map too with H bit 7).","comment":"Marked in use"},
        "3833": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3836": {"comment":"H bit 7: also in the second map (+$28)"},
        "3840": {"comment":"Its byte there"},
        "3847": {"synopsis":"Success.","comment":"To BANK_OK"},
        "3849": {"synopsis":"L = 2 to 4: L = 4 counts; otherwise bank E's byte (IX) and bit (C).","comment":"L = 4: rc_bank_available"},
        "3852": {"comment":"To BANK_AVAILABLE"},
        "3854": {"comment":"The bank ID in range?"},
        "3856": {"comment":"No: rc_badparam"},
        "3858": {"comment":"Its byte in the map"},
        "3865": {"comment":"IX = that byte"},
        "3867": {"comment":"Its bit in C"},
        "3872": {"comment":"Bit 0 for 0"},
        "3874": {"synopsis":"C one bit up."},
        "3879": {"synopsis":"L = 2 reserves, L = 3 frees.","comment":"The map byte"},
        "3882": {"comment":"L = 2: rc_bank_reserve"},
        "3885": {"comment":"Free: reserved now"},
        "3886": {"comment":"To BANK_MARK"},
        "3888": {"comment":"In use: H bit 7 clear is an error"},
        "3890": {"comment":"To BANK_IN_USE"},
        "3892": {"comment":"With H bit 7: fine if in the second map"},
        "3896": {"comment":"Reserved again"},
        "3898": {"comment":"Otherwise in use"},
        "3900": {"synopsis":"rc_bank_total: E = the count.","comment":"rc_bank_total: E = the total"},
        "3903": {"synopsis":"rc_bank_free: a bank in use is freed; one in the second map only with H bit 7.","comment":"L = 3: rc_bank_free (L 5 and up: error)"},
        "3904": {"comment":"To BANK_BADPARAM"},
        "3906": {"comment":"Free already: done"},
        "3909": {"comment":"In the second map"},
        "3913": {"comment":"No: cleared"},
        "3915": {"comment":"...only with H bit 7"},
        "3917": {"comment":"Without it: rc_inuse"},
        "3919": {"synopsis":"The bank's bit cleared in both maps.","comment":"C = every bit but the bank's"},
        "3922": {"comment":"Cleared in the map"},
        "3926": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3929": {"comment":"And in the second map"},
        "3933": {"comment":"Written back"},
        "3936": {"synopsis":"Carry: success.","comment":"Carry: success"},
        "3937": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 7's old page restored (NextReg $57 is still selected).","comment":"MMU slot 7 back (NextReg $57 still selected)"},
        "3940": {"comment":"The old page written"},
        "3943": {"synopsis":"Error 21 (rc_badparam), no carry.","comment":"Error 21, rc_badparam"},
        "3945": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "3948": {"synopsis":"rc_bank_available: E = the free banks of the B in the map.","comment":"E counts the free banks"},
        "3950": {"comment":"C = bit 0"},
        "3952": {"synopsis":"One bank's bit. The count is checked only at a byte's end (DEC B's Z is tested after INC\nIX), so it assumes whole bytes.","comment":"This one free?"},
        "3958": {"comment":"Free: one more"},
        "3959": {"synopsis":"The next bit, the next byte after the eighth.","comment":"The next bit; carry after the byte's last"},
        "3961": {"comment":"Z when the count runs out"},
        "3964": {"comment":"The next byte (INC IX keeps the flags)"},
        "3966": {"comment":"Until the count ends at a byte's end"},
        "3968": {"comment":"To BANK_OK"},
        "3970": {"synopsis":"Runs a BASIC line kept elsewhere: copies it from HL (to its CR) to E_LINE, adds the $80 end\nmarker and moves WORKSP, STKBOT and STKEND past it, then runs it as IDE_BASIC does. Page 1\n(at its $2BF4 and $2BFA) runs this ROM's LOAD lines at $2034 and $2050 with it.\nEntry: HL = the line.","comment":"DE = E_LINE"},
        "3974": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3975": {"synopsis":"One byte of the line.","comment":"The line copied, its CR too"},
        "3979": {"comment":"Up to the CR"},
        "3983": {"comment":"DE = past it"},
        "3984": {"comment":"The end marker"},
        "3986": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "3987": {"comment":"WORKSP, STKBOT and STKEND past it"},
        "3996": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "3997": {"synopsis":"IDE_BASIC ($01C0): runs the tokenized BASIC line at HL, ended by CR (the API document's\ncall): $5B68 bit 0 set while it runs, ERR_NR = $FF, the stack frame saved by $27AD and\nrestored by $27D7 round ROM 1's RUN_LINE_SAVED.\nEntry: HL = the line.\nExit: ERR_NR = the BASIC error code - 1 ($FF: none).","comment":"DE = the line"},
        "3998": {"comment":"$5B68 bit 0: a run for ROM 2"},
        "4001": {"comment":"Set"},
        "4003": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no error"},
        "4007": {"comment":"The run's frame ($27AD)"},
        "4010": {"comment":"ROM 1's RUN_LINE_SAVED"},
        "4015": {"comment":"The frame undone ($27D7)"},
        "4018": {"comment":"$5B68 bit 0 cleared"},
        "4021": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "4024": {"synopsis":"IDE_INTEGER_VAR ($01C9): gets or sets a NextBASIC integer variable (the API document's\ncall). The words are not in this ROM: a plain variable is at $3264 + 2 x C, an array's\nelement at $3300 + 128 x C + 2 x L; the DivMMC calls ($07, $2855) and ($07, $2860) set and\nget them.\nEntry: B = 0 plain, 1 array; C = the variable (0-25); L = the index (0-63); H = 1 sets, 0\ngets; DE = the value to set.\nExit: carry and DE, or NC with A = 21 (rc_badparam).","comment":"Variable number 26 or more?"},
        "4027": {"comment":"Error 21, rc_badparam"},
        "4030": {"comment":"The index (L) and get/set (H) kept"},
        "4031": {"comment":"B = 1: an array?"},
        "4032": {"comment":"B = 0: a plain variable"},
        "4034": {"comment":"Arrays at $3300, 128 bytes each"},
        "4037": {"comment":"BC = the number x 128"},
        "4044": {"comment":"HL = the array's base"},
        "4045": {"comment":"B = get/set, C = the index"},
        "4046": {"comment":"Index 64 or more?"},
        "4049": {"comment":"Error 21, rc_badparam"},
        "4052": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4053": {"comment":"BC = the index"},
        "4055": {"comment":"To INTVAR_INDEX"},
        "4057": {"synopsis":"A plain variable: from $3264.","comment":"Variables at $3264, 2 bytes each"},
        "4059": {"comment":"HL = the base"},
        "4062": {"synopsis":"HL = the word's address; H decides.","comment":"HL = the word's address (BC x 2 on)"},
        "4064": {"comment":"B = H: 1 sets, 0 gets"},
        "4065": {"comment":"H = 0: INTVAR_GET"},
        "4067": {"comment":"DivMMC call ($07, $2855): the word set to DE"},
        "4071": {"comment":"Carry: success"},
        "4073": {"synopsis":"Gets the word into DE.","comment":"DivMMC call ($07, $2860): DE = the word"},
        "4077": {"comment":"Carry: success"},
        "4079": {"synopsis":"IDE_RTC ($01CC): reads the real-time clock (the API document's call) through the DivMMC call\n($00, $00F2), whose carry is inverted for the API: carry is success (BC = the date, DE = the\ntime, H, L), NC that no RTC is there (A = $3A, rc_notimp).","comment":"DivMMC call ($00, $00F2): the RTC read"},
        "4083": {"comment":"rc_notimp ($3A) if it fails"},
        "4085": {"comment":"Its carry turned over"},
        "4087": {"synopsis":"IDE_DRIVER ($01CF): calls the driver API (the API document's call; the same as M_DRVAPI)\nthrough the DivMMC call ($00, $00F5), whose carry is inverted for the API (carry: success).\nEntry: C = the driver ID, B = the call ID, HL, DE as the call needs.","comment":"DivMMC call ($00, $00F5): the driver call"},
        "4091": {"comment":"Its carry turned over"},
        "4093": {"synopsis":"IDE_MODE ($01D5): queries or changes the NextBASIC display mode (the API document's call).\n1. A = 1 changes it: B = the layer (0-2), C = layer 1's sub-mode (0-3); for layers 0 and 1\n   Layer 2 is hidden (port $123B and $5B7B = 0); ROM 1's $13F2 (in MODE_COMMAND) with A =\n   the layer and D = the sub-mode ($FF for layer 0, 1 for layer 2). Other values are error\n   21 (rc_badparam).\n2. Then, or with A = 0, the query: with page $10 in MMU slot 7, A = $5C7F bits 3-0 (the\n   mode). Layer 0: H = 22, L = 32, E = ATTR_P, D = 0, B = 8, C = 0, IX unchanged. Otherwise\n   IX = the window record at $F200 + A x 256: E = the ink (+$1F), D = the paper (+$20), C =\n   the flags (+$25), B = the character width (+$0F), L = the columns (+$1C), H = the lines\n   (+$12), or 32 with bit 6 of +$19 set (16 in lo-res).\nExit: carry and the above, or NC with A = 21.","comment":"A = 0: the query"},
        "4094": {"comment":"To MODE_QUERY"},
        "4096": {"comment":"A = 2 and up: error"},
        "4097": {"comment":"To MODE_BADPARAM"},
        "4099": {"comment":"Layer 3 or more: error"},
        "4102": {"comment":"To MODE_BADPARAM"},
        "4104": {"comment":"Layer 0 or 2?"},
        "4106": {"comment":"To MODE_LAYER_0_2"},
        "4108": {"comment":"Layer 1 with sub-mode 0-3"},
        "4111": {"comment":"Fine: MODE_L2_OFF"},
        "4113": {"synopsis":"Error 21 (rc_badparam), no carry.","comment":"Error 21, rc_badparam"},
        "4115": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "4117": {"synopsis":"Layer 0 (C = $FF) or layer 2 (C = 1).","comment":"Layer 0: C = $FF"},
        "4118": {"comment":"To MODE_LAYER_0"},
        "4120": {"comment":"Layer 2: C = 1"},
        "4122": {"comment":"To MODE_SET"},
        "4124": {"synopsis":"Layer 0: C = $FF."},
        "4126": {"synopsis":"Layers 0 and 1: Layer 2 hidden.","comment":"Layers 0 and 1: Layer 2 hidden"},
        "4128": {"comment":"Port $123B = 0"},
        "4133": {"comment":"$5B7B = 0 as well"},
        "4136": {"comment":"The layer and sub-mode back"},
        "4137": {"synopsis":"The mode set by ROM 1.","comment":"A = the layer, D = the sub-mode"},
        "4139": {"comment":"ROM 1's $13F2 (in MODE_COMMAND)"},
        "4144": {"synopsis":"The current mode's details.","comment":"MMU slot 7's page"},
        "4147": {"comment":"NextReg $57"},
        "4151": {"comment":"BC = $253B"},
        "4152": {"comment":"...kept in D"},
        "4154": {"comment":"Page $10 at $E000"},
        "4158": {"comment":"The current mode: $5C7F bits 3-0"},
        "4161": {"comment":"Bits 1-0 the layer, 3-2 the sub-mode"},
        "4163": {"comment":"Kept, with Z for layer 0"},
        "4164": {"comment":"The old page kept"},
        "4165": {"comment":"Layer 0: 22 lines, 32 columns"},
        "4168": {"comment":"E = ATTR_P"},
        "4172": {"comment":"Width 8, flags 0"},
        "4175": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "4176": {"comment":"Layer 0: done"},
        "4178": {"comment":"The mode's window record at $F200 + A x 256"},
        "4180": {"comment":"IX's high byte"},
        "4185": {"comment":"E = the ink"},
        "4188": {"comment":"D = the paper"},
        "4191": {"comment":"C = the flags"},
        "4194": {"comment":"B = the character width"},
        "4197": {"comment":"L = the columns"},
        "4200": {"comment":"H = the lines"},
        "4203": {"comment":"Reduced height (bit 6 at +$19)?"},
        "4207": {"comment":"Not reduced: as it is"},
        "4209": {"comment":"32 lines"},
        "4211": {"comment":"...or 16 in lo-res (mode 1)"},
        "4213": {"comment":"Not lo-res: 32"},
        "4215": {"comment":"Lo-res: 16"},
        "4217": {"synopsis":"MMU slot 7 restored; A = the mode, carry.","comment":"MMU slot 7 back"},
        "4218": {"comment":"The page written"},
        "4221": {"comment":"A = the mode"},
        "4222": {"comment":"Carry: success"},
        "4224": {"synopsis":"IDE_TOKENISER ($01D8, as documented): converts a BASIC line between plain text and tokens;\nthe work is done by the alternate ROM's $14A7.\nEntry: B = 0 to tokenise, 1 to detokenise; C = the 8K bank of the plain-text buffer, HL =\nits offset in it; DE = the tokenised line (detokenising).\n1. B above 1: error $15 (bad parameter).\n2. B and TV_FLAG kept as one byte each on the stack; TV_FLAG bit 7 cleared.\n3. $27AD keeps BASIC's state (ERR_SP, $5B6C, DEFADD and a GO SUB stack entry of type $2F);\n   the alternate ROM's $14A7 is called through $3E18; $27D7 puts the state back.\n4. TV_FLAG back. After a tokenised line, when CH_ADD is at or past E_LINE (a line being run\n   from the edit area), CH_ADD and NXTLIN move up by BC, the new line's length.\n5. ERR_NR = $FF.\nExit: as the alternate ROM leaves it (documented: carry; tokenising HL = E_LINE, BC = the\nlength, Z for a syntax error with DE = the characters taken; detokenising HL = the offset\nafter the text). Carry clear and A = the error on failure.","comment":"B above 1 is a bad parameter ($15)"},
        "4229": {"comment":"B kept as one byte on the stack"},
        "4231": {"comment":"TV_FLAG kept as one byte too"},
        "4236": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 7 cleared"},
        "4240": {"comment":"BASIC's state kept, a GO SUB stack entry put ($27AD)"},
        "4243": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's $14A7 does the conversion"},
        "4248": {"comment":"BASIC's state back ($27D7)"},
        "4251": {"comment":"HL = the result; L = TV_FLAG, H = B as given"},
        "4252": {"comment":"TV_FLAG back"},
        "4255": {"comment":"The results kept"},
        "4257": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "4259": {"comment":"Detokenising (B = 1)?"},
        "4262": {"comment":"Is CH_ADD at or past E_LINE?"},
        "4274": {"comment":"CH_ADD up by BC, the new line's length"},
        "4279": {"comment":"NXTLIN up by BC too"},
        "4286": {"synopsis":"The results back; ERR_NR = $FF (no report).","comment":"The results back"},
        "4289": {"comment":"ERR_NR = $FF: no report"},
        "4294": {"synopsis":"IDE_BROWSER ($01BA, as documented): the file browser, ROM 0's IDE_BROWSER, with the bytes at\n$D5B8 (the state byte) and $D5E9 kept over it and put back.\nEntry and exit: as ROM 0's IDE_BROWSER (HL = the filetypes, DE = the help text, A = the\ncapabilities).","comment":"HL and A kept"},
        "4296": {"comment":"A = the state byte at $D5B8"},
        "4299": {"comment":"L = the byte at $D5E9"},
        "4302": {"comment":"H = the state byte"},
        "4303": {"comment":"A back"},
        "4304": {"comment":"The two bytes kept, HL back"},
        "4305": {"comment":"ROM 0's IDE_BROWSER"},
        "4310": {"comment":"HL = the two bytes kept"},
        "4312": {"comment":"$D5B8 back"},
        "4316": {"comment":"$D5E9 back"},
        "4320": {"comment":"The browser's A and HL back"},
        "4323": {"synopsis":"Finds stream A's word in STRMS ($5C10, streams -3 to 15).\nEntry: A = the stream.\nExit: carry set, HL = the word's address, BC = the word (its channel's offset from CHANS\nplus 1, or 0 when closed); carry clear and A = $17 for a stream outside -3 to 15.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"A = 0-18 for streams -3 to 15"},
        "4325": {"comment":"Outside -3 to 15?"},
        "4329": {"comment":"Two bytes a stream"},
        "4330": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word in STRMS"},
        "4337": {"comment":"BC = the word"},
        "4340": {"comment":"HL back at the word"},
        "4343": {"synopsis":"A word dropped, then error $17.","comment":"The text's length dropped"},
        "4344": {"synopsis":"Error $17, carry clear.","comment":"Error $17"},
        "4348": {"synopsis":"Steps past an entry's word, then on to the next entry (TBL_FIND).","comment":"Past the routine's word"},
        "4350": {"synopsis":"Looks for character C in a table of 3-byte entries (a character, then a routine's address)\nended by 0.\nEntry: HL = the table, C = the character.\nExit: carry set and HL at the entry's word; carry clear when not found.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The entry's character"},
        "4352": {"comment":"The table's end? Carry clear"},
        "4354": {"comment":"The one looked for?"},
        "4357": {"comment":"Found: HL at its routine's word"},
        "4359": {"synopsis":"Reads \",n\" from the text (NUM_AFTER_COMMA) and checks that n is not above a limit that\ndepends on the screen mode (the low 4 bits of $5C7F): H in mode 1, L in the others.\nEntry: HL = the two limits, DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set and HL = n when there is one within the limit; carry clear with HL = n when\nit is above it; with no \",n\", carry clear and HL = the limit. DE and BC past it.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The screen mode, the low 4 bits of $5C7F"},
        "4364": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "4368": {"comment":"Mode 1: the limit in H"},
        "4369": {"synopsis":"HL = the limit for this mode, kept while the number is read.","comment":"HL = the limit"},
        "4371": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4372": {"comment":"A comma and a number?"},
        "4375": {"comment":"None?"},
        "4377": {"comment":"DE = n, HL = the text"},
        "4378": {"comment":"HL = the limit, the text kept"},
        "4379": {"comment":"Is n above the limit?"},
        "4382": {"comment":"Carry: within it"},
        "4383": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "4384": {"comment":"DE = the text, HL = n"},
        "4386": {"synopsis":"No number: HL = the limit, carry clear.","comment":"No number: HL = the limit"},
        "4388": {"synopsis":"Reads a comma and a number after it (NUM_PARSE) from the text.\nEntry: DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set and HL = the number; carry clear when the text has ended (Z) or goes on with\nsomething other than a comma (NZ).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The text's end?"},
        "4391": {"comment":"A comma next?"},
        "4394": {"comment":"No: carry clear, NZ"},
        "4397": {"comment":"Past the comma"},
        "4399": {"synopsis":"Reads a decimal number from the text, skipping spaces, up to the first other character or\nthe end of the text.\nEntry: DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set, HL = the number (0 for none); DE at the first other character, BC the\nlength left.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = 0 so far"},
        "4402": {"synopsis":"One character: a space is skipped, a digit taken in, anything else ends the number.","comment":"The text's end?"},
        "4404": {"comment":"Yes: carry set"},
        "4406": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "4407": {"comment":"A space is skipped"},
        "4411": {"comment":"Below '0'? Carry set: the number ends"},
        "4414": {"comment":"Above '9'? Carry set: the number ends"},
        "4418": {"comment":"The text kept"},
        "4419": {"comment":"HL x 2, kept in DE"},
        "4422": {"comment":"HL x 8"},
        "4424": {"comment":"HL x 10"},
        "4425": {"comment":"Plus the digit"},
        "4430": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"The next character"},
        "4434": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_OPEN ($0056, as documented): attaches stream A to the channel the text at DE\n(length BC) names:\n1. The stream must be closed or attached to K, S or P (error $17).\n2. One character: K, S or P (STD_CHAN_TABLE), the standard channels, words 1, 6 and $10.\n3. More: \"x>\" first names the kind, I, O, U, M, V, W or D (CHAN_TYPE_TABLE, small letters\n   too); with no \">\" the kind is I and all the text is the name. Its routine makes the\n   channel.\n4. The channel's offset goes into the stream's word in STRMS.\nEntry: A = the stream, DE = the text, BC = its length.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = $17 for a bad stream, $0E for any other\nfailure.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, the other register set.","comment":"The text's length kept"},
        "4435": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word, BC = its value"},
        "4438": {"comment":"A bad stream?"},
        "4440": {"comment":"Closed (0)?"},
        "4444": {"comment":"HL = the channel's letter (CHANS + word + 3)"},
        "4454": {"comment":"K, S or P may be replaced; others are error $17"},
        "4466": {"synopsis":"The text: one character names a standard channel, more a channel to make.","comment":"BC = the text's length"},
        "4467": {"comment":"The word's address kept"},
        "4468": {"comment":"The standard channels"},
        "4471": {"comment":"No text?"},
        "4475": {"comment":"Just one character?"},
        "4479": {"comment":"A = the first character"},
        "4480": {"comment":"One: a standard channel"},
        "4482": {"comment":"More: the kinds of channel to make"},
        "4485": {"comment":"Is the second character '>'?"},
        "4490": {"comment":"No '>': kind I, all the text the name"},
        "4494": {"comment":"Yes: A = the kind"},
        "4495": {"comment":"DE and BC past \"x>\""},
        "4499": {"synopsis":"Finds the kind's routine in the table at HL and calls it; DE (the channel's offset) goes\ninto the stream's word.","comment":"Capital letter"},
        "4501": {"comment":"C = the letter to find"},
        "4503": {"comment":"Its routine in the table at HL"},
        "4507": {"comment":"Not in the table?"},
        "4509": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "4513": {"comment":"The channel made: DE = its offset + 1"},
        "4516": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "4517": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "4519": {"comment":"The stream's word = DE"},
        "4524": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: called, it calls the routine at HL.","comment":"Called: runs the routine at HL"},
        "4525": {"synopsis":"A word dropped, then error $0E.","comment":"The word's address dropped"},
        "4526": {"synopsis":"Error $0E, carry clear.","comment":"Error $0E"},
        "4530": {"synopsis":"The standard channels a stream can be attached to (TBL_FIND): K SOPEN_K, S SOPEN_S, P\nSOPEN_P, then 0."},
        "4540": {"synopsis":"K: DE = 1, the channel at CHANS.","comment":"K: the word 1"},
        "4544": {"synopsis":"S: DE = 6.","comment":"S: the word 6"},
        "4548": {"synopsis":"P: DE = $10.","comment":"P: the word $10"},
        "4550": {"synopsis":"D = 0 and carry set: DE is the offset.","comment":"D = 0; carry: done"},
        "4554": {"synopsis":"The kinds of channel to make (TBL_FIND): I SOPEN_I, O SOPEN_O, U SOPEN_U, M SOPEN_M, V\nSOPEN_V, W SOPEN_W, D SOPEN_D, then 0."},
        "4576": {"synopsis":"U: a file opened for reading and writing: access 3 (exclusive read-write), DOS_OPEN's create\naction 2, open action 2.","comment":"U: create action 2, open action 2"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Access 3, exclusive read-write"},
        "4583": {"synopsis":"O: a file opened for writing: access 2 (exclusive write), create action 2, open action 4\n(the old one erased).","comment":"O: create action 2, open action 4"},
        "4586": {"comment":"Access 2, exclusive write"},
        "4590": {"synopsis":"I: a file opened for reading: access 5 (shared read), create action 0 (it must exist), open\naction 2.","comment":"I: create action 0, open action 2"},
        "4593": {"comment":"Access 5, shared read"},
        "4595": {"synopsis":"Makes a channel F for a file:\n1. The name (up to 255 characters) is copied to $DA31 in bank 7, ended by $FF, a character\n   at a time (BANK7_STACK, BANK0_STACK round each store).\n2. A free file number from $05F4 (a DivMMC call with B = 2); none: its error.\n3. The file is opened by DOS_OPEN ($0106) with C = the access and D, E the actions, with\n   bank 7 in.\n4. A 14-byte channel is made from F_CHAN_TEMPL (CHAN_NEW) with the file number at +$0D.\nEntry: A = the access, HL = the create (H) and open (L) actions, DE = the name, BC = its\nlength.\nExit: carry set and DE = the channel's offset plus 1; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The access kept"},
        "4596": {"comment":"The actions kept"},
        "4597": {"comment":"The name goes to $DA31"},
        "4600": {"comment":"Over 255 characters?"},
        "4604": {"comment":"B = the length"},
        "4607": {"synopsis":"255 characters at most.","comment":"B = 255 at most"},
        "4609": {"synopsis":"Copies the name to bank 7 a character at a time.","comment":"HL = the text, DE = $DA31"},
        "4610": {"synopsis":"One character: read with bank 0 in, written with bank 7 in.","comment":"A character, read with bank 0 in"},
        "4612": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "4615": {"comment":"Stored at $DA31 on"},
        "4617": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "4620": {"comment":"Every character"},
        "4622": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "4625": {"comment":"The name ended by $FF"},
        "4628": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "4631": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "4634": {"comment":"B = a free file number ($05F4)"},
        "4637": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "4640": {"comment":"Found one?"},
        "4642": {"comment":"No: the actions and access dropped"},
        "4645": {"synopsis":"A free file number in B: the file opened as it, then the channel made.","comment":"HL = the name"},
        "4648": {"comment":"D = the create action, E = the open action"},
        "4649": {"comment":"C = the access"},
        "4651": {"comment":"The file number kept"},
        "4652": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "4655": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN"},
        "4658": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "4661": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "4662": {"comment":"Failed: the error in A"},
        "4663": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4664": {"comment":"A 14-byte channel F, 13 bytes from F_CHAN_TEMPL"},
        "4676": {"comment":"HL at the channel's +$0D"},
        "4680": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "4681": {"comment":"Stored at +$0D"},
        "4684": {"synopsis":"The first 13 bytes of a channel F (a file), copied by CHAN_NEW: output and input both $5B4D\n(the RAM routine that selects ROM 0), the letter F, ROM 0's FCH_OUT ($0530), FCH_IN ($0527)\nand FCH_PTR ($0508), and the length $000E. The file number follows at +$0D."},
        "4697": {"synopsis":"M: a channel M over memory, from \"M>a,n\": a 19-byte channel from M_CHAN_TEMPL, with n at\n+$0D-$0E and a at +$11-$12. No \",n\", text left over or n = 0: nothing made, carry clear.","comment":"HL = the address"},
        "4700": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4701": {"comment":"HL = the length after a comma"},
        "4704": {"comment":"DE = the address"},
        "4705": {"comment":"No length: nothing made"},
        "4706": {"comment":"Text left over: nothing made"},
        "4709": {"comment":"A length of 0: nothing made"},
        "4712": {"comment":"The address and the length kept"},
        "4714": {"comment":"A 19-byte channel M, 13 bytes from M_CHAN_TEMPL"},
        "4726": {"comment":"HL at the channel's +$0D"},
        "4730": {"comment":"+$0D-$0E = the length"},
        "4734": {"comment":"Past +$0F-$10"},
        "4737": {"comment":"+$11-$12 = the address"},
        "4741": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4743": {"synopsis":"The first 13 bytes of a channel M (memory): output and input $5B4D, the letter M, ROM 0's\nMEM_OUT ($0033), MEM_IN ($049A) and MEM_POINTER ($049F), and the length $0013."},
        "4756": {"synopsis":"V: a channel V over a string variable, from \"V>name$\": a channel of the name's length + 16\nbytes from V_CHAN_TEMPL, its length at +$0B-$0C, the name (with its '$') copied to +$0F on\nand '(' after it. Text not ending in '$': nothing made, carry clear. X_PTR holds the text\nmeanwhile.","comment":"No text: nothing made"},
        "4759": {"comment":"HL at the text's last character"},
        "4764": {"comment":"'$'? Else nothing made"},
        "4769": {"comment":"BC = the channel's length, the text's + 16"},
        "4773": {"comment":"The text kept at X_PTR"},
        "4777": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "4778": {"comment":"The channel, 11 bytes from V_CHAN_TEMPL"},
        "4787": {"comment":"BC = the channel's length"},
        "4788": {"comment":"The channel's offset kept"},
        "4789": {"comment":"+$0B-$0C = the length"},
        "4796": {"comment":"Past +$0D-$0E"},
        "4799": {"comment":"DE = the channel's +$0F"},
        "4800": {"comment":"BC = the text's length"},
        "4804": {"comment":"The name copied to +$0F on"},
        "4809": {"comment":"Then '('"},
        "4812": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "4815": {"synopsis":"The first 11 bytes of a channel V (a string variable): output and input $5B4D, the letter V,\nROM 0's VCH_OUT ($3EF7), VCH_IN ($3EE0) and VCH_PTR ($3F03). SOPEN_V writes the length after\nthem."},
        "4826": {"synopsis":"D: a channel D, run by a driver, from \"D>X\" (X the driver's id), \"D>X>string\" or\n\"D>X,p1[,p2]\" (the forms the API document gives for the driver's open call):\n1. HL = DE = 0 for \"D>X\"; HL = the string and DE = its length after '>'; DE = p1 and HL = p2\n   (0 when missing) after ','.\n2. IDE_DRIVER ($01CF) with C = the id and B = $F9 (open channel) returns the channel's\n   handle in A.\n3. A 7-byte channel from D_CHAN_TEMPL with the id at +$05 and the handle at +$06.\nAnything else after the id, text left after the numbers, or a refusal by the driver: nothing\nmade, carry clear.\nExit: carry set and DE = the channel's offset plus 1.","comment":"No text: nothing made"},
        "4829": {"comment":"A = the driver's id"},
        "4832": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4833": {"comment":"HL = 0"},
        "4836": {"comment":"Nothing after the id?"},
        "4840": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "4843": {"comment":"'>': a string follows"},
        "4847": {"comment":"',': numbers follow"},
        "4851": {"synopsis":"Nothing made: the id dropped, carry clear.","comment":"Anything else: nothing made"},
        "4853": {"synopsis":"\",p1[,p2]\": DE = p1, HL = p2 (0 when missing); text left over makes nothing.","comment":"HL = the first number"},
        "4856": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4857": {"comment":"The second one, 0 when missing"},
        "4863": {"comment":"Text left over?"},
        "4865": {"comment":"BC = the first number"},
        "4866": {"comment":"Yes: nothing made"},
        "4868": {"synopsis":"Nothing after the id: HL = DE = 0.","comment":"Two exchanges: HL stays as it is"},
        "4869": {"synopsis":"The driver's open call: HL, DE as the form gives them; C = the id, B = $F9.","comment":"HL = the string after '>', or as it was"},
        "4870": {"comment":"DE = BC: the string's length, p1 or 0"},
        "4872": {"comment":"A = the driver's id"},
        "4873": {"comment":"C = the id, B = $F9: open channel"},
        "4876": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4877": {"comment":"IDE_DRIVER"},
        "4880": {"comment":"E = the id"},
        "4881": {"comment":"Refused: nothing made"},
        "4882": {"comment":"D = the handle the driver gave"},
        "4883": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4884": {"comment":"A 7-byte channel D, 5 bytes from D_CHAN_TEMPL"},
        "4896": {"comment":"HL at the channel's +$05"},
        "4901": {"comment":"+$05 = the id"},
        "4903": {"comment":"+$06 = the handle"},
        "4906": {"synopsis":"The first 5 bytes of a channel D (a driver's): output and input $5B4D, the letter D. The id\nand the handle follow at +$05 and +$06."},
        "4911": {"synopsis":"Three words dropped: nothing made."},
        "4912": {"synopsis":"Two words dropped: nothing made."},
        "4913": {"synopsis":"One word dropped: nothing made."},
        "4915": {"synopsis":"W: a channel W, a window of the screen, from \"W>row,column,height,width[,character\nwidth[,address]]\":\n1. Row 0-23 (0-11 in mode 1, the low 4 bits of $5C7F), column 0-31 (0-15), height up to 24\n   (12) less the row, width up to 32 (16) less the column (NUM_LIMITED).\n2. The character width, 3 to 8 (8 when not given), chooses a character set from\n   W_FONT_TABLE; a sixth number gives one's address instead (256 is taken off it; below\n   $4000 makes nothing).\n3. A 48-byte channel from W_CHAN_TEMPL: +$0D-$0E the character set, +$0F the character\n   width, +$10 a mask of that many top bits, +$11 the width, +$12 the height, +$13 the\n   column, +$14 the row, +$15 the right column, +$16 the bottom row, +$17 the row x 8, +$18\n   (the bottom row + 1) x 8, +$1C the characters a line (the width's pixels, doubled in mode\n   9, over the character width), +$1D 8 (16 in mode 9), +$1E the mode, +$1F the colour\n   (ATTR_P in mode 0, else the byte at $5B5E + mode for modes 1-4 or $5B60 + mode / 4\n   above), +$20 byte $20 of the mode's record at $F200 + 256 x mode for modes 1-4 (read with\n   MMU 7 = page $10), else 0, +$21 the column, +$22 the row x 8.\nAny number out of range: nothing made, carry clear. The width alone is not refused: without\nit the limit is taken, and one too large is kept as it is.\nExit: carry set and DE = the channel's offset plus 1.","comment":"HL = the row"},
        "4918": {"comment":"Above 255: nothing made"},
        "4921": {"comment":"24 rows"},
        "4923": {"comment":"The screen mode"},
        "4928": {"comment":"Mode 1?"},
        "4932": {"comment":"12 rows there"},
        "4934": {"synopsis":"The row must be below the mode's rows; then the column, height and width.","comment":"Past the last row?"},
        "4937": {"comment":"The row kept"},
        "4938": {"comment":"Column limits: 31, or 15 in mode 1"},
        "4941": {"comment":"HL = the column"},
        "4944": {"comment":"Too large?"},
        "4946": {"comment":"A = the column"},
        "4947": {"comment":"L = the row, H = the column"},
        "4949": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4950": {"comment":"The height's limit in mode 1: 12 less the row"},
        "4954": {"comment":"Otherwise 24 less the row"},
        "4958": {"comment":"HL = the height"},
        "4961": {"comment":"Too large?"},
        "4963": {"comment":"The height kept, HL = the column and row"},
        "4964": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4965": {"comment":"The width's limit: 32 less the column"},
        "4969": {"comment":"In mode 1: 16 less the column"},
        "4973": {"comment":"HL = the width (the limit when none)"},
        "4976": {"comment":"A = the width"},
        "4977": {"comment":"HL = the column and row"},
        "4978": {"comment":"HL = the height; the column and row kept"},
        "4979": {"comment":"H = the width, L = the height"},
        "4980": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4981": {"comment":"A character width?"},
        "4984": {"comment":"8 when none"},
        "4988": {"comment":"Above 255?"},
        "4992": {"comment":"Below 3?"},
        "4998": {"comment":"Above 8?"},
        "5002": {"comment":"The width kept"},
        "5003": {"comment":"A character set's address too?"},
        "5008": {"comment":"A = the width"},
        "5009": {"synopsis":"Takes the character set for width A from W_FONT_TABLE.","comment":"Kept"},
        "5010": {"comment":"The character sets by width"},
        "5013": {"comment":"Width 3 is the first word"},
        "5017": {"synopsis":"Moves on one word of W_FONT_TABLE per width above 3.","comment":"One word a width above 3"},
        "5022": {"synopsis":"HL = the character set from the table.","comment":"HL = the character set"},
        "5028": {"synopsis":"A character set's address given: below $4000 makes nothing; 256 is taken off it.","comment":"Below $4000? Nothing made"},
        "5033": {"comment":"256 off it"},
        "5034": {"synopsis":"Makes the channel when all the text was used, and fills it in.","comment":"Text left over? Nothing made"},
        "5038": {"comment":"The character set kept"},
        "5039": {"comment":"A 48-byte channel W, 13 bytes from W_CHAN_TEMPL"},
        "5051": {"comment":"HL at the channel's +$0D"},
        "5055": {"comment":"+$0D-$0E = the character set"},
        "5060": {"comment":"+$0F = the character width"},
        "5063": {"comment":"B = the width"},
        "5064": {"comment":"A = a mask of its B top bits"},
        "5065": {"synopsis":"Sets one more top bit of the mask, B times."},
        "5069": {"comment":"+$10 = the mask"},
        "5071": {"comment":"B = the width in characters, C = the height"},
        "5072": {"comment":"+$11 = the width, +$12 = the height"},
        "5076": {"comment":"DE = the column and row, the offset kept"},
        "5079": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5080": {"comment":"+$13 = the column, +$14 = the row"},
        "5084": {"comment":"A = the row"},
        "5085": {"comment":"D = column + width, E = row + height"},
        "5088": {"comment":"Less one: the right column and bottom row"},
        "5090": {"comment":"+$15 = the right column, +$16 = the bottom row"},
        "5094": {"comment":"A = the row x 8"},
        "5097": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5098": {"comment":"+$17 = the top pixel line"},
        "5100": {"comment":"+$18 = (the bottom row + 1) x 8"},
        "5107": {"comment":"+$19-$1B = 0"},
        "5114": {"comment":"HL back at +$0F"},
        "5119": {"comment":"C = the character width"},
        "5120": {"comment":"HL = the width in characters"},
        "5123": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "5124": {"comment":"HL = the width in pixels"},
        "5127": {"comment":"The screen mode"},
        "5132": {"comment":"Mode 9?"},
        "5134": {"comment":"Kept, with its Z"},
        "5135": {"comment":"A counts the characters"},
        "5137": {"comment":"Mode 9: twice the pixels"},
        "5140": {"synopsis":"Counts how many characters of width BC go into HL.","comment":"One more character of width BC?"},
        "5146": {"comment":"A = the characters that fit"},
        "5147": {"comment":"HL at +$1C"},
        "5148": {"comment":"+$1C = the characters a line"},
        "5150": {"comment":"The mode and its Z"},
        "5151": {"comment":"+$1D = 8"},
        "5155": {"comment":"16 in mode 9"},
        "5157": {"synopsis":"+$1E = the mode; then the colour by the mode.","comment":"+$1E = the mode"},
        "5160": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "5162": {"comment":"Mode 0?"},
        "5165": {"comment":"Mode 5 or above?"},
        "5169": {"comment":"Modes 1-4: kept"},
        "5170": {"comment":"DE = byte $20 of the record at $F200 + 256 x mode"},
        "5175": {"comment":"The interrupt state kept"},
        "5178": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "5180": {"comment":"MMU 7's page read and kept"},
        "5190": {"comment":"MMU 7 = page $10"},
        "5194": {"comment":"C = the byte there"},
        "5196": {"comment":"MMU 7's page back"},
        "5200": {"comment":"Interrupts back on if they were"},
        "5205": {"synopsis":"Modes 1-4: A = the byte at $5B5E + the mode.","comment":"A = the mode"},
        "5206": {"comment":"E = $5E + the mode"},
        "5210": {"synopsis":"Mode 0: the colour is ATTR_P.","comment":"Mode 0: A = ATTR_P"},
        "5215": {"synopsis":"Modes 5 and above: the byte at $5B60 + the mode / 4.","comment":"Modes 5 up: E = $60 + mode / 4"},
        "5221": {"synopsis":"A = the byte at $5B00 + E.","comment":"A = the byte at $5B00 + E"},
        "5225": {"synopsis":"+$1F = the colour, +$20 = C, +$21 the column, +$22 the row x 8.","comment":"+$1F = the colour"},
        "5227": {"comment":"+$20 = C"},
        "5229": {"comment":"A = the top pixel line"},
        "5230": {"comment":"D = the column"},
        "5231": {"comment":"+$21 = the column, +$22 = the top pixel line"},
        "5234": {"comment":"DE = the channel's offset + 1"},
        "5237": {"synopsis":"The character sets for character widths 3 to 8 (SOPEN_W_FONT): $EC00, $EC00, $EF00, $EF00,\n$F700 and $FB00 (used as they are; an address given in the text has 256 taken off)."},
        "5249": {"synopsis":"The first 13 bytes of a channel W (a window): output and input $5B4D, the letter W, ROM 0's\nWIN_PRINT_A ($275B), WAIT_KEY ($11E0) and WIN_FUNC_4 ($2B9A), and the length $0030."},
        "5262": {"synopsis":"Makes a channel of BC bytes at the end of CHANS, just before its end marker (at PROG - 1):\nthe room is made by ROM 0's CHANS_MAKE_ROOM (HL and BC handed over in the other set), the\nfirst DE bytes are copied from the template at HL and the rest cleared.\nEntry: HL = the template, DE = the bytes in it, BC = the channel's length.\nExit: HL = the channel, DE = its offset from CHANS plus 1 (the word for STRMS).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the other register set.","comment":"The template, its length and the channel's kept"},
        "5265": {"comment":"HL = PROG - 1, the end marker of CHANS"},
        "5269": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5270": {"comment":"HL and BC to the other set"},
        "5271": {"comment":"ROM 0's CHANS_MAKE_ROOM: BC bytes at HL"},
        "5276": {"comment":"DE = the channel"},
        "5277": {"comment":"HL = its length"},
        "5278": {"comment":"BC = the template's"},
        "5279": {"comment":"HL = the bytes to clear"},
        "5282": {"comment":"HL = the template, the count kept"},
        "5283": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5284": {"comment":"The template copied"},
        "5286": {"comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "5287": {"comment":"BC = the bytes left"},
        "5288": {"synopsis":"Clears the rest of the channel, BC bytes at DE.","comment":"All cleared?"},
        "5292": {"comment":"One more 0"},
        "5298": {"synopsis":"DE = the channel's offset from CHANS plus 1.","comment":"The channel kept"},
        "5299": {"comment":"DE = its offset from CHANS + 1"},
        "5308": {"comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "5310": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_CLOSE ($0059, as documented): closes stream A and its channel:\n1. A closed stream: carry set at once.\n2. The channel's letter chooses its routine from CLOSE_TABLE (an unknown one: error $17),\n   called with DE = the channel + 4; its failure gives error $12.\n3. The stream's word gets its first value back: the word from STRMS_DEFAULTS for streams -3\n   to 3, 0 for the others.\nEntry: A = the stream.\nExit: carry set for success; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; the other register set.\nCalled by ROM 1's CLOSE_STREAMS for streams 0-2.","comment":"HL = the stream's word, BC = its value"},
        "5313": {"comment":"A bad stream?"},
        "5314": {"comment":"Already closed: carry set"},
        "5318": {"comment":"The word's address kept"},
        "5319": {"comment":"HL = the channel's letter (CHANS + word + 3)"},
        "5326": {"comment":"C = the letter"},
        "5327": {"comment":"DE = the channel + 4"},
        "5328": {"comment":"The close routines by letter"},
        "5331": {"comment":"Not in the table?"},
        "5334": {"comment":"Error $17"},
        "5337": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "5341": {"comment":"Run it"},
        "5344": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "5345": {"comment":"Failed: error $12"},
        "5348": {"comment":"Streams 4 up get 0"},
        "5351": {"comment":"HL = the word's address less $5C1E"},
        "5356": {"comment":"Stream 4 or above?"},
        "5358": {"comment":"HL at its word in STRMS_DEFAULTS"},
        "5362": {"comment":"BC = that word"},
        "5365": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the stream's word.","comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "5366": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5369": {"synopsis":"K, S or P: nothing to close, carry set.","comment":"Success"},
        "5371": {"synopsis":"The close routines by channel letter (TBL_FIND): K, S and P SCLOSE_STD, F SCLOSE_F, M, V and\nW SCLOSE_RECLAIM, D SCLOSE_D, then 0."},
        "5396": {"synopsis":"The first words of STRMS for streams -3 to 3 ($5C10-$5C1D), put back when one is closed: 1,\n6, $0B, 1, 1, 6 and $10 (the same as ROM 3's STREAM_DATA)."},
        "5410": {"synopsis":"F: the channel's file (number at the channel's +$0D) closed by DOS_CLOSE ($0109) with bank 7\nin and the stack moved; then the channel removed (SCLOSE_RECLAIM).","comment":"HL at the channel's +$0D"},
        "5414": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "5415": {"comment":"The channel + 4 kept"},
        "5416": {"comment":"Bank 7 in"},
        "5419": {"comment":"DOS_CLOSE"},
        "5422": {"comment":"Bank 0 back"},
        "5426": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5427": {"synopsis":"Removes the channel from CHANS: its length (word at +$0B) and its address go to ROM 0's\nCHANS_RECLAIM (in the other set).\nEntry: DE = the channel + 4.\nExit: carry set.","comment":"HL at the channel's +$0B"},
        "5431": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "5434": {"synopsis":"Removes BC bytes at the channel (DE = the channel + 4).","comment":"DE back at the channel"},
        "5438": {"comment":"HL = the channel"},
        "5439": {"comment":"HL and BC to the other set"},
        "5440": {"comment":"ROM 0's CHANS_RECLAIM"},
        "5445": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5447": {"synopsis":"D: the driver's close call, IDE_DRIVER ($01CF) with C = the id (+$05), D = the handle\n(+$06), B = $FA; refused: error $24 (in use). Then the 7-byte channel removed.","comment":"HL = the channel + 4"},
        "5448": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5449": {"comment":"C = the driver's id (+$05)"},
        "5452": {"comment":"D = the handle (+$06)"},
        "5453": {"comment":"B = $FA: close channel"},
        "5455": {"comment":"IDE_DRIVER"},
        "5458": {"comment":"DE = the channel + 4"},
        "5459": {"comment":"Refused: error $24"},
        "5462": {"comment":"A channel D is 7 bytes long"},
        "5467": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_OUT ($005F, as documented): writes the byte in C (in the caller's set, moved to\nthe other) to the current stream, by ROM 0's CHAN_IO_ROM2 with DE = 0.\nChanges: the main and the other register set.","comment":"The caller's registers to the other set"},
        "5468": {"comment":"DE = 0: output"},
        "5471": {"synopsis":"Calls ROM 0's CHAN_IO_ROM2 with the DE given (0 output, 2 input, 4 pointer).","comment":"ROM 0's CHAN_IO_ROM2"},
        "5477": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_IN ($005C, as documented): reads a byte from the current stream into A, by ROM\n0's CHAN_IO_ROM2 with DE = 2; unlike the others the register sets are not exchanged first.","comment":"DE = 2: input"},
        "5482": {"synopsis":"IDE_STREAM_PTR ($0062, as documented): the pointer operation of the current stream (B in the\ncaller's set, moved to the other), by ROM 0's CHAN_IO_ROM2 with DE = 4.","comment":"The caller's registers to the other set"},
        "5483": {"comment":"DE = 4: the pointer"},
        "5488": {"synopsis":"Pages RAM bank 0 in at $C000 with this ROM (NextReg $8E = $0A), then swaps SP with the stack\npointer kept at $5B6A, the return address moved to the other stack. Undoes BANK7_STACK.\nChanges: AF' only.","comment":"RAM bank 0 at $C000, this ROM kept"},
        "5492": {"comment":"AF kept in AF'"},
        "5493": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "5494": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "5497": {"comment":"SP swapped with the one kept at $5B6A"},
        "5505": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5508": {"comment":"The return address on the new stack"},
        "5509": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "5511": {"synopsis":"Swaps SP with the stack pointer kept at $5B6A, the return address moved to the other stack,\nthen pages RAM bank 7 in at $C000 with this ROM (NextReg $8E = $7A). BANK0_STACK undoes it.\nChanges: AF' only.","comment":"AF kept in AF'"},
        "5512": {"comment":"AF = the return address"},
        "5513": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "5516": {"comment":"SP swapped with the one kept at $5B6A"},
        "5524": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5527": {"comment":"The return address on the new stack"},
        "5528": {"comment":"AF back"},
        "5529": {"comment":"RAM bank 7 at $C000, this ROM kept"},
        "5534": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_LINEIN ($01C3, as documented): line input in the current window channel: IX =\nCURCHL, then ROM 0's IDE_WIN_LINEIN. Entry and exit as that routine's.","comment":"IX = CURCHL, the window's channel"},
        "5538": {"comment":"ROM 0's IDE_WIN_LINEIN"},
        "5544": {"synopsis":"IDE_WINDOW_STRING ($01C6, as documented): prints a string to the current window channel: IX\n= CURCHL, then ROM 0's IDE_WIN_STRING. Entry and exit as that routine's.","comment":"IX = CURCHL, the window's channel"},
        "5548": {"comment":"ROM 0's IDE_WIN_STRING"},
        "5554": {"synopsis":"Checks that the handle at IX (a 19-byte record of the table at $E46C) is a swap one, type 2.\nExit: carry set when it is; carry clear and A = $3D (not a swap partition) otherwise.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The handle's type"},
        "5557": {"comment":"2, a swap one? Carry set"},
        "5561": {"comment":"No: error $3D"},
        "5565": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_POS ($00E8, as documented): returns the current block number of the swap handle at\nIX.\nExit: carry set, BC = the block (+$0C-$0D); carry clear and A = $3D for a handle that is not\na swap one.","comment":"A swap handle?"},
        "5569": {"comment":"BC = the current block"},
        "5577": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_MOVE ($00EB, as documented): sets the current block number of the swap handle at IX\nto BC.\nExit: carry set; carry clear with A = $15 when BC is above the last block number (+$0E-$0F),\nor $3D for a handle that is not a swap one.","comment":"A swap handle?"},
        "5581": {"comment":"HL = the last block number"},
        "5588": {"comment":"Is BC above it?"},
        "5593": {"comment":"Yes: error $15"},
        "5596": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the current block, carry set.","comment":"The current block = BC"},
        "5604": {"synopsis":"Works out the first sector of the current block of the swap handle at IX and moves the block\nnumber on one; a block past the last one is taken as block 0.\nExit: carry set, C:DE = the sector (block x the sectors a block, $07ED), B and HL as given;\ncarry clear and A = $3D for a handle that is not a swap one.\nChanges: AF, C, DE.","comment":"A swap handle?"},
        "5608": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "5610": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "5611": {"comment":"DE = the current block"},
        "5617": {"comment":"HL = the last block"},
        "5623": {"comment":"Past it?"},
        "5628": {"comment":"Then block 0"},
        "5631": {"synopsis":"C:DE = block DE times the sectors a block (+$0B); the block stored one on.","comment":"The block kept"},
        "5632": {"comment":"B = the sectors a block"},
        "5635": {"comment":"A:DE = the block x the sectors ($07ED)"},
        "5638": {"comment":"C:DE = the block's first sector"},
        "5639": {"comment":"HL = the block one on"},
        "5641": {"comment":"Stored as the current block"},
        "5647": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5648": {"comment":"B = the bank"},
        "5652": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_IN ($00E2, as documented): reads the current block of the swap handle at IX into\nmemory at HL with RAM bank B at $C000, and moves the block number on:\n1. RP_NEXT_SECTOR gives the block's first sector; SD_SECTOR_ADDR the card address.\n2. CMD18 (read many blocks), then for each sector of the block: the data token $FE, 512\n   bytes from port $EB to HL, two CRC bytes skipped.\n3. Bank 7 back at $C000 ($3E4C), CMD12 ends the reading ($195A).\nExit: carry set, HL past the data; carry clear and A = the error (0 when a token did not\ncome).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"C:DE = the block's first sector, the block one on"},
        "5655": {"comment":"Not a swap handle?"},
        "5656": {"comment":"The bank and the address kept"},
        "5658": {"comment":"HL:DE = the card address; Z for card 0"},
        "5661": {"comment":"Past the end?"},
        "5663": {"comment":"CMD18: read many blocks from there"},
        "5668": {"comment":"Refused?"},
        "5670": {"comment":"Wait for the data token $FE ($191D)"},
        "5673": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "5674": {"comment":"No token?"},
        "5676": {"comment":"B = the bank"},
        "5677": {"comment":"D = the sectors to read"},
        "5680": {"comment":"Bank B at $C000 ($3E4C)"},
        "5684": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5685": {"comment":"C = port $EB, the card's data"},
        "5687": {"synopsis":"One sector: 32 rounds of 16 bytes.","comment":"E = 32 rounds of 16 bytes"},
        "5689": {"synopsis":"16 bytes from the card to HL.","comment":"16 bytes from the card to HL"},
        "5721": {"comment":"512 in all"},
        "5725": {"comment":"The two CRC bytes skipped"},
        "5731": {"synopsis":"Waits while the card sends $FF; then the next token must be $FE.","comment":"Wait while the card sends $FF"},
        "5737": {"comment":"The next sector's token $FE?"},
        "5741": {"comment":"Every sector of the block"},
        "5744": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5745": {"synopsis":"Bank 7 back at $C000; the reading stopped (CMD12, $195A); BC back.","comment":"Kept"},
        "5746": {"comment":"Bank 7 back at $C000"},
        "5751": {"comment":"Z for card 0"},
        "5755": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "5756": {"comment":"CMD12 ends the reading ($195A)"},
        "5760": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "5761": {"comment":"BC as given"},
        "5763": {"synopsis":"No token: error 0, carry clear.","comment":"Error 0, carry clear"},
        "5768": {"synopsis":"The card refused: the address dropped, the error in A.","comment":"The address dropped"},
        "5771": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_OUT ($00DF, as documented): writes memory at HL with RAM bank B at $C000 as the\ncurrent block of the swap handle at IX, a sector at a time (IDE_SECTOR_WRITE), and moves the\nblock number on.\nExit: carry set, HL past the data; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL.","comment":"C:DE = the block's first sector, the block one on"},
        "5774": {"comment":"Not a swap handle?"},
        "5775": {"comment":"A = the sectors a block"},
        "5778": {"synopsis":"Writes one sector C:DE from HL, then the next, until the count in A runs out.","comment":"The count and the sector kept"},
        "5780": {"comment":"One sector written from HL, HL 512 on"},
        "5783": {"comment":"The sector back"},
        "5784": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5786": {"comment":"The next sector"},
        "5789": {"comment":"Carry into C?"},
        "5792": {"synopsis":"One sector fewer to write; carry set when all are done.","comment":"One sector fewer"},
        "5796": {"comment":"All written"},
        "5798": {"synopsis":"A write failed: the count dropped, the error in A.","comment":"The count dropped"},
        "5800": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_EX ($00E5, as documented): not implemented, error $3A, carry clear.","comment":"Error $3A, not implemented"},
        "5804": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_OPEN ($00D9, as documented): opens a swap file.\nEntry: A bits 6-0 = the block size in sectors (1-32); bit 7 clear: BC = the last block\nnumber wanted, from a system swap file (SWOPEN_SYSTEM); bit 7 set: BC = the file's name,\nended by $FF.\n1. A size of 0 or above 32: error $15.\n2. A named file: opened by $2226 (type 2; its record at IX = $F700, with the start sector at\n   +$01-$04 and the last sector at +$07-$0A; its first two sectors read to BC = $F75F), then\n   SWOPEN_FILE.\nExit: carry set and IX = the handle; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Bit 7: a file named at BC? (Z: no)"},
        "5806": {"comment":"A = the block size in sectors"},
        "5808": {"comment":"Kept, with the Z"},
        "5809": {"comment":"0 sectors?"},
        "5812": {"comment":"Above 32?"},
        "5814": {"synopsis":"A size out of range: error $15 (also the way out for the failures that follow, the size\ndropped).","comment":"Either: error $15"},
        "5818": {"comment":"The size and its Z"},
        "5820": {"comment":"No name: a system swap file"},
        "5822": {"comment":"Type 2: the file named at BC opened ($2226)"},
        "5827": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5829": {"comment":"A = the size"},
        "5830": {"synopsis":"Makes a swap handle from the file just opened by $2226 (its record at IX, its first sectors\nat BC), for blocks of A sectors:\n1. A file with a header ($23D5, Z): byte $20 of it must be 2 (else error 9); the first\n   sector, the header's, is skipped (one sector fewer, the start one on, $236A).\n2. The last block number: the last sector (+$07-$08) over the size (DIV_BC_DE), less one\n   unless the rest is the size less one: the whole blocks less one.\n3. RP_SET_SIZE, then a free slot of the table at $E46C ($0605; none: error $3C and $04F4)\n   gets the 19-byte record.\nExit: carry set and IX = the handle; carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"Kept"},
        "5831": {"comment":"A header in the first sectors? ($23D5, Z)"},
        "5834": {"comment":"BC = the file's last sector (+$07-$08)"},
        "5840": {"comment":"No header?"},
        "5842": {"comment":"HL at byte $20 of the header"},
        "5846": {"comment":"It must be 2, else error 9"},
        "5855": {"comment":"One sector fewer"},
        "5856": {"comment":"DE = the record's +$01, the start sector"},
        "5863": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5864": {"comment":"The start one on, past the header ($236A)"},
        "5868": {"synopsis":"BC over the size: the number of whole blocks.","comment":"A = the block size"},
        "5870": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "5873": {"comment":"BC = the sectors / the size, HL = the rest"},
        "5876": {"comment":"The size back"},
        "5877": {"comment":"A rest of size - 1?"},
        "5881": {"comment":"No: the last block number one less"},
        "5882": {"synopsis":"The size and the last block set, the current block 0.","comment":"A = the size"},
        "5883": {"comment":"Last block BC, size A, current block 0"},
        "5886": {"comment":"The record made kept"},
        "5888": {"comment":"IX = a free slot of the table at $E46C ($0605)"},
        "5891": {"synopsis":"A free slot found: the record copied into it, IX = the handle.","comment":"Kept"},
        "5892": {"comment":"None free: $04F4"},
        "5896": {"comment":"HL = the record made"},
        "5897": {"comment":"None free?"},
        "5898": {"comment":"DE = the free slot"},
        "5901": {"comment":"The 19-byte record copied; IX = the handle"},
        "5907": {"synopsis":"A system swap file: the files matching \"SWP-?.P3S\" ($2018) are listed at $FB70 by $1C99\n(13-byte entries); for each, its character goes into the name at $D827 (at $D837), the file\nis opened ($2226) and made a handle with 1-sector blocks (SWOPEN_FILE), then IDE_SWAP_RESIZE\nasks for the size and blocks wanted; too small a file is closed again.\nExit: carry set and IX = the handle; carry clear and A = $40 (no suitable swap partition)\nwhen none will do, or the listing's error.","comment":"The last block number kept"},
        "5908": {"comment":"The pattern \"SWP-?.P3S\" at $2018"},
        "5911": {"comment":"The matching files listed at $FB70 ($1C99)"},
        "5916": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5918": {"comment":"B = the files found; none?"},
        "5919": {"comment":"None: error $40"},
        "5924": {"comment":"HL = the first file's entry"},
        "5927": {"synopsis":"Tries one file of the list.","comment":"The count and the entry kept"},
        "5929": {"comment":"Its character into the name at $D827"},
        "5933": {"comment":"Type 2: open the file named at $D827 ($2226)"},
        "5941": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5943": {"comment":"A handle, blocks of 1 sector"},
        "5948": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5950": {"comment":"The entry, the count, last block, size back"},
        "5958": {"comment":"Room for the blocks wanted? (IDE_SWAP_RESIZE)"},
        "5961": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "5963": {"comment":"No: closed again"},
        "5966": {"synopsis":"The next entry of the list, until the count runs out.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "5967": {"comment":"The next entry, 13 bytes on"},
        "5971": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "5972": {"comment":"Every file found"},
        "5974": {"comment":"None big enough: error $40"},
        "5979": {"synopsis":"A file that will do: the entry, the count and the last block number dropped; carry set.","comment":"The entry, the count and the last block dropped"},
        "5982": {"comment":"The size dropped"},
        "5983": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5985": {"synopsis":"The last block number and the size back, then RP_SET_SIZE.","comment":"The last block number back"},
        "5986": {"comment":"The size back"},
        "5987": {"synopsis":"Sets the swap handle at IX for blocks of A sectors with BC the last block number (+$0B,\n+$0E-$0F), and the current block to 0 (RP_POS_STORE).\nExit: carry set.","comment":"+$0E-$0F = the last block number"},
        "5993": {"comment":"+$0B = the sectors a block"},
        "5996": {"comment":"The current block = 0"},
        "6002": {"synopsis":"Drops three words from the stack and returns, the error in A: the way out of RP_LAST_SECTOR\n(its return address and the two words IDE_SWAP_RESIZE pushed)."},
        "6003": {"synopsis":"Drops two words from the stack and returns, the error in A."},
        "6006": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_CLOSE ($00DC, as documented): closes the swap handle at IX: $04F4 with its record,\nthen its slot marked free (type 0).\nExit: carry set; carry clear and A = $3D for a handle that is not a swap one.","comment":"A swap handle?"},
        "6010": {"comment":"$04F4 with the handle's record"},
        "6013": {"comment":"The slot free again"},
        "6017": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6019": {"synopsis":"Works out the last sector of BC + 1 blocks of A sectors: L:DE = A x BC + A - 1.\nEntry: A = the sectors a block, BC = the last block number.\nExit: L:DE = the sector. A above 32: error $15, returning past the caller (RP_POP3).","comment":"A:HL = 0"},
        "6022": {"comment":"D = the size, the count of additions"},
        "6023": {"comment":"E = the size - 1"},
        "6025": {"comment":"Above 32 sectors? Error $15, past the caller"},
        "6031": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "6032": {"synopsis":"Adds BC into A:HL D times.","comment":"A:HL + BC"},
        "6035": {"comment":"The size times"},
        "6038": {"comment":"Plus the size - 1"},
        "6040": {"comment":"DE = the low word"},
        "6041": {"comment":"L = the high byte"},
        "6043": {"synopsis":"IDE_SWAP_RESIZE ($00EE, as documented): sets the swap handle at IX to hold BC + 1 blocks of\nA sectors, when their last sector is not above the file's (+$07-$09), with the current block\n0.\nExit: carry set; carry clear and A = $15 when they do not fit or A is above 32, $3D for a\nhandle that is not a swap one.","comment":"The size kept in D"},
        "6044": {"comment":"A swap handle?"},
        "6048": {"comment":"A = the size"},
        "6049": {"comment":"The size and the last block kept"},
        "6051": {"comment":"L:DE = the last sector the blocks need"},
        "6054": {"comment":"Within the file's last sector? High byte"},
        "6062": {"comment":"Then the middle byte"},
        "6070": {"comment":"Then the low byte"},
        "6076": {"synopsis":"Too big: the two words dropped, error $15.","comment":"The last block and the size dropped"},
        "6078": {"comment":"Error $15"},
        "6082": {"synopsis":"Divides BC by DE, a bit at a time, taking DE off HL and putting it back when it does not go.\nEntry: BC = the dividend, DE = the divisor.\nExit: BC = the quotient, HL = the remainder.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"A:C = the dividend"},
        "6083": {"comment":"HL = the remainder so far"},
        "6086": {"comment":"16 bits"},
        "6088": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "6089": {"synopsis":"One bit of the quotient (inverted, from the carry).","comment":"Inverted quotient bit in, the next bit out"},
        "6092": {"comment":"Into the remainder"},
        "6094": {"comment":"Take DE off; put it back if it did not go"},
        "6099": {"synopsis":"Every bit.","comment":"Every bit"},
        "6101": {"comment":"The last quotient bit in"},
        "6104": {"comment":"BC = the quotient, the bits inverted back"},
        "6110": {"synopsis":"The size of SD card C (0 or 1), from its CSD register (read by $18EB to $F700); reached from\n$0682 for units 5 and 6. Cf. IDE_CAPACITY ($01B4), which documents DEHL = the card's\ncapacity in 512-byte sectors.\n1. A card above 1: error $41 (invalid device).\n2. $18EB returns A nonzero: the layout with READ_BL_LEN (byte 5 bits 3-0), C_SIZE (byte 6\n   bits 1-0, byte 7, byte 8 bits 7-6) and C_SIZE_MULT (byte 9 bits 1-0, byte 10 bit 7):\n   (C_SIZE + 1) shifted left by READ_BL_LEN + C_SIZE_MULT - 7. B = 0.\n3. A = 0: a 22-bit size from bytes 7 (bits 5-0), 8 and 9, plus 1, times 1024; above 32 bits,\n   $FFFFFFFF. B = 2.\nExit: carry set, DE:HL = the size in 512-byte sectors, C = $80; carry clear and A = 0 when\nthe register could not be read.","comment":"Card 0 or 1?"},
        "6113": {"comment":"No: error $41"},
        "6116": {"comment":"Z for card 0"},
        "6118": {"comment":"The card's CSD register read to $F700 ($18EB)"},
        "6124": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6126": {"comment":"A = 0: the other layout"},
        "6129": {"comment":"L = CSD byte 6, H = byte 7"},
        "6132": {"comment":"HL = bits 1-0 of byte 6, then byte 7"},
        "6137": {"comment":"And bits 7-6 of byte 8: HL = C_SIZE"},
        "6146": {"comment":"C_SIZE + 1"},
        "6147": {"comment":"C = byte 9, B = byte 10"},
        "6151": {"comment":"Bits 1-0 of byte 9"},
        "6154": {"comment":"And bit 7 of byte 10: C_SIZE_MULT"},
        "6158": {"comment":"Plus READ_BL_LEN (byte 5), less 7"},
        "6166": {"comment":"DE:HL = C_SIZE + 1, shifted A times"},
        "6169": {"synopsis":"Shifts DE:HL left, A times.","comment":"DE:HL x 2"},
        "6174": {"comment":"A times"},
        "6177": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "6179": {"synopsis":"C = $80, carry set.","comment":"C = $80; carry: success"},
        "6183": {"synopsis":"The register could not be read: A = 0, carry clear.","comment":"Failed: A = 0"},
        "6186": {"synopsis":"The other layout: bytes 7-9 as the size field.","comment":"HL = bytes 8 and 9 of the CSD"},
        "6189": {"comment":"H = byte 8, L = byte 9"},
        "6192": {"comment":"A = bits 5-0 of byte 7: A:HL = the field"},
        "6197": {"comment":"Plus 1"},
        "6202": {"comment":"Times 4"},
        "6206": {"comment":"Times 256: DE:HL = (field + 1) x 1024"},
        "6210": {"comment":"B = 2"},
        "6212": {"comment":"Within 32 bits?"},
        "6214": {"comment":"No: $FFFFFFFF"},
        "6218": {"synopsis":"IDE_SECTOR_READ ($00AC, as documented as a low-level sector read): reads sector C:DE of the\npartition at IX (a 19-byte handle) into memory at HL, with RAM bank B at $C000, by CMD17\n($192C).\nExit: carry set, HL 512 bytes on; carry clear and A = the error (2 past the partition's\nend).\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "6219": {"comment":"Bit 7 clear: a read"},
        "6221": {"synopsis":"Reads (A bit 7 clear) or writes (bit 7 set) one sector for IDE_SECTOR_READ and\nIDE_SECTOR_WRITE: the card address (SD_SECTOR_ADDR), IX = the memory address meanwhile, RAM\nbank A AND $7F at $C000 ($3E4C), CMD17 ($192C) or CMD24 ($1961), then bank 7 back.","comment":"BC, DE and HL kept"},
        "6224": {"comment":"HL:DE = the card address; Z for card 0"},
        "6227": {"comment":"IX = the memory address, the handle kept"},
        "6229": {"comment":"Past the end?"},
        "6231": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6232": {"comment":"Bank A at $C000 ($3E4C)"},
        "6237": {"comment":"A write?"},
        "6243": {"comment":"CMD24: one sector written from IX ($1961)"},
        "6249": {"synopsis":"A read: CMD17, one sector to IX ($192C).","comment":"CMD17: one sector read to IX ($192C)"},
        "6253": {"synopsis":"IX back; bank 7 back at $C000; DE and BC back.","comment":"The handle back"},
        "6255": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6256": {"comment":"Bank 7 back at $C000"},
        "6261": {"comment":"The result back"},
        "6262": {"comment":"DE and BC as given"},
        "6265": {"synopsis":"IDE_SECTOR_WRITE ($00AF, as documented as a low-level sector write): writes memory at HL,\nwith RAM bank B at $C000, as sector C:DE of the partition at IX, by CMD24 ($1961).\nExit: carry set, HL 512 bytes on; carry clear and A = the error.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "6266": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: a write"},
        "6270": {"synopsis":"Works out the card address of sector C:DE of the partition at IX: the sector must not be\nabove the last one at +$07-$0A (else error 2), then the start at +$01-$04 is added; unless\n+$10 bit 1 is set (a block-addressed card) it is made a byte address (times 512).\nExit: carry set, HL:DE = the address (HL the high word), Z for card 0 (+$10 bit 0 clear);\ncarry clear and A = 2 when it is past the end.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"B = 0: the sector is C:DE"},
        "6272": {"comment":"Is the sector within the last one at +$07-$0A?"},
        "6289": {"comment":"Yes?"},
        "6291": {"comment":"No: error 2"},
        "6295": {"synopsis":"Within the partition: its start added, then the address made.","comment":"Plus the partition's start at +$01-$04"},
        "6302": {"comment":"HL:DE = the sector on the card"},
        "6311": {"comment":"Block-addressed card (+$10 bit 1)?"},
        "6317": {"comment":"No: times 256"},
        "6322": {"comment":"Then times 2: the byte address"},
        "6327": {"synopsis":"Z for card 0; carry set.","comment":"Z for card 0 (+$10 bit 0); carry"},
        "6333": {"synopsis":"Sends command A with the argument 0 (SD_COMMAND).","comment":"Argument 0"},
        "6335": {"synopsis":"Sends command A with the argument H, 0, 0, 0 (SD_COMMAND).","comment":"Argument H, 0, 0, 0"},
        "6337": {"comment":"D = E = L: the argument's low bytes"},
        "6339": {"synopsis":"Sends a command to SD card 0 (Z) or 1 (NZ) and waits for its response: port $E7 = $FE or $FD\nselects the card, a byte is clocked, then the command, the argument H, L, D, E and the CRC\nbyte $FF go to port $EB; $190F waits for a byte other than $FF.\nEntry: A = the command ($40 + its number: $49 CMD9, $51 CMD17, $52 CMD18, $58 CMD24, $4C\nCMD12), HLDE = the argument.\nExit: carry set when the response is 0; carry clear and A = the response otherwise.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"B = $FF in place of a CRC"},
        "6341": {"comment":"C = the command byte","synopsis":"Sends one command to an SD card over the SPI ports and waits for its first answer byte:\n1. Port $E7 = $FE (card 0, Z) or $FD (card 1, NZ): that card's chip select low (zxnext.vhd:\n   port $E7 bits 0 and 1 are the SD0/SD1 selects); one byte is clocked in through port $EB.\n2. The command byte, the four argument bytes and B go out through port $EB.\n3. SD_WAIT_BYTE gives the answer (R1).\nThe card stays selected; SD_DESELECT ends the exchange. Also called by SD_CARD_INIT for CMD0\nand CMD8.\nEntry: A = the command byte, H, L, D, E = the argument, B = the CRC byte, Z = card 0, NZ =\ncard 1.\nExit: carry, A = 0 when R1 is 0; else NC, A = R1 ($FF after a timeout).\nChanges: AF, BC."},
        "6342": {"comment":"$FE: card 0's chip select low"},
        "6346": {"comment":"$FD: card 1's"},
        "6348": {"synopsis":"The chip select chosen: A = $FE or $FD.","comment":"Card selected"},
        "6350": {"comment":"One byte clocked before the command"},
        "6352": {"comment":"The command byte out through the SPI port"},
        "6353": {"comment":"To port $EB, the card's data"},
        "6357": {"comment":"The argument, most significant byte first"},
        "6369": {"comment":"Then the CRC byte"},
        "6372": {"comment":"A = the card's answer (R1)"},
        "6375": {"comment":"R1 not 0? NC, A = R1"},
        "6377": {"comment":"R1 = 0: carry"},
        "6378": {"comment":"Carry: accepted"},
        "6379": {"synopsis":"Starts an SD card and reads its 16-byte CSD register:\n1. SD_CARD_INIT on the card (Z = card 0); its D (0 block, 1 byte addressing) is kept.\n2. CMD9 ($49) with argument 0; after the data token $FE, 18 bytes (the CSD and its two CRC\n   bytes) go to HL.\n3. The card is deselected (SD_DESELECT).\nA failed SD_CARD_INIT is not tested: CMD9 is sent anyway.\nCalled by IDE_INTERFACE (HL = $E090) and $17E9.\nEntry: HL = an 18-byte buffer, A and Z = the card (0 with Z, 1 with NZ).\nExit: carry, A = D from SD_CARD_INIT when read; NC when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Buffer kept"},
        "6380": {"comment":"Card choice kept"},
        "6381": {"comment":"Start the card"},
        "6385": {"comment":"D = its addressing kind"},
        "6386": {"comment":"CMD9: read the CSD register"},
        "6388": {"comment":"Sent with argument 0"},
        "6391": {"comment":"Addressing kind back"},
        "6392": {"comment":"Buffer back"},
        "6393": {"comment":"No answer or R1 not 0? Fail"},
        "6395": {"comment":"Wait for the data token"},
        "6398": {"comment":"Token?"},
        "6400": {"comment":"None: NC"},
        "6401": {"comment":"Fail"},
        "6403": {"synopsis":"The token came: 18 bytes into HL.","comment":"18 bytes: the CSD and two CRC bytes"},
        "6407": {"synopsis":"One byte (INI).","comment":"Into the buffer at HL"},
        "6409": {"comment":"Until 18 bytes are in"},
        "6411": {"comment":"Carry, A = the addressing kind"},
        "6412": {"comment":"A = the addressing kind"},
        "6413": {"synopsis":"Deselects the card, result kept.","comment":"Deselect and return"},
        "6415": {"synopsis":"Reads port $EB until a byte other than $FF comes, at most 50 x 256 times.\nExit: A = the byte, NZ; or A = $FF and Z after the last try.\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"50 x 256 tries"},
        "6418": {"synopsis":"One read of the SPI port.","comment":"A byte from the card"},
        "6420": {"comment":"Anything but $FF ends the wait"},
        "6423": {"comment":"Next try"},
        "6426": {"comment":"Next round of 256"},
        "6428": {"comment":"Timed out: A = $FF, Z"},
        "6429": {"synopsis":"Waits for a data token: up to ten SD_WAIT_BYTE calls, stopping at the first byte of $FE or\nbelow.\nExit: Z, A = $FE when the start token came; NZ, A = the byte for a lower one (an error\ntoken). After ten timeouts it also returns Z (with A = $FF), so its callers take that as the\ntoken.\nChanges: AF, BC, E.","comment":"Ten waits"},
        "6431": {"synopsis":"One wait.","comment":"Next byte that is not $FF"},
        "6434": {"comment":"$FE, the data token? Z"},
        "6438": {"comment":"Below $FE (an error token)? Stop, NZ"},
        "6440": {"comment":"$FF: wait again"},
        "6443": {"synopsis":"Z for the token."},
        "6444": {"synopsis":"Reads one 512-byte block from an SD card (called from $186A):\n1. CMD17 ($51) with the argument HLDE (a block number or a byte address, by the card's\n   kind).\n2. After the data token, 512 bytes to IX; the two CRC bytes are read and dropped.\n3. The card is deselected.\nEntry: H, L, D, E = the argument, IX = the buffer, Z = card 0, NZ = card 1.\nExit: carry when read; NC, A = 0 (rc_ready, drive not ready) when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"CMD17: read one block"},
        "6446": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6449": {"synopsis":"A = 0 for a failure.","comment":"A = 0 (rc_ready) for a failure"},
        "6451": {"comment":"R1 not 0? Fail"},
        "6453": {"comment":"Wait for the data token"},
        "6456": {"comment":"Token?"},
        "6458": {"comment":"No: NC"},
        "6459": {"comment":"Fail"},
        "6461": {"synopsis":"The data: two runs of 256 bytes into IX.","comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "6464": {"comment":"B = 0 (256 bytes), C = SPI port $EB"},
        "6467": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "6471": {"comment":"The two CRC bytes, dropped"},
        "6475": {"comment":"Second CRC byte"},
        "6477": {"comment":"Carry: read"},
        "6478": {"synopsis":"Ends an exchange with an SD card: one byte clocked in, port $E7 = $FF (no card selected),\nanother byte clocked in. AF is kept, so the result of the exchange goes back to the caller.\nAlso the end of SD_READ_CSD, SD_READ_BLOCK, SD_WRITE_BLOCK and SD_CARD_INIT ($1A4C).","comment":"Result kept"},
        "6479": {"comment":"One byte clocked"},
        "6481": {"comment":"No card selected"},
        "6483": {"comment":"All four chip selects high"},
        "6486": {"comment":"One more byte"},
        "6488": {"comment":"Result back"},
        "6490": {"synopsis":"CMD12 ($4C) with argument 0 to the card (Z = card 0), then SD_DESELECT. SD_CARD_INIT sends\nit first; also called from $167C.\nExit: carry when R1 was 0.","comment":"CMD12, argument 0"},
        "6492": {"comment":"Then deselect"},
        "6495": {"comment":"Deselect"},
        "6497": {"synopsis":"Writes one 512-byte block to an SD card (called from $1864):\n1. CMD24 ($58) with the argument HLDE.\n2. The start token $FE, 512 bytes from IX, two dummy CRC bytes $FF.\n3. The data response must have status 5 (accepted); then the card's busy $00 bytes are\n   waited out.\n4. CMD13 ($4D) reads the status: a second status byte of 0 is success.\nEntry: H, L, D, E = the argument, IX = the data, Z = card 0, NZ = card 1.\nExit: carry, A = 0 when written; else NC with A = 0 (rc_ready: no answer, data refused), 1\n(rc_wp: second status byte bit 0, 1 or 5 set) or 3 (rc_crc: other status bits).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"Card choice kept"},
        "6498": {"comment":"CMD24: write one block"},
        "6500": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6503": {"comment":"R1 not 0? Fail"},
        "6505": {"comment":"The start token"},
        "6509": {"comment":"Port $EB, B = 0 (256 bytes)"},
        "6512": {"comment":"HL = the data"},
        "6515": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "6519": {"comment":"Two dummy CRC bytes"},
        "6525": {"comment":"Second CRC byte"},
        "6527": {"comment":"The data response"},
        "6530": {"comment":"Its status: 5 = accepted?"},
        "6532": {"comment":"Accepted?"},
        "6534": {"comment":"Refused? Fail"},
        "6536": {"synopsis":"Waits while the card answers $00 (busy).","comment":"Wait while the card is busy ($00)"},
        "6539": {"comment":"Still $00?"},
        "6542": {"comment":"Card choice back"},
        "6543": {"comment":"CMD13: read the status"},
        "6545": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "6546": {"comment":"Sent with argument 0"},
        "6550": {"comment":"R1 not 0? Fail"},
        "6552": {"comment":"The second status byte"},
        "6554": {"comment":"0? Carry, A = 0: written"},
        "6555": {"comment":"Carry for success"},
        "6558": {"comment":"Lock or write protect bits?"},
        "6560": {"comment":"A = 1 (rc_wp), NC"},
        "6564": {"comment":"Other errors: A = 3 (rc_crc), NC"},
        "6568": {"synopsis":"A failure with the card choice still on the stack.","comment":"Drop the card choice"},
        "6569": {"synopsis":"NC, A = 0 (rc_ready).","comment":"A = 0 (rc_ready), NC"},
        "6572": {"synopsis":"Deselects the card, result kept.","comment":"Deselect and return"},
        "6574": {"synopsis":"IDE_INTERFACE (jump table $00A3; the API document: initialise card interfaces): SD_READ_CSD\non SD card 0, then card 1, both into $E090, counting the cards that answer. Also called by\nIDE_MOUNT_SD ($1B4E).\nExit: A = the number of SD cards found (0-2).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"B = 2 cards, C = count 0"},
        "6577": {"synopsis":"One card: A = 2 - B (0, then 1), Z for card 0.","comment":"A = 0, then 1: Z for card 0"},
        "6580": {"comment":"Buffer for the CSD"},
        "6584": {"comment":"Start the card and read its CSD"},
        "6588": {"comment":"Answered? Count it"},
        "6590": {"comment":"No: C unchanged"},
        "6591": {"synopsis":"The card answered: C + 1.","comment":"Count it"},
        "6592": {"comment":"Next card"},
        "6594": {"comment":"A = the cards found"},
        "6595": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6596": {"synopsis":"Puts an SD card into SPI mode and finds how it is addressed:\n1. SD_STOP_CMD; CMD0 ($40) with its CRC $95 must answer 1 (idle).\n2. CMD8 ($48) with argument $000001AA and its CRC $87: an illegal-command answer (R1 bit 2)\n   leaves the ACMD41 argument 0; an answer of 1 must have 1 in the low nibble of its third\n   byte and $AA in its fourth, which makes the argument $40000000. Other answers retry CMD8,\n   up to 120 x 256 times.\n3. CMD55 ($77) and ACMD41 ($69) with that argument, repeated while the answer is 1 (no\n   limit); 0 goes on, anything else fails.\n4. CMD58 (SD_READ_OCR): bits 31 and 30 of the OCR both set leave D = 0 (block addressed);\n   otherwise CMD16 ($50) sets 512-byte blocks and D = 1 (byte addressed).\n5. The card is deselected.\nCalled by SD_READ_CSD.\nEntry: Z = card 0, NZ = card 1 (A kept with it on the stack).\nExit: carry, D = 0 or 1 when the card is ready; NC when not.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"Card choice kept"},
        "6597": {"comment":"CMD12 first"},
        "6600": {"comment":"Card choice back"},
        "6601": {"comment":"Card choice on the stack for the steps below"},
        "6602": {"comment":"CMD0: go idle"},
        "6609": {"comment":"With its CRC $95"},
        "6611": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6614": {"comment":"R1 must be 1 (idle)"},
        "6617": {"comment":"Retries: 120 rounds of 256"},
        "6620": {"synopsis":"One try of CMD8.","comment":"Card choice"},
        "6622": {"comment":"Retry count kept"},
        "6623": {"comment":"CMD8 with argument $000001AA"},
        "6631": {"comment":"With its CRC $87"},
        "6633": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6637": {"comment":"Illegal command? An older card"},
        "6639": {"comment":"H = 0: the ACMD41 argument"},
        "6643": {"comment":"R1 not 1? Retry"},
        "6646": {"comment":"The answer's four bytes: H and L dropped later"},
        "6648": {"comment":"First answer byte"},
        "6650": {"comment":"Second"},
        "6654": {"comment":"Third: the low nibble in D"},
        "6659": {"comment":"Fourth must echo $AA"},
        "6664": {"comment":"Low nibble not 1? Fail"},
        "6667": {"comment":"H = $40: argument bit 30 set"},
        "6669": {"synopsis":"CMD55 and ACMD41 with argument H, 0, 0, 0.","comment":"Card choice"},
        "6670": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "6671": {"comment":"Argument kept"},
        "6672": {"comment":"CMD55: an application command follows"},
        "6674": {"comment":"Sent with argument 0"},
        "6678": {"comment":"Card choice again"},
        "6680": {"comment":"Argument kept"},
        "6681": {"comment":"ACMD41, argument H, 0, 0, 0"},
        "6683": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6687": {"comment":"R1 = 0? Ready"},
        "6689": {"comment":"R1 = 1 (still idle)? Again"},
        "6692": {"synopsis":"An unexpected answer: fails.","comment":"Anything else: fail"},
        "6694": {"synopsis":"Counts one CMD8 retry.","comment":"Next CMD8 retry"},
        "6697": {"comment":"Next round"},
        "6699": {"comment":"Retries spent: fail"},
        "6701": {"synopsis":"ACMD41 answered 0: reads the OCR.","comment":"Card choice"},
        "6703": {"comment":"Read the OCR"},
        "6706": {"comment":"No answer? Fail"},
        "6708": {"comment":"D = 0 when bits 31 and 30 are both set"},
        "6709": {"comment":"Block addressed: done"},
        "6711": {"comment":"Byte addressed: card choice"},
        "6713": {"comment":"CMD16 with argument $200: 512-byte blocks"},
        "6720": {"comment":"Sent"},
        "6723": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6725": {"comment":"D = 1: byte addressed"},
        "6727": {"synopsis":"Carry: the card is ready.","comment":"Carry: ready"},
        "6730": {"synopsis":"NC: the card did not start.","comment":"NC: failed"},
        "6731": {"synopsis":"Drops the card choice and deselects.","comment":"Drop the card choice"},
        "6732": {"comment":"Deselect and return"},
        "6735": {"synopsis":"CMD58 ($7A) with argument 0 and its four answer bytes: H = the first with only bits 7 and 6\n(OCR bits 31 and 30), L and E the next two, the last dropped. The card stays selected.\nEntry: Z = card 0, NZ = card 1.\nExit: NC when R1 was not 0; else carry, and A = 0 with Z when both bits are set.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"CMD58: read the OCR"},
        "6737": {"comment":"Sent with argument 0"},
        "6740": {"comment":"R1 not 0? NC"},
        "6741": {"comment":"OCR bits 31 and 30"},
        "6743": {"comment":"Top byte, those bits only"},
        "6747": {"comment":"Next two bytes into L and E"},
        "6751": {"comment":"Third byte to E"},
        "6755": {"comment":"Last byte dropped"},
        "6757": {"comment":"A = 0 when both bits are set"},
        "6759": {"comment":"Carry: read"},
        "6760": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6761": {"synopsis":"Tests whether an SD card is block addressed: SD_READ_OCR's two top bits both set. Called by\n$07D5 (which then sets bit 1 of a partition record's byte $10). The card is left selected.\nEntry: Z = card 0, NZ = card 1.\nExit: carry when both bits are set, NC otherwise.","comment":"Read the OCR"},
        "6764": {"comment":"Failed: NC"},
        "6765": {"comment":"Both bits set: carry"},
        "6766": {"comment":"Else NC"},
        "6768": {"synopsis":"IDE_VERSION (jump table $00A0; the API document: get IDEDOS version number): DE = $0109,\ncarry.","comment":"Version $0109"},
        "6771": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "6773": {"synopsis":"IDE_MOUNT (jump table $01D2; the API document: unmount or remount the SD cards):\n1. A = 1: IDE_MOUNT_SD. Other values but 0: NC, A = $15 (rc_badparam).\n2. A = 0: DOS_CLOSE on files 15 down to 0.\n3. IDE_SWAP_CLOSE ($00DC) with IX at each of the 20 19-byte partition records from $E46C,\n   results ignored.\n4. IDE_DOS_MAPPING on drives A-P; a drive mapped to unit $FF (a filesystem image) is\n   unmapped (IDE_DOS_UNMAP); then every drive A-P is unmapped.\n5. Two calls into the DivMMC memory (bank 0, $318A and $3167) with B = 1.\nAfter each call in steps 2 and 4 MOUNT_ERR_CHECK returns at once with NC and the error,\nexcept for rc_number and rc_invpartition.\nExit: carry when done; NC, A = the error code.","comment":"A = 1? Mount"},
        "6775": {"comment":"To IDE_MOUNT_SD"},
        "6777": {"comment":"Not 0? NC, A = $15 (rc_badparam)"},
        "6781": {"comment":"Files 15 down to 0"},
        "6783": {"synopsis":"Closes file B - 1."},
        "6784": {"comment":"B = the file number"},
        "6785": {"comment":"DOS_CLOSE"},
        "6789": {"comment":"Stop on a real error"},
        "6792": {"comment":"Next file"},
        "6794": {"comment":"20 partition records, 19 bytes each"},
        "6800": {"synopsis":"One partition record.","comment":"Count kept"},
        "6801": {"comment":"Record kept"},
        "6803": {"comment":"IDE_SWAP_CLOSE, result ignored"},
        "6808": {"comment":"Next record"},
        "6811": {"comment":"Next record, 19 bytes on"},
        "6814": {"comment":"Next"},
        "6816": {"comment":"Drives A to P"},
        "6818": {"synopsis":"One drive letter (B): unmapped if it is an image.","comment":"Letter kept"},
        "6819": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "6820": {"comment":"BC = 0 as the buffer"},
        "6823": {"comment":"IDE_DOS_MAPPING"},
        "6827": {"comment":"Stop on a real error"},
        "6830": {"comment":"Not mapped? Next"},
        "6832": {"comment":"Not unit $FF (an image)? Next"},
        "6833": {"comment":"Not an image: next"},
        "6835": {"comment":"Letter kept"},
        "6836": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "6837": {"comment":"IDE_DOS_UNMAP"},
        "6841": {"comment":"Stop on a real error"},
        "6844": {"synopsis":"Next letter, up to P.","comment":"Next letter"},
        "6846": {"comment":"Up to P"},
        "6848": {"comment":"Next letter"},
        "6850": {"comment":"Then every drive A to P"},
        "6852": {"synopsis":"Unmaps drive letter B."},
        "6853": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "6854": {"comment":"IDE_DOS_UNMAP"},
        "6858": {"comment":"Stop on a real error"},
        "6861": {"comment":"Next letter"},
        "6863": {"comment":"Up to P"},
        "6865": {"comment":"Next letter"},
        "6867": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "6869": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $318A"},
        "6873": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "6875": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $3167"},
        "6879": {"synopsis":"IDE_INIT (jump table $00A6; the API document: initialise IDEDOS): nothing to do, carry set.\nThe two bytes are IDE_MOUNT's own end.","comment":"Carry: done"},
        "6881": {"synopsis":"The result of a call in IDE_MOUNT: carry, rc_number ($1D, file not open) and rc_invpartition\n($38) go back to go on; any other error drops the return address, so IDE_MOUNT itself\nreturns with NC and A = the error.","comment":"Success? Go on"},
        "6882": {"comment":"rc_number (file not open)? Go on"},
        "6884": {"comment":"Back to go on"},
        "6885": {"comment":"rc_invpartition? Go on"},
        "6887": {"comment":"Back to go on"},
        "6888": {"comment":"Other errors: NC"},
        "6889": {"comment":"Drop the return: IDE_MOUNT returns with it"},
        "6891": {"synopsis":"Mounts the SD cards and maps the drives (IDE_MOUNT with A = 1; page 1's SD_REMOUNT calls it\nwith its own A):\n1. $5B8A-$5BFE (117 bytes) are saved at $DA33 and SP at $DA31; the stack is moved to $5BFF.\n2. The default drive is the DivMMC memory's byte at $2007 (bank 0) when $2008 holds its\n   complement, else 2 (C:).\n3. $DBA0-$E399 and $E3F7-$F510 are zeroed, then $E300-$E32C, $E36D-$E399 and $E3CA-$E3E9 set\n   to $FF.\n4. IDE_INTERFACE counts the cards; the DivMMC memory's $04DB, $04DC (bank 0, on $2300-$312C\n   and $2300-$232F), $04DB (bank $0D, $37F0-$3FFC) and $0166 (HL = $2300, DE = 0) are\n   called.\n5. MAP_UNITS_2: the partitions of units 0 and 1 from drive C:.\n6. Entry A = 0 only: LOAD_SYSTEM.\n7. The DivMMC memory's $0166 with HL = $2302, DE = $024D; SD_UNITS_SETUP with the entry A.\n8. Unit 4 (the RAMdisk, as the API document numbers it) as M:, then units 5 and 6 from the\n   next free letter.\n9. The images c:/nextzxos/DRV-x and CPM-x (.P3D or .DSK) are mapped to drive x (CATALOG_SYS,\n   MAP_IMAGES).\n10. $5B8A-$5BFE and SP are restored; the default drive is set (DOS_SET_DRIVE), C: if that\n    fails, and stored in $5B79 and $5B7A.\nEntry: A = 0 for a full start with the system files, otherwise not 0.\nExit: A = the default drive letter.","comment":"Save $5B8A-$5BFE (117 bytes) at $DA33"},
        "6894": {"comment":"From $5B8A to $DA33, 117 bytes"},
        "6902": {"comment":"Save SP"},
        "6906": {"comment":"Stack in the saved area"},
        "6909": {"comment":"D = the entry A"},
        "6910": {"comment":"DivMMC memory's $2007: the default drive"},
        "6913": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "6917": {"comment":"E = it"},
        "6918": {"comment":"$2008: its complement"},
        "6919": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "6923": {"comment":"Complement right?"},
        "6924": {"comment":"Same?"},
        "6927": {"comment":"No: A = 2 (C:)"},
        "6929": {"synopsis":"A = the default drive number (0-15).","comment":"Default drive kept"},
        "6930": {"comment":"Entry A kept"},
