        "7170": {"synopsis":"Next partition.","comment":"Next partition"},
        "7171": {"comment":"Map it"},
        "7173": {"synopsis":"IDE_DOS_MAP failed: by its error.","comment":"rc_unsuit? Next partition, same letter"},
        "7175": {"comment":"Same letter"},
        "7177": {"comment":"Same partition"},
        "7178": {"comment":"rc_mapped? Next letter, same partition"},
        "7180": {"comment":"Next letter"},
        "7182": {"comment":"Other errors: next unit"},
        "7183": {"comment":"Next unit"},
        "7184": {"comment":"Units left?"},
        "7186": {"comment":"HL = next unit and letter"},
        "7187": {"synopsis":"Maps disk images found by CATALOG_SYS: for each of the B entries from $FB6C (13 bytes each),\na name that starts with the three letters at DE, has a letter A-P as its fifth character and\nthe extension \"P3D\" or \"DSK\" becomes c:/nextzxos/ and its 11 name bytes at $D827, mapped to\nthat letter by IDE_DOS_MAP (A = $FF, a filesystem image); a mapped drive gets its saved\ndirectory (DRIVE_DIR_SET). Bit 7 of each compared character is cleared in the buffer.\nEntry: DE = the prefix (\"DRV\" or \"CPM\"), B = the number of entries.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = the second catalogue entry"},
        "7190": {"synopsis":"One catalogue entry.","comment":"Entries left"},
        "7191": {"comment":"Prefix"},
        "7192": {"comment":"Entry"},
        "7193": {"comment":"Starts with the prefix?"},
        "7196": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "7198": {"comment":"Fifth character: the drive letter"},
        "7201": {"comment":"Without the attribute bit"},
        "7203": {"comment":"A to P only"},
        "7205": {"comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "7207": {"comment":"Past 'P'?"},
        "7211": {"comment":"C = the drive letter"},
        "7212": {"comment":"To the extension"},
        "7215": {"comment":"\"P3D\"?"},
        "7219": {"comment":"Compare it"},
        "7223": {"comment":"Matched"},
        "7225": {"comment":"Or \"DSK\"?"},
        "7228": {"comment":"Neither: next"},
        "7233": {"synopsis":"A wanted image: its path built.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "7235": {"comment":"After \"c:/nextzxos/\" at $D827"},
        "7238": {"comment":"11 name bytes, attribute bits cleared"},
        "7240": {"synopsis":"One name byte, attribute bit cleared."},
        "7244": {"comment":"To the path"},
        "7248": {"comment":"Ended by $FF"},
        "7250": {"comment":"End byte"},
        "7251": {"comment":"L = the drive letter"},
        "7252": {"comment":"A = $FF: a filesystem image"},
        "7254": {"comment":"BC = the image's path"},
        "7258": {"comment":"IDE_DOS_MAP"},
        "7261": {"comment":"Unit and letter back"},
        "7262": {"comment":"Mapped: its saved directory back"},
        "7265": {"synopsis":"Next entry, 13 bytes on.","comment":"Entry back"},
        "7266": {"comment":"Prefix back"},
        "7267": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "7271": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "7272": {"comment":"Entries left?"},
        "7275": {"synopsis":"Gives a newly mapped drive its directory back: the 256 bytes at $2000 + 256 x (drive) in the\nDivMMC memory's bank 9 are copied to $E090 ($0769). When their second byte is the complement\nof the first, $050A is called with A = that second byte (low nibble the drive, high nibble\nthe user area for DOS_SET_USER) and HL = the path from $E092; otherwise, or when that fails,\nwith A = the drive (0-15) and HL = \"/\".\nEntry: L = the drive letter.\nExit: B, C = the entry H, L; the flags from $050A.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"Unit and letter kept"},
        "7276": {"comment":"A = $20 + the drive number"},
        "7279": {"comment":"BC = 256 bytes"},
        "7282": {"comment":"HL = $2000 + 256 x the drive"},
        "7284": {"comment":"Into $E090"},
        "7288": {"comment":"From DivMMC bank 9 ($0769)"},
        "7290": {"comment":"Copy 256 bytes from bank 9 to $E090"},
        "7295": {"comment":"Second byte the first's complement?"},
        "7298": {"comment":"Same?"},
        "7299": {"comment":"HL = the saved path"},
        "7300": {"comment":"NC"},
        "7302": {"comment":"Valid: $050A with it"},
        "7303": {"comment":"Restore it"},
        "7307": {"comment":"B, C = unit and letter"},
        "7308": {"comment":"Done?"},
        "7309": {"comment":"A = the drive (0-15)"},
        "7310": {"comment":"Drive number 0-15"},
        "7312": {"comment":"The path \"/\""},
        "7315": {"comment":"Ended by $FF"},
        "7318": {"comment":"$050A with it"},
        "7321": {"synopsis":"Catalogues files in c:/nextzxos/: the path (NEXTZXOS_PATH) with the pattern at HL, the\nbuffer at $FB5F with its first 13-byte entry zeroed, then DOS_CATALOG with B = 64 entries\nand C = $21. Called by IDE_MOUNT_SD (HL = IMAGE_PATTERN) and $1719.\nEntry: HL = the pattern, A = its length.\nExit: DOS_CATALOG's (B = entries found + 1, carry when done).","comment":"Path c:/nextzxos/ + pattern at $D827"},
        "7325": {"comment":"Zero the first entry at $FB5F"},
        "7334": {"comment":"Zero the buffer's first entry"},
        "7338": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "7341": {"comment":"B = 64 entries, C = $21"},
        "7344": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "7345": {"comment":"DOS_CATALOG"},
        "7348": {"synopsis":"Compares three characters at DE with three at HL, clearing bit 7 of each at HL first.\nExit: Z when all three match; HL and DE past the last compared.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"Three characters"},
        "7350": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"Clear the attribute bit"},
        "7352": {"comment":"Same?"},
        "7354": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "7355": {"comment":"Next"},
        "7357": {"comment":"Three in all"},
        "7359": {"comment":"Z: all three"},
        "7360": {"synopsis":"Sets up the SD card units (called from IDE_MOUNT_SD with its entry A):\n1. A is kept only when DOS_GET_1346 gives HL = $0080; else A = 0.\n2. $24A2 with A, HL = $0080, DE = 0; the DivMMC memory's $34F4 (bank $0D, through $05EF).\n3. SD_UNIT_RECORD for unit 5 (unit record $E458, partition record $E46C) and unit 6 ($E462,\n   $E47F).","comment":"Entry A kept"},
        "7361": {"comment":"DOS_GET_1346"},
        "7364": {"comment":"HL = $0080?"},
        "7367": {"comment":"Entry A"},
        "7369": {"comment":"Compare"},
        "7371": {"comment":"Yes: A kept"},
        "7373": {"comment":"No: A = 0"},
        "7374": {"synopsis":"HL = $0080, DE = 0.","comment":"HL = $0080, DE = 0"},
        "7380": {"comment":"DE = 0 kept"},
        "7381": {"comment":"$24A2"},
        "7385": {"comment":"DivMMC bank $0D's $34F4"},
        "7388": {"comment":"Unit 5 (card 0): $E458, record $E46C"},
        "7396": {"comment":"Set it up"},
        "7399": {"comment":"Unit 6 (card 1): $E462, record $E47F"},
        "7407": {"comment":"Set it up"},
        "7410": {"comment":"Done"},
        "7411": {"synopsis":"Loads the system files (IDE_MOUNT_SD with A = 0); a failure prints \"Error reading file:\" and\nthe path and stops (FILE_READ_ERROR):\n1. c:/machines/next/enAltZX.rom into the alternate ROM ($0E37 with A = $10); its $0003 is\n   run through the stub at $3E18 and must give DE = $0208 (CHECK_VERSION).\n2. c:/nextzxos/enSystem.sys: its first word must be $0208; the rest goes in pieces through\n   bank 7's $C000 to the DivMMC memory: $0EC0 bytes to bank 0 $3140, $0700 to bank 1 $2000,\n   $0580 to bank 1 $3180, $1400 to bank $0C $2300, $17F0 to bank $0D $2000, $1500 to bank\n   $0A $2000, $1140 to bank 7 $2000. Only the first read is checked.\n3. c:/nextzxos/rtc.sys: 512 bytes to bank 1 $2700; when it cannot be opened, $C9 (RET) bytes\n   stand in its place.\nChanges: all.","comment":"c:/machines/next/enAltZX.rom"},
        "7416": {"comment":"Path at $D827"},
        "7419": {"comment":"Path kept"},
        "7420": {"comment":"Into the alternate ROM"},
        "7422": {"comment":"Load the file into the alternate ROM"},
        "7425": {"comment":"Path back"},
        "7426": {"comment":"Failed? Error and stop"},
        "7429": {"comment":"Alternate ROM's $0003 (enAltZX.rom): DE = its version"},
        "7434": {"comment":"Must be $0208"},
        "7437": {"comment":"Check its version"},
        "7440": {"comment":"c:/nextzxos/enSystem.sys"},
        "7445": {"comment":"$0EC2 bytes to $C000; version $0208?"},
        "7448": {"comment":"Open, read and check"},
        "7451": {"comment":"$0EC0 after the version word"},
        "7457": {"comment":"To DivMMC bank 0's $3140"},
        "7462": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7465": {"comment":"Next $0700 bytes"},
        "7473": {"comment":"Read"},
        "7478": {"comment":"To bank 1's $2000"},
        "7482": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7486": {"comment":"Next $0580 bytes"},
        "7497": {"comment":"To bank 1's $3180"},
        "7500": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7504": {"comment":"Next $1400 bytes"},
        "7515": {"comment":"To bank $0C's $2300"},
        "7520": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7524": {"comment":"Next $0BF8 bytes"},
        "7536": {"comment":"To bank $0D's $2000"},
        "7541": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7544": {"comment":"Count back"},
        "7548": {"comment":"$0BF8 more"},
        "7554": {"comment":"To bank $0D's $2BF8"},
        "7559": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7563": {"comment":"Next $1500 bytes"},
        "7574": {"comment":"To bank $0A's $2000"},
        "7579": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7583": {"comment":"Last $1140 bytes"},
        "7590": {"comment":"File closed"},
        "7593": {"comment":"Count"},
        "7594": {"comment":"To bank 7's $2000"},
        "7599": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7602": {"comment":"c:/nextzxos/rtc.sys"},
        "7607": {"comment":"$C000 preset with RET ($C9)"},
        "7609": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "7612": {"comment":"Open and read"},
        "7615": {"comment":"Close it"},
        "7618": {"comment":"To bank 1's $2700"},
        "7621": {"comment":"512 bytes"},
        "7624": {"synopsis":"TO_DIVMMC with A = 1.","comment":"Bank 1"},
        "7626": {"synopsis":"Copies into the DivMMC memory through its routine at $0703: by the callers, BC bytes from HL\nto DE in DivMMC bank A.\nEntry: HL = the source, DE = the target ($2000-$3FFF), BC = the count, A = the bank.","comment":"DivMMC $0703: BC bytes from HL to bank A's DE"},
        "7630": {"comment":"Back"},
        "7631": {"synopsis":"DOS_CLOSE on file 0; HL = $C000 again.","comment":"File 0"},
        "7633": {"comment":"DOS_CLOSE"},
        "7636": {"comment":"HL = $C000 again"},
        "7640": {"synopsis":"OPEN_AND_READ with fill byte 0, then the file's first word (at $C000) must be the version\n$0208 (CHECK_VERSION, path at $D827); a failed read goes to FILE_READ_ERROR.\nEntry: HL = the name, A = its length, DE = the bytes to read.","comment":"Fill byte 0"},
        "7642": {"comment":"Open and read"},
        "7645": {"comment":"DE = the file's first word"},
        "7649": {"comment":"HL = the path"},
        "7652": {"comment":"Read? Check its version"},
        "7655": {"synopsis":"Prints \"Error reading file:\" and the path at HL, then stops (HALT_WITH_MSG).","comment":"Path kept"},
        "7656": {"comment":"\"Error reading file:\""},
        "7659": {"comment":"Print it"},
        "7662": {"comment":"Then the path, and stop"},
        "7663": {"comment":"Path and stop"},
        "7666": {"synopsis":"Opens c:/nextzxos/ + the name at HL (A characters) as file 0 (DOS_OPEN, C = 1, DE = $0002),\nsets $C000 and $C001 to B, and reads DE bytes into bank 7's $C000 (READ_FILE0).\nExit: NC when it did not open (the two bytes still set) or the read failed; carry otherwise.\nChanges: all.","comment":"Fill byte kept"},
        "7667": {"comment":"Count kept"},
        "7668": {"comment":"Path at $D827"},
        "7671": {"comment":"C = 1: the access mode"},
        "7672": {"comment":"DE = $0002: the create and open actions"},
        "7675": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN as file 0"},
        "7678": {"comment":"DE = the count"},
        "7679": {"comment":"$C000 and $C001 = the fill byte"},
        "7683": {"comment":"Preset the first two bytes"},
        "7686": {"comment":"Not opened? NC"},
        "7687": {"synopsis":"DOS_READ of DE bytes from file 0 to HL in bank 7.\nExit: carry when read or at the end of the file (rc_eof $19); NC, A = the error otherwise.","comment":"File 0, bank 7"},
        "7690": {"comment":"DOS_READ"},
        "7693": {"comment":"Read? Carry"},
        "7694": {"comment":"rc_eof? Carry as well"},
        "7696": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "7698": {"comment":"Other errors: NC"},
        "7700": {"synopsis":"Builds the path of a machine ROM file at $D827: \"c:/machines/next/\" and the name at\nROM_FILE_NAMES + A (8 bytes: $00 zx80.rom, $08 zx81.rom, $10 128.rom, $18 48.rom), or\n\"128-2.rom\" for an odd A. Called by LOAD_MACHINE_ROM ($0D70, A = $10 or $18).\nExit: HL = $D827, the path ended by $FF.","comment":"HL = the name for A"},
        "7703": {"comment":"Plus A"},
        "7705": {"comment":"Odd A?"},
        "7707": {"comment":"8 characters"},
        "7709": {"comment":"Even: 8 characters"},
        "7711": {"comment":"Odd: 9 characters"},
        "7712": {"comment":"\"128-2.rom\""},
        "7715": {"synopsis":"Builds \"c:/machines/next/\" and A characters from HL at $D827, ended by $FF.\nExit: HL = $D827.","comment":"Name kept"},
        "7716": {"comment":"\"c:/machines/next/\", 17 characters"},
        "7722": {"comment":"Build it"},
        "7724": {"synopsis":"Builds \"c:/nextzxos/\" and A characters from HL at $D827, ended by $FF.\nExit: HL = $D827, BC = 0.","comment":"Name kept"},
        "7725": {"comment":"\"c:/nextzxos/\", 12 characters"},
        "7728": {"comment":"12 characters"},
        "7731": {"synopsis":"The prefix (BC bytes from HL) to $D827, then the name.","comment":"Prefix to $D827"},
        "7736": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "7737": {"comment":"BC = A characters"},
        "7738": {"comment":"Copy the name"},
        "7740": {"comment":"Ended by $FF"},
        "7743": {"comment":"HL = the whole path"},
        "7747": {"synopsis":"Start-up checks (page 0 calls it at $032A):\n1. Unless NextReg $00 (machine ID) is 8 (an emulator), the core version from NextRegs $01\n   and $0E must be 3.01.10 or later, else \"Core 3.01.10 needed\" and a stop.\n2. DIVMMC_SIG_CODE, run at $ED27, reads the DivMMC memory's $0004-$0007: \"DV\" and a version\n   word.\n3. Without \"DV\": \"enNxtmmc.rom invalid\" and a stop; with it, the version must be $0208\n   (CHECK_VERSION).","comment":"NextReg $00: the machine ID"},
        "7748": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "7751": {"comment":"8, an emulator? No core check"},
        "7755": {"comment":"NextReg $01: core major and minor"},
        "7757": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "7760": {"comment":"H = it"},
        "7761": {"comment":"NextReg $0E: core sub-minor"},
        "7763": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "7766": {"comment":"L = it"},
        "7767": {"comment":"3.01.10 or later?"},
        "7771": {"comment":"Compare"},
        "7773": {"comment":"\"Core 3.01.10 needed\""},
        "7776": {"comment":"Older: stop"},
        "7778": {"synopsis":"No core check (or passed): the DivMMC memory's signature.","comment":"Signature check to $ED27"},
        "7787": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7789": {"comment":"Run it in RAM"},
        "7792": {"comment":"enNxtmmc.rom"},
        "7795": {"comment":"\"DV\"? Check its version"},
        "7797": {"comment":"Else its name"},
        "7800": {"comment":"Then \" invalid\", and stop"},
        "7803": {"comment":"Print it and stop"},
        "7805": {"synopsis":"Returns when DE = $0208; otherwise prints \"Version mismatch:\", \"0208 enNextZX.rom\", DE as\nfour lower-case hex digits, a space and the name at HL, and stops (HALT_WITH_MSG).\nEntry: DE = the version found, HL = the file's name ended by $FF.","comment":"Name kept"},
        "7806": {"comment":"Expected version $0208"},
        "7810": {"comment":"Compare"},
        "7813": {"comment":"Same? Done"},
        "7814": {"comment":"Name kept"},
        "7815": {"comment":"\"Version mismatch:\", then \"0208 ...\""},
        "7818": {"comment":"Print it"},
        "7821": {"comment":"HL = the version found"},
        "7822": {"comment":"Four hex digits"},
        "7824": {"synopsis":"One hex digit, the top nibble of HL.","comment":"Top nibble"},
        "7829": {"comment":"To '0'-'9'"},
        "7831": {"comment":"Above 9?"},
        "7833": {"comment":"Digit?"},
        "7835": {"comment":"'a'-'f'"},
        "7837": {"synopsis":"Prints it.","comment":"ROM 0's RST_PRINT_A"},
        "7842": {"comment":"Next nibble to the top"},
        "7843": {"comment":"HL x 16"},
        "7846": {"comment":"Next digit"},
        "7848": {"comment":"A space"},
        "7850": {"comment":"ROM 0's RST_PRINT_A"},
        "7855": {"comment":"HL = the file's name"},
        "7856": {"synopsis":"Prints the text at HL (PRINT_MSG), turns the border red and loops for ever.","comment":"Print it"},
        "7859": {"comment":"Red border"},
        "7861": {"comment":"Border colour 2"},
        "7863": {"synopsis":"The end: a jump to itself.","comment":"Stop here for good"},
        "7865": {"synopsis":"20 bytes of code BOOT_CHECKS copies to $ED27 and runs there: the DivMMC memory paged in with\nCONMEM (port $E3 = $80), HL = its word at $0004, DE = at $0006, paged out again.\nExit: Z when HL = $5644 (the bytes \"DV\").","comment":"DivMMC memory in (CONMEM)"},
        "7867": {"comment":"Port $E3 bit 7: CONMEM"},
        "7869": {"comment":"Its words at $0004 and $0006"},
        "7876": {"comment":"Paged out"},
        "7877": {"comment":"DivMMC control 0"},
        "7879": {"comment":"\"DV\" at $0004? Z"},
        "7882": {"comment":"\"DV\"?"},
        "7885": {"synopsis":"Prints a text from this ROM: 512 bytes from HL copied to $E090, then ROM 0's PRINT_TO_FF on\nthe copy.\nEntry: HL = the text, ended by $FF.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL; DE kept.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "7886": {"comment":"Text copied to $E090"},
        "7893": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7895": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "7896": {"comment":"ROM 0's PRINT_TO_FF"},
        "7901": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "7902": {"comment":"Back"},
        "7903": {"synopsis":"Called by page 0 at $01D4 once the RAM is counted: NextReg $8E = $7A (this ROM, RAM bank 7\nat $C000), DIVMMC_RET_CODE copied to $ED27 and jumped to, so its RET is this routine's.","comment":"ROM 2 and RAM bank 7 at $C000"},
        "7907": {"comment":"22 bytes to $ED27"},
        "7916": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7918": {"comment":"Run them there"},
        "7921": {"synopsis":"22 bytes run at $ED27: a RET ($C9) is put at $2009 of the DivMMC memory's bank 1 and at\n$3D00 of bank 0 (port $E3 = $81, then $80, both with CONMEM), then the DivMMC memory is\npaged out.","comment":"DivMMC memory in, bank 1"},
        "7923": {"comment":"DivMMC control"},
        "7925": {"comment":"RET at its $2009"},
        "7927": {"comment":"RET there"},
        "7930": {"comment":"Bank 0"},
        "7932": {"comment":"DivMMC control"},
        "7934": {"comment":"RET at its $3D00"},
        "7936": {"comment":"RET there"},
        "7939": {"comment":"DivMMC memory out"},
        "7940": {"comment":"DivMMC control 0"},
        "7942": {"comment":"Back to page 0"},
        "7943": {"synopsis":"Sets up the records of SD card unit A (5 or 6):\n1. The partition record at DE gets SYS_REC_DEFAULT; $07D5 stores its card (A - 5) and\n   addressing kind in it.\n2. The unit record at HL gets UNIT_REC_DEFAULT and, after its 8 bytes, the partition\n   record's address.\n3. IDE_PARTITION_FIND ($00B5) looks for \"PLUSIDEDOS\" on the unit; when it is not found or\n   the entry at $F722 is not of type 1, bit 7 of the partition record's byte 1 is set and it\n   is looked for again.\n4. Found: the 8 bytes at $F732 go to the unit record and $0765 fills the partition record\n   from $F722; not found: the unit record's first word and the partition record's first byte\n   are zeroed.\nEntry: A = the unit, HL = its unit record, DE = its partition record.","comment":"Partition record kept"},
        "7944": {"comment":"Unit record kept"},
        "7945": {"comment":"SYS_REC_DEFAULT into the partition record"},
        "7951": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7953": {"comment":"DE = the unit record"},
        "7954": {"comment":"IX = the partition record"},
        "7956": {"comment":"Unit record kept"},
        "7957": {"comment":"Its card and addressing kind"},
        "7961": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "7963": {"comment":"Unit record kept"},
        "7964": {"comment":"UNIT_REC_DEFAULT into the unit record"},
        "7970": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "7972": {"comment":"HL = the word after it"},
        "7973": {"comment":"BC = the unit record"},
        "7974": {"comment":"DE = the partition record"},
        "7977": {"comment":"The word = the partition record's address"},
        "7978": {"comment":"High byte"},
        "7980": {"comment":"Unit kept"},
        "7981": {"comment":"Find \"PLUSIDEDOS\" on it"},
        "7984": {"comment":"Find it"},
        "7987": {"comment":"B = the unit"},
        "7988": {"comment":"Not found? Try again"},
        "7990": {"comment":"Entry of type 1?"},
        "7993": {"comment":"Type 1?"},
        "7995": {"comment":"Yes: use it"},
        "7997": {"synopsis":"Not found: bit 7 of byte 1 set, a second search.","comment":"HL = the unit record"},
        "7998": {"comment":"IX = the partition record"},
        "8000": {"comment":"Bit 7 of its byte 1 set"},
        "8007": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "8008": {"comment":"Find it again"},
        "8011": {"comment":"Find it"},
        "8014": {"comment":"Not found?"},
        "8016": {"comment":"Type 1?"},
        "8021": {"comment":"No: none"},
        "8023": {"synopsis":"Found: the unit record and the partition record filled.","comment":"DE = the unit record"},
        "8024": {"comment":"8 bytes from $F732"},
        "8030": {"comment":"Copy it"},
        "8032": {"comment":"IX = the partition record"},
        "8034": {"comment":"A = 5 + its card: the unit"},
        "8039": {"comment":"Plus 5"},
        "8041": {"comment":"Fill the record from $F722"},
        "8044": {"comment":"IX back"},
        "8046": {"comment":"Back"},
        "8047": {"synopsis":"Not found: the records marked unused.","comment":"None: zero the unit record's first word"},
        "8049": {"comment":"Zero the first two bytes"},
        "8052": {"comment":"And the partition record's first byte"},
        "8053": {"comment":"Zero it"},
        "8055": {"synopsis":"16 bytes for a new partition record (SD_UNIT_RECORD): 1 (in use), then zeros. Its last five\nbytes are also the first five of UNIT_REC_DEFAULT. The same job and bytes as the +3E ROM 2's\nSYS_REC_DEFAULT."},
        "8066": {"synopsis":"8 bytes for a unit record until its system partition is read (SD_UNIT_RECORD): $01 $00 $02\n$80 $00 $01 $00 $00."},
        "8074": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITIONS (jump table $01A5; the API document: get the number of open partitions):\ncounts the in-use records among the 20 19-byte partition records from $E46C whose card bit\n(bit 0 of byte $10) equals A and whose partition number (bytes $11-$12) is not 0. The same\ncode as the +3E ROM 2's HD_UNIT_MAPPED.\nExit: carry, A = the count, HL = the last unused record (0 for none).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"C = the card wanted"},
        "8075": {"comment":"20 records from $E46C"},
        "8079": {"comment":"20 records"},
        "8081": {"comment":"E = 0, HL = 0"},
        "8085": {"synopsis":"One record.","comment":"In use?"},
        "8089": {"comment":"No: remember it"},
        "8091": {"comment":"Its card bit"},
        "8096": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "8097": {"comment":"Not the card wanted: next"},
        "8099": {"comment":"Partition number 0?"},
        "8105": {"comment":"Partition 0: next"},
        "8107": {"comment":"No: count it"},
        "8108": {"synopsis":"Next record, 19 bytes on."},
        "8109": {"comment":"19 bytes on"},
        "8115": {"comment":"Next"},
        "8117": {"comment":"A = the count, carry"},
        "8118": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "8120": {"synopsis":"An unused record: HL = it.","comment":"HL = this record"},
        "8123": {"comment":"Next record"},
        "8125": {"synopsis":"Machine ROM file names for ROM_FILE_PATH, 8 bytes apart: \"zx80.rom\", \"zx81.rom\", \"128.rom\"\n$FF, \"48.rom\" $FF."},
        "8156": {"synopsis":"\"enAltZX.rom\" (11 characters, no end byte): LOAD_SYSTEM's first file."},
        "8167": {"synopsis":"\"128-2.rom\" (9 characters): ROM_FILE_PATH's name for an odd A."},
        "8176": {"synopsis":"\"enNxtmmc.rom\", ended by $FF: the name BOOT_CHECKS reports."},
        "8189": {"synopsis":"\"Mount=\" (6 bytes, no end marker), copied to $F700 by IDE_DOS_MAPPING ($0495) ahead of a\ndrive's description; also read at $258C."},
        "8195": {"synopsis":"\"???-?.???\": the pattern IDE_MOUNT_SD catalogues in c:/nextzxos/."},
        "8204": {"synopsis":"\"DRV\": the prefix of drive image files (MAP_IMAGES)."},
        "8207": {"synopsis":"\"CPM\": the other image prefix."},
        "8210": {"synopsis":"\"P3D\": an image file's extension."},
        "8213": {"synopsis":"\"DSK\": the other extension."},
        "8216": {"synopsis":"\"SWP-?.P3S\" (9 characters), read at $1714."},
        "8225": {"synopsis":"\"enSystem.sys\" (12 characters): LOAD_SYSTEM's second file."},
        "8237": {"synopsis":"\"rtc.sys\" (7 characters): LOAD_SYSTEM's third file."},
        "8244": {"synopsis":"A tokenised BASIC line: LOAD ($EF) \"c:/nextzxos/autoexec.1st\" ENTER. Page 1 runs it through\n$0F82 with HL = $2034."},
        "8272": {"synopsis":"A tokenised BASIC line: LOAD ($EF) \"c:/nextzxos/autoexec.bas\" ENTER, run by page 1 through\n$0F82 with HL = $2050. Its \"c:/nextzxos/\" is also NEXTZXOS_DIR."},
        "8274": {"synopsis":"\"c:/nextzxos/\": the 12 bytes NEXTZXOS_PATH copies, inside the second BASIC line (to its\nclosing quote and ENTER at $206B)."},
        "8300": {"synopsis":"\"c:/machines/next/\" (17 characters) for MACHINE_PATH."},
        "8317": {"synopsis":"The system partition's name, \"PLUSIDEDOS\" and six spaces, that SD_UNIT_RECORD looks for. The\nsame bytes as the +3E ROM 2's SYS_PART_NAME."},
        "8333": {"synopsis":"\"Core 3.01.10 needed\", ended by $FF (BOOT_CHECKS)."},
        "8353": {"synopsis":"\" invalid\", ended by $FF (BOOT_CHECKS)."},
        "8362": {"synopsis":"\"Error reading file:\", ENTER, $FF (FILE_READ_ERROR)."},
        "8383": {"synopsis":"\"Version mismatch:\", ENTER, \"0208 enNextZX.rom\", ENTER, $FF (CHECK_VERSION)."},
        "8420": {"synopsis":"DOS_REF_XDPB (jump table $0151; the API document: point at the XDPB for low-level disk\naccess): for a drive letter A to P in either case, IX = its XDPB (DRIVE_XDPB).\nEntry: A = the drive letter.\nExit: carry when the drive's word in the table at $E2A0 is not 0; else NC, A = $16\n(rc_nodrive).\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL, IX.","comment":"Upper case"},
        "8422": {"comment":"Drive number"},
        "8424": {"comment":"Below 'A'? NC"},
        "8427": {"comment":"Past 'P'? NC"},
        "8431": {"comment":"BC = its XDPB, HL = its word"},
        "8434": {"comment":"IX = the XDPB"},
        "8437": {"comment":"Word not 0? Carry"},
        "8440": {"comment":"Carry if it is not 0"},
        "8442": {"synopsis":"A = $16 (rc_nodrive); the carry is already set by the test.","comment":"A = $16 (rc_nodrive)"},
        "8445": {"synopsis":"Finds a drive's XDPB: drive A at $E2C0, B at $E32D, M at $E39A, any other at $E5E8 + 48 x\nthe drive. Also called from $2142, $2156 and $2456.\nEntry: A = the drive (0-15).\nExit: BC = the XDPB, HL = the drive's word at $E2A0 + 2 x drive, DE = $E5E8 + 48 x drive, A\n= 2 x drive; Z for A, B and M.","comment":"E = the drive"},
        "8446": {"comment":"48 bytes per drive"},
        "8448": {"comment":"DE = 48 x the drive"},
        "8450": {"comment":"Plus $E5E8"},
        "8454": {"comment":"A = 2 x the drive"},
        "8455": {"comment":"HL = its word in the table at $E2A0"},
        "8460": {"comment":"Drive A: $E2C0"},
        "8464": {"comment":"Drive A: done"},
        "8465": {"comment":"Drive B: $E32D"},
        "8468": {"comment":"Drive B?"},
        "8471": {"comment":"Drive M: $E39A"},
        "8474": {"comment":"Drive M?"},
        "8477": {"comment":"Others: $E5E8 + 48 x the drive"},
        "8478": {"comment":"BC = DE"},
        "8480": {"synopsis":"Maps drive E to device D (probably IDE_DOS_MAP's work; nothing in the four pages refers to\n$2120, so it is probably entered from the DivMMC memory's side of the call):\n1. D below 4 is rc_invdevice ($41). D = 4 is the RAM disk: refused with $41 when there is\nnone (bit 7 of its letter byte at $E844) and with rc_partopen ($3B) when it is mapped\nalready; otherwise the drive's letter goes to $E844 and the RAM disk's 48-byte parameter\nblock at $E828 is copied to the drive's block (from $20FD).\n2. D of 5 or more: DRIVE_MAP_DEV.\n3. DRIVE_XDPB_SET: the block's address into the drive's word at $E2A0 + 2 x E, and part of\nthe block passed to the DivMMC memory.\nEntry: D = the device, E = the drive (0-15).\nExit: carry; or NC with A = the error.","comment":"Device 5 or more: a partition or an image"},
        "8485": {"comment":"HL = the RAM disk's letter byte"},
        "8488": {"comment":"Device 4: the RAM disk"},
        "8492": {"synopsis":"rc_invdevice ($41), NC.","comment":"Devices 0-3: rc_invdevice, NC"},
        "8496": {"synopsis":"Device 4, the RAM disk.","comment":"No RAM disk (bit 7 of its letter byte)?"},
        "8501": {"comment":"Mapped to a drive already: rc_partopen"},
        "8504": {"comment":"The drive's letter marks the RAM disk mapped"},
        "8508": {"comment":"HL = $E828, the RAM disk's parameter block"},
        "8513": {"comment":"BC = the drive's block, HL = its word"},
        "8517": {"comment":"The word's address stacked; HL = $E828"},
        "8518": {"comment":"DE = the drive's block"},
        "8521": {"comment":"The 48 bytes copied"},
        "8526": {"comment":"DE = the block, HL = its word"},
        "8528": {"comment":"The word set; on to the DivMMC memory"},
        "8531": {"synopsis":"Device 5 or more:\n1. The drive's block and word found ($20FD).\n2. D bit 7 set: an image file, registered by IMAGE_REGISTER with A = 3 and BC = the header\nthe caller read (IMAGE_OPEN's); HL = its parameter block. Otherwise partition BC of unit\nD: its entry read to $F712 (IDE_PARTITION_READ), its type ($F722) must be 3 (else\nrc_unsuit), then opened (IDE_PARTITION_OPEN, $0740); HL = $F732, the parameter block in\nthe entry.\n3. 28 bytes from HL to the drive's block; after them +$1C the drive's letter, +$1D the unit\n(D without bit 7), 12 zero bytes and the words $2E96, $2E98 and $2EE3.\n4. (IX+5) = the block's +$1B bits 4-5 with its sector size code (+$0F); (IX+6) = its +$14;\nthe 19 bytes at IX go to the DivMMC memory (bank $0C, $376E + 19 x the drive) and the\nblock's +$28 holds IX.\n5. DRIVE_XDPB_SET.","comment":"The caller's BC and DE kept"},
        "8533": {"comment":"BC = the drive's block, HL = its word"},
        "8537": {"comment":"DE = the device and the drive"},
        "8538": {"comment":"The word's address stacked; HL = the caller's BC"},
        "8539": {"comment":"The block and DE stacked"},
        "8541": {"comment":"BC = the partition number, or the header read"},
        "8543": {"comment":"Device bit 7 clear: a partition"},
        "8548": {"comment":"An image: registered as type 3"},
        "8553": {"comment":"Done: HL = its parameter block"},
        "8555": {"synopsis":"Failed: NC with the error in A; the three stacked words dropped.","comment":"NC: the error in A, the stack cleared"},
        "8560": {"synopsis":"A partition: its entry read and checked, the partition opened.","comment":"Partition BC of unit A: its entry to $F712"},
        "8568": {"comment":"Its type ($F722) must be 3"},
        "8573": {"comment":"Else rc_unsuit"},
        "8577": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "8580": {"comment":"The partition opened (IDE_PARTITION_OPEN)"},
        "8586": {"comment":"HL = $F732: the parameter block in the entry"},
        "8589": {"synopsis":"The parameter block at HL copied to the drive's block and completed.","comment":"A = the device, DE = the drive's block"},
        "8593": {"comment":"28 bytes of parameter block copied"},
        "8598": {"comment":"HL past them"},
        "8599": {"comment":"B = the device, C = the drive"},
        "8600": {"comment":"+$1C: the drive's letter"},
        "8605": {"comment":"+$1D: the unit, bit 7 left out"},
        "8610": {"comment":"+$1E to +$29: 12 zero bytes"},
        "8612": {"synopsis":"One zero byte."},
        "8617": {"comment":"+$2A to +$2F: the words $2E96, $2E98, $2EE3"},
        "8634": {"comment":"Back to +$1B: its bits 4 and 5"},
        "8641": {"comment":"With the sector size code (+$0F)"},
        "8646": {"comment":"(IX+5) = them"},
        "8649": {"comment":"(IX+6) = the first sector number (+$14)"},
        "8657": {"comment":"HL = IX, kept"},
        "8661": {"comment":"DE = $376E + 19 x the drive"},
        "8670": {"comment":"19 bytes from IX"},
        "8673": {"comment":"To the DivMMC memory ($04DD, bank $0C)"},
        "8677": {"comment":"DE = IX, HL = the drive's block"},
        "8680": {"comment":"+$28 = IX"},
        "8687": {"comment":"DE = the block, HL = the drive's word"},
        "8689": {"synopsis":"The drive's word (HL) = its block (DE). Then the block's first 15 bytes go to $F72F, $F73E =\nits +$1A bit 6 with its +$1B, $F73F = its +$1C (the letter); these 17 bytes go to the DivMMC\nmemory (bank $0D) at $3870 + 22 x the drive.\nExit: carry.","comment":"The drive's word = the block"},
        "8692": {"comment":"HL = the block; its first 15 bytes to $F72F"},
        "8702": {"comment":"+$1A: bit 6"},
        "8709": {"comment":"With +$1B, to $F73E"},
        "8714": {"comment":"+$1C, the letter, to $F73F"},
        "8716": {"comment":"HL = $F72F"},
        "8720": {"comment":"A = the letter less 'A': the drive"},
        "8725": {"comment":"DE = $3870 + 22 x the drive"},
        "8732": {"comment":"17 bytes"},
        "8734": {"comment":"To the DivMMC memory ($04DD, bank $0D)"},
        "8738": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "8740": {"synopsis":"IMAGE_OPEN with type 3, a disk image (from IDE_DOS_MAP's $03FB).","comment":"Type 3: a disk image"},
        "8742": {"synopsis":"Opens the file named at BC as an image of type A and reads its first 1K (from $16C0 with A =\n2, the swap file, and $1732):\n1. $F700-$F712 filled with B, $F700 = A; the name's extension after its last '.' to\n$F713-$F715, upper case, padded with spaces.\n2. $05F4 (the DivMMC memory's $03B2 with B = 2); the DivMMC memory's $034F gives the drive\nin its low 4 bits (C).\n3. The file opened (DOS_OPEN, access 1, DE = 2); its length (DOS_GET_EOF) to $F70B-$F70D.\n4. The DivMMC memory's $344F with A = the file number, HL = $F717, DE = 2: its A goes to\n$F710, and with bit 7 set to $F716; the file closed (DOS_CLOSE).\n5. Refused: E not 1 after it, rc_fragmented ($4A); a zero word at $F71B, rc_unsuit (9).\n6. $F707 = that word - 1; $F71B = the drive; the start ($F717-$F71A) to $F701-$F704,\ndivided by 512 when bit 1 of $F710 is clear.\n7. The DivMMC memory's $1394 with IX = $F71C ((IX+$10) = $80): carry from it is\nrc_nohandle ($3C); its HL, kept at $F711, is the handle.\n8. Sectors 0 and 1 read to $F75F and $F95F (IDE_SECTOR_READ, IX = $F700).\n9. 6 bytes from $F716 to the handle in the DivMMC memory ($04DD).\nEntry: A = the type, BC = the name ($FF-ended).\nExit: carry, BC = $F75F, IX = $F700 (the image's 19-byte block); or NC with A = the error.","comment":"The name kept"},
        "8743": {"comment":"$F700-$F712 filled with B"},
        "8755": {"comment":"$F700 = the type"},
        "8758": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8760": {"synopsis":"One character of the name, looking for a '.'.","comment":"End of the name?"},
        "8766": {"comment":"A '.'?"},
        "8770": {"synopsis":"A '.': the place after it kept while the rest is scanned.","comment":"Kept: the place after the '.'"},
        "8771": {"synopsis":"One more character.","comment":"The rest scanned"},
        "8777": {"comment":"Another '.'?"},
        "8781": {"comment":"Yes: the one kept dropped"},
        "8784": {"synopsis":"HL = the place after the last '.'.","comment":"HL = after the last '.'"},
        "8785": {"synopsis":"The extension: three characters, upper case, padded with spaces.","comment":"Three characters to $F713"},
        "8787": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"End of the name?"},
        "8793": {"comment":"Below 'a'?"},
        "8797": {"comment":"Above 'z'?"},
        "8801": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "8805": {"synopsis":"Past the end: a space.","comment":"Past the end: a space"},
        "8807": {"synopsis":"The character stored.","comment":"The character stored"},
        "8811": {"comment":"$05F4: the DivMMC memory's $03B2, B = 2"},
        "8814": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "8817": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $034F"},
        "8822": {"comment":"C = the drive (low 4 bits)"},
        "8826": {"comment":"DOS_OPEN: access 1, DE = 2"},
        "8837": {"comment":"DOS_GET_EOF: the length"},
        "8841": {"comment":"Failed: closed, the error kept"},
        "8843": {"comment":"The length to $F70B-$F70D"},
        "8851": {"comment":"A = the file number"},
        "8852": {"comment":"HL = $F717, DE = 2"},
        "8858": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $344F"},
        "8863": {"comment":"Its A kept at $F710"},
        "8867": {"comment":"And with bit 7 set at $F716"},
        "8873": {"comment":"A = rc_unsuit if it failed"},
        "8875": {"synopsis":"The file closed (DOS_CLOSE), the earlier result kept; then the checks.","comment":"DOS_CLOSE, the result kept"},
        "8884": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "8885": {"comment":"E not 1: rc_fragmented"},
        "8890": {"comment":"A zero word at $F71B: rc_unsuit"},
        "8898": {"comment":"$F707 = that word - 1"},
        "8902": {"comment":"$F71B = the drive"},
        "8906": {"comment":"HL:DE = the start, from $F717"},
        "8913": {"comment":"Bit 1 of $F710 clear: bytes, so / 512"},
        "8920": {"comment":"Shifted down 8 bits"},
        "8925": {"comment":"And 1 more"},
        "8931": {"synopsis":"The start sector to $F701-$F704; the handle; the first two sectors.","comment":"The start sector to $F701-$F704"},
        "8938": {"comment":"IX = $F71C, +$10 = $80"},
        "8946": {"comment":"BC = DE = 0"},
        "8951": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $1394"},
        "8955": {"comment":"Carry from it: rc_nohandle"},
        "8959": {"comment":"HL kept at $F711 and stacked"},
        "8963": {"comment":"IX = the image's block at $F700"},
        "8967": {"comment":"Sector 0 to $F75F (IDE_SECTOR_READ)"},
        "8978": {"comment":"Sector 1 to $F95F"},
        "8990": {"comment":"DE = the handle"},
        "8992": {"comment":"6 bytes from $F716"},
        "8998": {"comment":"To the handle in the DivMMC memory ($04DD)"},
        "9002": {"comment":"BC = the first 1K"},
        "9007": {"synopsis":"Registers the image whose 19-byte block is at IX (IMAGE_OPEN's) in a free slot of the table\nat $E46C ($0605), by the header read to BC:\n1. A header starting \"P3D\" $1A with a good checksum (P3D_HEADER_TEST): its byte $20 must be\nthe type A (else rc_unsuit, 9); its parameter block is at +4.\n2. Otherwise only type 3 is taken (else rc_unsuit): a disk image whose header starts\n\"EXTENDED\" or \"MV - CPC\", with 1 at +$31 (one side). The first sector number (+$11A)\nchooses the format: bit 6 FORMAT_SPEC_1, bit 7 FORMAT_SPEC_2; neither, the 10 bytes at\n+$200 (the first sector), or FORMAT_SPECS when all ten are the same. DD_L_XDPB makes\nthe parameter block at $F72F from it, with +$1A = 0, +$1B = $30 and +$0B = $8000.\n3. IMAGE_SLOT_FILL.\nEntry: A = the type, BC = the header, IX = the image's block.\nExit: carry, HL = the parameter block; or NC with A = the error.","comment":"The type kept"},
        "9008": {"comment":"A P3D header?"},
        "9011": {"comment":"No: a disk image perhaps"},
        "9013": {"comment":"B = the type"},
        "9014": {"synopsis":"rc_unsuit (9), NC, when NZ.","comment":"rc_unsuit when NZ"},
        "9019": {"comment":"The header's type byte (+$20)"},
        "9024": {"comment":"The one wanted?"},
        "9027": {"comment":"HL = +4: its parameter block"},
        "9031": {"synopsis":"The 19 bytes at IX into a free slot of $E46C's table ($0605; none is rc_nohandle); bit 4 of\nthe parameter block's +$1B set (an image); when its bit 5 is clear the slot's start sector\n(+1 to +4) goes up one, past the header.\nEntry: HL = the parameter block.","comment":"A free slot at $E46C into IX ($0605)"},
        "9037": {"comment":"HL = the image's block, DE = the parameter block"},
        "9039": {"comment":"None free: rc_nohandle"},
        "9040": {"comment":"DE = the slot"},
        "9044": {"comment":"The 19 bytes copied"},
        "9049": {"comment":"HL = the parameter block"},
        "9051": {"comment":"+$1B: bit 4 set (an image)"},
        "9057": {"comment":"Bit 5 set: done"},
        "9062": {"comment":"DE = the slot's start sector (+1)"},
        "9066": {"synopsis":"The 32-bit number at DE (low byte first) one up. Called from $16E8 too.\nExit: carry as on entry.\nChanges: F, B, DE.","comment":"Four bytes"},
        "9068": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"One byte up"},
        "9072": {"comment":"No wrap: done"},
        "9076": {"synopsis":"No P3D header: type 3 only, a disk image with one side.","comment":"Not P3D: only type 3 (a disk image)"},
        "9081": {"comment":"\"EXTENDED\" at the start?"},
        "9089": {"comment":"Or \"MV - CPC\"?"},
        "9097": {"synopsis":"One side?","comment":"+$31: one side?"},
        "9105": {"comment":"+$11A: the first sector's number"},
        "9110": {"comment":"Bit 7 or 6 set?"},
        "9114": {"comment":"HL = +$200: the first sector's bytes"},
        "9120": {"comment":"Ten bytes all the same?"},
        "9122": {"comment":"C = the first"},
        "9124": {"synopsis":"One byte compared with the first.","comment":"Another one"},
        "9126": {"comment":"Different: the disk's own format"},
        "9131": {"comment":"All the same: format 0"},
        "9136": {"synopsis":"Bit 7 or 6 of the first sector number: format 2 or 1.","comment":"Bit 7 to the carry"},
        "9137": {"comment":"$40: format 1"},
        "9142": {"comment":"$C0: format 2"},
        "9145": {"synopsis":"The parameter block at $F72F from the format at HL (DD_L_XDPB); then IMAGE_SLOT_FILL.","comment":"The parameter block at $F72F (DD_L_XDPB)"},
        "9156": {"comment":"+$1A = 0, +$1B = $30"},
        "9162": {"comment":"+$0B and +$0C = $8000"},
        "9167": {"comment":"HL = it; registered"},
        "9173": {"synopsis":"Tests the 512 bytes at BC for a P3D header: Z when they start with P3D_SIGNATURE and the\nlast equals $1F plus the sum of the 511 before it (low byte). Called from $16C7 too.\nEntry: BC = the header.\nExit: Z for a good header; HL = BC.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE.","comment":"HL = the header"},
        "9175": {"comment":"Its first 4 bytes the signature?"},
        "9183": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "9185": {"comment":"The sum from $1F"},
        "9187": {"comment":"255 + 256 bytes"},
        "9190": {"synopsis":"One byte into the sum.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9197": {"comment":"Equal to the last byte?"},
        "9200": {"synopsis":"Compares 8 bytes at DE with those at HL (CMP_B with B = 8).\nExit: Z when equal; HL kept.\nChanges: AF, B, DE.","comment":"Eight bytes"},
        "9202": {"synopsis":"Compares B bytes at DE with those at HL.\nExit: Z when equal; HL kept.\nChanges: AF, B, DE."},
        "9203": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Equal?"},
        "9207": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "9211": {"synopsis":"HL back.","comment":"HL back"},
        "9213": {"synopsis":"\"P3D\" and $1A: the start of a P3D header (P3D_HEADER_TEST)."},
        "9217": {"synopsis":"\"MV - CPC\": the start of a disk image's header (IMAGE_DSK_TEST)."},
        "9225": {"synopsis":"\"EXTENDED\": the start of the other kind of disk image header (IMAGE_DSK_TEST)."},
        "9233": {"synopsis":"Unmaps drive A (probably IDE_DOS_UNMAP's work; nothing in the four pages refers to $2411):\n1. The DivMMC memory's $344D with A = the letter ($05EA, bank $0D); NC: its error.\n2. The drive's word at HL cleared; the RAM disk's letter byte ($E844) cleared when it is\nthis drive.\n3. The first byte of the block whose address is at the parameter block's +$28 cleared, when\nthere is one.\nEntry: A = the drive (0-15), HL = its word, IX = its parameter block.\nExit: carry; or NC with A = the error.","comment":"IX and the drive kept"},
        "9236": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "9239": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $344D (bank $0D)"},
        "9243": {"comment":"D = the drive"},
        "9246": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "9247": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "9250": {"comment":"The drive's word cleared"},
        "9255": {"comment":"The RAM disk's drive?"},
        "9261": {"comment":"Yes: no longer mapped"},
        "9262": {"synopsis":"The block at +$28.","comment":"HL = the block at +$28"},
        "9268": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "9272": {"comment":"Its first byte cleared"},
        "9274": {"synopsis":"Says what drive A is mapped to, as text at BC (probably IDE_DOS_MAPPING's work; nothing in\nthe four pages refers to $243A):\n1. The RAM disk's drive: \"4>RAMdisk\" (RAMDISK_NAME, $FF-ended); A = 4.\n2. Otherwise the drive's parameter block ($20FD): an image (bit 4 of +$1B) gives A = $FF and\nno text. Otherwise the block at its +$28 gives the device (5 + bit 0 of +$10) and the\npartition number (+$11, +$12), whose entry is read to $F712 (IDE_PARTITION_READ); the\ntext is the device's digit, '>' and the entry's 16-byte name, $FF-ended; A = the\ndevice, BC = the partition number.\nEntry: A = the drive, BC = the buffer.\nExit: carry (also when the entry cannot be read).","comment":"A = the letter"},
        "9276": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "9278": {"comment":"The RAM disk's drive?"},
        "9282": {"comment":"HL = \"4>RAMdisk\", 10 bytes"},
        "9288": {"comment":"No: another device"},
        "9290": {"comment":"A = 4, the device"},
        "9293": {"comment":"The text copied"},
        "9297": {"synopsis":"Not the RAM disk: an image or a partition.","comment":"IX and the buffer kept"},
        "9300": {"comment":"The drive's parameter block"},
        "9305": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "9308": {"comment":"A = $FF for an image"},
        "9310": {"comment":"An image (+$1B bit 4)?"},
        "9316": {"comment":"IX = the block at its +$28"},
        "9325": {"comment":"A = 5 or 6: the device"},
        "9332": {"comment":"BC = the partition number"},
        "9340": {"comment":"Its entry to $F712 (IDE_PARTITION_READ)"},
        "9346": {"comment":"H = the device, DE = the buffer"},
        "9349": {"comment":"Not read: no text"},
        "9351": {"comment":"The device's digit"},
        "9356": {"comment":"Then '>'"},
        "9360": {"comment":"The partition number kept"},
        "9361": {"comment":"A = the device"},
        "9362": {"comment":"The 16-byte name copied"},
        "9370": {"comment":"$FF after it"},
        "9373": {"synopsis":"An image: A = $FF, no text.","comment":"BC = the partition number (or the buffer)"},
        "9374": {"synopsis":"IX back; carry.","comment":"IX back; carry"},
        "9378": {"synopsis":"Sets the RAM disk up (from $1CD5):\n1. RAMDISK_XDPB_END to $E843 (the parameter block at $E828 from +$1B on); RAMDISK_SPEC to\n$E3EF.\n2. Fewer than 4 tracks (E): RAMDISK_NONE.\n3. Its tracks ($E3F1) = D + E, its reserved tracks ($E3F4) = D.\n4. With A = 0 each track from D on is set up by the DivMMC memory's $362D (bank $0D, A =\nthe track).\n5. DD_L_DPB makes the parameter block at $E828; the track count ($E3F1) goes to the DivMMC\nmemory's $3E76 (bank $0D).\n6. The letter byte ($E844) one up when its bit 7 is set.\nEntry: A = 0 to set the tracks up; HL: H = the first track, L = the count.","comment":"A and HL kept"},
        "9380": {"comment":"21 bytes to $E843 (+$1B on)"},
        "9393": {"comment":"HL for DE later"},
        "9394": {"comment":"IX = the RAM disk's parameter block"},
        "9398": {"comment":"The 8-byte format to $E3EF"},
        "9409": {"comment":"D = the first track, E = the count"},
        "9411": {"comment":"Fewer than 4?"},
        "9416": {"comment":"Tracks = D + E"},
        "9420": {"comment":"Reserved tracks = D"},
        "9424": {"comment":"A not 0: no set-up"},
        "9428": {"synopsis":"One track set up.","comment":"Each track set up by the DivMMC memory's $362D"},
        "9435": {"comment":"The next one"},
        "9439": {"synopsis":"The parameter block made; the count passed to the DivMMC memory.","comment":"The parameter block from the format (DD_L_DPB)"},
        "9445": {"comment":"The track count, 1 byte"},
        "9454": {"comment":"To the DivMMC memory's $3E76 ($04DD, bank $0D)"},
        "9458": {"comment":"Letter byte bit 7 clear: done"},
        "9464": {"comment":"Otherwise one up"},
        "9468": {"synopsis":"Fewer than 4: the drive unmapped (IDE_DOS_UNMAP with L = its letter) and the letter byte\n$FF (no RAM disk).","comment":"A dropped"},
        "9469": {"comment":"L = the letter"},
        "9474": {"comment":"IDE_DOS_UNMAP"},
        "9479": {"comment":"No RAM disk: $FF"},
        "9485": {"synopsis":"The RAM disk's format, 8 bytes in FORMAT_SPECS' layout (the gaps left out), copied to $E3EF\nby RAMDISK_SETUP: format 0, one side, the tracks (+2) and reserved tracks (+5) filled in\nthere, 1 sector of 512 bytes per track, 1K blocks, the directory blocks worked out."},
        "9493": {"synopsis":"21 bytes copied to $E843 by RAMDISK_SETUP, the RAM disk's parameter block from +$1B: $08,\nthe letter byte 0, $FF, 12 zeros, then the word $2E96 three times (cf. DRIVE_MAP_DEV's\n$2E96, $2E98, $2EE3)."},
        "9514": {"synopsis":"DOS_INITIALISE ($0100, as documented): nothing to do here; carry set."},
        "9516": {"synopsis":"DOS_VERSION ($0103, as documented): fixed values, the same 16 bytes as the +3E ROM 2's\nFIXED_NUMBERS.\nExit: A = 0, BC = 0, DE = $0101, HL = $0069, carry set, NZ.","comment":"NZ and carry from the SUB"},
        "9520": {"comment":"A = B = C = 0"},
        "9524": {"comment":"DE = $0101"},
        "9527": {"comment":"HL = $0069"},
        "9530": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "9532": {"synopsis":"DOS_BOOT ($012A, as documented): starts the program in drive A's boot sector, the same job\nas\nthe +3E ROM 2's BOOT_DISK. Page 1's TAPE_COMMAND calls it (its $1646) for the name \"*\" and\ntests for error $23.\n1. The DivMMC memory's $34A5 (bank $0D) with A = 'A', B = 7, HL = $E090: probably the\nsector read to $E090.\n2. The 512 bytes summed: rc_notboot ($23) unless the low byte is 3.\n3. Interrupts off; 8K pages 6 and 7 (16K bank 3) at $8000-$BFFF (MMU 4, 5) and the sector\ncopied to $BE00 there; NextReg $8E = $3A (bank 3 at $C000, ROM 2): it is now at $FE00;\nSP = $FE00.\n4. $5B5C = 3, $5B67 = 4; $0E14 (NextRegs $82-$85, the internal port decoding, and more).\n5. BOOT_JUMP_STUB to $FDFB, entered with BC = $1FFD and A = 7: port $1FFD = 7 leaves RAM in\nall four quarters (banks 4, 7, 6, 3: zxnext.vhd), and the jump goes to $FE10.\nExit (only on failure): NC, A = the error.","comment":"Drive A"},
        "9534": {"comment":"B = 7, HL = $E090"},
        "9539": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9540": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $34A5 (bank $0D)"},
        "9545": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "9546": {"comment":"A 512-byte sum"},
        "9551": {"synopsis":"One byte into the sum.","comment":"One byte"},
        "9558": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9559": {"comment":"Low byte 3?"},
        "9561": {"comment":"No: rc_notboot"},
        "9564": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "9565": {"comment":"8K pages 6 and 7 (bank 3) at $8000-$BFFF"},
        "9574": {"comment":"The sector to $BE00 (bank 3 + $1E00)"},
        "9582": {"comment":"Bank 3 at $C000 with ROM 2: the sector at $FE00"},
        "9586": {"comment":"The stack below it"},
        "9589": {"comment":"$5B5C = 3"},
        "9594": {"comment":"$5B67 = 4"},
        "9598": {"comment":"$0E14: port decoding and more"},
        "9601": {"comment":"BOOT_JUMP_STUB to $FDFB"},
        "9612": {"comment":"Port $1FFD = 7 there, then $FE10"},
        "9620": {"synopsis":"Five bytes DOS_BOOT copies to $FDFB and jumps to, with BC = $1FFD and A = 7: port $1FFD = 7,\nthen on at $FE10, byte $10 of the boot sector. They run only from that copy.","comment":"Port $1FFD = 7: all RAM, bank 3 at $C000"},
        "9622": {"comment":"Byte $10 of the boot sector"},
        "9625": {"synopsis":"The deprecated calls DOS_MAP_B, DD_WRITE_SECTOR, DD_CHECK_SECTOR, DD_FORMAT, DD_READ_ID,\nDD_TEST_UNSUITABLE, DD_LOGIN, DD_SEL_FORMAT, DD_EQUIPMENT and DD_L_WRITE ($0154,\n$0166-$0178, $0181, $0193): rc_notimp, as documented.\nExit: NC, A = $3A.","comment":"rc_notimp (58)"},
        "9627": {"comment":"NC"},
        "9629": {"synopsis":"DD_INTERFACE, DD_INIT, DD_SETUP, DD_SET_RETRY, DD_L_SEEK, DD_L_ON_MOTOR, DD_L_T_OFF_MOTOR\nand\nDD_L_OFF_MOTOR ($0157-$0160, $018D, $0196-$019C, as documented): nothing done; carry set."},
        "9631": {"synopsis":"DOS_SET_MESSAGE ($014E, as documented): nothing is kept; HL = 0. Flags as they were.","comment":"HL = 0: no routine"},
        "9635": {"synopsis":"Builds the 765's READ DATA command for one sector in the command block at $E400, the job of\nthe +3E ROM 2's READ_CMD_BUILD and SECTOR_CMD_BUILD together:\n1. CMD_HEAD_BUILD with the command byte (IX+$19) OR 6.\n2. E + the first sector number (+$14), passed to the sector hook at $E419 when one is set\n(DD_ENCODE), which may change E.\n3. +$0A the sector, +$0B the size code (+$0F), +$0C the same sector, +$0D the gap (+$17),\n+$08 the track, +$09 the head, +$05 = 9 (the command's length), +$0E $FF.\nEntry: IX = the parameter block, B = the bank, HL = the buffer, C = the unit, D = the\nlogical track, E = the sector.\nExit: D = the track, E = the sector number before the hook; B = the head, C = the unit and\nhead; HL = $E40E.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"The command byte: READ DATA ($06)"},
        "9640": {"comment":"Bank, buffer, unit and head"},
        "9643": {"comment":"E = the sector + the first number"},
        "9648": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9649": {"comment":"A sector hook?"},
        "9654": {"comment":"Called: it may change E"},
        "9657": {"comment":"+$0A: R, the sector"},
        "9661": {"comment":"+$0B: N, the size code; +$0C: EOT"},
        "9668": {"comment":"+$0D: the gap"},
        "9674": {"comment":"+$08: the track, +$09: the head"},
        "9679": {"comment":"+$05: 9 command bytes"},
        "9684": {"comment":"+$0E: DTL, $FF"},
        "9689": {"comment":"DE as before the hook"},
        "9691": {"synopsis":"Starts the command block at $E400: +$01 the buffer, +$00 the bank, the track and head\n(TRACK_TO_SIDE), +$06 the command byte, +$07 the unit and head, +$03 the byte count = the\nsector size (+$15).\nEntry: A = the command byte, B = the bank, HL = the buffer, C = the unit, D = the logical\ntrack, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: B = the head, C = the unit and head, D = the track.\nChanges: AF, BC, D, HL.","comment":"+$01: the buffer"},
        "9694": {"comment":"L = the command byte"},
        "9695": {"comment":"+$00: the bank"},
        "9699": {"comment":"Track and head from D"},
        "9702": {"comment":"+$06: the command, +$07: unit and head"},
        "9706": {"comment":"+$03: the sector size"},
        "9716": {"synopsis":"Turns logical track D into the track and the head by the sides byte (+$11, bit 7 left out):\n0\none side; 1 alternating (track D / 2, the head D's bit 0); 2 or more one side after the\nother\n(head 1 from the tracks per side (+$12) on, the track 2 x tracks per side - 1 - D).\nEntry: D, C = the unit, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: D = the track, B = the head, C = the unit with the head in bit 2.\nChanges: AF, B, C, D.","comment":"The sides byte"},
        "9721": {"comment":"Head 0; one side: done"},
        "9724": {"comment":"Alternating?"},
        "9727": {"comment":"Track / 2, the head its bit 0"},
        "9735": {"synopsis":"One side after the other.","comment":"Below the tracks per side: head 0"},
        "9741": {"comment":"From there: counted back on head 1"},
        "9747": {"synopsis":"The head into bit 2 of C.","comment":"The head into bit 2 of C"},
        "9753": {"synopsis":"DD_ENCODE ($0184, as documented): sets the routine called with each sector number before a\nsector command (READ_CMD_BUILD), its address kept at $E419; the job of the +3E ROM 2's\nSECTOR_HOOK_SET.\nEntry: A = 0 for none, else HL = the routine.\nExit: HL = the one it replaced (0 for none).\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"A = 0: none"},
        "9759": {"synopsis":"The new routine in, the old one out to HL.","comment":"The new one in, the old one to HL"},
        "9768": {"synopsis":"DD_L_XDPB ($0187, as documented): sets the parameter block (XDPB) at IX from a 10-byte\nformat\nat HL (FORMAT_SPECS' layout), as the +3E ROM 2's FORMAT_FROM_SPEC: +$14 the first sector\nnumber ($41 for format 1, $C1 for 2, $01 otherwise), +$11 the sides, +$12 tracks per side,\n+$13 sectors per track, +$17 and +$18 the gaps, +$15 the sector size ($80 x 2^n), +$19 =\n$60; then DD_L_DPB. Also from IMAGE_DSK_XDPB.\nEntry: HL = the format, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: as DD_L_DPB.","comment":"The format kept"},
        "9770": {"comment":"Its number"},
        "9771": {"comment":"1: sectors from $41"},
        "9776": {"comment":"2: from $C1"},
        "9781": {"comment":"Others: from $01"},
        "9783": {"synopsis":"The first sector number into +$14, and the rest of the format.","comment":"+$14: the first sector number"},
        "9787": {"comment":"+$11: the sides byte"},
        "9792": {"comment":"+$12: tracks per side"},
        "9797": {"comment":"+$13: sectors per track"},
        "9802": {"comment":"B = the sector size code"},
        "9803": {"comment":"Past +5 to +7"},
        "9807": {"comment":"+$17: the read/write gap"},
        "9812": {"comment":"+$18: the format gap"},
        "9816": {"comment":"The size: $80 x 2^n"},
        "9822": {"comment":"+$15 and +$16"},
        "9828": {"comment":"+$19: $60"},
        "9832": {"comment":"On with the format"},
        "9834": {"synopsis":"DD_L_DPB ($018A, as documented): works out the rest of the parameter block at IX from a\n10-byte format at HL, as the +3E ROM 2's PARAMS_FROM_SPEC; n is the sector size code, c the\nblock size code:\n+$00 the 128-byte records per track; +$02 c, +$03 2^c - 1; +$04 2^(c - 3) - 1, or\n2^(c - 4) - 1 above 256 blocks; +$05 the blocks less 1; +$07 the directory entries less 1;\n+$09, +$0A a bit per directory block from the top; +$0B the entries / 4 + 1; +$0D the\nreserved tracks (+$0E 0); +$0F n, +$10 2^n - 1. A format's +7 of 0 gives\n(blocks - 1) x 2 / 256 + 1 directory blocks, at least 2. Also from RAMDISK_SETUP.\nEntry: HL = the format, IX = the parameter block.\nExit: carry; A = the format's number; DE = (blocks - 1) / 4 + 2; HL = 4 x the directory\nentries.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"BC and the format kept"},
        "9836": {"comment":"DE = the format"},
        "9837": {"comment":"+4: the sector size code n"},
        "9842": {"comment":"+$0F: n"},
        "9846": {"comment":"+$10: 2^n - 1"},
        "9852": {"comment":"The sectors per track"},
        "9856": {"comment":"x 2^n: 128-byte records"},
        "9860": {"comment":"+$00 and +$01"},
        "9866": {"comment":"+6: the block size code c"},
        "9871": {"comment":"+$02: c"},
        "9876": {"comment":"+$03: 2^c - 1"},
        "9882": {"comment":"+5: the reserved tracks"},
        "9884": {"comment":"+$0D and +$0E"},
        "9891": {"comment":"B = sectors, D = tracks, A = sides"},
        "9898": {"comment":"HL = the tracks"},
        "9902": {"comment":"Two sides: doubled"},
        "9907": {"synopsis":"The tracks less the reserved ones, times the sectors per track.","comment":"Less the reserved ones"},
        "9910": {"comment":"x the sectors per track"},
        "9913": {"synopsis":"One more track's sectors."},
        "9916": {"comment":"B = c - n"},
        "9921": {"comment":"Sectors to blocks"},
        "9924": {"comment":"+$05 and +$06: the blocks less 1"},
        "9931": {"comment":"B = 3, or 4 above 256 blocks"},
        "9938": {"synopsis":"+$04 = 2^(c - B) - 1; then the directory.","comment":"+$04: 2^(c - B) - 1"},
        "9946": {"comment":"DE = the format + 6"},
        "9947": {"comment":"The blocks less 1 kept"},
        "9948": {"comment":"/ 4 + 2, stacked for the exit"},
        "9956": {"comment":"+7: the directory blocks"},
        "9959": {"comment":"0: worked out from the blocks"},
        "9968": {"comment":"At least 2"},
        "9969": {"synopsis":"B = the directory blocks: that many bits from the top.","comment":"As many bits from the top"},
        "9973": {"synopsis":"One more bit from the top."},
        "9980": {"comment":"+$09 and +$0A"},
        "9986": {"comment":"HL = the directory blocks"},
        "9989": {"comment":"x 2^(c + 2): the entries"},
        "9995": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9996": {"comment":"+$07 and +$08: the entries less 1"},
        "10003": {"comment":"/ 4 + 1"},
        "10009": {"comment":"+$0B and +$0C"},
        "10015": {"comment":"HL = 4 x the entries"},
        "10018": {"comment":"DE = (blocks - 1) / 4 + 2"},
        "10019": {"comment":"A = the format's number"},
        "10022": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "10024": {"synopsis":"Four disk formats, 10 bytes each, the same 40 bytes as the +3E ROM 2's FORMAT_SPECS: +0 the\nformat number, +1 the sides byte, +2 tracks per side, +3 sectors per track, +4 the sector\nsize code, +5 reserved tracks, +6 the block size code, +7 directory blocks (0: worked out),\n+8 and +9 the gaps (DD_L_XDPB, DD_L_DPB).\nFormat 0: one side, 40 tracks of 9 512-byte sectors, 1 reserved track, 1K blocks, 2\ndirectory blocks, gaps $2A and $52. IMAGE_REGISTER takes it for a disk image whose first\nsector carries no format."},
        "10034": {"synopsis":"Format 1: format 0 with 2 reserved tracks (sectors from $41). For a disk image whose first\nsector number has bit 6 set (IMAGE_SPEC_ID)."},
        "10044": {"synopsis":"Format 2: format 0 with no reserved track (sectors from $C1). For a disk image whose first\nsector number has bit 7 set."},
        "10054": {"synopsis":"Format 3: two sides alternating (bit 7 of the sides byte set), 80 tracks of 9 512-byte\nsectors, 1 reserved track, 2K blocks, 4 directory blocks. Nothing in this page reads it."},
        "10064": {"synopsis":"DD_ASK_1 ($017B, as documented): tells whether unit 1 is there, by DD_DRIVE_STATUS for unit\n1.\nExit: carry and A = $20 when its bit 5 is set; otherwise A = 0, NC, Z.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"Unit 1"},
        "10070": {"comment":"Bit 5 or 6?"},
        "10074": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "10076": {"synopsis":"JP (HL): CALL $275C calls the routine at HL (the sector hook, from READ_CMD_BUILD)."},
        "10077": {"synopsis":"A = 2^A - 1, the low A bits set (0 for 0).\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"0: 0"},
        "10080": {"comment":"1 doubled A times"},
        "10082": {"synopsis":"Doubled once."},
        "10085": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "10087": {"synopsis":"HL = HL x 2^B.\nChanges: AF, B (0 after a shift), HL.","comment":"B = 0: nothing"},
        "10090": {"synopsis":"One bit left."},
        "10094": {"synopsis":"HL = HL / 2^B, rounded down.\nChanges: AF, B (0 after a shift), HL.","comment":"B = 0: nothing"},
        "10097": {"synopsis":"One bit right."},
        "10104": {"synopsis":"DD_DRIVE_STATUS ($017E, as documented): for unit 0 or 1 (C bit 0) the status is bit 5 of\n+$1B\nof drive A's ($E2DB) or drive B's ($E348) parameter block, with the unit in bit 0. Also from\nDD_ASK_1.\nExit: A = that, carry; C = the unit.\nChanges: AF, C.","comment":"C = the unit, 0 or 1"},
        "10108": {"comment":"Drive A's +$1B"},
        "10113": {"comment":"Unit 1: drive B's"},
        "10116": {"synopsis":"Bit 5, the unit in bit 0; carry.","comment":"Bit 5 with the unit"},
        "10121": {"synopsis":"DD_READ_SECTOR ($0163, as documented): reads one sector: the READ DATA command block at\n$E400\n(READ_CMD_BUILD), then the DivMMC memory's $30CC (bank $0C) with HL = $E400 (kept at $5B52\nby RST $08).\nEntry: as READ_CMD_BUILD.\nExit: carry when the byte after the one at the HL it returns equals C (the unit and head);\notherwise A = 0, NC.","comment":"The command block"},
        "10126": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "10129": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $30CC runs it (bank $0C)"},
        "10135": {"comment":"Unit and head as sent?"},
        "10140": {"comment":"No: A = 0, NC"},
        "10142": {"synopsis":"DD_L_READ ($0190, as documented): the DivMMC memory's $30CC (bank $0C) with the caller's HL,\nthe command block.","comment":"The DivMMC memory's $30CC, HL as given"},
        "10147": {"synopsis":"\"4>RAMdisk\" and $FF: DRIVE_MAPPING's text for the RAM disk's drive; its first character,\nless '0', is the device number."},
        "10157": {"synopsis":"Keeps BASIC's state in a frame on the machine stack round a call that runs BASIC (from\nIDE_BASIC's $0FA7 and IDE_TOKENISER's $1090), undone by RUN_FRAME_DROP:\n1. The return address into IX.\n2. Stacked: HL, DE, ERR_SP, $5B6C, $5C0B, a word with high byte $3E (the low byte left from\n$5C0B), BC.\n3. ROM 1's GOSUB_PUSH ($3A40) with A = $2F: an 11-byte entry of type $2F below the two top\nwords (BC and the $3Exx word, which ERR_SP then marks).\n4. BC, DE and HL back; on to the address in IX.\nChanges: AF, IX, the stack.","comment":"IX = the return address"},
        "10159": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "10161": {"comment":"ERR_SP"},
        "10165": {"comment":"$5B6C"},
        "10169": {"comment":"$5C0B"},
        "10173": {"comment":"A word $3Exx"},
        "10176": {"comment":"BC on top"},
        "10177": {"comment":"Entry type $2F"},
        "10179": {"comment":"ROM 1's GOSUB_PUSH"},
        "10184": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "10185": {"comment":"DE and HL back from the frame"},
        "10197": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "10199": {"synopsis":"Undoes RUN_FRAME_SET's frame: ROM 1's GOSUB_RESTORE ($3AC8) on its GO SUB entry, then $5C0B,\n$5B6C and ERR_SP from the frame; SP past it; FLAGS bit 7 set. AF, BC, DE, HL as on entry.\nChanges: IX, HL'.","comment":"Registers kept"},
        "10203": {"comment":"HL + 1 = the GO SUB entry"},
        "10207": {"comment":"ROM 1's GOSUB_RESTORE"},
        "10214": {"comment":"$5C0B back"},
        "10222": {"comment":"$5B6C back"},
        "10230": {"comment":"ERR_SP back"},
        "10238": {"comment":"Past DE and HL"},
        "10242": {"comment":"AF, BC, DE back"},
        "10245": {"comment":"HL back; the frame's end on top"},
        "10246": {"comment":"SP past the frame, IX = the return"},
        "10252": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7: running"},
        "10256": {"comment":"Back to the caller"},
        "10258": {"synopsis":"DOS_DELETE ($0124, as documented; page 0's ERASE_FILE calls it at its $397D): deletes the\nfile named at HL ($021D), then its metadata file (META_NAME's name at $F700, $021D again,\nthe result ignored), as the document's note on F_UNLINK says DOS_DELETE does.\nExit: carry; or NC with A = the error from the first delete.","comment":"The name kept"},
        "10259": {"comment":"The file deleted ($021D)"},
        "10263": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "10264": {"comment":"Its metadata file's name at $F700"},
        "10270": {"comment":"Deleted too, if made"},
        "10273": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "10275": {"synopsis":"DOS_RENAME ($0127, as documented; page 0 calls it at its $3ABC): renames the file at HL to\nthe name at DE, and its metadata file with it (the document's note on F_RENAME):\n1. The metadata names of both (META_NAME_RESOLV) to $F700 (old) and $FB00 (new).\n2. When the old one ends in '/', that '/' is cut, and a \".{}\" at the end of the new one too\n(Z then).\n3. RENAME_BASE.\nExit: carry; or NC with A = the error.","comment":"Both names kept"},
        "10277": {"comment":"The old one's metadata name to $F700"},
        "10283": {"comment":"HL = the new name"},
        "10285": {"comment":"The old one's end kept"},
        "10286": {"comment":"The new one's to $FB00"},
        "10292": {"comment":"HL = the old one's end"},
        "10293": {"comment":"Ends in '/'?"},
        "10299": {"comment":"Cut there"},
        "10301": {"comment":"HL = the new one's end"},
        "10303": {"comment":"Ends in '}'?"},
        "10308": {"comment":"\".{}\" cut"},
        "10312": {"synopsis":"The file renamed ($0598); failed: its error. Then the new metadata name's directories made\n(META_MAKE_DIRS); with Z (from DOS_RENAME's step 2) the last one deleted again (IDE_PATH, A\n= 3); the old metadata file renamed to the new name ($0598), the result ignored.","comment":"DE = the new name, HL = the old"},
        "10314": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "10315": {"comment":"The file renamed ($0598)"},
        "10319": {"comment":"Failed: its error"},
        "10321": {"comment":"The new metadata directories made"},
        "10327": {"comment":"Z: the last one deleted again"},
        "10334": {"comment":"DE = the new metadata name"},
        "10335": {"comment":"The old metadata file renamed"},
        "10341": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "10343": {"synopsis":"Builds at $F700 the name of the metadata file of the file named at HL (META_NAME_BUILD with\nNC). From DOS_OPEN's $03B3 (access mode bit 3) and DOS_DELETE.","comment":"DE = $F700"},
        "10346": {"comment":"NC: with the name"},
        "10349": {"synopsis":"META_NAME_BUILD for the name at HL into DE, after the DivMMC memory's $034F and $0218 (bank\n0) and, with S from them, its $1C23; the carry left (set when S is clear) asks for the path\nonly. From DOS_RENAME.","comment":"Buffer and name kept"},
        "10351": {"comment":"The DivMMC memory's $034F"},
        "10355": {"comment":"Then its $0218"},
        "10359": {"comment":"BC = the name, DE = the buffer"},
        "10361": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "10364": {"comment":"Carry; S clear: on"},
        "10368": {"comment":"S set: the DivMMC memory's $1C23"},
        "10372": {"synopsis":"HL = the name, DE = the buffer.","comment":"HL = the name, DE = the buffer"},
        "10374": {"synopsis":"Builds a metadata file name at DE for the file named at HL ($FF-ended):\n1. META_PREFIX, \"C:/NEXTZXOS/METADATA/\".\n2. The name copied after it; the place after its last ':', '/' or '\\' noted (the bare name).\n3. IDE_PATH (A = 1, rc_path_get) on the copy: the current path of that location written\nthere; NC is its error.\n4. Every ':' in it made '_'.\n5. With NC on entry the bare name and \".{}\" are added.\nEntry: HL = the name, DE = the buffer, carry for the path only.\nExit: carry, HL = the buffer, DE at its $FF; or NC with A = the error.","comment":"Buffer and flags kept"},
        "10377": {"comment":"\"C:/NEXTZXOS/METADATA/\" first"},
        "10385": {"comment":"HL = the name"},
        "10386": {"comment":"The place after it kept"},
        "10388": {"synopsis":"One character of the name copied.","comment":"One character copied"},
        "10392": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "10396": {"comment":"'/'?"},
        "10400": {"comment":"'\\'?"},
        "10404": {"synopsis":"A separator: the place after it noted.","comment":"The place after it noted"},
        "10406": {"synopsis":"On to the $FF.","comment":"To the $FF"},
        "10409": {"comment":"HL = the bare name"},
        "10410": {"comment":"HL = the copy; the bare name kept"},
        "10412": {"comment":"rc_path_get: the path written there"},
        "10417": {"comment":"HL = the path, DE = the bare name"},
        "10419": {"comment":"Failed: the error"},
        "10421": {"synopsis":"':' made '_', up to the $FF.","comment":"':' made '_'"},
        "10428": {"synopsis":"The next character."},
        "10432": {"comment":"HL at the $FF"},
        "10433": {"comment":"Carry on entry: the path only"},
        "10437": {"synopsis":"The bare name copied on.","comment":"The bare name added"},
        "10444": {"comment":"Then \".{}\" and $FF"},
        "10456": {"synopsis":"Carry.","comment":"Carry"},
        "10457": {"synopsis":"HL = the buffer, DE = its end.","comment":"DE = the end"},
        "10458": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "10461": {"synopsis":"Makes each directory of the path at HL, from after its first 3 characters (\"C:/\"): at every\n'/' or '\\' the text up to it is made a directory (IDE_PATH, A = 2, rc_path_make) and the\nseparator put back as '/'; one that exists (rc_exists, $18) is fine. From DOS_OPEN's $03BC\nand RENAME_BASE.\nEntry: HL = the path, $FF-ended.\nExit: carry, HL = the path; or NC with A = the error.","comment":"The path kept"},
        "10462": {"comment":"Past \"C:/\""},
        "10465": {"synopsis":"One character.","comment":"'/'?"},
        "10470": {"comment":"'\\'?"},
        "10474": {"synopsis":"The next one, to the $FF (after a directory, the A IDE_PATH left is tested).","comment":"On to the $FF"},
        "10478": {"comment":"All made: carry"},
        "10481": {"synopsis":"A separator: the directory up to here made.","comment":"The path cut here"},
        "10483": {"comment":"HL = the path"},
        "10485": {"comment":"rc_path_make"},
        "10490": {"comment":"HL at the cut"},
        "10492": {"comment":"'/' back"},
        "10494": {"comment":"Made: on"},
        "10496": {"comment":"rc_exists: on"},
        "10500": {"comment":"Other errors: NC"},
        "10503": {"synopsis":"\"C:/NEXTZXOS/METADATA/\", 21 bytes with no end mark: copied by META_NAME_BUILD before each\nmetadata file name."},
        "10524": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3CFB."},
        "15612": {"synopsis":"The way into the DivMMC memory (from RST08_DIVMMC at $3F3D): NextReg $8E = 3 selects ROM 3,\nand the fetch from $3D00 that follows, with ROM 3 paged in, maps the DivMMC memory in (its\nautomap on $3Dxx, NextReg $BB bit 7; zxnext.vhd), so the code that runs there is its, not\nthe\nzeros here.","comment":"ROM 3: the fetch at $3D00 maps the DivMMC in"},
        "15616": {"synopsis":"$00 up to $3DFF, never run: a fetch here with ROM 3 paged in runs the DivMMC memory instead."},
        "15872": {"synopsis":"CALL $3E00 with a word after it: calls that address in ROM 0. The word is read (the return\naddress moved past it), ROM0_SELECT's address pushed as the way back (ROM 0's own $3E13\nselects ROM 2 again), then the address; BC kept through $5B54; ROM0_SELECT selects ROM 0 and\nits RET, fetched from ROM 0, goes to the address. The same bytes as page 0's CALL_ROM2.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "15876": {"comment":"BC = the word, the return past it"},
        "15882": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 0's $3E13"},
        "15886": {"comment":"The address"},
        "15887": {"synopsis":"BC back from $5B54; ROM 0; on to the address on the stack. From CALL_ALT_ROM0.","comment":"BC back"},
        "15891": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8E = 0: ROM 0 (bit 3 clear: only the ROM changes); RET, fetched from ROM 0. The way\ninto ROM 0, and the way back for page 0's calls into this ROM (its CALL $3E00 and RST $20).","comment":"ROM 0"},
        "15896": {"synopsis":"Calls the address in the word after the CALL in the alternate ROM, with ROM select 0, as\npage 1's CALL_ALT_ROM0 does:\n1. BC = the word.\n2. Pushed, last-run first: $3E13 (ROM 0's way back to this ROM), $007B, the routine, $007B.\n3. ROM0_GO: BC back and ROM 0; the RET goes to ROM 0's $007B (ALT_ROM_ON), which pages the\nalternate ROM in and enters the routine.\n4. The routine returns through the alternate ROM's $007B, then ROM 0's $3E13 selects ROM 2.\nFrom $1093 (word $14A7) and $1D05 (word $0003).","comment":"BC kept"},
        "15900": {"comment":"BC = the word, the return past it"},
        "15906": {"comment":"Last: ROM 0's $3E13 selects ROM 2"},
        "15910": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's $007B, the routine"},
        "15915": {"comment":"ROM 0's $007B: the alternate ROM in"},
        "15919": {"comment":"BC back, ROM 0"},
        "15922": {"synopsis":"CALL_ALT_ROM0 with ROM select 1: $3F13 (ROM 1's way back to this ROM) pushed, then ROM1_GO\nand ROM 1's $007B. Nothing in this page calls it.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "15926": {"comment":"BC = the word, the return past it"},
        "15932": {"comment":"Last: ROM 1's $3F13 selects ROM 2"},
        "15936": {"comment":"The alternate ROM's $007B, the routine"},
        "15941": {"comment":"ROM 1's $007B: the alternate ROM in"},
        "15945": {"comment":"BC back, ROM 1"},
        "15948": {"synopsis":"Puts 16K bank A at $C000 (MMU 6 = 2A, MMU 7 = 2A + 1) and gives the bank that was there\n(NextReg $56 read through ports $243B and $253B, halved). Called from $1631, $1674, $185A,\n$1872.\nEntry: A = the bank.\nExit: A = the old bank.\nChanges: F; the NextReg selected is $56.","comment":"HL and BC kept"},
        "15950": {"comment":"NextReg $56 (MMU 6) selected"},
        "15957": {"comment":"L = the 8K page there"},
        "15960": {"comment":"MMU 6 = 2A"},
        "15964": {"comment":"MMU 7 = 2A + 1"},
        "15968": {"comment":"A = the old bank"},
        "15974": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3EFF."},
        "16128": {"synopsis":"CALL $3F00 with a word after it: calls that address in ROM 1, as CALL_ROM0 does, with\nROM1_SELECT the way in and ROM 1's own $3F13 the way back.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "16132": {"comment":"BC = the word, the return past it"},
        "16138": {"comment":"The way back: ROM 1's $3F13"},
        "16142": {"comment":"The address"},
        "16143": {"synopsis":"BC back from $5B54; ROM 1; on to the address. From CALL_ALT_ROM1.","comment":"BC back"},
        "16147": {"synopsis":"NextReg $8E = 1: ROM 1; RET. The way into ROM 1, and the way back for page 1's calls into\nthis ROM (its CALL $3F00 and RST $00).","comment":"ROM 1"},
        "16152": {"synopsis":"RST $08 (the JP at $0008): calls a routine in the DivMMC memory, the byte and the word after\nthe RST giving A and HL:\n1. HL kept at $5B52, AF at $5B56 (for the routine to read).\n2. A = the byte, HL = the word; the return address moved past the three bytes.\n3. The interrupt state (P/V from LD A,I) kept with A; interrupts off; IY stacked.\n4. Port $E3 = 0 (the DivMMC memory paged out), $0448 pushed, DIVMMC_ENTER: ROM 3, and the\nfetch at $3D00 maps the DivMMC memory in; its code runs with A = the byte, HL = the word,\nBC and DE as the caller left them.\nThe way back is not in this page: $0448 is an address on the DivMMC side; DIVMMC_BACK undoes\nsteps 3 and 2 and is probably where it ends. By its uses the byte is the DivMMC RAM bank for\nthe call ($07 with $2855 and $2860, which page 1 reaches with port $E3 = $87; $0C and $0D\nwith\nthe copy routine $04DD) and the word the routine's address.","comment":"The caller's HL kept"},
        "16155": {"comment":"AF kept at $5B56"},
        "16160": {"comment":"HL = the inline bytes"},
        "16161": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "16162": {"comment":"A = the byte"},
        "16164": {"comment":"DE = the word"},
        "16167": {"comment":"The return past them"},
        "16168": {"comment":"DE back, the return on the stack"},
        "16169": {"comment":"HL = the word"},
        "16170": {"synopsis":"RST08_DIVMMC from step 3: from $05DD, with A = the byte, HL = the word, $5B52 set."},
        "16171": {"comment":"A parked in H"},
        "16172": {"comment":"P/V = IFF2: interrupts on?"},
        "16174": {"comment":"A = the byte again"},
        "16176": {"comment":"Interrupts off"},
        "16177": {"synopsis":"RST08_DIVMMC from step 3's PUSH, interrupts as they are: the IM 1 handler at $0038 calls it\n(CALL $3F31 with A = 0, HL = $0045).","comment":"The byte and the interrupt state kept"},
        "16178": {"comment":"IY kept"},
        "16181": {"comment":"DivMMC memory out (port $E3 = 0)"},
        "16185": {"comment":"The way back, in the DivMMC memory"},
        "16189": {"comment":"ROM 3, then $3D00: the DivMMC memory"},
        "16192": {"synopsis":"Undoes RST08_DIVMMC's stacking: IY back; the kept byte and flags swapped with HL; interrupts\non again when bit 2 of those flags (P/V from LD A,I) is set; AF and HL as the DivMMC code\nleft them; RET past the inline bytes. Nothing in the four pages jumps here: probably reached\nfrom the DivMMC side's way back ($0448).","comment":"IY back"},
        "16194": {"comment":"HL = the kept byte and flags"},
        "16195": {"comment":"AF from the call kept"},
        "16196": {"comment":"Interrupts were on?"},
        "16200": {"comment":"On again"},
        "16201": {"synopsis":"AF and HL back; return.","comment":"AF and HL back; past the inline bytes"},
        "16204": {"synopsis":"Unused: $00 up to $3FFF."}
      }
    },
