        "4932": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "4935": {"synopsis":"The flag characters of STR_MODIFIERS, searched by CPIR: '(' '^' '-' '+' '~' '>' '<' and the\n<> token ($C9); the one at place i (0-7) sets bit i of D."},
        "4943": {"synopsis":"Passes over one item of a list in brackets, from HL: strings in quotes and the hidden\nnumbers ($0E and 5 bytes) are passed whole, '(' and ')' counted (C, deeper than 127 stops\nwith error code $1F). Ends after a ',' at depth 0 (HL = the next item); a ')' at depth 0 is\nthe list's end: HL = the item's start, DE = the ')', B = 1.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"DE = the item's start"},
        "4945": {"comment":"C = 0: the depth"},
        "4947": {"synopsis":"The next byte of the item.","comment":"The byte"},
        "4948": {"comment":"One on"},
        "4949": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "4951": {"comment":"Then to the closing one"},
        "4953": {"comment":"A number marker?"},
        "4955": {"comment":"Then past its 5 bytes"},
        "4957": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "4959": {"comment":"Then deeper"},
        "4961": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "4963": {"comment":"Then out"},
        "4965": {"comment":"','?"},
        "4967": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "4969": {"comment":"At depth 0?"},
        "4971": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "4973": {"comment":"Yes: the item passed"},
        "4974": {"synopsis":"Inside quotes: on to the closing quote.","comment":"The byte"},
        "4976": {"comment":"The closing quote?"},
        "4978": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "4980": {"comment":"Yes: back to the item"},
        "4982": {"synopsis":"Past the 5 bytes of a hidden number.","comment":"Past the 5 bytes"},
        "4986": {"comment":"On"},
        "4988": {"synopsis":"'(': one deeper; past 127 stops with error code $1F.","comment":"One deeper"},
        "4989": {"comment":"Not too deep: on"},
        "4992": {"comment":"Too deep: error $1F"},
        "4994": {"synopsis":"')': one out; below depth 0 it is the list's end.","comment":"One out"},
        "4995": {"comment":"Still inside: on"},
        "4998": {"comment":"The end: HL = the item's start"},
        "4999": {"comment":"DE = the ')'"},
        "5000": {"comment":"B = 1: the end"},
        "5003": {"synopsis":"Unused: six zero bytes."},
        "5009": {"synopsis":"Report messages, in the keyword table's form (PRINT_MESSAGE's): entry 0 is empty ($80),\nentries 1-28 are the texts of reports 0-9 and A-R, \"OK\" to \"Tape loading error\". The bytes\nare the 48K ROM's, but nothing in this page loads their address (the 48K's report printer is\nnot here). START_MESSAGES follows straight on."},
        "5430": {"synopsis":"A table of its own from here in the 48K ROM: entry 0 is the last byte of \"Tape loading\nerror\", entry 1 is \", \", whose final space is START_MESSAGES' entry 0. Nothing in this page\nreads it."},
        "5432": {"synopsis":"Start-up messages, in PRINT_MESSAGE's form: entry 0 is a lone space, entry 1 the copyright\nline (the $7F character, then \" 1982 Sinclair Research Ltd\"), the 48K ROM's. Nothing in this\npage reads them."},
        "5461": {"synopsis":"GET_CHAR's work (RST $18 jumps here; also $273D): HL = CH_ADD, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "5464": {"comment":"The test"},
        "5467": {"synopsis":"NEXT_SKIP's work (RST $20 jumps here): CH_ADD + 1, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "5470": {"synopsis":"HL + 1, CH_ADD = HL and SKIP_CHAR: the character after the one at HL, past what is skipped.\nAlso called from $08C6, $0983 and $26B0.\nChanges: AF, HL; CH_ADD.","comment":"One on"},
        "5471": {"synopsis":"CH_ADD = HL, then SKIP_CHAR.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "5474": {"synopsis":"A = the character at HL; $21 and up and $0D are kept (return, no carry). Anything else moves\non: $18-$20 and the codes below $10 by one byte, $10-$15 by two, $16-$17 by three (the code\nand its operands), CH_ADD following.\nExit: A = the character, HL = CH_ADD, its address.","comment":"A = the character"},
        "5475": {"comment":"$21 and up: kept"},
        "5478": {"comment":"ENTER: kept"},
        "5481": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "5482": {"comment":"$18-$20: skipped"},
        "5486": {"comment":"Below $10: skipped"},
        "5490": {"comment":"$10-$15: one operand"},
        "5494": {"comment":"$16-$17: two"},
        "5497": {"synopsis":"HL = HL x DE with the Z80N MUL D,E (DE = D x E): one of H and D must be 0, or the product\ndoes not fit. Called from HL_MULT_FAST and $30DF.\nExit: carry when the product does not fit; otherwise HL = it, Z when 0.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.\nObserved: HL = 300, DE = 200 gave HL = 60000; $1234 x $0300 gave carry; 0 x 5 gave Z.","comment":"Carry: does not fit"},
        "5498": {"comment":"D = 0?"},
        "5500": {"comment":"Then on"},
        "5502": {"comment":"Both high bytes not 0?"},
        "5504": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "5505": {"synopsis":"The three byte products, H x E and D x L into the high byte, L x E added.","comment":"BC = DE"},
        "5507": {"comment":"D = H"},
        "5508": {"comment":"DE = H x E"},
        "5510": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "5512": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "5513": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "5514": {"comment":"D = the old D"},
        "5515": {"comment":"E = L"},
        "5516": {"comment":"DE = D x L"},
        "5518": {"comment":"Over 255?"},
        "5520": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "5521": {"comment":"A = the high byte"},
        "5522": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "5523": {"comment":"D = L"},
        "5524": {"comment":"E = the old E"},
        "5525": {"comment":"DE = L x E"},
        "5527": {"comment":"H = the high byte"},
        "5528": {"comment":"L = 0"},
        "5530": {"comment":"HL = the product"},
        "5531": {"comment":"Too big"},
        "5532": {"comment":"Z when 0, no carry"},
        "5535": {"synopsis":"HL = HL x DE when running (MUL_HL_DE), as HL_MULT does; too big stops with report 4 ($1F15).\nChecking syntax returns at once.\nKeeps BC, DE.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "5538": {"comment":"Then nothing"},
        "5539": {"comment":"BC and DE kept"},
        "5541": {"comment":"HL = HL x DE"},
        "5544": {"comment":"Back"},
        "5546": {"comment":"It fits"},
        "5547": {"comment":"Too big: report 4"},
        "5550": {"synopsis":"An unused $FF byte."},
        "5551": {"synopsis":"Channel data, in the 48K start-up's form: four 5-byte channels (output routine, input\nroutine, letter), then $80 to end the area. K: $09F4 and $10A8; S: $09F4 and CHAN_NO_INPUT;\nR: $0F81 and CHAN_NO_INPUT; P: PRINTER_OUT and CHAN_NO_INPUT. Nothing in this page reads it."},
        "5572": {"synopsis":"The input routine of channels S, R and P: stops with error code $12 (report J), as input\nfrom them is not possible."},
        "5574": {"synopsis":"Stream table, the 48K start-up's source for STRMS: a word per stream from -3 to 3, its\nchannel's offset in the channel area plus one: K (1) for -3, 0 and 1; S (6) for -2 and 2; R\n(11) for -1; P (16) for 3. Nothing in this page reads it."},
        "5588": {"synopsis":"Waits for a key from the current channel: calls its input routine (CHAN_INPUT) until one\ncomes (carry). Sets TV_FLAG bit 3 first unless bit 5 is set. An input routine giving NZ and\nno carry stops with error code 7 (report 8, \"End of file\").\nExit: A = the key.","comment":"Bit 5: the lower screen to be cleared?"},
        "5594": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 3: show the edit line"},
        "5598": {"synopsis":"Calls the input routine: carry is a key, Z means none yet.","comment":"The input routine"},
        "5601": {"comment":"Carry: a key"},
        "5602": {"comment":"Z: none yet"},
        "5604": {"comment":"Otherwise report 8"},
        "5606": {"synopsis":"Calls the current channel's input routine, the second word at CURCHL, with the alternate\nregister set in use (CALL_AT_HL).","comment":"The alternate set"},
        "5607": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "5608": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "5611": {"comment":"HL to the input routine's word"},
        "5615": {"synopsis":"Prints A + \"0\" through the current channel (PRINT_A_CHAN).","comment":"E = \"0\""},
        "5617": {"comment":"+ A"},
        "5618": {"synopsis":"PRINT_A's work: calls the current channel's output routine (the first word at CURCHL) with\nthe alternate register set in use, so the caller's BC, DE and HL are untouched; HL' is kept\ntoo.","comment":"The alternate set"},
        "5619": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "5620": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL: the output routine's word"},
        "5623": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine whose address is the word at HL: the output routine from PRINT_A_CHAN, or\nthe input routine when the code at $15E6 comes here with HL two bytes on. Then HL' back and\nthe main register set again.","comment":"DE = the routine"},
        "5626": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "5627": {"comment":"Called"},
        "5630": {"comment":"HL' back"},
        "5631": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "5633": {"synopsis":"Makes stream A (-3 to 15) current: its STRMS word less one is its channel's offset in CHANS,\nand CURCHL = that channel. A stream with a zero word stops with error code $17 (report O).\nThen CHAN_SET_FLAGS: FLAGS2 bit 4 cleared, and the channel's letter picks the flags to set\nthrough CHAN_LETTERS.\nChanges: AF, C, DE, HL; CURCHL.","comment":"A x 2"},
        "5636": {"comment":"STRMS + 6 + 2A: stream -3 is the first word"},
        "5639": {"comment":"DE = the stream's word"},
        "5642": {"comment":"No channel?"},
        "5646": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $17 (report O): a stream with no channel. Also jumped to from\nelsewhere."},
        "5648": {"synopsis":"CURCHL = CHANS + the offset - 1.","comment":"Less 1"},
        "5649": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5652": {"comment":"+ the offset: the channel"},
        "5653": {"synopsis":"STREAM_SELECT's second half, also called on its own with HL = a channel's address already in\nCURCHL: clears FLAGS2 bit 4 and sets the flags its letter asks for: CHAN_K_FLAGS,\nCHAN_S_FLAGS or CHAN_P_FLAGS; another letter (R) sets none.","comment":"CURCHL = it"},
        "5656": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 4 clear: not channel K"},
        "5660": {"comment":"HL to the channel's letter"},
        "5664": {"comment":"C = the letter"},
        "5665": {"comment":"HL = CHAN_LETTERS"},
        "5668": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "5671": {"comment":"Not there: no flags"},
        "5672": {"comment":"DE = the offset"},
        "5675": {"comment":"HL = the routine"},
        "5676": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL: a CALL here calls the routine at HL."},
        "5677": {"synopsis":"Channel letters and offsets for CHAN_SET_FLAGS (TABLE_LOOKUP): K to CHAN_K_FLAGS, S to\nCHAN_S_FLAGS, P to CHAN_P_FLAGS; 0 ends it. Each offset counts from its own byte."},
        "5684": {"synopsis":"Channel K's flags: TV_FLAG bit 0 set (the lower screen), FLAGS bit 5 cleared, FLAGS2 bit 4\nset; then as for S (CHAN_KS_COMMON)."},
        "5698": {"synopsis":"Channel S's flags: TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared (the upper screen)."},
        "5702": {"synopsis":"K and S: FLAGS bit 1 cleared (not the printer), then the temporary colours\n(COLOURS_TO_TEMP)."},
        "5709": {"synopsis":"Channel P's flags: FLAGS bit 1 set (the printer)."},
        "5714": {"synopsis":"Makes room for one byte before HL (MAKE_ROOM with BC = 1).","comment":"One byte"},
        "5717": {"synopsis":"Opens BC bytes of room before HL: checks they fit (TEST_ROOM, report 4 when not), moves the\npointer variables past HL up by BC (MOVE_POINTERS), then everything from HL to the old\nSTKEND up by BC.\nExit: DE = the room's last byte (HL + BC - 1), HL = the given HL - 1, BC = 0.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "5718": {"comment":"Room?"},
        "5721": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5722": {"comment":"The pointers moved"},
        "5725": {"comment":"HL = the old STKEND"},
        "5728": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the new"},
        "5729": {"comment":"Everything moved up"},
        "5732": {"synopsis":"A jump to the pointer-moving routine at $3B86; MAKE_ROOM and RECLAIM call $3B86 directly,\nand nothing in this ROM jumps here.","comment":"To $3B86"},
        "5735": {"synopsis":"A string array's element, from SV_RPT_C with its offset on the stack and DE at the last\ndimension: GET_DIM gives the string length, the offset x that length (the multiply at $159F)\nplus the data's start is the element, stacked as a string (STK_ST_0). Then ')' ends it, ','\nslices it (STR_SLICE), anything else is report 3; more '(' slices may follow\n(SV_SLICE_TEST).","comment":"DE = the length, HL at its high byte"},
        "5738": {"comment":"HL = the offset; the data pointer kept"},
        "5739": {"comment":"Offset x length"},
        "5742": {"comment":"BC = the byte before the data"},
        "5743": {"comment":"Plus it"},
        "5744": {"comment":"HL = the element's first character"},
        "5745": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "5747": {"comment":"DE = the element"},
        "5748": {"comment":"Stacked as a string"},
        "5751": {"comment":"The character after the subscripts"},
        "5752": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "5756": {"comment":"','? A slice of the element"},
        "5758": {"comment":"Neither: report 3"},
        "5761": {"synopsis":"A slice (STR_SLICE), then past its ')'.","comment":"Sliced"},
        "5764": {"synopsis":"Past the ')'; then any further slices (SV_SLICE_TEST).","comment":"Past the ')'"},
        "5765": {"synopsis":"Another '(' is another slice (SV_STR_SLICE); otherwise FLAGS bit 6 is cleared (a string) and\nthe subscripts are done.","comment":"Another '('?"},
        "5769": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "5775": {"synopsis":"Two zero bytes: LINE_NO_PREV reads them as line number 0 when there is no line."},
        "5777": {"synopsis":"HL is not a line (bits 6-7 of its first byte set: the variables): tries the line at DE, and\nthen ZERO_WORD's 0.","comment":"HL = the line at DE"},
        "5778": {"comment":"DE = ZERO_WORD"},
        "5781": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of the line at HL (high byte first); when HL is not a line, the number of\nthe line at DE, or 0 (LINE_NO_PREV).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The first byte"},
        "5782": {"comment":"Bits 6-7: not a line?"},
        "5786": {"comment":"D = the number's high byte"},
        "5788": {"comment":"E = its low byte"},
        "5790": {"synopsis":"The rest of WORK_ROOM: opens the room before STKBOT - 1 (MAKE_ROOM), so that byte's copy\nlands in the room; WORKSP is put back (MOVE_POINTERS moves it when the workspace is empty).","comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "5793": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "5794": {"comment":"The room before it"},
        "5797": {"comment":"HL past the room"},
        "5799": {"comment":"BC = the old WORKSP"},
        "5800": {"comment":"WORKSP back"},
        "5804": {"comment":"BC = the count"},
        "5805": {"comment":"DE = past the room, HL = its last byte"},
        "5806": {"comment":"HL past the room"},
        "5808": {"synopsis":"Empties the edit line to a single $0D (K_CUR on it) followed by $80, then the workspace and\nthe calculator stack (CLEAR_WS).\nChanges: HL; K_CUR, WORKSP, STKBOT, STKEND, MEM.","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "5811": {"comment":"The $0D"},
        "5813": {"comment":"K_CUR on it"},
        "5817": {"comment":"The $80"},
        "5820": {"comment":"WORKSP after it"},
        "5823": {"synopsis":"Empties the workspace and the calculator stack: STKBOT = WORKSP, then CALC_RESET.\nChanges: HL; STKBOT, STKEND, MEM.","comment":"HL = WORKSP"},
        "5826": {"comment":"STKBOT = it"},
        "5829": {"synopsis":"Empties the calculator stack: STKEND = STKBOT, MEM = MEMBOT ($5C92).\nExit: HL = STKBOT.\nChanges: HL; STKEND, MEM.","comment":"HL = STKBOT"},
        "5832": {"comment":"STKEND = it"},
        "5835": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "5836": {"comment":"HL = MEMBOT"},
        "5839": {"comment":"MEM = it"},
        "5842": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "5844": {"comment":"DE = E_LINE: no caller in this ROM"},
        "5848": {"comment":"Removes from E_LINE up to HL (RECLAIM_DE_HL)"},
        "5851": {"synopsis":"Past the offset byte to the next pair."},
        "5852": {"synopsis":"Looks C up in a table of (code, offset) byte pairs at HL, ended by a zero code.\nExit: carry and HL = the matching offset byte; no carry when C is not there.\nChanges: AF, HL.","comment":"The code"},
        "5853": {"comment":"0: the end, no carry"},
        "5855": {"comment":"This one?"},
        "5856": {"comment":"HL to its offset"},
        "5857": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5859": {"comment":"Carry: found"},
        "5861": {"synopsis":"CLOSE #s: the stream's channel letter is looked up (CLOSE_CHANNEL, which changes nothing for\nK, S and P), then the stream word is put back: streams -3 to 3 to their channels at start-up\n(STREAM_DATA), 4-15 to 0 (closed). 16 or more is report O.\nObserved: after OPEN #4,\"s\", CLOSE #4 left stream 4's word 0 and PRINT #4 gave report O;\nafter OPEN #2,\"k\" (word 1), CLOSE #2 put it back to 6.","comment":"HL = the stream's word, BC = its value"},
        "5864": {"comment":"The channel's letter looked up"},
        "5867": {"comment":"0: closed"},
        "5870": {"comment":"$A3E2 + the word's address: carry for streams 4 and up"},
        "5873": {"comment":"HL = the word's address, DE = it"},
        "5874": {"comment":"Streams 4 and up: carry"},
        "5875": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "5877": {"comment":"Otherwise the start-up word: STREAM_DATA's ($15D4 + ...)"},
        "5880": {"comment":"HL = the word in STREAM_DATA"},
        "5881": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "5884": {"synopsis":"Stores BC as the stream's word.","comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "5885": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5889": {"synopsis":"Looks the stream's channel letter up in CLOSE_LETTERS and jumps to its entry; all three\nentries lead to CLOSE_DONE, so nothing more is done. HL kept.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "5890": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5893": {"comment":"+ the stream's value"},
        "5894": {"comment":"HL to the channel's letter"},
        "5897": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5898": {"comment":"DE = the stream's word"},
        "5899": {"comment":"HL = CLOSE_LETTERS"},
        "5902": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "5905": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "5908": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "5909": {"comment":"Into it"},
        "5910": {"synopsis":"CLOSE's channel letters for TABLE_LOOKUP: K, S and P, each offset leading to CLOSE_DONE."},
        "5916": {"synopsis":"HL back, and return."},
        "5918": {"synopsis":"The STRMS word of stream A (0-15; 16 or more is report O): HL = its address, BC = its value.\nChanges: AF, BC, HL.","comment":"A = the stream"},
        "5921": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "5923": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5925": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $17 (report O, \"Invalid stream\").\nObserved: FORMAT \"a\" gave \"O Invalid stream, 0:1\"."},
        "5927": {"synopsis":"HL = STRMS + 2 x (A + 3): the stream's word (stream -3 is the first).","comment":"+ 3: stream -3 first"},
        "5929": {"comment":"Times 2"},
        "5930": {"comment":"HL = STRMS"},
        "5936": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word"},
        "5937": {"comment":"BC = its value"},
        "5940": {"comment":"HL back to its low byte"},
        "5942": {"synopsis":"OPEN #s,c$: a stream already open on another channel than K, S or P is report O; the channel\n(OPEN_CHANNEL) gives the stream's word: K 1, S 6, P 16.\nObserved: OPEN #4,\"s\" set stream 4's word to 6 and PRINT #4 printed on the screen; OPEN\n#4,\"P\" then set it to 16; OPEN #16,\"s\" gave report O.","comment":"The stream number on top"},
        "5945": {"comment":"HL = the stream's word, BC = its value"},
        "5948": {"comment":"Closed?"},
        "5950": {"comment":"Then open it"},
        "5952": {"comment":"DE = the word's address"},
        "5953": {"comment":"HL = CHANS"},
        "5956": {"comment":"+ the value"},
        "5957": {"comment":"HL to its letter"},
        "5960": {"comment":"A = the letter"},
        "5961": {"comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "5962": {"comment":"K?"},
        "5966": {"comment":"S?"},
        "5970": {"comment":"P?"},
        "5972": {"comment":"Another: report O"},
        "5974": {"synopsis":"The stream's word = DE.","comment":"DE = the new value"},
        "5977": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "5981": {"synopsis":"The channel's name, one letter, either case: its offset from OPEN_LETTERS (DE = 1, 6 or 16);\nan empty name, another letter or a longer name is report F.\nObserved: OPEN #5,\"q\", OPEN #5,\"ss\" and OPEN #5,\"\" gave \"F Invalid file name\".","comment":"The word's address kept"},
        "5982": {"comment":"DE = the name, BC = its length"},
        "5985": {"comment":"Empty?"},
        "5987": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "5989": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0E (report F, \"Invalid file name\")."},
        "5991": {"synopsis":"The first letter, upper case (AND $DF), looked up.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "5992": {"comment":"The first letter"},
        "5993": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "5995": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "5996": {"comment":"HL = OPEN_LETTERS"},
        "5999": {"comment":"Looked up"},
        "6002": {"comment":"Not there: report F"},
        "6004": {"comment":"C = the offset"},
        "6007": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "6008": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "6009": {"comment":"Into it"},
        "6010": {"synopsis":"OPEN's channel letters for TABLE_LOOKUP: K to OPEN_K, S to OPEN_S, P to OPEN_P; 0 ends it."},
        "6017": {"synopsis":"K: offset 1.","comment":"K: 1"},
        "6021": {"synopsis":"S: offset 6.","comment":"S: 6"},
        "6025": {"synopsis":"P: offset 16.","comment":"P: 16"},
        "6027": {"synopsis":"The name must be one letter long (report F otherwise); D = 0.","comment":"Less 1"},
        "6028": {"comment":"One letter?"},
        "6030": {"comment":"No: report F"},
        "6032": {"comment":"D = 0"},
        "6033": {"comment":"HL = the word's address"},
        "6035": {"synopsis":"A function's operand must be a string (FLAGS bit 6 clear; a number is report C) and its\nresult is a number (bit 6 set). Then FN_RESULT runs the routine at IX.","comment":"A = $FF: FLAGS kept"},
        "6037": {"comment":"A string operand?"},
        "6039": {"comment":"The result a number"},
        "6041": {"comment":"Yes: run it"},
        "6043": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C): an operand of the wrong type for the function."},
        "6045": {"synopsis":"A function's operand must be a number and its result is a string: A = $BF, which clears\nFLAGS bit 6 in FN_RESULT.","comment":"A = $BF: bit 6 to be cleared"},
        "6049": {"synopsis":"A function's operand must be a number and so is its result: A = $FF.","comment":"A = $FF: FLAGS kept"},
        "6051": {"synopsis":"The operand must be a number (FLAGS bit 6 set), else report C.","comment":"A number operand?"},
        "6053": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "6055": {"synopsis":"FLAGS = FLAGS AND A, the result's type; when running (bit 7 of the result) the routine at IX\nruns through $0013 (JP (IX)). Then SCAN_OPERATOR.","comment":"The result's type"},
        "6057": {"comment":"Running (sign set): JP (IX)"},
        "6060": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "6063": {"synopsis":"Entry from $396A with D a value that goes on as USR's D (not $FF): no carry, then as USR\n(USR_KIND).","comment":"A = D"},
        "6064": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "6067": {"synopsis":"USR (operand table entry $C0): A = $FF and carry, then USR_KIND.","comment":"Carry"},
        "6068": {"comment":"A = $FF"},
        "6069": {"synopsis":"Which form follows the keyword (BRACKET_ARG):\n1. A '(' with one argument: USR_BRACKET.\n2. No '(': with '$' after the keyword USR_DOLLAR; otherwise, from OP_USR, the prefix\n   operation $ED of priority 16 (USR_PREFIX); from USR_BANK_ENTRY, operation $C0 with D and\n   $C0 pushed under it (USR_OTHER).","comment":"A and the carry kept"},
        "6071": {"comment":"A bracket after the keyword?"},
        "6074": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "6075": {"comment":"Yes: USR_BRACKET"},
        "6077": {"comment":"No: CH_ADD kept"},
        "6078": {"comment":"The character after the keyword"},
        "6079": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "6082": {"comment":"Yes: USR_DOLLAR"},
        "6084": {"comment":"CH_ADD back at the keyword"},
        "6087": {"comment":"A and carry back"},
        "6088": {"comment":"From USR_BANK_ENTRY?"},
        "6090": {"comment":"OP_USR: operation $ED"},
        "6092": {"synopsis":"Pushes operation C with priority 16 and reads the operand ($082D)."},
        "6095": {"synopsis":"DE = D and $C0, pushed, then operation $C0 with priority 16 ($3977).","comment":"E = $C0"},
        "6097": {"comment":"D = A"},
        "6098": {"comment":"To $3977"},
        "6101": {"synopsis":"The keyword with '$' after it: a '(' gives USR_DOL_BRACKET; without one, OP_USR's form is\nthe prefix $77 (USR_PREFIX), the other pushes '$' and D under operation $40 of priority 16.","comment":"A bracket after the '$'?"},
        "6104": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6106": {"comment":"A and carry back"},
        "6107": {"comment":"C = $77"},
        "6109": {"comment":"OP_USR: the prefix $77"},
        "6111": {"comment":"E = '$'"},
        "6113": {"comment":"D = A"},
        "6114": {"comment":"Priority 16, operation $40"},
        "6117": {"comment":"DE under it"},
        "6118": {"comment":"Pushed; the operand read ($082F)"},
        "6121": {"synopsis":"USR(...) or the other keyword's (...): DE = the A and flags pushed by USR_KIND. A ',' after\nthe first argument is the long form (USR_ARGS). One argument: a number runs $2188\n(USR_NUM_IX) through FN_TAKES_NUM; a string runs CALC_USR_STR ($34BC) through FN_TAKES_STR.","comment":"D = USR_KIND's A"},
        "6122": {"comment":"A ',' (NZ): more arguments"},
        "6124": {"comment":"IX = USR_NUM_IX"},
        "6128": {"comment":"A number?"},
        "6130": {"comment":"Yes: number to number"},
        "6132": {"comment":"IX = CALC_USR_STR"},
        "6136": {"comment":"A string to a number"},
        "6138": {"synopsis":"The '$' form with a bracket: one argument runs $2184 (USR_STR_IX) through FN_GIVES_STR; with\na ',' it goes on as USR_ARGS with no carry (a string result).","comment":"IX = USR_STR_IX"},
        "6142": {"comment":"D = USR_KIND's A"},
        "6143": {"comment":"One argument: number to string"},
        "6145": {"comment":"No carry: a string result"},
        "6146": {"synopsis":"The long form, KEY(a, b, c ...): a must be a number (report C), b a number or a string, and\nup to 16 more expressions follow, each left on the calculator stack, C counting them and DE\ntaking a bit for each (set for a number) from the top. Then ')' (report C) and USR_RUN,\nwhich calls address a with HL = the bits, DE and BC = b (a string's start and length, or a\nnumber in BC) and A = the count; carry asks for a number result.","comment":"D and the flags kept"},
        "6147": {"comment":"The carry kept"},
        "6148": {"comment":"The first a number?"},
        "6150": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "6153": {"comment":"The second argument"},
        "6156": {"comment":"Carry back"},
        "6157": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6160": {"comment":"The second a number?"},
        "6162": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6163": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "6165": {"comment":"A string: running?"},
        "6167": {"comment":"DE, BC = it"},
        "6170": {"comment":"On"},
        "6172": {"synopsis":"The second argument a number: BC = it (TAKE_WORD) when running.","comment":"Running?"},
        "6174": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "6177": {"synopsis":"The second argument kept (BC, DE); BC = the first (TAKE_WORD) when running, kept; C = 0\nextra arguments.","comment":"The second argument kept"},
        "6179": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "6183": {"comment":"BC = the first"},
        "6186": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6187": {"comment":"C = 0: no more yet"},
        "6189": {"synopsis":"Each ',' and expression after them: counted in C (17 or more is report C), its type's bit\n(FLAGS bit 6) shifted into DE from the top.","comment":"The character after the argument"},
        "6190": {"comment":"','?"},
        "6192": {"comment":"No: the end"},
        "6194": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6195": {"comment":"16 already?"},
        "6197": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "6200": {"comment":"Count and bits kept"},
        "6202": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "6207": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "6208": {"comment":"A = FLAGS"},
        "6211": {"comment":"Bit 6 into carry"},
        "6213": {"comment":"Into DE's top bit"},
        "6217": {"comment":"The next"},
        "6219": {"synopsis":"')' must end the arguments (report C); the registers are set out for USR_RUN, which calls\nthe code; then SCAN_OPERATOR.","comment":"')'?"},
        "6221": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "6224": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6225": {"comment":"HL = the bits"},
        "6226": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "6227": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "6228": {"comment":"HL = the first argument"},
        "6230": {"comment":"DE, BC = the second"},
        "6232": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "6233": {"comment":"C = the count"},
        "6234": {"comment":"The carry: the result's type"},
        "6236": {"comment":"DE = USR_KIND's A and flags"},
        "6237": {"comment":"The code called"},
        "6240": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "6269": {"synopsis":"Prints a line's text from HL to its $0D, with no space before a first keyword (FLAGS bit 0\nset). EDIT_LINE_SHOW enters here for the edit line."},
        "6273": {"synopsis":"Starts in K mode (FLAGS bit 2 clear), or L for INPUT's line (FLAGX bit 5); FLAGS2 bit 2\n(inside quotes) cleared.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "6274": {"comment":"DE = the text"},
        "6275": {"comment":"FLAGS2 bit 2 clear: not in quotes"},
        "6279": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6282": {"comment":"K mode"},
        "6284": {"comment":"INPUT?"},
        "6290": {"comment":"Then L mode"},
        "6292": {"synopsis":"One character: a flashing '?' first where X_PTR points (a syntax error), and the cursor\nwhere K_CUR points (PRINT_CURSOR); hidden numbers skipped (SKIP_NUMBER); the character\nthrough PRINT_LIST_CHR.","comment":"HL = X_PTR"},
        "6296": {"comment":"The error's place?"},
        "6300": {"comment":"'?'"},
        "6302": {"comment":"Flashing"},
        "6305": {"synopsis":"The cursor, then the character at DE.","comment":"The cursor, if here"},
        "6308": {"comment":"HL = the character's address"},
        "6309": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "6310": {"comment":"Past a hidden number"},
        "6313": {"comment":"On"},
        "6314": {"comment":"$0D?"},
        "6318": {"comment":"DE = the next"},
        "6319": {"comment":"Printed (PRINT_LIST_CHR)"},
        "6322": {"comment":"Again"},
        "6324": {"synopsis":"The $0D: done, DE back."},
        "6326": {"synopsis":"When A is the number marker $0E, moves HL past the hidden 5-byte number after it; A = the\nbyte there.\nChanges: A, HL.","comment":"The marker?"},
        "6329": {"comment":"Six bytes on"},
        "6335": {"comment":"A = the byte there"},
        "6337": {"synopsis":"Prints A flashing: ATTR_T bit 7 (FLASH) set and MASK_T's cleared, P_FLAG 0, for this one\ncharacter (SCREEN_OUTPUT); then all three back. Keeps the main registers (EXX).","comment":"The alternate set"},
        "6338": {"comment":"L = ATTR_T, H = MASK_T"},
        "6341": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6342": {"comment":"MASK_T bit 7 clear"},
        "6344": {"comment":"FLASH on"},
        "6346": {"comment":"Set"},
        "6349": {"comment":"HL = P_FLAG"},
        "6352": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "6353": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6354": {"comment":"P_FLAG = 0"},
        "6356": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6359": {"comment":"H = the old P_FLAG"},
        "6360": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6363": {"comment":"HL = the old ATTR_T, MASK_T"},
        "6364": {"comment":"Back"},
        "6367": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "6369": {"synopsis":"When DE = K_CUR, prints the cursor letter flashing (PRINT_FLASH): E or G for MODE 1 or 2;\notherwise K, or L when FLAGS bit 2 is set (L mode), or C instead of L with CAPS LOCK (FLAGS2\nbit 3). FLAGS bit 3 is set for L or C, cleared for K.\nObserved: the edit line showed PRINT 123L, then K at its start, E and G in those modes.","comment":"HL = K_CUR"},
        "6373": {"comment":"Here?"},
        "6375": {"comment":"No"},
        "6376": {"comment":"A = MODE"},
        "6379": {"comment":"Times 2"},
        "6381": {"comment":"MODE 0"},
        "6383": {"comment":"2 gives 'E', 4 'G'"},
        "6387": {"synopsis":"MODE 0: K, L or C.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "6390": {"comment":"Bit 3 clear: K"},
        "6392": {"comment":"'K'"},
        "6394": {"comment":"L mode?"},
        "6398": {"comment":"Bit 3 set"},
        "6400": {"comment":"'L'"},
        "6401": {"comment":"CAPS LOCK?"},
        "6407": {"comment":"'C'"},
        "6409": {"synopsis":"Prints the letter (PRINT_FLASH), DE kept."},
        "6415": {"synopsis":"DE = the number of the line after the one in the word at HL (FIND_LINE for that number + 1,\nthen LINE_NO), stored back (SET_LINE_WORD). KEY_DOWN uses it on E_PPC.","comment":"DE = the number"},
        "6418": {"comment":"The word's high byte kept"},
        "6419": {"comment":"HL = the number"},
        "6420": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "6421": {"comment":"HL = that line, or the next"},
        "6424": {"comment":"DE = its number"},
        "6427": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6437": {"synopsis":"A zero digit before the first: E is printed instead ($20, a space), or nothing when E is\n$FF.","comment":"A = E"},
        "6439": {"comment":"$FF: nothing"},
        "6440": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6442": {"synopsis":"Prints the digit of HL for the power of ten -BC: HL is left with the rest. A zero before the\nfirst digit is E (DIGIT_ZERO); a digit goes through PRINT_A_DIGIT, which leaves E = \"0\", so\nlater zeros print as 0.","comment":"A = 0"},
        "6443": {"synopsis":"Counts how many times the power fits.","comment":"HL less the power"},
        "6444": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "6445": {"comment":"Until below 0"},
        "6447": {"comment":"Added back"},
        "6449": {"comment":"A = the digit"},
        "6450": {"comment":"0: DIGIT_ZERO"},
        "6452": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "6455": {"synopsis":"Prints A (RST $10) and keeps FLAGS bit 2, the K/L mode the cursor shows: digits and codes\nbelow $21 leave it; THEN ($CB), and \":\" outside quotes and outside INPUT, clear it (K); a\nquote toggles FLAGS2 bit 2 (inside quotes); anything else sets it (L).","comment":"A digit?"},
        "6458": {"comment":"A digit: no change"},
        "6460": {"comment":"Below $21?"},
        "6464": {"comment":"K mode for now"},
        "6468": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "6472": {"comment":"':'?"},
        "6490": {"synopsis":"A quote: FLAGS2 bit 2 toggled.","comment":"A quote?"},
        "6494": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6495": {"comment":"A = FLAGS2"},
        "6498": {"comment":"Bit 2 toggled"},
        "6503": {"comment":"A back"},
        "6504": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bit 2 set: L mode."},
        "6508": {"synopsis":"Prints A."},
        "6510": {"synopsis":"Finds line HL: HL = the first line whose number is HL or more (or the variables area when\nnone), DE = the line before it (PROG when it is the first).\nExit: Z when the line is there.","comment":"The number kept"},
        "6511": {"comment":"HL = PROG"},
        "6514": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6516": {"comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6517": {"comment":"This line's number against it","synopsis":"The line at HL against BC (CMP_LINE_NO): returns when it is not smaller; otherwise DE = it\nand HL the line after it (NEXT_LINE), and again."},
        "6520": {"comment":"Not smaller: found"},
        "6522": {"comment":"DE = the next line"},
        "6525": {"comment":"DE = this one"},
        "6528": {"synopsis":"Compares the line number at HL (high byte first) with BC: Z when equal, carry when smaller.\nHL kept.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"The high bytes"},
        "6530": {"comment":"Different: done"},
        "6532": {"comment":"The low bytes"},
        "6533": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6536": {"comment":"No caller in this ROM: past a line's number and length"},
        "6539": {"synopsis":"Finds statement D of the line at HL (CH_ADD = HL), counting ':' and THEN outside quotes;\nwith E a token, stops at that token first.\nExit: Z when statement D is reached (CH_ADD before it); NC and A = E when the token is\nfound; carry at the line's ENTER.","comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "6542": {"comment":"C = 0: outside quotes"},
        "6544": {"synopsis":"One statement fewer to go; none: Z, found."},
        "6546": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "6547": {"comment":"The token?"},
        "6550": {"comment":"No carry: found"},
        "6552": {"synopsis":"The next byte."},
        "6554": {"synopsis":"Hidden numbers skipped (SKIP_NUMBER), CH_ADD kept; a quote toggles C bit 0 (inside quotes)."},
        "6557": {"comment":"CH_ADD = HL"},
        "6560": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "6564": {"comment":"Toggled"},
        "6565": {"synopsis":"':' or THEN: a statement starts, unless inside quotes.","comment":"':'?"},
        "6569": {"comment":"THEN?"},
        "6573": {"synopsis":"Outside quotes? Then the count."},
        "6577": {"synopsis":"ENTER ends the search: D - 1 and carry.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "6581": {"comment":"One less"},
        "6582": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "6584": {"synopsis":"Finds the item after the one at HL, a program line or a variable, by its first byte: $3F or\nbelow is a line (NEXT_LINE), above it a variable (VAR_SKIP). Then DIFFERENCE.\nExit: DE = the next item, HL = this one, BC = the length.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"This item kept"},
        "6585": {"comment":"$3F"},
        "6587": {"comment":"A line (the byte $3F or below)?"},
        "6588": {"comment":"Yes: past it"},
        "6591": {"comment":"A variable: past it"},
        "6594": {"comment":"DE = this item"},
        "6595": {"comment":"DIFFERENCE"},
        "6598": {"synopsis":"HL from a program line's first byte to the line after it: past its number, DE = its length\nword, added.\nExit: no carry (unless HL went past $FFFF).\nChanges: DE, HL, F.","comment":"Past the number"},
        "6600": {"comment":"DE = the length"},
        "6603": {"comment":"HL = the text"},
        "6604": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "6606": {"synopsis":"Pushes $5B48 and HL and jumps to the RAM routine at $5B4D: a call, from $391E, of the code\nat HL elsewhere, returning through $5B48 (an address in the RAM routines, not this ROM).","comment":"The way back: $5B48"},
        "6610": {"comment":"The address to call"},
        "6611": {"comment":"Through the RAM routine at $5B4D"},
        "6621": {"synopsis":"BC = HL - DE; then HL and DE swapped (HL = the old DE).\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL."},
        "6622": {"comment":"HL less DE"},
        "6624": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "6626": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "6627": {"comment":"Swapped"},
        "6629": {"synopsis":"Removes the bytes from DE up to, not including, HL (DIFFERENCE, then RECLAIM)."},
        "6632": {"synopsis":"Removes BC bytes at HL: moves the pointer variables past them down by BC (MOVE_POINTERS with\n-BC), then everything after them down.\nExit: HL = the old HL, now the first byte after the removed ones; BC = 0.\nChanges: F, BC, DE, HL.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "6633": {"comment":"BC = -BC"},
        "6640": {"comment":"The pointers moved down"},
        "6643": {"comment":"DE = HL, the first byte to remove"},
        "6644": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "6645": {"comment":"HL = the first byte after them"},
        "6646": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6647": {"comment":"Everything after them moved down"},
        "6649": {"comment":"HL = the old HL"},
        "6651": {"synopsis":"Reads the edit line's line number into BC through the calculator (CH_ADD left after it, the\ncalculator stack emptied at the end); 0 when there is none. 10000 or more stops with report\nC (REPORT_C).","comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "6654": {"comment":"Less 1"},
        "6655": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "6658": {"comment":"The first character"},
        "6659": {"comment":"HL = MEMBOT"},
        "6662": {"comment":"STKEND = it: the calculator stack there for the moment"},
        "6665": {"comment":"The digits"},
        "6668": {"comment":"BC = the number"},
        "6673": {"comment":"Carry when BC is 10000 or more ($D8F0 = -10000)"},
        "6677": {"synopsis":"Report C when the number did not fit 16 bits (FP_TO_BC's carry) or is 10000 or more (the\ncarry of adding -10000)."},
        "6680": {"comment":"The calculator stack emptied"},
        "6683": {"synopsis":"Prints BC as a decimal number with no leading zeros (E = $FF), for the report's line and\nstatement numbers. A number with B bit 7 set prints as 0.","comment":"DE and HL kept"},
        "6685": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "6686": {"comment":"B bit 7?"},
        "6688": {"comment":"Then 0"},
        "6690": {"comment":"HL = BC"},
        "6692": {"comment":"No leading zeros"},
        "6696": {"synopsis":"Prints the line number at HL (high byte first) in four characters, leading zeros as spaces\n(E = $20).\nExit: HL = the number's low byte.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "6697": {"comment":"DE = the number"},
        "6700": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "6701": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "6702": {"comment":"Spaces for leading zeros"},
        "6704": {"synopsis":"The thousands, hundreds and tens (DIGIT_OUT), then the units.","comment":"Thousands"},
        "6710": {"comment":"Hundreds"},
        "6716": {"comment":"Tens"},
        "6721": {"comment":"A = the units"},
        "6722": {"synopsis":"The last digit: A printed as a digit (PRINT_A_DIGIT), then HL and DE back. PRINT_BC_NUM\njumps here with A = 0 for a number with B bit 7 set.","comment":"Printed as a digit"},
        "6725": {"comment":"HL and DE back"},
        "6728": {"synopsis":"HL from a variable's first byte to the next variable:\n1. $7F, a string with a long name: the byte after it, the name up to a byte with bit 7 set,\n   a length word and its characters (VS_LONG_STR).\n2. Bit 5 clear (strings and arrays): a length word after the byte (VS_LENGTH).\n3. Bits 6 and 5 set: $60-$7F 6 bytes, $E0-$FF 19 (a FOR variable).\n4. Bit 6 clear, bit 5 set ($A0-$BF): a long name up to a byte with bit 7 set, then 6 bytes,\n   or 19 when that last letter has bit 5 clear (VS_LONG_NAME).\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The first byte"},
        "6729": {"comment":"$7F?"},
        "6731": {"comment":"Yes: a long string name"},
        "6733": {"comment":"Bit 5 clear?"},
        "6735": {"comment":"Yes: a length word"},
        "6737": {"comment":"Bit 6 to the sign, bit 7 to carry"},
        "6738": {"comment":"Bit 6 set: a short name"},
        "6741": {"synopsis":"A long number name: on to its last letter (bit 7 set); that letter's bit 5 clear gives carry\n(a FOR variable).","comment":"The next letter"},
        "6743": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry"},
        "6744": {"comment":"Not the last: on"},
        "6746": {"comment":"Bits 6, then 5, into carry"},
        "6748": {"comment":"Carry when bit 5 is clear"},
        "6749": {"synopsis":"6 bytes on, or 19 ($13) with carry.","comment":"6 bytes"},
        "6752": {"comment":"No carry: those"},
        "6755": {"comment":"Carry: 19"},
        "6760": {"synopsis":"$7F: past it and the byte after it.","comment":"Past the $7F"},
        "6761": {"synopsis":"On to the name's last letter (bit 7 set).","comment":"The next byte"},
        "6762": {"comment":"The last letter?"},
        "6764": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6766": {"synopsis":"DE = the length word after HL; HL past it.","comment":"Past the byte"},
        "6767": {"comment":"DE = the line's length"},
        "6771": {"comment":"HL = the $0D","synopsis":"HL + DE: the next variable."},
        "6773": {"synopsis":"Compares the long name at HL (a variable's first byte, then letters, the last with bit 7\nset) with the name in the line at the alternate HL + 1, spaces skipped and case ignored (OR\n$20); a last letter with bit 5 clear (a FOR variable's) matches too. The line's name must\nend there: the next character that is not a space must not be a letter or digit (ALPHANUM).\nExit: no carry when they match; carry otherwise.\nChanges: AF, DE, HL.","comment":"The line's name"},
        "6776": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6777": {"comment":"Past its first letter"},
        "6778": {"synopsis":"The next letter of the variable.","comment":"The variable's next letter"},
        "6779": {"synopsis":"The line's next character, spaces skipped.","comment":"The line's next"},
        "6781": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "6783": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "6785": {"comment":"Lower case"},
        "6787": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "6788": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "6790": {"comment":"With bit 7: the last letter?"},
        "6792": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "6793": {"comment":"Yes: the end"},
        "6795": {"comment":"Bit 5 clear: a FOR variable's"},
        "6797": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "6798": {"comment":"Carry: no match"},
        "6799": {"comment":"Different"},
        "6800": {"synopsis":"The variable's name ended: the line's must too (ALPHANUM gives carry for a letter or digit).","comment":"The line's next character"},
        "6802": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "6804": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "6806": {"comment":"Carry for a letter or digit"},
        "6809": {"synopsis":"256 bytes, one for each character code, read by SCAN_OP_LOOKUP: the operation for a\ncharacter after an operand. $3B: not an operator. '&' $FD, '*' $C4, '+' $CF, '-' $C3, '/'\n$C5, '<' $CD, '=' $CE, '>' $CC, '^' $C6, '|' $FE, $8B $FC, $8C $C1, $8D $C2, OR $C7, AND\n$C8, <= $C9, >= $CA, <> $CB; '?' $00 and '[' $01 send SCAN_OP_LOOKUP to $11B7. Each\noperation's priority is in OP_PRIORITIES."},
        "7065": {"synopsis":"NEW_STR_NAMED's end, with A = IXh x 2: with IXh bit 7 clear the string (DEST its last byte)\nis copied to the room's end (LDDR); then the name at the room's start (WRITE_STR_NAME) and\nthe length word after it.","comment":"IXh bit 7: no copy"},
        "7067": {"comment":"BC + 1 bytes"},
        "7068": {"comment":"HL = DEST: the string's last"},
        "7071": {"comment":"Copied to the room's end"},
        "7073": {"synopsis":"The name written at the room's start, then the string's length after it.","comment":"DE = the room's start"},
        "7074": {"comment":"The name"},
        "7077": {"comment":"HL = its last byte"},
        "7078": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7079": {"comment":"The length word"},
        "7083": {"comment":"Done"},
        "7084": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "7085": {"synopsis":"Writes a variable's name at DE from the name at K_CUR (NEW_STR_NAMED keeps it there): its\nfirst letter's bits 0-4 OR IXh ($40, a string) as the first byte; with more than one letter\n(IXl the count) that byte goes after a $7F (WRITE_NAME_REST).","comment":"HL = the name (in K_CUR)"},
        "7088": {"comment":"Its first letter"},
        "7089": {"comment":"The letter's bits"},
        "7091": {"comment":"The form from IXh"},
        "7093": {"comment":"B = the count of letters"},
        "7095": {"comment":"One letter?"},
        "7096": {"comment":"Then only that byte"},
        "7098": {"comment":"HL = the room"},
        "7099": {"comment":"$7F first"},
        "7102": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "7103": {"synopsis":"Stores A at DE, then B more letters of the name after HL, spaces skipped, in lower case; the\nlast with bit 7 set.\nChanges: AF, B, DE, HL.","comment":"The first byte"},
        "7104": {"synopsis":"The next letter, spaces skipped.","comment":"The next character"},
        "7106": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "7108": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "7110": {"comment":"Lower case"},
        "7112": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7114": {"comment":"All of them"},
        "7116": {"comment":"The last with bit 7"},
        "7118": {"synopsis":"Stores A."},
        "7120": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "7121": {"synopsis":"COUNT_NAME for the name at DEST.","comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "7124": {"synopsis":"Counts the letters and digits after HL, spaces skipped, up to the first other character\n(ALPHANUM).\nExit: HL at it, A = it, B = $FF less the count; 255 of them is report C.\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"B = 0"},
        "7126": {"comment":"Counted down from $FF"},
        "7128": {"synopsis":"The next character, spaces skipped.","comment":"The next character"},
        "7130": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "7132": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "7134": {"comment":"A letter or digit?"},
        "7137": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "7138": {"synopsis":"Counted; 255 is report C.","comment":"Counted"},
        "7140": {"comment":"Too many: report C"},
        "7142": {"comment":"Not reached"},
        "7150": {"synopsis":"The end of a statement's operands. Running: returns, and the command's routine runs.\nChecking: the return address and the two words under it are taken off, and the second of\nthem (HL) is jumped to with $0956 pushed as its return address ($0956 is not an instruction\nstart in this ROM).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7153": {"comment":"No: the command runs"},
        "7154": {"comment":"The return dropped"},
        "7155": {"comment":"HL = the word under it"},
        "7156": {"comment":"And the one under that"},
        "7157": {"comment":"The return address: $0956"},
        "7161": {"comment":"To the second word"},
        "7162": {"synopsis":"CLASS_4's end: DE (from LOOK_VARS) kept at $5B8C, then as class 1 (CLASS_VAR).","comment":"DE kept at $5B8C"},
        "7166": {"comment":"As class 1"},
        "7169": {"synopsis":"Operand classes: 12 bytes, one for each class 0-$0B, each a relative pointer to the class's\nroutine (this byte's address plus its value): CLASS_0 to CLASS_B."},
        "7181": {"synopsis":"Class 3, an optional number (RUN, RESTORE, RANDOMIZE, CLEAR): FETCH_NUM, then as class 0.","comment":"The number, if any"},
        "7184": {"synopsis":"Class 0: no more operands; Z set, then CLASS_5: the statement must end (STATEMENT_END)\nbefore the routine runs.","comment":"Z: the statement must end"},
        "7185": {"synopsis":"Class 5: the command's routine, whose address follows at T_ADDR, runs now, when checking and\nwhen running; it checks its own operands. (Class 0 enters with Z, which ends the statement\nfirst.)","comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7186": {"comment":"Z: STATEMENT_END first"},
        "7189": {"comment":"DE = CH_ADD's pointer, kept"},
        "7190": {"comment":"HL = T_ADDR: the routine's address"},
        "7193": {"comment":"BC = the command's routine"},
        "7196": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7197": {"comment":"Onto the stack"},
        "7198": {"comment":"Into the command's routine"},
        "7199": {"synopsis":"Class 1, a variable to assign to (LET): looks it up (LOOK_VARS). FLAGX = 0; a missing simple\nvariable is new (FLAGX bit 1), a missing array report 2.","comment":"The variable"},
        "7202": {"synopsis":"FLAGX = 0 and the found/not-found test: class 4's way in.","comment":"FLAGX = 0"},
        "7206": {"comment":"Found?"},
        "7208": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 1: a new variable"},
        "7212": {"comment":"Not an array: DEST and STRLEN set"},
        "7214": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 1 (report 2, \"Variable not found\"): a missing array."},
        "7216": {"synopsis":"Found: subscripts or slicing (VAR_SUBSCRIPTS); for a string when running, its start and\nlength (STK_FETCH) and FLAGX bit 0 from A.","comment":"Subscripts or slices"},
        "7219": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "7223": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7225": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "7226": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "7229": {"comment":"Running: the string's start and length"},
        "7232": {"comment":"HL = FLAGX"},
        "7235": {"comment":"A's bit 0 added"},
        "7236": {"comment":"FLAGX"},
        "7237": {"comment":"HL = the string's start"},
        "7238": {"synopsis":"STRLEN = BC, DEST = HL: what LET_ASSIGN uses.","comment":"STRLEN = BC"},
        "7242": {"comment":"DEST = HL","synopsis":"DEST = HL only (a number: STRLEN left as it is)."},
        "7246": {"synopsis":"Class 2, the value LET assigns: VAL_FETCH, then STATEMENT_END. Ends the entry.","comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7247": {"comment":"The value"},
        "7250": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7254": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the expression (SCAN_EXPR); it must be the type FLAGS bit 6 had before (the\nvariable's), else report C. When running, LET_ASSIGN stores it.","comment":"A = FLAGS: the variable's type"},
        "7257": {"synopsis":"VAL_FETCH with A already holding the FLAGS value whose bit 6 the result must match.","comment":"Kept"},
        "7258": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "7261": {"comment":"A = the old FLAGS"},
        "7262": {"comment":"D = FLAGS now"},
        "7265": {"comment":"Compared"},
        "7266": {"comment":"Bit 6: types differ?"},
        "7268": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "7270": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7272": {"comment":"Then LET_ASSIGN stores it"},
        "7276": {"synopsis":"Class 4, a FOR or NEXT variable: looked up (LOOK_VARS_A); C bit 5 must be set (a number\nvariable, one letter or a long name), else report C. Then CLASS_4_SAVE keeps DE at $5B8C and\ngoes on as class 1.","comment":"The variable"},
        "7279": {"comment":"Flags kept"},
        "7280": {"comment":"A number variable?"},
        "7282": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7284": {"comment":"The flags back"},
        "7285": {"comment":"DE kept, then as class 1"},
        "7289": {"synopsis":"Past one character, then CLASS_8.","comment":"Past the character"},
        "7290": {"synopsis":"Class 8, two numbers separated by ',' (POKE, BEEP, OUT, PLOT).","comment":"The first number"},
        "7293": {"comment":"','?"},
        "7295": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7297": {"comment":"Past it","synopsis":"Past one character (RST $20), then a number (CLASS_6)."},
        "7298": {"synopsis":"Class 6, a number: the expression (SCAN_EXPR) must be numeric (FLAGS bit 6 set), else report\nC.\nObserved: GO TO \"a\" was refused.","comment":"The expression"},
        "7301": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "7305": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7306": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0B (report C, \"Nonsense in BASIC\")."},
        "7308": {"synopsis":"Class $0A, a string: the expression must be a string (FLAGS bit 6 clear), else report C.","comment":"The expression"},
        "7311": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "7315": {"comment":"No, a string: done"},
        "7316": {"comment":"Else report C"},
        "7318": {"synopsis":"Class 7, the colour commands INK to OVER: the item (COL_TEMP_ITEM, chosen by T_ADDR) is set\nas a temporary colour, then the statement ends, and when running the temporary colours\nbecome the permanent ones (ATTR_P, MASK_P, and P_FLAG's permanent bits from the temporary).\nEnds the entry.","comment":"FLAGS bit 7: running?"},
        "7322": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: the main screen"},
        "7326": {"comment":"Running: COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "7329": {"comment":"The SYNTAX_NEXT return dropped"},
        "7330": {"comment":"A = T_ADDR's low byte"},
        "7333": {"comment":"Less $13: the colour command's code"},
        "7335": {"comment":"The colour item"},
        "7338": {"comment":"The statement must end"},
        "7341": {"comment":"HL = ATTR_T and MASK_T"},
        "7344": {"comment":"ATTR_P and MASK_P = them"},
        "7347": {"comment":"HL = P_FLAG"},
        "7350": {"comment":"A = P_FLAG"},
        "7351": {"comment":"Temporary bits moved onto the permanent ones"},
        "7352": {"comment":"Odd bits from it, even bits kept"},
        "7356": {"comment":"P_FLAG"},
        "7358": {"synopsis":"Class 9, PLOT, DRAW and CIRCLE: when running, the temporary colours with MASK_T's top five\nbits set and P_FLAG bit 6 cleared; then colour items in the statement (COL_ITEMS) and two\nnumbers (CLASS_8).","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7361": {"comment":"Yes: the items only"},
        "7363": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 cleared: the main screen"},
        "7367": {"comment":"The temporary colours"},
        "7370": {"comment":"HL = MASK_T"},
        "7373": {"comment":"A = MASK_T"},
        "7374": {"comment":"Top five bits set"},
        "7376": {"comment":"MASK_T"},
        "7377": {"comment":"P_FLAG bit 6 cleared"},
        "7381": {"comment":"A = the current character"},
        "7382": {"synopsis":"Colour items (COL_ITEMS), then the two numbers.","comment":"The colour items"},
        "7385": {"comment":"Then the two numbers"},
        "7387": {"synopsis":"Class $0B, the last entry of CLASS_TABLE: a JP to itself, so a statement of this class would\nnever end; the 48K's tape commands have no class routine in this ROM.","comment":"Jumps to itself"},
        "7390": {"synopsis":"An optional number: at ENTER or ':' there is none, and running stacks 0 (USE_ZERO);\notherwise CLASS_6.","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "7392": {"comment":"Then no number"},
        "7394": {"comment":"':'?","synopsis":"FETCH_NUM's second test, entered from $08C9 and $0986 with A the character: ':' means no\nnumber (USE_ZERO), anything else is a number (CLASS_6)."},
        "7396": {"comment":"No: a number (CLASS_6)"},
        "7398": {"synopsis":"Running: 0 onto the calculator stack.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "7401": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "7402": {"comment":"Running: 0 stacked"},
        "7406": {"synopsis":"FOR's values (its STEP is read outside this ROM): the value is moved above the limit and the\nstep and assigned (LET_ASSIGN). The variable becomes a FOR variable, unless it is one: a\none-letter name byte gets bit 7 set, a long name's last letter bit 5 cleared, and 13 bytes\nof room are made after its value (FOR_MAKE_ROOM). A variable above STKEND (a local one) gets\nits room from $3AD4 instead, its entry's length word growing by 13 (FOR_ROOM). Then\nFOR_STORE."},
        "7413": {"comment":"The value assigned"},
        "7416": {"comment":"HL = the value, kept"},
        "7417": {"comment":"HL = the name's last byte"},
        "7418": {"comment":"A one-letter name ($60 + letter)?"},
        "7420": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7422": {"comment":"A long name: bit 5 clear?"},
        "7424": {"comment":"Then a FOR variable already"},
        "7426": {"comment":"Cleared: a FOR variable now"},
        "7428": {"comment":"Room for it"},
        "7430": {"synopsis":"A one-letter name: bit 7 of the name byte; already set means a FOR variable already.","comment":"A FOR variable already?"},
        "7432": {"comment":"Then no room needed"},
        "7434": {"comment":"Set: a FOR variable now"},
        "7436": {"synopsis":"13 bytes of room after the value: MAKE_ROOM for a variable below STKEND; above it, $3AD4\nmakes the room and the length word before the entry's name (the variable now 13 bytes lower)\ngrows by 13.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "7437": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7438": {"comment":"HL = past the value"},
        "7442": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7443": {"comment":"BC = STKEND"},
        "7447": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "7448": {"comment":"Below STKEND?"},
        "7450": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7451": {"comment":"13 bytes"},
        "7454": {"comment":"Below: MAKE_ROOM"},
        "7456": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7457": {"comment":"The room made by $3AD4"},
        "7460": {"comment":"BC = 13"},
        "7461": {"comment":"HL = the variable ($5B8C)"},
        "7464": {"comment":"Less 14"},
        "7465": {"comment":"HL at the length word's high byte"},
        "7467": {"comment":"DE = the length word"},
        "7470": {"comment":"Plus 13"},
        "7473": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "7476": {"comment":"HL = the old value address"},
        "7477": {"comment":"Less 13: where it is now"},
        "7479": {"comment":"On"},
        "7481": {"synopsis":"13 bytes of room after the value (MAKE_ROOM).","comment":"The room"},
        "7484": {"synopsis":"HL = the value.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "7485": {"synopsis":"MEM = the value (memory 0 the value, 1 the limit, 2 the step); the limit and the step come\noff the calculator stack and are copied after the value, then the line (PPC) and the\nstatement (SUBPPC). Then NEXT_LOOP: carry when the loop is over before it starts.","comment":"Kept"},
        "7486": {"comment":"MEM = the value"},
        "7493": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "7494": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "7498": {"comment":"DE = it, HL = the limit"},
        "7499": {"comment":"Ten bytes: the limit and the step"},
        "7501": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "7503": {"comment":"HL = PPC"},
        "7506": {"comment":"DE = the line, HL = where it goes"},
        "7507": {"comment":"The line stored"},
        "7510": {"comment":"D = SUBPPC"},
        "7514": {"comment":"The statement stored"},
        "7515": {"comment":"Over at once? (NEXT_LOOP)"},
        "7517": {"synopsis":"The operand $81 (operand table entry $81): with '$' after it, a string through $1063 with DE\n= $1F23 (ESX_CALL_8E). Otherwise the frame count FRAMES as a number: its low word and top\nbyte, the top byte read again when the low word is 0; when running stacked by $3932 (top\nbyte x 65536 + low word). Then a number (SET_NUMERIC).","comment":"The character after it"},
        "7518": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "7520": {"comment":"DE = ESX_CALL_8E"},
        "7523": {"comment":"Yes: a string through $1063"},
        "7526": {"comment":"E = FRAMES' top byte"},
        "7530": {"comment":"HL = its low word"},
        "7533": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "7535": {"comment":"No"},
        "7537": {"comment":"Then the top byte again"},
        "7540": {"comment":"E = it"},
        "7541": {"synopsis":"D = 0; when running the value E x 65536 + HL is stacked ($3932). A number.","comment":"D = 0"},
        "7543": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "7546": {"comment":"Then stacked"},
        "7549": {"comment":"A number"},
        "7558": {"synopsis":"Tests the NEXT variable (CLASS_4, the variable at $5B8C):\n1. Not found (FLAGX bit 1): B = 1, NZ.\n2. B = 0. Not a FOR variable: returns NC (a name byte with bit 7 clear) or NZ (a long name\n   whose last letter, at DEST, has bit 5 set).\n3. MEM = its value; Z when the 3 bytes after its value, limit and step (the FOR's line and\n   statement) are the same as the 3 at DE + 7.\nChanges: AF, BC, DE, HL; MEM.","comment":"Not found?"},
        "7562": {"comment":"B = 1"},
        "7564": {"comment":"Then NZ"},
        "7565": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "7566": {"comment":"HL = the variable"},
        "7569": {"comment":"Its name byte"},
        "7570": {"comment":"Bit 7: a FOR variable or a long name?"},
        "7571": {"comment":"No: NC"},
        "7572": {"comment":"Bit 6 into carry"},
        "7573": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "7576": {"comment":"A one-letter FOR variable"},
        "7578": {"comment":"A long name: bit 5 of its last letter?"},
        "7580": {"comment":"Set: not a FOR variable"},
        "7581": {"synopsis":"A FOR variable: MEM = its value; HL to its line, DE + 7, three bytes compared.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "7582": {"comment":"MEM = it"},
        "7585": {"comment":"HL = the line number"},
        "7589": {"comment":"DE + 7"},
        "7593": {"comment":"Three bytes"},
        "7595": {"synopsis":"One byte of each; a difference returns NZ.","comment":"DE's byte"},
        "7597": {"comment":"The same?"},
        "7599": {"comment":"No: NZ"},
        "7600": {"comment":"All three?"},
        "7603": {"comment":"Z: the same"},
        "7604": {"synopsis":"The loop's value + step into memory 0 (the variable at MEM), then NEXT_LOOP."},
        "7611": {"synopsis":"Carry when the loop is over: the value past the limit, above it for a step of 0 or more,\nbelow it for a negative step. Uses the variable at MEM: memory 0 the value, 1 the limit, 2\nthe step."},
        "7624": {"comment":"No carry: not over"},
        "7626": {"synopsis":"The end-calc ($38) the jump-true at $1DC5 lands on: the calculator ends here and the Z80\ngoes on at NEXT_LOOP_OVER."},
        "7627": {"synopsis":"The loop is over: carry set."},
        "7629": {"synopsis":"Makes the string of a number in the base in memory 1, jumped to with AF on the machine stack\n(A = the digits wanted after the point) and the calculator stack holding the fraction and,\non top, the whole part:\n1. The whole part's digits, lowest first, each its remainder (n-mod-m, DIGIT_CHAR), kept a\n   byte at a time on the machine stack (PUSH AF, INC SP), until IS_ZERO gives carry; then\n   '-' when memory 3 is negative ($5CA2 bit 7). 256 characters is report 6.\n2. They come off the machine stack in order into workspace room (BC_SPACES).\n3. With A > 0, '.' and A digits of the fraction, each the whole part of fraction x base\n   (NBS_FRAC_LOOP). The two values are deleted and the string is the result (STRING_RESULT).","comment":"BC = 0: no characters yet"},
        "7632": {"synopsis":"One digit of the whole part: its remainder by the base.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7638": {"comment":"A = the remainder"},
        "7641": {"comment":"Its character"},
        "7644": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "7645": {"comment":"The character on the machine stack"},
        "7646": {"comment":"One byte only"},
        "7647": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "7648": {"synopsis":"256 characters: report 6.","comment":"256: report 6"},
        "7651": {"comment":"The rest zero?"},
        "7654": {"comment":"No: the next digit"},
        "7656": {"comment":"Memory 3 negative?"},
        "7660": {"comment":"A = '-'"},
        "7662": {"comment":"No: no sign"},
        "7664": {"comment":"The '-' on the machine stack"},
        "7666": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "7667": {"comment":"256: report 6"},
        "7669": {"synopsis":"C characters of room (BC_SPACES; DE = its start); the characters come off the machine stack\ninto it, highest digit first.","comment":"The room"},
        "7670": {"comment":"HL = its start"},
        "7672": {"comment":"B = the count"},
        "7673": {"synopsis":"One character off the machine stack (DEC SP, POP AF) into the room.","comment":"Back one byte"},
        "7674": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "7675": {"comment":"Into the room"},
        "7677": {"comment":"All of them"},
        "7679": {"comment":"A = the digits after the point"},
        "7680": {"comment":"The string's start kept"},
        "7681": {"comment":"None?"},
        "7682": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "7684": {"comment":"BC = the length with them"},
        "7686": {"comment":"And the point"},
        "7687": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "7688": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "7689": {"comment":"A + 1 bytes"},
        "7693": {"comment":"Room for them"},
        "7694": {"comment":"'.'"},
        "7696": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7698": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "7699": {"synopsis":"One digit of the fraction: fraction x base, its whole part the digit; the fraction left is\nthat less the digit.","comment":"The count kept"},
        "7700": {"comment":"The place kept"},
        "7709": {"comment":"Evaluated and assigned"},
        "7712": {"comment":"Its character"},
        "7715": {"comment":"DE = the place"},
        "7716": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7718": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "7719": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "7720": {"comment":"More?"},
        "7722": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7723": {"synopsis":"The two values deleted; DE = the string, BC = its length: STRING_RESULT.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "7728": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "7729": {"comment":"DE = the start"},
        "7730": {"comment":"The string the result"},
        "7737": {"synopsis":"Skips the statement whose keyword is A: back to it (CPDR from HL), then FIND_STATEMENT to\nthe statement after it.","comment":"B = the token"},
        "7738": {"comment":"Back to it"},
        "7740": {"comment":"D = 2: the next statement, E = 0: no token"},
        "7743": {"comment":"Run from there"},
        "7746": {"synopsis":"A = the character of the digit A (0-35): '0'-'9', then 'A' up.\nChanges: AF.","comment":"'0' up"},
        "7748": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "7750": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "7751": {"comment":"'A' up"},
        "7759": {"synopsis":"RANDOMIZE: SEED = n (TAKE_WORD); for 0 or no number, the low word of FRAMES.\nObserved: RANDOMIZE 5 left SEED 5; RANDOMIZE alone SEED = FRAMES' low word at the time.","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "7762": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "7764": {"comment":"No: SEED = it"},
        "7766": {"comment":"BC = FRAMES' low word"},
        "7770": {"synopsis":"SEED = BC.","comment":"SEED = BC"},
        "7775": {"synopsis":"From $3AD0: pushes $5B48, $007B, HL and $007B and jumps to the RAM routine at $5B4D, a call\nof code outside this ROM; $5B48 is the RAM routines' way back.","comment":"The way back: $5B48"},
        "7779": {"comment":"$007B"},
        "7783": {"comment":"HL"},
        "7784": {"comment":"$007B again"},
        "7788": {"comment":"Through the RAM routine at $5B4D"},
        "7791": {"synopsis":"An optional byte parameter (from $39D0 on): D shifted right, its bit 0 to carry. Set: the\nparameter is absent, C = 0, carry. Clear: A = the number on the calculator stack\n(TAKE_BYTE), DE kept.","comment":"D's bit 0 to carry"},
        "7793": {"comment":"C = 0"},
        "7795": {"comment":"Absent: done"},
        "7796": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "7797": {"comment":"A = the parameter"},
        "7802": {"synopsis":"OUT: writes the byte to the port (TWO_PARAM: A the byte, BC the port).","comment":"A = the byte, BC = the port"},
        "7805": {"comment":"Out to the port"},
        "7808": {"synopsis":"POKE: stores the byte at the address (TWO_PARAM: A the byte, BC the address).\nObserved: POKE 30001,-1 stored 255; POKE 30001,300 was report B.","comment":"A = the byte, BC = the address"},
        "7811": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "7813": {"synopsis":"Two numbers off the calculator stack: A = the top one, a byte (FP_TO_A; -255 to 255, a\nnegative one taken as 256 less it; else report B), BC = the one below (TAKE_WORD).","comment":"A = the byte"},
        "7816": {"comment":"Over 255: report B"},
        "7818": {"comment":"Positive?"},
        "7820": {"comment":"Negative: 256 less it"},
        "7822": {"synopsis":"A kept while BC is fetched.","comment":"Kept"},
        "7823": {"comment":"BC = the number below"},
        "7826": {"comment":"A back"},
        "7828": {"synopsis":"A = the number on top of the calculator stack, 0-255 (FP_TO_A); otherwise report B\n(TAKE_INT_TEST).","comment":"A = the number"},
        "7831": {"comment":"Tested"},
        "7833": {"synopsis":"BC = the number on top of the calculator stack, 0-65535 (FP_TO_BC); otherwise report B\n(TAKE_INT_TEST).","comment":"BC = the number"},
        "7836": {"synopsis":"Too big (carry) or negative (NZ): report B.","comment":"Too big: report B"},
        "7838": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "7839": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"Integer out of range\")."},
        "7841": {"synopsis":"An exponent after a number (from READ_NUMBER, $2CEE and $2CFF): E or e, and only in base 10\n(the base at $5CAD); a sign, then digits (BASE_DIGIT; none is report C) read as a byte\n(FP_TO_BYTE; 128 or more is report 6), negated for '-', and the number multiplied by 10 to\nthat power (CALC_E_TO_FP).","comment":"'e'?"},
        "7845": {"comment":"'E'?"},
        "7847": {"comment":"Neither: no exponent"},
        "7848": {"synopsis":"Base 10 only; B = $FF, made 0 by a '-'.","comment":"The number base"},
        "7851": {"comment":"Base 10?"},
        "7853": {"comment":"No: no exponent"},
        "7854": {"comment":"B = $FF: positive"},
        "7856": {"comment":"The character after the E"},
        "7857": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "7861": {"comment":"'-'?"},
        "7865": {"comment":"B = 0: negative"},
        "7866": {"synopsis":"Past the sign."},
        "7867": {"synopsis":"The exponent's digits: a digit must come (report C); read (DIGITS_TO_FP) and taken as a\nbyte.","comment":"The sign kept"},
        "7868": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "7871": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "7874": {"comment":"The digits read"},
        "7877": {"comment":"A = the exponent"},
        "7880": {"comment":"The sign back"},
        "7881": {"comment":"Over 255: report 6"},
        "7884": {"comment":"128 or more?"},
        "7885": {"comment":"Then report 6"},
        "7888": {"comment":"B = 0 (negative)?"},
        "7891": {"comment":"Negated"},
        "7893": {"synopsis":"The number x 10 to the power A (CALC_E_TO_FP)."},
        "7896": {"synopsis":"Is A a digit of the number base at $5CAD (IY + $73)? '0'-'9' are 0-9, letters of either case\n10 up.\nExit: no carry and A = the digit's value when it is one; carry and A unchanged when not.\nChanges: AF, B.","comment":"B = the character"},
        "7897": {"comment":"Less '0'"},
        "7899": {"comment":"Below: not a digit"},
        "7901": {"comment":"0-9?"},
        "7903": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "7905": {"comment":"Upper case"},
        "7907": {"comment":"'A' is 10"},
        "7909": {"comment":"Below: not a digit"},
        "7911": {"comment":"Between '9' and 'A'?"},
        "7913": {"comment":"Then not a digit"},
        "7915": {"synopsis":"Below the base: no carry.","comment":"Below the base?"},
        "7918": {"comment":"Carry when not"},
        "7919": {"comment":"A digit: no carry"},
        "7920": {"synopsis":"Not a digit: A = the character, carry.","comment":"A back"},
        "7922": {"synopsis":"From $39A7 and $39F5: pushes $5B48, $007B, BC and $007B and jumps to the RAM routine at\n$5B3E, a call of code outside this ROM; $5B48 is the RAM routines' way back.","comment":"The way back: $5B48"},
        "7926": {"comment":"$007B"},
        "7930": {"comment":"BC"},
        "7931": {"comment":"$007B again"},
        "7935": {"comment":"Through the RAM routine at $5B3E"},
        "7941": {"synopsis":"Checks that BC more bytes fit: STKEND + BC + $50 must stay below the machine stack. Returns\nwith carry when they do; stops with report 4 otherwise (NO_ROOM).\nChanges: F, DE, HL.","comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "7944": {"comment":"Plus BC"},
        "7945": {"comment":"Over 65535: report 4"},
        "7947": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "7948": {"comment":"HL = $50"},
        "7951": {"comment":"Plus it"},
        "7952": {"comment":"Over 65535: report 4"},
        "7954": {"comment":"Below the machine stack?"},
        "7956": {"comment":"Yes: room"},
        "7957": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 3 (report 4): no room. USR_CALL jumps here too when $332C refuses a\nbank (NZ)."},
        "7962": {"synopsis":"BC = STKEND + $50 - SP (TEST_ROOM with BC = 0): minus the free bytes.","comment":"BC = 0"},
        "7965": {"comment":"HL = STKEND + $50 - SP"},
        "7968": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "7971": {"synopsis":"RST $08 with the byte $8E after it, then, unless it returns with carry, the routines at\n$3747 (with HL) and $373B (with L = the H it returned) outside this ROM, called through\n$32CD and $32C5. $8E is not a 48K report code: RST $08 is taken as a call that returns.\nOP_FRAMES passes this address to $1063.","comment":"RST $08, $8E"},
        "7973": {"comment":"Carry: done"},
        "7974": {"comment":"HL kept"},
        "7975": {"comment":"$3747 called"},
        "7981": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "7982": {"comment":"L = H"},
        "7983": {"comment":"$373B called"},
        "7994": {"synopsis":"PAUSE: waits n interrupts (HALT), or until a key (FLAGS bit 5), which is then taken. PAUSE 0\nwaits for a key only: its count never reaches 0.","comment":"BC = the count"},
        "7997": {"synopsis":"One interrupt; the count one down.","comment":"One interrupt"},
        "7998": {"comment":"One down"},
        "7999": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "8001": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8003": {"comment":"$FFFF (PAUSE 0): back to 0, no end"},
        "8004": {"comment":"$FFFF?"},
        "8006": {"comment":"No"},
        "8008": {"comment":"Yes: back to 0"},
        "8009": {"synopsis":"A key ends the pause.","comment":"FLAGS bit 5: a key?"},
        "8013": {"comment":"No: wait on"},
        "8015": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared: the key is taken.","comment":"FLAGS bit 5 cleared"},
        "8020": {"synopsis":"Tests BREAK: carry unless both SPACE (port $7FFE bit 0) and CAPS SHIFT (port $FEFE bit 0)\nare down. When both are, the routine at $3E75 outside this ROM is called through $32C5: NZ\nfrom it is still no BREAK (carry).\nChanges: AF, BC.","comment":"Port $7FFE: B to SPACE"},
        "8022": {"comment":"The row read"},
        "8024": {"comment":"Bit 0: SPACE into carry"},
        "8025": {"comment":"Not pressed: carry, no BREAK"},
        "8026": {"comment":"Port $FEFE: SHIFT to V"},
        "8028": {"comment":"The row read"},
        "8030": {"comment":"Bit 0: CAPS SHIFT into carry"},
        "8032": {"comment":"Both down: $3E75 asked"},
        "8038": {"comment":"Carry"},
        "8039": {"comment":"NZ: no BREAK"},
        "8040": {"comment":"BREAK: no carry"},
        "8042": {"synopsis":"USR_CALL from $38FB with the alternate AF first.","comment":"The other AF"},
        "8043": {"synopsis":"Calls the machine code at HL (USR_JUMP). D = $FF: in the memory as it is. Otherwise D is a\nbank: the stack switched to the one at $5B6A, the bank asked of $332C outside this ROM\n(through $32CD; NZ is report 4), its two 8K pages (C x 2, + 1) put in MMU 6 and 7 (NextRegs\n$56, $57) and the address moved into $C000-$FFFF. After the code: NextReg $8E = $0B (RAM\nbank 0 at $C000, ROM 3; nextreg.txt) and the stack back. IY = $5C3A at the end.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "8044": {"comment":"$FF?"},
        "8045": {"comment":"Yes: no paging"},
        "8047": {"comment":"DE = the address"},
        "8048": {"comment":"HL = the other stack"},
        "8051": {"comment":"This one kept there"},
        "8055": {"comment":"Switched"},
        "8056": {"comment":"The address kept"},
        "8057": {"comment":"The bank asked of $332C"},
        "8063": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "8064": {"comment":"Not there: report 4"},
        "8067": {"comment":"A = the page pair"},
        "8068": {"comment":"Times 2: the 8K page"},
        "8069": {"comment":"In MMU 6"},
        "8072": {"comment":"The next page"},
        "8073": {"comment":"In MMU 7"},
        "8076": {"comment":"The address into $C000-$FFFF"},
        "8080": {"synopsis":"The code called (USR_JUMP), the flags kept; after a banked call NextReg $8E = $0B and the\nstack switched back.","comment":"Z: no paging"},
        "8081": {"comment":"The code"},
        "8084": {"comment":"Back"},
        "8085": {"comment":"No paging: done"},
        "8087": {"comment":"RAM bank 0, ROM 3"},
        "8091": {"comment":"The stack back"},
        "8099": {"synopsis":"IY = $5C3A."},
        "8104": {"synopsis":"Jumps to HL as a routine (pushed, then RET) with the paging copies at $5B5C ($10) and $5B67\n($04) saying ROM 3 and RAM bank 0; EXX and EX AF,AF' come first, so the code gets the other\nregister set and AF. Its RET comes back after the CALL USR_JUMP.","comment":"The routine's address"},
        "8105": {"comment":"Port $7FFD's copy"},
        "8110": {"comment":"Port $1FFD's copy"},
        "8115": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "8116": {"comment":"The other AF"},
        "8117": {"comment":"Into the routine"},
        "8131": {"synopsis":"Returns to its caller only when running. When checking it drops the return address, so it\nreturns from the caller instead: what follows a CALL RUN_ONLY runs only when running.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "8134": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "8135": {"comment":"Checking: back from the caller"},
        "8136": {"comment":"Running: back to the caller"},
        "8137": {"synopsis":"Operator priorities, read by SCAN_OP_LOOKUP at operation - $3B (AND $3F): 22 bytes. $3B (not\nan operator) 0; $FC 8, $FD (&) 3, $FE (|) 2, $C1 and $C2 12, - 6, * 8, / 8, ^ 10, OR 2, AND\n3, <= >= <> > < = 5, + 6. The bytes for $FF, $40 and the last ($FF) are not reached from\nOPERATOR_CODES."},
        "8159": {"synopsis":"Prints a list of items and separators (PRINT and INPUT's prompt): separators by PRINT_SEP,\nitems by PRINT_ITEM, until the end of the statement or a ')'. A list that does not end with\na separator ends with ENTER (PRINT_NEWLINE).\nObserved: PRINT \"no newline\"; left the position on the same line.","comment":"The current character"},
        "8160": {"comment":"The end already?"},
        "8163": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "8165": {"synopsis":"Separators, as many as there are.","comment":"A separator?"},
        "8168": {"comment":"Yes: more separators"},
        "8170": {"comment":"One item"},
        "8173": {"comment":"A separator after it?"},
        "8176": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "8178": {"synopsis":"The end: at ')' nothing more (INPUT's bracket); otherwise ENTER.","comment":"')'?"},
        "8180": {"comment":"Yes: no ENTER"},
        "8181": {"synopsis":"ENTER through RST $10, when running.","comment":"Only when running"},
        "8184": {"comment":"A = ENTER"},
        "8186": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8188": {"synopsis":"One print item: AT line,column (control code $16, then the two bytes), TAB column ($17 and\nthe column's two bytes), a colour item (PRINT_COLOUR), '#' and a stream (STREAM_ALTER), or\nan expression: a number by PRINT_FP, a string character by character (PRINT_STRING). Each is\nonly checked when checking (RUN_ONLY).","comment":"The current character"},
        "8189": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "8191": {"comment":"No: TAB?"},
        "8193": {"comment":"Past AT, then the two numbers"},
        "8196": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "8199": {"comment":"C = the line, B = the column"},
        "8202": {"comment":"AT's control code"},
        "8204": {"comment":"Printed with its operands"},
        "8206": {"synopsis":"TAB: one number (CLASS_6), TAKE_WORD; A = $17.","comment":"TAB?"},
        "8208": {"comment":"No: a colour item, a stream or an expression"},
        "8210": {"comment":"Past TAB"},
        "8211": {"comment":"The column"},
        "8214": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "8217": {"comment":"BC = the column"},
        "8220": {"comment":"TAB's control code"},
        "8222": {"synopsis":"Prints A, C and B through RST $10: the control code and its two operands.","comment":"The control code"},
        "8223": {"comment":"A = the first operand"},
        "8224": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8225": {"comment":"A = the second operand"},
        "8226": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8228": {"synopsis":"Not AT or TAB: a colour item or a stream change ends the item; otherwise the expression\n(SCAN_EXPR).","comment":"A colour item?"},
        "8231": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8232": {"comment":"A stream ('#')?"},
        "8235": {"comment":"Yes: done"},
        "8236": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "8239": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
        "8242": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6: a number?"},
        "8246": {"comment":"A string: DE = its start, BC = its length"},
        "8249": {"comment":"A number: PRINT_FP"},
        "8252": {"synopsis":"Prints the BC characters at DE.","comment":"Characters left?"},
        "8254": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "8255": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "8256": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "8257": {"comment":"DE on"},
        "8258": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8259": {"comment":"Again"},
        "8261": {"synopsis":"Z at the end of a print list: ')', ENTER or ':'.\nChanges: F.","comment":"')'?"},
        "8263": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "8264": {"synopsis":"Z at ENTER or ':' (PRINT_END_Z without the ')').","comment":"ENTER?"},
        "8266": {"comment":"Yes: Z"},
        "8267": {"comment":"':'? Z when it is"},
        "8270": {"synopsis":"A separator: ';' nothing, ',' the comma control code ($06) when running, \"'\" ENTER when\nrunning. Then past it; Z returned. After a separator at the end of the list, PRINT_LIST is\nleft without its ENTER. NZ when there is no separator.","comment":"The current character"},
        "8271": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "8273": {"comment":"Yes: nothing printed"},
        "8275": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8277": {"comment":"No: maybe \"'\""},
        "8279": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "8282": {"comment":"Then nothing printed"},
        "8284": {"comment":"The comma control code"},
        "8286": {"comment":"Printed"},
        "8287": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8289": {"synopsis":"\"'\": ENTER (PRINT_NEWLINE).","comment":"\"'\"?"},
        "8291": {"comment":"No: NZ, no separator"},
        "8292": {"comment":"ENTER printed (when running)"},
        "8295": {"synopsis":"Past the separator; at the end of the list the caller's return is dropped.","comment":"Past the separator"},
        "8296": {"comment":"The end of the list?"},
        "8299": {"comment":"No: Z returned"},
        "8301": {"comment":"The caller's return dropped"},
        "8302": {"synopsis":"Z: a separator was taken.","comment":"Z: a separator taken"},
        "8304": {"synopsis":"'#' and a number: that stream becomes current (STREAM_SELECT; 16 or more is report O). Carry\nwhen there is no '#'.","comment":"'#'?"},
        "8306": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "8307": {"comment":"No: carry, no stream"},
        "8308": {"comment":"Past '#'"},
        "8309": {"comment":"The stream number"},
        "8312": {"comment":"Carry clear: a stream"},
        "8313": {"comment":"Checking: done"},
