        "8360": {"comment":"Yes: the position kept"},
        "8362": {"comment":"Otherwise the left column"},
        "8364": {"comment":"And the line just above the lower screen"},
        "8365": {"synopsis":"S_POSN = the upper position, moved to the line above the lower screen when DF_SZ reached it.","comment":"S_POSN = BC"},
        "8369": {"comment":"25"},
        "8371": {"comment":"Less the line"},
        "8372": {"comment":"SCR_CT: the lines before the scroll prompt"},
        "8375": {"comment":"TV_FLAG bit 0 clear: the upper screen"},
        "8379": {"comment":"Its print position set"},
        "8382": {"comment":"The lower screen cleared"},
        "8385": {"synopsis":"IN with a bracket (from $0827, after BRACKET_ARG). One argument, IN(port), is CALC_IN, a\nnumber to a number (FN_TAKES_NUM). After a ',', IN(s$, t$ [, n [, c$]]): s$ must be a string\n(report C); t$ is looked for in s$ from character n (default 1), forward, or backward from\n-n for a negative n; c$'s first character (default the byte $7F at $1539) matches any\ncharacter. The result is the position, 0 when t$ is not there (or empty, or n 0 or past the\nend). ')' must end it.","comment":"IX = CALC_IN"},
        "8389": {"comment":"IN(port)"},
        "8392": {"comment":"The first a number?"},
        "8394": {"comment":"Then report C"},
        "8397": {"comment":"t$"},
        "8400": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8402": {"comment":"No: the defaults"},
        "8404": {"comment":"n"},
        "8407": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8409": {"comment":"No: c$'s default"},
        "8411": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8412": {"comment":"c$"},
        "8415": {"comment":"On"},
        "8417": {"synopsis":"No n: 1 stacked when running.","comment":"Running?"},
        "8420": {"comment":"A = 1"},
        "8422": {"comment":"Then stacked"},
        "8425": {"synopsis":"No c$: the one byte at $1539 ($7F) stacked as a string when running.","comment":"Running?"},
        "8428": {"comment":"DE = $1539"},
        "8431": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "8434": {"comment":"Then stacked"},
        "8437": {"comment":"The current character","synopsis":"')' must follow (report C); checking ends with a number result. Running: A = c$'s first\ncharacter (0 for an empty one), BC = n (report B over 65535), its sign kept in the alternate\nF; n = 0 is the result 0."},
        "8438": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "8440": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8443": {"comment":"Past ')'"},
        "8444": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "8447": {"comment":"Then a number"},
