        "8850": {"comment":"MASK_T's bit"},
        "8852": {"synopsis":"BORDER: the colour (0-7, else report K) goes to port $FE, which sets the border and leaves\nMIC and EAR 0; BORDCR becomes that colour as the paper (bits 3-5) with ink 7 on a dark one\n(0-3) or 0 on a light one (4-7), the lower screen's colours.\nObserved: BORDER 2 left BORDCR $17, BORDER 5 $28.","comment":"A = the colour"},
        "8855": {"comment":"8 or more?"},
        "8857": {"comment":"Then report K"},
        "8859": {"comment":"The border colour out"},
        "8861": {"comment":"Moved to the paper bits"},
        "8864": {"comment":"Light (bit 5 of the paper)? Ink 0, else 7"},
        "8866": {"comment":"Light: ink 0"},
        "8868": {"comment":"Dark: ink 7"},
        "8870": {"synopsis":"BORDCR = A.","comment":"BORDCR = A"},
        "8873": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8874": {"synopsis":"The display byte of pixel x = C, y = B (y counting up from the bottom, 0-175; more is report\nB): HL = its address, A = x AND 7, the pixel's place counting from the byte's left (bit 7).\nChanges: AF, B, HL.","comment":"175"},
        "8876": {"comment":"Less y: the line from the top"},
        "8877": {"comment":"Over 175: report B"},
        "8880": {"comment":"B = the line from the top"},
        "8881": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "8882": {"comment":"Line / 2"},
        "8883": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "8884": {"comment":"Bit 7 set: $40 and line / 4"},
        "8885": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "8886": {"comment":"$40 and line / 8"},
        "8887": {"comment":"High bits from A, bits 0-2 from B"},
        "8891": {"comment":"H = the address's high byte"},
        "8892": {"comment":"A = x"},
        "8893": {"comment":"Rotated left 3"},
        "8896": {"comment":"Bits 3-5 from the line, the rest from x"},
        "8900": {"comment":"Rotated left 2"},
        "8902": {"comment":"L = line bits 3-5 and x / 8"},
        "8903": {"comment":"A = x"},
        "8904": {"comment":"The pixel's place in the byte"},
        "8907": {"synopsis":"POINT's value: 1 when the pixel at x, y (TAKE_TWO_BYTES, PIXEL_BYTE) is set, else 0, stacked\n(STACK_A).\nObserved: after PLOT 5,7, POINT (5,7) gave 1 and POINT (6,7) 0.","comment":"C = x, B = y"},
        "8910": {"comment":"HL = the byte, A = the place"},
        "8913": {"comment":"B = the place + 1"},
        "8915": {"comment":"A = the display byte"},
        "8916": {"synopsis":"The pixel's bit rotated round into bit 0.","comment":"Rotated left"},
        "8917": {"comment":"Until the pixel is in bit 0"},
        "8919": {"comment":"Only that bit"},
        "8921": {"comment":"Stacked: 1 or 0"},
        "8924": {"synopsis":"PLOT: the pixel at x, y (TAKE_TWO_BYTES, PLOT_SUB), then the temporary colours back\n(COLOURS_TO_TEMP).\nObserved: PLOT 0,0 lit the bottom left pixel; PLOT 0,176 gave report B.","comment":"C = x, B = y"},
        "8927": {"comment":"The pixel plotted"},
        "8930": {"comment":"The temporary colours back"},
        "8933": {"synopsis":"Plots pixel x = C, y = B: COORDS = them; the pixel set, or with OVER 1 (P_FLAG bit 0)\ntoggled, or with INVERSE 1 (bit 2) cleared, or with both left as it is; then the cell's\nattribute (OUT_ATTR).\nObserved: PLOT 3,0 then PLOT OVER 1;3,0 left it clear; PLOT INVERSE 1;3,0 cleared it.","comment":"COORDS = x, y"},
        "8937": {"comment":"HL = the byte, A = the place"},
        "8940": {"comment":"B = the place + 1"},
        "8942": {"comment":"A mask with bit 0 clear"},
        "8944": {"synopsis":"B = a mask with 0 at the pixel ($FE rotated right x AND 7 + 1 times).","comment":"Rotated right"},
        "8945": {"comment":"Until the 0 is at the pixel"},
        "8947": {"comment":"B = the mask"},
        "8948": {"comment":"A = the display byte"},
        "8949": {"comment":"C = P_FLAG"},
        "8952": {"comment":"OVER 1?"},
        "8954": {"comment":"Yes: the pixel kept"},
        "8956": {"comment":"The pixel cleared"},
        "8957": {"synopsis":"INVERSE 0: the pixel set (XOR, CPL), or toggled after OVER 1.","comment":"INVERSE 1?"},
        "8959": {"comment":"Yes: the byte as it is"},
        "8961": {"comment":"The other bits inverted"},
        "8962": {"comment":"All inverted: the pixel flipped"},
        "8963": {"synopsis":"The byte back; the attribute (OUT_ATTR).","comment":"The byte back"},
        "8964": {"comment":"The cell's attribute"},
        "8967": {"synopsis":"Takes two numbers off the calculator stack (TAKE_BYTE_SIGN each): B = the top one, C = the\none below; D and E their signs (1 or $FF).","comment":"The top number"},
        "8970": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "8971": {"comment":"Kept, its sign in C"},
        "8972": {"comment":"The number below"},
        "8975": {"comment":"E = its sign"},
        "8976": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "8977": {"comment":"D = the top one's sign"},
        "8978": {"comment":"C = the one below"},
        "8979": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8980": {"synopsis":"A = the number on top of the calculator stack (FP_TO_A), C = its sign: 1, or $FF when\nnegative; over 255 is report B.","comment":"A = the number, Z when positive"},
        "8983": {"comment":"Over 255: report B"},
        "8986": {"comment":"C = 1"},
        "8988": {"comment":"Positive: done"},
        "8989": {"comment":"Negative: C = $FF"},
        "8991": {"comment":"Done"},
        "8992": {"synopsis":"CIRCLE x,y,r (the colour items and x, y by CLASS_9): r = |r|. Under 1 it plots x, y only.\nOtherwise the circle is drawn as chords: CHORD_COUNT picks their number from the radius (a\nmultiple of 4, at most 252) and the rotation from one to the next (memories 3 and 4); the\nfirst point is set in COORDS and ARC_LOOP draws them with DRAW_LINE.\nObserved: CIRCLE 128,88,40 lit (168,88), (128,128) and (128,48) and left COORDS 168,83;\nCIRCLE 20,20,0.5 plotted (20,20) only.","comment":"The current character"},
        "8993": {"comment":"','?"},
        "8995": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "8998": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "8999": {"comment":"The radius"},
        "9002": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "9005": {"comment":"The value r made |r|"},
        "9009": {"comment":"r below 1?"},
        "9010": {"comment":"Exponent $81 or more: r 1 or more?"},
        "9012": {"comment":"Yes: the circle"},
        "9014": {"comment":"The value r dropped"},
        "9017": {"comment":"Only x, y plotted (PLOT_CMD)"},
        "9019": {"synopsis":"The angle, memory 5 = 2 x pi (pi/2 with its exponent set to $83); CHORD_COUNT.","comment":"Pi / 2 stacked"},
        "9022": {"comment":"pi/2 x 4: 2 x pi"},
        "9024": {"comment":"Memory 5 = 2 x pi"},
        "9028": {"comment":"The chords' count and the angles"},
        "9031": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "9032": {"comment":"The value r times memory 1"},
        "9037": {"comment":"The product's exponent"},
        "9038": {"comment":"$80 or more: 0.5 or more?"},
        "9040": {"comment":"Yes: the circle drawn"},
        "9042": {"comment":"Two values dropped"},
        "9046": {"comment":"The count dropped"},
        "9047": {"comment":"Only x, y plotted (PLOT_CMD)"},
        "9050": {"synopsis":"The first chord's end and start in the memories, COORDS = the first point (TAKE_BYTE twice),\nthen ARC_LOOP.","comment":"The first chord's values in the memories"},
        "9070": {"comment":"Memory 2 doubled (its exponent + 1)"},
        "9073": {"comment":"A = the top number"},
        "9076": {"comment":"L = it"},
        "9077": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "9078": {"comment":"A = the next number"},
        "9081": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "9082": {"comment":"H = it"},
        "9083": {"comment":"COORDS = the first point"},
        "9086": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "9087": {"comment":"The chords drawn"},
        "9090": {"synopsis":"DRAW x,y[,a] (the colour items and x, y by CLASS_9): without a, a straight line from COORDS\nby x, y (LINE_DRAW). With a, an arc turning through a radians (DRAW_ARC).\nObserved: PLOT 10,10: DRAW 20,5 left COORDS 30,15; DRAW 250,0 from there drew to the right\nedge and gave report B; PLOT 100,50: DRAW 50,0,PI ended at 150,50.","comment":"The current character"},
        "9091": {"comment":"','?"},
        "9093": {"comment":"Yes: an angle follows"},
        "9095": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "9098": {"comment":"A straight line"},
        "9101": {"synopsis":"DRAW's angle a: memory 5 = a; sin(a/2) = 0 (a = 0, a multiple of 2 pi) is a straight line;\notherwise DRAW_ARC_CALC goes on with the arc's size.","comment":"Past the ','"},
        "9102": {"comment":"The angle"},
        "9105": {"comment":"The statement must end here"},
        "9108": {"comment":"Memory 5 = a; sin(a / 2) tested"},
        "9120": {"comment":"Zero: a straight line"},
        "9123": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $239C lands on, so the listing cannot decode them after\nRST $28: st-mem-0, delete, st-mem-1, delete, duplicate, abs, get-mem-1, exchange, get-mem-1,\nabs, addition, get-mem-0, division, abs, get-mem-0, exchange, re-stack, end-calc. The Z80\ngoes on at DRAW_ARC_SIZE."},
        "9141": {"synopsis":"A short arc (the value's exponent below $81): a straight line instead (LINE_DRAW).","comment":"A = the value's exponent"},
        "9142": {"comment":"Below $81: under 1?"},
        "9144": {"comment":"No: an arc"},
        "9146": {"comment":"Two values dropped"},
        "9150": {"comment":"A straight line"},
        "9153": {"synopsis":"The arc's chords: CHORD_COUNT for their number, the first chord and the start point in the\nmemories; then ARC_START with the first.","comment":"The chords' count"},
        "9156": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "9157": {"comment":"The first chord and the start point"},
        "9213": {"comment":"A = the deleted value's exponent"},
        "9214": {"comment":"Below $81: under 1?"},
        "9216": {"comment":"B = the chord count back"},
        "9217": {"comment":"Under 1 (exponent below $81): a straight line"},
        "9224": {"comment":"A = COORDS x"},
        "9227": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9235": {"comment":"A = COORDS y"},
        "9238": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9247": {"comment":"B = the chord count back"},
        "9248": {"synopsis":"The chords one by one: B counts them; the last goes to the exact end (ARC_END).","comment":"One chord fewer"},
        "9249": {"comment":"Only one: ARC_END"},
        "9251": {"comment":"Otherwise the first chord (ARC_START)"},
        "9253": {"synopsis":"The next chord: its (x, y) rotated by the step (memories 3 and 4: cos and sin), into\nmemories 1 and 2."},
        "9273": {"synopsis":"The chord's end in pixels, relative to COORDS, then DRAW_LINE.","comment":"Count kept"},
        "9281": {"comment":"A = COORDS x"},
        "9284": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9296": {"comment":"A = COORDS y"},
        "9299": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9305": {"comment":"The chord drawn (DRAW_LINE)"},
        "9309": {"comment":"The next chord, until the last"},
        "9311": {"synopsis":"The last chord: to the arc's end point exactly, from COORDS."},
        "9316": {"comment":"A = COORDS x"},
        "9319": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9326": {"comment":"A = COORDS y"},
        "9329": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9335": {"synopsis":"A straight line (DRAW_LINE), then the temporary colours back (COLOURS_TO_TEMP).","comment":"The line drawn (DRAW_LINE)"},
        "9338": {"comment":"Then COLOURS_TO_TEMP"},
        "9341": {"synopsis":"The number of chords for an arc or circle: from the size on the calculator stack, rounded\ndown to a multiple of 4 and plus 4, at most $FC (CHORD_COUNT_MAX), stacked; then the angle\n(memory 5) per chord: memory 4 = sin(a/n), memory 3 = cos(a/n), memory 1 = sin(a/2n).\nExit: B = the number."},
        "9354": {"comment":"A = the size (FP_TO_BYTE)"},
        "9357": {"comment":"Over 255: the most"},
        "9359": {"comment":"Down to a multiple of 4"},
        "9361": {"comment":"Plus 4"},
        "9363": {"comment":"Not past 255: kept"},
        "9365": {"synopsis":"At most $FC chords."},
        "9367": {"synopsis":"A = the number, kept and stacked; the memories from it."},
        "9368": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9397": {"comment":"B = the number"},
        "9399": {"synopsis":"Draws a straight line from COORDS by x, y (TAKE_TWO_BYTES: C = |x|, B = |y|, E and D their\nsigns): along the longer of the two a pixel at a time, a step along the shorter one each\ntime the running sum passes the longer, each pixel by PLOT_SUB. A point off the screen is\nreport B.\nObserved: DRAW 250,0 from 10,10 stopped at x 255 with report B.","comment":"C = |x|, B = |y|; E, D their signs"},
        "9402": {"comment":"A = |x|"},
        "9403": {"comment":"Smaller than |y|?"},
        "9404": {"comment":"No: DL_X_LARGER"},
        "9406": {"comment":"L = |x|, the shorter"},
        "9407": {"comment":"Both signs kept, for a diagonal step"},
        "9409": {"comment":"E = 0: no x step on a straight one"},
        "9410": {"comment":"To DL_STEPS"},
        "9412": {"synopsis":"|x| the larger: it counts the steps (nothing at all for 0, 0).","comment":"|x| 0 too?"},
        "9413": {"comment":"Then nothing to draw"},
        "9414": {"comment":"L = |y|, the shorter"},
        "9415": {"comment":"B = |x|, the longer"},
        "9416": {"comment":"Both signs kept, for a diagonal step"},
        "9417": {"comment":"D = 0: no y step on a straight one"},
        "9419": {"synopsis":"H = the steps, B the count; the running sum starts at half of them.","comment":"H = the longer"},
        "9421": {"comment":"Halved: the sum's start"},
        "9422": {"synopsis":"One step: the sum plus the shorter side; past the longer side, a diagonal step.","comment":"Plus the shorter"},
        "9423": {"comment":"Past 255: a diagonal step"},
        "9425": {"comment":"Below the longer?"},
        "9426": {"comment":"Yes: a straight step"},
        "9428": {"synopsis":"A diagonal step: both signs (BC').","comment":"The longer taken off"},
        "9429": {"comment":"C = the sum"},
        "9430": {"comment":"The alternate set"},
        "9431": {"comment":"BC' = both signs"},
        "9432": {"comment":"Kept again"},
        "9435": {"synopsis":"A straight step: the longer axis's sign only.","comment":"C = the sum"},
        "9436": {"comment":"The straight step's signs"},
        "9438": {"comment":"BC' = them"},
        "9439": {"synopsis":"The new point: COORDS + the step; an x off the screen is report B (DL_RANGE), a y off it is\nPIXEL_BYTE's report B.","comment":"HL = COORDS: L = x, H = y"},
        "9442": {"comment":"The y step"},
        "9443": {"comment":"Plus y"},
        "9444": {"comment":"B = the new y"},
        "9445": {"comment":"The x step"},
        "9446": {"comment":"Plus 1, so that x = -1 gives 0"},
        "9447": {"comment":"Plus x"},
        "9448": {"comment":"Carry: x past 254"},
        "9450": {"comment":"Zero: x = -1, report B"},
        "9452": {"synopsis":"Plots it (PLOT_SUB) and on to the next step.","comment":"Back to the new x"},
        "9453": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "9454": {"comment":"PLOT_SUB"},
        "9457": {"comment":"The main set back"},
        "9458": {"comment":"A = the sum"},
        "9459": {"comment":"The next step, until B is 0"},
        "9461": {"comment":"The signs dropped"},
        "9463": {"synopsis":"Report B unless the point is in range.","comment":"Zero: x = 255, in range"},
        "9465": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B, \"Integer out of range\"); TAKE_BYTE_SIGN jumps here for\na number over 255."},
        "9467": {"synopsis":"Evaluates the expression at CH_ADD, by operator priority, checking (FLAGS bit 7 clear) or\nrunning. Leaves FLAGS bit 6 set for a number, clear for a string, and when running the value\non the calculator stack; CH_ADD at the character after it.\n1. An expression that starts with '%' goes to $0605.\n2. A 0 priority goes on the machine stack: the bottom of the pending operations.\n3. SCAN_OPERAND reads an operand through the table of words at $0600, one for each character\n   code, or a prefix (unary minus, NOT, a function) that pushes its operation and reads the\n   next operand.\n4. SCAN_OPERATOR takes the operator after it (OPERATOR_CODES, OP_PRIORITIES); every pending\n   operation of no lower priority runs first, then the new one is pushed and the next\n   operand read. A character that is not an operator has priority 0: everything pending runs\n   and the expression ends.","comment":"A = the first character (GET_CHAR)"},
        "9468": {"comment":"'%'?"},
        "9470": {"comment":"Then $0605"},
        "9473": {"comment":"B = 0: the bottom priority"},
        "9475": {"comment":"Pushed"},
        "9476": {"synopsis":"Reads an operand: jumps to the word at $0600 + 2 x A, A the character at CH_ADD (HL kept in\nDE).","comment":"HL kept in DE"},
        "9477": {"comment":"HL = $0600 + 2 x A"},
        "9482": {"comment":"HL = the word there"},
        "9486": {"comment":"To it"},
        "9487": {"synopsis":"Inside a string: the next character (NEXT_CHAR), BC + 1; ENTER before the closing quote is\nreport C. Returns at the closing quote with Z when another quote follows (a doubled quote\ninside the string).","comment":"The next character (NEXT_CHAR)"},
        "9491": {"comment":"ENTER?"},
        "9493": {"comment":"Then report C: no closing quote"},
        "9496": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "9500": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9503": {"comment":"Another quote?"},
        "9506": {"synopsis":"The \"(x,y)\" of SCREEN$, ATTR and POINT: two numbers (NEXT_2NUM) and ')', else report C; then\nSYNTAX_Z, so NZ when running.","comment":"Past the keyword"},
        "9507": {"comment":"'('?","synopsis":"TWO_COORDS with A already the character after the keyword (from $088E)."},
        "9509": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9511": {"comment":"Two numbers (NEXT_2NUM)"},
        "9514": {"comment":"A = the character after them"},
        "9515": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9517": {"synopsis":"Report C unless Z (the ')'); then SYNTAX_Z."},
        "9520": {"synopsis":"Z when checking syntax (FLAGS bit 7 clear), NZ when running.\nChanges: F.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9525": {"synopsis":"SCREEN$'s value: compares the cell at line C, column B (TAKE_TWO_BYTES) with the 96\ncharacters of the character set, row by row, plain or inverted. A match gives a\none-character string (WORK_ROOM), none an empty one; stacked by STK_STO_STR.\nObserved: \"Q\" printed at 0,0 gave SCREEN$ (0,0) = \"Q\".","comment":"C = the line, B = the column"},
        "9528": {"comment":"HL = CHARS"},
        "9531": {"comment":"HL = CHARS + 256: the space's pattern"},
        "9539": {"comment":"Its low 3 bits, times 32"},
        "9541": {"comment":"Plus the column"},
        "9542": {"comment":"E = the cell's low byte"},
        "9544": {"comment":"Its third of the screen"},
        "9546": {"comment":"In the screen, $4000 up"},
        "9548": {"comment":"D = the high byte"},
        "9549": {"comment":"96 characters to try"},
        "9551": {"synopsis":"One character: its 8 rows against the cell's."},
        "9554": {"comment":"The cell's top row"},
        "9555": {"comment":"Against the pattern's"},
        "9556": {"comment":"Same: a plain match so far"},
        "9558": {"comment":"Every bit different ($FF)?"},
        "9559": {"comment":"No: not this character"},
        "9561": {"comment":"A = $FF: an inverted match"},
        "9562": {"synopsis":"The first row matched (C = 0) or matched inverted (C = $FF): the other 7 must match the same\nway.","comment":"C = 0 or $FF"},
        "9563": {"comment":"7 more rows"},
        "9565": {"synopsis":"The next row: the screen's 256 bytes on, the pattern's 1.","comment":"The screen's next row"},
        "9566": {"comment":"The pattern's next row"},
        "9567": {"comment":"A = the screen's row"},
        "9568": {"comment":"Against the pattern's"},
        "9569": {"comment":"Inverted as the first?"},
        "9570": {"comment":"Differs: not this character"},
        "9572": {"comment":"All 7 rows"},
        "9576": {"comment":"B = the count left"},
        "9577": {"comment":"A = $80"},
        "9579": {"comment":"Less the count: the character's code"},
        "9580": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9583": {"comment":"Room for it (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9584": {"comment":"The character in it"},
        "9586": {"synopsis":"No match: the next character, 8 bytes on."},
        "9587": {"comment":"The next character's 8 bytes"},
        "9593": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "9595": {"comment":"BC = 0: an empty string"},
        "9600": {"synopsis":"ATTR's value: the attribute byte of line C, column B (TAKE_TWO_BYTES), stacked (STACK_A).\nObserved: ATTR (0,0) gave 56.","comment":"C = the line, B = the column"},
        "9604": {"comment":"Rotated right 3 times"},
        "9607": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "9608": {"comment":"Its low 3 bits, times 32"},
        "9610": {"comment":"Plus the column"},
        "9611": {"comment":"L = the address's low byte"},
        "9613": {"comment":"Its bits 3-4: the third"},
        "9615": {"comment":"In the attributes, $5800 up"},
        "9617": {"comment":"H = the high byte"},
        "9618": {"comment":"A = the attribute"},
        "9619": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "9622": {"synopsis":"Pushes DE and BC and reads an operand (SCAN_OPERAND with A the character at CH_ADD). Nothing\nin this ROM jumps here.","comment":"DE pushed"},
        "9623": {"comment":"BC pushed"},
        "9624": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "9625": {"comment":"The operand"},
        "9637": {"synopsis":"'|' as an operand (operand table entry $7C): only straight after '^', whose pending\noperation ($C6) becomes $FF, the priority kept; anything else is report C. Then past it, the\nnext operand.","comment":"The pending operation"},
        "9638": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "9639": {"comment":"'^'?"},
        "9641": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9644": {"comment":"Operation $FF"},
        "9646": {"comment":"Pushed back"},
        "9647": {"synopsis":"A unary plus: skipped.","comment":"Past the '+'"},
        "9648": {"comment":"The operand after it (SCAN_OPERAND)"},
        "9651": {"synopsis":"A string in quotes: its length counted to the closing quote (QUOTE_NEXT), a doubled quote\nstanding for one quote. When running it is copied into the workspace (WORK_ROOM), the\ndoubled quotes made single, and stacked (STRING_RESULT).\nObserved: \"say \"\"hi\"\"\" printed say \"hi\".","comment":"HL = CH_ADD, the opening quote"},
        "9652": {"comment":"HL = the string's first character"},
        "9654": {"comment":"BC counts the characters"},
        "9657": {"comment":"To the closing quote (QUOTE_NEXT)"},
        "9660": {"comment":"Not doubled: the string's end"},
        "9662": {"synopsis":"Past a doubled quote: on to the next.","comment":"To the next closing quote"},
        "9665": {"comment":"Doubled again?"},
        "9667": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9670": {"comment":"Then no copy"},
        "9672": {"comment":"BC bytes of room (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9673": {"comment":"HL = the first character"},
        "9674": {"comment":"The room's start kept"},
        "9675": {"synopsis":"Copies the string's characters; a doubled quote is copied once."},
        "9679": {"comment":"A quote?"},
        "9683": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "9685": {"comment":"Another quote (doubled)?"},
        "9687": {"comment":"Yes: copied once, on"},
        "9689": {"synopsis":"BC - 1: the closing quote not counted."},
        "9690": {"comment":"DE = the start (the room's when running)"},
        "9691": {"synopsis":"A string result: FLAGS bit 6 cleared; when running STK_STO_STR stacks DE, BC. Then\nSCAN_OPERATOR.","comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9694": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "9696": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9698": {"comment":"Then stacked (STK_STO_STR)"},
        "9701": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "9704": {"synopsis":"A bracket: the expression inside (SCAN_EXPR) and ')', else report C.","comment":"Past the '('"},
        "9705": {"comment":"The expression inside (SCAN_EXPR)"},
        "9708": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9710": {"comment":"No: report C","synopsis":"Report C unless Z (the ')')."},
        "9714": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "9717": {"synopsis":"FN: jumps to $0898."},
        "9720": {"synopsis":"RND (operand table entry $A5). RND(n): n (TAKE_WORD) is given in DE to $2A2C in the DivMMC\nmemory (DIVMMC_CALL), and the BC it returns is the value (STACK_BC at $2D2F); ')' must\nfollow (report C). RND alone: RND_PLAIN.","comment":"Past RND"},
        "9721": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "9723": {"comment":"No: RND alone"},
        "9725": {"comment":"n"},
        "9728": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "9730": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "9732": {"comment":"Checking?"},
        "9735": {"comment":"Then past ')', a number"},
        "9737": {"comment":"BC = n"},
        "9740": {"comment":"DE = n"},
        "9742": {"comment":"$2A2C in the DivMMC memory"},
        "9747": {"comment":"BC = its result"},
        "9749": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "9752": {"comment":"Past ')', a number"},
        "9754": {"synopsis":"RND alone, when running: $2A36 in the DivMMC memory with DE = $FFFF; DE and SEED then make a\n32-bit fraction (DE the high word), shifted left until its top bit is set, the exponent\ncounting down from $80; stacked (STK_STORE) with its top bit cleared (positive). A number.","comment":"Checking?"},
        "9757": {"comment":"Then a number"},
        "9759": {"comment":"DE = $FFFF"},
        "9762": {"comment":"$2A36 in the DivMMC memory"},
        "9767": {"comment":"HL = SEED"},
        "9770": {"comment":"A = $80: the exponent"},
        "9772": {"synopsis":"DE:HL shifted left until DE bit 15 is set, A one lower each time.","comment":"Top bit set?"},
        "9774": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "9776": {"comment":"HL x 2"},
        "9777": {"comment":"Its carry into DE"},
        "9781": {"comment":"Exponent - 1"},
        "9782": {"comment":"Again"},
        "9784": {"synopsis":"The top bit cleared (a positive number); the four bytes into E, D, C, B (DE's high byte\nfirst) and stacked with exponent A.","comment":"Positive"},
        "9786": {"comment":"E = DE's high byte"},
        "9787": {"comment":"D = its low byte"},
        "9789": {"comment":"C = HL's high byte"},
        "9790": {"comment":"B = its low byte"},
        "9791": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "9794": {"synopsis":"A number: SET_NUMERIC."},
        "9796": {"synopsis":"PI, when running: pi/2 from the calculator's constants, its exponent + 1.\nObserved: PRINT PI gave 3.1415927.","comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "9799": {"comment":"Then only past PI"},
        "9804": {"comment":"Exponent + 1: times 2"},
        "9805": {"synopsis":"Past the keyword; a number (SET_NUMERIC)."},
        "9809": {"synopsis":"INKEY$: with '#' a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX, operation $1A). Otherwise, when\nrunning, the key held now (READ_KEYS, KEY_MAIN_CODE, KEY_DECODE in L mode, MODE 0, so a\nletter gives a letter, never a keyword) as a one-character string, or an empty one.\nObserved: with no key, PRINT \"[\";INKEY$;\"]\" printed [].","comment":"Priority 16, operation $5A"},
        "9812": {"comment":"Past INKEY$"},
        "9813": {"comment":"'#'?"},
        "9815": {"comment":"Then a function of the stream (PUSH_PREFIX)"},
        "9818": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "9821": {"comment":"Bit 6 clear: a string"},
        "9823": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "9825": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9827": {"comment":"The keys held (READ_KEYS)"},
        "9830": {"comment":"C = 0: an empty string so far"},
        "9832": {"comment":"Too many keys: empty"},
        "9834": {"comment":"Its main code (KEY_MAIN_CODE)"},
        "9837": {"comment":"No key: empty"},
        "9839": {"comment":"D = $FF: bit 3 set, L mode"},
        "9840": {"comment":"E = the main code"},
        "9841": {"comment":"The key's code (KEY_DECODE, MODE 0)"},
        "9845": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "9848": {"comment":"Room for it (WORK_ROOM)"},
        "9850": {"comment":"Into the room"},
        "9851": {"comment":"C = 1: one character"},
        "9853": {"synopsis":"Stacks the string (STK_STO_STR): C = its length."},
        "9855": {"comment":"Stacked (STK_STO_STR)"},
        "9858": {"synopsis":"To SCAN_OPERATOR."},
        "9869": {"synopsis":"A number in the line (digits, '.', or BIN). Checking: read (READ_NUMBER) and put after the\ndigits in its hidden form, the marker $0E and its 5 bytes, taken off the calculator stack.\nRunning: NUMBER_RUN.\nObserved: 10 PRINT 2.5 was stored with 0E 82 20 00 00 00 after the digits.","comment":"Running?"},
        "9872": {"comment":"Then NUMBER_RUN"},
        "9874": {"comment":"Read onto the calculator stack (READ_NUMBER)"},
        "9877": {"comment":"HL = CH_ADD, the character after it"},
        "9878": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "9881": {"comment":"Room before it (MAKE_ROOM)"},
        "9884": {"comment":"HL = the room's first byte"},
        "9885": {"comment":"The hidden number's marker"},
        "9887": {"comment":"HL = where the 5 bytes go"},
        "9889": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "9892": {"comment":"BC = 5"},
        "9895": {"comment":"HL = the number's start"},
        "9897": {"comment":"STKEND = it: the number taken off"},
        "9900": {"comment":"The 5 bytes after the marker"},
        "9903": {"comment":"HL = the last of them"},
        "9904": {"comment":"CH_ADD = past it (CH_ADD_PLUS1)"},
        "9907": {"comment":"A number (SET_NUMERIC)"},
        "9909": {"synopsis":"Running: past the digits to the $0E marker, and the hidden 5 bytes copied onto the\ncalculator stack (PUSH_NUMBER).","comment":"HL = CH_ADD"},
        "9910": {"synopsis":"The next byte, up to the marker.","comment":"The next byte"},
        "9912": {"comment":"The marker?"},
        "9916": {"comment":"HL = the 5 bytes"},
        "9917": {"comment":"Stacked (PUSH_NUMBER)"},
        "9920": {"comment":"CH_ADD = past them"},
        "9923": {"synopsis":"FLAGS bit 6 set: the operand is a number."},
        "9927": {"comment":"To SCAN_OPERATOR"},
        "9929": {"synopsis":"A letter (operand table entries for the letters): HL back from DE (SCAN_OPERAND swapped\nthem), then OP_VARIABLE.","comment":"HL back"},
        "9930": {"synopsis":"A variable: LOOK_VARS, report 2 when it is not there; subscripts or slicing\n(VAR_SUBSCRIPTS); a number's 5 bytes are stacked (PUSH_NUMBER) when running.\nObserved: PRINT zz with no zz gave \"2 Variable not found\".","comment":"Found (LOOK_VARS)?"},
        "9933": {"comment":"No: report 2"},
        "9936": {"comment":"A string or an array: VAR_SUBSCRIPTS"},
        "9939": {"comment":"A = FLAGS"},
        "9942": {"comment":"Running, and a number (bits 7, 6)?"},
        "9944": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "9946": {"comment":"HL = the value's 5 bytes"},
        "9947": {"comment":"Stacked (PUSH_NUMBER)"},
        "9950": {"synopsis":"To SCAN_OPERATOR."},
        "9954": {"synopsis":"DIVMMC_CALL with A = the value for port $E3: BC kept at $5B54; the routine's address is the\nword after the CALL, which the return skips. Pushes $26F3 (the way back, an address in the\nDivMMC RAM paged in at $2000-$3FFF), the address and A; A = the caller's A from $5B56; then\nDIVMMC_OUT.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "9958": {"comment":"HL = the return address"},
        "9959": {"comment":"BC = the word there"},
        "9962": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "9963": {"comment":"The return past it"},
        "9964": {"synopsis":"BC = the routine's address, A = the value for port $E3 (from $060A, $0612 and $2879): pushes\n$26F3 (the way back), BC and AF; A = $5B56.","comment":"The way back: $26F3"},
        "9968": {"comment":"The address"},
        "9969": {"comment":"The port value"},
        "9970": {"comment":"A = the caller's A"},
        "9973": {"comment":"On"},
        "9975": {"synopsis":"DIVMMC_OUT with BC kept at $5B54 first. Nothing in this ROM jumps here.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "9979": {"synopsis":"Port $E3 (DivMMC control) = B of the word on the stack; BC back from $5B54, and RET into the\naddress under it. $87 sets CONMEM with RAM bank 7: DivMMC ROM at $0000-$1FFF and its RAM\nbank 7 at $2000-$3FFF (divmmc.vhd).","comment":"B = the port value"},
        "9980": {"comment":"Port $E3"},
        "9982": {"comment":"DivMMC paged"},
        "9984": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "9988": {"comment":"Into the routine"},
        "9989": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine whose address is the word after the CALL (DIVMMC_CALL_A with A = $87) with\nthe DivMMC memory paged in: CONMEM, RAM bank 7 (port $E3). A goes to the routine through\n$5B56; the routine returns to $26F3 in that memory.","comment":"A kept"},
        "9992": {"comment":"CONMEM, bank 7"},
        "9994": {"comment":"On"},
        "10002": {"synopsis":"The character after an operand: '(' slices a string (STR_SLICE) and is looked at again;\notherwise an operator: its operation from OPERATOR_CODES and its priority from OP_PRIORITIES\n(SCAN_OP_LOOKUP); not an operator: priority 0.","comment":"A = the character (GET_CHAR)"},
        "10003": {"synopsis":"A '(' after a string: slicing; after a number it ends the operand.","comment":"'('?"},
        "10005": {"comment":"No: an operator?"},
        "10007": {"comment":"After a number?"},
        "10011": {"comment":"Then the operand has ended"},
        "10013": {"comment":"Sliced (STR_SLICE)"},
        "10017": {"comment":"Looked at again"},
        "10019": {"synopsis":"The character's operation from OPERATOR_CODES (C) and its priority from OP_PRIORITIES at\noperation - $3B, AND $3F (B); $3B, not an operator, has priority 0. Operations $00 and $01\n('?' and '[') go to $11B7.","comment":"HL = OPERATOR_CODES"},
        "10022": {"comment":"Plus the character"},
        "10024": {"comment":"C = the operation"},
        "10025": {"comment":"HL = OPERATORS"},
        "10028": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "10029": {"comment":"Less $3B"},
        "10031": {"comment":"$00 or $01: $11B7"},
        "10034": {"comment":"The table's index"},
        "10036": {"comment":"Plus it"},
        "10038": {"comment":"B = its priority"},
        "10039": {"synopsis":"The pending operation on the machine stack (D = its priority, E = its operation) against the\nnew one (B, C): a lower priority waits (SCAN_OP_PUSH). Otherwise it runs now\n(SCAN_OP_APPLY); when it is the bottom 0, the expression is over (GET_CHAR).","comment":"D, E = the pending one"},
        "10041": {"comment":"Lower than the new one?"},
        "10042": {"comment":"Then it waits (SCAN_OP_PUSH)"},
        "10044": {"comment":"The bottom 0?"},
        "10045": {"comment":"Then done: A = the character (GET_CHAR)"},
        "10048": {"synopsis":"Runs the pending operation E (SCAN_OP_APPLY), the new one (BC) kept; OP_APPLY_NOW enters\nhere.","comment":"The new one kept"},
        "10049": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "10052": {"comment":"A = the pending operation"},
        "10053": {"comment":"USR ($ED)?"},
        "10055": {"comment":"No: as it is"},
        "10057": {"comment":"On a number?"},
        "10059": {"comment":"Yes: as it is"},
        "10061": {"comment":"USR of a string: $99"},
        "10063": {"synopsis":"Runs the pending operation E: checking, SCAN_OP_CHECK; running, the calculator's operation E\nAND $3F straight from its table (CALC_OP_DIRECT), STKEND = DE after it; operation 0 goes to\n$3886. USR of a string becomes operation $99 ($19)."},
        "10064": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "10066": {"comment":"No: SCAN_OP_CHECK"},
        "10068": {"comment":"A = the operation"},
        "10069": {"comment":"The calculator's code"},
        "10071": {"comment":"0: $3886"},
        "10074": {"comment":"The operation run"},
        "10077": {"comment":"STKEND = DE"},
        "10081": {"synopsis":"The result's type: FLAGS bit 6 = E bit 7 (set: a number). Then the next pending one."},
        "10082": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "10085": {"comment":"A number for now"},
        "10087": {"comment":"Bit 7: a number result?"},
        "10089": {"comment":"Yes: left set"},
        "10091": {"comment":"No: a string"},
        "10093": {"synopsis":"BC back, and the next pending operation (SCAN_OP_LOOP)."},
        "10094": {"comment":"The next pending one"},
        "10099": {"synopsis":"Pushes the new operation and reads the next operand. With a string on its left it becomes\nthe string form (code + 8): + joins strings, AND gives the string or an empty one (its right\noperand a number), the comparisons compare strings, giving a number, and * becomes operation\n$7B (STR_OP_MULT); any other operator is report C.","comment":"The pending one put back"},
        "10100": {"comment":"A = the new operation"},
        "10101": {"comment":"A number on the left?"},
        "10105": {"comment":"Then as it is"},
        "10107": {"comment":"Its calculator code"},
        "10109": {"comment":"The string form: + 8"},
        "10112": {"comment":"AND ($10)?"},
        "10114": {"comment":"No: the others"},
        "10116": {"comment":"Its right operand a number (bit 6)"},
        "10118": {"comment":"Pushed"},
        "10120": {"synopsis":"Below $10 on a string: STR_OP_MULT ('*', $0C, is allowed, the others report C). $17 (+,\njoining strings) keeps a string result; the comparisons set bit 7 (a number).","comment":"Below $10: STR_OP_MULT"},
        "10122": {"comment":"+ ($17)?"},
        "10124": {"comment":"Then a string result"},
        "10126": {"comment":"A comparison: a number result"},
        "10128": {"synopsis":"Pushes BC and reads the next operand (SCAN_OPERAND).","comment":"Pushed"},
        "10129": {"comment":"Past the operator"},
        "10130": {"comment":"The next operand (SCAN_OPERAND)"},
        "10133": {"synopsis":"A string with '*' ($0C, the string form of multiply): operation $7B, pushed (SCAN_OP_SAVE);\nany other operation below $10 is report C.","comment":"'*'?"},
        "10135": {"comment":"C = $7B"},
        "10137": {"comment":"Yes: pushed"},
        "10139": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "10141": {"synopsis":"Runs calculator operation A from SCAN_OP_APPLY: its address from the word table at $32D7 (2\nx A on; its entries from code 3 are the 48K's, and the calculator itself uses $3B02) is\npushed for the RET. B = A; DE = STKEND and HL = the last value for operations $18-$3A (one\noperand), else DE = the last value and HL = the one before it.","comment":"HL = the table at $32D7"},
        "10144": {"comment":"Plus 2 x A"},
        "10148": {"comment":"BC = the routine"},
        "10151": {"comment":"Pushed"},
        "10152": {"comment":"B = the operation"},
        "10153": {"comment":"DE = -5"},
        "10156": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "10159": {"comment":"$18-$3A?"},
        "10163": {"comment":"Yes: one operand"},
        "10165": {"comment":"Two: HL back 5"},
        "10166": {"synopsis":"DE = HL, HL = DE - 5; RET into the routine.","comment":"DE = HL"},
        "10167": {"comment":"HL = DE - 5"},
        "10168": {"comment":"Into the routine"},
        "10169": {"synopsis":"Checking: operation 0 drops the word under it; then E bit 6 and FLAGS bit 6 must agree (a\nnumber or a string operand), else report C (OP_REPORT_C).","comment":"BC = the pending operation"},
        "10170": {"comment":"A = it"},
        "10171": {"comment":"Operation 0?"},
        "10173": {"comment":"No"},
        "10175": {"comment":"Yes: the word under it"},
        "10176": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "10177": {"comment":"The return address back"},
        "10178": {"synopsis":"E bit 6 against FLAGS bit 6: the same, SCAN_OP_TYPE.","comment":"BC kept"},
        "10179": {"comment":"A = the operation"},
        "10180": {"comment":"Against FLAGS"},
        "10183": {"comment":"Bit 6 the same?"},
        "10185": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10187": {"synopsis":"Report C: an operand of the wrong type, or another syntax error of an expression."},
        "10190": {"synopsis":"B = 0 with C, pushed, and the pending operation under it run (SCAN_OP_DO). Nothing in this\nROM jumps here.","comment":"Priority 0"},
        "10192": {"comment":"Pushed"},
        "10193": {"comment":"Run"},
        "10196": {"synopsis":"Is a bracket after the keyword at CH_ADD? Then the expression in it (SCAN_EXPR), which must\nend with ')' or ','; past that character, carry set, Z for ')', NZ for ','; A = the next\ncharacter, HL = FLAGS. With no bracket CH_ADD stays at the keyword and A is the keyword, no\ncarry.","comment":"HL = the keyword"},
        "10197": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10198": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "10199": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "10201": {"comment":"No"},
        "10203": {"comment":"Dropped"},
        "10204": {"comment":"Past '('"},
        "10205": {"comment":"The expression"},
        "10208": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "10210": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10212": {"comment":"','?"},
        "10214": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "10217": {"comment":"NZ for ','"},
        "10218": {"synopsis":"Past the ')' or ','; A = the character after it, HL = FLAGS, carry set.","comment":"The flags kept"},
        "10219": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10220": {"comment":"Z for ')'"},
        "10221": {"comment":"A = the next character"},
        "10222": {"comment":"HL = FLAGS"},
        "10225": {"comment":"Carry: a bracket"},
        "10227": {"synopsis":"No bracket: CH_ADD back at the keyword ($155F).","comment":"HL = the keyword"},
        "10228": {"comment":"CH_ADD = it"},
        "10231": {"synopsis":"n MOD m: n-mod-m on the calculator stack and the quotient deleted. Nothing in this ROM calls\nit."},
        "10236": {"synopsis":"LET of a whole string to a variable above STKEND (from LET_WHOLE_STR): an entry of the list\nat $5C0B, a length word before its name. When the entry has too little room for the new\nstring, $3AD4 makes the difference and the entry's length word grows by it (the new string's\naddress moved too when it lies between the variable and STKEND). Then the new length, and\nunless IXh bit 7 is set the characters (LSL_STORE).","comment":"DEST kept"},
        "10237": {"comment":"DE = the new string, BC = its length"},
        "10240": {"comment":"DEST back"},
        "10241": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "10242": {"comment":"The string kept"},
        "10243": {"comment":"HL = the length word"},
        "10245": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10246": {"comment":"A counts the name's bytes"},
        "10247": {"comment":"One byte before it","synopsis":"Back over the name's letters (bit 5 set), A counting them down."},
        "10248": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "10249": {"comment":"A letter (bit 5)?"},
        "10251": {"comment":"Yes: on back"},
        "10253": {"comment":"One byte only?"},
        "10255": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10257": {"comment":"Past the $7F too"},
        "10258": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "10259": {"synopsis":"DE = the entry's length word (its address into the alternate HL); the room for characters\n(that less 2 and the name) against the new length: enough, LSL_STORE.","comment":"The word before the entry"},
        "10260": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "10263": {"comment":"Its address"},
        "10264": {"comment":"Into the other HL"},
        "10267": {"comment":"Less 2"},
        "10269": {"comment":"HL = it"},
        "10270": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "10271": {"comment":"BC = -(the name's bytes)"},
        "10274": {"comment":"Less them"},
        "10275": {"comment":"BC = the new length"},
        "10277": {"comment":"Room enough?"},
        "10279": {"comment":"Yes: LSL_STORE"},
        "10281": {"comment":"BC = the bytes short"},
        "10288": {"comment":"HL = the length word"},
        "10289": {"comment":"DE = the new string"},
        "10290": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "10292": {"comment":"The string below the variable?"},
        "10294": {"comment":"Yes: it does not move"},
        "10296": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "10300": {"comment":"Above STKEND?"},
        "10302": {"comment":"Yes: it does not move"},
        "10305": {"comment":"It moves down by BC"},
        "10309": {"synopsis":"$3AD4 makes the BC bytes; the entry's length word, BC lower now, grows by BC.","comment":"HL = the length word"},
        "10310": {"comment":"The string kept"},
        "10311": {"comment":"BC kept"},
        "10312": {"comment":"The room made"},
        "10315": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "10316": {"comment":"BC back"},
        "10317": {"comment":"The word BC lower"},
        "10319": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "10322": {"comment":"Plus BC"},
        "10325": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "10328": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "10329": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "10330": {"synopsis":"The new length into the length word; unless IXh bit 7 is set, the characters after it\n(LDIR).","comment":"HL = the length word"},
        "10331": {"comment":"DE = the new string"},
        "10332": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "10333": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "10336": {"comment":"IXh bit 7?"},
        "10339": {"comment":"Set: no characters"},
        "10340": {"comment":"HL = where they go"},
        "10341": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "10342": {"comment":"None?"},
        "10345": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "10348": {"synopsis":"A '%' variable (LOOK_VARS): FLAGS2 bit 2 set (LET_ASSIGN tests it), a number; the variable\nis looked up by $27BD in the DivMMC memory (DIVMMC_GO, port value $87). C = $60 when it\nreturned H = $32, else 0.\nExit: NZ and no carry: found.","comment":"FLAGS2 bit 2: a '%' variable"},
        "10352": {"comment":"A number"},
        "10356": {"comment":"BC = $27BD"},
        "10359": {"comment":"CONMEM, bank 7"},
        "10361": {"comment":"In the DivMMC memory"},
        "10364": {"comment":"C = $60"},
        "10366": {"comment":"H = $32?"},
        "10369": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10371": {"comment":"No: C = 0"},
        "10373": {"synopsis":"NZ, no carry: found.","comment":"A = 1: NZ, no carry"},
        "10376": {"synopsis":"An entry of the list at $5C0B with the same name byte: a long number name is compared in\nfull (LV_LOC_LONG); a one-letter one needs the line's name to end there (NAME_ENDS). Type 0\n(B = 0) is found (LV_LOC_DONE); type 1 is LV_LOC_ALIAS.","comment":"The name's form"},
        "10378": {"comment":"A long number name?"},
        "10380": {"comment":"Yes: compared in full"},
        "10383": {"comment":"The line's name ends?"},
        "10386": {"comment":"No: the next entry"},
        "10389": {"comment":"Type 0: found"},
        "10391": {"comment":"The entry kept"},
        "10392": {"synopsis":"A type 1 entry: the byte after its name. Not 0: that is the name to look for now (C), B =\n$80 so that the entries up to the list's next separator are skipped (LV_LOC_NEXT). 0: C\nback, HL 4 on from the name's last byte, FLAGS bit 0 set, and found (LV_FOUND).","comment":"A = C"},
        "10393": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "10394": {"comment":"HL = the name's last byte"},
        "10395": {"comment":"C kept in A'"},
        "10396": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10397": {"comment":"The byte after it"},
        "10398": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "10399": {"comment":"Zero?"},
        "10400": {"comment":"The main set"},
        "10401": {"comment":"B bit 7: skip on"},
        "10403": {"comment":"C = the other name"},
        "10404": {"comment":"Not 0: look for it"},
        "10406": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "10407": {"comment":"A = C"},
        "10408": {"comment":"C back"},
        "10409": {"comment":"Two more on"},
        "10411": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 0 set"},
        "10415": {"synopsis":"Found (LV_FOUND)."},
        "10418": {"synopsis":"Looks up the variable named at CH_ADD: a letter, then letters and digits (a long name,\nspaces and case ignored), '$' (a string) or '(' (an array); '%' is an integer variable\n(INT_VAR_LOOK). C = the name's form ($40 + letter a string, $60 + letter a one-letter\nnumber, $20 + letter a long number, the letter alone an array). Checking: no search\n(LV_CHECK_ONLY). Running: the list at $5C0B first (LV_RUN_TEST), then VARS (LV_RUN). Exit\n(LV_EXIT): carry when not found; DE = the variable, A = B = its first byte, HL = it or its\nname's last byte; CH_ADD past the name.","comment":"A = the character at CH_ADD"},
        "10419": {"synopsis":"LOOK_VARS with A already the character at CH_ADD.","comment":"'%'?"},
        "10421": {"comment":"Yes: an integer variable"},
        "10424": {"synopsis":"FLAGS2 bit 2 cleared; a letter must start the name (report C). Also from $2C02.","comment":"Not a '%' variable"},
        "10428": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "10431": {"comment":"No: report C"},
        "10434": {"synopsis":"A number for now; the name's start into the alternate HL; C = the letter's code (bits 0-4),\nB counts the letters and digits after it (LV_NAME_LOOP).","comment":"A number for now"},
        "10438": {"comment":"The name's start"},
        "10439": {"comment":"Into the other HL"},
        "10441": {"comment":"The letter's bits"},
        "10443": {"comment":"C = them"},
        "10444": {"comment":"B = 0"},
        "10446": {"synopsis":"Past the name's letters and digits, B counting.","comment":"The next character"},
        "10447": {"comment":"A letter or digit?"},
        "10450": {"comment":"Counted"},
        "10451": {"comment":"Yes: on"},
        "10453": {"comment":"'(': an array?"},
        "10455": {"comment":"Yes: searched for"},
        "10457": {"comment":"C = $40 + letter, a string"},
        "10459": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "10461": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "10463": {"comment":"C = $60 + letter, a number"},
        "10465": {"comment":"One letter?"},
        "10466": {"comment":"Then $60 + letter"},
        "10468": {"comment":"A long name: $20 + letter"},
        "10470": {"comment":"On"},
        "10472": {"synopsis":"A '$': past it; FLAGS bit 6 cleared (a string)."},
        "10477": {"synopsis":"Checking: LV_CHECK_ONLY. Running: the list at $5C0B (from its second byte), whose bytes are:\n0 or 1, an entry (a length word, then the variable, its name first: compared with C);\n$22-$3D a separator (LV_LOC_FLAG), skipped with the 10 bytes after it, as is a byte below\n$22 (not 0 or 1); $40 the end, the search going on in VARS (LV_RUN); any other, with bit 6\ncleared, the count of bytes to skip.","comment":"Running?"},
        "10481": {"comment":"No: LV_CHECK_ONLY"},
        "10484": {"comment":"HL = the list"},
        "10487": {"comment":"DE = 0"},
        "10490": {"synopsis":"A separator: B bit 7 cleared, entries compared again.","comment":"B bit 7 cleared"},
        "10492": {"synopsis":"HL one on, then DE on: the next byte of the list.","comment":"One on"},
        "10493": {"synopsis":"HL + DE; the byte there: 0 or 1 is an entry.","comment":"DE on"},
        "10494": {"comment":"The byte"},
        "10495": {"comment":"0 or 1?"},
        "10497": {"comment":"No: LV_LOC_OTHER"},
        "10499": {"comment":"DE = the entry's length"},
        "10503": {"comment":"HL = its name"},
        "10504": {"comment":"Skipping?"},
        "10506": {"comment":"Then past the entry"},
        "10508": {"comment":"B = the type"},
        "10509": {"comment":"The name byte"},
        "10510": {"comment":"Bit 7 removed"},
        "10512": {"comment":"The same as C?"},
        "10513": {"comment":"Yes: LV_LOC_MATCH"},
