        "11007": {"synopsis":"Assigns the value just evaluated to the variable at DEST (CLASS_1); IXh = $40 (a string's\nform for WRITE_STR_NAME).\n1. A '%' variable (FLAGS2 bit 2): $060D.\n2. A new number (FLAGX bit 1): room for its name and its 5 bytes at the end of the variables\n   (MAKE_ROOM at E_LINE - 1); a single letter as $60 + letter, a longer name as $A0 + letter\n   and the rest of the name (WRITE_NAME_REST); the value's 5 bytes moved off the calculator\n   stack after it. A new string: NEW_STRING.\n3. An existing number (LET_EXISTING): its 5 bytes overwritten.\n4. Part of a string (FLAGX bit 0 clear): the new value over the old characters, padded with\n   spaces; a longer one goes to $0067.\n5. A whole string (LET_WHOLE_STR): a variable above STKEND is LOCAL_STR_LET's; otherwise a\n   new copy is made (NEW_STR_NAMED) and the old one reclaimed.\nExit: HL = the value's first byte for a number.","comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "11010": {"comment":"A '%' variable?"},
        "11014": {"comment":"Then $060D"},
        "11017": {"comment":"IXh = $40: a string's form"},
        "11020": {"comment":"A new variable?"},
        "11024": {"comment":"Skipped"},
        "11026": {"comment":"The name counted"},
        "11029": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "11031": {"comment":"Yes: a new string"},
        "11034": {"comment":"BC = 5 + the letters"},
        "11040": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "11043": {"comment":"HL = the variables' end-marker"},
        "11044": {"comment":"BC bytes of room there"},
        "11047": {"comment":"HL = the room's first byte"},
        "11049": {"comment":"HL = the name in the line"},
        "11052": {"comment":"A = the letters after the first"},
        "11054": {"comment":"B = them"},
        "11055": {"comment":"The first letter"},
        "11056": {"comment":"$60 + letter"},
        "11058": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "11059": {"comment":"One letter: done"},
        "11061": {"comment":"$A0 + letter"},
        "11063": {"comment":"C = it"},
        "11064": {"comment":"The rest of the name (WRITE_NAME_REST)"},
        "11067": {"comment":"A back"},
        "11068": {"comment":"The next place","synopsis":"The value's 5 bytes off the calculator stack (STKEND - 5) to DE + 1.\nExit: HL = its first byte."},
        "11072": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "11075": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "11076": {"comment":"HL = the value on the calculator stack"},
        "11078": {"comment":"STKEND = it"},
        "11081": {"comment":"The value's place kept"},
        "11082": {"comment":"The 5 bytes moved"},
        "11084": {"comment":"HL = the value"},
        "11086": {"synopsis":"An existing variable: a number's 5 bytes overwritten (LET_NUM_VALUE); a string by its kind\n(FLAGX bit 0).","comment":"A number?"},
        "11090": {"comment":"DE = DEST"},
        "11091": {"comment":"A = its byte"},
        "11092": {"comment":"Yes: the 5 bytes"},
        "11094": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "11095": {"comment":"BC = STRLEN"},
        "11099": {"comment":"FLAGX bit 0: the whole string?"},
        "11103": {"comment":"Then a new copy"},
