        "11123": {"comment":"Then nothing to copy"},
        "11125": {"comment":"The value over the spaces"},
        "11127": {"synopsis":"BC = the slot's length less the new value's: the spaces to pad with.","comment":"BC = the difference"},
        "11128": {"synopsis":"HL past the copied value; the rest of the slot filled with spaces (L_PAD_LOOP).","comment":"HL = past the copied value"},
        "11129": {"comment":"Nothing?","synopsis":"BC spaces."},
        "11131": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "11132": {"comment":"A space"},
        "11134": {"comment":"On"},
        "11135": {"comment":"One fewer"},
        "11136": {"comment":"Again"},
        "11138": {"synopsis":"A whole existing string: a variable above STKEND is LOCAL_STR_LET's. Otherwise back from\nDEST over its length word and name (bit 7 cleared on each letter, bit 6 set on the first\nbyte), a new copy made with the same name (NEW_STR_NAMED), and the old variable reclaimed\n(RECLAIM).\nExit: HL = the new copy's place, less the old length.","comment":"DE = DEST"},
        "11139": {"comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "11142": {"comment":"DEST above it?"},
        "11144": {"comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "11145": {"comment":"Yes: a local variable"},
        "11148": {"comment":"Back over the length word"},
        "11152": {"comment":"A counts the name's bytes"},
        "11153": {"synopsis":"Back over the name's letters (bit 5 set), each with bit 7 cleared, A counting down; the\nfirst byte gets bit 6 set (a string).","comment":"Counted"},
        "11154": {"comment":"Back one"},
        "11155": {"comment":"One more to reclaim"},
        "11156": {"comment":"Bit 7 cleared"},
        "11158": {"comment":"A letter?"},
        "11160": {"comment":"Yes: on back"},
        "11162": {"comment":"Bit 6: a string"},
        "11164": {"comment":"The variable kept"},
        "11165": {"comment":"Its length kept"},
        "11166": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "11167": {"comment":"B = -(the count)"},
        "11168": {"comment":"The new copy"},
        "11171": {"comment":"The count back"},
        "11172": {"comment":"The length back"},
        "11173": {"comment":"HL = the old variable"},
        "11174": {"comment":"One byte only?"},
        "11175": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "11177": {"comment":"The $7F too"},
        "11178": {"comment":"One more"},
        "11179": {"comment":"Its length kept","synopsis":"The old variable reclaimed (RECLAIM)."},
        "11180": {"comment":"The old variable removed"},
        "11183": {"comment":"The old length back"},
        "11184": {"comment":"HL = the old variable"},
        "11189": {"synopsis":"A new string variable (LET_ASSIGN with '$', B = -(the letters)): the name at DEST, then\nNEW_STR_NAMED.","comment":"HL = DEST"},
        "11192": {"synopsis":"Makes a string variable at the end of the variables from the string on the calculator stack\n(STK_FETCH), named by the name at HL (kept in K_CUR for WRITE_STR_NAME), B = -(its letters):\nIXl = the count of letters; DEST = the string's last byte; room for the string, its length\nword and the name (1 byte, or the count + 1 with the $7F) before E_LINE - 1 (MAKE_ROOM);\nthen NEW_STR_COPY.","comment":"K_CUR = the name"},
        "11195": {"comment":"The count kept"},
        "11196": {"comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "11199": {"comment":"A = -(the count)"},
        "11200": {"comment":"The count"},
        "11202": {"comment":"IXl = it"},
        "11204": {"comment":"One letter?"},
        "11205": {"comment":"Then A = 0"},
        "11207": {"comment":"Else A = the count"},
        "11208": {"synopsis":"The room: BC = the length + A + 3.","comment":"The length kept"},
        "11209": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "11210": {"comment":"Plus its length"},
        "11211": {"comment":"Its last byte"},
        "11212": {"comment":"DEST = it"},
        "11215": {"comment":"Plus the name's extra bytes"},
        "11217": {"comment":"Plus 3: the name and the length"},
        "11220": {"comment":"HL = E_LINE"},
        "11223": {"comment":"HL = the variables' end-marker"},
        "11224": {"comment":"The room; DE = its last byte"},
        "11227": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "11228": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11229": {"comment":"HL = the room's start"},
        "11230": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11231": {"comment":"A = IXh"},
        "11233": {"comment":"Bit 7 into carry"},
        "11234": {"comment":"NEW_STR_COPY"},
        "11249": {"synopsis":"Takes the top number off the calculator stack into A, E, D, C and B.","comment":"HL = STKEND"},
        "11252": {"comment":"Back one"},
        "11253": {"comment":"B = the last byte"},
        "11255": {"comment":"C"},
        "11257": {"comment":"D"},
        "11259": {"comment":"E"},
        "11261": {"comment":"A = the first byte"},
        "11262": {"comment":"STKEND down by 5"},
        "11266": {"synopsis":"DIM: as the 48K ROM's, for array names of one letter or more. The name looked up (the\nroutine at $28B8; else report C); its HL kept in DEST, DE in K_CUR. Checking: the subscripts\nchecked (VAR_SUBSCRIPTS) and the statement's end. Running (DIM_RUN):\n1. Each dimension (SUBSCRIPT, report 3) multiplied into the elements' size (the routine at\n   $159F; report 4 on overflow).\n2. The length (elements + 2 x the count + 1) must be below $C100, else report 4; the sizes\n   kept on the calculator stack (STK_STORE).\n3. An old array of the name: its length zeroed and its body reclaimed, then DIM_OLD_NAME; a\n   new name: DIM_NEW. Both make the array at the end of the variables.\n4. The count stored, the elements filled with 0 or spaces, the dimensions stored\n   (DIM_COUNT).","comment":"The name looked up (LOOK_VARS)"},
        "11269": {"synopsis":"Report C."},
        "11272": {"comment":"HL kept in DEST"},
        "11275": {"comment":"DE kept in K_CUR"},
        "11279": {"comment":"Checking syntax (C bit 7 set)?"},
        "11281": {"comment":"No: running"},
        "11283": {"comment":"Checked as a number array"},
        "11285": {"comment":"The subscripts checked (VAR_SUBSCRIPTS)"},
        "11288": {"comment":"The statement's end (STATEMENT_END)"},
        "11291": {"synopsis":"Running: F (carry when the array is not there yet) kept at $5B52, the name byte with bit 7\nin IXh, a count of 0 dimensions on the stack, DE = the element size: 1 for a string array, 5\nfor numbers.","comment":"F kept at $5B52: carry when not there"},
        "11296": {"comment":"Bit 7: an array"},
        "11298": {"comment":"IXh = the name byte"},
        "11300": {"comment":"B = 0 dimensions so far"},
        "11302": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11303": {"comment":"DE = 1, a character's size"},
        "11306": {"comment":"A string array?"},
        "11308": {"comment":"Then 1"},
        "11310": {"comment":"Otherwise 5 for a number"},
        "11312": {"synopsis":"One dimension (SUBSCRIPT, report 3 when out of range): kept on the stack, counted, and\nmultiplied in (HL_MULT); ',' for another, ')' to end.","comment":"Past '(' or ','"},
        "11313": {"comment":"HL = $FF00 or more: any limit"},
        "11315": {"comment":"BC = the dimension"},
        "11318": {"comment":"Zero or too big: report 3"},
        "11321": {"comment":"HL = the name and the count"},
        "11322": {"comment":"The dimension kept"},
        "11323": {"comment":"One more dimension"},
        "11324": {"comment":"The name and the count kept"},
        "11325": {"comment":"HL = the dimension"},
        "11327": {"comment":"Times the product so far ($159F, report 4 on overflow)"},
        "11330": {"comment":"DE = the new product"},
        "11331": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "11332": {"comment":"','?"},
        "11334": {"comment":"Then another dimension"},
        "11336": {"comment":"')'?"},
        "11338": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "11340": {"comment":"Past ')'"},
        "11341": {"comment":"B = the count, C = the name"},
        "11342": {"comment":"HL = the count"},
        "11345": {"comment":"Times 2: the dimension words"},
        "11346": {"comment":"Plus 1: the count byte"},
        "11347": {"comment":"Plus the elements' bytes"},
        "11348": {"comment":"The elements' size kept"},
        "11349": {"comment":"The length kept"},
        "11350": {"comment":"The count and the name kept"},
        "11351": {"synopsis":"Report 4 when the length overflowed or is $C100 or more (CP $C0 with H).","comment":"Over 64K: report 4"},
        "11354": {"comment":"$C100 or more?"},
        "11357": {"comment":"Then report 4"},
        "11359": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "11361": {"comment":"Sizes kept on the calculator stack (STK_STORE)"},
        "11364": {"comment":"F back from $5B52"},
        "11369": {"comment":"Not there: a new array"},
        "11371": {"comment":"HL = the DE LOOK_VARS left"},
        "11374": {"comment":"Its bit 7 set"},
        "11376": {"comment":"HL = the old array's first byte"},
        "11379": {"comment":"To its length"},
        "11380": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "11381": {"comment":"BC = the old length, the field zeroed"},
        "11386": {"comment":"HL = the old body"},
        "11387": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11388": {"comment":"DE = the body"},
        "11389": {"comment":"HL = STKEND - the body"},
        "11394": {"comment":"HL = the body, DE = the bytes up to STKEND"},
        "11395": {"comment":"The old body reclaimed"},
        "11398": {"comment":"On with the old name"},
        "11400": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a letter or a digit (ALPHA, DIGIT_TEST).\nChanges: F.","comment":"Carry unless a digit (DIGIT_TEST)"},
        "11403": {"comment":"Carry: a digit"},
        "11404": {"comment":"A digit: done"},
        "11405": {"synopsis":"Carry when A is a letter, A-Z or a-z.\nChanges: F.","comment":"Below 'A'?"},
        "11407": {"comment":"Carry: 'A' or above"},
        "11408": {"comment":"No: below 'A'"},
        "11409": {"comment":"Up to 'Z'?"},
        "11411": {"comment":"Yes: a capital"},
        "11412": {"comment":"Below 'a'?"},
        "11414": {"comment":"Carry: 'a' or above"},
        "11415": {"comment":"No: between 'Z' and 'a'"},
        "11416": {"comment":"Carry: up to 'z'"},
        "11419": {"synopsis":"An array of the name was there: its body is gone already; the routine at $2B82 (BC = 0, HL =\nthe old body) makes the new array with the old name and takes the old header away. Then\nDIM_COUNT.","comment":"BC = 0"},
        "11422": {"comment":"HL = where the old body was"},
        "11423": {"comment":"The new array, the old header gone ($2B82)"},
        "11426": {"comment":"On to the count"},
        "11428": {"synopsis":"No array of the name yet: the name in the line measured from DEST (the routine at $1BD1),\nthen the new array made with it (the routine at $2BB5).","comment":"The name in the line measured ($1BD1)"},
        "11431": {"comment":"The new array made ($2BB5)"},
        "11434": {"synopsis":"Stores the count of dimensions (A, off the stack) after the name and length, then fills the\nelements: 0 for a number array, spaces for a string array (IXh bit 6), the last byte set and\ncopied down by LDDR.","comment":"HL to the count's place"},
        "11435": {"comment":"A = the count"},
        "11436": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "11437": {"comment":"A = the name byte"},
        "11439": {"comment":"Sign: bit 6, a string array"},
        "11440": {"comment":"A = the count again"},
        "11441": {"comment":"BC = the length"},
        "11442": {"comment":"HL = past the array"},
        "11443": {"comment":"HL = its last byte"},
        "11444": {"comment":"DE = the one below"},
        "11447": {"comment":"BC = the elements' size"},
        "11448": {"comment":"A 0 there"},
        "11450": {"comment":"Number array: 0"},
        "11453": {"comment":"String array: a space"},
        "11455": {"synopsis":"The elements filled (LDDR from the last byte down); HL to the last dimension's place.","comment":"Filled down"},
        "11457": {"comment":"HL = the last dimension's high byte"},
        "11459": {"synopsis":"Stores the dimensions off the stack, the last first (high byte, then low byte, downwards).","comment":"DE = a dimension"},
        "11460": {"comment":"Its high byte"},
        "11461": {"comment":"Back one"},
        "11462": {"comment":"Its low byte"},
        "11463": {"comment":"Back one"},
        "11464": {"comment":"One less to go"},
        "11465": {"comment":"More?"},
        "11468": {"synopsis":"Reads the number at CH_ADD onto the calculator stack, in a base its prefix gives: '$' base\n16, BIN or '@' base 2 (the prefix skipped), anything else base 10 (not skipped).\n1. BASE_SET: the base into memory 5 (its third byte, $5CAD, is what the digit test at $1ED8\n   compares with), memory 4 = 1, 0 stacked.\n2. The whole part in the base (DIGITS_IN_BASE).\n3. A '.' and the fraction (NUM_FRAC_LOOP), each digit divided by the next power of the base.\n4. Then the exponent part at $1EA1 (E or e, in base 10 only).\nCalled from the expression scanner ($2692).","comment":"C = 16"},
        "11470": {"comment":"'$'?"},
        "11472": {"comment":"Then hexadecimal"},
        "11474": {"comment":"C = 2"},
        "11476": {"comment":"BIN?"},
        "11478": {"comment":"Then binary"},
        "11480": {"comment":"'@'?"},
        "11482": {"comment":"Also binary"},
        "11484": {"comment":"C = 10, decimal"},
        "11486": {"comment":"The character kept"},
        "11488": {"synopsis":"Past the prefix ('$', BIN or '@').","comment":"Past the prefix"},
        "11489": {"synopsis":"The base C set up (BASE_SET).","comment":"A = the base"},
        "11490": {"comment":"Set up (BASE_SET)"},
        "11493": {"synopsis":"A '.' tested in A as BASE_SET leaves it ($33), so this jump is never taken (a leading '.'\nreaches the fraction through the test after the whole part); then the whole part\n(DIGITS_IN_BASE) and, after a '.', the fraction (NUM_FRAC_LOOP); otherwise the exponent part\n($1EA1).","comment":"A '.'? (A is $33 here)"},
        "11495": {"comment":"Never taken: A is $33"},
        "11497": {"comment":"The whole part in the base"},
        "11500": {"comment":"Then a '.'?"},
        "11502": {"comment":"No: an exponent? ($1EA1)"},
        "11505": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "11506": {"comment":"Yes: the fraction"},
        "11508": {"comment":"Past the '.'","synopsis":"A '.' first (only from the jump at $2CE7): past it; a digit must follow (the test at $1ED8),\nelse report C; then the fraction."},
        "11509": {"comment":"A digit must follow"},
        "11512": {"synopsis":"Report C when carry: no digit. Also from the exponent's digits ($1EBF).","comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "11515": {"comment":"The current character"},
        "11516": {"synopsis":"One fraction digit (DIGIT_TO_STACK): memory 4 x the base, the digit divided by it and added.\nNo digit: on to the exponent part ($1EA1).","comment":"A digit stacked?"},
        "11519": {"comment":"No: an exponent? ($1EA1)"},
        "11530": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11531": {"comment":"The next digit"},
        "11533": {"synopsis":"BASE_SET with A = 10.","comment":"A = 10"},
        "11535": {"synopsis":"Sets up a number's reading in base A: A stacked and stored in memory 5 (so its third byte,\n$5CAD, holds the base), memory 4 = 1, and a 0 left on the calculator stack for the value.\nExit: A = $33 (end-calc's POP AF).","comment":"The base stacked (STACK_A)"},
        "11546": {"comment":"Memory 5 = the base, 4 = 1, 0 stacked"},
        "11547": {"synopsis":"Carry unless A is a digit (\"0\"-\"9\").\nChanges: F.","comment":"Below '0': carry"},
        "11550": {"comment":"Up to '9': carry, flipped below"},
        "11552": {"comment":"Carry when above '9'"},
        "11554": {"synopsis":"Stacks A as a digit in the current base (the test at $1ED8: 0-9, letters for 10 up, below\nthe base in $5CAD give their value). Exit: carry, A = the character, when it is not one.","comment":"The digit's value, carry if none ($1ED8)"},
        "11557": {"comment":"Not a digit: carry, A = the character"},
        "11558": {"comment":"Filler where a SUB stood: A is the value"},
        "11560": {"synopsis":"Stacks A as a number (STACK_BC with BC = A)."},
        "11561": {"comment":"BC = A"},
        "11563": {"synopsis":"Stacks BC as a small integer (positive), IY restored to $5C3A first; HL and DE left at the\ncalculator stack's top (end-calc). No carry.","comment":"IY as the system variables need"},
        "11567": {"comment":"A and E = 0: the exponent and sign bytes","synopsis":"STACK_BC without setting IY first: BC stacked as a small integer; HL and DE at the stack's\ntop. No carry."},
        "11569": {"comment":"D = the low byte, C = the high byte"},
        "11571": {"comment":"B = 0, the fifth byte"},
        "11572": {"comment":"The five bytes stacked"},
        "11575": {"comment":"HL and DE to the stack's top"},
        "11577": {"comment":"No carry"},
        "11579": {"synopsis":"Reads a run of decimal digits at CH_ADD as a number (BASE_TEN, then DIGITS_IN_BASE). Used\nfor line numbers ($1A09) and exponents ($1EC2).","comment":"Base 10 (BASE_TEN)"},
        "11582": {"synopsis":"Reads a run of digits in the current base (memory 5) at CH_ADD: the value x the base + each\ndigit (DIGIT_TO_STACK), CH_ADD past them.\nExit: carry, A = the character after them.","comment":"The current character"},
        "11583": {"synopsis":"The next digit, or the end.","comment":"A digit stacked?"},
        "11586": {"comment":"No: done"},
        "11593": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "11598": {"synopsis":"e-to-fp with A = D (PRINT_FP's NP_FRAC_ONLY).","comment":"A = D"},
        "11599": {"synopsis":"e-to-fp ($3C): the number on the stack x 10 ^ A (A a signed byte): memory 0 = 1 for a\nnegative A (divide), 0 for a positive one (multiply); the power 10 squared for each bit of\n|A|, the number multiplied or divided by it where the bit is 1.\nObserved: VAL \"1E3\" 1000; 1.5E-5 printed .000015.","comment":"Bit 7 into the carry"},
        "11600": {"comment":"A as it was"},
        "11601": {"comment":"Positive"},
        "11603": {"comment":"Negative: A = |A|"},
        "11605": {"synopsis":"Memory 0 = the sign (STORE_0_OR_1 at MEMBOT); 10 stacked.","comment":"|A| kept"},
        "11606": {"comment":"HL = memory 0 (MEMBOT)"},
        "11609": {"comment":"Memory 0 = 1 for a negative A (the carry), else 0"},
        "11615": {"comment":"A = |A|"},
        "11616": {"synopsis":"The next bit of |A|: a 1 bit multiplies or divides (memory 0 chooses) by the power.","comment":"The next bit into the carry"},
        "11618": {"comment":"0: no multiply or divide"},
        "11620": {"comment":"The bits left kept"},
        "11629": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $2D68 and the jump at $2D6B land on (the listing cannot\ndecode them after RST $28): division (the negative case), get-mem-1, end-calc. The Z80 goes\non at TENS_BIT_DONE."},
        "11632": {"synopsis":"AF back.","comment":"The bits left back"},
        "11633": {"synopsis":"More bits: the power squared (duplicate, multiply).","comment":"None left: done"},
        "11635": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "11643": {"synopsis":"The power deleted."},
        "11647": {"synopsis":"Reads the small integer at HL (5 bytes: 0, the sign $00 or $FF, the value's low and high\nbyte in two's complement, 0): C = the sign, DE = its magnitude (negated back for a negative\nsign). HL at its high byte."},
        "11648": {"comment":"C = the sign"},
        "11650": {"comment":"The low byte"},
        "11651": {"comment":"Negated when the sign is $FF (complemented, +1)"},
        "11655": {"comment":"The high byte, with the borrow"},
        "11657": {"comment":"Complemented for $FF"},
        "11658": {"comment":"DE = the magnitude"},
        "11660": {"synopsis":"SMALL_INT_PUT with C = 0 (positive)."},
        "11662": {"synopsis":"Stores DE with sign C as a small integer at HL (0, C, the value, 0). HL kept.\nObserved: LET v=-5 stored 00 FF FB FF 00; LET z=65535 00 00 FF FF 00."},
        "11663": {"comment":"0: the exponent byte"},
        "11666": {"comment":"The sign"},
        "11668": {"comment":"The low byte, negated when the sign is $FF"},
        "11673": {"comment":"The high byte, with the carry"},
        "11678": {"comment":"The fifth byte 0"},
        "11682": {"synopsis":"Takes the number off the calculator stack into BC, rounded to the nearest whole number (+\n1/2, int, unless it is already a small integer).\nExit: BC = |the value|, A = C; carry when it does not fit 16 bits; Z for positive, NZ for\nnegative."},
        "11684": {"comment":"The top number's exponent byte"},
        "11686": {"comment":"0: a small integer already"},
        "11693": {"synopsis":"Deleted from the stack; its value read (SMALL_INT_GET)."},
        "11696": {"comment":"HL and DE kept"},
        "11698": {"comment":"HL = the deleted number"},
        "11699": {"comment":"B = its exponent byte: 0 for a small integer"},
        "11700": {"comment":"C = the sign, DE = the magnitude"},
        "11703": {"comment":"Carry unless B is 0: not a small integer, too big"},
        "11705": {"comment":"Z for a positive number"},
        "11707": {"comment":"BC = the magnitude"},
        "11709": {"comment":"A = C"},
        "11713": {"synopsis":"A = INT (A x log10 2) (0.30103): the decimal digits a binary exponent A stands for.","comment":"D = A"},
        "11714": {"comment":"Its sign into the carry"},
        "11715": {"comment":"E and C = $FF for a negative A"},
        "11718": {"comment":"A and B = 0"},
        "11720": {"comment":"A stacked as a signed small integer"},
        "11733": {"synopsis":"Takes the number off the calculator stack into A (FP_TO_BC). Exit: carry when it is over\n255; Z for positive, NZ for negative."},
        "11736": {"comment":"Over 16 bits"},
        "11737": {"comment":"The flags kept"},
        "11738": {"comment":"B 0?"},
        "11740": {"comment":"Yes: in range"},
        "11742": {"comment":"Otherwise carry"},
        "11745": {"synopsis":"AF back: in range."},
        "11747": {"synopsis":"Prints the number on top of the calculator stack through the current channel (and takes it\noff):\n1. 0 prints \"0\". A negative number prints '-' (NP_MINUS) and goes on positive.\n2. The whole part becomes decimal digits (BCD, then bytes in memories 3-5 from $5CA1); a\n   large one is first scaled down (LOG10_ESTIMATE, e-to-fp); then the fraction's digits (x\n   10, MUL10_ADD): at most 8 significant digits, rounded on the ninth (NP_ROUND).\n3. Plainly (NP_PLAIN) when the decimal point's place is from -4 to 8: \"0\" before the point\n   only when the first digit follows it; otherwise in E form, one digit, '.', the rest, E,\n   the exponent's sign and digits (NP_E_FORM).\nObserved: 1E9 1E+9, 123456789 1.2345679E+8, 12345678 12345678, .0001 .0001, .001 .001, .5\n0.5, -.5 -0.5, 1.5E-5 .000015, 2E10 2E+10, 1/7 0.14285714, 0 and -0 0, 1E38 1E+38."},
        "11758": {"comment":"Zero: '0'"},
        "11762": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $2DE6 lands on for a negative number: abs, end-calc. The\nZ80 goes on at NP_MINUS."},
        "11764": {"synopsis":"Prints '-'; then the calculator again, memories 3-5 cleared.","comment":"'-'"},
        "11774": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "11777": {"synopsis":"Splits the number: the whole part (INT) left on the stack, the fraction in memory 2."},
        "11787": {"comment":"The whole part's exponent byte"},
        "11789": {"comment":"Not a small integer: a large number"},
        "11791": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "11794": {"comment":"16 bits"},
        "11796": {"comment":"A high byte?"},
        "11800": {"comment":"The low byte 0 too?"},
        "11801": {"comment":"No whole part"},
        "11803": {"comment":"Only a low byte: moved up, 8 bits"},
