        "12794": {"synopsis":"The bits counted (B from $DF).","comment":"One bit more"},
        "12795": {"comment":"Negative still: the next bit"},
        "12798": {"comment":"The 33rd bit kept"},
        "12799": {"comment":"B = 0: one more, for the rounding (doubled first)"},
        "12801": {"comment":"The quotient into D'E'DE"},
        "12806": {"comment":"The rounding bits into B'"},
        "12813": {"comment":"B and C = the exponents"},
        "12814": {"comment":"HL = the result"},
        "12815": {"comment":"The dividend's exponent less the divisor's"},
        "12817": {"comment":"The result's exponent"},
        "12820": {"synopsis":"truncate ($3A): the number with its fraction bits cleared (rounding towards 0); one that\nfits becomes a small integer.","comment":"A = the exponent"},
        "12822": {"comment":"Zero (or a small integer): done"},
        "12823": {"comment":"Exponent below $81 (|x| below 1)?"},
        "12827": {"comment":"Then 0: the exponent cleared"},
        "12829": {"comment":"And all 32 mantissa bits"},
        "12833": {"synopsis":"Exponent $81 or more: below $91 the small integer (TRUNC_SMALL), $91 and up its fraction\nbits (the JP at $3223 goes to TRUNC_SMALL's JR NC; -65536 gets no case of its own).","comment":"Exponent below $91 (|x| below 65536)?"},
        "12835": {"comment":"Carry: TRUNC_SMALL; otherwise its fraction bits"},
        "12838": {"synopsis":"The 16-bit sum of two small integers was 0:\n1. No carry (both values 0): the first number stands (INT_SUM_DONE).\n2. Carry, signs differing: a positive 0 (INT_SUM_STORE with A = 0).\n3. Carry, signs the same: 65536 or -65536 in the full form: exponent $91, the first mantissa\n   byte $00 or $80, the rest 0.","comment":"No carry: both were 0"},
        "12840": {"comment":"The signs differ?"},
        "12841": {"comment":"A = 0 (E)"},
        "12842": {"comment":"Then a positive 0"},
        "12845": {"comment":"The first's sign byte"},
        "12846": {"comment":"$80 for negative, 0 for positive"},
        "12848": {"comment":"Back to the exponent"},
        "12849": {"comment":"$91: 2 ^ 16"},
        "12851": {"comment":"To the first mantissa byte"},
        "12852": {"comment":"Stored, 0 after it (INT_SUM_STORE)"},
        "12855": {"synopsis":"The high byte D stored; HL back to the result.","comment":"To the high byte's place"},
        "12856": {"comment":"The high byte"},
        "12857": {"comment":"HL back to the result"},
        "12859": {"synopsis":"HL to the result's first byte; DE back."},
        "12860": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "12861": {"comment":"Done"},
        "12862": {"comment":"Unused byte"},
        "12863": {"synopsis":"Below $91: becomes a small integer (TRUNC_SMALL).","comment":"Above $91: its fraction bits"},
        "12865": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "12866": {"comment":"A = $90 - the exponent: the shifts to make it a whole number"},
        "12870": {"comment":"D and E = the top two mantissa bytes"},
        "12873": {"comment":"HL back to the exponent"},
        "12875": {"comment":"C = the sign: 0, or $FF for a negative number"},
        "12882": {"synopsis":"The implicit 1 and the sign.","comment":"The implicit 1"},
        "12884": {"comment":"Eight shifts or more?"},
        "12888": {"comment":"Fewer: shifted bit by bit"},
        "12890": {"comment":"Eight at once: the top byte down"},
        "12893": {"comment":"Eight fewer to go"},
        "12894": {"synopsis":"Stored as a small integer.","comment":"No shifts left"},
        "12896": {"comment":"B = the shifts"},
        "12897": {"synopsis":"Shifts the value into place.","comment":"DE shifted right"},
        "12903": {"synopsis":"SMALL_INT_PUT.","comment":"Stored as a small integer with sign C"},
        "12906": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "12908": {"synopsis":"A full number: the fraction bits ($A0 - exponent of them) cleared; none at $A0 and over.","comment":"A = the exponent"},
        "12909": {"synopsis":"The count of bits to clear.","comment":"$A0 or more: no fraction bits"},
        "12911": {"comment":"Then done"},
        "12912": {"comment":"A = $A0 - the exponent: the bits to clear"},
        "12914": {"synopsis":"Clears A bits from the end: whole bytes, then the rest with a mask.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "12915": {"comment":"DE = the number, HL = its end"},
        "12916": {"comment":"HL at its last byte"},
        "12917": {"comment":"B = whole bytes to clear (A / 8)"},
        "12924": {"comment":"None"},
        "12926": {"synopsis":"Whole bytes zeroed.","comment":"Zeroed"},
        "12929": {"comment":"Back towards the exponent"},
        "12931": {"synopsis":"The rest.","comment":"Bits left over in the next byte"},
        "12933": {"comment":"None: done"},
        "12935": {"comment":"B = their count"},
        "12936": {"comment":"A mask of ones"},
        "12938": {"synopsis":"The mask.","comment":"The low B bits cleared"},
        "12942": {"comment":"The byte masked"},
        "12944": {"synopsis":"Done.","comment":"HL = the number again"},
        "12945": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "12947": {"synopsis":"Both operands into the full floating form (re-stack on DE, then on HL).","comment":"re-stack on DE first"},
        "12950": {"synopsis":"re-stack on the number at DE (HL and DE swapped).","comment":"HL = the number at DE"},
        "12951": {"synopsis":"re-stack ($3D): a small integer at HL into the full floating form (exponent $91 or $89 and\nthe shifted value); a full number is left as it is.\nObserved: LET w=1.5 stored 81 40 00 00 00.","comment":"A = the exponent byte"},
        "12953": {"comment":"Not 0: already in the full form"},
        "12954": {"comment":"DE kept"},
        "12955": {"comment":"C = the sign, DE = the value"},
        "12958": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "12959": {"comment":"The fourth and fifth bytes zeroed"},
        "12963": {"comment":"B = $91: the exponent for a 16-bit value"},
        "12965": {"comment":"A high byte?"},
        "12967": {"comment":"Yes: shift"},
        "12969": {"comment":"A zero value?"},
        "12970": {"comment":"B = 0: the exponent of 0"},
        "12971": {"comment":"Zero: stored as all 0"},
        "12973": {"comment":"Only a low byte: moved up"},
        "12975": {"comment":"B = $89: the exponent for an 8-bit value"},
        "12977": {"synopsis":"The value shifted left until its top bit is 1, the exponent lowered each time.","comment":"HL = the value"},
        "12978": {"synopsis":"One shift.","comment":"The exponent one less for each shift"},
        "12979": {"comment":"Shifted left until a 1 comes out"},
        "12982": {"comment":"The sign (C) into the carry"},
        "12984": {"comment":"Shifted back in as bit 7, over the implicit 1"},
        "12988": {"comment":"DE = the mantissa's two bytes"},
        "12989": {"synopsis":"The exponent and the mantissa stored."},
        "12990": {"comment":"The second byte"},
        "12992": {"comment":"The first, with the sign"},
        "12994": {"comment":"The exponent"},
        "12995": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "12997": {"synopsis":"Calls the routine at BC in another ROM: $5B48 and BC pushed, then a jump to the RAM routine\nat $5B3E (evidently it pages the other ROM in and returns into BC, which comes back through\n$5B48). Called with BC = $3308 to turn a bank number into a page ($38D8, $3A7C).","comment":"$5B48: the way back"},
        "13001": {"comment":"The routine in the other ROM"},
        "13002": {"comment":"Paged in by the RAM routine at $5B3E"},
        "13005": {"synopsis":"CALL_OTHER_BC with the address in HL.","comment":"$5B48: the way back"},
        "13009": {"comment":"The routine in the other ROM"},
        "13010": {"comment":"Paged in by the RAM routine at $5B3E"},
        "13015": {"synopsis":"The expression scanner's table of operation routines, read at $279D (HL = $32D7 + 2 x the\ncode), which calls them directly instead of through the calculator: 64 words for codes\n$00-$3F. $01 SHIFT_LEFT_OP, $02 SHIFT_RIGHT_OP; $03-$30 the same routines as CALC_OP_TABLE\n(subtract to not); $31 $1071 (reads a NextReg through ports $243B/$253B), $32 BIT_NOT, $33\nWORD_PEEK, $34-$36 STREAM_FN, $37 USR_NO_STR, $38 E3_SIGNED_FN, $39-$3A 0, $3B $0926, $3C\n$27F7, $3D BIT_AND, $3E BIT_OR, $3F BIT_XOR; $00 is 0. Codes from $3B take two operands, as\nthose below $18 do. Four $FF bytes follow."},
        "13147": {"synopsis":"The calculator: runs the operation codes that follow the call (RST $28) one by one, on the\ncalculator stack (STKEND) and its six memories (MEM), until end-calc:\n1. B goes to BREG (the count dec-jr-nz uses). HL' points at the codes.\n2. Each code: below $18 the routine gets two operands (HL the first, DE the second, 5 bytes\n   below STKEND, HL set by ADD HL,-5); $18-$3F one (HL, DE = STKEND); $80 and up are groups\n   with the index in bits 0-4: series ($80), stk-const ($A0), st-mem ($C0), get-mem ($E0).\n3. The routine's address comes from CALC_OP_TABLE at $3B02; it returns to CALC_LOOP, which\n   sets STKEND = DE. Observed (on the 48K ROM): 2+3*4 printed 14, 7/2 3.5, 1/3 0.33333333.","comment":"HL = the top number, DE = STKEND"},
        "13150": {"synopsis":"The calculator entered with BREG = B already set by the caller (CALL $335E).","comment":"B into BREG"},
        "13154": {"synopsis":"The calculator entered keeping BREG (CALL $3362)."},
        "13155": {"comment":"HL' = the codes after the call; the caller's HL' kept on the stack"},
        "13157": {"synopsis":"After each operation: STKEND = DE, the next code.","comment":"STKEND = DE: the stack's end after the last operation"},
        "13162": {"comment":"The next code"},
        "13164": {"synopsis":"Reads the next code (HL'): plain codes $00-$7F, or a group code.","comment":"The code pointer kept"},
        "13165": {"comment":"Bit 7 clear: a plain code"},
        "13169": {"comment":"D = the code"},
        "13170": {"comment":"Its group, bits 5-6"},
        "13172": {"comment":"Bits 5-6 down to 1-2: 0, 2, 4 or 6"},
        "13174": {"comment":"L = $7C-$82: the index of series, stk-const, st-mem or get-mem"},
        "13177": {"comment":"A = the code's bits 0-4, the routine's parameter"},
        "13183": {"comment":"Unused byte after the jump"},
        "13184": {"synopsis":"A plain code: below $18 HL is moved to the first of two operands (DE the second).","comment":"Codes from $18 work on one operand"},
        "13186": {"comment":"Codes $18 up: one operand"},
        "13188": {"comment":"The other set: HL', DE'"},
        "13189": {"comment":"DE' = STKEND"},
        "13191": {"comment":"HL' = DE' - 5: the first operand"},
        "13195": {"comment":"Back"},
        "13196": {"synopsis":"The table index: 2 x the code.","comment":"A x 2"},
        "13197": {"comment":"L = it"},
        "13198": {"synopsis":"HL = $3B02 + L: the routine's entry in CALC_OP_TABLE (a group code comes here with L already\nthe index x 2).","comment":"H = 0"},
        "13200": {"comment":"HL = the entry in CALC_OP_TABLE"},
        "13204": {"comment":"DE = the routine"},
        "13207": {"comment":"CALC_LOOP as its return, the code pointer back into HL"},
        "13211": {"comment":"The routine, for the RET that follows"},
        "13213": {"comment":"B = BREG"},
        "13217": {"synopsis":"delete ($02): nothing to do; the loop sets STKEND = DE, the second operand's start, dropping\nit.","comment":"Into the routine pushed above (for delete itself, back to CALC_LOOP)"},
        "13218": {"synopsis":"fp-calc-2's routine, as in the 48K ROM: runs the single operation whose code is in BREG.\nCALC_OP_TABLE's entry for $3B is 0 here and nothing in this page jumps to it.","comment":"CALC_LOOP's return dropped"},
        "13219": {"comment":"A = the code in BREG"},
        "13223": {"comment":"Run as if it came next"},
        "13225": {"synopsis":"Checks there is room for 5 bytes more (TEST_ROOM). Keeps DE and HL."},
        "13227": {"comment":"5 bytes"},
        "13236": {"synopsis":"Copies the 5-byte number at HL onto the calculator stack (COPY_FP_ROOM to STKEND); STKEND\nmoves on 5.","comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "13240": {"comment":"Copied, after the room check (COPY_FP_ROOM)"},
        "13243": {"comment":"STKEND moved on"},
        "13248": {"synopsis":"Copies 5 bytes from HL to DE, after checking there is room (ROOM_FOR_5). Nothing in this\npage calls it: duplicate and the other copies use COPY_FP_ROOM."},
        "13251": {"comment":"The 5 bytes (BC = 5 still)"},
        "13254": {"synopsis":"stk-data ($34): the literal after the code goes onto the stack (UNPACK_LITERAL, HL' moved\npast it).","comment":"DE = STKEND, the literal's place; HL the same"},
        "13256": {"synopsis":"Unpacks a compact literal at HL' to DE: the first byte's bits 6-7 + 1 give the mantissa\nbytes that follow, bits 0-5 the exponent (or the next byte when 0), + $50; the bytes missing\nup to 5 are zero.","comment":"Room for 5 more? (ROOM_FOR_5_FAST)"},
        "13259": {"comment":"HL' (the code pointer) kept"},
        "13262": {"comment":"HL = the code pointer, the place kept"},
        "13263": {"comment":"The first byte's bits 6-7"},
        "13266": {"comment":"Down to bits 0-1"},
        "13268": {"comment":"C = the mantissa bytes that follow, 1-4"},
        "13270": {"comment":"The first byte's bits 0-5"},
        "13273": {"comment":"Not 0: the exponent"},
        "13275": {"comment":"0: the exponent is the next byte"},
        "13277": {"synopsis":"The exponent + $50.","comment":"The exponent stored"},
        "13280": {"comment":"A = the zero bytes to add, + 1"},
        "13283": {"comment":"HL and DE to the mantissa"},
        "13285": {"comment":"The C mantissa bytes copied"},
        "13289": {"comment":"HL = the place, the code pointer kept"},
        "13291": {"comment":"HL' = the code pointer, past the literal"},
        "13293": {"comment":"B = the count + 1"},
        "13294": {"comment":"A = 0"},
        "13295": {"synopsis":"Zero bytes up to 5.","comment":"Up to five bytes in all"},
        "13297": {"comment":"A zero byte"},
        "13318": {"synopsis":"HL = HL + 5 x A: the address of memory A from MEM. Changes: AF, C, HL."},
        "13319": {"comment":"A x 4"},
        "13321": {"comment":"+ A: A x 5"},
        "13322": {"comment":"HL + A (Z80N ADD HL,A)"},
        "13327": {"synopsis":"get-mem ($E0-$E5): memory A (from MEM) copied onto the stack.","comment":"DE (STKEND) kept"},
        "13328": {"comment":"HL = MEM"},
        "13331": {"comment":"HL = memory A"},
        "13334": {"comment":"Copied to STKEND"},
        "13337": {"comment":"HL = the old STKEND, the number's place"},
        "13339": {"synopsis":"stk-const ($A0-$A4): constant A of CALC_CONSTANTS ($3C02 + 5 x A, kept unpacked) copied onto\nthe stack (COPY_FP_ROOM).","comment":"HL = the constants"},
        "13342": {"comment":"A x 5: C = A"},
        "13343": {"comment":"A x 4"},
        "13345": {"comment":"+ A"},
        "13346": {"comment":"HL = constant A"},
        "13348": {"comment":"DE kept: its place"},
        "13349": {"comment":"Copied to STKEND (COPY_FP_ROOM)"},
        "13352": {"comment":"HL = the new number"},
        "13353": {"comment":"Done"},
        "13357": {"synopsis":"st-mem ($C0-$C5): the top number copied into memory A; it stays on the stack.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "13358": {"comment":"DE = the top number"},
        "13359": {"comment":"HL = MEM"},
        "13362": {"comment":"HL = memory A"},
        "13365": {"comment":"HL = the number, DE = the memory"},
        "13366": {"comment":"Copied (COPY_FP_5)"},
        "13369": {"comment":"DE = STKEND again"},
        "13370": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "13372": {"synopsis":"exchange ($01): the top two numbers swap places.","comment":"5 bytes"},
        "13374": {"synopsis":"One byte of each swapped, 5 times.","comment":"A = the second's byte, C = the first's"},
        "13376": {"comment":"Swapped in place"},
        "13381": {"comment":"All five"},
        "13383": {"comment":"HL and DE back as they were"},
        "13385": {"synopsis":"series ($80+): sums a series of the number z on the calculator stack, with the coefficients\nas stk-data literals after the code (B of them, the code's low bits); the Clenshaw\nrecurrence for a Chebyshev series:\n1. Memory 0 = 2z; memory 2 = 0; 0 stacked as the running term.\n2. For each coefficient c: new term = 2z x term - memory 2 + c, memory 1 = the old memory 2,\n   memory 2 = the old term (dec-jr-nz).\n3. The result is the last term minus memory 1 (the term two steps back).\nChanges: memories 0-2.","comment":"B = the count of coefficients"},
        "13386": {"comment":"The calculator, BREG = B"},
        "13402": {"comment":"The next coefficient, from the caller's codes (stk-data)"},
        "13405": {"comment":"The calculator again, BREG kept for dec-jr-nz"},
        "13418": {"synopsis":"abs ($2A): the sign cleared (SIGN_BIT_SET with B = $FF).\nObserved: ABS -3 printed 3.","comment":"B = $FF: the sign cleared"},
        "13422": {"synopsis":"negate ($1B): the sign flipped; 0 stays 0 (IS_ZERO)."},
        "13425": {"comment":"0: stays 0"},
        "13426": {"comment":"B = 0: the sign flipped"},
        "13428": {"synopsis":"Sets the sign from B (abs) or flips it (negate); a small integer goes through\nSIGN_SMALL_INT.","comment":"Exponent 0: a small integer"},
        "13433": {"comment":"Bit 7 of B: set for abs"},
        "13436": {"comment":"ORed into the first mantissa byte"},
        "13437": {"comment":"Bit 7 flipped through the carry"},
        "13440": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "13443": {"synopsis":"A small integer: its value negated or made positive and stored back (SMALL_INT_GET,\nSMALL_INT_PUT)."},
        "13445": {"comment":"C = the sign, DE = the value"},
        "13449": {"comment":"B ($FF for abs) OR the sign, complemented: abs gives 0, negate the other sign"},
        "13453": {"comment":"Stored with the new sign"},
        "13458": {"synopsis":"sgn ($29): 1, -1, or 0 for 0.\nObserved: SGN -5 -1, SGN 0 0."},
        "13461": {"comment":"0: stays 0"},
        "13463": {"comment":"DE = 1"},
        "13467": {"comment":"The sign bit into the carry"},
        "13470": {"comment":"C = $FF for a negative number"},
        "13472": {"comment":"1 with that sign: 1 or -1"},
        "13477": {"synopsis":"in ($2C): the byte read from port n (TAKE_WORD), stacked.","comment":"BC = the port"},
        "13480": {"comment":"A = the byte read"},
        "13484": {"synopsis":"peek ($2B): the byte at address n (TAKE_WORD), stacked.","comment":"BC = the address"},
        "13487": {"comment":"A = the byte there"},
        "13488": {"synopsis":"STACK_A."},
        "13491": {"synopsis":"usr-no ($2D): carry set (a number result), D = $FE, then the shared USR code at $218C (the\naddress taken by TAKE_WORD, the code run, its BC stacked).","comment":"Carry: a number result"},
        "13492": {"synopsis":"D = $FE, then the USR code at $218C with the carry as given.","comment":"D = $FE"},
        "13494": {"comment":"The USR code at $218C"},
        "13497": {"synopsis":"SCAN_OP_TABLE's $37: the USR code at $218C with carry clear, which makes the result a string\n(FLAGS bit 6 cleared, STK_STO_STR).","comment":"No carry: a string result"},
        "13498": {"comment":"On"},
        "13500": {"synopsis":"usr-$ ($19): the address of a UDG: the one-character string must be a letter (made $90 up by\nLETTER_TO_UDG, a to z as A to Z) or a code from $90; UDG + 8 x (code - $90) is stacked.\nBelow $90 is report A; the 48K's limit of 21 UDGs is tested only when the address passes\n$FFFF.","comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "13503": {"comment":"One character?"},
        "13506": {"comment":"No: report A"},
        "13508": {"comment":"A = the character"},
        "13509": {"comment":"A letter becomes its UDG code (LETTER_TO_UDG)"},
        "13512": {"comment":"Less $90"},
        "13514": {"comment":"Below $90: report A"},
        "13516": {"comment":"HL = the index"},
        "13519": {"comment":"Times 8"},
        "13522": {"comment":"BC = UDG"},
        "13526": {"comment":"+ UDG"},
        "13527": {"comment":"BC = the address"},
        "13529": {"comment":"No wrap: stacked"},
        "13531": {"comment":"Wrapped: past the 21st?"},
        "13533": {"comment":"Then report A"},
        "13535": {"synopsis":"BC stacked (STACK_BC_NO_IY).","comment":"Stacked (STACK_BC_NO_IY)"},
        "13538": {"synopsis":"Makes stream A current (STREAM_SELECT), which then returns into the routine at HL (pushed).\nFrom CALC_STR_STR.","comment":"The routine as STREAM_SELECT's return"},
        "13539": {"comment":"Stream A made current"},
        "13542": {"comment":"Unused byte"},
        "13543": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 9 (report A, \"Invalid argument\")."},
        "13545": {"synopsis":"Carry when the number at HL is 0: its first four bytes all zero. Keeps every register but F."},
        "13547": {"comment":"A kept in B"},
        "13548": {"comment":"The first four bytes ORed"},
        "13555": {"comment":"A back"},
        "13558": {"comment":"Not 0: no carry"},
        "13559": {"comment":"0: carry"},
        "13561": {"synopsis":"greater-0 ($37): 1 when the number is above 0, else 0."},
        "13564": {"comment":"0 is not above 0, and stays 0"},
        "13565": {"comment":"A = $FF: the sign flipped"},
        "13569": {"synopsis":"not ($30): 1 for 0, 0 for anything else.\nObserved: NOT 0 1, NOT 7 0."},
        "13572": {"comment":"Carry (0) stored as 1"},
        "13574": {"synopsis":"less-0 ($36): 1 when the number is below 0, else 0.","comment":"A = 0: the sign as it is"},
        "13575": {"synopsis":"The sign bit, flipped by A, into carry."},
        "13576": {"comment":"The sign byte, flipped for greater-0"},
        "13578": {"comment":"Its bit 7 into the carry"},
        "13579": {"synopsis":"Stores carry as the small integer 1 or 0 at HL."},
        "13580": {"comment":"A = 0, the carry kept"},
        "13582": {"comment":"The exponent and sign bytes 0"},
        "13586": {"comment":"The carry into bit 0: the value 0 or 1"},
        "13588": {"comment":"A = 0 again"},
        "13590": {"comment":"The high byte and the fifth 0"},
        "13595": {"synopsis":"or ($07): x OR y is x when y is 0, else 1.","comment":"Is y (at DE) 0?"},
        "13600": {"comment":"Yes: x stays"},
        "13601": {"comment":"No: 1"},
        "13604": {"synopsis":"no-&-no ($08): x AND y is x when y is not 0, else 0."},
        "13609": {"comment":"y not 0: x stays"},
        "13610": {"comment":"y is 0: the result is 0"},
        "13613": {"synopsis":"str-&-no ($10): a$ AND y is a$ when y is not 0, else an empty string (its length made 0).","comment":"Is y (at DE) 0?"},
        "13618": {"comment":"No: a$ stays"},
        "13620": {"comment":"DE back to a$'s entry: its length in the last two bytes"},
        "13621": {"comment":"The length 0"},
        "13627": {"synopsis":"The comparisons, numbers ($09-$0E: <=, >=, <>, >, <, =) and strings ($11-$16, the same\norder): the operands exchanged where needed so that each test is \"greater than\" or \"equal\";\nnumbers are subtracted (CALC_SUBTRACT), strings compared character by character (a string\nthat is the start of a longer one is the smaller); the result 1 for true, 0 for false.\nObserved: 2<=2 1, 3>=4 0, 2<>2 0, \"ab\"<\"abc\" 1, \"a\"<\"b\" 1.","comment":"A = the code"},
        "13628": {"comment":"Less 8: 1-6 for numbers, 9-14 for strings"},
        "13630": {"comment":"Bit 2: >, < and ="},
        "13634": {"comment":"<=, >= and <> one less"},
        "13635": {"synopsis":"Whether to exchange the operands (bit 0 after the shift).","comment":"Bit 0 into the carry: >= and < exchange the operands"},
        "13638": {"comment":"The operands exchanged"},
        "13643": {"comment":"HL and DE as before"},
        "13646": {"synopsis":"Numbers: subtract; strings: CMP_STRINGS.","comment":"Strings?"},
        "13650": {"comment":"The next bit kept with the flags"},
        "13652": {"comment":"Numbers: the first less the second"},
        "13657": {"synopsis":"Two strings (STK_FETCH twice): compared byte by byte.","comment":"The next bit kept with the flags"},
        "13659": {"comment":"The second string, X: DE, BC"},
        "13662": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13664": {"comment":"The first string, Y: DE = its address, BC = its length"},
        "13667": {"comment":"HL = X's length"},
        "13668": {"synopsis":"The next pair of characters, or an end.","comment":"Has X ended?"},
        "13670": {"comment":"HL = X's address, X's length on the stack"},
        "13672": {"comment":"X has not"},
        "13674": {"comment":"X has: has Y too?"},
        "13675": {"synopsis":"The first string ended.","comment":"X's length dropped"},
        "13676": {"comment":"Both ended: equal"},
        "13678": {"comment":"Y is the longer: the flags inverted"},
        "13682": {"synopsis":"Both ended together."},
        "13685": {"synopsis":"The second ended: the first is greater.","comment":"Has Y ended?"},
        "13686": {"comment":"Yes: Y is the shorter"},
        "13688": {"comment":"Y's character less X's"},
        "13690": {"comment":"Y's is lower"},
        "13692": {"comment":"Y's is higher"},
        "13694": {"comment":"The same: on to the next pair"},
        "13697": {"comment":"HL = X's length"},
        "13698": {"comment":"One less"},
        "13701": {"synopsis":"A character differs, or the second ended first.","comment":"X's length dropped"},
        "13703": {"comment":"Carry cleared"},
        "13704": {"synopsis":"A zero on the stack for the result.","comment":"The test's flags kept"},
        "13708": {"synopsis":"Turns the subtraction's or the strings' outcome into 1 or 0 (NOT, GREATER_0)."},
        "13710": {"comment":"Carry: NOT"},
        "13715": {"comment":"No carry: greater-0"},
        "13719": {"comment":"The next bit into the carry"},
        "13720": {"comment":"Clear: NOT again, the inverted tests (<=, >= and <>)"},
        "13724": {"synopsis":"strs-add ($17): the two strings joined in the workspace (WORK_ROOM), stacked.","comment":"The second string: DE, BC"},
        "13729": {"comment":"The first string"},
        "13732": {"comment":"HL = the second's length"},
        "13733": {"comment":"Kept again, with the first's address and length"},
        "13736": {"comment":"BC = the total length"},
        "13739": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (DE = its start)"},
        "13740": {"comment":"The joined string stacked"},
        "13743": {"comment":"BC and HL = the first's length and address"},
        "13747": {"comment":"Empty: nothing to copy"},
        "13749": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13751": {"synopsis":"The second string copied after the first.","comment":"BC and HL = the second's"},
        "13755": {"comment":"Empty: nothing to copy"},
        "13757": {"comment":"Copied after it"},
        "13759": {"synopsis":"HL = STKEND - 5 (the top number), DE = STKEND.\nChanges: DE, HL."},
        "13762": {"comment":"DE = STKEND"},
        "13764": {"comment":"HL = STKEND - 5"},
        "13769": {"synopsis":"chr$ ($2F): a one-character string of code n (0-255, else report B).","comment":"A = n"},
        "13772": {"comment":"Over 255: report B"},
        "13774": {"comment":"Negative: report B"},
        "13777": {"comment":"Room for one character"},
        "13782": {"comment":"The character"},
        "13783": {"comment":"Stacked as a string","synopsis":"Stacks the string DE, BC (STK_STO_STR); DE = STKEND, HL its start. Shared by chr$ and str$."},
        "13788": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code $0A (report B)."},
        "13790": {"synopsis":"val ($1D) and val$ ($18): the string is copied into the workspace with an ENTER after it,\nchecked as an expression of the result's type (a number for val, a string for val$; report C\notherwise), then evaluated (SCAN_EXPR) with CH_ADD there, and CH_ADD put back.\nObserved: VAL \"2*3\" 6, VAL$ \"\"\"a\"\"+\"\"b\"\"\" ab; VAL of a string expression report C.","comment":"CH_ADD kept"},
        "13794": {"comment":"A = the code: $1D val, $18 val$"},
        "13795": {"comment":"A carry for val only"},
        "13797": {"comment":"A = $FF for val, 0 for val$"},
        "13798": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13799": {"comment":"DE = the string, BC = its length"},
        "13802": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13803": {"comment":"One more, for an ENTER"},
        "13804": {"comment":"Room in the workspace (DE = its start)"},
        "13805": {"comment":"HL = the string"},
        "13806": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the copy"},
        "13810": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "13811": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "13814": {"comment":"HL at the extra byte"},
        "13815": {"comment":"An ENTER after it"},
        "13817": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 clear: checking"},
        "13821": {"comment":"The expression checked"},
        "13824": {"comment":"The character after it"},
        "13825": {"comment":"Must be the ENTER"},
        "13827": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "13829": {"comment":"HL = the copy"},
        "13830": {"comment":"A = $FF for val, 0 for val$"},
        "13831": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 6 (a number) against it"},
        "13834": {"comment":"Not 0: the wrong type"},
        "13836": {"synopsis":"Report C, or CH_ADD into the copy for the run."},
        "13839": {"comment":"CH_ADD = the copy again"},
        "13842": {"comment":"FLAGS bit 7 set: running"},
        "13846": {"comment":"The expression evaluated"},
        "13849": {"comment":"CH_ADD back"},
        "13853": {"comment":"HL and DE to the stack's top"},
        "13855": {"synopsis":"str$ ($2E): STR_VIA_PRINTER with DE = PRINT_FP.","comment":"DE = PRINT_FP"},
        "13858": {"synopsis":"Prints the number on the calculator stack into the workspace with the routine at DE and\nstacks the text as a string: one byte of room (RST $30), K_CUR = its start, stream -1 made\ncurrent and the routine run (SELECT_THEN_HL); the old channel back, the length from K_CUR,\nthen STR_RESULT. Also called with DE = $2089 ($1067).","comment":"The printing routine kept"},
        "13859": {"comment":"One byte"},
        "13862": {"comment":"Room in the workspace"},
        "13863": {"comment":"K_CUR = its start: channel R writes there"},
        "13866": {"comment":"HL = the routine, the start kept"},
        "13867": {"comment":"The routine kept"},
        "13868": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "13871": {"comment":"Kept, HL = the routine"},
        "13872": {"comment":"Stream -1: channel R"},
        "13874": {"comment":"Stream -1 made current, then the routine runs"},
        "13877": {"comment":"HL = the old channel"},
        "13878": {"comment":"Made current again"},
        "13881": {"comment":"DE = the text's start"},
        "13882": {"comment":"HL = its end"},
        "13886": {"comment":"BC = its length"},
        "13890": {"comment":"Stacked as a string (STR_RESULT)"},
        "13893": {"synopsis":"read-in ($1A, INKEY$ #s): one call of the stream's input routine (CHAN_INPUT): one\ncharacter, or an empty string when there is none; the channel is put back. A stream of 16 or\nmore is report B.","comment":"A = the stream"},
        "13896": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "13898": {"comment":"Then report B"},
        "13901": {"comment":"CURCHL kept"},
        "13905": {"comment":"The stream made current"},
        "13908": {"comment":"Its input routine once: carry and A when there is a character"},
        "13911": {"comment":"BC = 0: an empty string"},
        "13914": {"comment":"None"},
        "13916": {"comment":"BC = 1"},
        "13917": {"comment":"Room for it"},
        "13918": {"comment":"The character"},
        "13919": {"synopsis":"Stacks the string (STK_STO_STR)."},
        "13922": {"comment":"HL = the old channel"},
        "13923": {"comment":"Made current again"},
        "13926": {"comment":"HL and DE to the stack's top"},
        "13929": {"synopsis":"code ($1C): the first character's code, 0 for an empty string.\nObserved: CODE \"\" 0."},
        "13932": {"comment":"An empty string?"},
        "13934": {"comment":"Yes: A = 0"},
        "13936": {"comment":"A = the first character"},
        "13937": {"synopsis":"STACK_A."},
        "13940": {"synopsis":"len ($1E): the string's length stacked (STK_FETCH, STACK_BC)."},
        "13943": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_BC_NO_IY)"},
        "13946": {"synopsis":"dec-jr-nz ($35): BREG - 1; not 0: a jump by the next byte (CALC_JUMP_REL); 0: past it.","comment":"The code pointer's register set"},
        "13947": {"comment":"HL' kept"},
        "13948": {"comment":"HL = BREG"},
        "13951": {"comment":"Counted down"},
        "13952": {"comment":"HL' back"},
        "13953": {"comment":"Not 0: the jump"},
        "13955": {"comment":"0: past the displacement"},
        "13958": {"synopsis":"jump ($33): the code pointer moves by the signed byte after the code."},
        "13959": {"synopsis":"HL' + the signed byte.","comment":"E = the displacement"},
        "13961": {"comment":"D = its sign"},
        "13964": {"comment":"HL' moved by it"},
        "13967": {"synopsis":"jump-true ($00): the jump when the top number (a 0 or 1 result) is not 0; it stays on the\nstack.","comment":"DE to the top number's value byte"},
        "13970": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "13972": {"comment":"Not 0: the jump"},
        "13976": {"comment":"0: past the displacement"},
        "13979": {"synopsis":"end-calc ($38): the calculator ends; the Z80 goes on after this byte.","comment":"CALC_LOOP's return dropped"},
        "13981": {"comment":"HL' = the caller's again, the code pointer the return address"},
        "13983": {"comment":"Back to the Z80 code after end-calc"},
        "13984": {"synopsis":"n-mod-m ($32): from n and m, n - m x INT (n/m) and INT (n/m) on the stack (memory 0 used).","comment":"The codes of n-mod-m follow"},
        "13999": {"synopsis":"int ($27): truncate; for a negative number with a fraction, one less (CALC_INT_NEG).\nObserved: INT 2.5 2, INT -2.5 -3, INT -3 -3.","comment":"The codes of int follow"},
        "14007": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $36B2 lands on (the listing cannot decode them after RST\n$28): duplicate, truncate, st-mem-0, subtract, get-mem-0, exchange, not, jump-true (+3),\nstk-one, subtract, end-calc. The Z80 goes on at CALC_INT_END."},
        "14019": {"synopsis":"Returns."},
        "14020": {"synopsis":"exp ($26): e ^ x as 2 ^ (x / ln 2):\n1. y = x x 1.442695 (1/ln 2); n = INT y in memory 3, f = y - n (0 to 1).\n2. 2 ^ f from series-08 of 2f - 1 (CALC_SERIES).\n3. n added to the result's exponent byte: over 255 is report 6; a negative n taking it to 0\n   or below gives 0.\nObserved: EXP 1 2.7182818, EXP -1 0.36787944; EXP 100 report 6; EXP -100 0."},
        "14073": {"comment":"A = |n|; NZ for a negative n, carry over 255"},
        "14076": {"comment":"Negative"},
        "14078": {"comment":"Over 255: report 6"},
        "14080": {"comment":"n added to the exponent of 2 ^ f"},
        "14081": {"comment":"No carry: in range"},
        "14083": {"synopsis":"Stops with error code 5 (report 6, \"Number too big\")."},
        "14085": {"synopsis":"n negative: under -255, or not less than the exponent, is 0; otherwise the exponent less\n|n|.","comment":"Below -255: 0"},
        "14087": {"comment":"|n| less the exponent"},
        "14088": {"comment":"Not below it: 0"},
        "14090": {"comment":"A = the exponent less |n|"},
        "14092": {"synopsis":"The new exponent stored.","comment":"The result's new exponent"},
        "14094": {"synopsis":"Underflow: the result is 0."},
        "14099": {"synopsis":"ln ($25): the natural logarithm; x of 0 or less stops with error code 9 (report A, \"Invalid\nargument\"):\n1. x split into its binary exponent e (exponent byte - 128) and mantissa m (exponent byte\n   $80, 0.5 to 1); m of 0.8 or less is doubled and e lessened by 1 (m then 0.8 to 1.6).\n2. ln x = e x ln 2 (0.693147) + (m - 1) x series-0C of 2.5 (m - 1) - 0.5 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: LN 1 0, LN 10 2.3025851; LN 0 report A."},
        "14108": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $3717 lands on for x above 0 (the listing cannot decode\nthem after RST $28): stk-zero, delete, end-calc. The Z80 goes on at LN_SPLIT."},
        "14111": {"synopsis":"The exponent byte taken (A) and replaced by $80 (m from 0.5 to 1); e = A - 128 stacked\n(STACK_A), then the calculator compares m with 0.8.","comment":"A = the exponent byte"},
        "14112": {"comment":"m: the mantissa from 0.5 to 1"},
        "14114": {"comment":"The exponent byte stacked"},
        "14117": {"comment":"The mantissa m against 0.8, and the rest of ln"},
        "14139": {"comment":"Doubles m (its exponent + 1)"},
        "14140": {"comment":"On: e x ln 2 plus the series"},
        "14211": {"synopsis":"get-argt ($39): reduces an angle x (radians) to z from -1 to 1 so that SIN x = SIN (z x\nPI/2), for sin and cos:\n1. y = x x 0.159155 (1/(2 PI)) less INT (that + 0.5): -0.5 to 0.5 turns; z = 4y (-2 to 2).\n2. |z| above 1 (memory 0 = 1, else 0): reflected to 2 - z, or -2 - z for a negative z\n   (ARGT_REFLECT).\nChanges: memory 0, read by cos."},
        "14241": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $379C lands on for |z| above 1 (the listing cannot decode\nthem after RST $28): stk-one, subtract, exchange, less-0, jump-true to the end-calc, negate,\nend-calc: |z| - 2, negated for a positive z. The Z80 goes on at $37A9."},
        "14249": {"comment":"Returns"},
        "14250": {"synopsis":"cos ($20): COS x = SIN (PI/2 - x): get-argt's z made 1 - |z| (|z| - 1 negated, or kept when\nmemory 0 says z was reflected), then sin's series.\nObserved: COS 0 1, COS PI -1, COS 1 0.54030231."},
        "14261": {"synopsis":"sin ($1F): get-argt's z, then z x series-06 of 2z^2 - 1 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: SIN 0 0, SIN (PI/2) 1, SIN PI 0, SIN 1 0.84147098, SIN 1000 0.82687939."},
        "14298": {"synopsis":"tan ($21): SIN x / COS x (division: report 6 when COS x is 0).\nObserved: TAN 1 1.5574077."},
        "14306": {"synopsis":"atn ($24): the arctangent:\n1. |x| below 1 (an exponent byte below $81): w = x with c = 0 (ATN_SMALL).\n2. Otherwise w = -1/x with c = PI/2, or -PI/2 for a negative x.\n3. ATN x = c + w x series-0C of 2w^2 - 1 (CALC_SERIES).\nObserved: ATN 1 0.78539816, ATN -2 -1.1071487.","comment":"The full form"},
        "14309": {"comment":"A = the exponent byte"},
        "14310": {"comment":"|x| below 1?"},
        "14312": {"comment":"Yes: c = 0"},
        "14314": {"comment":"No: w = -1/x, c = PI/2 with x's sign"},
        "14328": {"synopsis":"|x| below 1: c = 0."},
        "14387": {"synopsis":"asn ($22): ASN x = 2 x ATN (x / (1 + SQR (1 - x^2))); |x| above 1 makes sqr's ln stop with\nreport A.\nObserved: ASN .5 0.52359878; ASN 2 report A."},
        "14403": {"synopsis":"acs ($23): ACS x = PI/2 - ASN x.\nObserved: ACS .5 1.0471976."},
        "14410": {"synopsis":"sqr ($28): 0 gives 0 (the jump-true to $386C's end-calc); otherwise x ^ 0.5 by falling into\nto-power.\nObserved: SQR 2 1.4142136, SQR 0 0; SQR -1 report A."},
        "14417": {"synopsis":"to-power ($06): x ^ y with x below y on the stack:\n1. x not 0: EXP (y x LN x) (CALC_EXP), so a negative x stops in ln with report A.\n2. x = 0 (POWER_ZERO_BASE): y = 0 gives 1, y above 0 gives 0, y below 0 is 1/0, report 6.\nObserved: 2^10 1024, 2^.5 1.4142136, 0^0 1, 0^3 0; 0^-1 report 6, (-2)^2 report A."},
        "14426": {"comment":"EXP (y x LN x)"},
        "14429": {"synopsis":"Calculator codes the jump-true at $3855 lands on for x = 0 (the listing cannot decode them\nafter RST $28): delete, duplicate, not, jump-true (y = 0) to the delete at $386A, stk-zero,\nexchange, greater-0, jump-true (y above 0) to the end-calc at $386C, stk-one, exchange,\ndivision (1/0), delete, stk-one, end-calc. sqr's jump-true at $384D also lands on the\nend-calc at $386C. The Z80 goes on at $386D."},
        "14445": {"comment":"Returns"},
        "14446": {"synopsis":"The frame interrupt's keyboard call (CALL $386E at $004A): a jump to KEYBOARD.","comment":"KEYBOARD"},
        "14462": {"synopsis":"OUT_UDG_TOKEN's body (the JP at $0B52): codes $A5 and up are keywords (OUT_TOKEN), $90-$A4\nUDGs (the code at $0B56).","comment":"A keyword ($A5 up)?"},
        "14464": {"comment":"Then OUT_TOKEN"},
        "14467": {"comment":"Otherwise a UDG"},
        "14470": {"synopsis":"The expression scanner's operation with code 0 (the marker $10C0 BANK_FN_PUSH leaves; the JP\nZ at $2757): DE = the BANK item from below it on the stack (D = the bank, E = the token\nafter BANK). Checking: on at $27B9. Running, with $2761 pushed as the return:\n1. E = $24: on to the USR code at $2184.\n2. Otherwise BC = the operand (TAKE_WORD).\n3. E = $9E or $E8 (SPRITE, SPRITE CONTINUE): SPRITE_FN_RUN.\n4. Otherwise BANK_READ at HL = the operand: a byte for PEEK ($BE), a word for DPEEK ($8A), a\n   call for USR ($C0); the BC it gives stacked.","comment":"HL = the marker"},
        "14471": {"comment":"BC = the item below it"},
        "14472": {"comment":"DE = the BANK item: D = bank, E = token"},
        "14473": {"comment":"BC and the marker back"},
        "14475": {"comment":"Checking syntax?"},
        "14478": {"comment":"Then on in the scanner"},
        "14481": {"comment":"$2761 as the return"},
        "14485": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "14486": {"comment":"$24?"},
        "14488": {"comment":"Then the USR code at $2184"},
        "14491": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14492": {"comment":"BC = the operand (TAKE_WORD)"},
        "14495": {"comment":"D, E back"},
        "14496": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "14497": {"comment":"$9E (SPRITE)?"},
        "14499": {"comment":"Then SPRITE_FN_RUN"},
        "14501": {"comment":"$E8 (CONTINUE)?"},
        "14503": {"comment":"Then SPRITE_FN_RUN too"},
        "14505": {"comment":"HL = the address"},
        "14507": {"comment":"BC = what is there"},
        "14510": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_BC_NO_IY)"},
        "14513": {"synopsis":"E = the operand's low byte, L = the token; the high byte must be 0 (else report B), then the\nother ROM's $099B (SPRITE_CALL).","comment":"E = the value's low byte"},
        "14514": {"comment":"L = the token"},
        "14515": {"comment":"The high byte 0?"},
        "14517": {"comment":"Then the call"},
        "14520": {"comment":"Otherwise report B"},
        "14522": {"synopsis":"SCAN_OP_TABLE's $38: the number as a signed 16-bit value (FP_TO_BC, negated when negative;\nover 16 bits is report B) to DE, the routine at $2E82 run through $2705 (with port $E3, the\nDivMMC control, = $87); the HL it gives back stacked (STACK_HL).","comment":"BC = the number, rounded"},
        "14525": {"comment":"Over 16 bits: report B"},
        "14528": {"comment":"Positive: as it is"},
        "14530": {"comment":"Negative: BC = -BC"},
        "14537": {"synopsis":"DE = the value; the $2705 call with its inline address $2E82.","comment":"DE = the value"},
        "14539": {"comment":"The routine at $2E82, port $E3 = $87"},
        "14542": {"synopsis":"The inline address after CALL $2705: $2E82, the routine run with port $E3 = $87."},
        "14544": {"comment":"HL = its result"},
        "14545": {"comment":"Stacked (STACK_HL)"},
        "14547": {"synopsis":"Reads at HL in bank D: the other ROM's $3308 (CALL_OTHER_BC) turns D into the page in A',\nthen by E: $C0 (USR) BANK_USR; $BE (PEEK) BC = the byte (B = 0); anything else BC = the\nword, low byte first (the routine at $08FC each).","comment":"Kept"},
        "14548": {"comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14549": {"comment":"BC = $3308"},
        "14552": {"comment":"The bank's page, in the other ROM"},
        "14555": {"comment":"The page into A'"},
        "14556": {"comment":"D, E back"},
        "14557": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "14558": {"comment":"USR?"},
        "14560": {"comment":"Then BANK_USR"},
        "14563": {"comment":"C = the byte at HL in the bank"},
        "14566": {"comment":"HL to the next"},
        "14569": {"comment":"A = the token"},
        "14570": {"comment":"PEEK ($BE)?"},
        "14572": {"comment":"No: B = the next byte"},
        "14575": {"comment":"BC = the byte or the word"},
        "14576": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14577": {"synopsis":"USR in a bank: BC = H'L' = the address, D' = the bank, NZ and carry, then the USR runner at\n$1F6A.","comment":"A = the bank"},
        "14578": {"comment":"The address kept"},
        "14579": {"comment":"BC = it"},
        "14581": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "14582": {"comment":"D' = the bank"},
        "14583": {"comment":"HL' = the address"},
        "14584": {"comment":"NZ and carry"},
        "14587": {"comment":"The USR runner at $1F6A"},
        "14594": {"synopsis":"SCAN_OP_TABLE's $34-$36: functions of a stream. The stream (TAKE_BYTE) made current, then\nthe other ROM's $03E5 (via $19CE) with B = 0, 1 or 2 (the code less $34) and DE = 4, 2 or 4;\nthe old channel back (CHAN_SET_FLAGS). Code $35 stacks the byte A it gives; $34 and $36\nstack HL + 65536 x DE.","comment":"The code kept"},
        "14595": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL"},
        "14598": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14599": {"comment":"The code kept again"},
        "14600": {"comment":"A = the stream (TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14603": {"comment":"Made current (STREAM_SELECT)"},
        "14606": {"comment":"A = the code"},
        "14607": {"comment":"0, 1 or 2"},
        "14609": {"comment":"B = it"},
        "14610": {"comment":"The other set"},
        "14611": {"comment":"A x 2"},
        "14612": {"comment":"Not 0: 2 or 4"},
        "14614": {"comment":"Otherwise DE = 4"},
        "14616": {"synopsis":"DE = A, the second parameter.","comment":"DE = A"},
        "14619": {"comment":"HL = $03E5, the routine in the other ROM"},
        "14622": {"comment":"Run ($19CE)"},
        "14625": {"comment":"HL = CURCHL, the result HL kept"},
        "14626": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14627": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "14628": {"comment":"The old channel back (CHAN_SET_FLAGS)"},
        "14631": {"comment":"A back"},
        "14632": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "14633": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "14634": {"comment":"BC = A"},
        "14637": {"comment":"A = the code"},
        "14638": {"comment":"$35?"},
        "14640": {"comment":"Then A is the result"},
        "14642": {"synopsis":"Stacks HL + 65536 x DE (both by STACK_BC_NO_IY, then multiplied and added). Also from $1D7A.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "14643": {"comment":"BC = HL"},
        "14645": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "14648": {"comment":"BC = DE"},
        "14649": {"comment":"Stacked"},
        "14652": {"comment":"x 65536, +"},
        "14661": {"comment":"Done"},
        "14662": {"synopsis":"SCAN_OP_TABLE's $33: the word at address n (TAKE_WORD), read by an LD HL,(nn) and RET that\nthe routine at $0918 builds at MEMBOT and runs; stacked (STACK_HL).","comment":"BC = the address (TAKE_WORD)"},
        "14665": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "14667": {"comment":"HL = the word there ($0918's LD HL,(nn))"},
        "14670": {"synopsis":"Stacks HL (STACK_BC_NO_IY).","comment":"BC = HL"},
        "14672": {"synopsis":"STACK_BC_NO_IY.","comment":"Stacked (STACK_BC_NO_IY)"},
        "14675": {"synopsis":"Token $9A (BANK) in an expression (the scanner's character table, word at $0734): the bank\nnumber (a number, TAKE_BYTE when running) into D, then by the token after it:\n- $A8 (FN): on at $089C;\n- $87 (PEEK$): PEEK_STR_BANK;\n- $C0 (USR): on at $17AF;\n- $BE (PEEK) or $8A (DPEEK): BANK_FN_PUSH;\n- anything else: report C.","comment":"Past BANK, a number"},
        "14678": {"comment":"Running?"},
        "14681": {"comment":"A = the bank (TAKE_BYTE)"},
        "14684": {"comment":"D = it"},
        "14685": {"comment":"The token after it"},
        "14686": {"comment":"FN?"},
        "14688": {"comment":"Then $089C"},
        "14691": {"comment":"PEEK$ ($87)?"},
        "14693": {"comment":"Then PEEK_STR_BANK"},
        "14696": {"comment":"USR?"},
        "14698": {"comment":"Then $17AF"},
        "14701": {"comment":"PEEK?"},
        "14703": {"comment":"Then BANK_FN_PUSH"},
        "14705": {"comment":"DPEEK ($8A)?"},
        "14707": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "14710": {"synopsis":"E = the token; DE pushed for BANK_OP_APPLY, then the marker BC = $10C0 (priority $10, code\n0) through $082F, which goes past the token and scans the operand.","comment":"E = the token"},
        "14711": {"synopsis":"DE pushed (D, E as given), then the marker (BANK_FN_PUSH). From $17D2 with E = $C0.","comment":"The BANK item"},
        "14712": {"comment":"The marker: priority $10, code 0"},
        "14715": {"comment":"Past the token, the operand scanned ($082F)"},
        "14718": {"synopsis":"Token $9E (SPRITE) in an expression (the character table's word at $073C), by the token\nafter it: $E8 (CONTINUE) BANK_FN_PUSH with E = $E8; AT ($AC) SPRITE_AT_FN; OVER ($DE)\nSPRITE_OVER_FN; otherwise CH_ADD back one and BANK_FN_PUSH with E = $9E.","comment":"The token after SPRITE"},
        "14719": {"comment":"CONTINUE ($E8)?"},
        "14721": {"comment":"Then BANK_FN_PUSH"},
        "14723": {"comment":"AT?"},
        "14725": {"comment":"Then SPRITE_AT_FN"},
        "14727": {"comment":"OVER ($DE)?"},
        "14729": {"comment":"Then SPRITE_OVER_FN"},
        "14731": {"comment":"Back one"},
