        "14767": {"synopsis":"SPRITE OVER (a,b [TO c] [,d [,e]]): '(' and two numbers, then the optional parts (the\nroutine at $0FF5 each, a bit in D for each one present), ')'. Running: the optional values\ntaken (0 when left out, the routine at $1E6F each; c is b when left out), then a and b, and\nthe other ROM's $0934 (through $1EF2); the A it gives stacked. Then SET_NUMERIC.","comment":"The next character"},
        "14768": {"comment":"'('?"},
