        "14850": {"synopsis":"Token $87 (PEEK$) in an expression (the character table's word at $070E): PEEK_STR_BANK with\nD = $FF, no bank.","comment":"D = $FF: no bank"},
        "14852": {"synopsis":"PEEK$(addr,n), PEEK$(addr,~) or PEEK$(addr,~t), with $25DB (the scanner's string result) as\nthe return and D = the bank ($FF for none):\n1. Checked: '(', a number, ',', then a length, '~' alone, or '~' and a terminator, ')'.\n2. Running: DE = addr; n bytes, up to and including the first byte with bit 7 set (~), or up\n   to and not including byte t (~t; over 255 is report B).\n3. No bank: the string is the memory itself, its length counted (PEEK_STR_SCAN). With a\n   bank: the bytes copied into the workspace (PEEK_STR_COPY).\nExit: DE = the string, BC = its length.","comment":"$25DB, the string result, as the return"},
        "14856": {"comment":"The bank kept"},
        "14857": {"comment":"The next character"},
        "14858": {"comment":"'('?"},
        "14860": {"synopsis":"Report C when NZ.","comment":"Otherwise report C"},
        "14863": {"comment":"The address, a number"},
        "14866": {"comment":"','?"},
        "14868": {"comment":"Otherwise report C"},
