        "15611": {"synopsis":"A XOR (HL).","comment":"A XOR (HL)"},
        "15612": {"comment":"Back"},
        "15616": {"synopsis":"Character set: the pictures of the 96 character codes $20-$7F, 8 bytes each, 768 bytes up to\nthe ROM's end, as in the 48K ROM. A byte is one pixel row, top row first, bit 7 the leftmost\npixel; code c's picture is at CHARACTER_SET + (c - $20) x 8, which is CHARS + c x 8 when\nCHARS = $3C00. Readers in this page:\n- printing: OUT_CHAR draws code c from CHARS + c x 8, so pointing CHARS elsewhere replaces\nthe set;\n- SCREEN$: SCREENS_VALUE compares a screen cell with the 96 pictures from CHARS + $100.\nThis page sets neither CHARS nor the UDGs: RST $00 goes to SOFT_RESET.\nCodes $80-$8F (block graphics), $90 up (UDGs) and keywords have no pictures here.\n$20 - Character: ' '"},
        "15624": {"synopsis":"$21 - Character: '!'"},
